p directions clear, and follow steps in order. Example scenario prompt for pairs: \"Your younger sister left her dolls on the bed. What 2 things will you ask her to do?\" IV. EVALUATION Use an informal checklist to assess each student during the role-play: Uses polite Gives clear Listens language (can 2-step directions carefully and Criteria you, please) in the correct follows peer’s when giving order directions directions accurately Excellent Good Satisfactory Note: Assess by observing each pair once. Give positive feedback like, \"Great job asking nicely!\" or \"Perfect order of steps!\" V. AGREEMENT For homework, students will: Find a time to give one 2-step direction to a family member (sibling, parent, or grandparent) using polite language (e.g., \"Can you please pass the spoon and put it on my plate?\"). Ask the family member if they understood the directions. Share what direction they gave and how it went with the class in our next lesson.',0,1,'none'),
