(246,14,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-031.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-031.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,31,'B. Games\n  Scavenger Hunt: Look for five things that start\nwith the sound /r/.\n\n\n\n\nV. Agreement\nDraw/ cut 5 pictures which has an initial\nsound of letter /r/.',1,1,'drawing'),
(247,15,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say the word slowly. Listen for the vowel sound in the middle.',NULL,'[]','Say the word slowly. Listen for the vowel sound in the middle.',NULL,0,32,'Phoneme Isolation (Middle/Medial\n\nReview:\n       Show picture of a\n    What do you call this picture? (hat)\nAsk the learners to say the sound of each\nletter. /h/ /a/ /t/ What is the beginning sound\nof the word hat ? /h/\n\n\nDevelopmental Activities\nWhen we isolate the sounds of the words, we\ncan hear the individual sounds in a word.\nI will say the sound of the word and please\nlisten carefully. (My Turn)\n\n  A. The word car has three different sounds.\n     /c/ /a/ /r/.\n     The middle sound of\n     the word car is /a/.\n\n  B. The word car has three different sounds.\n  /c/ /a/ /r/. (Your turn)\n  Now, say the sounds with me, /c/ /a/ /r/.\n\n  C. Tell me the middle sound of the word\n  car. Very good. It is /a/',0,1,'none'),
(248,15,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-034.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-034.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,34,'C. The word mat has         three\n   different sounds.\n          /m/ /a/ /t/.\n          (Your turn)\n            Now, say the sounds with me, /m/ /a/ /t/.\nD. Tell me the middle sound of the word mat. Very good. It\n   is /a/\nE. Again, what is the sound of the word mat? /m/ /a/ /t/.\n   (Our turn)\nWhat is the middle sound of the word mat? It is ……. /a/.\n\n\nGuided Practice:\n     Speak Whale – like in Finding Nemo- Say the\n    word as Dory would when speaking whale,\n    really stretching it out…” LAAAAAP.” Did\n    they hear the /a/ sound?\n\n    Generalization\n         The sounds that will be produced in the\n    middle of the words can be called middle or\n    medial sounds. Say the middle sound of the\n    following pictures.',1,1,'drawing'),
(249,15,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-035.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-035.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,35,'Evaluation\n\n\n     Phoneme                    . Worksheet\n     Isolation           Middle Sound Isolation\n\n\n     A. Instruction. What is the middle sound of the\n        picture given?\n\n\n\n1.           i__k      A. /n/ B.      /k/     C.   /t/\n\n\n\n2.           r__t A.      /a/ B.      /e/     C.    /o/\n\n\n\n\n3.           b__y   A.    /a/    B.   /o/     C.   /u/\n\n\n\n\n4.           p__n A. /a/          B. /e/      C.\n                                                   /i/',1,1,'drawing'),
(250,15,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-036.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-036.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,36,'/a/          /e/        /i/\n5.           t___n A.           B.          C.\n\n\n\n\n      B. Directions: Look at the pictures. Spell each word\n        using the letter clues.\n\n\n\n      1.                        k                t\n\n\n     2.                         r                g\n\n\n     3.                              b                 n\n\n\n     4.                              c                 w\n\n\n     5.\n                                     t                 n\n\n\n      a          e          i               o              u',1,1,'drawing'),
(251,15,NULL,'learn',5,'Your turn · sheet 4','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-037.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-037.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,37,'V. Agreement\nDraw or cut 5 pictures which has an initial\nsound of /a/',1,1,'drawing'),
(252,16,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say each word. Listen closely to its last sound.',NULL,'[]','Say each word. Listen closely to its last sound.',NULL,0,38,'Activity 3. Phoneme Isolation\n        Ending/ Final Sounds Isolation\n\nReview\nShow picture of a\nWhat do you call this picture? (hat)\nAsk the learners to say the sounds/ of each\nletter. /h/ /a/ /t/\nWhat is the beginning sound of the word? The middle\nsound?\nDevelopmental activities\nWhen we isolate the sounds of the words, we can hear\nthe individual sounds in a word.\nI will say the sounds of the word and please listen\ncarefully.\n  A. The word tap has three different sounds.\n     /t/ /a/ /p/.\n    The ending sound of the word\n    tap is /p/.\n\n  B. The word tap has three different\n     sounds. /t/ /a/ /p/.\nNow, say the sounds with me, /t/ /a/ /p/.\n\n   C. Tell me the ending sound of the word tap. Very\n     good. It is /p/',0,1,'none'),
(253,16,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-040.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-040.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,40,'B. The word box has three different                sounds.\n         /b/ /o/ /x/.\n\n(Your turn)\nNow, say the sounds with me, /b/ /o/ /x/.\nC. Tell me the ending sound of the word box. Very good.\nIt is /x/.\n\nD. Again, what is the sound of box? /b/ /o/ /x/.\n\n(Our turn)\nWhat is the ending sound of the word box? It is ……. /x/.\n\n\nGuided Practice:\n    Games:\n    Toy Thief is one of my most favorite phoneme isolation\ngames. Tape 5-7 pictures/ toys to a door. Have your child\nrescue the ones by their ending sound. Keep in mind that\nwords like “horse “have an ending sound of /s/. Call out,\n“Rescue the animal with the ending sound /t/.',1,1,'drawing'),
(254,16,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-041.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-041.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,41,'Generalization: The sounds that will be\n    produced in the end of the words can be\n    called as ending or final sounds.\n\n\n\n    IV. Evaluation\n\n\n                             Worksheet\n    Phoneme\n                      Ending Sound Isolation\n     Isolation\n\n\n\n\nAgreement\nDraw/ cut 5 pictures which has an initial sound /d/',1,1,'drawing'),
(255,17,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say the picture names. Find words that start with the same sound.',NULL,'[]','Say the picture names. Find words that start with the same sound.',NULL,0,45,'Activity 4: Initial Phoneme Identification\n\n\n1.   Motivation:\n        Show different pictures to the pupils and say….\n\n\n        This is a mat .\n\n\n        This is a milk.\n\n\n        This is a moon.\n\n\n2.   Developmental activities:\n       Let the pupils say the name of the picture\n         mat, milk , moon\n         Emphasize the initial sound\n\n\n       Call a pupil, let him/her name the picture.\n           mat, milk , moon\nAsk: Did you hear a sound?\nWhat sound do you hear at the beginning?\nDo they have the same initial sound?\nWhat sound do they all have the same?\n    This morning/afternoon, we are going to know the name of\nthe picture that has the same initial or beginning sound.',0,1,'none'),
(256,17,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-047.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-047.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,47,'Activity 1. Connect Me\n       Direction: Draw a line to the picture that has same initial or\nbeginning sound.\n\n\n\n1.\n\n\n\n\n2.\n\n\n\n\n3.\n\n\n\n\n4.\n\n\n\n\n5.\n\n\n\n\n5. Generalization\n   What is Phoneme Identification?\n\n\n    Phoneme identification is the ability to recognize the\n common sound in different words.',1,1,'drawing'),
(257,17,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-048.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-048.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,48,'IV. Evaluation\n\n\n\n       Activity 2. Identify Me\n\n       Direction: Name each picture and identify the\ncommon sound that they have. Write your answer inside\nthe cloud.\n1.\n                                 cup                         /___ /\n             man                                 mop\n\n\n2.\n               can               cut              cow            /___ /\n\n\n\n3.\n               hat               hug             ham             /___ /\n\n\n\n4.\n                kid              key               kit       /___ /\n\n\n5.\n                                  rat            red             /___ /\n               run\n\n\n\n\nV. Agreement\n\n  Think three words that has initial sound of /s/ and draw it.',1,1,'drawing'),
(258,18,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Stretch each word and listen for its middle vowel sound.',NULL,'[]','Stretch each word and listen for its middle vowel sound.',NULL,0,49,'Activity 5: Medial Phoneme Identification\n\n\n1.   Review:\n        Listen to the teacher carefully. Identify the common sound\nthat the following words have.\n     nut     net nip\n     bed bad bit\n     tip      tap tud\n\n\n2.   Motivation:\n           Show different pictures to the pupils and say….\n\n\n           This is a can .\n\n\n           This is a bag.\n\n\n           This is a map.\n\n\n3.   Developmental activities:\n       Let the pupils say the name of the picture\n            can, bag , map\n            Emphasize the medial sound\n       Call a pupil, let him/her name the picture.\n             can, bag , map\nAsk: Did you hear a sound?',0,1,'none'),
(259,18,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-051.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-051.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,51,'5.   Practice\n\n\n       Activity 3. Circle Me\n\n Directions: Name each picture and identify its medial\nsound. Then, encircle the picture that has different medial\nsound.\n1.\n\n\n\n\n2.\n\n\n\n\n3.\n\n\n\n\n4.\n\n\n\n\n5.',1,1,'drawing'),
(260,18,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-052.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-052.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,52,'6. Generalization\n   In identifying the phoneme we should hear the sound carefully\n   so that we can be able to identify phoneme correctly.\n\n\n  IV. Evaluation\n\n         Activity 4. Check Me\n\nDirections: Read each word below. Put a check ( / ) to\nthe words that have the same medial sound as the\npicture.\n\n\n                          Nun\n\n\n\n\n     mat                                    tub\n                         gun\n\n      hut                                    jog',1,1,'drawing'),
(261,18,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-053.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-053.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,53,'V. Agreement\n\n  Direction: Write 5 words that has the same medial sound.\n\n  1.\n\n  2.\n\n  3.\n\n  4.\n\n  5.',1,1,'drawing'),
(262,19,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Listen to the last sound. Find words with matching endings.',NULL,'[]','Listen to the last sound. Find words with matching endings.',NULL,0,54,'Activity 6: Final Phoneme Identification\n\n\n     1. Review: (Oral Activity)\n     Directions: Name each picture and identify its medial\nsound.\n\n     1.                       2.          3.\n\n\n\n\n 4.                           5.\n\n\n2.        Motivation:\n             Show different pictures to the pupils and say….\n             This is a wax .\n\n\n\n             This is a box.\n\n\n             This is a six.\n\n\n3.        Developmental activities:\n            Let the pupils say the name of the picture\n              wax             box   six\n              ( Emphasize the final sound)',0,1,'none'),
(263,19,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-056.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-056.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,56,'5.   Practice\nDistribute to the pupils the activity sheets and let them answer the\nactivity 5. Box Me.\n\n\n\n\n          Activity 5. Check Me\n\nDirections: Listen to the teacher carefully. Box the three\nflowers that has the same final sound.\n\n\n\n\n1.      bed             Ted            mad              bib\n\n\n\n2.      mop              lip            pet            map\n\n\n\n3.      wed              yet            met              set\n\n\n        cab            ham               lab               nab\n4.\n\n\n5.       sip             hip            hat            hop',1,1,'drawing'),
(264,19,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-057.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-057.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,57,'5. Generalization\n   In identifying the final phoneme is the last sound you hear.\n\n\n  IV. Evaluation\n\n\n               Activity 6. Color Me\nDirections: Listen to your teacher and look at the picture\ncarefully. Know its name and its final sound. Color the\ncircle beside the drawing.\n\n\n   Color it red if   Color it blue    Color it yellow    Color it black\n   has /n/ final       if has /g/     if has /d/ final   if has /t/ final\n      sound          final sound           sound             sound',1,1,'drawing'),
(265,20,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say the words together. Which beginning sound does not belong?',NULL,'[]','Say the words together. Which beginning sound does not belong?',NULL,0,61,'Activity 7: INITIAL PHONEME CATEGORIZATION\n\n1. Motivation\n Instructions: Show the following pictures and ask:\n\n a. What do you see in the first picture?   sky\n b. How about the second picture?                 sun\n c. How about the third?                    Rabbit\n d. What have you observed in the given pictures?\n\n (the teacher will say again the name of the pictures emphasizing their\n   . sound)\n initial\n\n     e. Which picture do not belong to the set?\n\nUnlocking\n\nRead the following and understand.\n          Initial- beginning, phoneme- sound\n\n2. Presentation\n      This time, you will be learning about Initial Phoneme\n    .\nCategorization   . It is identifying the words and pictures that have the\ndifferent beginning sound.\nExample:               ball        bat         can\n\n  3. Discussion\n  Show a set of words.\n\n\n\n                      cat                    mat               carrot\n\n What have you observed in the set of words?',0,1,'none'),
(266,20,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-062.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-062.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,62,'Can you point out the word that does not belong to the\n group? (call a learner to give the answer)\n\n\nThe teacher will give more examples.\n( sun, rain seed), (can cat ball)\n(table key kite)\n\n4. Practice',1,1,'drawing'),
