(274,22,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-072.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-072.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,72,'5.\n\n\n\n\n          nip                  ikt                ellb\n\n\n     V. Agreement\n. Directions: Underline the words that have the different\n  final sound.\n        1.       sweet        hit           ram\n        2.       bag          rag           bin\n        3.       pad          paper         zipper\n        4.       hay          toy           wall\n        5.       lock         ot            stick\n\n .\n\n\n\n\n             .',1,1,'drawing'),
(275,23,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Listen to each sound, then slide them together to say a whole word.',NULL,'[]','Listen to each sound, then slide them together to say a whole word.',NULL,0,75,'Activity 10: YOU PUT ME TOGETHER\n\n\nMotivation:\n\n  Show different pictures to the pupils and let them say their\n  sounds.\n\n\n\n\n  Ask them some animals or things and let them say the sounds\n  they produce.\n\n  Tell to the pupils that different things and animals have its own\n  different sounds.\n\nDevelopmental activities:\n\n  Show cards containing the letter and say to them letter sound.\n\n\n            /c/        /a/          /t/\n  Have a review on the different letter sounds.\n\nAnalysis/Discussion\n\n  Show the picture to the pupils\n\n\n\n     Say:\n\n     Ask the pupils what is the picture.',0,1,'none'),
(276,23,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-077.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-077.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,77,'Practice\n\nDistribute to the pupils the activity sheets and let them pupils answer\nthe activity 1. You Put me Together.\n\n\n\n\n                         Phoneme Blending\n\n__           Activity 10: YOU PUT ME TOGETHER\n     Activity 1. Put the sounds together for each group of\n     sounds below that I say. Check the box of your\n     correct answer.\n\n\n\n\nGeneralization\n\n  What is Phoneme Blending?',1,1,'drawing'),
(277,23,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-078.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-078.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,78,'Conclusion: Phoneme blending is the ability to hear the\nindividual sounds in a word, put the sounds together, and say the\nword that is made.\n\n\nEvaluation\n\n                    Phoneme Blending\n\n               Activity 10: BLEND AND READ\n\n        Directions; produce the sound of each letter\n        and blend to form a word.',1,1,'drawing'),
(278,23,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-079.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-079.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,79,'Agreement\n\n\n\n\nName:\nDirections: Blend the sounds together to form the complete word.\nWrite the full word on the space provided.\n\n\n  1. /b/   /i/   /t/                  bit\n                              _____________________\n\n  2. /p/   /e/   /t/          _____________________\n\n  3. /m/ /a/     /n/          _____________________\n\n  4. /p/   /u/   /t/          _____________________\n\n  5. /s/   /i/   /t/          _____________________',1,1,'drawing'),
(279,24,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Listen for two consonant sounds at the beginning. Keep both sounds as you blend.',NULL,'[]','Listen for two consonant sounds at the beginning. Keep both sounds as you blend.',NULL,0,80,'Activity 11: Beginning Consonant\n                            Phoneme Blending\n\nReview:\n    Show picture of a cat\n\n\n\n                      /c/ /a/ /t/            cat\n\n\nAsk the pupils to blend the different sounds of the letters to form a\nword cat.\n\nMotivation\n     Let the learners sing the song\n\n           Little playmates dance with me\n           Both my hands I gave to thee\n           1,2,3, 1,2,3 dance around so merrily\n           With your hands go clap! clap! clap!\n           With your feet go stamp! stamp! stamp!\n           1,2,3, 1,2,3 dance around so merrily.\n\n\nDevelopmental activities:\n\n  Now lets identify words from the song with initial consonant blend\n\n\n         /cl/          /a/            /p/              Clap\n\n\n\n\n         /st/        /a/            /m/     /p/               stamp',0,1,'none'),
(280,24,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-082.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-082.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,82,'Practice\nDistribute to the pupils the activity sheets and let them pupils answer\nthe Activity 1. You Math Me\n\n\n     Phoneme Blending\n                               Activity 11: MATCH ME\nDirection: Match the sound I make to the correct picture. Encircle\nyour answer.\n\n\n\n\n  /sh/      /i/      /p/\n          ship\n\n\n   /c/     /a/       /t/\n          cat\n\n   /fl/     /a/    /g/\n          flag\n\n\n\n   /tr/     /e/      /e/\n          tree\n\n\n   /st/     /a/      /r/\n          star\n\n\nConclusion\n\n   What is Phoneme Blending?\n      Phoneme blending is the ability to hear the individual sounds\nin a word, put the sounds together, and say the word that is made.',1,1,'drawing'),
(281,24,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-083.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-083.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,83,'Evaluation\n                            Phoneme Blending\n\n\n                        Activity 11: BLEND HUNT\n\n    Directions: Hunt to complete the word by finding\n    the consonant blend from the list to complete the\n    word.\n\n\n                   cr      dr        gl\n       sh                                    gr\n              fr                sn                            fl\n                                                    sp\n\n              __ __ ider                          __ __ apes\n\n\n\n              __ __ ess                           __ __ ab\n\n                __ __ og\n              dress                                   __ __ ass\n\n\n               __ __ oes                          __ __ ail\n\n               s\n                   __ __ower                      __ __ ass\n\nAgreement\n\n  Think and list of letters. Say their sounds and form 5 words.\n  Write it on your paper.',1,1,'drawing'),
(282,25,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Listen for the consonant sounds at the end of the word.',NULL,'[]','Listen for the consonant sounds at the end of the word.',NULL,0,84,'Activity 12: Ending Consonant Phoneme\n                                 Blending\n\n\nReview:\n    Show picture of hands clapping\n\n\n\n                     /cl/ /a/ /p/            clap\n\n\nAsk the pupils to blend the different sounds of the letter to form a\nword clap.\n\nGive more examples:\n\nDevelopmental activities:\n\n  Show cards containing the letter and say to them letter sound.\n\n\n         /m/            /i/         /lk/              milk\n\n\n  Tell to the pupils:\n     We blend final consonant letters with vowels in forming\n  phoneme.\n\n  Analysis/Discussion\n\n  Show the picture to the pupils:\n\n\n                            fish',0,1,'none'),
