(285,25,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-088.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-088.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,88,'Evaluation\n\n\n                              Phoneme Blending\n\n                   Activity 12: YOU COMPLETE\n                   ME\n Directions: Complete the word with the correct\n final consonant blend.\n\n\n    ck       rl   rd     lk   rn        ck   nd sk lt      nt\n\n                   sa __ __\n                                                       bla __ __\n\n\n\n                       bi __ __\n                                                     ma__ __\n\n\n                         mi__ __                     sa __ __\n\n\n                        ho __ __\n                                                         be __\n                                                         __\n\n                          gi __ __                    te __ __\n\n\n\nAgreement\n\n  Think and list of letters. Say their sounds and form 5 words.',1,1,'drawing'),
(286,26,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say a word slowly. Move one counter for each sound you hear. Sounds and letters are not always the same.',NULL,'[]','Say a word slowly. Move one counter for each sound you hear. Sounds and letters are not always the same.',NULL,0,92,'Activity13: Phoneme Segmenting\n\n\n1.Motivation:\n          Show this picture to the pupils and say….\n\n\n           This is a cat.\n\n\n\n\n      A cat….. cat…. /c/ /a/ / t/\n\n\n2.   Developmental activities:\n         Let the pupils say the name of the picture\n           A cat….. A cat….. /c/ /a/ / t/\n           Emphasize each sound of the word.\n         Call a pupil, let him/her name the picture.\n           A cat….. A cat….. /c/ /a/ / t/\nAsk: Did you hear a sound?\nWhat sound do you hear at the beginning?\nWhat sound do you hear at the middle?\nWhat sound do you hear at the end?\nDo they have the same sound?\n\n\nToday, we are going to practice the sounds we hear in\nwords.\nListen and watch. I’ll say the sounds in the word “cat.” (Show one',0,1,'none'),
(287,26,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-094.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-094.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,94,'Another example:\nLook at the picture….\n\n\n\n\nTell me the name of the picture…… map\nTell me all the sound of the name of the picture. /m/ /a/ /p/\nHow many sounds did you hear from the word map?\n4.   Practice\nDistribute to the pupils the activity sheets and let them answer\nactivity 1. Color Me\n\n\n\n           Activity 13.1: Color Me\nDirections: Quietly say the name of each picture. Color\none circle for every sound that you say.\n      1.\n\n\n\n\n      2.',1,1,'drawing'),
(288,26,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-095.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-095.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,95,'4.\n\n\n\n\n     5.\n\n\n\n\n5. Generalization\n   What is Phoneme Segmentation?\n   Phoneme Segmentation is the ability to break words\ndown into individual sounds.',1,1,'drawing'),
(289,26,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-096.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-096.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,96,'IV. Evaluation\n\n Distribute to the learners the activity sheets and let them answer\n activity 2. Tell Me\n\n\n\n               Activity 13. 2: Tell Me\n Directions: Look at each picture and tell me every sound\n of its name.\n\n1.                        3.                           5.\n\n\n\n2.                        4.\n\n\n\n V. Agreement\n\n     Give every sound of the following words orally.\n     1. log =\n     2. mart=\n     3. bit =\n     4. door=\n     5. sand =',1,1,'drawing'),
(290,27,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say the whole word, then separate the sounds you hear.',NULL,'[]','Say the whole word, then separate the sounds you hear.',NULL,0,97,'Activity 14: Phoneme Segmenting\n1.       Review:\n          Phoneme Jumping\n       Directions: Prepare a colored paper green, yellow, red and\nblue on the floor. When the teacher says a word, the learner will\njump according to the sounds he/she hears. While jumping to the\ncolored paper he/she will repeat the sound he/she hears. Then\nafter will shout how many moves she/he does.\nExample:\nlap        /l/      /a/     /p/           - - - - - - - - shout 3\nmask         /m/      /a/     /s/   /k/     - - - - - - - - shout 4\nhood          /h/     /o/     /d/           - - - - - - - - shout 3\n\n\n          Listen to the teacher carefully.\n1. hen\n2. pit\n3. Bert\n4.food\n5.band\n\n\n2.Motivation:\n            Show these pictures to the pupils and say….\n\n\n             This is a wig.',0,1,'none'),
(291,27,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','physical','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Follow the jumping-and-sounds instructions shown with your teacher. Choose Done after you have tried the activity.','assets/images/level2a/page-097.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-097.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Follow the jumping-and-sounds instructions shown with your teacher. Choose Done after you have tried the activity.',NULL,10,97,'Activity 14: Phoneme Segmenting\n1.       Review:\n          Phoneme Jumping\n       Directions: Prepare a colored paper green, yellow, red and\nblue on the floor. When the teacher says a word, the learner will\njump according to the sounds he/she hears. While jumping to the\ncolored paper he/she will repeat the sound he/she hears. Then\nafter will shout how many moves she/he does.\nExample:\nlap        /l/      /a/     /p/           - - - - - - - - shout 3\nmask         /m/      /a/     /s/   /k/     - - - - - - - - shout 4\nhood          /h/     /o/     /d/           - - - - - - - - shout 3\n\n\n          Listen to the teacher carefully.\n1. hen\n2. pit\n3. Bert\n4.food\n5.band\n\n\n2.Motivation:\n            Show these pictures to the pupils and say….\n\n\n             This is a wig.',1,1,'perform'),
(292,27,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-100.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-100.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,100,'Write each sound in the box. Only use as many boxes as you\nneed.\nExample:\ndoor      /d/ /o/ /r/\n\nwork     /w/ /o/ /r/ /k/\n\n\n\n5.     Practice\nDistribute to the learners the activity sheets and let them answer\nactivity 3. Circle Me\n\n\n\n\n                  Activity 14.1: Circle Me\nDirections: Identify the picture and encircle the correct\nphoneme/sound of every picture.\n\n\n1.\n\n                               /c/ /a/ /r/            /w/ /a/ /r/\n\n\n2.\n                               /t/ /e/ /n/            /p/ /e/ /n/\n\n\n3.\n                               /b/ /i/ /n/            /t/ /i/ /n/',1,1,'drawing'),
(293,27,NULL,'learn',4,'Your turn · sheet 3','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-101.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-101.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,101,'4.\n\n                              /s/ /a/ /n/           /s/ /a/ /n/ /d/\n\n\n\n5.\n\n                              /f/ /o/ /u/ /r/        /f/ /o/ /r/\n\n\n\n\n5. Generalization\n   Why Phoneme Segmentation important?\n    Phoneme segmentation is essential in developing\n reading and spelling skills.\n\n\n\n\n  IV. Evaluation\n\nDistribute to the pupils the activity sheets and let them answer\nactivity 2. Break Me.',1,1,'drawing'),
