(295,28,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say the word. Leave out its first sound. What is left?',NULL,'[]','Say the word. Leave out its first sound. What is left?',NULL,0,105,'Activity 15. Phoneme Deletion\n\n\nBeginning Sound Deletion\n          Recognizing the word after taking initial sound\nfrom a word.\n    When we take away the initial sound from a word,\nwe can hear another word with another meaning.\n\n\n\n\n          meat    take away /m/                eat',0,1,'none'),
(296,28,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-107.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-107.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,107,'Phoneme           Activity 15. Worksheet\n   Deletion\n  Name :\n\n\n        Exercise A.\nDirections: What is the new word after taking away the\n            first sound ?\n\n\n\n\n           -t                 - c              -s\n        twig                clock             stop\n\n\n\n\n            -r                -f               -t\n           rice             fear              trip',1,1,'drawing'),
(297,28,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-108.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-108.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,108,'Excercise B.\nDirections. Listen to the sounds your teacher is saying.\n     Blend them together to form a word.\n  1.           remove /w/ = ______________\n\n  2.           remove /k/       = ______________\n\n  3.           remove / m/      = ______________\n\n\n  4.           remove / c/      = _____________\n\n\n  5.           remove /c/       =_____________\n  Exercise C.\n Directions. Remove the beginning sound in these\n              words.\n\n A. Delete the /s/ sound from the following words.\n What do you get\n              ?\n\n stop= ________ sand=_________ soak=________\n B. Delete the /t/ sound from the following words.\n What do you get ?\n tear= ________    Train= _________    Trap= ________\n\n C. Delete the /b/ sound from the following words.\n What do you get?\n Bam=Day 16. Phoneme\n      ________         Deletion\n                  Bat= __________   Bash= ________',1,1,'drawing'),
(298,29,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say the word, remove the sound named in the activity, and say what remains.',NULL,'[]','Say the word, remove the sound named in the activity, and say what remains.',NULL,0,109,'Activity 16. Phoneme Deletion\n\n\n\nEnding/Medial Sound Deletion\n    Recognizing the word after taking medial/final sound\nfrom a word.\n     When we take away the medial/final sound from a\nword, we can hear another word and the word becomes\ndifferent and the meaning may differ also.\n\n\n\n (My turn)\n    The teacher will show the picture of a band and\n    ask.\n    What is the picture ?\n\n                    take away /d/\n\n          band take away /d/                           ban\nThe teacher will show pictures and ask:\n   What is the picture? Yes, it is. It is the same picture\nabove.\n\n\n\n\n                        take away /b/               and\n            band       take away /b/                 and',0,1,'none'),
