(310,31,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-131.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-131.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,131,'V. Agreement\n\nList five words and add a phoneme to each to form a new word.\n\n\n          /s/    pin       spin\n\n     1.\n\n     2.\n\n     3.\n\n     4.\n\n     5.\n\nDistribute the activity sheets to the pupils and let them answer the\npost test.',1,1,'drawing'),
(311,32,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say a word. Replace only its first sound with the new sound.',NULL,'[]','Say a word. Replace only its first sound with the new sound.',NULL,0,135,'Activity 19: PHONEME TRADE AND HUNT\n\n\n\n              A. Motivation\n        Have a picture parade and let the learners\n     identify the beginning sound they produce when\n     naming the animals or things.\n\n\n\n\nAsk them other examples of animals or things and let them identify\nthe beginning sound.\n\n\nB. Developmental Activities\n\nLet the learners sing the song “Sounds of the Alphabet”\n\n\n           Https://youtu.be/r2frjzrc5jg\n\n\n           Have a review on letter sound\n\n\nC. Discussion (I do)\n  Show the picture of a cat to the learners. (I do)',0,1,'none'),
(312,32,NULL,'learn',2,'Your turn · sheet 1','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.','assets/images/level2a/page-138.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-138.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text.',NULL,10,138,'D. Practice (you do)\n\n\n        Distribute to the learners the activity sheets and\n\nlet them answer the activity.\n\n\n\n    Exercise 1: Change the beginning sound to form a new\nword.\n\n\n\n     Name:\n\n         Activity 1: Phoneme Trade\nDirections: Change the beginning sound each word\nto form a new word that matches the picture. Write\nyour answer in the blank space.\n\n\n\n\nConclusion:\n       Beginning Sound Substitution – is the change of\ninitial sound to form a new word.',1,1,'drawing'),
(313,32,NULL,'learn',3,'Your turn · sheet 2','drawing','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy.','Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.','assets/images/level2a/page-139.webp','[\"assets/images/level2a/page-139.webp\"]','Look closely at the original activity sheet. You can open a larger copy. Work through every numbered item on this sheet. Write answers with their numbers, or use the pen to mark the sheet. You can also speak an answer and check the detected text. Complete any home-practice task shown on this page; describe what you did or draw your work.',NULL,10,139,'Name:\n\n\n\n         Activity 19.1: Phoneme Hunt\nDirections: Change the beginning sound to form a new word.\n         Choose the letter from the jungle box.\n\n\n\n                f\n          d                    n              h\n\n                                    t\n          w                p\n                b                         c\n\n\n\n\nV. Agreement\n\n             List down 5 words and perform phoneme\nsubstitution in the initial or beginning sound.',1,1,'drawing'),
(314,33,NULL,'learn',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Say a word. Replace only its last sound with the new sound.',NULL,'[]','Say a word. Replace only its last sound with the new sound.',NULL,0,140,'Activity 20: I CAN CHANGE IT\n\n\n     A. Motivation\n\n          Have a mystery box with pictures of things and\n\n     animals and let the pupils come in front to identify the\n\n     ending sound they produce when naming the animals\n\n     or things.\n\n          (The pictures in the mystery box are found below)\n\n\n\n\n    Ask them other examples of animals or things and let\nthem identify ending sound.\n    B. Developmental Activities\n\n          Let the pupils watch the video about substituting\nphoneme in the final sound. Link found below)\n    Https://youtu.be/56agYENzrZc\n\n     C. Discussion (I do)\n          Show the picture of a bug to the learners. (I\n           do)',0,1,'none'),
