(400,60,NULL,'learn',1,'Meet the short “a” sound','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Look at the pictures. Their names have the short “a” sound.\nName each picture.\n\nListen as we blend the sounds:\nb + a + t = bat\nc + a + t = cat','assets/images/level3/l01-intro-bat.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l01-intro-bat.webp\", \"assets/images/level3/l01-intro-cat.webp\"]','Look at the pictures. Their names have the short “a” sound.\nName each picture.\n\nListen as we blend the sounds:\nb + a + t = bat\nc + a + t = cat',NULL,0,13,'5\nLesson 1: CVC Short “a”\nTeacher’s Activity:\n1.\nShow pictures with short “a” name.\n2. Ask learner/s to name the picture.\n3. Teacher sound out or blend the sample word/s.\nb + a + t= bat\nc + a + t= cat\n4. The teacher will present and read the following words,\nthen ask the learners to sound out the given sample\nwords with the short ‘a’ sound. (This can be done\nindividually, in pairs, by row, or in groups.)\nNote: This activity can be done in many variations.\nShort “a”\ncab\nfan\ntap\nmad\nman\ncat\nbag\nvan\nfat\nrag\nlap\nhat\njam\nmap\nmat\n5. Do the following activities:',1,1,'none'),
