(488,72,NULL,'learn',3,'Activity 1: Map-Based Word Search','group','Play this with your teacher and classmates. Choose Done when your turn is finished.','Act as a tourist guide. Lead the teacher to the dr- “country” on the word map.\n\nHow to play:\n1. Place the large “Our Word Map” poster on the floor so everyone can see the regions named after dr- words (e.g., Dragon, Drum, Dress).\n2. Each illustrated section of the island is a country the class will “visit” today.\n3. The teacher is a tourist who needs a student tourist guide.\n4. The teacher says, for example: “I want to explore the beautiful Dragon country; please bring me there!”\n5. The student guide finds the correct dr- country and leads the teacher to that spot.\n6. Take turns being the guide and choose different destinations like “Drum Land” or “Drink Province”.','assets/images/level3/l13-map.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l13-map.webp\"]','Act as a tourist guide. Lead the teacher to the dr- “country” on the word map.',NULL,10,79,'71\n71\nActivity 1: Map-Based Word Search\nDirection: Students will act as tourist guides by identifying and leading the\nteacher to specific \'dr-\' blend \'countries\' illustrated on the large floor word\nmap.\nProcedure:\n1. Place the large \"Our Word Map\" poster on the floor, ensuring all students\ncan see the different regions named after \"dr-\" words (e.g., Dragon, Drum,\nDress).\n2. Explain that each illustrated section of the island is a unique country that the\nclass will \"visit\" today.\n3. The teacher introduces themselves as a tourist who has never seen this\nisland before and needs a student \"tourist guide\" to navigate the terrain.\n4. The teacher expresses a desire to visit a specific land, saying: \"I want to\nexplore the beautiful Dragon country; please bring me there!\".\n5. The student guide identifies the correct \"dr-\" country on the map and\nphysically leads the teacher to that spot.\n6. Students take turns being the guide, choosing different destinations like\n\"Drum Land\" or \"Drink Province\" to practice reading and identifying the\n\"dr-\" blends.',1,1,'perform'),
