(506,74,NULL,'learn',4,'Activity 2: Grab and Read!','group','Play this with your teacher and classmates. Choose Done when your turn is finished.','Choose your favorite shirt from the clothesline, say “I love this shirt!”, and read the word on it loudly for the class to hear.\n\nHow to play:\n1. Display the clothesline and review the g sound combined with l and r.\n2. Learners form a line and one by one “walk the runway” to the board, choose a shirt, and announce, “I love this shirt!”\n3. The teacher asks the learner to read the word on the shirt loudly.\n4. A learner can use a “Lifeline” by choosing a classmate to help; the teacher gives a gentle prompt if needed.\n5. When the word is read correctly, the class gives a quick “sparkle clap”.','assets/images/level3/l15-shirts.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l15-shirts.webp\"]','Choose your favorite shirt from the clothesline, say “I love this shirt!”, and read the word on it loudly for the class to hear.',NULL,10,98,'90\n90\nActivity 2: Grab and Read!\nDirection: Choose your favorite shirt from the clothesline, say \'I love this\nshirt,\' and read the word on it loudly for the class to hear.\nProcedure:\n1. Display the clothesline on the board and briefly review the \"g\" sound\ncombined with \"l\" and \"r\" (the consonant blends).\n2. Have learners form a line. One by one, they \"walk the runway\" to the\nboard, choose their favorite shirt, and enthusiastically announce, \"I love\nthis shirt!\".\n3. The teacher asks the learner to read the word on their chosen shirt\nloudly for the class.\n4. If a learner finds a word tricky, they can use a \"Lifeline\" by choosing a\nclassmate to help them sound it out. If they are still stuck, the teacher\nprovides a gentle prompt.\n5. Once the word is read correctly, the class gives a quick \"sparkle clap\"\nbefore the next student takes their turn.',1,1,'perform'),
(507,74,44,'post',1,'Assessment: Individual Reading','reading','Read the following words correctly.','glad   grapes   globe   green   gloves   graph   glass   grill   glue   graduate',NULL,'[]','Read the following words correctly.','glad   grapes   globe   green   gloves   graph   glass   grill   glue   graduate',10,99,'91\n91\nAssessment (Individual Reading) (To be done until the end of the\nallotted time. Can also be given to learners for home\nreading)\nDirection: Read the following words correctly.',1,1,'answer'),
