(522,77,NULL,'learn',1,'Meet the blends sh-, sl-','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Look at the pictures. Their names begin with the consonant blend sh- and sl-.\n\nBlend the sounds:\ns + h = sh   s + l = sl\n\nNow read the words:\nsh + ip = ship   sl + eep = sleep','assets/images/level3/l18-intro-ship.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l18-intro-ship.webp\", \"assets/images/level3/l18-intro-sleep.webp\"]','Look at the pictures. Their names begin with the consonant blend sh- and sl-.\n\nBlend the sounds:\ns + h = sh   s + l = sl\n\nNow read the words:\nsh + ip = ship   sl + eep = sleep',NULL,0,115,'107\n107\nLesson 18: Consonant Blend sh- and sl-\nTeacher’s Activity:\n1. Show pictures with consonant sh- and sl.\n2. Ask any learner/s who can blend the |sh-| and\n|sl-|. If none, the teacher will demonstrate the\nblending.\ns + h = sh\ns + l = sl\n3.\nAsk any learner/s who can blend the |sh-| and |sl-|\nsounds. If no volunteer, the teacher will demonstrate\nthe activity.\nsh + ip = ship\nsl + eep = sleep\n4. Teacher will let the learners read more words with\n|sh-| and |sl-| blends.\n5. Proceed by doing the following activities:',1,1,'none'),
(523,77,NULL,'learn',2,'Activity 1: Map-Based Word Search','group','Play this with your teacher and classmates. Choose Done when your turn is finished.','Act as a local scout and lead the curious traveler to the correct “country” on the Word Map based on the clues about each sh- or sl- destination.\n\nHow to play:\n1. Lay the Word Map on the floor. Every “country” on this island is named after a special sound (sh- or sl-).\n2. One student is the Local Scout (tourist guide); the teacher or another student is the Curious Traveler.\n3. The Traveler describes a country with clues, e.g., “I want to visit the country where the sun is always bright!” (Shine).\n4. The Scout leads the Traveler to the correct spot. The class “unlocks” the border by chanting the word with a gesture.\n5. The Scout becomes the Traveler for the next round.','assets/images/level3/l18-map.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l18-map.webp\"]','Act as a local scout and lead the curious traveler to the correct “country” on the Word Map based on the clues about each sh- or sl- destination.',NULL,10,116,'108\n108\nActivity 1: Map-Based Word Search\nDirection: Act as a local scout and lead the curious traveler to the correct\n\'country\' on the Word Map based on the clues they give you about each sh-\nor sl- destination.\nProcedure:\n1. Lay the Word Map on the floor and explain that this is a newly discovered\nisland where every \"country\" is named after a special sound (sh- or sl-).\n2. Appoint one student as the Local Scout (Tourist Guide) who knows the\nisland\'s secrets, and the teacher (or another student) as the Curious Traveler.\n3. Instead of just naming the country, the Traveler describes it using clues.\n(Example: \"I want to visit the country where the sun is always bright!\" (Target:\nShine)).\n4. The Scout leads the Traveler to the correct spot on the map. Once they\narrive, the whole class must \"unlock\" the border by chanting the word\ntogether and making a corresponding gesture (e.g., pretending to shovel\nor slide).\n5. The Scout becomes the Traveler for the next round, ensuring high\nengagement and movement.',1,1,'perform'),
(524,77,NULL,'learn',3,'Activity 2: Word-Image Association','open','Match each picture with the correct word.','Match each picture with the correct word.',NULL,'[]','Match each picture with the correct word.',NULL,10,117,'109\n109\nActivity 2: Word- Image Association\nDirection: Match each picture with the correct word by drawing a\nline connecting them.',1,1,'answer'),
