(536,80,NULL,'learn',1,'Meet the sight words','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s First 100 list:\nsaid   were   one   come   does   two   they   their   what   where\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,'[]','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s First 100 list:\nsaid   were   one   come   does   two   they   their   what   where\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,0,130,'122\n122\nLesson 21: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s\nFirst 100 Lists)\nList of words:\nsaid, were, one, come, does, two, they, their, what, where\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Fishing Sight Words\nDirection: Pick a fish from the basin and read the word on it aloud.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a big basin with fish cutouts that have words on\nthem (e.g., said, were, one, come, does, two, they, their, what,\nwhere, when, why).\n2. The learners gather around the basin.\n3. Each learners takes a turn to pick one fish.\n4. The learner reads the word written on the fish aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.',1,1,'none'),
(537,80,NULL,'learn',2,'Activity 1: Fishing Sight Words','group','Play this with your teacher and classmates. Choose Done when your turn is finished.','Pick a fish from the basin and read the word on it aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a big basin with fish cutouts that have words on them (e.g., said, were, one, come, does, two, they, their, what, where, when, why).\n2. The learners gather around the basin.\n3. Each learner takes a turn to pick one fish.\n4. The learner reads the word written on the fish aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.','assets/images/level3/l21-fish.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l21-fish.webp\"]','Pick a fish from the basin and read the word on it aloud.',NULL,10,130,'122\n122\nLesson 21: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s\nFirst 100 Lists)\nList of words:\nsaid, were, one, come, does, two, they, their, what, where\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Fishing Sight Words\nDirection: Pick a fish from the basin and read the word on it aloud.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a big basin with fish cutouts that have words on\nthem (e.g., said, were, one, come, does, two, they, their, what,\nwhere, when, why).\n2. The learners gather around the basin.\n3. Each learners takes a turn to pick one fish.\n4. The learner reads the word written on the fish aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.',1,1,'perform'),
(538,80,NULL,'learn',3,'Activity 2: Reading Phrases','reading','Read each phrase aloud.','what they said\nwhere they were\ndoes it come\none or two\nwhy they went',NULL,'[]','Read each phrase aloud.','what they said\nwhere they were\ndoes it come\none or two\nwhy they went',10,131,'123\n123\nActivity 2: Reading Phrases\n1. what they said\n2. where they were\n3. does it come\n4. one or two\n5. why they went\nActivity 3: Reading Simple Sentences\n1. They said it was fun.\n2. Where were you yesterday?\n3. Does she come every day?\n4. I saw one dog and two cats.\n5. Why is their bag on the floor?\nAssessment (Individual Reading) (To be done until the end of\nthe allotted time. Can also be given to learners for home\nreading).\nDirection: Read the following words correctly.',1,1,'answer'),
