(541,81,NULL,'learn',1,'Meet the sight words','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 2nd 100 list:\nagain   because   around   every   know   only   people   right   their   would\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,'[]','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 2nd 100 list:\nagain   because   around   every   know   only   people   right   their   would\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,0,132,'124\n124\nLesson 22: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s 2nd\n100 Lists)\nList of words:\nagain, because, around, every, know, only, people, right, their, would\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Snake and Ladder Sight Words\nDirection: Roll the dice, move to the number, and read the word on that\nspace aloud.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a snake and ladder board with words and a dice.\n2. The learners line up in front of the board and each learners takes a turn to\nroll the dice.\n3. The learner moves to the correct number on the board.\n4. The learner reads the word on that space aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.',1,1,'none'),
(542,81,NULL,'learn',2,'Activity 1: Snake and Ladder Sight Words','group','Play this with your teacher and classmates. Choose Done when your turn is finished.','Roll the dice, move to the number, and read the word on that space aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a snake and ladder board with words and a dice.\n2. The learners line up and take turns rolling the dice.\n3. The learner moves to the correct number on the board.\n4. The learner reads the word on that space aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.','assets/images/level3/l22-snake-ladder.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l22-snake-ladder.webp\"]','Roll the dice, move to the number, and read the word on that space aloud.',NULL,10,132,'124\n124\nLesson 22: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s 2nd\n100 Lists)\nList of words:\nagain, because, around, every, know, only, people, right, their, would\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Snake and Ladder Sight Words\nDirection: Roll the dice, move to the number, and read the word on that\nspace aloud.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a snake and ladder board with words and a dice.\n2. The learners line up in front of the board and each learners takes a turn to\nroll the dice.\n3. The learner moves to the correct number on the board.\n4. The learner reads the word on that space aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.',1,1,'perform'),
(543,81,NULL,'learn',3,'Activity 2: Reading Phrases','reading','Read each phrase aloud.','again and again\nbecause they know\naround the corner\nonly the right answer\nevery people’s story',NULL,'[]','Read each phrase aloud.','again and again\nbecause they know\naround the corner\nonly the right answer\nevery people’s story',10,133,'125\n125\nActivity 2: Reading Phrases\n1. again and again\n2. because they know\n3. around the corner\n4. only the right answer\n5. every people’s story\nActivity 3: Reading Simple Sentences\n1. I would go again tomorrow.\n2. They walked around the park.\n3. She knows every word.\n4. People only want the truth.\n5. Their answer was right.\nAssessment (Individual Reading) (To be done until the end of\nthe allotted time. Can also be given to learners for home\nreading).\nDirection: Read the following words correctly.',1,1,'answer'),
