(546,82,NULL,'learn',1,'Meet the sight words','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 3rd 100 list:\nabove   enough   through   though   young   laugh   once   both   always   together\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,'[]','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 3rd 100 list:\nabove   enough   through   though   young   laugh   once   both   always   together\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,0,134,'126\n126\nLesson 23: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s 3rd\n100 Lists)\nList of words:\nabove, enough, through, though, young, laugh, once, both, always, together\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Spin the Wheel of Sight Words\nDirection: Spin the wheel and read the word it points to aloud.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a Spin Wheel with sight words.\n2. The learners line up in front of the wheel and each learners takes a turn to\nspin the wheel.\n3. The learner reads the word the arrow points to aloud.\n4. The class listens and claps after each turn.',1,1,'none'),
(547,82,NULL,'learn',2,'Activity 1: Spin the Wheel of Sight Words','group','Play this with your teacher and classmates. Choose Done when your turn is finished.','Spin the wheel and read the word it points to aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a Spin Wheel with sight words.\n2. The learners line up and take turns spinning the wheel.\n3. The learner reads the word the arrow points to aloud.\n4. The class listens and claps after each turn.','assets/images/level3/l23-wheel.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l23-wheel.webp\"]','Spin the wheel and read the word it points to aloud.',NULL,10,134,'126\n126\nLesson 23: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s 3rd\n100 Lists)\nList of words:\nabove, enough, through, though, young, laugh, once, both, always, together\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Spin the Wheel of Sight Words\nDirection: Spin the wheel and read the word it points to aloud.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a Spin Wheel with sight words.\n2. The learners line up in front of the wheel and each learners takes a turn to\nspin the wheel.\n3. The learner reads the word the arrow points to aloud.\n4. The class listens and claps after each turn.',1,1,'perform'),
(548,82,NULL,'learn',3,'Activity 2: Reading Phrases','reading','Read each phrase aloud.','above the clouds\nenough for everyone\nthrough the door\nyoung and strong\nalways together',NULL,'[]','Read each phrase aloud.','above the clouds\nenough for everyone\nthrough the door\nyoung and strong\nalways together',10,135,'127\n127\nActivity 2: Reading Phrases\n1. above the clouds\n2. enough for everyone\n3. through the door\n4. young and strong\n5. always together\nActivity 3: Reading Simple Sentences\n1. She climbed above the hill.\n2. I have enough food for lunch.\n3. We walked through the park.\n4. The young boy can laugh loudly.\n5. They always work together.\nAssessment (Individual Reading) (To be done until the end of\nthe allotted time. Can also be given to learners for home\nreading).\nDirection: Read the following words correctly.',1,1,'answer'),
