(551,83,NULL,'learn',1,'Meet the sight words','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 4th 100 list:\nbeautiful   country   different   important   against   enough   write   without   second   water\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,'[]','These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 4th 100 list:\nbeautiful   country   different   important   against   enough   write   without   second   water\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.',NULL,0,136,'128\n128\nLesson 24: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s 4th\n100 Lists)\nList of words:\nbeautiful, country, different, important, against, enough, write, without,\nsecond, water\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Mystery Box of Sight Words\nDirection: Learners line up to take turns drawing a word card from the decorated\nMystery Box and read it aloud as part of the sight word practice.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a decorated Mystery Box.\n2. Print the selected sight words, and places them inside the box.\n3. Learners form a line, take turns drawing one word card from the\nMystery Box, and read the word aloud for practice.',1,1,'none'),
(552,83,NULL,'learn',2,'Activity 1: Mystery Box of Sight Words','group','Play this with your teacher and classmates. Choose Done when your turn is finished.','Take turns drawing a word card from the decorated Mystery Box and read it aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a decorated Mystery Box.\n2. The teacher prints the selected sight words and places them inside the box.\n3. Learners form a line, take turns drawing one word card from the Mystery Box, and read the word aloud.','assets/images/level3/l24-mystery-box.webp','[\"assets/images/level3/l24-mystery-box.webp\"]','Take turns drawing a word card from the decorated Mystery Box and read it aloud.',NULL,10,136,'128\n128\nLesson 24: Basic Sight Words (10 Difficult Words to Read from Fry’s 4th\n100 Lists)\nList of words:\nbeautiful, country, different, important, against, enough, write, without,\nsecond, water\nPreliminaries: Review the words previously learned.\nActivity 1: Mystery Box of Sight Words\nDirection: Learners line up to take turns drawing a word card from the decorated\nMystery Box and read it aloud as part of the sight word practice.\nProcedure:\n1. The teacher prepares a decorated Mystery Box.\n2. Print the selected sight words, and places them inside the box.\n3. Learners form a line, take turns drawing one word card from the\nMystery Box, and read the word aloud for practice.',1,1,'perform'),
(553,83,NULL,'learn',3,'Activity 2: Reading Phrases','reading','Read each phrase aloud.','beautiful country\ndifferent people\nimportant work\nagainst the wall\nsecond water bottle',NULL,'[]','Read each phrase aloud.','beautiful country\ndifferent people\nimportant work\nagainst the wall\nsecond water bottle',10,137,'129\n129\nActivity 2: Reading Phrases\n1. beautiful country\n2. different people\n3. important work\n4. against the wall\n5. second water bottle\nActivity 3: Reading Simple Sentences\n1. The beautiful flower is in the garden.\n2. Our country is big and strong.\n3. She has a different idea.\n4. It is important to read every day.\n5. He drank enough water after the game.\nAssessment (Individual Reading) (To be done until the end of\nthe allotted time. Can also be given to learners for home\nreading).\nDirection: Read the following words correctly.',1,1,'answer'),
