(620,132,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: I Wanna Do Right','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy and speed.','Title: I Wanna Do Right\nWords: 100\n\nI wanna do right, wanna do what\'s right\nI\'m gonna give You all of my life\nI put my trust in You, Jesus\nAnd You\'ll show me, show me how to do right\nHey, hey, every word I say\nOoh, ooh, I wanna be like You\nOh, my, my, every day goes by\nI wanna be more like You\nI wanna be more like You\nBridge:\nI was made to give You praise\nMake me more like You\nI was made to give You praise\nMake me more like You\nIn all I do\n(Repeat Chorus)','assets/images/level4/g4-p21-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level4/g4-p21-1.webp\"]','I Wanna Do Right. I wanna do right, wanna do what\'s right I\'m gonna give You all of my life I put my trust in You, Jesus And You\'ll show me, show me how to do right Hey, hey, every word I say Ooh, ooh, I wanna be like You Oh, my, my, every day goes by I wanna be more like You I wanna be more like You Bridge: I was made to give You praise Make me more like You I was made to give You praise Make me more like You In all I do (Repeat Chorus)','I wanna do right, wanna do what\'s right I\'m gonna give You all of my life I put my trust in You, Jesus And You\'ll show me, show me how to do right Hey, hey, every word I say Ooh, ooh, I wanna be like You Oh, my, my, every day goes by I wanna be more like You I wanna be more like You Bridge: I was made to give You praise Make me more like You I was made to give You praise Make me more like You In all I do (Repeat Chorus)',20,21,'17 \n \n \n \nI Wanna Do Right \nhttps://youtu.be/RlxxuTV-5vk \n \n \n \nI wanna do right, wanna do what\'s right \nI\'m gonna give You all of my life \nI put my trust in You, Jesus \nAnd You\'ll show me, show me how to do right \nHey, hey, every word I say \nOoh, ooh, I wanna be like You \nOh, my, my, every day goes by \nI wanna be more like You \nI wanna be more like You \n \nBridge: \nI was made to give You praise \nMake me more like You \nI was made to give You praise \nMake me more like You \nIn all I do \n(Repeat Chorus) \nhttps://musicservices.com/license/song/detail/50075 \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n100 \nOral Reading Score = 100 _______ / 100 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(621,133,63,'post',1,'Let’s get ready','reference','Read or listen, then choose Next.','Your teacher will listen as you read a story aloud. Read at your own pace, the way you talk. If you do not know a word, try your best and keep going. Tap Start reading when you begin and I’m done when you finish.','assets/images/level4/g4-p23-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level4/g4-p23-1.webp\"]','Your teacher will listen as you read a story aloud. Read at your own pace, the way you talk. If you do not know a word, try your best and keep going. Tap Start reading when you begin and I’m done when you finish.',NULL,5,23,'19 \n \nPost test Passage \n \nMy First Baseball Game \nRandy Ryan \nI remember my first Cubs game. My uncle came to take my \nsister and me to it. It was a sunny Saturday. He drove all the way \nfrom Indiana to get us. Then we took the train to the ballpark. He \nsaid it would be hard to find a parking space there, so he didn’t \ndrive there.   He was right.  When we got there it was so crowded. \nWe had tickets that were for seats \nfar back. It seemed like I climbed \nabout 300 steps to get to them. \nBut when we got there and I \nturned around I could see every- \nthing. I saw the whole field. It \nwas much better than watching it \non TV. Then the game started. \nEveryone cheered. The man next \nto me said, “This is going to be the \nyear. \nThey \nare \nplaying \nreally \nwell.”  My uncle said to him, \n“Let’s hope this is the one.” But \nthen he whispered to us, “Jerome \nand Felicia, we’ll have to wait and \nsee. Remember last year? They \nstarted out well and then they lost \nat  the  end.”    “Hey,  Hey,  Hey!” \nThe Cub batter hit a ball far to the https://media.istockphoto.com/id/140233789/photo/young-slugger.jpg? \nwall. \ns=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=KuTiL8vpQSQpk7oHKHSDabjH4xWrDwimKSuu \nNBggSfQ= \nJust then I heard “Hot dogs!” “Peanuts!” I looked and saw a \nman with a big tray hanging from his shoulders. It was full of \nhotdogs in plastic wrap and bags of peanuts. “Three hot dogs,” my \nuncle shouted. Then he gave the man next to us $6. He passed it \nto the man with the hot dogs.  (251 Words) \nTypes of Mi',0,1,'none'),
(622,133,63,'post',2,'Read aloud: My First Baseball Game','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy and speed.','Title: My First Baseball Game\nAuthor: Randy Ryan\nWords: 255\n\nI remember my first Cubs game. My uncle came to take my sister and me to it. It was a sunny Saturday. He drove all the way from Indiana to get us. Then we took the train to the ballpark. He said it would be hard to find a parking space there, so he didn’t drive there. He was right. When we got there it was so crowded. We had tickets that were for seats far back. It seemed like I climbed about 300 steps to get to them. But when we got there and I turned around I could see everything. I saw the whole field. It was much better than watching it on TV. Then the game started. Everyone cheered. The man next to me said, “This is going to be the year. They are playing really well.” My uncle said to him, “Let’s hope this is the one.” But then he whispered to us, “Jerome and Felicia, we’ll have to wait and see. Remember last year? They started out well and then they lost at the end.” “Hey, Hey, Hey!” The Cub batter hit a ball far to the wall.\n\nJust then I heard “Hot dogs!” “Peanuts!” I looked and saw a man with a big tray hanging from his shoulders. It was full of hotdogs in plastic wrap and bags of peanuts. “Three hot dogs,” my uncle shouted. Then he gave the man next to us $6. He passed it to the man with the hot dogs.','assets/images/level4/g4-p23-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level4/g4-p23-1.webp\"]','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy and speed.','I remember my first Cubs game. My uncle came to take my sister and me to it. It was a sunny Saturday. He drove all the way from Indiana to get us. Then we took the train to the ballpark. He said it would be hard to find a parking space there, so he didn’t drive there. He was right. When we got