(717,172,NULL,'learn',5,'The Community Helpers · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','2. According to the passage, how do the people feel\nabout their community helpers?\na. They are afraid of them.\nb. They love them.\nc. They do not know them.\nd. They are angry with them.\n3. Which helper is most likely to help you if you are sick?\na. A policeman and a security guard\nb. A doctor and a nurse\nc. A fireman and a driver\nd. A carpenter and a laborer\n4. Which of the following helpers is NOT mentioned in the\npassage?\na. Fisherman\nb. Pilot\nc. Teacher\nd. Storekeeper\n5. Based on the passage, a community helper is\nsomeone who...\na. works only for money.\nb. lives in a big house.\nc. does a job that helps people in the area.\nd. travels to different countries.',NULL,'[]','2. According to the passage, how do the people feel about their community helpers? a. They are afraid of them. b. They love them. c. They do not know them. d. They are angry with them. 3. Which helper is most likely to help you if you are sick? a. A policeman and a security guard b. A doctor and a nurse c. A fireman and a driver d. A carpenter and a laborer 4. Which of the following helpers is NOT mentioned in the passage? a. Fisherman b. Pilot c. Teacher d. Storekeeper 5. Based on the passage, a community helper is someone who... a. works only for money. b. lives in a big house. c. does a job that helps people in the area. d. travels to different countries.',NULL,10,77,'2. According to the passage, how do the people feel\nabout their community helpers?\na. They are afraid of them.\nb. They love them.\nc. They do not know them.\nd. They are angry with them.\n3. Which helper is most likely to help you if you are sick?\na. A policeman and a security guard\nb. A doctor and a nurse\nc. A fireman and a driver\nd. A carpenter and a laborer\n4. Which of the following helpers is NOT mentioned in the\npassage?\na. Fisherman\nb. Pilot\nc. Teacher\nd. Storekeeper\n5. Based on the passage, a community helper is\nsomeone who...\na. works only for money.\nb. lives in a big house.\nc. does a job that helps people in the area.\nd. travels to different countries.',1,1,'answer'),
(718,173,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: In the Plaza','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','In The Plaza\nThis is our plaza.\nWe play in our plaza.\nOur plaza is very clean and beautiful.\nseesaw monkey bar','assets/images/level5/g1/p078-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p078-1.webp\"]','In The Plaza This is our plaza. We play in our plaza. Our plaza is very clean and beautiful. seesaw monkey bar',NULL,5,78,'In The Plaza\nThis is our plaza.\nWe play in our plaza.\nOur plaza is very clean and beautiful.\nseesaw monkey bar',1,1,'none'),
(719,173,NULL,'learn',2,'In the Plaza · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect descriptions or functions in Column B. Write\nthe letter of your answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______ Plaza\na. A place of playground\nequipment you down\nsitting or lying\n2. ______\nStatue\nb. A public open space\nin a city or town, often for\npeople to walk and play\n3. ______ Swing\nc. A structure of bars you\ncan swing across using\nyour hands','assets/images/level5/g1/p079-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p079-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p079-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p079-3.webp\"]','A. Vocabulary: Instructions: Match the words in Column A with their correct descriptions or functions in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on the line provided. Column A Column B 1. blank Plaza a. A place of playground equipment you down sitting or lying 2. blank Statue b. A public open space in a city or town, often for people to walk and play 3. blank Swing c. A structure of bars you can swing across using your hands',NULL,10,79,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect descriptions or functions in Column B. Write\nthe letter of your answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______ Plaza\na. A place of playground\nequipment you down\nsitting or lying\n2. ______\nStatue\nb. A public open space\nin a city or town, often for\npeople to walk and play\n3. ______ Swing\nc. A structure of bars you\ncan swing across using\nyour hands',1,1,'answer'),
(720,173,NULL,'learn',3,'In the Plaza · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','4. ______\nSlide\nd. A seat hanging from\nropes or chains that\nmoves back and forth\n5. ______\nMonkey bar\ne. A model of a person or\nanimal, made of stone\nor metal\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A plaza\nc. A garden\nd. A park','assets/images/level5/g1/p080-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p080-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p080-2.webp\"]','4. blank Slide d. A seat hanging from ropes or chains that moves back and forth 5. blank Monkey bar e. A model of a person or animal, made of stone or metal B. Listening Comprehension: Instructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a short passage. Then, answer the questions below. 1. What is the main place described in the passage? a. A school b. A plaza c. A garden d. A park',NULL,10,80,'4. ______\nSlide\nd. A seat hanging from\nropes or chains that\nmoves back and forth\n5. ______\nMonkey bar\ne. A model of a person or\nanimal, made of stone\nor metal\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A plaza\nc. A garden\nd. A park',1,1,'answer'),
(721,173,NULL,'learn',4,'In the Plaza · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','2. What do the children do in the plaza?\na. They study.\nb. They play.\nc. They work.\nd. They sleep.\n3. How is the plaza described?\na. Very big and busy\nb. Clean and beautiful\nc. Old and quiet\nd. Dark and scary\n4. Which of the following items is mentioned as being in\nthe plaza?\na. A swimming pool\nb. A basketball court\nc. A statue\nd. A fountain\n5. The word \"our\" in the passage suggests that the\nplaza...\na. is very far away.\nb. belongs to or is used by the speaker and their\ncommunity.\nc. is new.\nd. is only for children.',NULL,'[]','2. What do the children do in the plaza? a. They study. b. They play. c. They work. d. They sleep. 3. How is the plaza described? a. Very big and busy b. Clean and beautiful c. Old and quiet d. Dark and scary 4. Which of the following items is mentioned as being in the plaza? a. A swimming pool b. A basketball court c. A statue d. A fountain 5. The word \"our\" in the passage suggests that the plaza... a. is very far away. b. belongs to or is used by the speaker and their community. c. is new. d. is only for children.',NULL,10,81,'2. What do the children do in the plaza?\na. They study.\nb. They play.\nc. They work.\nd. They sleep.\n3. How is the plaza described?\na. Very big and busy\nb. Clean and beautiful\nc. Old and quiet\nd. Dark and scary\n4. Which of the following items is mentioned as being in\nthe plaza?\na. A swimming pool\nb. A basketball court\nc. A statue\nd. A fountain\n5. The word \"our\" in the passage suggests that the\nplaza...\na. is very far away.\nb. belongs to or is used by the speaker and their\ncommunity.\nc. is new.\nd. is only for children.',1,1,'answer'),
(722,174,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: In the Market','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','In The Market\nThis is OUr market.\nWe can buy our food in the market.\nbutchers weighing scale\nknife\nchopping board\nbutcher','assets/images/level5/g1/p082-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p082-1.webp\"]','In The Market This is OUr market. We can buy our food in the market. butchers weighing scale knife chopping board butcher',NULL,5,82,'In The Market\nThis is OUr market.\nWe can buy our food in the market.\nbutchers weighing scale\nknife\nchopping board\nbutcher',1,1,'none');
