(723,174,NULL,'learn',2,'In the Market · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','A. Vocabulary\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect meanings or uses in Column B. Write the letter of\nyour answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nButcher\na. A tool used to measure how\nheavy something is\n2. ______\nWeighing Scale\nb. A person whose job is to cut\nand sell meat\n3. ______\nChopping board\nc. Vegetables that grow\nunderground, like potatoes\nor carrots.\n4. ______\nGrains\nd. A hard board used for\ncutting good on.\n5. ______\nRoot crops\ne. Small hard seeds from plants\nlike rice or wheat, used for food.',NULL,'[]','A. Vocabulary Instructions: Match the words in Column A with their correct meanings or uses in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on the line provided. Column A Column B 1. blank Butcher a. A tool used to measure how heavy something is 2. blank Weighing Scale b. A person whose job is to cut and sell meat 3. blank Chopping board c. Vegetables that grow underground, like potatoes or carrots. 4. blank Grains d. A hard board used for cutting good on. 5. blank Root crops e. Small hard seeds from plants like rice or wheat, used for food.',NULL,10,83,'A. Vocabulary\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect meanings or uses in Column B. Write the letter of\nyour answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nButcher\na. A tool used to measure how\nheavy something is\n2. ______\nWeighing Scale\nb. A person whose job is to cut\nand sell meat\n3. ______\nChopping board\nc. Vegetables that grow\nunderground, like potatoes\nor carrots.\n4. ______\nGrains\nd. A hard board used for\ncutting good on.\n5. ______\nRoot crops\ne. Small hard seeds from plants\nlike rice or wheat, used for food.',1,1,'answer'),
(724,174,NULL,'learn',3,'In the Market · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','A. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a short\npassage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A market\nc. A farm\nd. A restaurant\n2. What is the main purpose of going to this place?\na. To play and have fun\nb. To study and learn\nc. To buy food\nd. To cook meals\n3. Which of the following is an example of a food you\ncan buy there?\na. A toy car\nb. A storybook\nc. A chair\nd. Fruits',NULL,'[]','A. Listening Comprehension: Instructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a short passage. Then, answer the questions below. 1. What is the main place described in the passage? a. A school b. A market c. A farm d. A restaurant 2. What is the main purpose of going to this place? a. To play and have fun b. To study and learn c. To buy food d. To cook meals 3. Which of the following is an example of a food you can buy there? a. A toy car b. A storybook c. A chair d. Fruits',NULL,10,84,'A. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a short\npassage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A market\nc. A farm\nd. A restaurant\n2. What is the main purpose of going to this place?\na. To play and have fun\nb. To study and learn\nc. To buy food\nd. To cook meals\n3. Which of the following is an example of a food you\ncan buy there?\na. A toy car\nb. A storybook\nc. A chair\nd. Fruits',1,1,'answer'),
(725,174,NULL,'learn',4,'In the Market · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','4. Who is the person you would find working with meat\nin this place?\na. The fisherman\nb. The butcher\nc. The farmer\nd. The driver\n5. Which tool would a seller use to tell you the weight\nof your fruits?\na. A chopping board\nb. A butcher\'s knife\nc. A weighing scale\nd. A shopping cart',NULL,'[]','4. Who is the person you would find working with meat in this place? a. The fisherman b. The butcher c. The farmer d. The driver 5. Which tool would a seller use to tell you the weight of your fruits? a. A chopping board b. A butcher\'s knife c. A weighing scale d. A shopping cart',NULL,10,85,'4. Who is the person you would find working with meat\nin this place?\na. The fisherman\nb. The butcher\nc. The farmer\nd. The driver\n5. Which tool would a seller use to tell you the weight\nof your fruits?\na. A chopping board\nb. A butcher\'s knife\nc. A weighing scale\nd. A shopping cart',1,1,'answer'),
(726,175,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: In the Farm','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','In The Farm\nThis is our farm.\nWe grow plants on our farm.\nWe have animals on our farm to\ncoconut banana cassava guava\nbottle guard cashew','assets/images/level5/g1/p086-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p086-1.webp\"]','In The Farm This is our farm. We grow plants on our farm. We have animals on our farm to coconut banana cassava guava bottle guard cashew',NULL,5,86,'In The Farm\nThis is our farm.\nWe grow plants on our farm.\nWe have animals on our farm to\ncoconut banana cassava guava\nbottle guard cashew',1,1,'none'),
(727,175,NULL,'learn',2,'In the Farm · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle the\nletter of the best answer.\n1. What is a farm?\na. A place where people go to work in offices.\nb. A place where animals are kept for display.\nc. An area of land used for growing crops and\nraising animals.\nd. A large building where machines make cars.\n2. Which word describes a large animal often used for\npulling plows in some countries?\na. Goat\nb. Carabao\nc. Chicken\nd. Bird\n3. What does it mean to grow plants?\na. To cook and eat them.\nb. To draw pictures of them.\nc. To cultivate and help them develop from seeds.\nd. To collect them from the forest.\n4. Which of the following is most likely a plant with a\nlarge, hard-shelled nut that grows on trees?\na. Cassava\nb. Pineapple\nc. Coconut\nd. Banana',NULL,'[]','A. Vocabulary: Instructions: Read each question carefully. Circle the letter of the best answer. 1. What is a farm? a. A place where people go to work in offices. b. A place where animals are kept for display. c. An area of land used for growing crops and raising animals. d. A large building where machines make cars. 2. Which word describes a large animal often used for pulling plows in some countries? a. Goat b. Carabao c. Chicken d. Bird 3. What does it mean to grow plants? a. To cook and eat them. b. To draw pictures of them. c. To cultivate and help them develop from seeds. d. To collect them from the forest. 4. Which of the following is most likely a plant with a large, hard-shelled nut that grows on trees? a. Cassava b. Pineapple c. Coconut d. Banana',NULL,10,87,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle the\nletter of the best answer.\n1. What is a farm?\na. A place where people go to work in offices.\nb. A place where animals are kept for display.\nc. An area of land used for growing crops and\nraising animals.\nd. A large building where machines make cars.\n2. Which word describes a large animal often used for\npulling plows in some countries?\na. Goat\nb. Carabao\nc. Chicken\nd. Bird\n3. What does it mean to grow plants?\na. To cook and eat them.\nb. To draw pictures of them.\nc. To cultivate and help them develop from seeds.\nd. To collect them from the forest.\n4. Which of the following is most likely a plant with a\nlarge, hard-shelled nut that grows on trees?\na. Cassava\nb. Pineapple\nc. Coconut\nd. Banana',1,1,'answer'),
(728,175,NULL,'learn',3,'In the Farm · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','5. If you see a bottle gourd on a farm, what are you\nlooking at?\na. A type of animal\nb. A tool for feeding animals\nc. A building for storing tools\nd. A type of vegetable that grows on a vine\nB Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main topic of the passage?\na. A family home\nb. A school playground\nc. A farm and what is on it\nd. A zoo with many animals\n2. What are the two main types of things found on this\nfarm?\na. Buildings and roads\nb. Toys and games\nc. Plants and animals\nd. Rivers and mountains',NULL,'[]','5. If you see a bottle gourd on a farm, what are you looking at? a. A type of animal b. A tool for feeding animals c. A building for storing tools d. A type of vegetable that grows on a vine B Listening Comprehension: Instructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the passage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for each question below. 1. What is the main topic of the passage? a. A family home b. A school playground c. A farm and what is on it d. A zoo with many animals 2. What are the two main types of things found on this farm? a. Buildings and roads b. Toys and games c. Plants and animals d. Rivers and mountains',NULL,10,88,'5. If you see a bottle gourd on a farm, what are you\nlooking at?\na. A type of animal\nb. A tool for feeding animals\nc. A building for storing tools\nd. A type of vegetable that grows on a vine\nB Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main topic of the passage?\na. A family home\nb. A school playground\nc. A farm and what is on it\nd. A zoo with many animals\n2. What are the two main types of things found on this\nfarm?\na. Buildings and roads\nb. Toys and games\nc. Plants and animals\nd. Rivers and mountains',1,1,'answer'),
(729,175,NULL,'learn',4,'In the Farm · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','3. Which of these animals is NOT mentioned as living on\nthe farm?\na. Goat\nb. Sheep\nc. Pig\nd. Chicken\n4. Based on the passage, which activity do the people\nmost likely do on this farm?\na. They go swimming.\nb. They grow fruits and raise animals.\nc. They build cars and machines.\nd. They buy and sell clothes.\n5. The passage says, \"This is our farm.\" What does this\nmost likely mean?\na. The farm belongs to someone else.\nb. The farm is a public park for everyone.\nc. The speaker and their family or community own or\nwork on the farm.\nd. The farm is very old',NULL,'[]','3. Which of these animals is NOT mentioned as living on the farm? a. Goat b. Sheep c. Pig d. Chicken 4. Based on the passage, which activity do the people most likely do on this farm? a. They go swimming. b. They grow fruits and raise animals. c. They build cars and machines. d. They buy and sell clothes. 5. The passage says, \"This is our farm.\" What does this most likely mean? a. The farm belongs to someone else. b. The farm is a public park for everyone. c. The speaker and their family or community own or work on the farm. d. The farm is very old',NULL,10,89,'3. Which of these animals is NOT mentioned as living on\nthe farm?\na. Goat\nb. Sheep\nc. Pig\nd. Chicken\n4. Based on the passage, which activity do the people\nmost likely do on this farm?\na. They go swimming.\nb. They grow fruits and raise animals.\nc. They build cars and machines.\nd. They buy and sell clothes.\n5. The passage says, \"This is our farm.\" What does this\nmost likely mean?\na. The farm belongs to someone else.\nb. The farm is a public park for everyone.\nc. The speaker and their family or community own or\nwork on the farm.\nd. The farm is very old',1,1,'answer'),
(730,176,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Buildings Around Me','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Buildings Around Me\nThere are many building in our place.\nEach building is very useful for us.\nWe keep our building safe and clean.\nchurch\n<a@iane SHOP>| [Ml [i\nfire station','assets/images/level5/g1/p090-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p090-1.webp\"]','Buildings Around Me There are many building in our place. Each building is very useful for us. We keep our building safe and clean. church <a@iane SHOP>| [Ml [i fire station',NULL,5,90,'Buildings Around Me\nThere are many building in our place.\nEach building is very useful for us.\nWe keep our building safe and clean.\nchurch\n<a@iane SHOP>| [Ml [i\nfire station',1,1,'none'),
(731,176,NULL,'learn',2,'Buildings Around Me · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle\nthe letter of the best answer.\n1. What is a building?\na. A natural formation like a mountain or a river.\nb. A vehicle used for transportation.\nc. A structure with a roof and walls, such as a\nhouse or school.\nd. A type of animal that lives in a forest.\n2. If you need to buy medicine,\nwhich building should you go to?\na. A bakery\nb. A pharmacy\nc. a bank\nd. a restaurant\n3. What does useful mean?\na. Old and beautiful\nb. Able to be used for a purpose; helpful.\nc. Very large and expensive\nd. New and modern\n4. The barangay hall is most likely a building that\nserves as what?\na. A place for local government and community\nmeetings.\nb. A place to watch movies.\nc. A place to buy fresh fish and vegetables.\nd. A place to repair cars.',NULL,'[]','A. Vocabulary: Instructions: Read each question carefully. Circle the letter of the best answer. 1. What is a building? a. A natural formation like a mountain or a river. b. A vehicle used for transportation. c. A structure with a roof and walls, such as a house or school. d. A type of animal that lives in a forest. 2. If you need to buy medicine, which building should you go to? a. A bakery b. A pharmacy c. a bank d. a restaurant 3. What does useful mean? a. Old and beautiful b. Able to be used for a purpose; helpful. c. Very large and expensive d. New and modern 4. The barangay hall is most likely a building that serves as what? a. A place for local government and community meetings. b. A place to watch movies. c. A place to buy fresh fish and vegetables. d. A place to repair cars.',NULL,10,91,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle\nthe letter of the best answer.\n1. What is a building?\na. A natural formation like a mountain or a river.\nb. A vehicle used for transportation.\nc. A structure with a roof and walls, such as a\nhouse or school.\nd. A type of animal that lives in a forest.\n2. If you need to buy medicine,\nwhich building should you go to?\na. A bakery\nb. A pharmacy\nc. a bank\nd. a restaurant\n3. What does useful mean?\na. Old and beautiful\nb. Able to be used for a purpose; helpful.\nc. Very large and expensive\nd. New and modern\n4. The barangay hall is most likely a building that\nserves as what?\na. A place for local government and community\nmeetings.\nb. A place to watch movies.\nc. A place to buy fresh fish and vegetables.\nd. A place to repair cars.',1,1,'answer'),
(732,176,NULL,'learn',3,'Buildings Around Me · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','5. What does it mean to keep our buildings safe\nand clean?\na. To forget about them.\nb. To destroy them and build new ones.\nc. To maintain or preserve them in that condition.\nd. To paint them all the same color.\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main idea of the passage?\na. There are many useful buildings in the community.\nb. Houses are the most important buildings.\nc. Buildings are very expensive to build.\nd. All buildings look the same.\n2. How do the people feel about the buildings in their\nplace?\na. They find them useless.\nb. They think they are ugly.\nc. They find them very useful.\nd. They are afraid of them.',NULL,'[]','5. What does it mean to keep our buildings safe and clean? a. To forget about them. b. To destroy them and build new ones. c. To maintain or preserve them in that condition. d. To paint them all the same color. B. Listening Comprehension: Instructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the passage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for each question below. 1. What is the main idea of the passage? a. There are many useful buildings in the community. b. Houses are the most important buildings. c. Buildings are very expensive to build. d. All buildings look the same. 2. How do the people feel about the buildings in their place? a. They find them useless. b. They think they are ugly. c. They find them very useful. d. They are afraid of them.',NULL,10,92,'5. What does it mean to keep our buildings safe\nand clean?\na. To forget about them.\nb. To destroy them and build new ones.\nc. To maintain or preserve them in that condition.\nd. To paint them all the same color.\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main idea of the passage?\na. There are many useful buildings in the community.\nb. Houses are the most important buildings.\nc. Buildings are very expensive to build.\nd. All buildings look the same.\n2. How do the people feel about the buildings in their\nplace?\na. They find them useless.\nb. They think they are ugly.\nc. They find them very useful.\nd. They are afraid of them.',1,1,'answer'),
(733,176,NULL,'learn',4,'Buildings Around Me · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','3. If someone needs to put out a fire, which building\nshould they call for help?\na. The hospital\nb. The barangay hall\nc. The fire station\nd. The market\n4. Which of the following is a building where you can\nbuy bread and pastries?\na. The restaurant\nb. The pharmacy\nc. The bakery\nd. The store\n5. What do the people do for their buildings?\na. They keep them safe and clean.\nb. They ignore them.\nc. They paint them every year.\nd. They sell them to other people.',NULL,'[]','3. If someone needs to put out a fire, which building should they call for help? a. The hospital b. The barangay hall c. The fire station d. The market 4. Which of the following is a building where you can buy bread and pastries? a. The restaurant b. The pharmacy c. The bakery d. The store 5. What do the people do for their buildings? a. They keep them safe and clean. b. They ignore them. c. They paint them every year. d. They sell them to other people.',NULL,10,93,'3. If someone needs to put out a fire, which building\nshould they call for help?\na. The hospital\nb. The barangay hall\nc. The fire station\nd. The market\n4. Which of the following is a building where you can\nbuy bread and pastries?\na. The restaurant\nb. The pharmacy\nc. The bakery\nd. The store\n5. What do the people do for their buildings?\na. They keep them safe and clean.\nb. They ignore them.\nc. They paint them every year.\nd. They sell them to other people.',1,1,'answer'),
(734,177,69,'post',1,'Post-assessment · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','POST TEST (Activity 1-10)\nVocabulary Development (1-10)\nA. Instructions: Draw a line to match the word to the\ncorrect picture.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Shovel\na.\n2. Nose\nb.\n3. Chair\nc.\n4. Teddy Bear\nd.\n5. Mother\ne.','assets/images/level5/g1/p095-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p095-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p095-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p095-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p095-3.webp\"]','POST TEST (Activity 1-10) Vocabulary Development (1-10) A. Instructions: Draw a line to match the word to the correct picture. Column A Column B 1. Shovel a. 2. Nose b. 3. Chair c. 4. Teddy Bear d. 5. Mother e.',NULL,10,95,'POST TEST (Activity 1-10)\nVocabulary Development (1-10)\nA. Instructions: Draw a line to match the word to the\ncorrect picture.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Shovel\na.\n2. Nose\nb.\n3. Chair\nc.\n4. Teddy Bear\nd.\n5. Mother\ne.',1,1,'answer'),
(735,177,69,'post',2,'Post-assessment · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','B. Instructions: Draw a line to match the meaning to\nthe correct picture.\n1. An animal that barks\na.\n2. Used for writing\nb.\n3. Comes from chicken\nc.\n4. The father of your mother\nd.\nor father\n5. A dish used for holding\ne.\nliquids often with handle','assets/images/level5/g1/p096-5.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p096-5.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p096-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p096-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p096-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p096-3.webp\"]','B. Instructions: Draw a line to match the meaning to the correct picture. 1. An animal that barks a. 2. Used for writing b. 3. Comes from chicken c. 4. The father of your mother d. or father 5. A dish used for holding e. liquids often with handle',NULL,10,96,'B. Instructions: Draw a line to match the meaning to\nthe correct picture.\n1. An animal that barks\na.\n2. Used for writing\nb.\n3. Comes from chicken\nc.\n4. The father of your mother\nd.\nor father\n5. A dish used for holding\ne.\nliquids often with handle',1,1,'answer'),
(736,177,69,'post',3,'Post-assessment · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','A. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\nsentences/passage. Then, answer the questions below.\nChoose the letter of the correct answer.\n1. (Read Aloud) “My Home” This is my home. We have\ntables and chairs in our home. We have rooms and beds\ninn our home. We have the kitchen and the comfort rooms\ntoo. What is the story about?\na. My Garden\nb. My Home\nc. My Kitchen\n2. (Read Aloud) “My Toys” These are my toys. My mother\nand father gives it to me! I can name my favorite toys. “My\nparents gave me something I can throw and catch. It’s\nround and bouncy. What is it?”\na. Kite\nb. Ball\nc. Doll\nd. Teddy Bear',NULL,'[]','A. Listening Comprehension: Instructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the sentences/passage. Then, answer the questions below. Choose the letter of the correct answer. 1. (Read Aloud) “My Home” This is my home. We have tables and chairs in our home. We have rooms and beds inn our home. We have the kitchen and the comfort rooms too. What is the story about? a. My Garden b. My Home c. My Kitchen 2. (Read Aloud) “My Toys” These are my toys. My mother and father gives it to me! I can name my favorite toys. “My parents gave me something I can throw and catch. It’s round and bouncy. What is it?” a. Kite b. Ball c. Doll d. Teddy Bear',NULL,10,97,'A. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\nsentences/passage. Then, answer the questions below.\nChoose the letter of the correct answer.\n1. (Read Aloud) “My Home” This is my home. We have\ntables and chairs in our home. We have rooms and beds\ninn our home. We have the kitchen and the comfort rooms\ntoo. What is the story about?\na. My Garden\nb. My Home\nc. My Kitchen\n2. (Read Aloud) “My Toys” These are my toys. My mother\nand father gives it to me! I can name my favorite toys. “My\nparents gave me something I can throw and catch. It’s\nround and bouncy. What is it?”\na. Kite\nb. Ball\nc. Doll\nd. Teddy Bear',1,1,'answer'),
(737,177,69,'post',4,'Post-assessment · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','3. (Read Aloud) “Our Tools” This is our tools. We have\nshovel and rake. We have to take care of our tools. Tools\nare very important for us. What is the main idea of the\nstory?\na. Tools are fun\nb. Tools are useful and we should take care of\nthem\nc. Tools are expensive\n4. (Read Aloud) “My Pets” These are my pets. I will take\ncare of my pets. I will give them food. I love my pets.\nWrite T if it is true and F if it is false.\n______ A dog can bark.\n______ A fish can fly in the sky\n5. (Read Aloud) “My Things” These are my things. I will take\ncare of my things. I will keep it clean.\nWhat should you do with your things?\na. Break them\nb. Take care of them\nc. Make it tidy\nWhat does “keep it clean” mean?\na. Make it dirty\nb. Make it new\nc. Make it tidy',NULL,'[]','3. (Read Aloud) “Our Tools” This is our tools. We have shovel and rake. We have to take care of our tools. Tools are very important for us. What is the main idea of the story? a. Tools are fun b. Tools are useful and we should take care of them c. Tools are expensive 4. (Read Aloud) “My Pets” These are my pets. I will take care of my pets. I will give them food. I love my pets. Write T if it is true and F if it is false. blank A dog can bark. blank A fish can fly in the sky 5. (Read Aloud) “My Things” These are my things. I will take care of my things. I will keep it clean. What should you do with your things? a. Break them b. Take care of them c. Make it tidy What does “keep it clean” mean? a. Make it dirty b. Make it new c. Make it tidy',NULL,10,98,'3. (Read Aloud) “Our Tools” This is our tools. We have\nshovel and rake. We have to take care of our tools. Tools\nare very important for us. What is the main idea of the\nstory?\na. Tools are fun\nb. Tools are useful and we should take care of\nthem\nc. Tools are expensive\n4. (Read Aloud) “My Pets” These are my pets. I will take\ncare of my pets. I will give them food. I love my pets.\nWrite T if it is true and F if it is false.\n______ A dog can bark.\n______ A fish can fly in the sky\n5. (Read Aloud) “My Things” These are my things. I will take\ncare of my things. I will keep it clean.\nWhat should you do with your things?\na. Break them\nb. Take care of them\nc. Make it tidy\nWhat does “keep it clean” mean?\na. Make it dirty\nb. Make it new\nc. Make it tidy',1,1,'answer'),
(738,177,69,'post',5,'Post-assessment · page 5','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','6. (Read Aloud) “My Family” This is my family. My mother\nand my father. My brother and my sister. And our baby\nboy. Who is in the family?\na. Friends\nb. Relatives\nc. Mother, Father, Brother, Sister, and Baby\n7. (Read Aloud) “My Food” These are the foods I eat.\nMy father buys them for me. My mother cook these for\nme. Who cooks the food in the story?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Friend\n8. “I love to play with my toy on the water. It has a sail\nand helps me pretend I’m a sailor. What am I playing\nwith?\na. Car\nb. Train\nc. Boat\nd. Yoyo',NULL,'[]','6. (Read Aloud) “My Family” This is my family. My mother and my father. My brother and my sister. And our baby boy. Who is in the family? a. Friends b. Relatives c. Mother, Father, Brother, Sister, and Baby 7. (Read Aloud) “My Food” These are the foods I eat. My father buys them for me. My mother cook these for me. Who cooks the food in the story? a. Father b. Mother c. Friend 8. “I love to play with my toy on the water. It has a sail and helps me pretend I’m a sailor. What am I playing with? a. Car b. Train c. Boat d. Yoyo',NULL,10,99,'6. (Read Aloud) “My Family” This is my family. My mother\nand my father. My brother and my sister. And our baby\nboy. Who is in the family?\na. Friends\nb. Relatives\nc. Mother, Father, Brother, Sister, and Baby\n7. (Read Aloud) “My Food” These are the foods I eat.\nMy father buys them for me. My mother cook these for\nme. Who cooks the food in the story?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Friend\n8. “I love to play with my toy on the water. It has a sail\nand helps me pretend I’m a sailor. What am I playing\nwith?\na. Car\nb. Train\nc. Boat\nd. Yoyo',1,1,'answer'),
(739,177,69,'post',6,'Post-assessment · page 6','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','POST TEST (Activity 1-15)\nA. Vocabulary Development\nInstructions: Draw a line to match the words in Column A\nwith their meanings/uses /color in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Librarian\na. Its color is orange\n2. Swing\nb. A container for waste\n3. Trash can\nc. Takes care of sick or\ninjured people in a\nhospital or clinic','assets/images/level5/g1/p100-3.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g1/p100-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p100-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g1/p100-2.webp\"]','POST TEST (Activity 1-15) A. Vocabulary Development Instructions: Draw a line to match the words in Column A with their meanings/uses /color in Column B. Column A Column B 1. Librarian a. Its color is orange 2. Swing b. A container for waste 3. Trash can c. Takes care of sick or injured people in a hospital or clinic',NULL,10,100,'POST TEST (Activity 1-15)\nA. Vocabulary Development\nInstructions: Draw a line to match the words in Column A\nwith their meanings/uses /color in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Librarian\na. Its color is orange\n2. Swing\nb. A container for waste\n3. Trash can\nc. Takes care of sick or\ninjured people in a\nhospital or clinic',1,1,'answer'),
