(743,178,70,'pre',1,'Pre-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Pretest: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nVOCABULARY PRETEST (15 ITEMS)\nDirections: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the underlined word.\n1. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n2. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To fall to the ground\nc) To hide\n3. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Bad smell\nb) No smell\nc) Good smell\n4. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Harmful things\nb) Things that help us grow\nc) Toys for us to play\n5. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Feeling sleepy\nc) Full of energy\n6. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n7. Fruits can taste sour or sweet. What does sour mean?\na) Not sweet\nb) Too salty\nc) Very cold',NULL,'[]','Pretest: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only ) VOCABULARY PRETEST (15 ITEMS) Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the underlined word. 1. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean? a) Something ugly b) Something nice to see c) Something loud 2. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean? a) To open and show petals b) To fall to the ground c) To hide 3. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean? a) Bad smell b) No smell c) Good smell 4. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean? a) Harmful things b) Things that help us grow c) Toys for us to play 5. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean? a) Feeling weak b) Feeling sleepy c) Full of energy 6. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean? a) Strong and well b) Sick c) Dirty 7. Fruits can taste sour or sweet. What does sour mean? a) Not sweet b) Too salty c) Very cold',NULL,10,5,'Pretest: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nVOCABULARY PRETEST (15 ITEMS)\nDirections: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the underlined word.\n1. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n2. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To fall to the ground\nc) To hide\n3. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Bad smell\nb) No smell\nc) Good smell\n4. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Harmful things\nb) Things that help us grow\nc) Toys for us to play\n5. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Feeling sleepy\nc) Full of energy\n6. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n7. Fruits can taste sour or sweet. What does sour mean?\na) Not sweet\nb) Too salty\nc) Very cold',1,1,'answer'),
(744,178,70,'pre',2,'Pre-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','8. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n9. Herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Ordinary\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Special or amazing\n10. Herbs can cure much illness. What does illness mean?\na) A sickness\nb) A birthday\nc) A school subject\n11. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that are broken\nc) Things that disappear\n12. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?\na) To ignore\nb) To look and listen carefully\nc) To run away\n13. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Helping nicely\nb) Playing in a mean or silly way\nc) Sleeping quietly\n14. The animals swim under the deep blue sea. What does deep mean?\na) Very shallow\nb) Very far down\nc) Very noisy\n15. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) Only in one place\nb) Not in many places\nc) In many places all around',NULL,'[]','8. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean? a) A place to stay safe b) A type of fruit c) A kind of game 9. Herbs are called magical. What does magical mean? a) Ordinary b) Cannot do anything c) Special or amazing 10. Herbs can cure much illness. What does illness mean? a) A sickness b) A birthday c) A school subject 11. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean? a) Things that are made b) Things that are broken c) Things that disappear 12. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean? a) To ignore b) To look and listen carefully c) To run away 13. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean? a) Helping nicely b) Playing in a mean or silly way c) Sleeping quietly 14. The animals swim under the deep blue sea. What does deep mean? a) Very shallow b) Very far down c) Very noisy 15. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean? a) Only in one place b) Not in many places c) In many places all around',NULL,10,6,'8. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n9. Herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Ordinary\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Special or amazing\n10. Herbs can cure much illness. What does illness mean?\na) A sickness\nb) A birthday\nc) A school subject\n11. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that are broken\nc) Things that disappear\n12. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?\na) To ignore\nb) To look and listen carefully\nc) To run away\n13. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Helping nicely\nb) Playing in a mean or silly way\nc) Sleeping quietly\n14. The animals swim under the deep blue sea. What does deep mean?\na) Very shallow\nb) Very far down\nc) Very noisy\n15. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) Only in one place\nb) Not in many places\nc) In many places all around',1,1,'answer'),
(745,178,70,'pre',3,'Pre-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','LISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nonly )\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because\nthey make places look bright and lovely.”\n1. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they are loud\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they taste sweet\n2. What do flowers give?\na) A good smell\nb) A loud noise\nc) A sour taste',NULL,'[]','LISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only ) Directions: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then choose the correct answer. Teacher reads: “Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because they make places look bright and lovely.” 1. Why do people like flowers? a) Because they are loud b) Because they look bright and lovely c) Because they taste sweet 2. What do flowers give? a) A good smell b) A loud noise c) A sour taste',NULL,10,7,'LISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nonly )\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because\nthey make places look bright and lovely.”\n1. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they are loud\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they taste sweet\n2. What do flowers give?\na) A good smell\nb) A loud noise\nc) A sour taste',1,1,'answer'),
(746,178,70,'pre',4,'Pre-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Teacher reads:\n“Vegetables help our body because they have nutrients. They keep us strong, active, and\nhealthy.”\n3. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Toys\nb) Nutrients\nc) Smoke\n4. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us sleepy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us noisy\nTeacher reads:\n“Fruits can taste sweet or sour. They help us stay healthy and give us vitamins.”\n5. How do fruits taste?\na) Sweet or sour\nb) Salty\nc) Bitter\n6. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\nTeacher reads:\n“Trees give us clean air. Birds live in trees because they are safe and high.”\n7. What do trees give us?\na) Dirty air\nb) Clean air\nc) Hot air\n8. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are noisy\nc) Trees are cold\nTeacher reads:\n“Some herbs are used to help sick people feel better. Herbs can cure small illnesses.”\n9. What can herbs do?\na) Make cars move\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make people laugh',NULL,'[]','Teacher reads: “Vegetables help our body because they have nutrients. They keep us strong, active, and healthy.” 3. What do vegetables give our body? a) Toys b) Nutrients c) Smoke 4. How do vegetables help us? a) They make us sleepy b) They make us strong and healthy c) They make us noisy Teacher reads: “Fruits can taste sweet or sour. They help us stay healthy and give us vitamins.” 5. How do fruits taste? a) Sweet or sour b) Salty c) Bitter 6. What do fruits give our body? a) Vitamins b) Sand c) Smoke Teacher reads: “Trees give us clean air. Birds live in trees because they are safe and high.” 7. What do trees give us? a) Dirty air b) Clean air c) Hot air 8. Why do birds live in trees? a) Trees are safe b) Trees are noisy c) Trees are cold Teacher reads: “Some herbs are used to help sick people feel better. Herbs can cure small illnesses.” 9. What can herbs do? a) Make cars move b) Help cure sickness c) Make people laugh',NULL,10,8,'Teacher reads:\n“Vegetables help our body because they have nutrients. They keep us strong, active, and\nhealthy.”\n3. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Toys\nb) Nutrients\nc) Smoke\n4. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us sleepy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us noisy\nTeacher reads:\n“Fruits can taste sweet or sour. They help us stay healthy and give us vitamins.”\n5. How do fruits taste?\na) Sweet or sour\nb) Salty\nc) Bitter\n6. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\nTeacher reads:\n“Trees give us clean air. Birds live in trees because they are safe and high.”\n7. What do trees give us?\na) Dirty air\nb) Clean air\nc) Hot air\n8. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are noisy\nc) Trees are cold\nTeacher reads:\n“Some herbs are used to help sick people feel better. Herbs can cure small illnesses.”\n9. What can herbs do?\na) Make cars move\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make people laugh',1,1,'answer'),
(747,178,70,'pre',5,'Pre-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 5','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','10. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people\nb) Robots\nc) Trees\nTeacher reads:\n“Many animals live on land. Some help farmers by carrying heavy loads or guarding the farm.”\n11. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Horse\nb) Whale\nc) Lobster\n12. Where do these animals live?\na) In the sea\nb) On land\nc) In the sky\nTeacher reads:\n“Woodland animals like squirrels and tarsiers live among trees. Some hide when they see people.”\n13. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They swim\nc) They fly to the sea\nTeacher reads:\n“In the meadow, we see butterflies, bees, and birds. They fly around flowers.”\n14. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They swim\nb) They fly around flowers\nc) They dig tunnels\nTeacher reads:\n“In the forest, animals like monkeys and deer hide among the trees. In the sea, animals like\ndolphins and whales swim together.”\n15. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Deer and monkeys\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Pigs and cows\nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST',NULL,'[]','10. Who uses herbs? a) Sick people b) Robots c) Trees Teacher reads: “Many animals live on land. Some help farmers by carrying heavy loads or guarding the farm.” 11. Which animal helps farmers? a) Horse b) Whale c) Lobster 12. Where do these animals live? a) In the sea b) On land c) In the sky Teacher reads: “Woodland animals like squirrels and tarsiers live among trees. Some hide when they see people.” 13. What do some woodland animals do when they see people? a) They hide b) They swim c) They fly to the sea Teacher reads: “In the meadow, we see butterflies, bees, and birds. They fly around flowers.” 14. What do animals in the meadow do? a) They swim b) They fly around flowers c) They dig tunnels Teacher reads: “In the forest, animals like monkeys and deer hide among the trees. In the sea, animals like dolphins and whales swim together.” 15. Which animals swim together in the sea? a) Deer and monkeys b) Dolphins and whales c) Pigs and cows LISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST',NULL,10,9,'10. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people\nb) Robots\nc) Trees\nTeacher reads:\n“Many animals live on land. Some help farmers by carrying heavy loads or guarding the farm.”\n11. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Horse\nb) Whale\nc) Lobster\n12. Where do these animals live?\na) In the sea\nb) On land\nc) In the sky\nTeacher reads:\n“Woodland animals like squirrels and tarsiers live among trees. Some hide when they see people.”\n13. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They swim\nc) They fly to the sea\nTeacher reads:\n“In the meadow, we see butterflies, bees, and birds. They fly around flowers.”\n14. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They swim\nb) They fly around flowers\nc) They dig tunnels\nTeacher reads:\n“In the forest, animals like monkeys and deer hide among the trees. In the sea, animals like\ndolphins and whales swim together.”\n15. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Deer and monkeys\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Pigs and cows\nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST',1,1,'answer'),
(748,179,71,'pre',1,'Comprehensive Pre-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','COMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20)\nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct answer.\n1. We use a blender to:\na) Wash plates\nb) Make juice\nc) Cook rice\n2. A television is used for:\na) Baking\nb) Watching shows\nc) Watering plants\n3. A pillow is used for:\na) Sleeping comfortably\nb) Cooking food\nc) Writing letters',NULL,'[]','COMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) GRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension PART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) Directions: Choose the correct answer. 1. We use a blender to: a) Wash plates b) Make juice c) Cook rice 2. A television is used for: a) Baking b) Watching shows c) Watering plants 3. A pillow is used for: a) Sleeping comfortably b) Cooking food c) Writing letters',NULL,10,10,'COMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20)\nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct answer.\n1. We use a blender to:\na) Wash plates\nb) Make juice\nc) Cook rice\n2. A television is used for:\na) Baking\nb) Watching shows\nc) Watering plants\n3. A pillow is used for:\na) Sleeping comfortably\nb) Cooking food\nc) Writing letters',1,1,'answer'),
(749,179,71,'pre',2,'Comprehensive Pre-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','4. Soap is used for:\na) Cleaning the body\nb) Sweeping the floor\nc) Cutting paper\n5. A car is found in the:\na) Garden\nb) Garage\nc) Bedroom\n6. A mountain is:\na) A tall landform\nb) A body of water\nc) A type of house\n7. A pond is:\na) A small body of water\nb) A large sea\nc) A mountain\n8. Gold is a type of:\na) Clothing\nb) Mineral\nc) Food\n9. A truck is used to:\na) Fly in the sky\nb) Carry heavy goods\nc) Swim in water\n10. Boracay Island is famous for its:\na) Snow\nb) White sand beach\nc) Tall buildings\n11. A soap dish is used to:\na) Store soap\nb) Plant flowers\nc) Keep toys\n12. A wardrobe is used to store:\na) Clothes\nb) Food\nc) Books\n13. A plateau is:\na) A flat land higher than the land around it\nb) A body of water\nc) A small hill',NULL,'[]','4. Soap is used for: a) Cleaning the body b) Sweeping the floor c) Cutting paper 5. A car is found in the: a) Garden b) Garage c) Bedroom 6. A mountain is: a) A tall landform b) A body of water c) A type of house 7. A pond is: a) A small body of water b) A large sea c) A mountain 8. Gold is a type of: a) Clothing b) Mineral c) Food 9. A truck is used to: a) Fly in the sky b) Carry heavy goods c) Swim in water 10. Boracay Island is famous for its: a) Snow b) White sand beach c) Tall buildings 11. A soap dish is used to: a) Store soap b) Plant flowers c) Keep toys 12. A wardrobe is used to store: a) Clothes b) Food c) Books 13. A plateau is: a) A flat land higher than the land around it b) A body of water c) A small hill',NULL,10,11,'4. Soap is used for:\na) Cleaning the body\nb) Sweeping the floor\nc) Cutting paper\n5. A car is found in the:\na) Garden\nb) Garage\nc) Bedroom\n6. A mountain is:\na) A tall landform\nb) A body of water\nc) A type of house\n7. A pond is:\na) A small body of water\nb) A large sea\nc) A mountain\n8. Gold is a type of:\na) Clothing\nb) Mineral\nc) Food\n9. A truck is used to:\na) Fly in the sky\nb) Carry heavy goods\nc) Swim in water\n10. Boracay Island is famous for its:\na) Snow\nb) White sand beach\nc) Tall buildings\n11. A soap dish is used to:\na) Store soap\nb) Plant flowers\nc) Keep toys\n12. A wardrobe is used to store:\na) Clothes\nb) Food\nc) Books\n13. A plateau is:\na) A flat land higher than the land around it\nb) A body of water\nc) A small hill',1,1,'answer'),
(750,179,71,'pre',3,'Comprehensive Pre-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','14. A funnel is used for:\na) Pouring liquids easily\nb) Playing music\nc) Carrying books\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Land\nb) Water\nc) Rails\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION (15 items)\nTeacher reads the passages assigned to each lesson.\nBased on Lesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The stove cooks\nvegetables and the rice cooker cooks’ rice. Plates and utensils are for eating.”\n16. What should we do in the kitchen?\na) Make it messy\nb) Keep it clean\nc) Leave water everywhere\n17. What do we put in the blender?\na) Rice\nb) Fruits\nc) Plates\nBased on Lesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the windows and a\nbookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do we sit?\na) Bookshelf\nb) Sofa\nc) Table\nBased on Lesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net protects from\ninsects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”',NULL,'[]','14. A funnel is used for: a) Pouring liquids easily b) Playing music c) Carrying books 15. A ship travels on: a) Land b) Water c) Rails PART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION (15 items) Teacher reads the passages assigned to each lesson. Based on Lesson 11 – Kitchen Teacher reads: “In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The stove cooks vegetables and the rice cooker cooks’ rice. Plates and utensils are for eating.” 16. What should we do in the kitchen? a) Make it messy b) Keep it clean c) Leave water everywhere 17. What do we put in the blender? a) Rice b) Fruits c) Plates Based on Lesson 12 – Living Room Teacher reads: “In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the windows and a bookshelf for books.” 18. Where do we sit? a) Bookshelf b) Sofa c) Table Based on Lesson 13 – Bedroom Teacher reads: “In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net protects from insects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”',NULL,10,12,'14. A funnel is used for:\na) Pouring liquids easily\nb) Playing music\nc) Carrying books\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Land\nb) Water\nc) Rails\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION (15 items)\nTeacher reads the passages assigned to each lesson.\nBased on Lesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The stove cooks\nvegetables and the rice cooker cooks’ rice. Plates and utensils are for eating.”\n16. What should we do in the kitchen?\na) Make it messy\nb) Keep it clean\nc) Leave water everywhere\n17. What do we put in the blender?\na) Rice\nb) Fruits\nc) Plates\nBased on Lesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the windows and a\nbookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do we sit?\na) Bookshelf\nb) Sofa\nc) Table\nBased on Lesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net protects from\ninsects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”',1,1,'answer'),
(751,179,71,'pre',4,'Comprehensive Pre-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','19. What protects us from insects?\na) Blanket\nb) Mosquito net\nc) Curtain\n20. Where do we keep clothes?\na) Wardrobe\nb) Table\nc) Floor\nBased on Lesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and poured into a\nbucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What do we use to wash hair?\na) Soap\nb) Shampoo\nc) Comb\n22. What do we step on after bathing?\na) Carpet\nb) Bath mat\nc) Soap dish\nBased on Lesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer help fix small\nparts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What lifts the car?\na) Hammer\nb) Trolley jack\nc) Wheel\n24. What tool is used to fix screws?\na) Screwdriver\nb) Funnel\nc) Pliers\nBased on Lesson 16 – Landforms\nTeacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide and flat. A\nshoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. What landform is tall?\na) Mountain',NULL,'[]','19. What protects us from insects? a) Blanket b) Mosquito net c) Curtain 20. Where do we keep clothes? a) Wardrobe b) Table c) Floor Based on Lesson 14 – Bathroom Teacher reads: “Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and poured into a bucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.” 21. What do we use to wash hair? a) Soap b) Shampoo c) Comb 22. What do we step on after bathing? a) Carpet b) Bath mat c) Soap dish Based on Lesson 15 – Garage Teacher reads: “In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer help fix small parts. A trolley jack lifts the car.” 23. What lifts the car? a) Hammer b) Trolley jack c) Wheel 24. What tool is used to fix screws? a) Screwdriver b) Funnel c) Pliers Based on Lesson 16 – Landforms Teacher reads: “A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide and flat. A shoreline is where land meets water.” 25. What landform is tall? a) Mountain',NULL,10,13,'19. What protects us from insects?\na) Blanket\nb) Mosquito net\nc) Curtain\n20. Where do we keep clothes?\na) Wardrobe\nb) Table\nc) Floor\nBased on Lesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and poured into a\nbucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What do we use to wash hair?\na) Soap\nb) Shampoo\nc) Comb\n22. What do we step on after bathing?\na) Carpet\nb) Bath mat\nc) Soap dish\nBased on Lesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer help fix small\nparts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What lifts the car?\na) Hammer\nb) Trolley jack\nc) Wheel\n24. What tool is used to fix screws?\na) Screwdriver\nb) Funnel\nc) Pliers\nBased on Lesson 16 – Landforms\nTeacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide and flat. A\nshoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. What landform is tall?\na) Mountain',1,1,'answer'),
(752,179,71,'pre',5,'Comprehensive Pre-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 5','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','b) Hill\nc) Basin\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Desert\nb) Shoreline\nc) Glacier\nBased on Lesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) Lake and pond\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) River and spring\n28. What should we keep clean?\na) Land\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Cars\nBased on Lesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Toys\nb) Treasure\nc) Houses\n30. Which mineral is mentioned?\na) Plastic\nb) Gold\nc) Wood',NULL,'[]','b) Hill c) Basin 26. Where does land meet water? a) Desert b) Shoreline c) Glacier Based on Lesson 17 – Bodies of Water Teacher reads: “The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean.” 27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”? a) Lake and pond b) Ocean and sea c) River and spring 28. What should we keep clean? a) Land b) Ocean and sea c) Cars Based on Lesson 18 – Mineral Resources Teacher reads the poem. 29. What is Earth rich in? a) Toys b) Treasure c) Houses 30. Which mineral is mentioned? a) Plastic b) Gold c) Wood',NULL,10,14,'b) Hill\nc) Basin\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Desert\nb) Shoreline\nc) Glacier\nBased on Lesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) Lake and pond\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) River and spring\n28. What should we keep clean?\na) Land\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Cars\nBased on Lesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Toys\nb) Treasure\nc) Houses\n30. Which mineral is mentioned?\na) Plastic\nb) Gold\nc) Wood',1,1,'answer'),
(753,180,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Flowers','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Plants around Me\nThis is my garden.\nI\'ll plant flowers, vegetables, and grains.\nHere are the seeds of trees and herbs.\nThe sun will shine; the rain will fall.\nThe seeds will sprout, up tall.','assets/images/level5/g2/p018-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p018-1.webp\"]','Plants around Me This is my garden. I\'ll plant flowers, vegetables, and grains. Here are the seeds of trees and herbs. The sun will shine; the rain will fall. The seeds will sprout, up tall.',NULL,5,18,'Plants around Me\nThis is my garden.\nI\'ll plant flowers, vegetables, and grains.\nHere are the seeds of trees and herbs.\nThe sun will shine; the rain will fall.\nThe seeds will sprout, up tall.',1,1,'none'),
(754,180,NULL,'learn',2,'Listen: Flowers','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Activity 1- Flowers\nFlowers\nFlowers are the beauty of nature.\nThey grow and bloom in different colors.\nThey gave us fragrant odor.\nFlowers are wonderful.\nOrchids\nDahlia\nRose\nSampaguita\nSunflower Sampaguita Tulips\nYellow Plumeria\nChrysanthemum\nAster','assets/images/level5/g2/p019-3.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-6.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-7.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-5.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-9.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p019-8.webp\"]','Activity 1- Flowers Flowers Flowers are the beauty of nature. They grow and bloom in different colors. They gave us fragrant odor. Flowers are wonderful. Orchids Dahlia Rose Sampaguita Sunflower Sampaguita Tulips Yellow Plumeria Chrysanthemum Aster',NULL,5,19,'Activity 1- Flowers\nFlowers\nFlowers are the beauty of nature.\nThey grow and bloom in different colors.\nThey gave us fragrant odor.\nFlowers are wonderful.\nOrchids\nDahlia\nRose\nSampaguita\nSunflower Sampaguita Tulips\nYellow Plumeria\nChrysanthemum\nAster',1,1,'none'),
(755,180,NULL,'learn',3,'Flowers · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 1A: Assessment\nA. Vocabulary (5 items)\nLesson 1A: Assessment\nDirections: Match the word with its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud the\nwords and meanings.)\n1. Beauty\na. Smells good\n2. Bloom\nb. Something nice to see\n3. Color\nc. To open like a flower\n4. Fragrant\nd. A shade like red, blue, or yellow\n5. Wonderful\ne. Very nice or amazing\nLesson 1B: Assessment\nB. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully to the teacher as the story is read aloud. Then\nanswer the questions.\n1. What is the beauty of nature in the story?\na. Trees\nb. flowers\nc. clouds\n2. What do flowers do?\na. They sleep\nb. They grow and bloom\nc. They jump\n3. Flowers bloom in different ______\n.\na. Colors\nb. sizes\nc. sounds\n4. What do flowers give us?\na. A fragrant odor\nb. A loud noise\nc. A bright light\n5. How does the story describe flowers?\na. Ugly\nb. wonderful\nc. scary',NULL,'[]','Activity 1A: Assessment A. Vocabulary (5 items) Lesson 1A: Assessment Directions: Match the word with its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud the words and meanings.) 1. Beauty a. Smells good 2. Bloom b. Something nice to see 3. Color c. To open like a flower 4. Fragrant d. A shade like red, blue, or yellow 5. Wonderful e. Very nice or amazing Lesson 1B: Assessment B. Listening Comprehension (5 items) Directions: Listen carefully to the teacher as the story is read aloud. Then answer the questions. 1. What is the beauty of nature in the story? a. Trees b. flowers c. clouds 2. What do flowers do? a. They sleep b. They grow and bloom c. They jump 3. Flowers bloom in different blank . a. Colors b. sizes c. sounds 4. What do flowers give us? a. A fragrant odor b. A loud noise c. A bright light 5. How does the story describe flowers? a. Ugly b. wonderful c. scary',NULL,10,20,'Activity 1A: Assessment\nA. Vocabulary (5 items)\nLesson 1A: Assessment\nDirections: Match the word with its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud the\nwords and meanings.)\n1. Beauty\na. Smells good\n2. Bloom\nb. Something nice to see\n3. Color\nc. To open like a flower\n4. Fragrant\nd. A shade like red, blue, or yellow\n5. Wonderful\ne. Very nice or amazing\nLesson 1B: Assessment\nB. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully to the teacher as the story is read aloud. Then\nanswer the questions.\n1. What is the beauty of nature in the story?\na. Trees\nb. flowers\nc. clouds\n2. What do flowers do?\na. They sleep\nb. They grow and bloom\nc. They jump\n3. Flowers bloom in different ______\n.\na. Colors\nb. sizes\nc. sounds\n4. What do flowers give us?\na. A fragrant odor\nb. A loud noise\nc. A bright light\n5. How does the story describe flowers?\na. Ugly\nb. wonderful\nc. scary',1,1,'answer'),
(756,181,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Vegetables','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Activity 2- Vegetables\nVegetables in our garden.\nLegumes, leafy vegetables and grains\nThey give nutrients to our body and brains,\nTo keep us active and healthy mind\ncarrots\ncabbage\nradish\nlettuce\nbroccoli\ncauliflower\npotatoes\ntomato\nbean\nstring bean','assets/images/level5/g2/p021-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p021-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p021-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p021-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p021-3.webp\"]','Activity 2- Vegetables Vegetables in our garden. Legumes, leafy vegetables and grains They give nutrients to our body and brains, To keep us active and healthy mind carrots cabbage radish lettuce broccoli cauliflower potatoes tomato bean string bean',NULL,5,21,'Activity 2- Vegetables\nVegetables in our garden.\nLegumes, leafy vegetables and grains\nThey give nutrients to our body and brains,\nTo keep us active and healthy mind\ncarrots\ncabbage\nradish\nlettuce\nbroccoli\ncauliflower\npotatoes\ntomato\nbean\nstring bean',1,1,'none'),
(757,181,NULL,'learn',2,'Vegetables · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 2 A: Assessment\nA. Matching Type: In column A is the picture of vegetables. In column B\nis the name of the vegetables. Match column A and B by\nconnecting it with a line.\nA. Picture of vegetables\nB. Name of vegetables\n1.\na. carrots\n2.\nb. stringbeans\n3.\nc. tomato\n4.\nd. potato\n5.\ne. cabbage\nActivity 2B: Assessment\nStory for the teacher to read:\nVegetables\nVegetables in our garden. Legumes, leafy and grains. They give nutrients to\nour body and brains, to keep us active and healthy mind.\nDirections: Listen carefully to the story. Then answer the questions.\nA. Listening and Vocabulary Questions (5 items)\n1. Where can we find the vegetables in the story?\na. in the garden\nb. in the store\nc. in the forest\n2. Which of the following is a kind of vegetable mentioned in the story?\na. Fruits b. legumes c. candies\n3. What do vegetables give to our body and brain?\na. Toys\nb. nutrients\nc. noise\n4. Why are nutrients important for us?','assets/images/level5/g2/p022-2.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p022-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p022-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p022-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p022-5.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p022-1.webp\"]','Activity 2 A: Assessment A. Matching Type: In column A is the picture of vegetables. In column B is the name of the vegetables. Match column A and B by connecting it with a line. A. Picture of vegetables B. Name of vegetables 1. a. carrots 2. b. stringbeans 3. c. tomato 4. d. potato 5. e. cabbage Activity 2B: Assessment Story for the teacher to read: Vegetables Vegetables in our garden. Legumes, leafy and grains. They give nutrients to our body and brains, to keep us active and healthy mind. Directions: Listen carefully to the story. Then answer the questions. A. Listening and Vocabulary Questions (5 items) 1. Where can we find the vegetables in the story? a. in the garden b. in the store c. in the forest 2. Which of the following is a kind of vegetable mentioned in the story? a. Fruits b. legumes c. candies 3. What do vegetables give to our body and brain? a. Toys b. nutrients c. noise 4. Why are nutrients important for us?',NULL,10,22,'Activity 2 A: Assessment\nA. Matching Type: In column A is the picture of vegetables. In column B\nis the name of the vegetables. Match column A and B by\nconnecting it with a line.\nA. Picture of vegetables\nB. Name of vegetables\n1.\na. carrots\n2.\nb. stringbeans\n3.\nc. tomato\n4.\nd. potato\n5.\ne. cabbage\nActivity 2B: Assessment\nStory for the teacher to read:\nVegetables\nVegetables in our garden. Legumes, leafy and grains. They give nutrients to\nour body and brains, to keep us active and healthy mind.\nDirections: Listen carefully to the story. Then answer the questions.\nA. Listening and Vocabulary Questions (5 items)\n1. Where can we find the vegetables in the story?\na. in the garden\nb. in the store\nc. in the forest\n2. Which of the following is a kind of vegetable mentioned in the story?\na. Fruits b. legumes c. candies\n3. What do vegetables give to our body and brain?\na. Toys\nb. nutrients\nc. noise\n4. Why are nutrients important for us?',1,1,'answer'),
(758,182,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Fruits','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Activity 3- Fruits\nFruits\nFruit makes us very strong.\nAnd keep us healthy for long.\nThey taste sour and sweet.\nThat everyone likes to eat.\ntiesa\ncashew\nguyabano\napple\natis\nstar apple santol\nmangosteen\nmacopa\nsiniguelas','assets/images/level5/g2/p023-2.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p023-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p023-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p023-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p023-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p023-5.webp\"]','Activity 3- Fruits Fruits Fruit makes us very strong. And keep us healthy for long. They taste sour and sweet. That everyone likes to eat. tiesa cashew guyabano apple atis star apple santol mangosteen macopa siniguelas',NULL,5,23,'Activity 3- Fruits\nFruits\nFruit makes us very strong.\nAnd keep us healthy for long.\nThey taste sour and sweet.\nThat everyone likes to eat.\ntiesa\ncashew\nguyabano\napple\natis\nstar apple santol\nmangosteen\nmacopa\nsiniguelas',1,1,'none'),
