t is the poem mostly talking about? a. Games Trees b. Trees c. Weather',NULL,10,26,'Activity 4- Assessment\nA. Vocabulary\nDirections: Match the word to its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud.)\nEverywhere a. To stay or make a home in\nFresh\noh Ww ny\nFresh b. Protection or a place to stay\nAir\nAir c. All around us; in many places\nShelter\nShelter d. What we breathe\nLive\nLive e. Clean or new\nListening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as the story is read aloud. Then answer the\nquestions.\nWhere are trees found according to the story?\na. In one place only\nb. Everywhere\nOnly in the city\nWhat do trees give us?\nDirty air\nb. Clean and fresh air\nNo air at all\nWho lives up in the trees?\na. Cats\nb. Little birds\nFish\nWhat is a shelter for the birds in the story?\nTrees\nb. Cars\nc. Houses\nWhat is the poem mostly talking about?\na. Games\nTrees\nb. Trees c. Weather',1,1,'answer'),
(762,184,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Herbs','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Activity 5- Herbs\nHerbs\nMagical herbs,\nGiven to this world.\nCan cure so much illness,\nYou’d never believe it would.\nlemongrass\npeppermint\ndill\noregano\neucalyptus\naloe vera\nRed basil\nsage\nTurmeric','assets/images/level5/g2/p027-3.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-7.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-6.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-5.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-8.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p027-2.webp\"]','Activity 5- Herbs Herbs Magical herbs, Given to this world. Can cure so much illness, You’d never believe it would. lemongrass peppermint dill oregano eucalyptus aloe vera Red basil sage Turmeric',NULL,5,27,'Activity 5- Herbs\nHerbs\nMagical herbs,\nGiven to this world.\nCan cure so much illness,\nYou’d never believe it would.\nlemongrass\npeppermint\ndill\noregano\neucalyptus\naloe vera\nRed basil\nsage\nTurmeric',1,1,'none'),
(763,184,NULL,'learn',2,'Herbs · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 5 Assessment\nPart 1: Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPart 1: Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension Direction: Choose the correct picture\n1. Which picture shows a “herb”?\na)\n(big tree)\nb)\n(small plant with leaves)\nc)\n(dog)\nWhich picture shows “cure”?\n(medicine) (gift) = c) (house)\na)\nWhich picture shows “magical”?\na) (sparkles) (apple) —c)\n4. What can the magical herb do?\na) (helps sick people) b) (makes art) c) (makes you run\nfast)\n5. Who received the magical herb? fast)\na)\nor a sad face if no (acat) c) (a king)\n6. Do you think herbs are helpful?\nPoint to a happy face\nyes\nor a sad face if no\nif yes\nInstructions for the Teacher:\n➢\nRead the poem/story aloud slowly and clearly.\n➢Ask the students to listen carefully because they will\nanswer some questions after.\nPart 2: Vocabulary\nChoose the correct answer.\n1. Choose the correct answer. What is a “herb”?\na)\na) Akind of magic wand\nb)\nb) A plant we can use for medicine or cooking\nc)\nc) A type of animal\nWhat does “cure” mean in the story?\na) To make someone feel better from illness\nb)\nb) To give someone a gift\nc)\nc) To make something disappear\nThe story says the herb is “magical.” What does “magical” mean?\na)\na) Ordinary\nb)\nb) Special and amazing\nc)\nc) Smal','assets/images/level5/g2/p028-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-9.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-5.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-6.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-7.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-8.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-10.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p028-11.webp\"]','Activity 5 Assessment Part 1: Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension Pa