(779,191,NULL,'learn',2,'Things Found in the Living Room · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nActivity 12: Things Found in the Living Room\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct word that fits.\n1. We sit on a sofa to:\na) Cook food\nb) Sit and relax\nc) Store books\n2. A television is used to:\na) Watch shows or movies\nb) Hold flowers\nc) Keep the room warm\n3. We put curtains on:\na) Windows\nb) Floor\nc) Walls\n4. A bookshelf is used to:\na) Sit on\nb) Store and display books\nc) Hold flowers\n5. A flower vase is used to:\na) Hold water and flowers\nb) Cover windows\nc) Tell time\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the passage below. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we can sit on the sofa and watch television. There is a\nbookshelf for books, a flower vase for decoration, and curtains on the\nwindows. A carpet and an electric fan keep the room comfortable. The\nclock tells the time.”\n6. Where do we sit in the living room to relax?\na) Bookshelf\nb) Sofa\nc) Television\n7. What do we use to hold flowers?\na) Flower vase\nb) Carpet\nc) Clock\n8. What keeps the room cool?\na) Carpet and electric fan\nb) Bookshelf\nc) Television\n9. Where do we keep our books in the living room?\na) Sofa\nb) Bookshelf\nc) Flower vase\n10. What is used to tell the time in the living room?\na) Carpet\nb) Clock\nc) Television',NULL,'[]','Formative Assessment – Grade 2 Activity 12: Things Found in the Living Room Part I: Vocabulary Directions: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct word that fits. 1. We sit on a sofa to: a) Cook food b) Sit and relax c) Store books 2. A television is used to: a) Watch shows or movies b) Hold flowers c) Keep the room warm 3. We put curtains on: a) Windows b) Floor c) Walls 4. A bookshelf is used to: a) Sit on b) Store and display books c) Hold flowers 5. A flower vase is used to: a) Hold water and flowers b) Cover windows c) Tell time Part II: Listening Comprehension (5 items) Directions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the passage below. Then choose the correct answer. Teacher reads: “In the living room, we can sit on the sofa and watch television. There is a bookshelf for books, a flower vase for decoration, and curtains on the windows. A carpet and an electric fan keep the room comfortable. The clock tells the time.” 6. Where do we sit in the living room to relax? a) Bookshelf b) Sofa c) Television 7. What do we use to hold flowers? a) Flower vase b) Carpet c) Clock 8. What keeps the room cool? a) Carpet and electric fan b) Bookshelf c) Television 9. Where do we keep our books in the living room? a) Sofa b) Bookshelf c) Flower vase 10. What is used to tell the time in the living room? a) Carpet b) Clock c) Television',NULL,10,44,'Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nActivity 12: Things Found in the Living Room\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct word that fits.\n1. We sit on a sofa to:\na) Cook food\nb) Sit and relax\nc) Store books\n2. A television is used to:\na) Watch shows or movies\nb) Hold flowers\nc) Keep the room warm\n3. We put curtains on:\na) Windows\nb) Floor\nc) Walls\n4. A bookshelf is used to:\na) Sit on\nb) Store and display books\nc) Hold flowers\n5. A flower vase is used to:\na) Hold water and flowers\nb) Cover windows\nc) Tell time\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the passage below. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we can sit on the sofa and watch television. There is a\nbookshelf for books, a flower vase for decoration, and curtains on the\nwindows. A carpet and an electric fan keep the room comfortable. The\nclock tells the time.”\n6. Where do we sit in the living room to relax?\na) Bookshelf\nb) Sofa\nc) Television\n7. What do we use to hold flowers?\na) Flower vase\nb) Carpet\nc) Clock\n8. What keeps the room cool?\na) Carpet and electric fan\nb) Bookshelf\nc) Television\n9. Where do we keep our books in the living room?\na) Sofa\nb) Bookshelf\nc) Flower vase\n10. What is used to tell the time in the living room?\na) Carpet\nb) Clock\nc) Television',1,1,'answer'),
