(786,195,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Landforms','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Me and My\nMe and My Surroundings\nGod created heaven and Earth.\nBeautiful surrounding with fresh air to breath.\nKeep our environment clean and green.\nMake our place safe to live in.','assets/images/level5/g2/p051-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p051-1.webp\"]','Me and My Me and My Surroundings God created heaven and Earth. Beautiful surrounding with fresh air to breath. Keep our environment clean and green. Make our place safe to live in.',NULL,5,51,'Me and My\nMe and My Surroundings\nGod created heaven and Earth.\nBeautiful surrounding with fresh air to breath.\nKeep our environment clean and green.\nMake our place safe to live in.',1,1,'none'),
(787,195,NULL,'learn',2,'Listen: Landforms','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Lesson 16- Landforms\nLandforms\nBeyond your imagination.\nLand has different forms.\nExperience the beauty of nature.\nmountain\nvalley\nplateau\nglacier\ndesert\nhill\nbasin\nshoreline\nplain','assets/images/level5/g2/p052-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p052-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p052-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p052-3.webp\"]','Lesson 16- Landforms Landforms Beyond your imagination. Land has different forms. Experience the beauty of nature. mountain valley plateau glacier desert hill basin shoreline plain',NULL,5,52,'Lesson 16- Landforms\nLandforms\nBeyond your imagination.\nLand has different forms.\nExperience the beauty of nature.\nmountain\nvalley\nplateau\nglacier\ndesert\nhill\nbasin\nshoreline\nplain',1,1,'none'),
(788,195,NULL,'learn',3,'Landforms · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 16: Landforms\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: mountain, valley, plateau, glacier, hill, desert, basin, shoreline,\nplain\n1. A ______\nis a high landform with steep sides that is taller than a hill.\na) mountain\nb) plain\nc) shoreline\n2. A ______\nis a wide, flat area of land.\na) hill\nb) plain\nc) glacier\n3. A ______\nis a low area between mountains or hills.\na) valley\nb) plateau\nc) desert\n4. A ______\nis a large area of flat land that is higher than the land\naround it.\na) shoreline\nb) plateau\nc) basin\n5. A ______\nis a very dry place with lots of sand.\na) desert\nb) glacier\nc) hill\nPart II: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n\"The Earth has many different landforms. A mountain is tall and reaches\nhigh into the sky, while a hill is smaller and gently rounded. A valley lies\nbetween mountains and hills. A plain is a wide, flat area where many\npeople build houses and farms. A plateau is also flat but stands higher than\nthe land around it. Some places have glaciers, which are large, slow-\nmoving ice. A desert is hot and dry with very little water. The shoreline is the\nplace where land meets the water. A basin is a low area that can hold\nwater. These landforms make the Earth beautiful and exciting to explore.\"\nWhich landform is tall and reaches high into the sky?\na) hill\nb) mountain\nc) basin\n7. What landform is a low area between mountains or hills?\na)\na) valley b) shoreline c) plateau\n8. Which landform is flat and good for farms and houses?\na)\na) glacier b) plain c) desert\n9. What landform is made of slow-moving ice?\na) basin\nb) glacier\nc) hill\nWhere does the land meet the water?\na)\na) shoreline b) desert c) plateau','assets/images/level5/g2/p053-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p053-1.webp\"]','Formative Assessment – Grade 2 Lesson 16: Landforms Part I: Vocabulary Directions: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits. Words to use: mountain, valley, plateau, glacier, hill, desert, basin, shoreline, plain 1. A blank is a high landform with steep sides that is taller than a hill. a) mountain b) plain c) shoreline 2. A blank is a wide, flat area of land. a) hill b) plain c) glacier 3. A blank is a low area between mountains or hills. a) valley b) plateau c) desert 4. A blank is a large area of flat land that is higher than the land around it. a) shoreline b) plateau c) basin 5. A blank is a very dry place with lots of sand. a) desert b) glacier c) hill Part II: Listening Comprehension Directions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then choose the correct answer. Teacher reads: \"The Earth has many different landforms. A mountain is tall and reaches high into the sky, while a hill is smaller and gently rounded. A valley lies between mountains and hills. A plain is a wide, flat area where many people build houses and farms. A plateau is also flat but stands higher than the land around it. Some places have glaciers, which are large, slow- moving ice. A desert is hot and dry with very little water. The shoreline is the place where land meets the water. A basin is a low area that can hold water. These landforms make the Earth beautiful and exciting to explore.\" Which landform is tall and reaches high into the sky? a) hill b) mountain c) basin 7. What landform is a low area between mountains or hills? a) a) valley b) shoreline c) plateau 8. Which landform is flat and good for farms and houses? a) a) glacier b) plain c) desert 9. What landform is made of slow-moving ice? a) basin b) glacier c) hill Where does the land meet the water? a) a) shoreline b) desert c) plateau',NULL,10,53,'Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 16: Landforms\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: mountain, valley, plateau, glacier, hill, desert, basin, shoreline,\nplain\n1. A ______\nis a high landform with steep sides that is taller than a hill.\na) mountain\nb) plain\nc) shoreline\n2. A ______\nis a wide, flat area of land.\na) hill\nb) plain\nc) glacier\n3. A ______\nis a low area between mountains or hills.\na) valley\nb) plateau\nc) desert\n4. A ______\nis a large area of flat land that is higher than the land\naround it.\na) shoreline\nb) plateau\nc) basin\n5. A ______\nis a very dry place with lots of sand.\na) desert\nb) glacier\nc) hill\nPart II: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n\"The Earth has many different landforms. A mountain is tall and reaches\nhigh into the sky, while a hill is smaller and gently rounded. A valley lies\nbetween mountains and hills. A plain is a wide, flat area where many\npeople build houses and farms. A plateau is also flat but stands higher than\nthe land around it. Some places have glaciers, which are large, slow-\nmoving ice. A desert is hot and dry with very little water. The shoreline is the\nplace where land meets the water. A basin is a low area that can hold\nwater. These landforms make the Earth beautiful and exciting to explore.\"\nWhich landform is tall and reaches high into the sky?\na) hill\nb) mountain\nc',1,1,'answer'),
(789,196,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Bodies of Water','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Lesson 17- Body of Water\nBody of Water\nThe spring, falls, pond, lake and river.\nEnhancing the beauty on Earth forever.\nOcean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean and garbage free.\nocean\nsea\nriver\nstream\nspring\nfalls\nlake\npond\nditch','assets/images/level5/g2/p054-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p054-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p054-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p054-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p054-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p054-6.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p054-7.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p054-5.webp\"]','Lesson 17- Body of Water Body of Water The spring, falls, pond, lake and river. Enhancing the beauty on Earth forever. Ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean and garbage free. ocean sea river stream spring falls lake pond ditch',NULL,5,54,'Lesson 17- Body of Water\nBody of Water\nThe spring, falls, pond, lake and river.\nEnhancing the beauty on Earth forever.\nOcean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean and garbage free.\nocean\nsea\nriver\nstream\nspring\nfalls\nlake\npond\nditch',1,1,'none'),
(790,196,NULL,'learn',2,'Bodies of Water · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Lesson 17: Body of Water\nPart I: Vocabulary (5 items)\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct body of water that fits.\n(Teacher may show pictures of each body of water while reading.)\n1. A small body of water where frogs and fish can live is a ______\n.\na) pond\nb) ocean\nc) river\n2. A very big body of water with big waves is called the\n______.\na) sea\nb) ocean\nc) lake\n3. Water that comes from a high place and falls down is called\n______.\na) spring\nb) falls\nc) river\n4. A long body of water that flows from one place to another is a ______\n.\na) river\nb) lake\nc) pond\n5. A large body of water that is bigger than a pond but calmer than the\nsea is a ______\n.\na) lake\nb) falls\nc) ocean c) ocean\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short poem. Then answer\nthe questions.\nTeacher Reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake and river, Enhancing the beauty on Earth\nforever. Ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean and garbage\nfree.”\nQuestions:\n6. What are named in the poem that make Earth beautiful?\na) mountains\nb) bodies of water\nc) animals\n7. Which two bodies of water are described as “nice to see”?\na) lake and pond\nb) ocean and sea\nc) river and spring\n8. What should we keep clean and garbage-free?\na) the ocean and sea b) the classroom c) the trees\n9. Which body of water flows from place to place?\na) river\nb) pond c) lake\n10. Which body of water comes from the ground and is mentioned first in\nthe poem?\na) pond b) spring\nc) sea',NULL,'[]','Lesson 17: Body of Water Part I: Vocabulary (5 items) Directions: Read each sentence. Choose the correct body of water that fits. (Teacher may show pictures of each body of water while reading.) 1. A small body of water where frogs and fish can live is a blank . a) pond b) ocean c) river 2. A very big body of water with big waves is called the blank . a) sea b) ocean c) lake 3. Water that comes from a high place and falls down is called blank . a) spring b) falls c) river 4. A long body of water that flows from one place to another is a blank . a) river b) lake c) pond 5. A large body of water that is bigger than a pond but calmer than the sea is a blank . a) lake b) falls c) ocean c) ocean Part II: Listening Comprehension (5 items) Directions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short poem. Then answer the questions. Teacher Reads: “The spring, falls, pond, lake and river, Enhancing the beauty on Earth forever. Ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean and garbage free.” Questions: 6. What are named in the poem that make Earth beautiful? a) mountains b) bodies of water c) animals 7. Which two bodies of water are described as “nice to see”? a) lake and pond b) ocean and sea c) river and spring 8. What should we keep clean and garbage-free? a) the ocean and sea b) the classroom c) the trees 9. Which body of water flows from place to place? a) river b) pond c) lake 10. Which body of water comes from the ground and is mentioned first in the poem? a) pond b) spring c) sea',NULL,10,55,'Lesson 17: Body of Water\nPart I: Vocabulary (5 items)\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct body of water that fits.\n(Teacher may show pictures of each body of water while reading.)\n1. A small body of water where frogs and fish can live is a ______\n.\na) pond\nb) ocean\nc) river\n2. A very big body of water with big waves is called the\n______.\na) sea\nb) ocean\nc) lake\n3. Water that comes from a high place and falls down is called\n______.\na) spring\nb) falls\nc) river\n4. A long body of water that flows from one place to another is a ______\n.\na) river\nb) lake\nc) pond\n5. A large body of water that is bigger than a pond but calmer than the\nsea is a ______\n.\na) lake\nb) falls\nc) ocean c) ocean\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short poem. Then answer\nthe questions.\nTeacher Reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake and river, Enhancing the beauty on Earth\nforever. Ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean and garbage\nfree.”\nQuestions:\n6. What are named in the poem that make Earth beautiful?\na) mountains\nb) bodies of water\nc) animals\n7. Which two bodies of water are described as “nice to see”?\na) lake and pond\nb) ocean and sea\nc) river and spring\n8. What should we keep clean and garbage-free?\na) the ocean and sea b) the classroom c) the trees\n9. Which body of water flows from place to place?\na) river\nb) pond c) lake\n10. Which body of water comes from the ground and is mentioned first in\nthe poem?\na) pond b) spring',1,1,'answer'),
(791,197,NULL,'learn',1,'Listen: Mineral Resources','reference','Listen as the page is read aloud. Look at the pictures and say the words.','Lesson 18- Mineral Resources\nMineral Resources\nEarth is rich in treasure.\nMore than we could ever measure.\nCoal, copper, gold and silver.\nElements on Earth layer upon layer.\ngold\nsilver\ncopper\nsalt\nlimestone\ncoal\naluminum\nsand and\nphosphate\ngravel','assets/images/level5/g2/p056-5.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p056-5.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p056-6.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p056-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p056-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p056-4.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p056-3.webp\"]','Lesson 18- Mineral Resources Mineral Resources Earth is rich in treasure. More than we could ever measure. Coal, copper, gold and silver. Elements on Earth layer upon layer. gold silver copper salt limestone coal aluminum sand and phosphate gravel',NULL,5,56,'Lesson 18- Mineral Resources\nMineral Resources\nEarth is rich in treasure.\nMore than we could ever measure.\nCoal, copper, gold and silver.\nElements on Earth layer upon layer.\ngold\nsilver\ncopper\nsalt\nlimestone\ncoal\naluminum\nsand and\nphosphate\ngravel',1,1,'none'),
(792,197,NULL,'learn',2,'Mineral Resources · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','PART A — VOCABULARY WITH PICTURES\nDirections:\nMatch the picture to the correct word. Write the letter of the correct\nanswer.\nPicture Icons\n– gold\n– silver\n– copper (use magnet icon to represent metal)\n– coal\n– salt\n– limestone\n– phosphate (fertilizer symbol\nsubstitute)\n– aluminium (aluminum can)\n– sand & gravel\nItems:\nWord List:\n1. ______\nA. Coal\n2. ______\nB. Silver\n3. ______\nC. Sand & Gravel\n4. ______\nD. Limestone\n5. ______\nE. Aluminium\n6. ______\nF. Gold\n7. ______\nG. Salt\n8. ______\nH. Phosphate\n9. ______\nI. Copper\nPART B — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the short story aloud. Story: Mineral Resources\nEarth is rich of treasure. More than we could ever measure. Coal, copper,\ngold and silver. Elements on Earth layer upon layer.\nDirections:\nListen to the story. Then answer the questions.\n1. What is the story talking about?\na. Animals\nb. Mineral resources\nc. Weather\n2. Which of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\na. Silver\nb. Coal\nc. Plastic\n3. Name one mineral you heard from the story.\na. Gold\nb. Tree\nc. Water\n4. What word in the poem means “precious things found on Earth”?\na. Treasure\nb. Rock\nc. Soil\nd. Sand\n5. What does the poem say Earth is full of?\na. Treasure\nb. Food\nc. Water only\nPART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections: Use the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: gold • coal • silver • copper\nPeople use to make jewelry.\nto make jewelry.\n2. Many machines use wires.\nis black and used for fuel.','assets/images/level5/g2/p057-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g2/p057-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p057-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p057-3.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g2/p057-4.webp\"]','PART A — VOCABULARY WITH PICTURES Directions: Match the picture to the correct word. Write the letter of the correct answer. P