(797,199,NULL,'learn',3,'Famous Locations · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','PART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections:\nUse the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: Boracay Island • Pagsanjan Falls • Bulkang Mayon • Banaue\nRice Terraces\n1. People visit ______\nto see beautiful beaches.\n2. ______\nis a famous volcano in the Philippines.\n3. You can ride a boat at ______\n.\n4. Farmers grow rice at ______\n.',NULL,'[]','PART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK Directions: Use the word bank to complete each sentence. Word Bank: Boracay Island • Pagsanjan Falls • Bulkang Mayon • Banaue Rice Terraces 1. People visit blank to see beautiful beaches. 2. blank is a famous volcano in the Philippines. 3. You can ride a boat at blank . 4. Farmers grow rice at blank .',NULL,10,62,'PART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections:\nUse the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: Boracay Island • Pagsanjan Falls • Bulkang Mayon • Banaue\nRice Terraces\n1. People visit ______\nto see beautiful beaches.\n2. ______\nis a famous volcano in the Philippines.\n3. You can ride a boat at ______\n.\n4. Farmers grow rice at ______\n.',1,1,'answer'),
(798,200,72,'post',1,'Post-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','POSTTEST: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nPart I: Vocabulary (15 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the\nunderlined word.\n1. Herbs can cure many illness. What does illness mean?\na) Birthday\nb) A sickness\nc) School subject\n2. Fruits can taste sweet or sour. What does sour mean?\na) Very cold\nb) Not sweet\nc) Too salty\n3. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n4. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) In many places all around\nb) Only in one place\nc) Not in many places\n5. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n6. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Full of energy\nc) Feeling sleepy\n7. Some herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Special or amazing\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Ordinary\n8. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?',NULL,'[]','POSTTEST: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only ) Part I: Vocabulary (15 items) Directions: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the underlined word. 1. Herbs can cure many illness. What does illness mean? a) Birthday b) A sickness c) School subject 2. Fruits can taste sweet or sour. What does sour mean? a) Very cold b) Not sweet c) Too salty 3. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean? a) Something ugly b) Something nice to see c) Something loud 4. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean? a) In many places all around b) Only in one place c) Not in many places 5. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean? a) Strong and well b) Sick c) Dirty 6. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean? a) Feeling weak b) Full of energy c) Feeling sleepy 7. Some herbs are called magical. What does magical mean? a) Special or amazing b) Cannot do anything c) Ordinary 8. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?',NULL,10,64,'POSTTEST: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nPart I: Vocabulary (15 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the\nunderlined word.\n1. Herbs can cure many illness. What does illness mean?\na) Birthday\nb) A sickness\nc) School subject\n2. Fruits can taste sweet or sour. What does sour mean?\na) Very cold\nb) Not sweet\nc) Too salty\n3. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n4. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) In many places all around\nb) Only in one place\nc) Not in many places\n5. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n6. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Full of energy\nc) Feeling sleepy\n7. Some herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Special or amazing\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Ordinary\n8. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?',1,1,'answer'),
(799,200,72,'post',2,'Post-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','a) To look and listen carefully\nb) To run away\nc) To ignore\n9. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that disappear\nc) Things that are broken\n10. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n11. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Things that help us grow\nb) Toys for us to play\nc) Harmful things\n12. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Playing in a mean or silly way\nb) Helping nicely\nc) Sleeping quietly\n13. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Good smell\nb) Bad smell\nc) No smell\n14. Fruits give vitamins that help us grow strong.\na) Weak\nb) Full of energy and healthy\nc) Sleepy\n15. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To hide\nc) To fall to the ground\n( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (15 items)\nonly)\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads the passage or question.\nChoose the correct answer.',NULL,'[]','a) To look and listen carefully b) To run away c) To ignore 9. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean? a) Things that are made b) Things that disappear c) Things that are broken 10. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean? a) A place to stay safe b) A type of fruit c) A kind of game 11. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean? a) Things that help us grow b) Toys for us to play c) Harmful things 12. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean? a) Playing in a mean or silly way b) Helping nicely c) Sleeping quietly 13. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean? a) Good smell b) Bad smell c) No smell 14. Fruits give vitamins that help us grow strong. a) Weak b) Full of energy and healthy c) Sleepy 15. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean? a) To open and show petals b) To hide c) To fall to the ground ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 Part II: Listening Comprehension (15 items) only) Directions: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads the passage or question. Choose the correct answer.',NULL,10,65,'a) To look and listen carefully\nb) To run away\nc) To ignore\n9. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that disappear\nc) Things that are broken\n10. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n11. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Things that help us grow\nb) Toys for us to play\nc) Harmful things\n12. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Playing in a mean or silly way\nb) Helping nicely\nc) Sleeping quietly\n13. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Good smell\nb) Bad smell\nc) No smell\n14. Fruits give vitamins that help us grow strong.\na) Weak\nb) Full of energy and healthy\nc) Sleepy\n15. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To hide\nc) To fall to the ground\n( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (15 items)\nonly)\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads the passage or question.\nChoose the correct answer.',1,1,'answer'),
(800,200,72,'post',3,'Post-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','16. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they taste sweet\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they are loud\n17. What do flowers give?\na) A loud noise\nb) A good smell\nc) A sour taste\n18. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us noisy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us sleepy\n19. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Smoke\nb) Toys\nc) Nutrients\n20. How do fruits taste?\na) Salty\nb) Bitter\nc) Sweet or sour\n21. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\n22. What do trees give us?\na) Hot air\nb) Clean air\nc) Dirty air\n23. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are cold\nc) Trees are noise\nLesson 5 – Herbs (Items 24–25)\n24. What can herbs do?\na) Make people laugh\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make cars move\n25. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people',NULL,'[]','16. Why do people like flowers? a) Because they taste sweet b) Because they look bright and lovely c) Because they are loud 17. What do flowers give? a) A loud noise b) A good smell c) A sour taste 18. How do vegetables help us? a) They make us noisy b) They make us strong and healthy c) They make us sleepy 19. What do vegetables give our body? a) Smoke b) Toys c) Nutrients 20. How do fruits taste? a) Salty b) Bitter c) Sweet or sour 21. What do fruits give our body? a) Vitamins b) Sand c) Smoke 22. What do trees give us? a) Hot air b) Clean air c) Dirty air 23. Why do birds live in trees? a) Trees are safe b) Trees are cold c) Trees are noise Lesson 5 – Herbs (Items 24–25) 24. What can herbs do? a) Make people laugh b) Help cure sickness c) Make cars move 25. Who uses herbs? a) Sick people',NULL,10,66,'16. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they taste sweet\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they are loud\n17. What do flowers give?\na) A loud noise\nb) A good smell\nc) A sour taste\n18. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us noisy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us sleepy\n19. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Smoke\nb) Toys\nc) Nutrients\n20. How do fruits taste?\na) Salty\nb) Bitter\nc) Sweet or sour\n21. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\n22. What do trees give us?\na) Hot air\nb) Clean air\nc) Dirty air\n23. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are cold\nc) Trees are noise\nLesson 5 – Herbs (Items 24–25)\n24. What can herbs do?\na) Make people laugh\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make cars move\n25. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people',1,1,'answer'),
(801,200,72,'post',4,'Post-test (Lessons 1–10) · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','b) Robots\nc) Trees\n26. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Whale\nb) Lobster\nc) Horse\n27. Where do these animals live?\na) On land\nb) In the sea\nc) In the sky\n28. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They fly to the sea\nc) They swim\n29. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They fly around flowers\nb) They dig tunnels\nc) They swim\n30. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Pigs and cows\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Deer and monkeys',NULL,'[]','b) Robots c) Trees 26. Which animal helps farmers? a) Whale b) Lobster c) Horse 27. Where do these animals live? a) On land b) In the sea c) In the sky 28. What do some woodland animals do when they see people? a) They hide b) They fly to the sea c) They swim 29. What do animals in the meadow do? a) They fly around flowers b) They dig tunnels c) They swim 30. Which animals swim together in the sea? a) Pigs and cows b) Dolphins and whales c) Deer and monkeys',NULL,10,67,'b) Robots\nc) Trees\n26. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Whale\nb) Lobster\nc) Horse\n27. Where do these animals live?\na) On land\nb) In the sea\nc) In the sky\n28. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They fly to the sea\nc) They swim\n29. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They fly around flowers\nb) They dig tunnels\nc) They swim\n30. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Pigs and cows\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Deer and monkeys',1,1,'answer'),
