b) A large sea\nc) A small body of water\n8. Gold is an example of a:\na) Mineral\nb) Food\nc) Clothing\n9. A truck is helpful for:\na) Flying in the sky\nb) Swimming in the ocean\nc) Carrying heavy goods\n10. Boracay Island is known for its:\na) Tall buildings\nb) White sand beach\nc) Snow\n11. A soap dish is used to:\na) Keep toys\nb) Store soap\nc) Grow plants\n12. We keep our clothes in the:\na) Bookshelf\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Refrigerator\n13. A plateau is:\na) A body of water\nb) A flat land higher than the land around it\nc) A small hill',1,1,'answer'),
(804,201,73,'post',3,'Comprehensive Post-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','14. A funnel helps us:\na) Carry books\nb) Pour liquids easily\nc) Play music\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Rails\nb) Land\nc) Water\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the passages before learner’s answer.\nLesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The\nstove cooks vegetables, and the rice cooker cooks rice. Plates and utensils are for\neating.”\n16. What must we do in the kitchen?\na) Keep it clean\nb) Spill water everywhere\nc) Make it messy\n17. What do we put inside the blender?\na) Plates\nb) Rice\nc) Fruits\nLesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the\nwindows and a bookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do people sit in the living room?\na) Sofa\nb) Table\nc) Bookshelf\nLesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net\nprotects from insects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”',NULL,'[]','14. A funnel helps us: a) Carry books b) Pour liquids easily c) Play music 15. A ship travels on: a) Rails b) Land c) Water PART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION Teacher reads the passages before learner’s answer. Lesson 11 – Kitchen Teacher reads: “In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The stove cooks vegetables, and the rice cooker cooks rice. Plates and utensils are for eating.” 16. What must we do in the kitchen? a) Keep it clean b) Spill water everywhere c) Make it messy 17. What do we put inside the blender? a) Plates b) Rice c) Fruits Lesson 12 – Living Room Teacher reads: “In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the windows and a bookshelf for books.” 18. Where do people sit in the living room? a) Sofa b) Table c) Bookshelf Lesson 13 – Bedroom Teacher reads: “In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net protects from insects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”',NULL,10,70,'14. A funnel helps us:\na) Carry books\nb) Pour liquids easily\nc) Play music\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Rails\nb) Land\nc) Water\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the passages before learner’s answer.\nLesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The\nstove cooks vegetables, and the rice cooker cooks rice. Plates and utensils are for\neating.”\n16. What must we do in the kitchen?\na) Keep it clean\nb) Spill water everywhere\nc) Make it messy\n17. What do we put inside the blender?\na) Plates\nb) Rice\nc) Fruits\nLesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the\nwindows and a bookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do people sit in the living room?\na) Sofa\nb) Table\nc) Bookshelf\nLesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net\nprotects from insects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”',1,1,'answer'),
(805,201,73,'post',4,'Comprehensive Post-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','19. What protects us from insects?\na) Curtain\nb) Blanket\nc) Mosquito net\n20. Where are clothes stored?\na) Floor\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Table\nLesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and\npoured into a bucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What is used to wash the hair?\na) Comb\nb) Shampoo\nc) Soap\n22. What do we step on after taking a bath?\na) Soap dish\nb) Carpet\nc) Bathmat\nLesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer\nhelp fix small parts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What tool lifts the car?\na) Wheel\nb) Hammer\nc) Trolley jack\n24. Which tool fixes screws?\na) Pliers\nb) Screwdriver\nc) Funnel\nLesson 16 – Landforms',NULL,'[]','19. What protects us from insects? a) Curtain b) Blanket c) Mosquito net 20. Where are clothes stored? a) Floor b) Wardrobe c) Table Lesson 14 – Bathroom Teacher reads: “Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and poured into a bucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.” 21. What is used to wash the hair? a) Comb b) Shampoo c) Soap 22. What do we step on after taking a bath? a) Soap dish b) Carpet c) Bathmat Lesson 15 – Garage Teacher reads: “In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer help fix small parts. A trolley jack lifts the car.” 23. What tool lifts the car? a) Wheel b) Hammer c) Trolley jack 24. Which tool fixes screws? a) Pliers b) Screwdriver c) Funnel Lesson 16 – Landforms',NULL,10,71,'19. What protects us from insects?\na) Curtain\nb) Blanket\nc) Mosquito net\n20. Where are clothes stored?\na) Floor\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Table\nLesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and\npoured into a bucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What is used to wash the hair?\na) Comb\nb) Shampoo\nc) Soap\n22. What do we step on after taking a bath?\na) Soap dish\nb) Carpet\nc) Bathmat\nLesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer\nhelp fix small parts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What tool lifts the car?\na) Wheel\nb) Hammer\nc) Trolley jack\n24. Which tool fixes screws?\na) Pliers\nb) Screwdriver\nc) Funnel\nLesson 16 – Landforms',1,1,'answer'),
(806,201,73,'post',5,'Comprehensive Post-test (Lessons 11–20) · page 5','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Teacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide\nand flat. A shoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. Which landform is tall?\na) Basin\nb) Hill\nc) Mountain\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Glacier\nb) Shoreline\nc) Desert\nLesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are\nnice to see. Keep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) River and spring\nb) Lake and pond\nc) Ocean and sea\n28. What should be kept clean?\na) Cars\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Land\nLesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Treasure\nb) Houses\nc) Toys\n30. Which mineral is mentioned in the poem?\na) Wood\nb) Gold\nc) Plastic',NULL,'[]','Teacher reads: “A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide and flat. A shoreline is where land meets water.” 25. Which landform is tall? a) Basin b) Hill c) Mountain 26. Where does land meet water? a) Glacier b) Shoreline c) Desert Lesson 17 – Bodies of Water Teacher reads: “The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean.” 27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”? a) River and spring b) Lake and pond c) Ocean and sea 28. What should be kept clean? a) Cars b) Ocean and sea c) Land Lesson 18 – Mineral Resources Teacher reads the poem. 29. What is Earth rich in? a) Treasure b) Houses c) Toys 30. Which mineral is mentioned in the poem? a) Wood b) Gold c) Plastic',NULL,10,72,'Teacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide\nand flat. A shoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. Which landform is tall?\na) Basin\nb) Hill\nc) Mountain\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Glacier\nb) Shoreline\nc) Desert\nLesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are\nnice to see. Keep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) River and spring\nb) Lake and pond\nc) Ocean and sea\n28. What should be kept clean?\na) Cars\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Land\nLesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Treasure\nb) Houses\nc) Toys\n30. Which mineral is mentioned in the poem?\na) Wood\nb) Gold\nc) Plastic',1,1,'answer'),
(807,202,74,'pre',1,'Pre-test · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','SET A\nPRE-TEST Day 1-10 grade 9 to 10\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write its\nletter on the line.\nSection 1: Reading Comprehension\n______ 1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n______ 2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n______ 3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n______ 4. Where did the magical treehouse take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n______ 5. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n______ 6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house',NULL,'[]','SET A PRE-TEST Day 1-10 grade 9 to 10 Instructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write its letter on the line. Section 1: Reading Comprehension blank 1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack? a) her homework b) her lunchbox c) her pencil d) her book blank 2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox? a) in the classroom b) in the cafeteria c) in the library d) on the bus blank 3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox? a) a book about animals b) a book about space c) a book about archaeology d) a book about dinosaurs blank 4. Where did the magical treehouse take Jack and Annie? a) to the desert b) to the mountains c) to a tropical rainforest d) to the beach blank 5. What did they hear in the rainforest? a) lions roaring b) monkeys chattering c) wolves howling d) elephants trumpeting blank 6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live? a) city b) habitat c) school d) house',NULL,10,6,'SET A\nPRE-TEST Day 1-10 grade 9 to 10\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write its\nletter on the line.\nSection 1: Reading Comprehension\n______ 1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n______ 2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n______ 3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n______ 4. Where did the magical treehouse take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n______ 5. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n______ 6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house',1,1,'answer'),
(808,202,74,'pre',2,'Pre-test · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','______ 7. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n______ 8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n______ 9. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n______ 10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n______ 11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n______ 12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\n______ 13. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n______ 14. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals',NULL,'[]','blank 7. What did Emily love to do? a) sing songs b) invent new things c) play sports d) read books blank 8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with? a) toys, games, and puzzles b) tools, wires, and gadgets c) books, pencils, and paper d) clothes, shoes, and hats blank 9. What did Emily call her robot? a) Rob Friend b) Handy Helper c) Super Cleaner d) Dust Buster blank 10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on? a) the Santa Maria b) the Mayflower c) the Nina d) the Pinta blank 11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food? a) the British b) the French c) the Spanish d) the Native Americans blank 12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest? a) Christmas b) Easter c) Thanksgiving d) Halloween blank 13. What blew the little seed far away? a) the sun b) the rain c) the wind d) the snow blank 14. What did the seed sprout? a) leaves and branches b) roots and a tiny stem c) fruit and vegetables d) flowers and petals',NULL,10,7,'______ 7. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n______ 8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n______ 9. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n______ 10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n______ 11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n______ 12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\n______ 13. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n______ 14. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals',1,1,'answer'),
(809,202,74,'pre',3,'Pre-test · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','______ 15. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n______ 16. Who was talking to each other in \"Summer Fun\"?\na. Lita and Lito\nb. Lina and Lino\nc. Lina and Leo\n______ 17. What were they talking about?\na. what to do during the summer\nb. what to have during the summer\nc. what to wear during the summer\n______ 18. The children in the story could be ______\na. brother and sister\nb. neighbors\nc. cousins\n______ 19. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na. pick flowers\nb. pick star apples\nc. go swimming\n______ 20. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na. doing something in the summer\nb. doing something in the house\nc. doing something that we like\n______ 21. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na. picking flowers\nb. cleaning up\nc. swimming\n______ 22. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain',NULL,'[]','blank 15. What did the bees collect from the flower? a) pollen b) nectar c) seeds d) water blank 16. Who was talking to each other in \"Summer Fun\"? a. Lita and Lito b. Lina and Lino c. Lina and Leo blank 17. What were they talking about? a. what to do during the summer b. what to have during the summer c. what to wear during the summer blank 18. The children in the story could be blank a. brother and sister b. neighbors c. cousins blank 19. Which of these will they do if they are hungry? a. pick flowers b. pick star apples c. go swimming blank 20. Doing something \"fun\" means blank . a. doing something in the summer b. doing something in the house c. doing something that we like blank 21. Which of these is the best example of being helpful? a. picking flowers b. cleaning up c. swimming blank 22. What is it that Nina does not like? a. playing tag b. playing house c. getting wet in the rain',NULL,10,8,'______ 15. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n______ 16. Who was talking to each other in \"Summer Fun\"?\na. Lita and Lito\nb. Lina and Lino\nc. Lina and Leo\n______ 17. What were they talking about?\na. what to do during the summer\nb. what to have during the summer\nc. what to wear during the summer\n______ 18. The children in the story could be ______\na. brother and sister\nb. neighbors\nc. cousins\n______ 19. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na. pick flowers\nb. pick star apples\nc. go swimming\n______ 20. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na. doing something in the summer\nb. doing something in the house\nc. doing something that we like\n______ 21. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na. picking flowers\nb. cleaning up\nc. swimming\n______ 22. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain',1,1,'answer'),
