(814,202,74,'pre',9,'Pre-test · page 8','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','SET B\nPRE-TEST Day 11-20 Grade 3-4\nInstructions: Read each question carefully and choose the best answer. Encircle the\nletter of your choice.\nVocabulary\n1. What is the best definition for coax?\na. to force someone\nb. to persuade gently\nc. to ignore someone\nd. to argue with someone\n2. If someone is distrustful, they are:\na. Very confident\nb. Lacking trust\nc. Extremely happy\nd. Easily persuaded\n3. The word despise most nearly means:\na. To admire greatly\nb. To dislike very much\nc. To feel sorry for\nd. To be jealous of\n4. A person who is arrogant:\na. Thinks they are better than others\nb. Is very shy and quiet\nc. Is kind to everyone\nd. Works very hard\n5. To apologize means to:\na. Express regret for a mistake\nb. Celebrate a victory\nc. Make a formal promise\nd. Give someone a gift\nGrammar and Writing\n6. Which sentence is punctuated correctly?\na. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice.\"',NULL,'[]','SET B PRE-TEST Day 11-20 Grade 3-4 Instructions: Read each question carefully and choose the best answer. Encircle the letter of your choice. Vocabulary 1. What is the best definition for coax? a. to force someone b. to persuade gently c. to ignore someone d. to argue with someone 2. If someone is distrustful, they are: a. Very confident b. Lacking trust c. Extremely happy d. Easily persuaded 3. The word despise most nearly means: a. To admire greatly b. To dislike very much c. To feel sorry for d. To be jealous of 4. A person who is arrogant: a. Thinks they are better than others b. Is very shy and quiet c. Is kind to everyone d. Works very hard 5. To apologize means to: a. Express regret for a mistake b. Celebrate a victory c. Make a formal promise d. Give someone a gift Grammar and Writing 6. Which sentence is punctuated correctly? a. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice.\"',NULL,10,14,'SET B\nPRE-TEST Day 11-20 Grade 3-4\nInstructions: Read each question carefully and choose the best answer. Encircle the\nletter of your choice.\nVocabulary\n1. What is the best definition for coax?\na. to force someone\nb. to persuade gently\nc. to ignore someone\nd. to argue with someone\n2. If someone is distrustful, they are:\na. Very confident\nb. Lacking trust\nc. Extremely happy\nd. Easily persuaded\n3. The word despise most nearly means:\na. To admire greatly\nb. To dislike very much\nc. To feel sorry for\nd. To be jealous of\n4. A person who is arrogant:\na. Thinks they are better than others\nb. Is very shy and quiet\nc. Is kind to everyone\nd. Works very hard\n5. To apologize means to:\na. Express regret for a mistake\nb. Celebrate a victory\nc. Make a formal promise\nd. Give someone a gift\nGrammar and Writing\n6. Which sentence is punctuated correctly?\na. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice.\"',1,1,'answer'),
(815,202,74,'pre',10,'Pre-test · page 9','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','b. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nc. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nd. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice\".\n7. What is the simple predicate (verb) in this sentence: \"The greedy lion chased the\ndeer.\"\na. The greedy lion\nb. chased\nc. the deer\nd. chased the deer\n8. Which word is an antonym for sincerity?\na. Honesty\nb. Dishonesty\nc. Friendship\nd. Kindness\n9. What part of speech is the word huge in this sentence: \"The elephant had a huge\nbody.\"?\na. Noun\nb. Verb\nc. Adjective\nd. Adverb\n10. Which sentence is written in the future tense?\na. The farmer calls his sons.\nb. The farmer called his sons.\nc. The farmer is calling his sons.\nd. The farmer will call his sons.\nReading Comprehension\nRead the short passage and answer questions 11-13.\n\"The ants were angry at the elephant for spraying them with water. They decided to\nteach him a lesson. They crept into his ears and started biting him. The elephant\ncried and apologized, learning never to trouble others again.\"\n11. Why were the ants angry?\na. The elephant stepped on their home.\nb. The elephant sprayed them with water.\nc. The elephant ate their food.\nd. The elephant ignored them.\n12. How did the ants teach the elephant a lesson?\na. They told the other animals.\nb. They bit him inside his ears.\nc. They stole his food.\nd. They sprayed him with water.',NULL,'[]','b. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\" c. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\" d. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice\". 7. What is the simple predicate (verb) in this sentence: \"The greedy lion chased the deer.\" a. The greedy lion b. chased c. the deer d. chased the deer 8. Which word is an antonym for sincerity? a. Honesty b. Dishonesty c. Friendship d. Kindness 9. What part of speech is the word huge in this sentence: \"The elephant had a huge body.\"? a. Noun b. Verb c. Adjective d. Adverb 10. Which sentence is written in the future tense? a. The farmer calls his sons. b. The farmer called his sons. c. The farmer is calling his sons. d. The farmer will call his sons. Reading Comprehension Read the short passage and answer questions 11-13. \"The ants were angry at the elephant for spraying them with water. They decided to teach him a lesson. They crept into his ears and started biting him. The elephant cried and apologized, learning never to trouble others again.\" 11. Why were the ants angry? a. The elephant stepped on their home. b. The elephant sprayed them with water. c. The elephant ate their food. d. The elephant ignored them. 12. How did the ants teach the elephant a lesson? a. They told the other animals. b. They bit him inside his ears. c. They stole his food. d. They sprayed him with water.',NULL,10,15,'b. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nc. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nd. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice\".\n7. What is the simple predicate (verb) in this sentence: \"The greedy lion chased the\ndeer.\"\na. The greedy lion\nb. chased\nc. the deer\nd. chased the deer\n8. Which word is an antonym for sincerity?\na. Honesty\nb. Dishonesty\nc. Friendship\nd. Kindness\n9. What part of speech is the word huge in this sentence: \"The elephant had a huge\nbody.\"?\na. Noun\nb. Verb\nc. Adjective\nd. Adverb\n10. Which sentence is written in the future tense?\na. The farmer calls his sons.\nb. The farmer called his sons.\nc. The farmer is calling his sons.\nd. The farmer will call his sons.\nReading Comprehension\nRead the short passage and answer questions 11-13.\n\"The ants were angry at the elephant for spraying them with water. They decided to\nteach him a lesson. They crept into his ears and started biting him. The elephant\ncried and apologized, learning never to trouble others again.\"\n11. Why were the ants angry?\na. The elephant stepped on their home.\nb. The elephant sprayed them with water.\nc. The elephant ate their food.\nd. The elephant ignored them.\n12. How did the ants teach the elephant a lesson?\na. They told the other animals.\nb. They bit him inside his ears.\nc. They stole his food.\nd. They sprayed him with water.',1,1,'answer'),
(816,202,74,'pre',11,'Pre-test · page 10','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','13. What was the result of the ants\' action?\na. The elephant became angrier.\nb. The elephant never troubled anyone again.\nc. The elephant chased the ants away.\nd. The elephant became friends with the ants.\nLiterary Concepts\n14. The central lesson or message of a story is called the:\na. Plot\nb. Moral\nc. Setting\nd. Conflict\n15. The main problem that characters face in a story is the:\na. Solution\nb. Climax\nc. Conflict\nd. Theme\n16. \"The wind whispered through the trees\" is an example of:\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole\n17. A story that uses animals as characters to teach a lesson is called a:\na. Biography\nb. Fable\nc. Mystery\nd. Fantasy\n18. The high point or most exciting part of a story is the:\na. Exposition\nb. Rising Action\nc. Climax\nd. Falling Action\nGeneral Knowledge & Inference\n19. What is the primary purpose of a fable?\na. To explain historical events\nb. To teach a moral lesson\nc. To describe a scientific process\nd. To tell a funny story with no lesson\n20. If a character is described as \"cunning,\" they are most likely to be:\na. Honest and kind\nb. Shy and quiet',NULL,'[]','13. What was the result of the ants\' action? a. The elephant became angrier. b. The elephant never troubled anyone again. c. The elephant chased the ants away. d. The elephant became friends with the ants. Literary Concepts 14. The central lesson or message of a story is called the: a. Plot b. Moral c. Setting d. Conflict 15. The main problem that characters face in a story is the: a. Solution b. Climax c. Conflict d. Theme 16. \"The wind whispered through the trees\" is an example of: a. Simile b. Metaphor c. Personification d. Hyperbole 17. A story that uses animals as characters to teach a lesson is called a: a. Biography b. Fable c. Mystery d. Fantasy 18. The high point or most exci