(817,202,74,'pre',12,'Pre-test · page 11','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','c. Clever and tricky\nd. Strong and brave\n21. What is the best source to find a synonym for the word \"huge\"?\na. A dictionary\nb. A thesaurus\nc. An encyclopedia\nd. An atlas\n22. What is the term for the feeling of sadness or pity you feel for a character?\na. Empathy\nb. Sympathy\nc. Anger\nd. Joy\n23. Which of these is a complete sentence?\na. The old tortoise slowly.\nb. Challenged the hare for a race.\nc. The hare ran very fast.\nd. Under the tree for some time.\n24. What do we call the narrator of a story who is also a character in the story?\na. First-person narrator\nb. Second-person narrator\nc. Third-person narrator\nd. Omniscient narrator\n25. What is the term for a word that means the opposite of another word?\na. Synonym\nb. Antonym\nc. Homophone\nd. Homonym\nContinuing with more general items...\n26. What is the opposite meaning of the word victory?\na. Success\nb. Defeat\nc. Contest\nd. Race\n27. Which word is a noun?\na. Run\nb. Beautiful\nc. Peace\nd. Quickly\n28. The phrase \"as slow as a tortoise\" is an example of a:\na. Metaphor\nb. Simile\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole',NULL,'[]','c. Clever and tricky d. Strong and brave 21. What is the best source to find a synonym for the word \"huge\"? a. A dictionary b. A thesaurus c. An encyclopedia d. An atlas 22. What is the term for the feeling of sadness or pity you feel for a character? a. Empathy b. Sympathy c. Anger d. Joy 23. Which of these is a complete sentence? a. The old tortoise slowly. b. Challenged the hare for a race. c. The hare ran very fast. d. Under the tree for some time. 24. What do we call the narrator of a story who is also a character in the story? a. First-person narrator b. Second-person narrator c. Third-person narrator d. Omniscient narrator 25. What is the term for a word that means the opposite of another word? a. Synonym b.