(819,202,74,'pre',14,'Pre-test · page 13','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','37. Which word best describes the fox in \"The Fox and the Crow\"?\na. Honest\nb. Generous\nc. Cunning\nd. Brave\n38. What is the best way to identify the moral of a fable?\na. Look at the title.\nb. Find the lesson the characters learn.\nc. Identify the main character.\nd. Count the number of animals.\n39. \"He was a lion in battle.\" This is an example of a:\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Onomatopoeia\n40. Which word is a verb?\na. Decision\nb. Decisive\nc. Decide\nd. Decisively\n41. What is the term for an exaggerated statement used for effect?\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole\n42. Which of these is a compound word?\na. Therefore\nb. Sunshine\nc. Elephant\nd. Together\n43. What is the primary purpose of narrative writing?\na. To convince the reader\nb. To tell a story\nc. to explain how to do something\nd. To describe a person or place\n44. Which sentence is an opinion?\na. The hare lost the race.\nb. The tortoise has a shell.\nc. The hare is the fastest animal.\nd. The race was to the riverbank.\n45. What is the term for the feelings and ideas associated with a word (beyond its\ndictionary definition)?\na. Denotation\nb. Connotation\nc. Definition\nd. Pronunciation',NULL,'[]','37. Which word best describes the fox in \"The Fox and the Crow\"? a. Honest b. Generous c. Cunning d. Brave 38. What is the best way to identify the moral of a fable? a. Look at the title. b. Find the lesson the characters learn. c. Identify the main character. d. Count the number of animals. 39. \"He was a lion in battle.\" This is an example of a: a. Simile b. Metaphor c. Personification d. Onomatopoeia 40. Which word is a verb? a. Decision b. Decisive c. Decide d. Decisively 41. What is the term for an exaggerated statement used for effect? a. Simile b. Metaphor c. Personification d. Hyperbole 42. W