(820,202,74,'pre',15,'Pre-test · page 14','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','46. What do you call the perspective from which a story is told?\na. Plot\nb. Setting\nc. Point of View\nd. Theme\n47. Which of these is a proper noun?\na. jungle\nb. farmer\nc. Birbal\nd. son\n48. What is the best way to understand a character\'s traits?\na. Look only at their name.\nb. See what they say, do, and what others say about them.\nc. Focus only on the story\'s setting.\nd. Read the first paragraph only.\n49. What is the name for a word that describes a verb (e.g., slowly, quickly)?\na. Adjective\nb. Adverb\nc. Noun\nd. Preposition\n50. The final part of a story where the conflict is resolved is called the:\na. Climax\nb. Rising Action\nc. Resolution\nd. Introduction\nPRE-TEST ANSWER KEY\n1.B\n11.B\n21.B\n31.B\n41.D\n2. B\n12.B\n22.B\n32.B\n42.B\n3. B\n13.B\n23.C\n33.B\n43.B\n4. A\n14.B\n24.A\n34.C\n44.C\n5. A\n15.C\n25.B\n35.C\n45.B\n6. B\n16.C\n26.B\n36.B\n46.C\n7. B\n17.B\n27.C\n37.C\n47.C\n8. B\n18.C\n28.B\n38.B\n48.B\n9. C\n19.B\n29.B\n39.B\n49.B\n10. D\n20.C\n30.B\n40.C\n50.C',NULL,'[]','46. What do you call the perspective from which a story is told? a. Plot b. Setting c. Point of View d. Theme 47. Which of these is a proper noun? a. jungle b. farmer c. Birbal d. son 48. What is the best way to understand a character\'s traits? a. Look only at their name. b. See what they say, do, and what others say about them. c. Focus only on the story\'s setting. d. Read the first paragraph only. 49. What is the name for a word that describes a verb (e.g., slowly, quickly)? a. Adjective b. Adverb c. Noun d. Preposition 50. The final part of a story where the conflict is resolved is called the: a. Climax b. Rising Action c. Resolution d. Introduction PRE-TEST ANSWER KEY 1.B 11.B 21.B 31.B 41.D 2. B 12.B 22.B 32.B 42.B 3. B 13.B 23.C 33.B 43.B 4. A 14.B 24.A 34.C 44.C 5. A 15.C 25.B 35.C 45.B 6. B 16.C 26.B 36.B 46.C 