(821,203,NULL,'learn',1,'The Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','GRADE 3 Intervention Activities\nActivity 1:\n\"The Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox\"\nSarah opened her backpack, but her lunchbox was gone! She looked\neverywhere. \"Where could it be?\" she wondered. She asked\nher friends, but no one had seen it. Suddenly, she remembered\nleaving it in the library after reading a book\nabout archaeology. She raced to the library and found it right where she left it.\nQuestions:\n1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs','assets/images/level5/g3/p022-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p022-1.webp\"]','GRADE 3 Intervention Activities Activity 1: \"The Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox\" Sarah opened her backpack, but her lunchbox was gone! She looked everywhere. \"Where could it be?\" she wondered. She asked her friends, but no one had seen it. Suddenly, she remembered leaving it in the library after reading a book about archaeology. She raced to the library and found it right where she left it. Questions: 1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack? a) her homework b) her lunchbox c) her pencil d) her book 2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox? a) in the classroom b) in the cafeteria c) in the library d) on the bus 3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox? a) a book about animals b) a book about space c) a book about archaeology d) a book about dinosaurs',NULL,10,22,'GRADE 3 Intervention Activities\nActivity 1:\n\"The Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox\"\nSarah opened her backpack, but her lunchbox was gone! She looked\neverywhere. \"Where could it be?\" she wondered. She asked\nher friends, but no one had seen it. Suddenly, she remembered\nleaving it in the library after reading a book\nabout archaeology. She raced to the library and found it right where she left it.\nQuestions:\n1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs',1,1,'answer'),
(822,204,NULL,'learn',1,'The Magical Tree House Adventure · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 2:\n\"The Magical Tree house Adventure\"\nJack and Annie climbed into their magical tree house. Today, the tree\nhouse took them to a tropical rainforest.\nThey saw colorful birds, heard monkeys\nchattering,\nand\ndiscovered\na\nhidden\nwaterfall. They learned about different\ntypes of plants and animals that live in the\nrainforest habitat.\nQuestions:\n1. Where did the magical tree house take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n2. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n3. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house','assets/images/level5/g3/p023-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p023-1.webp\"]','Activity 2: \"The Magical Tree house Adventure\" Jack and Annie climbed into their magical tree house. Today, the tree house took them to a tropical rainforest. They saw colorful birds, heard monkeys chattering, and discovered a hidden waterfall. They learned about different types of plants and animals that live in the rainforest habitat. Questions: 1. Where did the magical tree house take Jack and Annie? a) to the desert b) to the mountains c) to a tropical rainforest d) to the beach 2. What did they hear in the rainforest? a) lions roaring b) monkeys chattering c) wolves howling d) elephants trumpeting 3. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live? a) city b) habitat c) school d) house',NULL,10,23,'Activity 2:\n\"The Magical Tree house Adventure\"\nJack and Annie climbed into their magical tree house. Today, the tree\nhouse took them to a tropical rainforest.\nThey saw colorful birds, heard monkeys\nchattering,\nand\ndiscovered\na\nhidden\nwaterfall. They learned about different\ntypes of plants and animals that live in the\nrainforest habitat.\nQuestions:\n1. Where did the magical tree house take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n2. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n3. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house',1,1,'answer'),
(823,205,NULL,'learn',1,'The Inventor\'s Workshop · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 3:\n\"The Inventor\'s Workshop\"\nEmily loved inventing new things. Her workshop was filled\nwith tools, wires, and gadgets. One day, she decided to\nbuild a robot that could help her with her chores. After\nmany\nattempts, she finally created a robot that could sweep, dust, and even make her\nbed. She called it \"Handy Helper.\"\nQuestions:\n1. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n2. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n3. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster','assets/images/level5/g3/p024-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p024-1.webp\"]','Activity 3: \"The Inventor\'s Workshop\" Emily loved inventing new things. Her workshop was filled with tools, wires, and gadgets. One day, she decided to build a robot that could help her with her chores. After many attempts, she finally created a robot that could sweep, dust, and even make her bed. She called it \"Handy Helper.\" Questions: 1. What did Emily love to do? a) sing songs b) invent new things c) play sports d) read books 2. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with? a) toys, games, and puzzles b) tools, wires, and gadgets c) books, pencils, and paper d) clothes, shoes, and hats 3. What did Emily call her robot? a) Rob Friend b) Handy Helper c) Super Cleaner d) Dust Buster',NULL,10,24,'Activity 3:\n\"The Inventor\'s Workshop\"\nEmily loved inventing new things. Her workshop was filled\nwith tools, wires, and gadgets. One day, she decided to\nbuild a robot that could help her with her chores. After\nmany\nattempts, she finally created a robot that could sweep, dust, and even make her\nbed. She called it \"Handy Helper.\"\nQuestions:\n1. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n2. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n3. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster',1,1,'answer'),
(824,206,NULL,'learn',1,'The Story of the First Thanksgiving · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 4:\n“The Story of the First Thanksgiving”\nLong ago, the Pilgrims came to America on a ship called the Mayflower. They\nhad a difficult time finding food. The Native Americans, like the\nWampanoag tribe, helped them learn how to grow corn\nand other crops. The next year, they had a big feast to\ncelebrate their harvest. This feast is now known as\nThanksgiving.\nVocabulary Focus: Pilgrims, Mayflower, harvest, crops, tribe\nARAL Connection: Social studies vocabulary and understanding historical events.\nQuestions:\n1. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n2. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n4. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween','assets/images/level5/g3/p025-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p025-1.webp\"]','Activity 4: “The Story of the First Thanksgiving” Long ago, the Pilgrims came to America on a ship called the Mayflower. They had a difficult time finding food. The Native Americans, like the Wampanoag tribe, helped them learn how to grow corn and other crops. The next year, they had a big feast to celebrate their harvest. This feast is now known as Thanksgiving. Vocabulary Focus: Pilgrims, Mayflower, harvest, crops, tribe ARAL Connection: Social studies vocabulary and understanding historical events. Questions: 1. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on? a) the Santa Maria b) the Mayflower c) the Nina d) the Pinta 2. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food? a) the British b) the French c) the Spanish d) the Native Americans 4. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest? a) Christmas b) Easter c) Thanksgiving d) Halloween',NULL,10,25,'Activity 4:\n“The Story of the First Thanksgiving”\nLong ago, the Pilgrims came to America on a ship called the Mayflower. They\nhad a difficult time finding food. The Native Americans, like the\nWampanoag tribe, helped them learn how to grow corn\nand other crops. The next year, they had a big feast to\ncelebrate their harvest. This feast is now known as\nThanksgiving.\nVocabulary Focus: Pilgrims, Mayflower, harvest, crops, tribe\nARAL Connection: Social studies vocabulary and understanding historical events.\nQuestions:\n1. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n2. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n4. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween',1,1,'answer'),
(825,207,NULL,'learn',1,'The Little Seed\'s Journey · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 5:\n\"The Little Seed\'s Journey\"\nOnce upon a time, there was a little seed. The wind blew it far away from its\nparent plant. The seed landed in a field. Rain fell, and\nthe seed began to grow. It sprouted roots and a tiny\nstem.\nSoon, it became a beautiful flower. Bees came to collect\nnectar from the flower, helping it make more seeds.\nVocabulary Focus: parent, nectar, sprouted, stem, journey\nARAL Connection: Science-related vocabulary and understanding plant life cycles.\nQuestions:\n1. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n2. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n3. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water','assets/images/level5/g3/p026-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p026-1.webp\"]','Activity 5: \"The Little Seed\'s Journey\" Once upon a time, there was a little seed. The wind blew it far away from its parent plant. The seed landed in a field. Rain fell, and the seed began to grow. It sprouted roots and a tiny stem. Soon, it became a beautiful flower. Bees came to collect nectar from the flower, helping it make more seeds. Vocabulary Focus: parent, nectar, sprouted, stem, journey ARAL Connection: Science-related vocabulary and understanding plant life cycles. Questions: 1. What blew the little seed far away? a) the sun b) the rain c) the wind d) the snow 2. What did the seed sprout? a) leaves and branches b) roots and a tiny stem c) fruit and vegetables d) flowers and petals 3. What did the bees collect from the flower? a) pollen b) nectar c) seeds d) water',NULL,10,26,'Activity 5:\n\"The Little Seed\'s Journey\"\nOnce upon a time, there was a little seed. The wind blew it far away from its\nparent plant. The seed landed in a field. Rain fell, and\nthe seed began to grow. It sprouted roots and a tiny\nstem.\nSoon, it became a beautiful flower. Bees came to collect\nnectar from the flower, helping it make more seeds.\nVocabulary Focus: parent, nectar, sprouted, stem, journey\nARAL Connection: Science-related vocabulary and understanding plant life cycles.\nQuestions:\n1. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n2. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n3. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water',1,1,'answer'),
(826,208,NULL,'learn',1,'Summer Fun · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity\n6: SET A\nSUMMER FUN\n“Let’s have some\nfun this summer,”\nsays Leo. “Let’s\nswim in the river,”\nsays Lina.\n“Let’s get some star\napples from the\ntree,” says Leo.\n“Let’s pick flowers,”\nsays Lina.\n“That is so much\nfun!” says Mama.\n“But can you help\nme dust the\nshelves too?”\n“Yes, we can\nMama,” they say.\n“Helping can be\nfun too!”\nQuestions\n1. Who were talking to each other?\na. Lita and Lito\nb. Lina and Lino\nc. Lina and Leo\n2. What were they talking about?\na. what to do during the summer\nb. what to have during the summer\nc. what to wear during the summer\n3. The children in the story could be ______\na. brother and sister\nb. neighbors\nc. cousins\n4. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na. pick flowers\nb. pick star apples\nc. go swimming\n5. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na. doing something in the summer','assets/images/level5/g3/p027-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p027-1.webp\"]','Activity 6: SET A SUMMER FUN “Let’s have some fun this summer,” says Leo. “Let’s swim in the river,” says Lina. “Let’s get some star apples from the tree,” says Leo. “Let’s pick flowers,” says Lina. “That is so much fun!” says Mama. “But can you help me dust the shelves too?” “Yes, we can Mama,” they say. “Helping can be fun too!” Questions 1. Who were talking to each other? a. Lita and Lito b. Lina and Lino c. Lina and Leo 2. What were they talking about? a. what to do during the summer b. what to have during the summer c. what to wear during the summer 3. The children in the story could be blank a. brother and sister b. neighbors c. cousins 4. Which of these will they do if they are hungry? a. pick flowers b. pick star apples c. go swimming 5. Doing something \"fun\" means blank . a. doing something in the summer',NULL,10,27,'Activity\n6: SET A\nSUMMER FUN\n“Let’s have some\nfun this summer,”\nsays Leo. “Let’s\nswim in the river,”\nsays Lina.\n“Let’s get some star\napples from the\ntree,” says Leo.\n“Let’s pick flowers,”\nsays Lina.\n“That is so much\nfun!” says Mama.\n“But can you help\nme dust the\nshelves too?”\n“Yes, we can\nMama,” they say.\n“Helping can be\nfun too!”\nQuestions\n1. Who were talking to each other?\na. Lita and Lito\nb. Lina and Lino\nc. Lina and Leo\n2. What were they talking about?\na. what to do during the summer\nb. what to have during the summer\nc. what to wear during the summer\n3. The children in the story could be ______\na. brother and sister\nb. neighbors\nc. cousins\n4. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na. pick flowers\nb. pick star apples\nc. go swimming\n5. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na. doing something in the summer',1,1,'answer'),
(827,208,NULL,'learn',2,'Summer Fun · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','b. doing something in the house\nc. doing something that we like\n6. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na. picking flowers\nb. cleaning up\nc. swimming',NULL,'[]','b. doing something in the house c. doing something that we like 6. Which of these is the best example of being helpful? a. picking flowers b. cleaning up c. swimming',NULL,10,28,'b. doing something in the house\nc. doing something that we like\n6. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na. picking flowers\nb. cleaning up\nc. swimming',1,1,'answer'),
(828,209,NULL,'learn',1,'A Rainy Day · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 7:\nSET B\nA RAINY DAY\nNina and Ria are looking out the window.\n“I do not like getting wet in the rain,” says Nina.\n“What can we do?” asks Ria.\n“We can play house,” says Nina.\n“Or we can play tag,” says Ria.\n“Okay, let’s play tag. You’re it!” says Nina.\nNina runs from Ria and bumps a lamp.\n“Oh no!” says Nina.\n“We must not play tag in the house.”\nQuestions\n1. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain\n2. What does Nina want to do?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. gets wet in the rain\n3. Who wants to play tag?\na. Ria\nb. Nina\nc. Ria and Nina\n4. What is \"tag?\"\na. a card game\nb. a video game\nc. a running game\n5. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na. Something might break\nb. Someone might get tired\nc. Something might get lost\n6. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na. careless\nb. careful\nc. curious','assets/images/level5/g3/p029-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p029-1.webp\"]','Activity 7: SET B A RAINY DAY Nina and Ria are looking out the window. “I do not like getting wet in the rain,” says Nina. “What can we do?” asks Ria. “We can play house,” says Nina. “Or we can play tag,” says Ria. “Okay, let’s play tag. You’re it!” says Nina. Nina runs from Ria and bumps a lamp. “Oh no!” says Nina. “We must not play tag in the house.” Questions 1. What is it that Nina does not like? a. playing tag b. playing house c. getting wet in the rain 2. What does Nina want to do? a. playing tag b. playing house c. gets wet in the rain 3. Who wants to play tag? a. Ria b. Nina c. Ria and Nina 4. What is \"tag?\" a. a card game b. a video game c. a running game 5. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house? a. Something might break b. Someone might get tired c. Something might get lost 6. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be? a. careless b. careful c. curious',NULL,10,29,'Activity 7:\nSET B\nA RAINY DAY\nNina and Ria are looking out the window.\n“I do not like getting wet in the rain,” says Nina.\n“What can we do?” asks Ria.\n“We can play house,” says Nina.\n“Or we can play tag,” says Ria.\n“Okay, let’s play tag. You’re it!” says Nina.\nNina runs from Ria and bumps a lamp.\n“Oh no!” says Nina.\n“We must not play tag in the house.”\nQuestions\n1. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain\n2. What does Nina want to do?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. gets wet in the rain\n3. Who wants to play tag?\na. Ria\nb. Nina\nc. Ria and Nina\n4. What is \"tag?\"\na. a card game\nb. a video game\nc. a running game\n5. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na. Something might break\nb. Someone might get tired\nc. Something might get lost\n6. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na. careless\nb. careful\nc. curious',1,1,'answer'),
(829,210,NULL,'learn',1,'A Gift from Uncle · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity\n9: Set B\nA GIFT FROM UNCLE\nDo you have an uncle living far away?\nMiriam has. His name is Max. Miriam calls him\nUncle Max. He lives in New York.\nLast Christmas, Uncle Max sent Miriam a gift. It\ncame in a big heavy box. Father helped open the\nbox.\nThen they saw something very pretty. It was a big doll. It had round\nblue eyes and a small red mouth. It had a blue lace dress and curly black\nhair. Miriam called it Curly. She loved to play with it. What Miriam liked\nbest was the way Curly walked. Miriam would hold one of its hands and\nthey would walk together around the living room. Curly made Miriam\nhappy.\n1. Who was Curly?\na. a dog\nb. a doll\nc. a cat\n2. Who gave Curly to Miriam?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n3. Where does Uncle Max live?\na. Cebu\nb. Manila\nc. New York\n4. On what occasion was Curly given?\na. birthday\nb. Christmas c. graduation\n5. Who helped Miriam open the box?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n6. What words talk about the box?\na. big and light\nb. big and heavy\nc. small and light\n7. What words talk about Curly’s mouth?\na. red\nb. pink\nc. yellow\n8. What was Curly’s dress made of?\na. silk\nb. lace\nc. cotton\n9. What word talks about her hair?\na. curly\nb. brown\nc. straight\n10. What can Curly do?\na. talk\nb. sing c. walk','assets/images/level5/g3/p030-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p030-1.webp\"]','Activity 9: Set B A GIFT FROM UNCLE Do you have an uncle living far away? Miriam has. His name is Max. Miriam calls him Uncle Max. He lives in New York. Last Christmas, Uncle Max sent Miriam a gift. It came in a big heavy box. Father helped open the box. Then they saw something very pretty. It was a big doll. It had round blue eyes and a small red mouth. It had a blue lace dress and curly black hair. Miriam called it Curly. She loved to play with it. What Miriam liked best was the way Curly walked. Miriam would hold one of its hands and they would walk together around the living room. Curly made Miriam happy. 1. Who was Curly? a. a dog b. a doll c. a cat 2. Who gave Curly to Miriam? a. Father b. Mother c. Uncle Max 3. Where does Uncle Max live? a. Cebu b. Manila c. New York 4. On what occasion was Curly given? a. birthday b. Christmas c. graduation 5. Who helped Miriam open the box? a. Father b. Mother c. Uncle Max 6. What words talk about the box? a. big and light b. big and heavy c. small and light 7. What words talk about Curly’s mouth? a. red b. pink c. yellow 8. What was Curly’s dress made of? a. silk b. lace c. cotton 9. What word talks about her hair? a. curly b. brown c. straight 10. What can Curly do? a. talk b. sing c. walk',NULL,10,30,'Activity\n9: Set B\nA GIFT FROM UNCLE\nDo you have an uncle living far away?\nMiriam has. His name is Max. Miriam calls him\nUncle Max. He lives in New York.\nLast Christmas, Uncle Max sent Miriam a gift. It\ncame in a big heavy box. Father helped open the\nbox.\nThen they saw something very pretty. It was a big doll. It had round\nblue eyes and a small red mouth. It had a blue lace dress and curly black\nhair. Miriam called it Curly. She loved to play with it. What Miriam liked\nbest was the way Curly walked. Miriam would hold one of its hands and\nthey would walk together around the living room. Curly made Miriam\nhappy.\n1. Who was Curly?\na. a dog\nb. a doll\nc. a cat\n2. Who gave Curly to Miriam?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n3. Where does Uncle Max live?\na. Cebu\nb. Manila\nc. New York\n4. On what occasion was Curly given?\na. birthday\nb. Christmas c. graduation\n5. Who helped Miriam open the box?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n6. What words talk about the box?\na. big and light\nb. big and heavy\nc. small and light\n7. What words talk about Curly’s mouth?\na. red\nb. pink\nc. yellow\n8. What was Curly’s dress made of?\na. silk\nb. lace\nc. cotton\n9. What word talks about her hair?\na. curly\nb. brown\nc. straight\n10. What can Curly do?\na. talk\nb. sing c. walk',1,1,'answer'),
(830,211,NULL,'learn',1,'Taking Care of Animals · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 10:\nSet A\nTAKING CARE OF ANIMALS\nVictor lives on a farm. He lives with his parents\nin a little nipa house. Victor has an elder sister\nnamed Nora. Victor and Nora help their parents.\nThey help take care of their animals. They have a\ncarabao, a horse, a goat, and some chickens.\nFather takes care of the horse. Victor takes care\nof the carabao. Mother takes care of the chickens.\nNora takes care of the\ngoat. Their animals are all fat and healthy. Each one takes care of their animal\nvery well.\n1. Where does Victor live?\na. in the city\nb. on a farm\nc. near the sea\n2. Which word tells about their house?\na. nipa\nb. cement\nc. wooden\n3. Who is Victor’s sister?\na. Nina\nb. Nora\nc. Nida\n4. Who is older, Victor or Nora?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Does not tell\n5. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na. 3\nb. 4.\nc.5\n6. Which one they do not have?\na. cow\nb. horse\nc. carabao\n7. Who takes care of the horse?\na. Victor\nb. Father\nc. Mother\n8. Who takes care of the carabao?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Father\n9. Who takes care of the chickens?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Mother\n10. Which one does Nora take care of?\na. goat\nb. chickens\nc. carabao','assets/images/level5/g3/p031-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p031-1.webp\"]','Activity 10: Set A TAKING CARE OF ANIMALS Victor lives on a farm. He lives with his parents in a little nipa house. Victor has an elder sister named Nora. Victor and Nora help their parents. They help take care of their animals. They have a carabao, a horse, a goat, and some chickens. Father takes care of the horse. Victor takes care of the carabao. Mother takes care of the chickens. Nora takes care of the goat. Their animals are all fat and healthy. Each one takes care of their animal very well. 1. Where does Victor live? a. in the city b. on a farm c. near the sea 2. Which word tells about their house? a. nipa b. cement c. wooden 3. Who is Victor’s sister? a. Nina b. Nora c. Nida 4. Who is older, Victor or Nora? a. Nora b. Victor c. Does not tell 5. How many kinds of animals do they have? a. 3 b. 4. c.5 6. Which one they do not have? a. cow b. horse c. carabao 7. Who takes care of the horse? a. Victor b. Father c. Mother 8. Who takes care of the carabao? a. Nora b. Victor c. Father 9. Who takes care of the chickens? a. Nora b. Victor c. Mother 10. Which one does Nora take care of? a. goat b. chickens c. carabao',NULL,10,31,'Activity 10:\nSet A\nTAKING CARE OF ANIMALS\nVictor lives on a farm. He lives with his parents\nin a little nipa house. Victor has an elder sister\nnamed Nora. Victor and Nora help their parents.\nThey help take care of their animals. They have a\ncarabao, a horse, a goat, and some chickens.\nFather takes care of the horse. Victor takes care\nof the carabao. Mother takes care of the chickens.\nNora takes care of the\ngoat. Their animals are all fat and healthy. Each one takes care of their animal\nvery well.\n1. Where does Victor live?\na. in the city\nb. on a farm\nc. near the sea\n2. Which word tells about their house?\na. nipa\nb. cement\nc. wooden\n3. Who is Victor’s sister?\na. Nina\nb. Nora\nc. Nida\n4. Who is older, Victor or Nora?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Does not tell\n5. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na. 3\nb. 4.\nc.5\n6. Which one they do not have?\na. cow\nb. horse\nc. carabao\n7. Who takes care of the horse?\na. Victor\nb. Father\nc. Mother\n8. Who takes care of the carabao?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Father\n9. Who takes care of the chickens?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Mother\n10. Which one does Nora take care of?\na. goat\nb. chickens\nc. carabao',1,1,'answer'),
(831,212,NULL,'learn',1,'The Banana Peelings · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 11:\nTHE BANANA PEELINGS\nCelso was eating bananas one evening. He threw the peelings out of\nthe window. The next morning, Celso got ready for school. He did not want\nto be late for school. He walked fast.\n“Ouch!” Celso cried as he stepped on some banana\npeelings. Down he fell. His clothes became dirty. His\nbooks dropped.\n“Are you hurt?” Mother asked running to him.\n“No, Mother, I am not hurt,” Celso said as he got up.\nHe looked at the banana peelings.\n“Somebody did not use the garbage can,” Mother\nsaid.\n“I threw these peelings last night, Mother. Next time, I will use the garbage\ncan,” said Celso.\n1.\nWhat did Celso eat?\na. bananas\nb. mangoes\nc. oranges\n2.\nWhen did he eat the fruit?\na. last night\nb. that morning\nc. last week\n3.\nWhen did he throw the peeling?\na. into the basket b. out of the window c. into the garbage can\n4.\nWhere was Celso going?\na. to church\nb. to market\nc. to school\n5.\nWhat sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late?\na. He walked fast\nb. He walked slowly c. He played on the way\n6.\nWho stepped on the banana peelings?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Celso\n7.\nWho saw Celso fall?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Sister\n8.\nWho did not use the garbage can?\na. Mother\nb. Celso\nc. Sister\n9.\nWas Celso hurt?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell\n10.\nWhich word tells about Celso?\na. polite\nb. kind\nc. truthful','assets/images/level5/g3/p032-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p032-1.webp\"]','Activity 11: THE BANANA PEELINGS Celso was eating bananas one evening. He threw the peelings out of the window. The next morning, Celso got ready for school. He did not want to be late for school. He walked fast. “Ouch!” Celso cried as he stepped on some banana peelings. Down he fell. His clothes became dirty. His books dropped. “Are you hurt?” Mother asked running to him. “No, Mother, I am not hurt,” Celso said as he got up. He looked at the banana peelings. “Somebody did not use the garbage can,” Mother said. “I threw these peelings last night, Mother. Next time, I will use the garbage can,” said Celso. 1. What did Celso eat? a. bananas b. mangoes c. oranges 2. When did he eat the fruit? a. last night b. that morning c. last week 3. When did he throw the peeling? a. into the basket b. out of the window c. into the garbage can 4. Where was Celso going? a. to church b. to market c. to school 5. What sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late? a. He walked fast b. He walked slowly c. He played on the way 6. Who stepped on the banana peelings? a. Father b. Mother c. Celso 7. Who saw Celso fall? a. Father b. Mother c. Sister 8. Who did not use the garbage can? a. Mother b. Celso c. Sister 9. Was Celso hurt? a. Yes b. No c. Does not tell 10. Which word tells about Celso? a. polite b. kind c. truthful',NULL,10,32,'Activity 11:\nTHE BANANA PEELINGS\nCelso was eating bananas one evening. He threw the peelings out of\nthe window. The next morning, Celso got ready for school. He did not want\nto be late for school. He walked fast.\n“Ouch!” Celso cried as he stepped on some banana\npeelings. Down he fell. His clothes became dirty. His\nbooks dropped.\n“Are you hurt?” Mother asked running to him.\n“No, Mother, I am not hurt,” Celso said as he got up.\nHe looked at the banana peelings.\n“Somebody did not use the garbage can,” Mother\nsaid.\n“I threw these peelings last night, Mother. Next time, I will use the garbage\ncan,” said Celso.\n1.\nWhat did Celso eat?\na. bananas\nb. mangoes\nc. oranges\n2.\nWhen did he eat the fruit?\na. last night\nb. that morning\nc. last week\n3.\nWhen did he throw the peeling?\na. into the basket b. out of the window c. into the garbage can\n4.\nWhere was Celso going?\na. to church\nb. to market\nc. to school\n5.\nWhat sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late?\na. He walked fast\nb. He walked slowly c. He played on the way\n6.\nWho stepped on the banana peelings?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Celso\n7.\nWho saw Celso fall?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Sister\n8.\nWho did not use the garbage can?\na. Mother\nb. Celso\nc. Sister\n9.\nWas Celso hurt?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell\n10.\nWhich word tells about Celso?\na. polite\nb. kind\nc. truthful',1,1,'answer'),
(832,213,NULL,'learn',1,'The News Boy · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 12:\nTHE NEWS BOY\nAt five o’clock in the afternoon, the train arrives in Naga City.\nThe train carries the newspapers from Manila. Alfredo, a Grade Four\npupil, sells newspapers after class in the afternoon. He sells for two\nhours. At seven o’clock, he goes home. He has time to study his\nlessons.\nAlfredo earns one hundred pesos a day. He wants to give\nhis money to Mother. But Mother told him to put his money in his piggy bank. Alfredo’s\nparents are not poor. They can give him money he needs, but Alfredo wants to sell\nnewspapers. He wants to earn his own money.\n1.\nWhere does Alfredo live?\na. in Manila\nb. in Naga City\nc. on a farm\n2.\nWhat time does the train arrive in Naga City?\na. four o’clock\nb. five o’clock\nc. six o’clock\n3.\nWhat carries the newspapers to Naga City?\na. a car\nb. a truck\nc. a train\n4.\nWhere do the newspapers come from?\na. Manila\nb. Cebu City\nc. Pasay City\n5.\nWhat does Alfredo do?\na. sells fruit\nb. sells candies\nc. sells newspapers\n6.\nHow long does Alfredo sell newspapers?\na. one hour\nb. two hours\nc. three hours\n7.\nHow much does he earn a day?\na. five pesos\nb. seventy-five pesos\nc. one hundred pesos\n8.\nWhat does he do with the money?\na. gives it to his mother.\nb. buy cakes and candies.\nc. keeps it in his piggy bank.\n9.\nWhat kind of a boy is Alfredo?\na. clean\nb. polite\nc. industrious\n10.\nAre his parents poor?\na. yes\nb. no\nc. does not tell','assets/images/level5/g3/p033-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p033-1.webp\"]','Activity 12: THE NEWS BOY At five o’clock in the afternoon, the train arrives in Naga City. The train carries the newspapers from Manila. Alfredo, a Grade Four pupil, sells newspapers after class in the afternoon. He sells for two hours. At seven o’clock, he goes home. He has time to study his lessons. Alfredo earns one hundred pesos a day. He wants to give his money to Mother. But Mother told him to put his money in his piggy bank. Alfredo’s parents are not poor. They can give him money he needs, but Alfredo wants to sell newspapers. He wants to earn his own money. 1. Where does Alfredo live? a. in Manila b. in Naga City c. on a farm 2. What time does the train arrive in Naga City? a. four o’clock b. five o’clock c. six o’clock 3. What carries the newspapers to Naga City? a. a car b. a truck c. a train 4. Where do the newspapers come from? a. Manila b. Cebu City c. Pasay City 5. What does Alfredo do? a. sells fruit b. sells candies c. sells newspapers 6. How long does Alfredo sell newspapers? a. one hour b. two hours c. three hours 7. How much does he earn a day? a. five pesos b. seventy-five pesos c. one hundred pesos 8. What does he do with the money? a. gives it to his mother. b. buy cakes and candies. c. keeps it in his piggy bank. 9. What kind of a boy is Alfredo? a. clean b. polite c. industrious 10. Are his parents poor? a. yes b. no c. does not tell',NULL,10,33,'Activity 12:\nTHE NEWS BOY\nAt five o’clock in the afternoon, the train arrives in Naga City.\nThe train carries the newspapers from Manila. Alfredo, a Grade Four\npupil, sells newspapers after class in the afternoon. He sells for two\nhours. At seven o’clock, he goes home. He has time to study his\nlessons.\nAlfredo earns one hundred pesos a day. He wants to give\nhis money to Mother. But Mother told him to put his money in his piggy bank. Alfredo’s\nparents are not poor. They can give him money he needs, but Alfredo wants to sell\nnewspapers. He wants to earn his own money.\n1.\nWhere does Alfredo live?\na. in Manila\nb. in Naga City\nc. on a farm\n2.\nWhat time does the train arrive in Naga City?\na. four o’clock\nb. five o’clock\nc. six o’clock\n3.\nWhat carries the newspapers to Naga City?\na. a car\nb. a truck\nc. a train\n4.\nWhere do the newspapers come from?\na. Manila\nb. Cebu City\nc. Pasay City\n5.\nWhat does Alfredo do?\na. sells fruit\nb. sells candies\nc. sells newspapers\n6.\nHow long does Alfredo sell newspapers?\na. one hour\nb. two hours\nc. three hours\n7.\nHow much does he earn a day?\na. five pesos\nb. seventy-five pesos\nc. one hundred pesos\n8.\nWhat does he do with the money?\na. gives it to his mother.\nb. buy cakes and candies.\nc. keeps it in his piggy bank.\n9.\nWhat kind of a boy is Alfredo?\na. clean\nb. polite\nc. industrious\n10.\nAre his parents poor?\na. yes\nb. no\nc. does not tell',1,1,'answer'),
(833,214,NULL,'learn',1,'A Sick Classmate · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 13:\nA SICK CLASSMATE\nOne morning, Miss Luna said to her Grade 3 class, “I got a letter\nfrom Teresa’s mother. Teresa cannot come to school. She is sick. The doctor\ntold her to stay in bed for a few days. What shall we do for Teresa?” “Let\nus visit her this afternoon,” said Linda.\n“Yes, let us visit her,” said the other children. That afternoon, the\nchildren went to visit Teresa. The girls brought her some fruits. The boys\nbrought her a can of biscuits. Miss Luna brought her some roses. Teresa was sleeping when\nthey arrived. Soon, she woke up. She was happy to see her teacher and classmates.\n1. Who is Miss Luna?\na. A nurse\nb. A mother\nc. A teacher\n2. What did she get one morning?\na. A letter\nb. A telegram\nc. A newspaper\n3. Who sent a letter?\na. Teresa\nb. Teresa’s mother\nc. Teresa’s father\n4. Why was Teresa absent?\na. She was sick.\nb. She was busy.\nc. She was away.\n5. Did a doctor treat her?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell.\n6. What did the children do?\na. They visited her.\nb. They sent flowers.\nc. They sent her letter.\n7. What did the girls bring?\na. Milk\nb. Fruits\nc. flowers\n8. What did the boys bring?\na. Fruits\nb. Roses\nc. biscuits\n9. Who brought some roses?\na. The girls\nb. The boys\nc. Miss Luna\n10. When did they visit Teresa?\na. Morning\nb. Afternoon\nc. evening','assets/images/level5/g3/p034-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p034-1.webp\"]','Activity 13: A SICK CLASSMATE One morning, Miss Luna said to her Grade 3 class, “I got a letter from Teresa’s mother. Teresa cannot come to school. She is sick. The doctor told her to stay in bed for a few days. What shall we do for Teresa?” “Let us visit her this afternoon,” said Linda. “Yes, let us visit her,” said the other children. That afternoon, the children went to visit Teresa. The girls brought her some fruits. The boys brought her a can of biscuits. Miss Luna brought her some roses. Teresa was sleeping when they arrived. Soon, she woke up. She was happy to see her teacher and classmates. 1. Who is Miss Luna? a. A nurse b. A mother c. A teacher 2. What did she get one morning? a. A letter b. A telegram c. A newspaper 3. Who sent a letter? a. Teresa b. Teresa’s mother c. Teresa’s father 4. Why was Teresa absent? a. She was sick. b. She was busy. c. She was away. 5. Did a doctor treat her? a. Yes b. No c. Does not tell. 6. What did the children do? a. They visited her. b. They sent flowers. c. They sent her letter. 7. What did the girls bring? a. Milk b. Fruits c. flowers 8. What did the boys bring? a. Fruits b. Roses c. biscuits 9. Who brought some roses? a. The girls b. The boys c. Miss Luna 10. When did they visit Teresa? a. Morning b. Afternoon c. evening',NULL,10,34,'Activity 13:\nA SICK CLASSMATE\nOne morning, Miss Luna said to her Grade 3 class, “I got a letter\nfrom Teresa’s mother. Teresa cannot come to school. She is sick. The doctor\ntold her to stay in bed for a few days. What shall we do for Teresa?” “Let\nus visit her this afternoon,” said Linda.\n“Yes, let us visit her,” said the other children. That afternoon, the\nchildren went to visit Teresa. The girls brought her some fruits. The boys\nbrought her a can of biscuits. Miss Luna brought her some roses. Teresa was sleeping when\nthey arrived. Soon, she woke up. She was happy to see her teacher and classmates.\n1. Who is Miss Luna?\na. A nurse\nb. A mother\nc. A teacher\n2. What did she get one morning?\na. A letter\nb. A telegram\nc. A newspaper\n3. Who sent a letter?\na. Teresa\nb. Teresa’s mother\nc. Teresa’s father\n4. Why was Teresa absent?\na. She was sick.\nb. She was busy.\nc. She was away.\n5. Did a doctor treat her?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell.\n6. What did the children do?\na. They visited her.\nb. They sent flowers.\nc. They sent her letter.\n7. What did the girls bring?\na. Milk\nb. Fruits\nc. flowers\n8. What did the boys bring?\na. Fruits\nb. Roses\nc. biscuits\n9. Who brought some roses?\na. The girls\nb. The boys\nc. Miss Luna\n10. When did they visit Teresa?\na. Morning\nb. Afternoon\nc. evening',1,1,'answer'),
(834,215,NULL,'learn',1,'The Kitten · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 14: Set A\nTHE KITTEN\nOne rainy afternoon, Juan did not go straight home from\nschool. He had his raincoat on, so he did not get wet. Then he saw a\nkitten trembling in the grass. He stopped and looked at it. It began to\nmew very softly.\nJuan was sorry for the kitten. He picked it up and put it under his raincoat.\nHe brought it home. He put it near the stove with fire. The kitten looked at Juan and said,\n“\nMew, mew.” It wanted to say, “Thank you.” From that time on, the kitten became\nhis pet. He loved his pet very much.\n1. What time of the day was it?\na. Morning\nb. Noon\nc. afternoon\n2. What kind of afternoon was it?\na. Rainy\nb. Sunny\nc. cloudy\n3. Where was Juan going?\na. Home\nb. To school\nc. To church\n4. What was Juan wearing?\na. A hat\nb. A sweater\nc. A raincoat\n5. What did Juan see on the way?\na. Dog\nb. Kitten\nc. chick\n6. How did the kitten feel?\na. Hot\nb. Cold\nc. warm\n7. What did Juan feel for the kitten?\na. Pity\nb. Gladness\nc. happiness\n8. Where did he bring it?\na. Home\nb. School\nc. In the shade\n9. Where did he put the kitten?\na. Near the fire\nb. the table\nc. Near the bed\n10. Did the kitten like to stay near the fire?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell','assets/images/level5/g3/p035-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p035-1.webp\"]','Activity 14: Set A THE KITTEN One rainy afternoon, Juan did not go straight home from school. He had his raincoat on, so he did not get wet. Then he saw a kitten trembling in the grass. He stopped and looked at it. It began to mew very softly. Juan was sorry for the kitten. He picked it up and put it under his raincoat. He brought it home. He put it near the stove with fire. The kitten looked at Juan and said, “ Mew, mew.” It wanted to say, “Thank you.” From that time on, the kitten became his pet. He loved his pet very much. 1. What time of the day was it? a. Morning b. Noon c. afternoon 2. What kind of afternoon was it? a. Rainy b. Sunny c. cloudy 3. Where was Juan going? a. Home b. To school c. To church 4. What was Juan wearing? a. A hat b. A sweater c. A raincoat 5. What did Juan see on the way? a. Dog b. Kitten c. chick 6. How did the kitten feel? a. Hot b. Cold c. warm 7. What did Juan feel for the kitten? a. Pity b. Gladness c. happiness 8. Where did he bring it? a. Home b. School c. In the shade 9. Where did he put the kitten? a. Near the fire b. the table c. Near the bed 10. Did the kitten like to stay near the fire? a. Yes b. No c. Does not tell',NULL,10,35,'Activity 14: Set A\nTHE KITTEN\nOne rainy afternoon, Juan did not go straight home from\nschool. He had his raincoat on, so he did not get wet. Then he saw a\nkitten trembling in the grass. He stopped and looked at it. It began to\nmew very softly.\nJuan was sorry for the kitten. He picked it up and put it under his raincoat.\nHe brought it home. He put it near the stove with fire. The kitten looked at Juan and said,\n“\nMew, mew.” It wanted to say, “Thank you.” From that time on, the kitten became\nhis pet. He loved his pet very much.\n1. What time of the day was it?\na. Morning\nb. Noon\nc. afternoon\n2. What kind of afternoon was it?\na. Rainy\nb. Sunny\nc. cloudy\n3. Where was Juan going?\na. Home\nb. To school\nc. To church\n4. What was Juan wearing?\na. A hat\nb. A sweater\nc. A raincoat\n5. What did Juan see on the way?\na. Dog\nb. Kitten\nc. chick\n6. How did the kitten feel?\na. Hot\nb. Cold\nc. warm\n7. What did Juan feel for the kitten?\na. Pity\nb. Gladness\nc. happiness\n8. Where did he bring it?\na. Home\nb. School\nc. In the shade\n9. Where did he put the kitten?\na. Near the fire\nb. the table\nc. Near the bed\n10. Did the kitten like to stay near the fire?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell',1,1,'answer'),
(835,216,NULL,'learn',1,'The Coconut · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 14:\nSet B\nTHE COCONUT\nThe coconut is a tall palm tree. It has no branches. The trunk\nis strong. It makes a good post. We get oil from the ripe coconut\nmilk. The young coconut meat is good to eat. It is good for making\ncandies and salad.\nDoormats are made out of the coconut husk. The long coconut\nleaves are woven into baskets. Brooms are made from the midribs\nof the long leaves. Coconut shells are made into buttons, coconut\nshell banks, ash trays and many others. The stalk of the leaves how useful the coconut is!\nEvery part of it can be used.\n1. What word tells about the coconut tree?\na. Short\nb. Tall\nc. small\n2. Does the coconut tree have branches?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell\n3. What part of the coconut tree is good for a post?\na. Trunk\nb. Roots\nc. fruits\n4. From where can we get oil?\na. From coconut husk\nb. From ripe coconut milk\nc. From young coconut meat\n5. Which is good to eat?\na. Coconut husk\nb. Coconut shell\nc. Coconut meat\n6. What part is made into doormats?\na. Shell\nb. Husk\nc. midribs\n7. What can be made from the midribs?\na. Buttons\nb. Brooms\nc. candies\n8. What part is woven into baskets?\na. Husk\nb. Shell\nc. leaves\n9. Which part can be made into buttons?\na. Husk\nb. Shell\nc. midribs\n10. What is the use of the stalk of the leaves?\na. For fuel\nb. For post\nc. For food','assets/images/level5/g3/p036-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p036-1.webp\"]','Activity 14: Set B THE COCONUT The coconut is a tall palm tree. It has no branches. The trunk is strong. It makes a good post. We get oil from the ripe coconut milk. The young coconut meat is good to eat. It is good for making candies and salad. Doormats are made out of the coconut husk. The long coconut leaves are woven into baskets. Brooms are made from the midribs of the long leaves. Coconut shells are made into buttons, coconut shell banks, ash trays and many others. The stalk of the leaves how useful the coconut is! Every part of it can be used. 1. What word tells about the coconut tree? a. Short b. Tall c. small 2. Does the coconut tree have branches? a. Yes b. No c. Does not tell 3. What part of the coconut tree is good for a post? a. Trunk b. Roots c. fruits 4. From where can we get oil? a. From coconut husk b. From ripe coconut milk c. From young coconut meat 5. Which is good to eat? a. Coconut husk b. Coconut shell c. Coconut meat 6. What part is made into doormats? a. Shell b. Husk c. midribs 7. What can be made from the midribs? a. Buttons b. Brooms c. candies 8. What part is woven into baskets? a. Husk b. Shell c. leaves 9. Which part can be made into buttons? a. Husk b. Shell c. midribs 10. What is the use of the stalk of the leaves? a. For fuel b. For post c. For food',NULL,10,36,'Activity 14:\nSet B\nTHE COCONUT\nThe coconut is a tall palm tree. It has no branches. The trunk\nis strong. It makes a good post. We get oil from the ripe coconut\nmilk. The young coconut meat is good to eat. It is good for making\ncandies and salad.\nDoormats are made out of the coconut husk. The long coconut\nleaves are woven into baskets. Brooms are made from the midribs\nof the long leaves. Coconut shells are made into buttons, coconut\nshell banks, ash trays and many others. The stalk of the leaves how useful the coconut is!\nEvery part of it can be used.\n1. What word tells about the coconut tree?\na. Short\nb. Tall\nc. small\n2. Does the coconut tree have branches?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell\n3. What part of the coconut tree is good for a post?\na. Trunk\nb. Roots\nc. fruits\n4. From where can we get oil?\na. From coconut husk\nb. From ripe coconut milk\nc. From young coconut meat\n5. Which is good to eat?\na. Coconut husk\nb. Coconut shell\nc. Coconut meat\n6. What part is made into doormats?\na. Shell\nb. Husk\nc. midribs\n7. What can be made from the midribs?\na. Buttons\nb. Brooms\nc. candies\n8. What part is woven into baskets?\na. Husk\nb. Shell\nc. leaves\n9. Which part can be made into buttons?\na. Husk\nb. Shell\nc. midribs\n10. What is the use of the stalk of the leaves?\na. For fuel\nb. For post\nc. For food',1,1,'answer'),
(836,217,NULL,'learn',1,'Growing Vegetable · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 15:\nGROWING VEGETABLE\nLino went with mother to market. They bought some vegetables. Mother\nsaid, “I was able to buy only some with my money. Vegetables cost much\nnow.”\nLino was sorry for Mother. They did not have much money. So, he said,\n“Let’s plant vegetables in our backyard. Then we will not have to buy\nthem in the market. “So, Lino planted three plots of\ntomatoes, two plots of eggplants and a plot of pechay. He had some amargoso climbing on\nthe bamboo fence. Lino worked in his garden after class every afternoon. He grew more\nvegetables than they could eat. Mother sold some of them in the market.\n1. Where did Mother and Lino go?\na. church\nb. school\nc. market\n2. What did they buy?\na. Fish\nb. Meat\nc. vegetables\n3. Which word tells about the vegetables?\na. Very cheap\nb. Cost much\nc. Very many\n4. Where did Lino plant vegetables?\na. In school\nb. On the farm\nc. In the backyard\n5. How many plots of tomatoes did he plant?\na. Two\nb. Three\nc. four\n6. How many plots were planted to eggplants?\na. One\nb. Two\nc. Three\n7. How many plots were planted to pechay?\na. One\nb. Two\nc. Three\n8. How many plots did he have in all?\na. Four\nb. Five\nc. Six\n9. What vegetables were climbing on the fence?\na. Beans\nb. Squash\nc. Amargosos\n10. Why did mother sell some vegetables?\na. She had no money.\nb. She did not like vegetables.\nc. They had more than they could eat.','assets/images/level5/g3/p037-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p037-1.webp\"]','Activity 15: GROWING VEGETABLE Lino went with mother to market. They bought some vegetables. Mother said, “I was able to buy only some with my money. Vegetables cost much now.” Lino was sorry for Mother. They did not have much money. So, he said, “Let’s plant vegetables in our backyard. Then we will not have to buy them in the market. “So, Lino planted three plots of tomatoes, two plots of eggplants and a plot of pechay. He had some amargoso climbing on the bamboo fence. Lino worked in his garden after class every afternoon. He grew more vegetables than they could eat. Mother sold some of them in the market. 1. Where did Mother and Lino go? a. church b. school c. market 2. What did they buy? a. Fish b. Meat c. vegetables 3. Which word tells about the vegetables? a. Very cheap b. Cost much c. Very many 4. Where did Lino plant vegetables? a. In school b. On the farm c. In the backyard 5. How many plots of tomatoes did he plant? a. Two b. Three c. four 6. How many plots were planted to eggplants? a. One b. Two c. Three 7. How many plots were planted to pechay? a. One b. Two c. Three 8. How many plots did he have in all? a. Four b. Five c. Six 9. What vegetables were climbing on the fence? a. Beans b. Squash c. Amargosos 10. Why did mother sell some vegetables? a. She had no money. b. She did not like vegetables. c. They had more than they could eat.',NULL,10,37,'Activity 15:\nGROWING VEGETABLE\nLino went with mother to market. They bought some vegetables. Mother\nsaid, “I was able to buy only some with my money. Vegetables cost much\nnow.”\nLino was sorry for Mother. They did not have much money. So, he said,\n“Let’s plant vegetables in our backyard. Then we will not have to buy\nthem in the market. “So, Lino planted three plots of\ntomatoes, two plots of eggplants and a plot of pechay. He had some amargoso climbing on\nthe bamboo fence. Lino worked in his garden after class every afternoon. He grew more\nvegetables than they could eat. Mother sold some of them in the market.\n1. Where did Mother and Lino go?\na. church\nb. school\nc. market\n2. What did they buy?\na. Fish\nb. Meat\nc. vegetables\n3. Which word tells about the vegetables?\na. Very cheap\nb. Cost much\nc. Very many\n4. Where did Lino plant vegetables?\na. In school\nb. On the farm\nc. In the backyard\n5. How many plots of tomatoes did he plant?\na. Two\nb. Three\nc. four\n6. How many plots were planted to eggplants?\na. One\nb. Two\nc. Three\n7. How many plots were planted to pechay?\na. One\nb. Two\nc. Three\n8. How many plots did he have in all?\na. Four\nb. Five\nc. Six\n9. What vegetables were climbing on the fence?\na. Beans\nb. Squash\nc. Amargosos\n10. Why did mother sell some vegetables?\na. She had no money.\nb. She did not like vegetables.\nc. They had more than they could eat.',1,1,'answer'),
(837,218,NULL,'learn',1,'A Moonlight Night · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 16:\nA MOONLIGHT NIGHT\nThe moon was big and bright. The children played in the\nmoonlight. They played Hide and Seek. Mario hid behind the\nacacia tree. Andres hid\nbehind some bushes. Isabel hid behind a pile of hollow blocks. Rita\nis behind some banana plants. Edmund looked around but saw no\none. Just then someone moved behind the bushes. Edmund ran to\nsee who it was and found Andres. “One, two, three!” he said. “Now\nyou are ‘It’, Andres.’’ The children played and played. How happy they were!\n1. What part of the day was it?\na. night\nb. morning\nc. afternoon\n2. Where did the children play?\na. In the rain\nb. In the sunshine\nc. In the moonlight\n3. What game did the children play?\na. Hide and Seek\nb. Jump the Spine\nc. Cat and Mouse\n4. Who was the first ‘It’?\na. Mario\nb. Andres\nc. Edmund\n5. Who hid behind the acacia tree?\na. Mario\nb. Isabel\nc. Andres\n6. Who hid behind some bush?\na. Rita\nb. Isabel\nc. Andres\n7. Who hid behind hollow blocks?\na. Rita\nb. Mario\nc. Isabel\n8. Who hid behind some banana plants?\na. Rita\nb. Mario\nc. Isabel\n9. Who was the next ‘It’?\na. Mario\nb. Andres\nc. Edmund\n10. How did the children feel?\na. Tired\nb. happy\nc. sleepy','assets/images/level5/g3/p038-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p038-1.webp\"]','Activity 16: A MOONLIGHT NIGHT The moon was big and bright. The children played in the moonlight. They played Hide and Seek. Mario hid behind the acacia tree. Andres hid behind some bushes. Isabel hid behind a pile of hollow blocks. Rita is behind some banana plants. Edmund looked around but saw no one. Just then someone moved behind the bushes. Edmund ran to see who it was and found Andres. “One, two, three!” he said. “Now you are ‘It’, Andres.’’ The children played and played. How happy they were! 1. What part of the day was it? a. night b. morning c. afternoon 2. Where did the children play? a. In the rain b. In the sunshine c. In the moonlight 3. What game did the children play? a. Hide and Seek b. Jump the Spine c. Cat and Mouse 4. Who was the first ‘It’? a. Mario b. Andres c. Edmund 5. Who hid behind the acacia tree? a. Mario b. Isabel c. Andres 6. Who hid behind some bush? a. Rita b. Isabel c. Andres 7. Who hid behind hollow blocks? a. Rita b. Mario c. Isabel 8. Who hid behind some banana plants? a. Rita b. Mario c. Isabel 9. Who was the next ‘It’? a. Mario b. Andres c. Edmund 10. How did the children feel? a. Tired b. happy c. sleepy',NULL,10,38,'Activity 16:\nA MOONLIGHT NIGHT\nThe moon was big and bright. The children played in the\nmoonlight. They played Hide and Seek. Mario hid behind the\nacacia tree. Andres hid\nbehind some bushes. Isabel hid behind a pile of hollow blocks. Rita\nis behind some banana plants. Edmund looked around but saw no\none. Just then someone moved behind the bushes. Edmund ran to\nsee who it was and found Andres. “One, two, three!” he said. “Now\nyou are ‘It’, Andres.’’ The children played and played. How happy they were!\n1. What part of the day was it?\na. night\nb. morning\nc. afternoon\n2. Where did the children play?\na. In the rain\nb. In the sunshine\nc. In the moonlight\n3. What game did the children play?\na. Hide and Seek\nb. Jump the Spine\nc. Cat and Mouse\n4. Who was the first ‘It’?\na. Mario\nb. Andres\nc. Edmund\n5. Who hid behind the acacia tree?\na. Mario\nb. Isabel\nc. Andres\n6. Who hid behind some bush?\na. Rita\nb. Isabel\nc. Andres\n7. Who hid behind hollow blocks?\na. Rita\nb. Mario\nc. Isabel\n8. Who hid behind some banana plants?\na. Rita\nb. Mario\nc. Isabel\n9. Who was the next ‘It’?\na. Mario\nb. Andres\nc. Edmund\n10. How did the children feel?\na. Tired\nb. happy\nc. sleepy',1,1,'answer'),
(838,219,NULL,'learn',1,'Ramon’s Cake · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 17:\nRAMON’S CAKE\nIt was recess time. Pedro and Ramon went to buy cakes. Then\nthey sat near the gate. They began to eat their cakes. Just then Oscar\nran against Ramon. Ramon’s cake fell to the ground.\n“Look what you did to my cake,” Ramon said.\n“I am sorry, Ramon. I did not mean to knock your cake down,”\nsaid Oscar.\n“Why did you not look where you were going?” asked Ramon.\n“Tony ran after me and I did not look where I was going,” said Oscar.\nRamon was angry. He was about to box Oscar.\n“Never mind,” said Pedro. “Oscar did not mean to knock you cake down, Ramon.\nI still have my cake. Let us divide it.”\n1. What time was it?\na. noon time\nb. recess time\nc. time to go home\n2. What did Ramon and Pedro buy?\na. cakes\nb. banana\nc. ice cream\n3. Where did they sit?\na. Near the stair\nb. Near the door\nc. Near the gate\n4. Who ran against Ramon?\na. Tony\nb. Pedro\nc. Oscar\n5. What happened to Ramon’s cake?\na. It fell down.\nb. Oscar got it.\nc. Ramon ate it.\n6. Who ran after Oscar?\na. Tony\nb. Pedro\nc. Ramon\n7. Who was angry?\na. Pedro\nb. Oscar\nc. Ramon\n8. What was Ramon about to do?\na. Cry\nb. go home\nc. box Oscar\n9. What did Pedro do?\na. He went away.\nb. He boxed Oscar.\nc. He gave Ramon some cake.\n10. Which boy would you like for a friend?\na. Pedro\nb. Oscar\nc. Ramon','assets/images/level5/g3/p039-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p039-1.webp\"]','Activity 17: RAMON’S CAKE It was recess time. Pedro and Ramon went to buy cakes. Then they sat near the gate. They began to eat their cakes. Just then Oscar ran against Ramon. Ramon’s cake fell to the ground. “Look what you did to my cake,” Ramon said. “I am sorry, Ramon. I did not mean to knock your cake down,” said Oscar. “Why did you not look where you were going?” asked Ramon. “Tony ran after me and I did not look where I was going,” said Oscar. Ramon was angry. He was about to box Oscar. “Never mind,” said Pedro. “Oscar did not mean to knock you cake down, Ramon. I still have my cake. Let us divide it.” 1. What time was it? a. noon time b. recess time c. time to go home 2. What did Ramon and Pedro buy? a. cakes b. banana c. ice cream 3. Where did they sit? a. Near the stair b. Near the door c. Near the gate 4. Who ran against Ramon? a. Tony b. Pedro c. Oscar 5. What happened to Ramon’s cake? a. It fell down. b. Oscar got it. c. Ramon ate it. 6. Who ran after Oscar? a. Tony b. Pedro c. Ramon 7. Who was angry? a. Pedro b. Oscar c. Ramon 8. What was Ramon about to do? a. Cry b. go home c. box Oscar 9. What did Pedro do? a. He went away. b. He boxed Oscar. c. He gave Ramon some cake. 10. Which boy would you like for a friend? a. Pedro b. Oscar c. Ramon',NULL,10,39,'Activity 17:\nRAMON’S CAKE\nIt was recess time. Pedro and Ramon went to buy cakes. Then\nthey sat near the gate. They began to eat their cakes. Just then Oscar\nran against Ramon. Ramon’s cake fell to the ground.\n“Look what you did to my cake,” Ramon said.\n“I am sorry, Ramon. I did not mean to knock your cake down,”\nsaid Oscar.\n“Why did you not look where you were going?” asked Ramon.\n“Tony ran after me and I did not look where I was going,” said Oscar.\nRamon was angry. He was about to box Oscar.\n“Never mind,” said Pedro. “Oscar did not mean to knock you cake down, Ramon.\nI still have my cake. Let us divide it.”\n1. What time was it?\na. noon time\nb. recess time\nc. time to go home\n2. What did Ramon and Pedro buy?\na. cakes\nb. banana\nc. ice cream\n3. Where did they sit?\na. Near the stair\nb. Near the door\nc. Near the gate\n4. Who ran against Ramon?\na. Tony\nb. Pedro\nc. Oscar\n5. What happened to Ramon’s cake?\na. It fell down.\nb. Oscar got it.\nc. Ramon ate it.\n6. Who ran after Oscar?\na. Tony\nb. Pedro\nc. Ramon\n7. Who was angry?\na. Pedro\nb. Oscar\nc. Ramon\n8. What was Ramon about to do?\na. Cry\nb. go home\nc. box Oscar\n9. What did Pedro do?\na. He went away.\nb. He boxed Oscar.\nc. He gave Ramon some cake.\n10. Which boy would you like for a friend?\na. Pedro\nb. Oscar\nc. Ramon',1,1,'answer'),
(839,220,NULL,'learn',1,'Shine! · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 18:\nSHINE!\nAntonio was the eldest child. They were six children in the\nfamily. His family was poor. His father was sick. His mother\nworked hard to earn money. She washed clothes for other people.\nBut mother sent Antonio to school. He was in Grade Four.\nAntonio helped Mother earn money. He worked after classes in the\nafternoon. When he arrived from school, he usually carried his box\nand\nshouted “Shine! Shine!” He earned ₱ 80.00 or more on school days. On Saturdays\nand Sundays, he earned three times as much.\nWould like a boy like Antonio for a friend?\n1. Which word tells about Antonio’s family?\na. rich\nb. poor\nc. wealthy\n2. What happened to his father?\na. got sick\nb. was killed\nc. went away\n3. How many children were in the family?\na. four\nb. five\nc. six\n4. Which word tells about Antonio?\na. Youngest\nb. second\nc. eldest\n5. Who worked hard to earn money?\na. Father\nb. mother\nc. Antonio\n6. What did mother do to earn money?\na. sold fruits\nb. sold vegetables c. washed clothes\n7. In what grade was Antonio?\na. Grade Three\nb. Grade Four\nc. Grade Five\n8. What did he do to help mother?\na. Sold bottles\nb. Shined shoes\nc.\nSold newspaper\n9. About how much did he earn on school days?\na. ₱ 80.00\nb. ₱ 40.00\nc. ₱ 60.00\n10. How much did he earn on Saturdays and Sundays?\na. ₱ 90.00\nb. ₱ 60.00\nc. ₱ 240.00','assets/images/level5/g3/p040-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p040-1.webp\"]','Activity 18: SHINE! Antonio was the eldest child. They were six children in the family. His family was poor. His father was sick. His mother worked hard to earn money. She washed clothes for other people. But mother sent Antonio to school. He was in Grade Four. Antonio helped Mother earn money. He worked after classes in the afternoon. When he arrived from school, he usually carried his box and shouted “Shine! Shine!” He earned ₱ 80.00 or more on school days. On Saturdays and Sundays, he earned three times as much. Would like a boy like Antonio for a friend? 1. Which word tells about Antonio’s family? a. rich b. poor c. wealthy 2. What happened to his father? a. got sick b. was killed c. went away 3. How many children were in the family? a. four b. five c. six 4. Which word tells about Antonio? a. Youngest b. second c. eldest 5. Who worked hard to earn money? a. Father b. mother c. Antonio 6. What did mother do to earn money? a. sold fruits b. sold vegetables c. washed clothes 7. In what grade was Antonio? a. Grade Three b. Grade Four c. Grade Five 8. What did he do to help mother? a. Sold bottles b. Shined shoes c. Sold newspaper 9. About how much did he earn on school days? a. ₱ 80.00 b. ₱ 40.00 c. ₱ 60.00 10. How much did he earn on Saturdays and Sundays? a. ₱ 90.00 b. ₱ 60.00 c. ₱ 240.00',NULL,10,40,'Activity 18:\nSHINE!\nAntonio was the eldest child. They were six children in the\nfamily. His family was poor. His father was sick. His mother\nworked hard to earn money. She washed clothes for other people.\nBut mother sent Antonio to school. He was in Grade Four.\nAntonio helped Mother earn money. He worked after classes in the\nafternoon. When he arrived from school, he usually carried his box\nand\nshouted “Shine! Shine!” He earned ₱ 80.00 or more on school days. On Saturdays\nand Sundays, he earned three times as much.\nWould like a boy like Antonio for a friend?\n1. Which word tells about Antonio’s family?\na. rich\nb. poor\nc. wealthy\n2. What happened to his father?\na. got sick\nb. was killed\nc. went away\n3. How many children were in the family?\na. four\nb. five\nc. six\n4. Which word tells about Antonio?\na. Youngest\nb. second\nc. eldest\n5. Who worked hard to earn money?\na. Father\nb. mother\nc. Antonio\n6. What did mother do to earn money?\na. sold fruits\nb. sold vegetables c. washed clothes\n7. In what grade was Antonio?\na. Grade Three\nb. Grade Four\nc. Grade Five\n8. What did he do to help mother?\na. Sold bottles\nb. Shined shoes\nc.\nSold newspaper\n9. About how much did he earn on school days?\na. ₱ 80.00\nb. ₱ 40.00\nc. ₱ 60.00\n10. How much did he earn on Saturdays and Sundays?\na. ₱ 90.00\nb. ₱ 60.00\nc. ₱ 240.00',1,1,'answer'),
(840,221,NULL,'learn',1,'Fowls · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 19:\nSet A\nFOWLS\nFowls are animals. They are animals with two feet and two wings.\nTheir bodies are covered with feathers. They give us eggs. Their\nmeat is good to eat. Chicken, ducks, turkeys and geese\nare fowls. They eat grains such as palay and corn.\nChicken like worms. They scratch in the ground to look\nfor worms.\nDucks and geese like to swim. They like to stay in the water.\nThey are water birds so they have webbed feet. Turkeys\nhave beautiful feathers. The male turkey spreads its tail like a fan. Geese\nare good watchers. They make loud noise when people come near. Fowls\nare\ngood to raise. Many people get rich because of poultry rising.\n1. What are fowls?\na. Plant\nb. trees\nc. Animals\n2. How many feet do fowls have?\na. Two\nb. Four\nc. Many\n3. What covers their bodies?\na. Hair\nb. Hide\nc. Feathers\n4. What make them fly?\na. Feet\nb. Wings\nc. Feathers\n5. Which is not a grain?\na. Corn\nb. Meat\nc. Palay\n6. Which does not have webbed feet?\na. Duck\nb. chicken\nc. goose\n7. Which one do fowls not give us?\na. Milk\nb. Eggs\nc. Meat\n8. Where do ducks and geese like to stay?\na. In the sand\nb. On the water\nc. On the branches\nof tress\n9. Why do chickens scratch on the ground?\na. To look for fish\nb. to look for water\nc. to look\nfor worms\n10. Which are good watchers?\na. ducks\nb. geese\nc. turkeys','assets/images/level5/g3/p041-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p041-1.webp\"]','Activity 19: Set A FOWLS Fowls are animals. They are animals with two feet and two wings. Their bodies are covered with feathers. They give us eggs. Their meat is good to eat. Chicken, ducks, turkeys and geese are fowls. They eat grains such as palay and corn. Chicken like worms. They scratch in the ground to look for worms. Ducks and geese like to swim. They like to stay in the water. They are water birds so they have webbed feet. Turkeys have beautiful feathers. The male turkey spreads its tail like a fan. Geese are good watchers. They make loud noise when people come near. Fowls are good to raise. Many people get rich because of poultry rising. 1. What are fowls? a. Plant b. trees c. Animals 2. How many feet do fowls have? a. Two b. Four c. Many 3. What covers their bodies? a. Hair b. Hide c. Feathers 4. What make them fly? a. Feet b. Wings c. Feathers 5. Which is not a grain? a. Corn b. Meat c. Palay 6. Which does not have webbed feet? a. Duck b. chicken c. goose 7. Which one do fowls not give us? a. Milk b. Eggs c. Meat 8. Where do ducks and geese like to stay? a. In the sand b. On the water c. On the branches of tress 9. Why do chickens scratch on the ground? a. To look for fish b. to look for water c. to look for worms 10. Which are good watchers? a. ducks b. geese c. turkeys',NULL,10,41,'Activity 19:\nSet A\nFOWLS\nFowls are animals. They are animals with two feet and two wings.\nTheir bodies are covered with feathers. They give us eggs. Their\nmeat is good to eat. Chicken, ducks, turkeys and geese\nare fowls. They eat grains such as palay and corn.\nChicken like worms. They scratch in the ground to look\nfor worms.\nDucks and geese like to swim. They like to stay in the water.\nThey are water birds so they have webbed feet. Turkeys\nhave beautiful feathers. The male turkey spreads its tail like a fan. Geese\nare good watchers. They make loud noise when people come near. Fowls\nare\ngood to raise. Many people get rich because of poultry rising.\n1. What are fowls?\na. Plant\nb. trees\nc. Animals\n2. How many feet do fowls have?\na. Two\nb. Four\nc. Many\n3. What covers their bodies?\na. Hair\nb. Hide\nc. Feathers\n4. What make them fly?\na. Feet\nb. Wings\nc. Feathers\n5. Which is not a grain?\na. Corn\nb. Meat\nc. Palay\n6. Which does not have webbed feet?\na. Duck\nb. chicken\nc. goose\n7. Which one do fowls not give us?\na. Milk\nb. Eggs\nc. Meat\n8. Where do ducks and geese like to stay?\na. In the sand\nb. On the water\nc. On the branches\nof tress\n9. Why do chickens scratch on the ground?\na. To look for fish\nb. to look for water\nc. to look\nfor worms\n10. Which are good watchers?\na. ducks\nb. geese\nc. turkeys',1,1,'answer'),
(841,222,NULL,'learn',1,'The First Monkey · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Activity 20:\nTHE FIRST MONKEY\nLong time ago, there was a farmer who had a wide corn field.\nHe grew big and sweet corn. One day he saw some of his corn gone.\nMany corn plants had no more fruits. He wanted to catch whoever\nstole his corn.\nThe next day he hid behind a big mango tree. He carried a\nstick. He watched and watched until he saw a man coming.\nThe man passed through a broken part of the fence. The man began to pick some corn.\nThe farmer went from behind the mango tree and walked towards the man. The man\nsaw the farmer and started to run. The farmer ran after him but he could not catch him.\nThen he threw the stick at the man’s back and became a tail. The\nman went up the tree. He became smaller and smaller until he became the monkey.\n1. When did the story happen?\na. Last year\nb. A few years ago c. a long time ago\n2. What did the farmer have?\na. A rice field\nb. a camote field\nc. a corn field\n3. What words will tell about his corn?\na. Big and sweet\nb. small and sweet c. sweet and yellow\n4. What happened to his corn?\na. was stolen\nb. destroyed by insects\nc. destroyed by the\nwind\n5. Where did the farmer hide one day?\na. up the mango tree\nb. behind the guava tree c. behind the mango\ntree\n6. What did he carry?\na. A stick\nb. Some fruits\nc. some stones\n7. Who did he see come into the corn field?\na. A dog\nb. A man\nc. a monkey\n8. What did the farmer do to the man?\na. caught him\nb. threw the stick at him\nc. beat him with\nthe stick\n9. What happened with the stick?\na. was lost\nb. was broken\nc. became a tail\n10. What happened to the man?\na. became sick\nb. became a monkey\nc. became a corn\nplant','assets/images/level5/g3/p042-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g3/p042-1.webp\"]','Activity 20: THE FIRST MONKEY Long time ago, there was a farmer who had a wide corn field. He grew big and sweet corn. One day he saw some of his corn gone. Many corn plants had no more fruits. He wanted to catch whoever stole his corn. The next day he hid behind a big mango tree. He carried a stick. He watched and watched until he saw a man coming. The man passed through a broken part of the fence. The man began to pick some corn. The farmer went from behind the mango tree and walked towards the man. The man saw the farmer and started to run. The farmer ran after him but he could not catch him. Then he threw the stick at the man’s back and became a tail. The man went up the tree. He became smaller and smaller until he became the monkey. 1. When did the story happen? a. Last year b. A few years ago c. a long time ago 2. What did the farmer have? a. A rice field b. a camote field c. a corn field 3. What words will tell about his corn? a. Big and sweet b. small and sweet c. sweet and yellow 4. What happened to his corn? a. was stolen b. destroyed by insects c. destroyed by the wind 5. Where did the farmer hide one day? a. up the mango tree b. behind the guava tree c. behind the mango tree 6. What did he carry? a. A stick b. Some fruits c. some stones 7. Who did he see come into the corn field? a. A dog b. A man c. a monkey 8. What did the farmer do to the man? a. caught him b. threw the stick at him c. beat him with the stick 9. What happened with the stick? a. was lost b. was broken c. became a tail 10. What happened to the man? a. became sick b. became a monkey c. became a corn plant',NULL,10,42,'Activity 20:\nTHE FIRST MONKEY\nLong time ago, there was a farmer who had a wide corn field.\nHe grew big and sweet corn. One day he saw some of his corn gone.\nMany corn plants had no more fruits. He wanted to catch whoever\nstole his corn.\nThe next day he hid behind a big mango tree. He carried a\nstick. He watched and watched until he saw a man coming.\nThe man passed through a broken part of the fence. The man began to pick some corn.\nThe farmer went from behind the mango tree and walked towards the man. The man\nsaw the farmer and started to run. The farmer ran after him but he could not catch him.\nThen he threw the stick at the man’s back and became a tail. The\nman went up the tree. He became smaller and smaller until he became the monkey.\n1. When did the story happen?\na. Last year\nb. A few years ago c. a long time ago\n2. What did the farmer have?\na. A rice field\nb. a camote field\nc. a corn field\n3. What words will tell about his corn?\na. Big and sweet\nb. small and sweet c. sweet and yellow\n4. What happened to his corn?\na. was stolen\nb. destroyed by insects\nc. destroyed by the\nwind\n5. Where did the farmer hide one day?\na. up the mango tree\nb. behind the guava tree c. behind the mango\ntree\n6. What did he carry?\na. A stick\nb. Some fruits\nc. some stones\n7. Who did he see come into the corn field?\na. A dog\nb. A man\nc. a monkey\n8. What did the farmer do to the man?\na. caught him\nb. threw the stick at him\nc. beat him with\nthe stick\n9. What happened with the stick?\na. was lost\nb. was ',1,1,'answer'),
(842,223,75,'post',1,'Post-test · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','SET A\nPOST-TEST (Based on Days 1-10)\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write the\ncorresponding letter on your answer sheet.\n1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n4. Where did the magical tree house take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n5. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house\n7. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n9. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend',NULL,'[]','SET A POST-TEST (Based on Days 1-10) Instructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write the corresponding letter on your answer sheet. 1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack? a) her homework b) her lunchbox c) her pencil d) her book 2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox? a) in the classroom b) in the cafeteria c) in the library d) on the bus 3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox? a) a book about animals b) a book about space c) a book about archaeology d) a book about dinosaurs 4. Where did the magical tree h