(843,223,75,'post',2,'Post-test · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','b) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\nActivity 5: The Little Seed\'s Journey\n13. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n14. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n15. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n16. Who were talking to each other?\na) Lita and Lito\nb) Lina and Lino\nc) Lina and Leo\n17. What were they talking about?\na) what to do during the summer\nb) what to have during the summer\nc) what to wear during the summer\n18. The children in the story could be ______\na) brother and sister\nb) neighbors\nc) cousins',NULL,'[]','b) Handy Helper c) Super Cleaner d) Dust Buster 10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on? a) the Santa Maria b) the Mayflower c) the Nina d) the Pinta 11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food? a) the British b) the French c) the Spanish d) the Native Americans 12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest? a) Christmas b) Easter c) Thanksgiving d) Halloween Activity 5: The Little Seed\'s Journey 13. What blew the little seed far away? a) the sun b) the rain c) the wind d) the snow 14. What did the seed sprout? a) leaves and branches b) roots and a tiny stem c) fruit and vegetables d) flowers and petals 15. What did the bees collect from the flower? a) po