(846,223,75,'post',5,'Post-test · page 5','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','42. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na) 3\nb) 4\nc) 5\n43. Which one do they NOT have?\na) cow\nb) horse\nc) carabao\n44. Who takes care of the horse?\na) Victor\nb) Father\nc) Mother\n45. Who takes care of the carabao?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Father\n46. Who takes care of the chickens?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Mother\n47. Which one does Nora take care of?\na) goat\nb) chickens\nc) carabao\nVocabulary Focus\n48. In \"The Story of the First Thanksgiving,\" what does the\nword harvest mean?\na) a big ship\nb) a large feast\nc) the time when crops are gathered\n49. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word nectar mean?\na) a sweet liquid in flowers that bees collect\nb) the stem of a plant\nc) the journey a seed takes\n50. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word sprouted mean?\na) to be blown by the wind\nb) to be watered by the rain\nc) to start to grow',NULL,'[]','42. How many kinds of animals do they have? a) 3 b) 4 c) 5 43. Which one do they NOT have? a) cow b) horse c) carabao 44. Who takes care of the horse? a) Victor b) Father c) Mother 45. Who takes care of the carabao? a) Nora b) Victor c) Father 46. Who takes care of the chickens? a) Nora b) Victor c) Mother 47. Which one does Nora take care of? a) goat b) chickens c) carabao Vocabulary Focus 48. In \"The Story of the First Thanksgiving,\" what does the word harvest mean? a) a big ship b) a large feast c) the time when crops are gathered 49. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word nectar mean? a) a sweet liquid in flowers that bees collect b) the stem of a plant c) the journey a seed takes 50. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word sprouted mean? a) to be blown by the wind b) to be watered by the rain c) to start to grow',NULL,10,52,'42. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na) 3\nb) 4\nc) 5\n43. Which one do they NOT have?\na) cow\nb) horse\nc) carabao\n44. Who takes care of the horse?\na) Victor\nb) Father\nc) Mother\n45. Who takes care of the carabao?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Father\n46. Who takes care of the chickens?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Mother\n47. Which one does Nora take care of?\na) goat\nb) chickens\nc) carabao\nVocabulary Focus\n48. In \"The Story of the First Thanksgiving,\" what does the\nword harvest mean?\na) a big ship\nb) a large feast\nc) the time when crops are gathered\n49. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word nectar mean?\na) a sweet liquid in flowers that bees collect\nb) the stem of a plant\nc) the journey a seed takes\n50. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word sprouted mean?\na) to be blown by the wind\nb) to be watered by the rain\nc) to start to grow',1,1,'answer'),
(847,223,75,'post',7,'Post-test · page 6','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','SET B\nPOST-TEST (Based on Days 11-20)\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write\nthe corresponding letter on your answer sheet.\n1. What did Celso eat?\na) bananas b) mangoes c) oranges\n2. When did he eat the fruit?\na) last night b) that morning c) last week\n3. Where did he throw the peelings?\na) into the basket b) out of the window c) into the garbage can\n4. Where was Celso going?\na) to church b) to market c) to school\n5. What sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late?\na) He walked fast b) He walked slowly c) He played on the way\n6. Who stepped on the banana peelings?\na) Father b) Mother c) Celso\n7. Who saw Celso fall?\na) Father b) Mother c) Sister\n8. Who did not use the garbage can?\na) Mother b) Celso c) Sister\n9. Was Celso hurt?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n10. Which word tells about Celso?\na) polite b) kind c) truthful\n11. Where does Alfredo live?\na) in Manila b) in Naga City c) on a farm\n12. What time does the train arrive?\na) 4 o’clock b) 5 o’clock c) 6 o’clock\n13. What carries the newspapers to Naga City?\na) a car b) a truck c) a train\n14. Where do the newspapers come from?\na) Manila b) Cebu City c) Pasay City\n15. What does Alfredo do?\na) sells fruit b) sells candies c) sells newspapers\n16. How long does Alfredo sell newspapers?\na) one hour b) two hours c) three hours\n17. How much does he earn per day?\na) 5 pesos b) 75 pesos c) 100 pesos\n18. What does he do with the money?\na) gives it to mother b) buys cakes and candies c) keeps it in his piggy bank\n19. What kind of a boy is Alfredo?\na) clean b) polite c) industrious',NULL,'[]','SET B POST-TEST (Based on Days 11-20) Instructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write the corresponding letter on your answer sheet. 1. What did Celso eat? a) bananas b) mangoes c) oranges 2. When did he eat the fruit? a) last night b) that morning c) last week 3. Where did he throw the peelings? a) into the basket b) out of the window c) into the garbage can 4. Where was Celso going? a) to church b) to market c) to school 5. What sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late? a) He walked fast b) He walked slowly c) He played on the way 6. Who stepped on the banana peelings? a) Father b) Mother c) Celso 7. Who saw Celso fall? a) Father b) Mother c) Sister 8. Who did not use the garbage can? a) Mother b) Celso c) Sister 9. Was Celso hurt? a) Yes b) No c) Does not tell 10. Which word tells about Celso? a) polite b) kind c) truthful 11. Where does Alfredo live? a) in Manila b) in Naga City c) on a farm 12. What time does the train arrive? a) 4 o’clock b) 5 o’clock c) 6 o’clock 13. What carries the newspapers to Naga City? a) a car b) a truck c) a train 14. Where do the newspapers come from? a) Manila b) Cebu City c) Pasay City 15. What does Alfredo do? a) sells fruit b) sells candies c) sells newspapers 16. How long does Alfredo sell newspapers? a) one hour b) two hours c) three hours 17. How much does he earn per day? a) 5 pesos b) 75 pesos c) 100 pesos 18. What does he do with the money? a) gives it to mother b) buys cakes and candies c) keeps it in his piggy bank 19. What kind of a boy is Alfredo? a) clean b) polite c) industrious',NULL,10,54,'SET B\nPOST-TEST (Based on Days 11-20)\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write\nthe corresponding letter on your answer sheet.\n1. What did Celso eat?\na) bananas b) mangoes c) oranges\n2. When did he eat the fruit?\na) last night b) that morning c) last week\n3. Where did he throw the peelings?\na) into the basket b) out of the window c) into the garbage can\n4. Where was Celso going?\na) to church b) to market c) to school\n5. What sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late?\na) He walked fast b) He walked slowly c) He played on the way\n6. Who stepped on the banana peelings?\na) Father b) Mother c) Celso\n7. Who saw Celso fall?\na) Father b) Mother c) Sister\n8. Who did not use the garbage can?\na) Mother b) Celso c) Sister\n9. Was Celso hurt?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n10. Which word tells about Celso?\na) polite b) kind c) truthful\n11. Where does Alfredo live?\na) in Manila b) in Naga City c) on a farm\n12. What time does the train arrive?\na) 4 o’clock b) 5 o’clock c) 6 o’clock\n13. What carries the newspapers to Naga City?\na) a car b) a truck c) a train\n14. Where do the newspapers come from?\na) Manila b) Cebu City c) Pasay City\n15. What does Alfredo do?\na) sells fruit b) sells candies c) sells newspapers\n16. How long does Alfredo sell newspapers?\na) one hour b) two hours c) three hours\n17. How much does he earn per day?\na) 5 pesos b) 75 pesos c) 100 pesos\n18. What does he do with the money?\na) gives it to mother b) buys cakes and candies c) keeps',1,1,'answer'),
(848,223,75,'post',8,'Post-test · page 7','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','20. Are his parents poor?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n21. Who is Miss Luna?\na) nurse b) mother c) teacher\n22. What did she get one morning?\na) a letter b) a telegram c) a newspaper\n23. Who sent the letter?\na) Teresa b) Teresa’s mother c) Teresa’s father\n24. Why was Teresa absent?\na) She was sick b) She was busy c) She was away\n25. Did a doctor treat her?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n26. What did the children do?\na) visited her b) sent flowers c) sent her a letter\n27. What did the girls bring?\na) milk b) fruits c) flowers\n28. What did the boys bring?\na) fruits b) roses c) biscuits\n29. Who brought some roses?\na) girls b) boys c) Miss Luna\n30. When did they visit Teresa?\na) morning b) afternoon c) evening\n31. What time of the day was it?\na) morning b) noon c) afternoon\n32. What kind of afternoon was it?\na) rainy b) sunny c) cloudy\n33. Where was Juan going?\na) home b) school c) church\n34. What was Juan wearing?\na) hat b) sweater c) raincoat\n35. What did Juan see on the way?\na) dog b) kitten c) chick\n36. How did the kitten feel?\na) hot b) cold c) warm\n37. What did Juan feel for the kitten?\na) pity b) gladness c) happiness\n38. Where did he bring it?\na) home b) school c) in the shade\n39. Where did he put the kitten?\na) near the fire b) the table c) near the bed\n40. Did the kitten like to stay near the fire?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n41. What word tells about the coconut tree?\na) short b) tall c) small\n42. Does the coconut tree have branches?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n43. What part of the coconut tree is good for a post?',NULL,'[]','20. Are his parents poor? a) Yes b) No c) Does not tell 21. Who is Miss Luna? a) nurse b) mother c) teacher 22. What did she get one morning? a) a letter b) a telegram c) a newspaper 23. Who sent the letter? a) Teresa b) Teresa’s mother c) Tere