(851,224,76,'pre',1,'Pre-assessment (Activities 1–10) · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Pre- Assessment (Activities 1–10)\nInstructions: Choose the best word from the word bank to complete each\nsentence. Write the word on the line.\nHuge\nfriend\ngift\nClean\ndesk\nlearn\ndead\nCountry\npie\nabove\n1. The elephant was ______\n, towering over the other animals.\n2. Please keep your room ______\nand tidy.\n3. We took a vacation to the ______\nand enjoyed the scenery.\n4. A true ______\nis always there for you.\n5. I do my homework at my ______\n.\n6. We ate a delicious apple ______\nfor dessert.\n7. She gave him a ______\nfor his birthday.\n8. I want to ______\nhow to play the guitar.\n9. The plant is ______\nand dry.\n10. The airplane flew ______\nthe clouds.\nListening Comprehension Assessment (10 Items)\nInstructions: I will read a short sentence or passage. Listen carefully, then\nanswer the questions based on what you heard. Choose the best answer\nand write the letter of your choice on the line.\n(Read Aloud): \"The small, gray cat sat on the mat.\"\n11. What color was the cat? ______',NULL,'[]','Pre- Assessment (Activities 1–10) Instructions: Choose the best word from the word bank to complete each sentence. Write the word on the line. Huge friend gift Clean desk learn dead Country pie above 1. The elephant was blank , towering over the other animals. 2. Please keep your room blank and tidy. 3. We took a vacation to the blank and enjoyed the scenery. 4. A true blank is always there for you. 5. I do my homework at my blank . 6. We ate a delicious apple blank for dessert. 7. She gave him a blank for his birthday. 8. I want to blank how to play the guitar. 9. The plant is blank and dry. 10. The airplane flew blank the clouds. Listening Comprehension Assessment (10 Items) Instructions: I will read a short sentence or passage. Listen carefully, then answer the questions based on what you heard. Choose the best answer and write the letter of your choice on the line. (Read Aloud): \"The small, gray cat sat on the mat.\" 11. What color was the cat? blank',NULL,10,8,'Pre- Assessment (Activities 1–10)\nInstructions: Choose the best word from the word bank to complete each\nsentence. Write the word on the line.\nHuge\nfriend\ngift\nClean\ndesk\nlearn\ndead\nCountry\npie\nabove\n1. The elephant was ______\n, towering over the other animals.\n2. Please keep your room ______\nand tidy.\n3. We took a vacation to the ______\nand enjoyed the scenery.\n4. A true ______\nis always there for you.\n5. I do my homework at my ______\n.\n6. We ate a delicious apple ______\nfor dessert.\n7. She gave him a ______\nfor his birthday.\n8. I want to ______\nhow to play the guitar.\n9. The plant is ______\nand dry.\n10. The airplane flew ______\nthe clouds.\nListening Comprehension Assessment (10 Items)\nInstructions: I will read a short sentence or passage. Listen carefully, then\nanswer the questions based on what you heard. Choose the best answer\nand write the letter of your choice on the line.\n(Read Aloud): \"The small, gray cat sat on the mat.\"\n11. What color was the cat? ______',1,1,'answer'),
