(854,225,77,'pre',1,'Pre-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Pre- Assessment (Activities 11–20)\nA. Vocabulary Development (10 items)\nDirections: Read and complete the sentences by filling in the\nblank with the correct word from the box.\nWord Bank:\nheavy\nside\n1. I have muscles all over my ______\n.\n2. The chicken’s body is covered with ______\n.\n3. The duck has a big ______\n.\n4. A baby has twinkling ______\n.\n5. My two feet have long ______\n.\n6. The book is on the left ______\nof the table.\n7. The ______\nis full of words.\n8. The bag feels ______\n.\n9. The room is ______\nnow.\n10.\nThe food is ______\nfor everyone.\nB. Context clues.\nDirections: Supply the missing letters to make a meaningful word\nto complete the sentence.','assets/images/level5/g4/p011-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g4/p011-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g4/p011-2.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g4/p011-3.webp\"]','Pre- Assessment (Activities 11–20) A. Vocabulary Development (10 items) Directions: Read and complete the sentences by filling in the blank with the correct word from the box. Word Bank: heavy side 1. I have muscles all over my blank . 2. The chicken’s body is covered with blank . 3. The duck has a big blank . 4. A baby has twinkling blank . 5. My two feet have long blank . 6. The book is on the left blank of the table. 7. The blank is full of words. 8. The bag feels blank . 9. The room is blank now. 10. The food is blank for everyone. B. Context clues. Directions: Supply the missing letters to make a meaningful word to complete the sentence.',NULL,10,11,'Pre- Assessment (Activities 11–20)\nA. Vocabulary Development (10 items)\nDirections: Read and complete the sentences by filling in the\nblank with the correct word from the box.\nWord Bank:\nheavy\nside\n1. I have muscles all over my ______\n.\n2. The chicken’s body is covered with ______\n.\n3. The duck has a big ______\n.\n4. A baby has twinkling ______\n.\n5. My two feet have long ______\n.\n6. The book is on the left ______\nof the table.\n7. The ______\nis full of words.\n8. The bag feels ______\n.\n9. The room is ______\nnow.\n10.\nThe food is ______\nfor everyone.\nB. Context clues.\nDirections: Supply the missing letters to make a meaningful word\nto complete the sentence.',1,1,'answer'),
(855,225,77,'pre',2,'Pre-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','11. Mother cooked b _ _ ns, small seeds that we eat as food\nwith rice.\n12. I ate a ba_ an_ , a long yellow fruit that is sweet and soft\ninside.\n13. The tree has many le_ a_es, the green parts that grow on\nbranches and help the plant make food.\n14. We listened to the news on the r_ d_ o, a device that plays\nmusic and voices.\n15. The ring is made of g_ _ d, a shiny yellow metal that is very\nvaluable.\nn ______.\n16. A small insect that can crawl and bite is called an ______\n17. A young cat that plays and meows is called a k i _ _ e _.\n18. All people together, everyone included, are called co_ _ uni_ y.\n19. A type of large herbivore with antlers that lives on farms or\nin the forest is a d _ _ r.\n20.A tool that keeps you dry in the rain is an _ m b _ e _ _ a .\nII. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nA. Directions: Listen carefully as the teacher reads each\nsentence. Fill in the blank with the correct word you hear.\nThe cat is sleeping on my bed. She raised her hand to answer\nthe question. The sun rises in the east every morning. I ate a\npiece of cake for dessert. The dog wagged its tail happily.\n21. The cat is sleeping on my ______\n.\n22. She raised her ______\nto answer the question.\n23. The sun rises in the ______\n.\n24. I ate a piece of ______\nfor dessert.\n25. The dog wagged its ______\nhappily.',NULL,'[]','11. Mother cooked b _ _ ns, small seeds that we eat as food with rice. 12. I ate a ba_ an_ , a long yellow fruit that is sweet and soft inside. 13. The tree has many le_ a_es, the green parts that grow on branches and help the plant make food. 14. We listened to the news on the r_ d_ o, a device that plays music and voices. 15. The ring is made of g_ _ d, a shiny yellow metal that is very valuable. n blank . 16. A small insect that can crawl and bite is called an blank 17.