(856,225,77,'pre',3,'Pre-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','B. Direction: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her\ndog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park,\nLila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always\nbrings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the\nbirds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond\nQuestions:\n26. Who does Lila go to the park with? ______\n27. What color is Lila’s dog? ______\n28. Name two things Lila does at the park. ______\n29. What does Lila bring with her to the park? ______\n30. What animals does Lila watch at the park? ______\nC. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLast weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The\nplace was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card\nso our friends would know where we were. Around the camp\nwas a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance,\nwe could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky\nand saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our\ncountry.\n31. Where is the book placed?\nA. On the floor\nB. On the left side of the table\nC. Under the chair\nD. On the right side of the room',NULL,'[]','B. Direction: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the correct answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your answer on your paper. Lila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her dog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park, Lila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always brings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the birds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond Questions: 26. Who does Lila go to the park with? blank 27. What color is Lila’s dog? blank 28. Name two things Lila does at the park. blank 29. What does Lila bring with her to the park? blank 30. What animals does Lila watch at the park? blank C. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the correct answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your answer on your paper. Last weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The place was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card so our friends would know where we were. Around the camp was a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance, we could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky and saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our country. 31. Where is the book placed? A. On the floor B. On the left side of the table C. Under the chair D. On the right side of the room',NULL,10,13,'B. Direction: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her\ndog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park,\nLila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always\nbrings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the\nbirds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond\nQuestions:\n26. Who does Lila go to the park with? ______\n27. What color is Lila’s dog? ______\n28. Name two things Lila does at the park. ______\n29. What does Lila bring with her to the park? ______\n30. What animals does Lila watch at the park? ______\nC. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLast weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The\nplace was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card\nso our friends would know where we were. Around the camp\nwas a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance,\nwe could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky\nand saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our\ncountry.\n31. Where is the book placed?\nA. On the floor\nB. On the left side of the table\nC. Under the chair\nD. On the right side of the room',1,1,'answer'),
(857,225,77,'pre',4,'Pre-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','A. The bag\nB. The room\nC. The page\nD. The table\n33. How does the bag feel?\nA. Clean\nB. Gone\nC. Heavy\nD. Enough\n34. What is the room like now?\nA. Dirty\nB. Full\nC. Clean\nD. Heavy\n35. What must each student do carefully?\nA. Read\nB. Write\nC. Count\nD. Clean\nD. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.',NULL,'[]','A. The bag B. The room C. The page D. The table 33. How does the bag feel? A. Clean B. Gone C. Heavy D. Enough 34. What is the room like now? A. Dirty B. Full C. Clean D. Heavy 35. What must each student do carefully? A. Read B. Write C. Count D. Clean D. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the correct answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your answer on your paper.',NULL,10,14,'A. The bag\nB. The room\nC. The page\nD. The table\n33. How does the bag feel?\nA. Clean\nB. Gone\nC. Heavy\nD. Enough\n34. What is the room like now?\nA. Dirty\nB. Full\nC. Clean\nD. Heavy\n35. What must each student do carefully?\nA. Read\nB. Write\nC. Count\nD. Clean\nD. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.',1,1,'answer'),
(858,225,77,'pre',5,'Pre-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 5','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','The farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will\npress the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will\npay the workers. In March, the children will march in the\nparade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The\nteam will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the\nclothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very\nbusy. At night, the children dream of a better future.\n36. What will the farmer plant?\nA. Trees\nB. Flowers\nC. Seeds\nD. Fruits\n37. What does the farmer do to the soil?\nA. Waters it\nB. Presses it\nC. Removes it\nD. Dries it\n38. When do the children march in the parade?\nA. January\nB. February\nC. March\nD. April\n39. What should people NOT do to animals?\nA. Feed them\nB. Watch them\nC. Kill them',NULL,'[]','The farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will press the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will pay the workers. In March, the children will march in the parade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The team will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the clothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very busy. At night, the children dream of a better future. 36. What will the farmer plant? A. Trees B. Flowers C. Seeds D. Fruits 37. What does the farmer do to the soil? A. Waters it B. Presses it C. Removes it D. Dries it 38. When do the children march in the parade? A. January B. February C. March D. April 39. What should people NOT do to animals? A. Feed them B. Watch them C. Kill them',NULL,10,15,'The farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will\npress the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will\npay the workers. In March, the children will march in the\nparade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The\nteam will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the\nclothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very\nbusy. At night, the children dream of a better future.\n36. What will the farmer plant?\nA. Trees\nB. Flowers\nC. Seeds\nD. Fruits\n37. What does the farmer do to the soil?\nA. Waters it\nB. Presses it\nC. Removes it\nD. Dries it\n38. When do the children march in the parade?\nA. January\nB. February\nC. March\nD. April\n39. What should people NOT do to animals?\nA. Feed them\nB. Watch them\nC. Kill them',1,1,'answer'),
(859,225,77,'pre',6,'Pre-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 6','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','D. Care for them\n40. What do the children dream of at night?\nA. Playing games\nA. A better future\nB. Going to school\nC. Traveling far',NULL,'[]','D. Care for them 40. What do the children dream of at night? A. Playing games A. A better future B. Going to school C. Traveling far',NULL,10,16,'D. Care for them\n40. What do the children dream of at night?\nA. Playing games\nA. A better future\nB. Going to school\nC. Traveling far',1,1,'answer'),
(860,226,NULL,'learn',1,'Point Act Game · game','group','Play this activity with your teacher and classmates, then choose Done.','Point Act Game\nActivity 1\nDirections: Pick a word card inside the box or bag. Read the\nword. Find the words inside the classroom. Read, point, act\nand write them on the board (e.g. half ½, 9, 11, etc.) Do it again\nand again.\nwhite','assets/images/level5/g4/p018-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level5/g4/p018-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level5/g4/p018-2.webp\"]','Point Act Game Activity 1 Directions: Pick a word card inside the box or bag. Read the word. Find the words inside the classroom. Read, point, act and write them on the board (e.g. half ½, 9, 11, etc.) Do it again and again. white',NULL,10,18,'Point Act Game\nActivity 1\nDirections: Pick a word card inside the box or bag. Read the\nword. Find the words inside the classroom. Read, point, act\nand write them on the board (e.g. half ½, 9, 11, etc.) Do it again\nand again.\nwhite',1,1,'perform'),
