(885,247,79,'post',2,'Post-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','11. A young cat that plays and meows is called a k i _ _ e\n_.\n12. The ring is made of g_ _ d, a shiny yellow metal.\n13. A tool that keeps you dry in the rain is an _ m b _ e _ _\na.\n14. Mother cooked b _ _ ns, small seeds eaten with rice.\n15. A type of large herbivore with antlers is a d _ _ r.\n16. We listened to the news on the r_ d_ o.\n17. All people together are called co_ _ uni_ y.\n18. A small insect that can crawl and bite is an _ n _.\n19. I ate a ba_ an_, a long yellow fruit.\n20. The tree has many le_ a_es.\nII. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nA. Directions: Listen carefully as the teacher reads each\nsentence. Fill in the blank with the correct word you hear.\nThe cat is sleeping on my bed. She raised her hand to answer\nthe question. The sun rises in the east every morning. I ate a\npiece of cake for dessert. The dog wagged its tail happily.\n21. The dog wagged its ______\nhappily.\n22. The sun rises in the ______\n.\n23. The cat is sleeping on my ______\n.\n24. I ate a piece of ______\nfor dessert.\n25. She raised her ______\nto answer the question.',NULL,'[]','11. A young cat that plays and meows is called a k i _ _ e _. 12. The ring is made of g_ _ d, a shiny yellow metal. 13. A tool that keeps you dry in the rain is an _ m b _ e _ _ a. 14. Mother cooked b _ _ ns, small seeds eaten with rice. 15. A type of large herbivore with antlers is a d _ _ r. 16. We listened to the news on the r_ d_ o. 17. All people together are called co_ _ uni_ y. 18. A small insect that can crawl and bite is an _ n _. 19. I ate a ba_ an_, a long yellow fruit. 20. The tree has many le_ a_es. II. Listening Comprehension (5 items) A. Directions: Listen carefully as the teacher reads each sentence. Fill in the blank with the correct word you hear. The cat is sleeping on my bed. She raised her hand to answer the question. The sun rises in the east every morning. I ate a piece of cake for dessert. The dog wagged its tail happily. 21. The dog wagged its blank happily. 22. The sun rises in the blank . 23. The cat is sleeping on my blank . 24. I ate a piece of blank for dessert. 25. She raised her blank to answer the question.',NULL,10,45,'11. A young cat that plays and meows is called a k i _ _ e\n_.\n12. The ring is made of g_ _ d, a shiny yellow metal.\n13. A tool that keeps you dry in the rain is an _ m b _ e _ _\na.\n14. Mother cooked b _ _ ns, small seeds eaten with rice.\n15. A type of large herbivore with antlers is a d _ _ r.\n16. We listened to the news on the r_ d_ o.\n17. All people together are called co_ _ uni_ y.\n18. A small insect that can crawl and bite is an _ n _.\n19. I ate a ba_ an_, a long yellow fruit.\n20. The tree has many le_ a_es.\nII. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nA. Directions: Listen carefully as the teacher reads each\nsentence. Fill in the blank with the correct word you hear.\nThe cat is sleeping on my bed. She raised her hand to answer\nthe question. The sun rises in the east every morning. I ate a\npiece of cake for dessert. The dog wagged its tail happily.\n21. The dog wagged its ______\nhappily.\n22. The sun rises in the ______\n.\n23. The cat is sleeping on my ______\n.\n24. I ate a piece of ______\nfor dessert.\n25. She raised her ______\nto answer the question.',1,1,'answer'),
(886,247,79,'post',3,'Post-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','B. Direction : Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her\ndog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park,\nLila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always\nbrings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the\nbirds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond\nQuestions:\n26. What animals does Lila watch at the park? ______\n27. Who goes with Lila to the park? ______\n28. What does Lila bring with her? ______\n29. What color is Lila’s dog? ______\n30. Name two things Lila does at the park. ______\nE. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLast weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The\nplace was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card\nso our friends would know where we were. Around the camp\nwas a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance,\nwe could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky\nand saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our\ncountry.\n31. How does the bag feel?\nA. Gone\nB. Heavy\nC. Clean\nD. Enough\n32. What must each student do carefully?\nA. Write\nB. Read',NULL,'[]','B. Direction : Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the correct answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your answer on your paper. Lila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her dog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park, Lila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always brings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the birds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond Questions: 26. What animals does Lila watch at the park? blank 27. Who goes with Lila to the park? blank 28. What does Lila bring with her? blank 29. What color is Lila’s dog? blank 30. Name two things Lila does at the park. blank E. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the correct answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your answer on your paper. Last weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The place was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card so our friends would know where we were. Around the camp was a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance, we could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky and saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our country. 31. How does the bag feel? A. Gone B. Heavy C. Clean D. Enough 32. What must each student do carefully? A. Write B. Read',NULL,10,46,'B. Direction : Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her\ndog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park,\nLila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always\nbrings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the\nbirds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond\nQuestions:\n26. What animals does Lila watch at the park? ______\n27. Who goes with Lila to the park? ______\n28. What does Lila bring with her? ______\n29. What color is Lila’s dog? ______\n30. Name two things Lila does at the park. ______\nE. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLast weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The\nplace was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card\nso our friends would know where we were. Around the camp\nwas a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance,\nwe could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky\nand saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our\ncountry.\n31. How does the bag feel?\nA. Gone\nB. Heavy\nC. Clean\nD. Enough\n32. What must each student do carefully?\nA. Write\nB. Read',1,1,'answer'),
(887,247,79,'post',4,'Post-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','C. Count\nD. Clean\n33. What is full of words?\nA. The page\nB. The bag\nC. The table\nD. The room\n34. Where is the book placed?\nA. Under the chair\nB. On the floor\nC. On the left side of the table\nD. On the right side of the room\n35. What is the room like now?\nA. Heavy\nB. Dirty\nC. Clean\nD. Full\nF. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nThe farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will\npress the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will\npay the workers. In March, the children will march in the\nparade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The\nteam will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the\nclothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very\nbusy. At night, the children dream of a better future.\n36. What do the children dream of at night?\nA. Playing games\nB. Traveling far\nC. A better future\nD. Going to school\n37. When do the children march in the parade?\nA. April\nB. January',NULL,'[]','C. Count D. Clean 33. What is full of words? A. The page B. The bag C. The table D. The room 34. Where is the book placed? A. Under the chair B. On the floor C. On the left side of the table D. On the right side of the room 35. What is the room like now? A. Heavy B. Dirty C. Clean D. Full F. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the correct answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your answer on your paper. The farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will press the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will pay the workers. In March, the children will march in the parade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The team will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the clothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very busy. At night, the children dream of a better future. 36. What do the children dream of at night? A. Playing games B. Traveling far C. A better future D. Going to school 37. When do the children march in the parade? A. April B. January',NULL,10,47,'C. Count\nD. Clean\n33. What is full of words?\nA. The page\nB. The bag\nC. The table\nD. The room\n34. Where is the book placed?\nA. Under the chair\nB. On the floor\nC. On the left side of the table\nD. On the right side of the room\n35. What is the room like now?\nA. Heavy\nB. Dirty\nC. Clean\nD. Full\nF. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nThe farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will\npress the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will\npay the workers. In March, the children will march in the\nparade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The\nteam will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the\nclothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very\nbusy. At night, the children dream of a better future.\n36. What do the children dream of at night?\nA. Playing games\nB. Traveling far\nC. A better future\nD. Going to school\n37. When do the children march in the parade?\nA. April\nB. January',1,1,'answer'),
(888,247,79,'post',5,'Post-assessment (Activities 11–20) · page 5','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','C. February\nD. March\n38. What will the farmer plant?\nA. Fruits\nB. Seeds\nC. Trees\nD. Flowers\n39. What should people NOT do to animals?\nA. Feed them\nB. Kill them\nC. Care for them\nD. Watch them\nWhat does the farmer do to the soil?\nA. Dries it\nB. Removes it\nC. Presses it\nD. Waters it',NULL,'[]','C. February D. March 38. What will the farmer plant? A. Fruits B. Seeds C. Trees D. Flowers 39. What should people NOT do to animals? A. Feed them B. Kill them C. Care for them D. Watch them What does the farmer do to the soil? A. Dries it B. Removes it C. Presses it D. Waters it',NULL,10,48,'C. February\nD. March\n38. What will the farmer plant?\nA. Fruits\nB. Seeds\nC. Trees\nD. Flowers\n39. What should people NOT do to animals?\nA. Feed them\nB. Kill them\nC. Care for them\nD. Watch them\nWhat does the farmer do to the soil?\nA. Dries it\nB. Removes it\nC. Presses it\nD. Waters it',1,1,'answer'),
(889,248,80,'pre',1,'Pre-test · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Pre- Test Assessment (Activity 1-10)\nI. Vocabulary Development: Synonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the same meaning as the\nunderlined word.\n1. A tragic accident happened on the road.\na. twin\nb. crash\nc. reply\nd. risk\n2. The view of the mountain is so beautiful.\na. low\nb. wash\nc. pretty\nd. dirt\n3. Please answer the question honestly.\na. select\nb. go\nc. reply\nd. mind\n4. I need to bathe the baby before dinner.\na. cover\nb. fix\nc. wash\nd. glue\n5. The chief decided to end the meeting early.\na. audience\nb. disagree\nc. leader\nd. day\n6. Did you choose the right materials for the project?\na. end\nb. start\nc. select\nd. time\n7. He received a double amount of reward.\na. earth\nb. low\nc. twin\nd. supper\n8. They went against the mayor\'s decision.\na. time\nb. disagree\nc. alone\nd. eating\n9. She will go to the market this afternoon.\na. begin\nb. move\nc. finish\nd. round\n10. Look at the big blue ocean.\na. time\nb. sea\nc. soil\nd. date',NULL,'[]','Pre- Test Assessment (Activity 1-10) I. Vocabulary Development: Synonyms (10 items) Directions: Choose the letter of the word that has the same meaning as the underlined word. 1. A tragic accident happened on the road. a. twin b. crash c. reply d. risk 2. The view of the mountain is so beautiful. a. low b. wash c. pretty d. dirt 3. Please answer the question honestly. a. select b. go c. reply d. mind 4. I need to bathe the baby before dinner. a. cover b. fix c. wash d. glue 5. The chief decided to end the meeting early. a. audience b. disagree c. leader d. day 6. Did you choose the right materials for the project? a. end b. start c. select d. time 7. He received a double amount of reward. a. earth b. low c. twin d. supper 8. They went against the mayor\'s decision. a. time b. disagree c. alone d. eating 9. She will go to the market this afternoon. a. begin b. move c. finish d. round 10. Look at the big blue ocean. a. time b. sea c. soil d. date',NULL,10,6,'Pre- Test Assessment (Activity 1-10)\nI. Vocabulary Development: Synonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the same meaning as the\nunderlined word.\n1. A tragic accident happened on the road.\na. twin\nb. crash\nc. reply\nd. risk\n2. The view of the mountain is so beautiful.\na. low\nb. wash\nc. pretty\nd. dirt\n3. Please answer the question honestly.\na. select\nb. go\nc. reply\nd. mind\n4. I need to bathe the baby before dinner.\na. cover\nb. fix\nc. wash\nd. glue\n5. The chief decided to end the meeting early.\na. audience\nb. disagree\nc. leader\nd. day\n6. Did you choose the right materials for the project?\na. end\nb. start\nc. select\nd. time\n7. He received a double amount of reward.\na. earth\nb. low\nc. twin\nd. supper\n8. They went against the mayor\'s decision.\na. time\nb. disagree\nc. alone\nd. eating\n9. She will go to the market this afternoon.\na. begin\nb. move\nc. finish\nd. round\n10. Look at the big blue ocean.\na. time\nb. sea\nc. soil\nd. date',1,1,'answer'),
(890,248,80,'pre',2,'Pre-test · page 2','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','II. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning of\nthe underlined word.\n11. She began to cry after failing the test.\na. remember\nb. believe\nc. laugh\nd. worry\n12. We should act quickly to help the victim.\na. lie\nb. do nothing\nc. catch\nd. free\n13. Don\'t be careless when handling glass.\na. tomorrow\nb. careful\nc. south\nd. outdoors\n14. His camera produces blurry pictures.\na. end\nb. clear\nc. glad\nd. morning\n15. The sun rises in the evening.\na. start\nb. morning\nc. often\nd. lad\n16. She felt sad when her favorite toy broke.\na. truth\nb. glad\nc. strong\nd. ache\n17. He told a lie to avoid getting into trouble.\na. rejoice\nb. truth\nc. doubt\nd. worry\n18. He stays indoors all day when it rains.\na. outdoors\nb. lady\nc. sir\nd. yesterday\n19. The winter clothes are very thick.\na. weak\nb. thin\nc. healthy\nd. beautiful\n20. She visits her grandmother often.\na. tomorrow\nb. sometimes\nc. mountain\nd. men',NULL,'[]','II. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items) Directions: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning of the underlined word. 11. She began to cry after failing the test. a. remember b. believe c. laugh d. worry 12. We should act quickly to help the victim. a. lie b. do nothing c. catch d. free 13. Don\'t be careless when handling glass. a. tomorrow b. careful c. south d. outdoors 14. His camera produces blurry pictures. a. end b. clear c. glad d. morning 15. The sun rises in the evening. a. start b. morning c. often d. lad 16. She felt sad when her favorite toy broke. a. truth b. glad c. strong d. ache 17. He told a lie to avoid getting into trouble. a. rejoice b. truth c. doubt d. worry 18. He stays indoors all day when it rains. a. outdoors b. lady c. sir d. yesterday 19. The winter clothes are very thick. a. weak b. thin c. healthy d. beautiful 20. She visits her grandmother often. a. tomorrow b. sometimes c. mountain d. men',NULL,10,7,'II. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning of\nthe underlined word.\n11. She began to cry after failing the test.\na. remember\nb. believe\nc. laugh\nd. worry\n12. We should act quickly to help the victim.\na. lie\nb. do nothing\nc. catch\nd. free\n13. Don\'t be careless when handling glass.\na. tomorrow\nb. careful\nc. south\nd. outdoors\n14. His camera produces blurry pictures.\na. end\nb. clear\nc. glad\nd. morning\n15. The sun rises in the evening.\na. start\nb. morning\nc. often\nd. lad\n16. She felt sad when her favorite toy broke.\na. truth\nb. glad\nc. strong\nd. ache\n17. He told a lie to avoid getting into trouble.\na. rejoice\nb. truth\nc. doubt\nd. worry\n18. He stays indoors all day when it rains.\na. outdoors\nb. lady\nc. sir\nd. yesterday\n19. The winter clothes are very thick.\na. weak\nb. thin\nc. healthy\nd. beautiful\n20. She visits her grandmother often.\na. tomorrow\nb. sometimes\nc. mountain\nd. men',1,1,'answer'),
(891,248,80,'pre',3,'Pre-test · page 3','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','III. Vocabulary Development: Noun or Verb (5 items)\nDirections: Read the word and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V).\n21. Spoke:\na. N\nb. V\n22. Thumb:\na. N\nb. V\n23. Heart:\na. N\nb. V\n24. Follow:\na. N\nb. V\n25. Shadow:\na. N\nb. V\nIV. Listening Comprehension & Vocabulary: Homophones (10 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence and choose the correct word in the\nparenthesis that completes the meaning.\n26. She has a slim (waist / waste).\na. waste\nb. waist\n27. His hard work was put into (waist / waste).\na. waste\nb. waist\n28. Father (war / wore) a nice long sleeve.\na. war\nb. wore\n29. Our houses (coast / cost) five million.\na. coast\nb. cost\n30. I live near the (coast / cost).\na. coast\nb. cost\n31. He who lives with hope will (die / dye) by hunger.\na. die\nb. dye\n32. Christopher Columbus set (sail / sale) for around the World in 1492.\na. sail\nb. sale\n33. Please, (wait / weight) just a moment!\na. wait\nb. weight',NULL,'[]','III. Vocabulary Development: Noun or Verb (5 items) Directions: Read the word and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V). 21. Spoke: a. N b. V 22. Thumb: a. N b. V 23. Heart: a. N b. V 24. Follow: a. N b. V 25. Shadow: a. N b. V IV. Listening Comprehension & Vocabulary: Homophones (10 items) Directions: Read the sentence and choose the correct word in the parenthesis that completes the meaning. 26. She has a slim (waist / waste). a. waste b. waist 27. His hard work was put into (waist / waste). a. waste b. waist 28. Father (war / wore) a nice long sleeve. a. war b. wore 29. Our houses (coast / cost) five million. a. coast b. cost 30. I live near the (coast / cost). a. coast b. cost 31. He who lives with hope will (die / dye) by hunger. a. die b. dye 32. Christopher Columbus set (sail / sale) for around the World in 1492. a. sail b. sale 33. Please, (wait / weight) just a moment! a. wait b. weight',NULL,10,8,'III. Vocabulary Development: Noun or Verb (5 items)\nDirections: Read the word and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V).\n21. Spoke:\na. N\nb. V\n22. Thumb:\na. N\nb. V\n23. Heart:\na. N\nb. V\n24. Follow:\na. N\nb. V\n25. Shadow:\na. N\nb. V\nIV. Listening Comprehension & Vocabulary: Homophones (10 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence and choose the correct word in the\nparenthesis that completes the meaning.\n26. She has a slim (waist / waste).\na. waste\nb. waist\n27. His hard work was put into (waist / waste).\na. waste\nb. waist\n28. Father (war / wore) a nice long sleeve.\na. war\nb. wore\n29. Our houses (coast / cost) five million.\na. coast\nb. cost\n30. I live near the (coast / cost).\na. coast\nb. cost\n31. He who lives with hope will (die / dye) by hunger.\na. die\nb. dye\n32. Christopher Columbus set (sail / sale) for around the World in 1492.\na. sail\nb. sale\n33. Please, (wait / weight) just a moment!\na. wait\nb. weight',1,1,'answer'),
(892,248,80,'pre',4,'Pre-test · page 4','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','34. He spent the (hole / whole) day reading in bed.\na. hole\nb. whole\n35. This (rode / road) is too narrow for cars.\na. rode\nb. road\nV. Listening Comprehension: Context Clues (5 items)\nDirections: Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen carefully and\nwrite the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the line.\n36.(Teacher reads: \"A companion or colleague.\")\n37.(Teacher reads: \"A person who treats teeth and gums.\")\n38.(Teacher reads: \"Trousers or slacks.\")\n39.(Teacher reads: \"A vessel or a craft.\")\n40.(Teacher reads: \"The cause or explanation for something.\")',NULL,'[]','34. He spent the (hole / whole) day reading in bed. a. hole b. whole 35. This (rode / road) is too narrow for cars. a. rode b. road V. Listening Comprehension: Context Clues (5 items) Directions: Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen carefully and write the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the line. 36.(Teacher reads: \"A companion or colleague.\") 37.(Teacher reads: \"A person who treats teeth and gums.\") 38.(Teacher reads: \"Trousers or slacks.\") 39.(Teacher reads: \"A vessel or a craft.\") 40.(Teacher reads: \"The cause or explanation for something.\")',NULL,10,9,'34. He spent the (hole / whole) day reading in bed.\na. hole\nb. whole\n35. This (rode / road) is too narrow for cars.\na. rode\nb. road\nV. Listening Comprehension: Context Clues (5 items)\nDirections: Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen carefully and\nwrite the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the line.\n36.(Teacher reads: \"A companion or colleague.\")\n37.(Teacher reads: \"A person who treats teeth and gums.\")\n38.(Teacher reads: \"Trousers or slacks.\")\n39.(Teacher reads: \"A vessel or a craft.\")\n40.(Teacher reads: \"The cause or explanation for something.\")',1,1,'answ