(901,257,NULL,'learn',1,'Homophone · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings\nActivity 9- Homophone\nDirection: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis.\n1. She has a slim (waist, waste).\n2. His hard work was put into (waist, waste).\n3. Thank God, the (war, wore) has ended.\n4. Father (war, wore) a nice long sleeve.\n5. Ana has a slender (body, buddy).\n6. My friend is my (body, buddy).\n7. Our houses (coast, cost) five million.\n8. I live near the (coast, cost).\n9. I like to (die, dye) my hair\n10. He who lives with hope will (die, dye) by hunger.\n11. I am happy (each, itch) time you are here.\n12. The (itch, each) will not go away.\n13. This money is your back and (forth, fourth) fare.\n14. He ranks (forth, fourth) in his class.\n15. I love crushed (ice, eyes) with milk and sugar.',NULL,'[]','Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings Activity 9- Homophone Direction: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis. 1. She has a slim (waist, waste). 2. His hard work was put into (waist, waste). 3. Thank God, the (war, wore) has ended. 4. Father (war, wore) a nice long sleeve. 5. Ana has a slender (body, buddy). 6. My friend is my (body, buddy). 7. Our houses (coast, cost) five million. 8. I live near the (coast, cost). 9. I like to (die, dye) my hair 10. He who lives with hope will (die, dye) by hunger. 11. I am happy (each, itch) time you are here. 12. The (itch, each) will not go away. 13. This money is your back and (forth, fourth) fare. 14. He ranks (forth, fourth) in his class. 15. I love crushed (ice, eyes) with milk and sugar.',NULL,10,19,'Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings\nActivity 9- Homophone\nDirection: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis.\n1. She has a slim (waist, waste).\n2. His hard work was put into (waist, waste).\n3. Thank God, the (war, wore) has ended.\n4. Father (war, wore) a nice long sleeve.\n5. Ana has a slender (body, buddy).\n6. My friend is my (body, buddy).\n7. Our houses (coast, cost) five million.\n8. I live near the (coast, cost).\n9. I like to (die, dye) my hair\n10. He who lives with hope will (die, dye) by hunger.\n11. I am happy (each, itch) time you are here.\n12. The (itch, each) will not go away.\n13. This money is your back and (forth, fourth) fare.\n14. He ranks (forth, fourth) in his class.\n15. I love crushed (ice, eyes) with milk and sugar.',1,1,'answer'),
(902,258,NULL,'learn',1,'Homophone · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings\nActivity 10 - Homophone\nDirection: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis.\n1. Christopher Columbus set (sail, sale) for around the World in\n1492.\n2. Please, (wait, weight) just a moment!\n3. He spent the (hole, whole) day reading in bed.\n4. This (rode, road) is too narrow for cars.\n5. One (cent, sent) is still has a value.\n6. (Our, hour) library has many books.\n7. How much is the taxi (fare, fair) to the hotel?\n8. I’ve (heard, herd) the French version of this song.\n9. She put her piano up for (sale, sail)\n10. Let us meet at the park in one (our, hour).\n11. She got on her bike and (road, rode) away.\n12. The cowboys rounded up the (heard, herd) of cattle.\n13. There is a big (hole, whole) on the road.\n14. He (sent, cent) his car to the shop.\n15. His (weight, wait) is twice his older brother.',NULL,'[]','Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings Activity 10 - Homophone Direction: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis. 1. Christopher Columbus set (sail, sale) for around the World in 1492. 2. Please, (wait, weight) just a moment! 3. He spent the (hole, whole) day reading in bed. 4. This (rode, road) is too narrow for cars. 5. One (cent, sent) is still has a value. 6. (Our, hour) library has many books. 7. How much is the taxi (fare, fair) to the hotel? 8. I’ve (heard, herd) the French version of this song. 9. She put her piano up for (sale, sail) 10. Let us meet at the park in one (our, hour). 11. She got on her bike and (road, rode) away. 12. The cowboys rounded up the (heard, herd) of cattle. 13. There is a big (hole, whole) on the road. 14. He (sent, cent) his car to the shop. 15. His (weight, wait) is twice his older brother.',NULL,10,20,'Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings\nActivity 10 - Homophone\nDirection: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis.\n1. Christopher Columbus set (sail, sale) for around the World in\n1492.\n2. Please, (wait, weight) just a moment!\n3. He spent the (hole, whole) day reading in bed.\n4. This (rode, road) is too narrow for cars.\n5. One (cent, sent) is still has a value.\n6. (Our, hour) library has many books.\n7. How much is the taxi (fare, fair) to the hotel?\n8. I’ve (heard, herd) the French version of this song.\n9. She put her piano up for (sale, sail)\n10. Let us meet at the park in one (our, hour).\n11. She got on her bike and (road, rode) away.\n12. The cowboys rounded up the (heard, herd) of cattle.\n13. There is a big (hole, whole) on the road.\n14. He (sent, cent) his car to the shop.\n15. His (weight, wait) is twice his older brother.',1,1,'answer'),
(903,259,NULL,'learn',1,'Match to Complete the Sentence · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Matching Meanings\nActivity 11- Match to Complete the Sentence\nDirection: In column A are the phrases. In column B are the words.\nMatch\ncolumn A with column B by drawing a line.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. I worship and pray in the ______\n.\na. eleven\n2. You are hurt and you feel the ______\n.\nb. peach\n3. The ______\nassists the doctor.\nc. root\n4. When you study in a dark room, you use ______\n.\nd. church\n5. When I sleep, I love to hug my big ______\n.\ne. pain\n6. Mother uses a colorful floor covering called ______\n.\nf. lamp\n7. Use ______\nin measuring the length of your pen.\ng. rug\n8. A ______\nand arrow can be used for hunting.\nh. silk\n9. Sweet potato is an example of a ______\ncrop.\ni. drawer\n10. In the garden, you can see some ______\n.\nj. butterflies\n11. My favorite color is ______\n.\nk. lie\n12. Don’t ______\n, tell the truth.\nl. ruler\n13. A ______\nis produced by silkworms.\nm. pillow\n14. Get my jewelry in the ______\n.\nn. nurse\n15. ______\nis the number after ten.\no. bow',NULL,'[]','Matching Meanings Activity 11- Match to Complete the Sentence Direction: In column A are the phrases. In column B are the words. Match column A with column B by drawing a line. Column A Column B 1. I worship and pray in the blank . a. eleven 2. You are hurt and you feel the blank . b. peach 3. The blank assists the doctor. c. root 4. When you study in a dark room, you use blank . d. church 5. When I sleep, I love to hug my big blank . e. pain 6. Mother uses a colorful floor covering called blank . f. lamp 7. Use blank in measuring the length of your pen. g. rug 8. A blank and arrow can be used for hunting. h. silk 9. Sweet potato is an example of a blank crop. i. drawer 10. In the garden, you can see some blank . j. butterflies 11. My favorite color is blank . k. lie 12. Don’t blank