(905,261,NULL,'learn',1,'Context Clue · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Giving Hints\nActivity 13- Context Clue\nDirection: Read the context clues to identify the correct meaning\nof the underlined word below.\n1. An automobile is a road vehicle, typically with four wheels,\npowered by an engine and able to carry a small number of\npeople.\na. bicycle\nb. car\nc. carriage\nd. truck\n2. A strip of material used to bind a wound or to protect an injured\npart of the body is called a bandage.\na. cloth\nb. plaster\nc. ribbon\nd. string\n3. The wound is bleeding, losing more blood and it’s scary.\na.\nclosing\nb. fine\nc. healing\nd. hemorrhaging\n4. I like to write on the blackboard because I have plenty of\nchalk, it’s mounted on the wall and it’s smooth.\na. bond paper b. cardboard\nc. chalkboard\nd. colored paper\n5. Our classroom is dusty, please bring me a broom, that is long,\nhandle for sweeping.\na. brush\nb. rag\nc. scrub\nd. sweeper\n6. The stomach is an internal organ where digestion of food occurs\na. abdomen\nb. brain\nc. heart\nd. lung\n7. Sandro speaks wisely as he expresses his ideas to the public with\npride.\na. dream\nb. rejoice\nc. shout\nd. talk',NULL,'[]','Giving Hints Activity 13- Context Clue Direction: Read the context clues to identify the correct meaning of the underlined word below. 1. An automobile is a road vehicle, typically with four wheels, powered by an engine and able to carry a small number of people. a. bicycle b. car c. carriage d. truck 2. A strip of material used to bind a wound or to protect an injured part of the body is called a bandage. a. cloth b. plaster c. ribbon d. string 3. The wound is bleeding, losing more blood and it’s scary. a. closing b. fine c. healing d. hemorrhaging 4. I like to write on the blackboard because I have plenty of chalk, it’s mounted on the wall and it’s smooth. a. bond paper b. cardboard c. chalkboard d. colored paper 5. Our classroom is dusty, please bring me a broom, that is long, handle for sweeping. a. brush b. rag c. scrub d. sweeper 6. The stomach is an internal organ where digestion of food occurs a. abdomen b. brain c. heart d. lung 7. Sandro speaks wisely as he expresses his ideas to the public with pride. a. dream b. rejoice c. shout d. talk',NULL,10,23,'Giving Hints\nActivity 13- Context Clue\nDirection: Read the context clues to identify the correct meaning\nof the underlined word below.\n1. An automobile is a road vehicle, typically with four wheels,\npowered by an engine and able to carry a small number of\npeople.\na. bicycle\nb. car\nc. carriage\nd. truck\n2. A strip of material used to bind a wound or to protect an injured\npart of the body is called a bandage.\na. cloth\nb. plaster\nc. ribbon\nd. string\n3. The wound is bleeding, losing more blood and it’s scary.\na.\nclosing\nb. fine\nc. healing\nd. hemorrhaging\n4. I like to write on the blackboard because I have plenty of\nchalk, it’s mounted on the wall and it’s smooth.\na. bond paper b. cardboard\nc. chalkboard\nd. colored paper\n5. Our classroom is dusty, please bring me a broom, that is long,\nhandle for sweeping.\na. brush\nb. rag\nc. scrub\nd. sweeper\n6. The stomach is an internal organ where digestion of food occurs\na. abdomen\nb. brain\nc. heart\nd. lung\n7. Sandro speaks wisely as he expresses his ideas to the public with\npride.\na. dream\nb. rejoice\nc. shout\nd. talk',1,1,'answer'),
