(917,269,81,'post',1,'Post-test · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','Post-Test Assessment: (1-10)\nVocabulary and Listening Comprehension (Items 1–40)\nI. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning as\nthe underlined word.\n1. She felt glad when she won the medal.\na. strong\nb. sad\nc. truth\nd. ache\n2. The old photograph is very clear.\na. blurry\nb. light\nc. happy\nd. long\n3. He decided to lie about the broken vase.\na. truth\nb. doubt\nc. rejoice\nd. worry\n4. I will end my presentation with a summary.\na. often\nb. start\nc. tomorrow\nd. sir\n5. You must remember to lock the door.\na. forget\nb. lad\nc. act\nd. weak\n6. The children began to laugh at the funny story.\na. cry\nb. believe\nc. catch\nd. free\n7. He is too weak to lift the box.\na. strong\nb. thin\nc. ugly\nd. bad\n8. They went outdoors to play basketball.\na. north\nb. lady\nc. indoors\nd. sometimes\n9. She is very careful with her school supplies.\na. tomorrow\nb. careless\nc. south\nd. morning\n10. The blanket is too thin for this cold weather.\na. healthy\nb. thick\nc. beautiful\nd. pretty',NULL,'[]','Post-Test Assessment: (1-10) Vocabulary and Listening Comprehension (Items 1–40) I. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items) Directions: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning as the underlined word. 1. She felt glad when she won the medal. a. strong b. sad c. truth d. ache 2. The old photograph is very clear. a. blurry b. light c. happy d. long 3. He decided to lie about the broken vase. a. truth b. doubt c. rejoice d. worry 4. I will end my presentation with a summary. a. often b. start c. tomorrow d. sir 5. You must remember to lock the door. a. forget b. lad c. act d. weak 6. The children began to laugh at the funny story. a. cry b. believe c. catch d. free 7. He is too weak to lift the box. a. strong b. thin c. ugly d. bad 8. They went outdoors to play basketball. a. north b. lady c. indoors d. sometimes 9. She is very careful with her school supplies. a. tomorrow b. careless c. south d. morning 10. The blanket is too thin for this cold weather. a. healthy b. thick c. beautiful d. pretty',NULL,10,36,'Post-Test Assessment: (1-10)\nVocabulary and Listening Comprehension (Items 1–40)\nI. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning as\nthe underlined word.\n1. She felt glad when she won the medal.\na. strong\nb. sad\nc. truth\nd. ache\n2. The old photograph is very clear.\na. blurry\nb. light\nc. happy\nd. long\n3. He decided to lie about the broken vase.\na. truth\nb. doubt\nc. rejoice\nd. worry\n4. I will end my presentation with a summary.\na. often\nb. start\nc. tomorrow\nd. sir\n5. You must remember to lock the door.\na. forget\nb. lad\nc. act\nd. weak\n6. The children began to laugh at the funny story.\na. cry\nb. believe\nc. catch\nd. free\n7. He is too weak to lift the box.\na. strong\nb. thin\nc. ugly\nd. bad\n8. They went outdoors to play basketball.\na. north\nb. lady\nc. indoors\nd. sometimes\n9. She is very careful with her school supplies.\na. tomorrow\nb. careless\nc. south\nd. morning\n10. The blanket is too thin for this cold weather.\na. healthy\nb. thick\nc. beautiful\nd. pretty',1,1,'answer'),
