(943,290,82,'pre',1,'Pre-test · page 1','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','PRETEST\nPart A — Numbers & Colors (1–4)\nInstructions: Read, understand and answer the questions correctly.\n1. Write the number: “seven” → ______\n2. Write the number word: “12 → ______\n”\n3. What color is the sky on a clear day?\na. blue\nb. red\nc. green\n4. Which word is a color?\na. run\nb. yellow\nc. happy\nPart B — Adverbs (5–6)\n5. Choose the adverb:\na. slowly\nb. tiger\nc. table\n6. Choose the sentence that uses an adverb correctly:\na. The cat runs quickly.\nb. The cat quickly.\nc. The quick cat run.\nPart C — Antonyms (7–8)\n7. Find the opposite of “big”:\na. tall\nb. small\nc. long\n8. The antonym of “happy” is ______\n.\na. sad\nb. joyful\nc. glad',NULL,'[]','PRETEST Part A — Numbers & Colors (1–4) Instructions: Read, understand and answer the questions correctly. 1. Write the number: “seven” → blank 2. Write the number word: “12 → blank ” 3. What color is the sky on a clear day? a. blue b. red c. green 4. Which word is a color? a. run b. yellow c. happy Part B — Adverbs (5–6) 5. Choose the adverb: a. slowly b. tiger c. table 6. Choose the sentence that uses an adverb correctly: a. The cat runs quickly. b. The cat quickly. c. The quick cat run. Part C — Antonyms (7–8) 7. Find the opposite of “big”: a. tall b. small c. long 8. The antonym of “happy” is blank . a. sad b. joyful c. glad',NULL,10,6,'PRETEST\nPart A — Numbers & Colors (1–4)\nInstructions: Read, understand and answer the questions correctly.\n1. Write the number: “seven” → ______\n2. Write the number word: “12 → ______\n”\n3. What color is the sky on a clear day?\na. blue\nb. red\nc. green\n4. Which word is a color?\na. run\nb. yellow\nc. happy\nPart B — Adverbs (5–6)\n5. Choose the adverb:\na. slowly\nb. tiger\nc. table\n6. Choose the sentence that uses an adverb correctly:\na. The cat runs quickly.\nb. The cat quickly.\nc. The quick cat run.\nP