(966,311,83,'post',1,'Post-test · questions','open','Listen and look at the page. Type or say your answers with their numbers, for example 1-b, 2-a.','POST TEST\nPart A — Numbers (1–4)\n1. Write the number word: 3 = ______\n2. Write the number: “five” = ______\n3. Which is a number?\na) red b) six c) cat\n4. What number comes after 2? ______\nPart B — Colors (5–6)\n5. Which is a color?\na) blue b) run c) book\n6. The sun is ______\n.\na) yellow b) green c) black\nPart C — Adverbs (7–8)\n7. Choose the adverb:\na) quickly b) dog\nc) chair\n8. “She sings softly.”\nThe adverb is: ______\nPart D — Antonyms (Opposites) (9–10)\n9. Opposite of hot is ______\n.\n10. Opposite of big:\na) small b) tall c) long\nPart E — Synonyms (Same meaning) (11–12)\n11. “Happy” means the same as:\na) sad b) glad\nc) angry\n12. “Start” means the same as ______\n.\na) begin\nb) stop c) sleep\nPart F — Nouns (13–14)\n13. Which is a noun?\na) pencil\nb) run c) quickly\n14. Which is a place?\na) school b) blue c) jump',NULL,'[]','POST TEST Part A — Numbers (1–4) 1. Write the number word: 3 = blank 2. Write the number: “five” = blank 3. Which is a number? a) red b) six c) cat 4. What number comes after 2? blank Part B — Colors (5–6) 5. Which is a color? a) blue b) run c) book 6. The sun is blank . a) yellow b) green c) black Part C — Adverbs (7–8) 7. Choose the adverb: a) quickly b) dog c) chair 8. “She sings softly.” The adverb is: blank Part D — Antonyms (Opposites) (9–10) 9. Opposite of hot is blank . 10. Opposite of big: a) small b) tall c) long Part E — Synonyms (Same meaning) (11–12) 11. “Happy” means the same as: a) sad b) glad c) angry 12. “Start” means the same as blank . a) begin b) stop c) sleep Part F — Nouns (13–14) 13. Which is a noun? a) pencil b) run c) quickly 14. Which is a place? a) school b) blue c) jump',NULL,10,31,'POST TEST\nPart A — Numbers (1–4)\n1. Write the number word: 3 = ______\n2. Write the number: “five” = ______\n3. Which is a number?\na) red b) six c) cat\n4. What number comes after 2? ______\nPart B — Colors (5–6)\n5. Which is a color?\na) blue b) run c) book\n6. The sun is ______\n.\na) yellow b) green c) black\nPart C — Adverbs (7–8)\n7. Choose the adverb:\na) quickly b) dog\nc) chair\n8. “She sings softly.”\nThe adverb is: ______\nPart D — Antonyms (Opposites) (9–10)\n9. Opposite of hot is ______\n.\n10. Opposite of big:\na) small b) tall c) long\nPart E — Synonyms (Same meaning) (11–12)\n11. “Happy” means the same as:\na) sad b) glad\nc) angry\n12. “Start” means the same as ______\n.\na) begin\nb) stop c) sleep\nPart F — Nouns (13–14)\n13. Which is a noun?\na) pencil\nb) run c) quickly\n14. Which is a place?\na) school b) blue c) jump',1,1,'answer'),
