(987,328,NULL,'learn',1,'Snowball Fight','open','Direction: Read the story. Draw a line to match each cause on the left with its effect on the right.','Direction: Read the story. Draw a line to match each cause on the left with its effect on the right.\n\nSnowball Fight\nIt was winter. The snow fell and it was very cold.\nTim and Mark put on their mittens and boots then went outside to make snowballs.\nJan throw a snowball, but he was not fast enough. Mark saw him and threw one first.\nIt hit Jan and knock him down.\n\nColumn A\n1. Jan was hit by a snowball\n2. Mark throws a snowball\n3. They went outside\n4. The snow fell\n5. They saw a bear\nA. the snowball knocks Jan down.\nB. they ran fast.\nC. because he was not fast enough.\nD. it was very cold.\nE. to make snowballs.','assets/images/level6/g1/p025-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g1/p025-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the story. Draw a line to match each cause on the left with its effect on the right.\n\nSnowball Fight\nIt was winter. The snow fell and it was very cold.\nTim and Mark put on their mittens and boots then went outside to make snowballs.\nJan throw a snowball, but he was not fast enough. Mark saw him and threw one first.\nIt hit Jan and knock him down.\n\nColumn A\n1. Jan was hit by a snowball\n2. Mark throws a snowball\n3. They went outside\n4. The snow fell\n5. They saw a bear\nA. the snowball knocks Jan down.\nB. they ran fast.\nC. because he was not fast enough.\nD. it was very cold.\nE. to make snowballs.',NULL,10,25,'Direction: Read the story. Draw a line to match each cause on the left with its effect on the right.\n\nSnowball Fight\nIt was winter. The snow fell and it was very cold.\nTim and Mark put on their mittens and boots then went outside to make snowballs.\nJan throw a snowball, but he was not fast enough. Mark saw him and threw one first.\nIt hit Jan and knock him down.\n\nColumn A\n1. Jan was hit by a snowball\n2. Mark throws a snowball\n3. They went outside\n4. The snow fell\n5. They saw a bear\nA. the snowball knocks Jan down.\nB. they ran fast.\nC. because he was not fast enough.\nD. it was very cold.\nE. to make snowballs.',1,1,'answer'),
(988,329,NULL,'learn',1,'Alex and His Mother','open','Read the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.','Read the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nAlex and His Mother\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nAlex’s mother checked her list while she carried a basket. They went up from one lane to another. This perhaps means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother went to a picnic.\n☐ Alex and his mother went to a store.\n\nThe basket was getting full. They now had vegetables, fruits, and bananas in the basket. They still needed to get milk, bread, eggs, and rice. This perhaps means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother were buying.\n☐ Alex and his mother were eating.\n\nMany people are waiting in a lane, with baskets full of groceries. Then they stood in line and waited from one customer to another. This probably means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother were paying for their groceries.\n☐ Alex and his mother were choosing from the shelves.\n\nAlex hoped they would get home in time as they waited for a ride for him to go outside and play for a while. This probably means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother are at the park.\n☐ Alex and his mother are at the bus terminal.\n\nHis mother put their groceries on top of the table. He went to his room and immediately changed his clothes. This probably means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother are now inside their house.\n☐ Alex and his mother are now inside the bus.','assets/images/level6/g1/p026-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g1/p026-1.webp\"]','Read the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nAlex and His Mother\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nAlex’s mother checked her list while she carried a basket. They went up from one lane t