(991,332,NULL,'learn',1,'Fishing','open','Read the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.','Read the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nFishing\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nDad and Eric prepare a hook. This probably means that:\n☐ Father and Eric will go farming.\n☐ Father and Eric will go fishing.\n\nEric’s dad helped him put bait on his hook. This probably means that:\n☐ His dad does not want Eric to get hurt.\n☐ His dad does not care about Eric.\n\nHe doesn’t want Eric to be hurt. He showed Eric how to toss his hook out into the water. Then they waited. This probably means that:\n☐ They started fishing.\n☐ They started swimming.\n\nThe hook started to move. When his father took it, it caught a big fish. This probably means that:\n☐ Eric is happy.\n☐ Eric is sad.\n\nWhen they had caught enough fish, Eric’s father started to light a fire. This probably means that:\n☐ Eric’s father will swim.\n☐ Eric’s father will cook the fish they catch.','assets/images/level6/g1/p032-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g1/p032-1.webp\"]','Read the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nFishing\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nDad and Eric prepare a hook. This probably means that:\n☐ Father and Eric will go farming.\n☐ Father and Eric will go fishing.\n\nEric’s dad helped him put bait on his hook. This probably means that:\n☐ His dad does not want Eric to get hurt.\n☐ His dad does not care about Eric.\n\nHe doesn’t want Eric to be hurt. He showed Eric how to toss his hook out into the water. Then they waited. This probably means that:\n☐ They started fishing.\n☐ They started swimming.\n\nThe hook started to move. When his father took it, it