(999,334,86,'pre',4,'Pretest · Cause and Effect','open','Direction: After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.','Direction: After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed at night so…\n☐ the classes were cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jan studied hard so…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: She fell off her bike so…\n☐ she bruised her arm.\n☐ she ate ice cream.\n\nCause: Amora did not study so…\n☐ she failed the exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.',NULL,'[]','Direction: After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed at night so…\n☐ the classes were cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jan studied hard so…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: She fell off her bike so…\n☐ she bruised her arm.\n☐ she ate ice cream.\n\nCause: Amora did not study so…\n☐ she failed the exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.',NULL,10,46,'Direction: After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed at night so…\n☐ the classes were cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jan studied hard so…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: She fell off her bike so…\n☐ she bruised her arm.\n☐ she ate ice cream.\n\nCause: Amora did not study so…\n☐ she failed the exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.',1,1,'answer'),
(1000,334,86,'pre',5,'Pretest · In the Barn','open','Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.','Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIn the Barn\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nThe animals came to the barn. They told each other about their moms. “My mom lay me in the nest,” the chick said. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The chick came out of an egg.\n☐ The chick came out of a shell.\n\n“My mom is a big animal,” the calf said. “She eats plenty of grass to produce milk for me.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him milk.\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him an egg.\n\n“My mother stays in the pen. She says oink, oink, oink,” said the piglet. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also oink, oink, oink.\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also meow, meow, meow.\n\n“My mom loves to eat bones. She guards the master’s house.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ Her mom is a dog who barks at strangers.\n☐ Her mom is a cat who calls at strangers.\n\n“My mother pulls carriages and can be used for transportation,” said the baby horse. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His mother is hardworking.\n☐ His mother just sleeps all day.',NULL,'[]','Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIn the Barn\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nThe animals came to the barn. They told each other about their moms. “My mom lay me in the nest,” the chick said. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The chick came out of an egg.\n☐ The chick came out of a shell.\n\n“My mom is a big animal,” the calf said. “She eats plenty of grass to produce milk for me.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him milk.\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him an egg.\n\n“My mother stays in the pen. She says oink, oink, oink,” said the piglet. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also oink, oink, oink.\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also meow, meow, meow.\n\n“My mom loves to eat bones. She guards the master’s house.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ Her mom is a dog who barks at strangers.\n☐ Her mom is a cat who calls at strangers.\n\n“My mother pulls carriages and can be used for transportation,” said the baby horse. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His mother is hardworking.\n☐ His mother just sleeps all day.',NULL,10,46,'Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIn the Barn\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nThe animals came to the barn. They told each other about their moms. “My mom lay me in the nest,” the chick said. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The chick came out of an egg.\n☐ The chick came out of a shell.\n\n“My mom is a big animal,” the calf said. “She eats plenty of grass to produce milk for me.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him milk.\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him an egg.\n\n“My mother stays in the pen. She says oink, oink, oink,” said the piglet. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also oink, oink, oink.\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also meow, meow, meow.\n\n“My mom loves to eat bones. She guards the master’s house.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ Her mom is a dog who barks at strangers.\n☐ Her mom is a cat who calls at strangers.\n\n“My mother pulls carriages and can be used for transportation,” said the baby horse. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His mother is hardworking.\n☐ His mother just sleeps all day.',1,1,'answer'),
