(1004,338,NULL,'learn',1,'The King','open','Activity 1.4 · Noting details is answering questions from the story read. Direction: Read the selection and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Activity 1.4 · Noting details is answering questions from the story read. Direction: Read the selection and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nThe King\nIn a small Kingdom, a good King lives.\nHis palace is very big.\nIt is on top of the hill.\nEvery morning, he would sit on his balcony and look down at his kingdom.\nHis people make him happy.\n\nWhat is the story all about?\na. The King\nb. The man\nc. The Queen\n\nThe King lives in a very big ______.\na. cave\nb. house\nc. palace\n\nThe palace is on top of the ______.\na. hill\nb. mountain\nc. volcano\n\nWhere does the king sit to watch people?\na. balcony\nb. inside the palace\nc. office\n\nWhat makes the King happy?\na. foods\nb. money\nc. people','assets/images/level6/g2/p012-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p012-1.webp\"]','Activity 1.4 · Noting details is answering questions from the story read. Direction: Read the selection and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nThe King\nIn a small Kingdom, a good King lives.\nHis palace is very big.\nIt is on top of the hill.\nEvery morning, he would sit on his balcony and look down at his kingdom.\nHis people make him happy.\n\nWhat is the story all about?\na. The King\nb. The man\nc. The Queen\n\nThe King lives in a very big ______.\na. cave\nb. house\nc. palace\n\nThe palace is on top of the ______.\na. hill\nb. mountain\nc. volcano\n\nWhere does the king sit to watch people?\na. balcony\nb. inside the palace\nc. office\n\nWhat makes the King happy?\na. foods\nb. money\nc. people',NULL,10,12,'Activity 1.4 · Noting details is answering questions from the story read. Direction: Read the selection and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nThe King\nIn a small Kingdom, a good King lives.\nHis palace is very big.\nIt is on top of the hill.\nEvery morning, he would sit on his balcony and look down at his kingdom.\nHis people make him happy.\n\nWhat is the story all about?\na. The King\nb. The man\nc. The Queen\n\nThe King lives in a very big ______.\na. cave\nb. house\nc. palace\n\nThe palace is on top of the ______.\na. hill\nb. mountain\nc. volcano\n\nWhere does the king sit to watch people?\na. balcony\nb. inside the palace\nc. office\n\nWhat makes the King happy?\na. foods\nb. money\nc. people',1,1,'answer'),
(1005,339,NULL,'learn',1,'At the Park','open','Activity 2.1 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Reality is something that is real and can happen in everyday life; fantasy is imaginary and not real. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.','Activity 2.1 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Reality is something that is real and can happen in everyday life; fantasy is imaginary and not real. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.\n\nAt the Park\nI love to go bird watching at the park. I see a lot of birds there and they are all so colorful! Their little feet are so funny, too. They hop along and then they stretch out their wings and fluff up their feathers.\n\nBirds can be seen in the park.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe birds hop in the trees.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds read books in the library.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nI watch birds at the farm.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds fluff their feathers.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy','assets/images/level6/g2/p014-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p014-1.webp\"]','Activity 2.1 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Reality is something that is real and can happen in everyday life; fantasy is imaginary and not real. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.\n\nAt the Park\nI love to go bird watching at the park. I see a lot of birds there and they are all so colorful! Their little feet are so funny, too. They hop along and then they stretch out their wings and fluff up their feathers.\n\nBirds can be seen in the park.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe birds hop in the trees.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds read books in the library.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nI watch birds at the farm.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds fluff their feathers.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy',NULL,10,14,'Activity 2.1 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Reality is something that is real and can happen in everyday life; fantasy is imaginary and not real. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.\n\nAt the Park\nI love to go bird watching at the park. I see a lot of birds there and they are all so colorful! Their little feet are so funny, too. They hop along and then they stretch out their wings and fluff up their feathers.\n\nBirds can be seen in the park.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe birds hop in the trees.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds read books in the library.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nI watch birds at the farm.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds fluff their feathers.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy',1,1,'answer'),
(1006,340,NULL,'learn',1,'Molly Reads Stories','open','Activity 2.2 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.','Activity 2.2 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.\n\nMolly Reads Stories\nWhen Molly is reading a story, she is looking for clues in the text to help her visualize what is happening. She looks at the pictures and uses them to create a mental image of the story.\n\nShe also reads quickly, which helps her to understand what is happening in the story. When she has finishes reading, she is able to give a detailed description of the story. This shows that Molly is a good reader.\n\nMolly is reading a story.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nShe looks at the picture to create an image of the story.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe pictures in the book laughed at Molly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nAfter reading, the books quickly jumped with Molly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nMolly reads quickly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy','assets/images/level6/g2/p016-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p016-1.webp\"]','Activity 2.2 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.\n\nMolly Reads Stories\nWhen Molly is reading a story, she is looking for clues in the text to help her visualize what is happening. She looks at the pictures and uses them to create a mental image of the story.\n\nShe also reads quickly, which helps her to understand what is happening in the story. When she has finishes reading, she is able to give a detailed description of the story. This shows that Molly is a good reader.\n\nMolly is reading a story.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nShe looks at the picture to create an image of the story.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe pictures in the book laughed at Molly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nAfter reading, the books quickly jumped with Molly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nMolly reads quickly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy',NULL,10,16,'Activity 2.2 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.\n\nMolly Reads Stories\nWhen Molly is reading a story, she is looking for clues in the text to help her visualize what is happening. She looks at the pictures and uses them to create a mental image of the story.\n\nShe also reads quickly, which helps her to understand what is happening in the story. When she has finished reading, she is able to give a detailed description of the story. This shows that Molly is a good reader.\n\nMolly is reading a story.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nShe looks at the picture to create an image of the story.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe pictures in the book laughed at Molly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nAfter reading, the books quickly jumped with Molly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nMolly reads quickly.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy',1,1,'answer'),
