(1009,343,NULL,'learn',1,'Pushing and Pulling','open','Activity 3.1 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.','Activity 3.1 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nPushing and Pulling\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them. Heavy things are hard to move. We want to move things; we push them and move them away from us. Wheels make it easier to push heavy things. Engines help to push big and heavy things. When we want to move things, we pull them, we move them towards us. Wheels made it easier to pull heavy things. A cart has wheels to make it easier to pull the cart. Trucks have engines and wheels.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nEngines help to push big and heavy things.\nHeavy things are hard to move.\nWheels make it easier to push heavy things.\nTrucks have engines and wheels.\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them.','assets/images/level6/g2/p022-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p022-1.webp\"]','Activity 3.1 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nPushing and Pulling\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them. Heavy things are hard to move. We want to move things; we push them and move them away from us. Wheels make it easier to push heavy things. Engines help to push big and heavy things. When we want to move things, we pull them, we move them towards us. Wheels made it easier to pull heavy things. A cart has wheels to make it easier to pull the cart. Trucks have engines and wheels.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nEngines help to push big and heavy things.\nHeavy things are hard to move.\nWheels make it easier to push heavy things.\nTrucks have engines and wheels.\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them.',NULL,10,22,'Activity 3.1 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nPushing and Pulling\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them. Heavy things are hard to move. We want to move things; we push them and move them away from us. Wheels make it easier to push heavy things. Engines help to push big and heavy things. When we want to move things, we pull them, we move them towards us. Wheels made it easier to pull heavy things. A cart has wheels to make it easier to pull the cart. Trucks have engines and wheels.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nEngines help to push big and heavy things.\nHeavy things are hard to move.\nWheels make it easier to push heavy things.\nTrucks have engines and wheels.\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them.',1,1,'answer'),
(1010,344,NULL,'learn',1,'Ann','open','Activity 3.2 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the number 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.','Activity 3.2 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the number 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nAnn\nAnn rides her bicycle. Ann rides her little bicycle to work. Ann rides her little red bicycle to work every day. Nina rides the bus. Nina rides the big bus to work. Nina rides the big slow bus to work every day.\n\nLuis rides the train. Luis rides the big train work. Luis rides the big fast train to work every day.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nLuis rides the big fast train to work every day.\nNina rides the big bus to work.\nAnn rides her bicycle.\nLuis rides the train.\nNina rides the big slow bus to work every day.','assets/images/level6/g2/p024-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p024-1.webp\"]','Activity 3.2 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the number 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nAnn\nAnn rides her bicycle. Ann rides her little bicycle to work. Ann rides her little red bicycle to work every day. Nina rides the bus. Nina rides the big bus to work. Nina rides the big slow bus to work every day.\n\nLuis rides the train. Luis rides the big train work. Luis rides the big fast train to work every day.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nLuis rides the big fast train to work every day.\nNina rides the big bus to work.\nAnn rides her bicycle.\nLuis rides the train.\nNina rides the big slow bus to work every day.',NULL,10,24,'Activity 3.2 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the number 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nAnn\nAnn rides her bicycle. Ann rides her little bicycle to work. Ann rides her little red bicycle to work every day. Nina rides the bus. Nina rides the big bus to work. Nina rides the big slow bus to work every day.\n\nLuis rides the train. Luis rides the big train to work. Luis rides the big fast train to work every day.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nLuis rides the big fast train to work every day.\nNina rides the big bus to work.\nAnn rides her bicycle.\nLuis rides the train.\nNina rides the big slow bus to work every day.',1,1,'answer'),
(1011,345,NULL,'learn',1,'My Mom','open','Activity 3.3 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.','Activity 3.3 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nMy Mom\nI am George and she is my mother Franklin. My mother is a doctor. She plays with me and tells me bedtime stories. She takes good care of everyone in the family. She is the best mother in the world.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nShe takes good care of everyone in the family.\nHer name is George, and she is her mother, Franklin.\nShe is the best mother in the world.\nMy mother is a doctor.\nShe plays with George and tells her bedtime stories.','assets/images/level6/g2/p026-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p026-1.webp\"]','Activity 3.3 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nMy Mom\nI am George and she is my mother Franklin. My mother is a doctor. She plays with me and tells me bedtime stories. She takes good care of everyone in the family. She is the best mother in the world.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nShe takes good care of everyone in the family.\nHer name is George, and she is her mother, Franklin.\nShe is the best mother in the world.\nMy mother is a doctor.\nShe plays with George and tells her bedtime stories.',NULL,10,26,'Activity 3.3 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nMy Mom\nI am George and she is my mother Franklin. My mother is a doctor. She plays with me and tells me bedtime stories. She takes good care of everyone in the family. She is the best mother in the world.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nShe takes good care of everyone in the family.\nHer name is George, and she is her mother, Franklin.\nShe is the best mother in the world.\nMy mother is a doctor.\nShe plays with George and tells her bedtime stories.',1,1,'answer'),
(1012,346,NULL,'learn',1,'Pearl','open','Activity 3.4 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Read the story. Then write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.','Activity 3.4 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Read the story. Then write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\n\nPearl\nThis is Pearl. She is a quiet girl.\nShe loves to read.\nShe loves adventure stories.\nThey are stories about brave kids.\nShe loves to read about Sherlock Holmes, who is a brave detective.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nIt is stories about brave kids.\nShe loved to read about Sherlock Holmes, who was a brave detective.\nShe loves to read.\nShe is a quiet girl.\nShe loved adventures stories.','assets/images/level6/g2/p028-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p028-1.webp\"]','Activity 3.4 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Read the story. Then write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\n\nPearl\nThis is Pearl. She is a quiet girl.\nShe loves to read.\nShe loves adventure stories.\nThey are stories about brave kids.\nShe loves to read about Sherlock Holmes, who is a brave detective.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nIt is stories about brave kids.\nShe loved to read about Sherlock Holmes, who was a brave detective.\nShe loves to read.\nShe is a quiet girl.\nShe loved adventures stories.',NULL,10,28,'Activity 3.4 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Read the story. Then write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\n\nPearl\nThis is Pearl. She is a quiet girl.\nShe loves to read.\nShe loves adventure stories.\nThey are stories about brave kids.\nShe loves to read about Sherlock Holmes, who is a brave detective.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nIt is stories about brave kids.\nShe loved to read about Sherlock Holmes, who was a brave detective.\nShe loves to read.\nShe is a quiet girl.\nShe loved adventures stories.',1,1,'answer'),
(1013,347,NULL,'learn',1,'Cause and Effect 1','open','Activity 4.1 · Cause and Effect. A cause is WHY something happens. The effect is WHAT happens as a result. Read and check the most likely effect of each cause.','Activity 4.1 · Cause and Effect. A cause is WHY something happens. The effect is WHAT happens as a result. Read and check the most likely effect of each cause.\n\nCause: The dog saw a squirrel…\n☐ it barked and chased it.\n☐ it fell asleep.\n\nCause: It’s Gab’s birthday so…\n☐ her mom baked a cake.\n☐ Her mom scolded him.\n\nCause: The kids are on a field trip at the zoo so…\n☐ they took a Math test.\n☐ they saw a crocodile.\n\nCause: When Ana was little, she was afraid of the chickens on her grandpa’s farm. Because Ana was afraid of the chickens,…\n☐ Her grandpa no longer brings her to the farm.\n☐ Her grandpa showed him how to shoo the chickens away.\n\nCause: Ana learned to shoo the chickens away by waving her hand, saying “Shoo chicks, shoo chicks!” Because Ana learned to shoo the chickens away,…\n☐ She’s no longer afraid of the chickens anymore.\n☐ she played with his grandpa’s dog.',NULL,'[]','Activity 4.1 · Cause and Effect. A cause is WHY something happens. The effect is WHAT happens as a result. Read and check the most likely effect of each cause.\n\nCause: The dog saw a squirrel…\n☐ it barked and chased it.\n☐ it fell asleep.\n\nCause: It’s Gab’s birthday so…\n☐ her mom baked a cake.\n☐ Her mom scolded him.\n\nCause: The kids are on a field trip at the zoo so…\n☐ they took a Math test.\n☐ they saw a crocodile.\n\nCause: When Ana was little, she was afraid of the chickens on her grandpa’s farm. Because Ana was afraid of the chickens,…\n☐ Her grandpa no longer brings her to the farm.\n☐ Her grandpa showed him how to shoo the chickens away.\n\nCause: Ana learned to shoo the chickens away by waving her hand, saying “Shoo chicks, shoo chicks!” Because Ana learned to shoo the chickens away,…\n☐ She’s no longer afraid of the chickens anymore.\n☐ she played with his grandpa’s dog.',NULL,10,30,'Activity 4.1 · Cause and Effect. A cause is WHY something happens. The effect is WHAT happens as a result. Read and check the most likely effect of each cause.\n\nCause: The dog saw a squirrel…\n☐ it barked and chased it.\n☐ it fell asleep.\n\nCause: It’s Gab’s birthday so…\n☐ her mom baked a cake.\n☐ Her mom scolded him.\n\nCause: The kids are on a field trip at the zoo so…\n☐ they took a Math test.\n☐ they saw a crocodile.\n\nCause: When Ana was little, she was afraid of the chickens on her grandpa’s farm. Because Ana was afraid of the chickens,…\n☐ Her grandpa no longer brings her to the farm.\n☐ Her grandpa showed him how to shoo the chickens away.\n\nCause: Ana learned to shoo the chickens away by waving her hand, saying “Shoo chicks, shoo chicks!” Because Ana learned to shoo the chickens away,…\n☐ She’s no longer afraid of the chickens anymore.\n☐ she played with his grandpa’s dog.',1,1,'answer'),
(1014,348,NULL,'learn',1,'Cause and Effect 2','open','Activity 4.2 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.','Activity 4.2 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed last night thus…\n☐ the classes are cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jane studied hard therefore…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: Mary bruised her arm because…\n☐ she fell off her bike.\n☐ she ate a lot of ice cream.\n\nCause: Amara did not study so…\n☐ she failed the Exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.',NULL,'[]','Activity 4.2 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed last night thus…\n☐ the classes are cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jane studied hard therefore…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: Mary bruised her arm because…\n☐ she fell off her bike.\n☐ she ate a lot of ice cream.\n\nCause: Amara did not study so…\n☐ she failed the Exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.',NULL,10,32,'Activity 4.2 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed last night thus…\n☐ the classes are cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jane studied hard therefore…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: Mary bruised her arm because…\n☐ she fell off her bike.\n☐ she ate a lot of ice cream.\n\nCause: Amara did not study so…\n☐ she failed the Exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.',1,1,'answer'),
(1015,349,NULL,'learn',1,'Cause and Effect 3','open','Activity 4.3 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.','Activity 4.3 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: Because the wind blew away her balloon,…\n☐ little Cherry was unhappy.\n☐ little Cherry was tired.\n\nCause: Bell’s shirt was dirty because…\n☐ she played outside.\n☐ she watched too much TV.\n\nCause: Arman’s car is in the shop because…\n☐ It needs a new tire.\n☐ It needs to eat.\n\nCause: The bottle is empty so…\n☐ I will throw it in the garbage.\n☐ I will put it inside the cabinet.\n\nCause: Because Luis practiced playing basketball every day,…\n☐ he made the winning shot during the game.\n☐ he lost the game.',NULL,'[]','Activity 4.3 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: Because the wind blew away her balloon,…\n☐ little Cherry was unhappy.\n☐ little Cherry was tired.\n\nCause: Bell’s shirt was dirty because…\n☐ she played outside.\n☐ she watched too much TV.\n\nCause: Arman’s car is in the shop because…\n☐ It needs a new tire.\n☐ It needs to eat.\n\nCause: The bottle is empty so…\n☐ I will throw it in the garbage.\n☐ I will put it inside the cabinet.\n\nCause: Because Luis practiced playing basketball every day,…\n☐ he made the winning shot during the game.\n☐ he lost the game.',NULL,10,34,'Activity 4.3 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: Because the wind blew away her balloon,…\n☐ little Cherry was unhappy.\n☐ little Cherry was tired.\n\nCause: Bell’s shirt was dirty because…\n☐ she played outside.\n☐ she watched too much TV.\n\nCause: Arman’s car is in the shop because…\n☐ It needs a new tire.\n☐ It needs to eat.\n\nCause: The bottle is empty so…\n☐ I 