(1016,350,NULL,'learn',1,'Cause and Effect 4','open','Activity 4.4 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.','Activity 4.4 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: Joy got tired after joining the race so…\n☐ she continued running.\n☐ she rested under the tree.\n\nCause: Zen helped her grandpa clean the house so…\n☐ her grandpa bought her a toy.\n☐ Her grandpa scolded her.\n\nCause: Because someone threw a stone at his window,…\n☐ he went to the window and looked.\n☐ he did not mind and continued sleeping.\n\nCause: Since Grandma is not feeling well,…\n☐ she went to the zoo.\n☐ she went to the hospital.\n\nCause: The teacher started to talk which is why…\n☐ the learners run away.\n☐ The learners listened.',NULL,'[]','Activity 4.4 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: Joy got tired after joining the race so…\n☐ she continued running.\n☐ she rested under the tree.\n\nCause: Zen helped her grandpa clean the house so…\n☐ her grandpa bought her a toy.\n☐ Her grandpa scolded her.\n\nCause: Because someone threw a stone at his window,…\n☐ he went to the window and looked.\n☐ he did not mind and continued sleeping.\n\nCause: Since Grandma is not feeling well,…\n☐ she went to the zoo.\n☐ she went to the hospital.\n\nCause: The teacher started to talk which is why…\n☐ the learners run away.\n☐ The learners listened.',NULL,10,36,'Activity 4.4 · Cause and Effect. After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: Joy got tired after joining the race so…\n☐ she continued running.\n☐ she rested under the tree.\n\nCause: Zen helped her grandpa clean the house so…\n☐ her grandpa bought her a toy.\n☐ Her grandpa scolded her.\n\nCause: Because someone threw a stone at his window,…\n☐ he went to the window and looked.\n☐ he did not mind and continued sleeping.\n\nCause: Since Grandma is not feeling well,…\n☐ she went to the zoo.\n☐ she went to the hospital.\n\nCause: The teacher started to talk which is why…\n☐ the learners run away.\n☐ The learners listened.',1,1,'answer'),
(1017,351,NULL,'learn',1,'Going to the Movies','open','Activity 5.1 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. To draw conclusions, you need to think about what makes the most sense. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.','Activity 5.1 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. To draw conclusions, you need to think about what makes the most sense. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nGoing to the Movies\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nMy class is going to the movies on the field trip next week. We have to get permission slips signed before we go. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They must get permission from their parents.\n☐ They must ride a bus to go to movies.\n\nWe also need to ask our parents to drive us to the movie theater. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Their parents should not mind them.\n☐ Their parents should accompany them.\n\nWe love it when movies are made from books. It is fun to compare the movie to the book. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They usually like to watch movies based on books.\n☐ They usually liked to read books based on movies.\n\nWe get the movie early so we can buy popcorn. Some of us buy candy too. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They want to eat while watching movie.\n☐ They want to play.\n\nThe movie ended and everyone in the audience clapped. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They wanted to see another movie.\n☐ They all liked the movie.','assets/images/level6/g2/p038-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p038-1.webp\"]','Activity 5.1 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. To draw conclusions, you need to think about what makes the most sense. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nGoing to the Movies\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nMy class is going to the movies on the field trip next week. We have to get permission slips signed before we go. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They must get permission from their parents.\n☐ They must ride a bus to go to movies.\n\nWe also need to ask our parents to drive us to the movie theater. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Their parents should not mind them.\n☐ Their parents should accompany them.\n\nWe love it when movies are made from books. It is fun to compare the movie to the book. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They usually like to watch movies based on books.\n☐ They usually liked to read books based on movies.\n\nWe get the movie early so we can buy popcorn. Some of us buy candy too. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They want to eat while watching movie.\n☐ They want to play.\n\nThe movie ended and everyone in the audience clapped. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They wanted to see another movie.\n☐ They all liked the movie.',NULL,10,38,'Activity 5.1 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. To draw conclusions, you need to think about what makes the most sense. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nGoing to the Movies\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nMy class is going to the movies on the field trip next week. We have to get permission slips signed before we go. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They must get permission from their parents.\n☐ They must ride a bus to go to movies.\n\nWe also need to ask our parents to drive us to the movie theater. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Their parents should not mind them.\n☐ Their parents should accompany them.\n\nWe love it when movies are made from books. It is fun to compare the movie to the book. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They usually like to watch movies based on books.\n☐ They usually liked to read books based on movies.\n\nWe get the movie early so we can buy popcorn. Some of us buy candy too. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They want to eat while watching movie.\n☐ They want to play.\n\nThe movie ended and everyone in the audience clapped. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They wanted to see another movie.\n☐ They all liked the movie.',1,1,'answer'),
(1018,352,NULL,'learn',1,'Reward','open','Activity 5.2 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.','Activity 5.2 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nReward\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIda was a kind-hearted heart girl. One day when she’s crossing a bridge, she saw two boys on the stream, trying to drown a little dog. This perhaps means that…\n☐ She wanted to join the boys in drowning the dog.\n☐ She ran to the bank to help the dog.\n\nIda was crying loudly, “Oh! How can you be so cruel to that poor little dog?” This perhaps means that…\n☐ She feels sorry for the dog.\n☐ She wants to hit the boys.\n\nOne of the boys said, “Father told us to drown it.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The boys only followed their father.\n☐ The boys willingly wants to drown the dog.\n\nThe dog reached the bank and crept toward Ida. “Poor little fellow,” she said, patting him. This perhaps means that…\n☐ She wants to throw the dog away.\n☐ She wants to adopt the dog.\n\n“Yes,” said the boys, “You may have him.” Ida thanked the boys and ran home. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Ida is going home happy.\n☐ Ida is going home sad.','assets/images/level6/g2/p040-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p040-1.webp\"]','Activity 5.2 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nReward\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIda was a kind-hearted heart girl. One day when she’s crossing a bridge, she saw two boys on the stream, trying to drown a little dog. This perhaps m