(1020,354,NULL,'learn',1,'Rod and Wena','open','Activity 5.4 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.','Activity 5.4 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nRod and Wena\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nRod is a farmer. This perhaps means that…\n☐ He lives on the farm.\n☐ He lives in the sea.\n\nHe has a pet cow. His pet’s name begins with W. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His pet cow is Wena.\n☐ His pet cow is Mimo.\n\nWena gives him milk. She also pulls his cart. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Wena is giver and helpful.\n☐ Wena is bad and ugly.\n\nWena helps him till his land. She is an industrious cow. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Rod is cruel to his pet cow Wena.\n☐ Rod loves his pet cow Wena.\n\nRod feeds Wena. And she loves to eat grass, hay, and pellets. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Rod takes good care of Wena.\n☐ Rod does not care about Wena.','assets/images/level6/g2/p044-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g2/p044-1.webp\"]','Activity 5.4 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nRod and Wena\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nRod is a farmer. This perhaps means that…\n☐ He lives on the farm.\n☐ He lives in the sea.\n\nHe has a pet cow. His pet’s name begins with W. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His pet cow is Wena.\n☐ His pet cow is Mimo.\n\nWena gives him milk. She also pulls his cart. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Wena is giver and helpful.\n☐ Wena is bad and ugly.\n\nWena helps him till his land. She is an industrious cow. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Rod is cruel to his pet cow Wena.\n☐ Rod loves his pet cow Wena.\n\nRod feeds Wena. And she loves to eat grass, hay, and pellets. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Rod takes good care of Wena.\n☐ Rod does not care about Wena.',NULL,10,44,'Activity 5.4 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nRod and Wena\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nRod is a farmer. This perhaps means that…\n☐ He lives on the farm.\n☐ He lives in the sea.\n\nHe has a pet cow. His pet’s name begins with W. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His pet cow is Wena.\n☐ His pet cow is Mimo.\n\nWena gives him milk. She also pulls his cart. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Wena is giver and helpful.\n☐ Wena is bad and ugly.\n\nWena helps him till his land. She is an industrious cow. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Rod is cruel to his pet cow Wena.\n☐ Rod loves his pet cow Wena.\n\nRod feeds Wena. And she loves to eat grass, hay, and pellets. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Rod takes good care of Wena.\n☐ Rod does not care about Wena.',1,1,'answer'),
