(1033,360,NULL,'learn',1,'Lost and Found','open','Direction: Read the story below and encircle the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the story below and encircle the letter of the correct answer.\n\nLost and Found\nPedro and Jose came to school early. There were no other pupils in the school yet.\n\n“Look,” said Pedro. “There is a handbag under the stairs. It is a girl’s handbag.”\n\nJose got the handbag. He opened it. There was a red pencil, a pink handkerchief and fifty centavos in it.\n\n“Let’s look for the owner of this handbag.”\n\n“Good morning, Mr. Cruz. We found this bag under the stairs,” said Jose.\n\nMr. Cruz smiled and said, “Thank you boys. I shall help you find the owner.”\n\nWhat time was it?\nA. Morning\nB. afternoon\nC. noon\n\nWho are the boys in the story?\nA. Pedro and Juan\nB. Juan and Jose\nC. Pedro and Jose\n\nWhat did the boys find?\nA. a book\nB. a handbag\nC. a box\n\nWhere was the handbag found?\nA. Under the building\nB. Under the tree\nC. Under the stairs\n\nWhat kind of handbag was it?\nA. A girl’s handbag\nB. A man’s handbag\nC. A teacher’s hand bag\n\nWhy do you think finding it was so important to Jose and Pedro?\nA. to show greediness\nB. to show honesty\nC. to show dishonesty\n\nWhat would you do if you found something that was lost?\nA. Keep it.\nB. Tell nobody about it.\nC. Return it to the owner.\n\nWhat other way can they do to find the owner of the bag?\nA. announce it during flag ceremony\nB. keep it\nC. do nothing','assets/images/level6/g3/p021-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p021-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the story below and encircle the letter of the correct answer.\n\nLost and Found\nPedro and Jose came to school early. There were no other pupils in the school yet.\n\n“Look,” said Pedro. “There is a handbag under the stairs. It is a girl’s handbag.”\n\nJose got the handbag. He opened it. There was a red pencil, a pink handkerchief and fifty centavos in it.\n\n“Let’s look for the owner of this handbag.”