(1035,362,NULL,'learn',1,'Getting the General Significance','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFather who was sitting near the children, stopped reading the newspaper. “Today is Sunday. Two days from now your Uncle Fred will arrive from America. What day will it be?” Father asked.\n\n“It will be Wednesday,” Nestor said.\n\n“No, it will be Friday,” little Nenita said.\n\n“That will be on Tuesday,” ten-year-old Vita said.\n\nWho had the correct answer?\nA. Nestor\nB. Nenita\nC. Vita\n\nWhat is the story about?\nA. the coming of Uncle Fred\nB. the days of the week\nC. on a Sunday\n\nWhich sentence is correct?\nA. All the children have the same answer.\nB. Uncle Fred will come home soon\nC. The children do not like to see Uncle Fred.','assets/images/level6/g3/p025-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p025-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFather who was sitting near the children, stopped reading the newspaper. “Today is Sunday. Two days from now your Uncle Fred will arrive from America. What day will it be?” Father asked.\n\n“It will be Wednesday,” Nestor said.\n\n“No, it will be Friday,” little Nenita said.\n\n“That will be on Tuesday,” ten-year-old Vita said.\n\nWho had the correct answer?\nA. Nestor\nB. Nenita\nC. Vita\n\nWhat is the story about?\nA. the coming of Uncle Fred\nB. the days of the week\nC. on a Sunday\n\nWhich sentence is correct?\nA. All the children have the same answer.\nB. Uncle Fred will come home soon\nC. The children do not like to see Uncle Fred.',NULL,10,25,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFather who was sitting near the children, stopped reading the newspaper. “Today is Sunday. Two days from now your Uncle Fred will arrive from America. What day will it be?” Father asked.\n\n“It will be Wedn