(1038,363,NULL,'learn',2,'Getting the General Significance','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“All flowers are red,” six-year-old Rosa said.\n\n“No, all flowers are yellow,” four-year-old Jose said.\n\n“Come here, you two,” ten-year-old Tina said. “There are white, red, yellow, pink, violet, orange and green flowers. Sampaguita, our national flower is white. Ilang-ilang is green and some daisies are orange. There are red and yellow roses.\n\n“Now I know why flowers are beautiful,” Rosa said. “They are not of the same color.”\n\nWhich is a good title for the story?\nA. Our National Flower\nB. Colors of Flowers\nC. Care of Flowers\n\nWhich is true about flowers?\nA. They have the same color.\nB. They have different colors.\nC. All are white.\n\nWho knows best about flowers?\nA. Jose\nB. Tina\nC. Rosa','assets/images/level6/g3/p028-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p028-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“All flowers are red,” six-year-old Rosa said.\n\n“No, all flowers are yellow,” four-year-old Jose said.\n\n“Come here, you two,” ten-year-old Tina said. “There are white, red, yellow, pink, violet, orange and green flowers. Sampaguita, our national flower is white. Ilang-ilang is green and some daisies are orange. There are red and yellow roses.\n\n“Now I know why flowers are beautiful,” Rosa said. “They are not of the same color.”\n\nWhich is a good title for the story?\nA. Our National Flower\nB. Colors of Flowers\nC. Care of Flowers\n\nWhich is true about flowers?\nA. They have the same color.\nB. They have different colors.\nC. All are white.\n\nWho knows best about flowers?\nA. Jose\nB. Tina\nC. Rosa',NULL,10,28,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“All flowers are red,” six-year-old Rosa said.\n\n“No, all flowe