(1041,365,NULL,'learn',1,'Getting the General Significance','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nPr---r---r a k !\n\nMother went running to the sala. She saw Pina very pale and trembling. She was holding a broom. On the floor was a broken vase. “I am very sorry, Mother. The vase fell when I moved the table,” Pina said.\n\n“It’s all right. Now be careful in sweeping all the broken pieces away,” Mother said. “Be sure not a piece is left.”\n\nWhich is a good title for the story?\nA. An Honest Girl\nB. Helping At Home\nC. How Pina Trembled\n\nWhat word best describes Pina?\nA. honest\nB. kind\nC. bright\n\nWhat was Pina doing in the house?\nA. playing\nB. cleaning\nC. sleeping','assets/images/level6/g3/p031-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p031-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nPr---r---r a k !\n\nMother went running to the sala. She saw Pina very pale and trembling. She was holding a broom. On the floor was a broken vase. “I am very sorry, Mother. The vase fell when I moved the table,” Pina said.\n\n“It’s all right. Now be careful in sweeping all the broken pieces away,” Mother said. “Be sure not a piece is left.”\n\nWhich is a good title for the story?\nA. An Honest Girl\nB. Helping At Home\nC. How Pina Trembled\n\nWhat word best describes Pina?\nA. honest\nB. kind\nC. bright\n\nWhat was Pina doing in the house?\nA. playing\nB. cleaning\nC. sleeping',NULL,10,31,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nPr---r---r a k !\n\nMother went running to the sala. She saw Pina very pale and trembling. She was holding a broom. On the floor was a broken vase. “I am very sorry, Mother. The vase fell when I moved the table,” Pina said.\n\n“It’s all right. Now be careful in sweeping all the broken pieces away,” Mother said. “Be sure not a piece is left.”\n\nWhich is a good title for the story?\nA. An Honest Girl\nB. Helping At Home\nC. How Pina Trembled\n\nWhat word best describes Pina?\nA. honest\nB. kind\nC. bright\n\nWhat was Pina doing in the house?\nA. playing\nB. cleaning\nC. sleeping',1,1,'answer'),
(1042,365,NULL,'learn',2,'Getting the General Significance','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“I will buy an ice cream cone for the one who can tell the name of the fruit I will describe.” Father said to two-year-old Ofelia and Malu. “Go ahead and describe it,” his daughters replied.\n\n“It’s a fruit and seed at the same time. It has water inside surrounded by white meat,” Father described.\n\n“I don’t know,” Lety and Ofelia replied almost at the same time. “It’s coconut,” Malu, the eldest of the three, replied.\n\nWho got an ice cream cone?\nA. Lety\nB. Ofelia\nC. Malu\n\nWhat game was Father and his daughters playing?\nA. fruit game\nB. guessing game\nC. story game\n\nWhy did Lety and Ofelia not know the answer?\nA. They were still small.\nB. They were old.\nC. They were as old as Malu','assets/images/level6/g3/p032-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p032-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“I will buy an ice cream cone for the one who can tell the name of the fruit I will describe.” Father said to two-year-old Ofelia and Malu. “Go ahead and describe it,” his daughters replied.\n\n“It’s a fruit and seed at the same time. It has water inside surrounded by white meat,” Father described.\n\n“I don’t know,” Lety and Ofelia replied almost at the same time. “It’s coconut,” Malu, the eldest of the three, replied.\n\nWho got an ice cream cone?\nA. Lety\nB. Ofelia\nC. Malu\n\nWhat game was Father and his daughters playing?\nA. fruit game\nB. guessing game\nC. story game\n\nWhy did Lety and Ofelia not know the answer?\nA. They were still small.\nB. They were old.\nC. They were as old as Malu',NULL,10,32,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“I will buy an ice cream cone for the one who can tell the name of the fruit I will describe.” Father said to two-year-old Ofelia and Malu. “Go ahead and describe it,” his daughters replied.\n\n“It’s a fruit and seed at the same time. It has water inside surrounded by white meat,” Father described.\n\n“I don’t know,” Lety and Ofelia replied almost at the same time. “It’s coconut,” Malu, the eldest of the three, replied.\n\nWho got an ice cream cone?\nA. Lety\nB. Ofelia\nC. Malu\n\nWhat game was Father and his daughters playing?\nA. fruit game\nB. guessing game\nC. story game\n\nWhy did Lety and Ofelia not know the answer?\nA. They were still small.\nB. They were old.\nC. They were as old as Malu',1,1,'answer'),
(1043,366,NULL,'learn',1,'Getting the General Significance','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nNardo stopped in front of a small store and counted his money. “Five pesos and thirty centavos!” he said with a smile. He rested for a while. Soon he was on the streets again. “Journal, Bulletin, Inquirer!” he shouted. As he walked calling out his sales, he thought of the birthday gift he would buy his mother. “I will bring home a box of chocolate for her,” he thought.\n\nWhat does Nardo sell?\nA. chocolate\nB. newspapers\nC. cakes\n\nWhy does Nardo want to give his mother a gift?\nA. It was her birthday\nB. It was Mother’s Day\nC. It was Christmas Day\n\nWhat was Nardo’s work?\nA. a newsboy\nB. a bootblack\nC. a janitor','assets/images/level6/g3/p033-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p033-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nNardo stopped in front of a small store and counted his money. “Five pesos and thirty centavos!” he said with a smile. He rested for a while. Soon he was on the streets again. “Journal, Bulletin, Inquirer!” he shouted. As he walked calling out his sales, he thought of the birthday gift he would buy his mother. “I will bring home a box of chocolate for her,” he thought.\n\nWhat does Nardo sell?\nA. chocolate\nB. newspapers\nC. cakes\n\nWhy does Nardo want to give his mother a gift?\nA. It was her birthday\nB. It was Mother’s Day\nC. It was Christmas Day\n\nWhat was Nardo’s work?\nA. a newsboy\nB. a bootblack\nC. a janitor',NULL,10,33,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nNardo stopped in front of a small store and counted his money. “Five pesos and thirty centavos!” he said with a smile. He rested for a while. Soon he was on the streets again. “Journal, Bulletin, Inquirer!” he shouted. As he walked callin