(1051,370,NULL,'learn',1,'Caught in the Rain','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nCaught in the Rain\nThe sky was very dark. With his books, Jose ran as fast as he could. He was panting and perspiring. He was only about three blocks away from home when the rain fell. That night, Jose lay shivering on his bed. He was wrapped in thick blankets with a thermometer in his mouth.\n\nWhat happened to Jose?\nA. He was scared of ghosts.\nB. He caught a cold and developed a fever.\nC. He ate an ice\n\nWhen did the story happen?\nA. on a Sunday\nB. on a holiday\nC. on a school day\n\nWhere did Jose come from?\nA. from school\nB. from church\nC. from the market','assets/images/level6/g3/p041-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p041-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nCaught in the Rain\nThe sky was very dark. With his books, Jose ran as fast as he could. He was panting and perspiring. He was only about three blocks away from home when the rain fell. That night, Jose lay shivering on his bed. He was wrapped in thick blankets with a thermometer in his mouth.\n\nWhat happened to Jose?\nA. He was scared of ghosts.\nB. He caught a cold and developed a fever.\nC. He ate an ice\n\nWhen did the story happen?\nA. on a Sunday\nB. on a holiday\nC. on a school day\n\nWhere did Jose come from?\nA. from school\nB. from church\nC. from the market',NULL,10,41,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nCaught in the Rain\nThe sky was very dark. With his books, Jose ran as fast as he could. He was panting and perspiring. He was only about three blocks away from home when the rain fell. That night, Jose lay shivering on his bed. He was wrapped in thick blankets with a thermometer in his mouth.\n\nWhat happened to Jose?\nA. He was scared of ghosts.\nB. He caught a cold and developed a fever.\nC. He ate an ice\n\nWhen did the story happen?\nA. on a Sunday\nB. on a holiday\nC. on a school day\n\nWhere did Jose come from?\nA. from school\nB. from church\nC. from the market',1,1,'answer'),
(1052,370,NULL,'learn',2,'A Visit to the City','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Visit to the City\nMang Tibo had not visited the city lately. Every time he came to the city, he would write his son to pick him up at the station. Because he wanted to surprise his son, he did not write him about his coming this time.\n\nMang Tibo was surprised to see the many changes in the city. When he got down the bus, he did not know where to go.\n\nWhat happened to Mang Tibo?\nA. He got lost.\nB. He enjoyed looking around\nC. He took a walk around the place\n\nWhat should Mang Tibo have done?\nA. gone to the nearest radio and TV station\nB. gone back to the province at once\nC. looked for a policeman and asked for help\n\nWhat was Mang Tibo likely to decide?\nA. Never come to the city again\nB. Never leave the province\nC. Never come to the city without asking his son to meet him','assets/images/level6/g3/p042-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p042-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Visit to the City\nMang Tibo had not visited the city lately. Every time he came to the city, he would write his son to pick him up at the station. Because he wanted to surprise his son, he did not write him about his coming this time.\n\nMang Tibo was surprised to see the many changes in the city. When he got down the bus, he did not know where to go.\n\nWhat happened to Mang Tibo?\nA. He got lost.\nB. He enjoyed looking around\nC. He took a walk around the place\n\nWhat should Mang Tibo have done?\nA. gone to the nearest radio and TV station\nB. gone back to the province at once\nC. looked for a policeman and asked for help\n\nWhat was Mang Tibo likely to decide?\nA. Never come to the city again\nB. Never leave the province\nC. Never come to the city without asking his son to meet him',NULL,10,42,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Visit to the City\nMang Tibo had not visited the city lately. Every time he came to the city, he would write his son to pick him up at the station. Because he wanted to surprise his son, he did not write him about his coming this time.\n\nMang Tibo was surprised to see the many changes in the city. When he got down the bus, he did not know where to go.\n\nWhat happened to Mang Tibo?\nA. He got lost.\nB. He enjoyed looking around\nC. He took a walk around the place\n\nWhat should Mang Tibo have done?\nA. gone to the nearest radio and TV station\nB. gone back to the province at once\nC. looked for a policeman and asked for help\n\nWhat was Mang Tibo likely to decide?\nA. Never come to the city again\nB. Never leave the province\nC. Never come to the city without asking his son to meet him',1,1,'answer'),
(1053,371,NULL,'learn',1,'First Elevator Ride','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFirst Elevator Ride\nIt was Marcelo’s first trip to Manila. It was his first time to see a train, an electric light, a telephone, a television set and big buildings. It was his first time to ride in a car, an elevator and on an escalator. Marcelo rode in an elevator on his third day in the city. His mother took him to the office of his eldest brother. His brother’s office was in the seventh floor so they rode in the elevator. Inside the elevator Marcelo cried and said, “Let me out of this box!”\n\nWhat do you think did the people in the elevator do?\nA. They did nothing.\nB. They laughed at him.\nC. They told him not to be afraid.\n\nWhy did Marcelo want to go out?\nA. he could not breathe inside.\nB. He was afraid.\nC. He wanted to play.\n\nHow did Marcelo’s mother feel?\nA. proud of Marcelo\nB. ashamed of Marcelo\nC. happy about Marcelo','assets/images/level6/g3/p043-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p043-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFirst Elevator Ride\nIt was Marcelo’s first trip to Manila. It was his first time to see a train, an electric light, a telephone, a television set and big buildings. It was his first time to ride in a car, an elevator and on an escalator. Marcelo rode in an elevator on his third day in the city. His mother took him to the office of his eldest brother. His brother’s office was in the seventh floor so they rode in the elevator. Inside the elevator Marcelo cried and said, “Let me out of this box!”\n\nWhat do you think did the people in the elevator do?\nA. They did nothing.\nB. They laughed at him.\nC. They told him not to be afraid.\n\nWhy did Marcelo want to go out?\nA. he could not breathe inside.\nB. He was afraid.\nC. He wanted to play.\n\nHow did Marcelo’s mother feel?\nA. proud of Marcelo\nB. ashamed of Marcelo\nC. happy about Marcelo',NULL,10,43,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFirst Elevator Ride\nIt was Marcelo’s first trip to Manila. It was his first time to see a train, an electric light, a telephone, a television set and big buildings. It was his first time to ride in a car, an elevator and on an escalator. Marcelo rode in an elevator on his third day in the city. His mother took him to the office of his eldest brother. His brother’s office was in the seventh floor so they rode in the elevator. Inside the elevator Marcelo cried and said, “Let me out of this box!”\n\nWhat do you think did the people in the elevator do?\nA. They did nothing.\nB. They laughed at him.\nC. They told him not to be afraid.\n\nWhy did Marcelo want to go out?\nA. he could not breathe inside.\nB. He was afraid.\nC. He wanted to play.\n\nHow did Marcelo’s mother feel?\nA. proud of Marcelo\nB. ashamed of Marcelo\nC. happy about Marcelo',1,1,'answer'),
(1054,371,NULL,'learn',2,'Falling in Line','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFalling in Line\nA little boy was walking on the street. He was holding a pail. Also walking were an old man who was holding a can and a little girl holding a bottle. They would all join a line with people at the corner of the street. Some of the people were holding cans, others, pails and still others, bottles and pitchers. They seemed to be waiting for something.\n\nThen a big red truck was seen coming. How happy the people were! They would hardly keep still on the line.\n\nWhat was the content of the truck?\nA. rice\nB. water\nC. fish\n\nWhat would happen if the truck did not come?\na. the people would have nothing to drink\nb. the people would have nothing to eat\nc. the people would have nothing to sell\n\nHow did the people feel afterwards?\nA. angry\nB. happy\nC. proud','assets/images/level6/g3/p044-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p044-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFalling in Line\nA little boy was walking on the street. He was holding a pail. Also walking were an old man who was holding a can and a little girl holding a bottle. They would all join a line with people at the corner of the street. Some of the people were holding cans, others, pails and still others, bottles and pitchers. They seemed to be waiting for something.\n\nThen a big red truck was seen coming. How happy the people were! They would hardly keep still on the line.\n\nWhat was the content of the truck?\nA. rice\nB. water\nC. fish\n\nWhat would happen if the truck did not come?\na. the people would have nothing to drink\nb. the people would have nothing to eat\nc. the people would have nothing to sell\n\nHow did the people feel afterwards?\nA. angry\nB. happy\nC. proud',NULL,10,44,'Direction: Read the sele