(1055,372,NULL,'learn',1,'An Accident','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nAn Accident\nLety heard a jeep stopped very suddenly in front of their house. Then there was a loud cry. She ran to the window to see what happened.\n\nThere was already a crowd of people. Many more people were running to see what happened. Someone was crying loudly.\n\nWhat do you think happened?\nA. The jeep picked up a passenger.\nB. The jeep bumped somebody.\nC. A child got into the jeep.\n\nWhy was an ambulance needed?\nA. Somebody was dead.\nB. Somebody was hurt.\nC. For a joy ride\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Nobody got an ambulance.\nB. the people did not help at all.\nC. An ambulance came to help.','assets/images/level6/g3/p045-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p045-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nAn Accident\nLety heard a jeep stopped very suddenly in front of their house. Then there was a loud cry. She ran to the window to see what happened.\n\nThere was already a crowd of people. Many more people were running to see what happened. Someone was crying loudly.\n\nWhat do you think happened?\nA. The jeep picked up a passenger.\nB. The jeep bumped somebody.\nC. A child got into the jeep.\n\nWhy was an ambulance needed?\nA. Somebody was dead.\nB. Somebody was hurt.\nC. For a joy ride\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Nobody got an ambulance.\nB. the people did not help at all.\nC. An ambulance came to help.',NULL,10,45,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nAn Accident\nLety heard a jeep stopped very suddenly in front of their house. Then there was a loud cry. She ran to the window to see what happened.\n\nThere was already a crowd of people. Many more people were running to see what happened. Someone was crying loudly.\n\nWhat do you think happened?\nA. The jeep picked up a passenger.\nB. The jeep bumped somebody.\nC. A child got into the jeep.\n\nWhy was an ambulance needed?\nA. Somebody was dead.\nB. Somebody was hurt.\nC. For a joy ride\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Nobody got an ambulance.\nB. the people did not help at all.\nC. An ambulance came to help.',1,1,'answer'),
(1056,372,NULL,'learn',2,'A Surprise Gift','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Surprise Gift\nNorma’s fever was very high. She kept tossing in bed. After a while, she fell asleep. Then she began talking in her sleep.\n\n“Oh, Mother, please buy me a box of chocolate,” she said. Mother heard her. She went to the store as fast as she could. She was back before Norma woke up.\n\n“Is this mine, Mother?” Norma asked when she woke up. She was holding something.\n\nWhat was Norma holding?\nA. a bunch of flowers\nB. a box of chocolate\nC. a beautiful dress\n\nWhat was she likely to do with it?\nA. keep it\nB. eat it\nC. play with it\n\nHow do you think did Norma feel?\nA. She felt happy.\nB. She felt angry.\nC. She felt sad.','assets/images/level6/g3/p046-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p046-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Surprise Gift\nNorma’s fever was very high. She kept tossing in bed. After a while, she fell asleep. Then she began talking in her sleep.\n\n“Oh, Mother, please buy me a box of chocolate,” she said. Mother heard her. She went to the store as fast as she could. She was back before Norma woke up.\n\n“Is this mine, Mother?” Norma asked when she woke up. She was holding something.\n\nWhat was Norma holding?\nA. a bunch of flowers\nB. a box of chocolate\nC. a beautiful dress\n\nWhat was she likely to do with it?\nA. keep it\nB. eat it\nC. play with it\n\nHow do you think did Norma feel?\nA. She felt happy.\nB. She felt angry.\nC. She felt sad.',NULL,10,46,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Surprise Gift\nNorma’s fever was very high. She kept tossing in bed. After a while, she fell asleep. Then she began talking in her sleep.\n\n“Oh, Mother, please buy me a box of chocolate,” she said. Mother heard h