(1057,373,NULL,'learn',1,'Rico','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nRico\nRico is in the third grade. He goes to school every day. He listens well to his teacher. He tries to answer all questions asked of him. He works well with his classmates. He finished his school projects on time. At home he studies his lessons before going to bed. He dies his homework neatly and well. When he finishes all his school assignments he tries to help his mother. In this way he makes his mother happy.\n\nWhat grade will Rico likely receive?\nA. poor grades\nB. high grades\nC. failing grades\n\nWhat is likely to happen to Rico?\nA. will not finish his studies\nB. graduate with honors\nC. stop going to school\n\nWhat else will likely happen to Rico?\nA. becomes successful\nB. become lazy\nC. become sickly','assets/images/level6/g3/p047-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p047-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nRico\nRico is in the third grade. He goes to school every day. He listens well to his teacher. He tries to answer all questions asked of him. He works well with his classmates. He finished his school projects on time. At home he studies his lessons before going to bed. He dies his homework neatly and well. When he finishes all his school assignments he tries to help his mother. In this way he makes his mother happy.\n\nWhat grade will Rico likely receive?\nA. poor grades\nB. high grades\nC. failing grades\n\nWhat is likely to happen to Rico?\nA. will not finish his studies\nB. graduate with honors\nC. stop going to school\n\nWhat else will likely happen to Rico?\nA. becomes successful\nB. become lazy\nC. become sickly',NULL,10,47,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nRico\nRico is in the third grade. He goes to school every day. He listens well to his teacher. He tries to answer all questions asked of him. He works well with his classmates. He finished his school projects on time. At home he studies his lessons before going to bed. He dies his homework neatly and well. When he finishes all his school assignments he tries to help his mother. In this way he makes his mother happy.\n\nWhat grade will Rico likely receive?\nA. poor grades\nB. high grades\nC. failing grades\n\nWhat is likely to happen to Rico?\nA. will not finish his studies\nB. graduate with honors\nC. stop going to school\n\nWhat else will likely happen to Rico?\nA. becomes successful\nB. become lazy\nC. become sickly',1,1,'answer'),
(1058,373,NULL,'learn',2,'Why Lina Cried','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nWhy Lina Cried\nFour-year-old Lina came out of the room crying. She just woke up.\n\nMother, still holding needle and thread asked, “What do you want Lina?” Lina did not answer but continued crying.\n\nMother touched Lina. Her hands were hot. Her cheeks were red. Her eyes were red too.\n\n“Call a taxi at once,” Mother told father as she was changing Lina’s clothes.\n\nWhat was Mother doing when Lina woke up?\nA. cooking\nB. reading\nC. sewing\n\nWhy was Lina crying?\nA. She lost her money.\nB. She was sick.\nC. She was hungry.\n\nWhy did Mother need a taxi?\nA. She was taking Lina to a doctor.\nB. She was going to party with Lina.\nC. She was going to the market with Lina.','assets/images/level6/g3/p048-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p048-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nWhy Lina Cried\nFour-year-old Lina came out of the room crying. She just woke up.\n\nMother, still holding needle and thread asked, “What do you want Lina?” Lina did not answer but continued crying.\n\nMother touched Lina. Her hands were hot. Her cheeks were red. Her eyes were red too.\n\n“Call a taxi at once,” Mother told father as she was changing Lina’s clothes.\n\nWhat was Mother doing when Lina woke up?\nA. cooking\nB. reading\nC. sewing\n\nWhy was Lina crying?\nA. She lost her money.\nB. She was sick.\nC. She was hungry.\n\nWhy did Mother need a taxi?\nA. She was taking Lina to a doctor.\nB. She was going to party with Lina.\nC. She was going to the market with Lina.',NULL,10,48,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nWhy Lina Cried\nFour-year-old Lina came out of the room crying. She just woke up.\n\nMother, still holding needle and thread asked, “What do you want Lina?” Lina did not answer but continued crying.\n\nMother touched Lina. Her hands were hot. Her cheeks were red. Her eyes were red too.\n\n“Call a taxi at once,” Mother told father as she was changing Lina’s clothes.\n\nWhat was Mother doing when Lina woke up?\nA. cooking\nB. reading\nC. sewing\n\nWhy was Lina crying?\nA. She lost her money.\nB. She was sick.\nC. She was hungry.\n\nWhy did Mother need a taxi?\nA. She was taking Lina to a doctor.\nB. She was going to party with Lina.\nC. She was going to the market with Lina.',1,1,'answer'),
(1059,374,NULL,'learn',1,'A Letter from Father','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Letter from Father\n“Come, Leah, come, eric,” Mrs. Mislang said. “I have here a letter from your father.”\n\n“What does it say, Mother?” little Eric asked.\n\n“He says that Mindanao is really a land of promise. He wants us to go there soon.” Mrs. Mislang said. We will build our house there and stay there for some years.\n\n“Why did father go there?” Leah asked.\n\n“To earn money for us. He loves us that’s why,” Mrs. Mislang explained.\n\nWhere do you think the father is?\nA. Philippines\nB. America\nC. China\n\nWhat will Mrs. Mislang do?\nA. stay in Manila\nB. plan to go abroad\nC. prepare to live in Mindanao\n\nHow will this story end?\nA. Mrs. Mislang and her children went to Mindanao\nB. Mrs. Mislang and her children stayed in Manila\nC. Mrs. Mislang and her children went to Japan.','assets/images/level6/g3/p049-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p049-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Letter from Father\n“Come, Leah, come, eric,” Mrs. Mislang said. “I have here a letter from your father.”\n\n“What does it say, Mother?” little Eric asked.\n\n“He says that Mindanao is really a land of promise. He wants us to go there soon.” Mrs. Mislang said. We will build our house there and stay there for some years.\n\n“Why did father go there?” Leah asked.\n\n“To earn money for us. He loves us that’s why,” Mrs. Mislang explained.\n\nWhere do you think the father is?\nA. Philippines\nB. America\nC. China\n\nWhat will Mrs. Mislang do?\nA. stay in Manila\nB. plan to go abroad\nC. prepare to live in Mindanao\n\nHow will this story end?\nA. Mrs. Mislang and her children went to Mindanao\nB. Mrs. Mislang and her children stayed in Manila\nC. Mrs. Mislang and her children went to Japan.',NULL,10,4