(1060,374,NULL,'learn',2,'A Boy’s Wish','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Boy’s Wish\nAngel has been sick for a week. He is not getting any better. A good doctor visits him every day but he is still very ill. His mother is always near him.\n\nShe is not happy. The doctor said that angel’s sickness cannot be cured. In a few days he will die.\n\n“I want a beautiful schoolbag,” Angel said in his sleep one time. Mother heard it. While angel was still sleeping Mother went to the nearest store. She went to buy something for Angel.\n\nWhat do you think did Mother buy?\nA. ice cream for Angel\nB. schoolbag for Angel\nC. shirt for Angel\n\nHow did Angel feel about it?\nA. happy\nB. angry\nC. sad\n\nHow did this story end?\nA. Angel got mad at Mother.\nB. Angel died.\nC. Angel was happy','assets/images/level6/g3/p050-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p050-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Boy’s Wish\nAngel has been sick for a week. He is not getting any better. A good doctor visits him every day but he is still very ill. His mother is always near him.\n\nShe is not happy. The doctor said that angel’s sickness cannot be cured. In a few days he will die.\n\n“I want a beautiful schoolbag,” Angel said in his sleep one time. Mother heard it. While angel was still sleeping Mother went to the nearest store. She went to buy something for Angel.\n\nWhat do you think did Mother buy?\nA. ice cream for Angel\nB. schoolbag for Angel\nC. shirt for Angel\n\nHow did Angel feel about it?\nA. happy\nB. angry\nC. sad\n\nHow did this story end?\nA. Angel got mad at Mother.\nB. Angel died.\nC. Angel was happy',NULL,10,50,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Boy’s Wish\nAngel has been sick for a week. He is not getting any better. A good doctor visits him every day but he is still very ill. His mother is always near him.\n\nShe is not happy. The doctor said that angel’s sickness cannot be cured. In a few days he will die.\n\n“I want a beautiful schoolbag,” Angel said in his sleep one time. Mother heard it. While angel was still sleeping Mother went to the nearest store. She went to buy something for Angel.\n\nWhat do you think did Mother buy?\nA. ice cream for Angel\nB. schoolbag for Angel\nC. shirt for Angel\n\nHow did Angel feel about it?\nA. happy\nB. angry\nC. sad\n\nHow did this story end?\nA. Angel got mad at Mother.\nB. Angel died.\nC. Angel was happy',1,1,'answer'),
(1061,375,NULL,'learn',1,'Mina’s Father','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMina’s Father\nMina and mother were on their way to the bank. “What shall we do at the bank, Mother?” Mina asked.\n\n“We’ll deposit the money your father sent us,” Mother said.\n\n“What does father do to earn money?” Mina asked.\n\n“He checks if all letters mailed have correct stamps. He says that he works with friendly Arabs. He said, too, that he is the only Filipino in the office where he works.\n\nWhat is the work of Mina’s father?\nA. teacher\nB. doctor\nC. office worker\n\nWhere do you think does Mina’s father work?\nA. school\nB. post office\nC. hospital\n\nWhat will Mother likely do after depositing the money?\nA. write Father she received the money\nB. write Father she is sick\nC. write Father that she did not receive the money.','assets/images/level6/g3/p051-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p051-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMina’s Father\nMina and mother were on their way to the bank. “What shall we do at the bank, Mother?” Mina asked.\n\n“We’ll deposit the money your father sent us,” Mother said.\n\n“What does father do to earn money?” Mina asked.\n\n“He checks if all letters mailed have correct stamps. He says that he works with friendly Arabs. He said, too, that he is the only Filipino in the office where he works.\n\nWhat is the work of Mina’s father?\nA. teacher\nB. doctor\nC. office worker\n\nWhere do you think does Mina’s father work?\nA. school\nB. post office\nC. hospital\n\nWhat will Mother likely do after depositing the money?\nA. write Father she received the money\nB. write Father she is sick\nC. write Father that she did not receive the money.',NULL,10,51,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMina’s Father\nMina and mother were on their way to the bank. “What shall we do at the bank, Mother?” Mina asked.\n\n“We’ll deposit the money your father sent us,” Mother said.\n\n“What does father do to earn money?” Mina asked.\n\n“He checks if all letters mailed have correct stamps. He says that he works with friendly Arabs. He said, too, that he is the only Filipino in the office where he works.\n\nWhat is the work of Mina’s father?\nA. teacher\nB. doctor\nC. office worker\n\nWhere do you think does Mina’s father work?\nA. school\nB. post office\nC. hospital\n\nWhat will Mother likely do after depositing the money?\nA. write Father she received the money\nB. write Father she is sick\nC. write Father that she did not receive the money.',1,1,'answer'),
(1062,375,NULL,'learn',2,'Getting Ready','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nGetting Ready\nHow busy they were! Liza was wiping pieces of furniture. Maya was hanging new curtains. Nilo was sweeping the yard and Pepe was busy borrowing chairs from their neighbors. Mother with three other women were cooking in the kitchen. Father was roasting a pig at the backyard. “How delicious the litson smells!” Pepe said.\n\n“Your friends will enjoy your party, Maya,” Nilo said.\n\n“When I’ll be eighteen years old, will I have a big party like this, Ate Maya?” Liza asked.\n\nWhat was the family preparing for?\nA. a fiesta\nB. a birthday party\nC. a family reunion\n\nWhat is likely to happen?\nA. Many visitors would come.\nB. No visitor would come.\nC. Only father’s friends would come.\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Liza received many gifts.\nB. Maya received many gifts\nC. father received many gifts.','assets/images/level6/g3/p052-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p052-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nGetting Ready\nHow busy they were! Liza was wiping pieces of furniture. Maya was hanging new curtains. Nilo was sweeping the yard and Pepe was busy borrowing chairs from their neighbors. Mother with three other women were cooking in the kitchen. Father was roasting a pig at the backyard. “How delicious the litson smells!” Pepe said.\n\n“Your friends will enjoy your party, Maya,” Nilo said.\n\n“When I’ll be eighteen years old, will I have a big party like this, Ate Maya?” Liza asked.\n\nWhat was the family preparing for?\nA. a fiesta\nB. a birthday party\nC. a family reunion\n\nWhat is likely to happen?\nA. Many visitors would come.\nB. No visitor would come.\nC. Only father’s friends would come.\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Liza received many gifts.\nB. Maya received many gifts\nC. father received many gifts.',NULL,10,52,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nGetting Ready\nHow busy they were! Liza was wiping pieces of furniture. Maya was hanging new curtains. Nilo was sweeping the yard and Pepe was busy borrowing chairs from their neighbors. Mother with three other women were cooking in the kitchen. Father was roasting a pig at the backyard. “How delicious the litson smells!” Pepe said.\n\n“Your friends will enjoy your party, Maya,” Nilo said.\n\n“When I’ll be eighteen years old, will I have a big party like this, Ate Maya?” Liza asked.\n\nWhat was the family preparing for?\nA. a fiesta\nB. a birthday party\nC. a family reunion\n\nWhat is likely to happen?\nA. Many visitors would come.\nB. No visitor would come.\nC. Only father’s friends would come.\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Liza received many gifts.\nB. Maya received many gifts\nC. father received many gifts.',1,1,'answer'),
(1063,376,NULL,'learn',1,'One Sunday Morning','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nOne Sunday Morning\nIt was Sunday Morning. The church bells were ringing.\n\n“There is no need to hurry anyway,” Benilda said to herself as she tossed in bed. “I’ll just get up when I like. Sunday is a rest day,” she thought.\n\nSuddenly she got up. She remembered that she should be in church early. She would see Linda there. They were going to a party together.\n\n“Oh my, why did I forget?” Benilda said looking at the big clock.\n\nWhat do you think did Linda do when Benilda did not come?\nA. She attended the mass alone.\nB. She went to a party instead.\nC. She played in the church.\n\nHow do you think did Benilda feel?\nA. She was happy.\nB. She was sorry.\nC. She was sleepy.\n\nWhat was she likely to do?\nA. Go to mass alone, too.\nB. See a show.\nC. Go back to sleep.','assets/images/level6/g3/p053-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p053-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nOne Sunday Morning\nIt was Sunday Morning. The church bells were ringing.\n\n“There is no need to hurry anyway,” Benilda said to herself as she tossed in bed. “I’ll just get up when I like. Sunday is a rest day,” she thought.\n\nSuddenly she got up. She remembered that she should be in church early. She would see Linda there. They were going to a party together.\n\n“Oh my, why did I forget?” Benilda said looking at the big clock.\n\nWhat do you think did Linda do when Benilda did not come?\nA. She attended the mass alone.\nB. She went to a party instead.\nC. She played in the church.\n\nHow do you think did Benilda feel?\nA. She was happy.\nB. She was sorry.\nC. She was sleepy.\n\nWhat was she likely to do?\nA. Go to mass alone, too.\nB. See a show.\nC. Go back to sleep.',NULL,10,53,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nOne Sunday Morning\nIt was Sunday Morning. The church bells were ringing.\n\n“There is no need to hurry anyway,” Benilda said to herself as she tossed in bed. “I’ll just get up when I like. Sunday is a rest day,” she thought.\n\nSuddenly she got up. She remembered that she should be in church early. She would see Linda there. They were going to a party together.\n\n“Oh my, why did I forget?” Benilda said looking at the big clock.\n\nWhat do you think did Linda do when Benilda did not come?\nA. She attended the mass alone.\nB. She went to a party instead.\nC. She played in the church.\n\nHow do you think did Benilda feel?\nA. She was happy.\nB. She was sorry.\nC. She was sleepy.\n\nWhat was she likely to do?\nA. Go to mass alone, too.\nB. See a show.\nC. Go back to sleep.',1,1,'answer'),
(1064,376,NULL,'learn',2,'Just Pray','open','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nJust Pray\nMrs. Soriano’s house was very quiet. The people inside seemed to be talking in whispers. But everyone seemed to be actively moving around.\n\nSuddenly an ambulance stopped in front of the house. With it came a doctor and a nurse. Soon the eldest girl in the family came out holding two pillows. She was followed by her brother holding a bag and a blanket. Then a patient in the stretcher was placed in the ambulance.\n\nwhat was the ambulance for?\nA. to distribute medicines\nB. to give free injections\nC. to get a sick person\n\nWho was the sick person?\nA. the eldest girl\nB. Mother\nC. the boy\n\nHow did this story end?\nA. Mother was brought to the hospital.\nB. the eldest girl died.\nC. the ambulance stayed in front of the house','assets/images/level6/g3/p054-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p054-1.webp\"]','Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nJust Pray\nMrs. Soriano’s house was very quiet. The people inside seemed to be talking in whispers. But everyone seemed to be actively moving around.\n\nSuddenly an ambulance stopped in front of the house. With it came a doctor and a nurse. Soon the eldest girl in the family came out holding two pillows. She was followed by her brother holding a bag and a blanket. Then a patient in the stretcher was placed in the ambulance.\n\nwhat was the ambulance for?\nA. to distribute medicines\nB. to give free injections\nC. to get a sick person\n\nWho was the sick person?\nA. the eldest girl\nB. Mother\nC. the boy\n\nHow did this story end?\nA. Mother was brought to the hospital.\nB. the eldest girl died.\nC. the ambulance stayed in front of the house',NULL,10,54,'Direction: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nJust Pray\nMrs. Soriano’s house was very quiet. The people inside seemed to be talking in whispers. But everyone seemed to be actively moving around.\n\nSuddenly an ambulance stopped in front of the house. With it came a doctor and a nurse. Soon the eldest girl in the family came out holding two pillows. She was followed by her brother holding a bag and a blanket. Then a patient in the stretcher was placed in the ambulance.\n\nwhat was the ambulance for?\nA. to distribute medicines\nB. to give free injections\nC. to get a sick person\n\nWho was the sick person?\nA. the eldest girl\nB. Mother\nC. the boy\n\nHow did this story end?\nA. Mother was brought to the hospital.\nB. the eldest girl died.\nC. the ambulance stayed in front of the house',1,1,'answer'),
(1065,377,89,'post',1,'Growing Vegetables','open','Directions: Read the story carefully. Choose the correct answer for each question and encircle the letter.','Directions: Read the story carefully. Choose the correct answer for each question and encircle the letter.\n\nGrowing Vegetables\nLino went with mother to market. They bought some vegetables. Mother said, “I was able to buy only some with my money. Vegetables cost much now.” Lino was sorry for Mother. They did not have much money. So, he said, “Let’s plant vegetables in our backyard. Then we will not have to buy them in the market.”\n\nSo, Lino planted three plots of tomatoes, two plots of eggplants and a plot of pechay. He had some ampalaya climbing on the bamboo fence. Lino worked in his garden after class every afternoon. He grew more vegetables than they could eat. Mother sold some of them in the market.\n\nWhere did Lino and Mother go?\nA. To the farm\nB. To the market\nC. To school\nD. To the park\n\nWhat did they buy at the market?\nA. Fruits\nB. Clothes\nC. Vegetables\nD. Toys\n\nWhy did Lino suggest planting vegetables in their backyard?\nA. To make their backyard look nice\nB. Because vegetables were expensive at the market\nC. To sell vegetables to neighbors\nD. To have fun in the garden\n\nHow many plots of tomatoes did Lino plant?\nA. One\nB. Two\nC. Three\nD. Four\n\nWhich vegetable was climbing on the bamboo fence?\nA. Pechay\nB. Ampalaya\nC. Eggplant\nD. Tomato','assets/images/level6/g3/p056-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p056-1.webp\"]','Directions: Read the story carefully. Choose the correct answer for each question and encircle the letter.\n\nGrowing Vegetables\nLino went with mother to market. They bought some vegetables. Mother said, “I was able to buy only some with my money. Vegetables cost much now.” Lino was sorry for Mother. They did not have much money. So, he said, “Let’s plant vegetables in our backyard. Then we will not have to buy them in the market.”\n\nSo, Lino planted three plots of tomatoes, two plots of eggplants and a plot of pechay. He had some ampalaya climbing on the bamboo fence. Lino worked in his garden after class every afternoon. He grew more vegetables than they could eat. Mother sold some of them in the market.\n\nWhere did Lino and Mother go?\nA. To the farm\nB. To the market\nC. To school\nD. To the park\n\nWhat did they buy at the market?\nA. Fruits\nB. Clothes\nC. Vegetables\nD. Toys\n\nWhy did Lino suggest planting vegetables in their backyard?\nA. To make their backyard look nice\nB. Because vegetables were expensive at the market\nC. To sell vegetables to neighbors\nD. To have fun in the garden\n\nHow many plots of tomatoes did Lino plant?\nA. One\nB. Two\nC. Three\nD. Four\n\nWhich vegetable was climbing on the bamboo fence?\nA. Pechay\nB. Ampalaya\nC. Eggplant\nD. Tomato',NULL,10,56,'Directions: Read the story carefully. Choose the correct answer for each question and encircle the letter.\n\nGrowing Vegetables\nLino went with mother to market. They bought some vegetables. Mother said, “I was able to buy only some with my money. Vegetables cost much now.” Lino was sorry for Mother. They did not have much money. So, he said, “Let’s plant vegetables in our backyard. Then we will not have to buy them in the market.”\n\nSo, Lino planted three plots of tomatoes, two plots of eggplants and a plot of pechay. He had some ampalaya climbing on the bamboo fence. Lino worked in his garden after class every afternoon. He grew more vegetables than they could eat. Mother sold some of them in the market.\n\nWhere did Lino and Mother go?\nA. To the farm\nB. To the market\nC. To school\nD. To the park\n\nWhat did they buy at the market?\nA. Fruits\nB. Clothes\nC. Vegetables\nD. Toys\n\nWhy did Lino suggest planting vegetables in their backyard?\nA. To make their backyard look nice\nB. Because vegetables were expensive at the market\nC. To sell vegetables to neighbors\nD. To have fun in the garden\n\nHow many plots of tomatoes did Lino plant?\nA. One\nB. Two\nC. Three\nD. Four\n\nWhich vegetable was climbing on the bamboo fence?\nA. Pechay\nB. Ampalaya\nC. Eggplant\nD. Tomato',1,1,'answer'),
(1066,377,89,'post',2,'Fowls','open','Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct answer from the options provided and encircle the letter of your choice.','Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct answer from the options provided and encircle the letter of your choice.\n\nFowls\nFowls are animals. They are animals with two feet and two wings. Their bodies are covered with feathers. They give us eggs. Their meat is good to eat. Chickens, ducks, turkeys and geese are fowls. They eat grains such as palay and corn. Chickens like worms. Ducks and geese like to swim. They like to stay in the water They are water birds, so they have webbed feet. Turkeys have beautiful feathers. The male turkey spreads its tail like a fan. Geese are good watchers. They make loud noises when people come near. Fowls are good to raise. Many people get rich because of poultry raising.\n\nWhat is the main idea of the passage?\nA. Fowls are animals that give eggs and meat.\nB. Fowls only eat grains.\nC. Turkeys have beautiful feathers.\n\nWhy are fowls considered useful to humans?\nA. They make loud noises.\nB. They give eggs, meat, and can make people rich through poultry raising.\nC. They like to swim in water.\n\nWhat type of birds are ducks and geese?\nA. Land birds\nB. Water birds with webbed feet\nC. Birds with colorful feathers\n\nWhy do geese make loud noises?\nA. To call other geese\nB. To warn people or act as watchers\nC. To scare chickens\n\nWhat is the general significance of raising fowls?\nA. It provides food and livelihood for people\nB. It helps fowls grow beautiful feathers\nC. It teaches birds to swim','assets/images/level6/g3/p058-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p058-1.webp\"]','Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct answer from the options provided and encircle the letter of your choice.\n\nFowls\nFowls are animals. They are animals with two feet and two wings. Their bodies are covered with feathers. They give us eggs. Their meat is good to eat. Chickens, ducks, turkeys and geese are fowls. They eat grains such as palay and corn. Chickens like worms. Ducks and geese like to swim. They like to stay in the water They are water birds, so they have webbed feet. Turkeys have beautiful feathers. The male turkey spreads its tail like a fan. Geese are good watchers. They make loud noises when people come near. Fowls are good to raise. Many people get rich because of poultry raising.\n\nWhat is the main idea of the passage?\nA. Fowls are animals that give eggs and meat.\nB. Fowls only eat grains.\nC. Turkeys have beautiful feathers.\n\nWhy are fowls considered useful to humans?\nA. They make loud noises.\nB. They give eggs, meat, and can make people rich through poultry raising.\nC. They like to swim in water.\n\nWhat type of birds are ducks and geese?\nA. Land birds\nB. Water birds with webbed feet\nC. Birds with colorful feathers\n\nWhy do geese make loud noises?\nA. To call other geese\nB. To warn people or act as watchers\nC. To scare chickens\n\nWhat is the general significance of raising fowls?\nA. It provides food and livelihood for people\nB. It helps fowls grow beautiful feathers\nC. It teaches birds to swim',NULL,10,58,'Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct answer from the options provided and encircle the letter of your choice.\n\nFowls\nFowls are animals. They are animals with two feet and two wings. Their bodies are covered with feathers. They give us eggs. Their meat is good to eat. Chickens, ducks, turkeys and geese are fowls. They eat grains such as palay and corn. Chickens like worms. Ducks and geese like to swim. They like to stay in the water They are water birds, so they have webbed feet. Turkeys have beautiful feathers. The male turkey spreads its tail like a fan. Geese are good watchers. They make loud noises when people come near. Fowls are good to raise. Many people get rich because of poultry raising.\n\nWhat is the main idea of the passage?\nA. Fowls are animals that give eggs and meat.\nB. Fowls only eat grains.\nC. Turkeys have beautiful feathers.\n\nWhy are fowls considered useful to humans?\nA. They make loud noises.\nB. They give eggs, meat, and can make people rich through poultry raising.\nC. They like to swim in water.\n\nWhat type of birds are ducks and geese?\nA. Land birds\nB. Water birds with webbed feet\nC. Birds with colorful feathers\n\nWhy do geese make loud noises?\nA. To call other geese\nB. To warn people or act as watchers\nC. To scare chickens\n\nWhat is the general significance of raising fowls?\nA. It provides food and livelihood for people\nB. It helps fowls grow beautiful feathers\nC. It teaches birds to swim',1,1,'answer'),
(1067,377,89,'post',3,'The First Monkey','open','Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct answer from the options provided and encircle the letter of your choice.','Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct answer from the options provided and encircle the letter of your choice.\n\nThe First Monkey\nLong time ago, there was a farmer who had a wide corn field. He grew big and sweet corn. One day he saw some of his corn gone. Many corn plants had no more fruits. He wanted to catch whoever stole his corn.\n\nThe next day he hid behind a big mango tree. He carried a stick. He watched and watched until he saw a man coming. The man passed through a broken part of the fence. The man began to pick some corn.\n\nThe farmer went from behind the mango tree and walked towards the man. The farmer ran after him, but he could not catch up with him. Then he threw the stick at the man. The stick hit the man’s back and became a tail. The man went up the tree. He became smaller and smaller until he became a monkey.\n\nWhen did the story most likely take place?\nA. Last week\nB. Long time ago\nC. Tomorrow\n\nWhat did the farmer have?\nA. A mango tree\nB. A corn field\nC. A garden\n\nWhat words describe the farmer’s corn?\nA. Small and sour\nB. Big and sweet\nC. Rotten and old\n\nWhat happened to the farmer’s corn?\nA. It was eaten by animals\nB. Some of it was gone and plants had no fruits\nC. It was harvested for sale\n\nWhere did the farmer hide to catch the thief?\nA. Behind a mango tree\nB. In a corn plot\nC. On the roof','assets/images/level6/g3/p060-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g3/p060-1.webp\"]','Directions: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct answer from the options provided and encircle the letter of your choice.\n\nThe First Monkey\nLong time ago, there was a farmer who had a wide corn field. He grew big and sweet corn. One day he saw some of his corn gone. Many corn plants had no more fruits. He wanted to catch whoever 