pened?\nA. surprised\nB. gladdened\nC. angered\n\nWhat will this incident teach Carlos?\nA. to be more polite\nB. to be more obedient\nC. to be more careful with his things\n\nWhy does Carlo seem to be a careless boy?\nA. because he always listens to her Mom.\nB. because he doesn’t care\nC. because he is a good boy.\n\nWhose bag was torn by pet Liksi?\nA. Carlo\nB. Mom\nC. Father',1,1,'answer'),
(1071,378,90,'pre',3,'Guava Jam','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nGuava Jam\nThe cook had just prepared a kettle of guava jam. She placed the kettle on the table to cool. Some guava jam spilled on the table. In a short time, ants gathered at the jam on the table. “What fine guava jam!” they all said. The ants ate and ate. They continued eating even when they were already full. They did not want to leave the jam. They thought they would sleep on it so that when they wake up they could eat and eat again. But alas, the guava jam became thicker and thicker as it cooled.\n\nWhat fruit is the jam?\nA. Strawberry\nB. Guava\nC. Tamarind\n\nWhere these ants gathered to ate the jam?\nA. In the table.\nB. In the bed.\nC. In the floor\n\nWhat happened to the guava when it cooled?\nA. It became sticky\nB. It became watery\nC. It became thicker\n\nWhat happened to the ants?\nA. They became healthy.\nB. They stayed on the jam for a vacation.\nC. Their legs got stuck on the table and they died there.\n\nWhat should they have done?\nA. They should have eaten just enough and left.\nB. They should not have eaten any of the jam.\nC. They should have brought home the jam.\n\nWhat lesson did you get from his story?\nA. Don’t be too slow.\nB. Don’t be too greedy.\nC. Don’t be too industrious.\n\nWhy ants decide to sleep on the jam?\nA. to play there\nB. to study there\nC. to eat there','assets/images/level6/g4/p011-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p011-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nGuava Jam\nThe cook had just prepared a kettle of guava jam. She placed the kettle on the table to cool. Some guava jam spilled on the table. In a short time, ants gathered at the jam on the table. “What fine guava jam!” they all said. The ants ate and ate. They continued eating even when they were already full. They did not want to leave the jam. They thought they would sleep on it so that when they wake up they could eat and eat again. But alas, the guava jam became thicker and thicker as it cooled.\n\nWhat fruit is the jam?\nA. Strawberry\nB. Guava\nC. Tamarind\n\nWhere these ants gathered to ate the jam?\nA. In the table.\nB. In the bed.\nC. In the floor\n\nWhat happened to the guava when it cooled?\nA. It became sticky\nB. It became watery\nC. It became thicker\n\nWhat happened to the ants?\nA. They became healthy.\nB. They stayed on the jam for a vacation.\nC. Their legs got stuck on the table and they died there.\n\nWhat should they have done?\nA. They should have eaten just enough and left.\nB. They should not have eaten any of the jam.\nC. They should have brought home the jam.\n\nWhat lesson did you get from his story?\nA. Don’t be too slow.\nB. Don’t be too greedy.\nC. Don’t be too industrious.\n\nWhy ants decide to sleep on the jam?\nA. to play there\nB. to study there\nC. to eat there',NULL,10,11,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nGuava Jam\nThe cook had just prepared a kettle of guava jam. She placed the kettle on the table to cool. Some guava jam spilled on the table. In a short time, ants gathered at the jam on the table. “What fine guava jam!” they all said. The ants ate and ate. They continued eating even when they were already full. They did not want to leave the jam. They thought they would sleep on it so that when they wake up they could eat and eat again. But alas, the guava jam became thicker and thicker as it cooled.\n\nWhat fruit is the jam?\nA. Strawberry\nB. Guava\nC. Tamarind\n\nWhere these ants gathered to ate the jam?\nA. In the table.\nB. In the bed.\nC. In the floor\n\nWhat happened to the guava when it cooled?\nA. It became sticky\nB. It became watery\nC. It became thicker\n\nWhat happened to the ants?\nA. They became healthy.\nB. They stayed on the jam for a vacation.\nC. Their legs got stuck on the table and they died there.\n\nWhat should they have done?\nA. They should have eaten just enough and left.\nB. They should not have eaten any of the jam.\nC. They should have brought home the jam.\n\nWhat lesson did you get from his story?\nA. Don’t be too slow.\nB. Don’t be too greedy.\nC. Don’t be too industrious.\n\nWhy ants decide to sleep on the jam?\nA. to play there\nB. to study there\nC. t',1,1,'answer'),
(1072,378,90,'pre',4,'Playing with Circles','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nPlaying with Circles\n\nDraw five circles of the same size. Draw a straight line joining the circles through the middle.\n\nDraw a big circle. Divide it into four equal parts. Shade one part of it with your pencil.\n\nWrite what part of your circle in number 2 is not shaded.\n\nDraw a big circle. Write the word circle inside it.\n\nDraw another big circle. Draw aa smaller circle inside it.','assets/images/level6/g4/p013-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p013-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nPlaying with Circles\n\nDraw five circles of the same size. Draw a straight line joining the circles through the middle.\n\nDraw a big circle. Divide it into four equal parts. Shade one part of it with your pencil.\n\nWrite what part of your circle in number 2 is not shaded.\n\nDraw a big circle. Write the word circle inside it.\n\nDraw another big circle. Draw aa smaller circle inside it.',NULL,10,13,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nPlaying with Circles\n\nDraw five circles of the same size. Draw a straight line joining the circles through the middle.\n\nDraw a big circle. Divide it into four equal parts. Shade one part of it with your pencil.\n\nWrite what part of your circle in number 2 is not shaded.\n\nDraw a big circle. Write the word circle inside it.\n\nDraw another big circle. Draw aa smaller circle inside it.',1,1,'answer'),
(1073,378,90,'pre',5,'The Horse and the Snail','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Horse and Snail\nOne morning the horse and the snail met. The horse made fun of how the snail walked. This made the snail very angry. He decided to run a race with the horse. The snail walked slowly. But walked and walked. He did not look back. The horse laughed. He could easily beat the snail, the horse thought. He ran for a while. He saw the snail for behind him. He rested under a mango tree. Soon he fell asleep. The snail walked past the horse. He did not rest. When the horse woke up, he ran as fast as he could. But the snail was the first at the finish line.','assets/images/level6/g4/p014-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p014-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Horse and Snail\nOne morning the horse and the snail met. The horse made fun of how the snail walked. This made the snail very angry. He decided to run a race with the horse. The snail walked slowly. But walked and walked. He did not look back. The horse laughed. He could easily beat the snail, the horse thought. He ran for a while. He saw the snail for behind him. He rested under a mango tree. Soon he fell asleep. The snail walked past the horse. He did not rest. When the horse woke up, he ran as fast as he could. But the snail was the first at the finish line.',NULL,10,14,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Horse and Snail\nOne morning the horse and the snail met. The horse made fun of how the snail walked. This made the snail very angry. He decided to run a race with the horse. The snail walked slowly. But walked and walked. He did not look back. The horse laughed. He could easily beat the snail, the horse thought. He ran for a while. He saw the snail for behind him. He rested under a mango tree. Soon he fell asleep. The snail walked past the horse. He did not rest. When the horse woke up, he ran as fast as he could. But the snail was the first at the finish line.',1,1,'answer'),
(1074,379,NULL,'learn',1,'Pepe and the Guavas','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nPepe and the Guavas\nPepe climbed the guava tree near his house. It had many ripe fruits. He picked as many as he could and put them in his pockets. Then he sat on a branch and began eating them. While he was eating, he felt the branch break. He did not know it was a dead branch.\n\nDown, down he fell! After that, he did not know what happened. When he woke up, he was in a hospital bed. His two arms were in cast.\n\nWho climbed the guava tree?\nA. Pepe\nB. Pepe’s friend\nC. Pepe’s brother\n\nWhere was the guava tree?\nA. Near Pepe’s house\nB. In his neighbor’s yard\nC. Near his friend’s house\n\nWhat was the fruit on the tree?\nA. Ripe guava fruits\nB. green fruits\nC. Many birds\n\nWhere did Pepe put the fruits he picked?\nA. In his hat\nB. In a basket\nC. In his pocket\n\nWhy did Pepe fall down at the guava tree?\nA. He did not know it was a died branch\nB. He did not know what happened\nC. He felt the branch break\n\nWhen did he know that he fell down?\nA. His two arms were in cast\nB. When he woke up he was in a hospital bed\nC. He woke up at the branch of a tree\n\nHow did Pepe get on the top of the tree?\nA. He climbed the tree\nB. He sat on the branch\nC. He fall down on the tree','assets/images/level6/g4/p016-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p016-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer