Pepe’s friend\nC. Pepe’s brother\n\nWhere was the guava tree?\nA. Near Pepe’s house\nB. In his neighbor’s yard\nC. Near his friend’s house\n\nWhat was the fruit on the tree?\nA. Ripe guava fruits\nB. green fruits\nC. Many birds\n\nWhere did Pepe put the fruits he picked?\nA. In his hat\nB. In a basket\nC. In his pocket\n\nWhy did Pepe fall down at the guava tree?\nA. He did not know it was a died branch\nB. He did not know what happened\nC. He felt the branch break\n\nWhen did he know that he fell down?\nA. His two arms were in cast\nB. When he woke up he was in a hospital bed\nC. He woke up at the branch of a tree\n\nHow did Pepe get on the top of the tree?\nA. He climbed the tree\nB. He sat on the branch\nC. He fall down on the tree',1,1,'answer'),
(1075,380,NULL,'learn',1,'At the Public Playground','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nAt the Public Playground\nThe public playground was full of children. They were shouting with joy. The smaller children were playing in the sand boxes. They were digging the sand and filling their pails. The bigger boys and girls were having fun riding on swings.\n\nSome big boys were chinning the bar. Others were climbing the big tower and were sliding down. Some of them were busy playing on the seesaws, going up and going down. Some girls in bathing suits were swimming in the pool.\n\nWhere were the children?\nA. In school\nB. At the Rizal Park\nC. At the public playground\n\nHow did they show they were happy?\nA. They shouted with joy.\nB. They ran and jumped.\nC. They ran here and there.\n\nWho played in the sand boxes?\nA. small girls\nB. small boys\nC. smaller children\n\nWhat did they do?\nA. Made houses of sand.\nB. Filled their pails with sand.\nC. Walked without shoes on the sand.\n\nHow did the bigger boys and girls have fun?\nA. Rode in bicycles.\nB. Danced together.\nC. Rode on the swings.\n\nWho chinned the bar?\nA. A big boy.\nB. Some big girls.\nC. Some big boys.\n\nHow did the children go down the tower?\nA. Sliding\nB. Running\nC. Jumping\n\nWhat went up and down?\nA. Slides\nB. Seesaw\nC. Swings\n\nWho were swimming in the pool?\nA. Some girls\nB. Some boys\nC. Little children\n\nWhat were they wearing?\nA. Shorts\nB. Play suits\nC. Bathing suits','assets/images/level6/g4/p018-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p018-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nAt the Public Playground\nThe public playground was full of children. They were shouting with joy. The smaller children were playing in the sand boxes. They were digging the sand and filling their pails. The bigger boys and girls were having fun riding on swings.\n\nSome big boys were chinning the bar. Others were climbing the big tower and were sliding down. Some of them were busy playing on the seesaws, going up and going down. Some girls in bathing suits were swimming in the pool.\n\nWhere were the children?\nA. In school\nB. At the Rizal Park\nC. At the public playground\n\nHow did they show they were happy?\nA. They shouted with joy.\nB. They ran and jumped.\nC. They ran here and there.\n\nWho played in the sand boxes?\nA. small girls\nB. small boys\nC. smaller children\n\nWhat did they do?\nA. Made houses of sand.\nB. Filled their pails with sand.\nC. Walked without shoes on the sand.\n\nHow did the bigger boys and girls have fun?\nA. Rode in bicycles.\nB. Danced together.\nC. Rode on the swings.\n\nWho chinned the bar?\nA. A big boy.\nB. Some big girls.\nC. Some big boys.\n\nHow did the children go down the tower?\nA. Sliding\nB. Running\nC. Jumping\n\nWhat went up and down?\nA. Slides\nB. Seesaw\nC. Swings\n\nWho were swimming in the pool?\nA. Some girls\nB. Some boys\nC. Little children\n\nWhat were they wearing?\nA. Shorts\nB. Play suits\nC. Bathing suits',NULL,10,18,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nAt the Public Playground\nThe public playground was full of children. They were shouting wit