(1076,381,NULL,'learn',1,'A Family of Music Lovers','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nA Family of Music Lovers\nThe Santos family are fond of music. All of them have good singing voices and all can play the piano. Mr. Santos is their teacher and Mrs. Santos is their pianist. People enjoy listening to them when they are practicing, more so when they sing Filipino songs. The songs make the listeners happy. Lita, Raul, Emil, Nina and Anita sing with feeling. While singing they watch Mr. Santos’s hand, so they know when to sing louder or softer.\n\nHow many children are in the family?\nA. Five\nB. Six\nC. Seven\n\nWhat kind of family are the Santoses?\nA. Poetic\nB. Dramatic\nC. Music lovers\n\nWhat do all of them have?\nA. Good singing voices\nB. Weak singing voices\nC. Good speaking voices\n\nWhat instrument can they play?\nA. Guitar\nB. Violin\nC. Piano\n\nWho is their teacher?\nA. Their father\nB. Their mother\nC. Their brother\n\nWho is their pianist?\nA. Their father\nB. Their brother\nC. Their mother\n\nHow do people feel while they are listening to the Santoses?\nA. Sad\nB. Angry\nC. Happy\n\nHow do the children sing?\nA. Noisily\nB. With feeling\nC. Loud and clear\n\nWhat kind of songs make the listeners feel happier?\nA. English songs\nB. Filipino songs\nC. American songs\n\nWhat is the children’s sign in signing louder or softer?\nA. Mr. Santos’s eyes\nB. Mr. Santos’s hands\nC. Mrs. Santos’s body movement','assets/images/level6/g4/p020-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p020-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read 