tos is their pianist. People enjoy listening to them when they are practicing, more so when they sing Filipino songs. The songs make the listeners happy. Lita, Raul, Emil, Nina and Anita sing with feeling. While singing they watch Mr. Santos’s hand, so they know when to sing louder or softer.\n\nHow many children are in the family?\nA. Five\nB. Six\nC. Seven\n\nWhat kind of family are the Santoses?\nA. Poetic\nB. Dramatic\nC. Music lovers\n\nWhat do all of them have?\nA. Good singing voices\nB. Weak singing voices\nC. Good speaking voices\n\nWhat instrument can they play?\nA. Guitar\nB. Violin\nC. Piano\n\nWho is their teacher?\nA. Their father\nB. Their mother\nC. Their brother\n\nWho is their pianist?\nA. Their father\nB. Their brother\nC. Their mother\n\nHow do people feel while they are listening to the Santoses?\nA. Sad\nB. Angry\nC. Happy\n\nHow do the children sing?\nA. Noisily\nB. With feeling\nC. Loud and clear\n\nWhat kind of songs make the listeners feel happier?\nA. English songs\nB. Filipino songs\nC. American songs\n\nWhat is the children’s sign in signing louder or softer?\nA. Mr. Santos’s eyes\nB. Mr. Santo',1,1,'answer'),
(1077,382,NULL,'learn',1,'The Artesian Well','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Artesian Well\nNonoy lived in a little barrio far from the town. He had to wake up early every morning to fetch water from a well. He had to make several trips before he could fill a big jar.\n\nOne day men came to the barrio to drill an artesian well. In ten days, the artesian well was ready. It was like there was a fiesta. Barrio people lined up to get water. When Nonoy’s turn came, he took a long drink. How cool and satisfying the water tasted!\n\nWhere did Nonoy live?\nA. In a barrio\nB. In the town\nC. In a city\n\nWhat did he do every morning?\nA. Fetched water from a well.\nB. Fetched his sister from school.\nC. Bought bread from the store.\n\nHow long did it take him to get water?\nA. Two trips\nB. Several trips\nC. Several hours\n\nWhere did he put the water?\nA. On a big jar\nB. In a big can\nC. In a big bottle\n\nWhat did the men do in the barrio?\nA. Drilled an artesian well.\nB. Fetched water for the people.\nC. Dug a deep well in the ground.\n\nHow did the barrio people feel about it?\nA. Angry\nB. Happy\nC. Ashamed\n\nWhat would the well give them?\nA. Unsafe water\nB. Clean, safe water\nC. Water for the fields\n\nHow long did the men finish the work?\nA. Ten days\nB. Four days\nC. One week\n\nWhat did the barrio people do when it was ready?\nA. Lined up to get water\nB. Took bath near the well.\nC. Danced along the tree\n\nHow did the water taste to Nonoy?\nA. He did not like it.\nB. It was not so good.\nC. It tasted cool and satisfying.','assets/images/level6/g4/p022-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p022-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Artesian Well\nNonoy lived in a little barrio far from the town. He had to wake up early every morning to fetch water from a well. He had to make several trips before he could fill a big jar.\n\nOne day men came to the barrio to drill an artesian well. In ten days, the artesian well was ready. It was like there was a fiesta. Barrio people lined up to get water. When Nonoy’s turn came, he took a long drink. How cool and satisfying the water tasted!\n\nWhere did Nonoy live?\nA. In a barrio\nB. In the town\nC. In a city\n\nWhat did he do every morning?\nA. Fetched water from a well.\nB. Fetched his sister from school.\nC. Bought bread from the store.\n\nHow long did it take him to get water?\nA. Two trips\nB. Several trips\nC. Several hours\n\nWhere did he put the water?\nA. On a big jar\nB. In a big can\nC. In a big bottle\n\nWhat did the men do in the barrio?\nA. Drilled an artesian well.\nB. Fetched water for the people.\nC. Dug a deep well in the ground.\n\nHow did the barrio people feel about it?\nA. Angry\nB. Happy\nC. Ashamed\n\nWhat would the well give them?\nA. Unsafe water\nB. Clean, safe water\nC. Water for the fields\n\nHow long did the men finish the work?\nA. Ten days\nB. Four days\nC. One week\n\nWhat did the barrio people do when it was ready?\nA. Lined up to get water\nB. Took bath near the well.\nC. Danced along the tree\n\nHow did the water taste to Nonoy?\nA. He did not like it.\nB. It was not so good.\nC. It tasted cool and satisfying.',NULL,10,22,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Artesian Well\nNonoy lived in a little barrio far from the town. He had to wake up early every morning to fetch water from a well. He had to make several trips before he could fill a big jar.\n\nOne day men came to the barrio to drill an artesian well. In ten days, the artesian well was ready. It was like there was a fiesta. Barrio people lined up to get water. When Nonoy’s turn came, he took a long drink. How cool and satisfying the water tasted!\n\nWhere did Nonoy live?\nA. In a barrio\nB. In the town\nC. In a city\n\nWhat did he do every morning?\nA. Fetched water from a well.\nB. Fetched his sister from school.\nC. Bought bread from the store.\n\nHow long did it take him to get water?\nA. Two trips\nB. Several trips\nC. Several hours\n\nWhere did he put the water?\nA. On a big jar\nB. In a big can\nC. In a big bottle\n\nWhat did the men do in the barrio?\nA. Drilled an artesian well.\nB. Fetched water for the people.\nC. Dug a deep well in the ground.\n\nHow did the barrio people feel about it?\nA. Angry\nB. Happy\nC. Ashamed\n\nWhat would the well give them?\nA. Unsafe water\nB. Clean, safe water\nC. Water for the fields\n\nHow long did the men finish the work?\nA. Ten days\nB. Four days\nC. One week\n\nWhat did the barrio people do when it was ready?\nA. Lined up to get wat',1,1,'answer'),
(1078,383,NULL,'learn',1,'Raindrops','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nRaindrops\n“I’m going down to do my turn,”\nOnce said a drop of rain;\n“I hear a sign, a thirsty sigh,\nI’ll go with you.” “Me, too! Me, too!”\nCried all the raindrops near;\nSo down they fell, in merry mood,\nThe whole wide field to cheer.\n\nWhat is the best tittle for this poem?\nA. The field\nB. The rain\nC. The flowers\n\nWho are talking in the poem?\nA. The flower\nB. The raindrops\nC. The field\n\nWhich sentence tells about the rain?\nA. It waters plants to make them grow.\nB. It causes floods which destroy crops.\nC. It prevents children from going to school.','assets/images/level6/g4/p024-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p024-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nRaindrops\n“I’m going down to do my turn,”\nOnce said a drop of rain;\n“I hear a sign, a thirsty sigh,\nI’ll go with you.” “Me, too! Me, too!”\nCried all the raindrops near;\nSo down they fell, in merry mood,\nThe whole wide field to cheer.\n\nWhat is the best tittle for this poem?\nA. The field\nB. The rain\nC. The flowers\n\nWho are talking in the poem?\nA. The flower\nB. The raindrops\nC. The field\n\nWhich sentence tells about the rain?\nA. It waters plants to make them grow.\nB. It causes floods which destroy crops.\nC. It prevents children from going to school.',NULL,10,24,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nRaindrops\n“I’m going down to do my turn,”\nOnce said a drop of rain;\n“I hear a sigh, a thirsty sigh,\nI’ll go with you.” “Me, too! Me, too!”\nCried all the raindrops near;\nSo down they fell, in merry mood,\nThe whole wide field to cheer.\n\nWhat is the best tittle for this poem?\nA. The field\nB. The rain\nC. The flowers\n\nWho are talking in the poem?\nA. The flower\nB. The raindrops\nC. The field\n\nWhich sentence tells about the rain?\nA. It waters plants to make them grow.\nB. It causes floods which destroy crops.\nC. It prevents children from going to school.',1,1,'answer'),
(1079,384,NULL,'learn',1,'Carlos','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nCarlos\nCarlos is a fourth grader. His books are not covered. He loses his pencil very often. Every day, when he arrives from school he throws his bag and books around. One day, he left his schoolbag on the floor. His dog, Liksi, found the bag. It bit and tore the bag. It bit one book and tore the pages. It bit another book and tore the pages too.\n\nCarlos’s mother saw what happened. She quickly drove the dog away. She picked up the bag. It was torn to pieces. She picked up a book. Many pages were also torn.\n\nWhat is the story about?\nA. A careless boy.\nB. Carlos’s mother\nC. A dog named Liksi.\n\nHow did Carlos’s mother feel when she saw what happened?\nA. Surprised\nB. Gladdened\nC. Angered\n\nWhat will this incident teach Carlos?\nA. To be more polite.\nB. To be more obedient.\nC. to be more careful with his things.\n\nHow did Liksi ruin the bag and book?\nA. stepped on it\nB. bit and tore it\nC. throw it away\n\nWhat happened to the other book bitten by Liksi?\nA. it was wet\nB. it was lost\nC. it was to torn into pieces\n\nWhat do you think fits to describe the attitude of Liksi?\nA. playful\nB. naughty\nC. well-behaved\n\nIs Carlos’s behavior on taking care of his things is very good?\nA. Yes\nB. No\nC. Maybe','assets/images/level6/g4/p025-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p025-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter o