he same joke again to others.\nC. Do not play such a kind of joke anymore.\n\nWhy is that Carlito shouted?\nA. Because he wants to scare her sister.\nB. Because He was surprised seeing the mouse.\nC. Because He was angry seeing the mouse.',1,1,'answer'),
(1083,388,NULL,'learn',1,'The Birdlings','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Birdlings\nHigh on the tree top, four hungry bird lings lay chirping in their nest.\n\nMother bird was hunting food for its young ones. It was in the wide-open yard looking for fat worms.\n\nA boy with a slingshot came along. Slowly he went near mother bird and shot at it.\n\nWhat a good aim! Mother bird lay on the ground with a broken wing. “I’ll have my catch fried for my supper,” said the boy to himself as he went home whistling with the bird on his hand.\n\nWhat do you think happened to the birdlings?\nA. They learned to look for their own food.\nB. They died of hunger.\nC. The boy took care of them.\n\nWhat happened with Mother bird?\nA. It’s broken wing was treated and it was returned to the birdlings.\nB. It was killed and fried for supper.\nC. It was thrown away.\n\nWhat do you think did the boy have for his supper that evening?\nA. Fried bird\nB. Fried fish\nC. Pancit and soup','assets/images/level6/g4/p031-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p031-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Birdlings\nHigh on the tree top, four hungry bird lings lay chirping in their nest.\n\nMother bird was hunting food for its young ones. It was in the wide-open yard looking for fat worms.\n\nA boy with a slingshot came along. Slowly he went near mother bird and shot at it.\n\nWhat a good aim! Mother bird lay on the ground with a broken wing. “I’ll have my catch fried for my supper,” said the boy to himself as he went home whistling with the bird on his hand.\n\nWhat do you think happened to the birdlings?\nA. They learned to look for their own food.\nB. They died of hunger.\nC. The boy took care of them.\n\nWhat happened with Mother bird?\nA. It’s broken wing was treated and it was returned to the birdlings.\nB. It was killed and fried for supper.\nC. It was thrown away.\n\nWhat do you think did the boy have for his supper that evening?\nA. Fried bird\nB. Fried fish\nC. Pancit and soup',NULL,10,31,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Birdlings\nHigh on the tree top, four hungry bird lings lay chirping in their nest.\n\nMother bird was hunting food for its young ones. It was in the wide-open yard looking for fat worms.\n\nA boy with a slingshot came along. Slowly he went near mother bird and shot at it.\n\nWhat a good aim! Mother bird lay on the ground with a broken wing. “I’ll have my catch fried for my supper,” said the boy to himself as he went home whistling with the bird on his hand.\n\nWhat do you think happened to the birdlings?\nA. They learned to look for their own food.\nB. They died of hunger.\nC. The boy took care of them.\n\nWhat happened with Mother bird?\nA. It’s broken wing was treated and it was returned to the birdlings.\nB. It was killed and fried for supper.\nC. It was thrown away.\n\nWhat do you think did the boy have for his supper that evening?\nA. Fried bird\nB. Fried fish\nC. Pancit and soup',1,1,'answer'),
(1084,389,NULL,'learn',1,'The Pet Bird','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Pet Bird\nDolor had a pet bird which she loved very much. Every day she gave it ripe bananas to eat and fresh water to drink.\n\nOne day Dolor got sick and had to stay in bed. She asked her brother Jun to feed her pet every day. But Jun was very different from Dolor. He was not found of the bird.\n\nOne morning Jun hurriedly gave the bird a ripe banana and some water. Then, away he ran to his waiting friends.\n\nWhen Dolor woke up, she saw a little red feather on her blanket. She thought her bird was beside her. Then she found other feathers scattered on the floor. Slowly she got up and looked at her bird in the cage. The cage was empty.\n\nDolor cried bitterly. She cried and cried and would not eat. Her mother was worried. Jun was very sorry.\n\nThen Jun got his savings and went out. “I must do something for Dolor,” he said.\n\nWhat happen with the bird?\nA. It flew away.\nB. It got sick and die.\nC. It was eaten by the cat.\n\nWhat might happen to dolor due to the disappearance of her bird?\nA. She might get well very soon.\nB. She might get worse.\nC. She might become kinder.\n\nWhat will June do with his savings?\nA. give it to Dolor.\nB. buy doll for Dolor.\nC. buy another bird for Dolor.','assets/images/level6/g4/p032-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p032-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct an