(1095,399,91,'post',2,'Exercise','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nExercise\nCarlos is a fourth grader. His books are not covered. He loses his pencil very often. Every day, when he arrives from school he throws his bag and books around. One day, he left his schoolbag on the floor. His dog, Liksi, found the bag. It bit and tore the bag. It bit one book and tore the pages, too. Carlos’s mother saw what happened. She quickly drove the dog away. She picked up the bag. It was torn to pieces. She picked up a book. Many pages were also torn.\n\nWho is the boy in the story?\nA. Jhon\nB. Karla\nC. Carlos\n\nWhat pet is Liksi?\nA. Cow\nB. Dog\nC. Cat\n\nWhat is the story about?\nA. a careless boy\nB. Carlos’s mother\nC. a dog named Liksi\n\nHow did Carlos’s mother feel when she saw what happened?\nA. surprised\nB. gladdened\nC. angered\n\nWhat will this incident teach Carlos?\nA. to be more polite\nB. to be more obedient\nC. to be more careful with his things\n\nWhy is Carlos a careless boy?\nA. because he always listens to her Mom.\nB. because he doesn’t care\nC. because he is a good boy.\n\nWho owns the bag which was torn by Liksi?\nA. Carlos\nB. Mom\nC. Father','assets/images/level6/g4/p045-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p045-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nExercise\nCarlos is a fourth grader. His books are not covered. He loses his 