ned?\nA. surprised\nB. gladdened\nC. angered\n\nWhat will this incident teach Carlos?\nA. to be more polite\nB. to be more obedient\nC. to be more careful with his things\n\nWhy is Carlos a careless boy?\nA. because he always listens to her Mom.\nB. because he doesn’t care\nC. because he is a good boy.\n\nWho owns the bag which was torn by Liksi?\nA. Carlos\nB. Mom\nC. Father',1,1,'answer'),
(1096,399,91,'post',3,'Guava Jam','open','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nGuava Jam\nThe cook had just prepared a kettle of guava jam. She placed the kettle on the table to cool. Some guava jam spilled on the table. In a short time, ants gathered at the jam on the table. “What fine guava jam!” they all said. The ants ate and ate. They continued eating even when they were already full. They did not want to leave the jam. They thought they would sleep on it so that when they wake up they could eat and eat again. But alas, the guava jam became thicker and thicker as it cooled.\n\nWhat fruit is the jam?\nA. Strawberry\nB. Guava\nC. Tamarind\n\nWhere these ants gathered to ate the jam?\nA. In the table.\nB. In the bed.\nC. In the floor\n\nWhat happened to the guava when it cooled?\nA. It became sticky\nB. It became watery.\nC. It became thicker\n\nWhat happened to the ants?\nA. They became healthy.\nB. They stayed on the jam for a vacation.\nC. Their legs got stuck on the table and they died there.\n\nWhat should they have done?\nA. They should have eaten just enough and left.\nB. They should not have eaten any of the jam.\nC. They should have brought home the jam.\n\nWhat lesson did you get from his story?\nA. Don’t be too slow.\nB. Don’t be too greedy.\nC. Don’t be too industrious.\n\nWhy ants decided to sleep on the jam?\nA. to play there\nB. to study there\nC. to eat there','assets/images/level6/g4/p047-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p047-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nGuava Jam\nThe cook had just prepared a kettle of guava jam. She placed the kettle on the table to cool. Some guava jam spilled on the table. In a short time, ants gathered at the jam on the table. “What fine guava jam!” they all said. The ants ate and ate. They continued eating even when they were already full. They did not want to leave the jam. They thought they would sleep on it so that when they wake up they could eat and eat again. But alas, the guava jam became thicker and thicker as it cooled.\n\nWhat fruit is the jam?\nA. Strawberry\nB. Guava\nC. Tamarind\n\nWhere these ants gathered to ate the jam?\nA. In the table.\nB. In the bed.\nC. In the floor\n\nWhat happened to the guava when it cooled?\nA. It became sticky\nB. It became watery.\nC. It became thicker\n\nWhat happened to the ants?\nA. They became healthy.\nB. They stayed on the jam for a vacation.\nC. Their legs got stuck on the table and they died there.\n\nWhat should they have done?\nA. They should have eaten just enough and left.\nB. They should not have eaten any of the jam.\nC. They should have brought home the jam.\n\nWhat lesson did you get from his story?\nA. Don’t be too slow.\nB. Don’t be too greedy.\nC. Don’t be too industrious.\n\nWhy ants decided to sleep on the jam?\nA. to play there\nB. to study there\nC. to eat there',NULL,10,47,'Instructions: Read the given story carefully. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nGuava Jam\nThe cook had just prepared a kettle of guava jam. She placed the kettle on the table to cool. Some guava jam spilled on the table. In a short time, ants gathered at the jam on the table. “What fine guava jam!” they all said. The ants ate and ate. They continued eating even when they were already full. They did not want to leave the jam. They thought they would sleep on it so that when they wake up they could eat and eat again. But alas, the guava jam became thicker and thicker as it cooled.\n\nWhat fruit is the jam?\nA. Strawberry\nB. Guava\nC. Tamarind\n\nWhere these ants gathered to ate the jam?\nA. In the table.\nB. In the bed.\nC. In the floor\n\nWhat happened to the guava when it cooled?\nA. It became sticky\nB. It became watery.\nC. It became thicker\n\nWhat happened to the ants?\nA. They became healthy.\nB. They stayed on the jam for a vacation.\nC. Their legs got stuck on the table and they died there.\n\nWhat should they have done?\nA. They should have eaten just enough and left.\nB. They should not have eaten any of the jam.\nC. They should have brought home the jam.\n\nWhat lesson did you get from his story?\nA. Don’t be too slow.\nB. Don’t be too greedy.\nC. Don’t be too industrious.\n\nWhy ants decided to sleep on the jam?\nA. to play there\nB. to study there\nC.',1,1,'answer'),
(1097,399,91,'post',4,'Playing with Circles','open','Instructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.','Instructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.\n\nPlaying with Circles\n\nDraw five circles of the same size. Draw a straight line joining the circles through the middle.\n\nDraw a big circle. Divide it into four equal parts. Shade one part of it with your pencil.\n\nWrite what part of your circle in number 2 is not shaded.\n\nDraw a big circle. Write the word circle inside it.\n\nDraw another big circle. Draw a smaller circle inside it.','assets/images/level6/g4/p049-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p049-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.\n\nPlaying with Circles\n\nDraw five circles of the same size. Draw a straight line joining the circles through the middle.\n\nDraw a big circle. Divide it into four equal parts. Shade one part of it with your pencil.\n\nWrite what part of your circle in number 2 is not shaded.\n\nDraw a big circle. Write the word circle inside it.\n\nDraw another big circle. Draw a smaller circle inside it.',NULL,10,49,'Instructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.\n\nPlaying with Circles\n\nDraw five circles of the same size. Draw a straight line joining the circles through the middle.\n\nDraw a big circle. Divide it into four equal parts. Shade one part of it with your pencil.\n\nWrite what part of your circle in number 2 is not shaded.\n\nDraw a big circle. Write the word circle inside it.\n\nDraw another big circle. Draw a smaller circle inside it.',1,1,'answer'),
(1098,399,91,'post',5,'The Horse and the Snail','open','Instructions: Read the words or sentences aloud as quickly and correctly as you can. Start when your teacher says “Go.” Read clearly and do not skip any word.','Instructions: Read the words or sentences aloud as quickly and correctly as you can. Start when your teacher says “Go.” Read clearly and do not skip any word.\n\nThe Horse and Snail\nOne morning the horse and the snail met. The horse made fun of how the snail walked. This made the snail very angry. He decided to run a race with the horse. The snail walked slowly. But walked and walked. He did not look back. The horse laughed. He could easily beat the snail, the horse thought. He ran for a while. He saw the snail far behind him. He rested under a mango tree. Soon he fell asleep. The snail walked past the horse. He did not rest. When the horse woke up, he ran as fast as he could. But the snail was the first at the finish line.','assets/images/level6/g4/p050-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g4/p050-1.webp\"]','Instructions: Read the words or sentences aloud as quickly and correctly as you can. Start when your teacher says “Go.” Read clearly and do not skip any word.\n\nThe Horse and Snail\nOne morning the horse and the snail met. The horse made fun of how the snail walked. This made the snail very angry. He decided to run a race with the horse. The snail walked slowly. But walked and walked. He did not look back. The horse laughed. He could easily beat the snail, the horse thought. He ran for a while. He saw the snail far behind him. He rested under a mango tree. Soon he fell asleep. The snail walked past the horse. He did not rest. When the horse woke up, he ran as fast as he could. But the snail was the first at the finish line.',NULL,10,50,'Instructions: Read the words or sentences aloud as quickly and correctly as you can. Start when your teacher says “Go.” Read clearly and do not skip any word.\n\nThe Horse and Snail\nOne morning the horse and the snail met. The horse made fun of how the snail walked. This made the snail very angry. He decided to run a race with the horse. The snail walked slowly. But walked and walked. He did not look back. The horse laughed. He could easily beat the snail, the horse thought. He ran for a while. He saw the snail far behind him. He rested under a mango tree. Soon he fell asleep. The snail walked past the horse. He did not rest. When the horse woke up, he ran as fast as he could. But the snail was the first at the finish line.',1,1,'answer'),
(1099,400,92,'pre',1,'Magnets','open','Choose the letter of the correct answer.','Choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMagnets\nMagnets have the power of attracting objects made of steel, iron, and other metals.\n\nThe discovery of the magnet and the many things that have been made out of it have brought about many discoveries and useful things. The magnet makes possible the compass that was used and still being used by travelers - pilots, sailors, boy scouts, soldiers, engineers, and others. The magnet which makes use of electricity has made all types of electric and industrial motors.\n\nMagnets can attract objects made of ___________.\nA. plastic\nB. metals\nC. wood\nD. rubber\n\nThe discovery of magnets led to many ______________.\nA. inventions\nB. revolutions\nC. problems\nD. effects\n\nMagnets made possible the inventions of the ____________.\nA. compass\nB. computer\nC. camera\nD. cellphone\n\nPilots, sailors, boy scouts, soldiers and engineers depend much on ______.\nA. compass\nB. electricity\nC. motors\nD. laptop','assets/images/level6/g5/p008-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g5/p008-1.webp\", \"assets/images/level6/g5/p008-2.webp\"]','Choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMagnets\nMagnets have the power of attracting objects made of steel, iron, and other metals.\n\nThe discovery of the magnet and the many things that have been made out of it have brought about many discoveries and useful things. The magnet makes possible the compass that was used and still being used by travelers - pilots, sailors, boy scouts, soldiers, engineers, and others. The magnet which makes use of electricity has made all types of electric and industrial motors.\n\nMagnets can attract objects made of ___________.\nA. plastic\nB. metals\nC. wood\nD. rubber\n\nThe discovery of magnets led to many ______________.\nA. inventions\nB. revolutions\nC. problems\nD. effects\n\nMagnets made possible the inventions of the ____________.\nA. compass\nB. computer\nC. camera\nD. cellphone\n\nPilots, sailors, boy scouts, soldiers and engineers depend much on ______.\nA. compass\nB. electricity\nC. motors\nD. laptop',NULL,10,8,'Choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMagnets\nMagnets have the power of attracting objects made of steel, iron, and other metals.\n\nThe discovery of the magnet and the many things that have been made out of it have brought about many discoveries and useful things. The magnet makes possible the compass that was used and still being used by travelers - pilots, sailors, boy scouts, soldiers, engineers, and others. The magnet which makes use of electricity has made all types of electric and industrial motors.\n\nMagnets can attract objects made of ___________.\nA. plastic\nB. metals\nC. wood\nD. rubber\n\nThe discovery of magnets led to many ______________.\nA. inventions\nB. revolutions\nC. problems\nD. effects\n\nMagnets made possible the inventions of the ____________.\nA. compass\nB. computer\nC. camera\nD. cellphone\n\nPilots, sailors, boy scouts, soldiers and engineers depend much on ______.\nA. compass\nB. electricity\nC. motors\nD. laptop',1,1,'answer'),
(1100,400,92,'pre',2,'Exercise 1','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nOur body remains at a certain temperature all the time. When we get very warm, little beads of water called sweat form on our skin. Sweat is mostly water mixed with salt from the body. This is also called perspiration. Perspiring is a quick method of cooling off the body. As a little bead of sweat evaporates, it carries away a little heat from the body, and we feel a little cooler.\n\nWhat happens to our body when we feel hot?\nA. Our body perspires\nB. Our body evaporates\nC. Our body burns\nD. Our body dies\n\nWhat is the paragraph about?\nA. It is about maintaining the body temperature.\nB. It is about keeping the body warm.\nC. It is about keeping the body cool.\nD. It is about living a meaningful life.\n\nWhat does the selection explain?\nA. perspiring is not good for the body.\nB. perspiring is good for the body.\nC. perspiring is a sign of illness.\nD. Perspiring can make us tired.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nOur body remains at a certain temperature all the time. When we get very warm, little beads of water called sweat form on our skin. Sweat is mostly water mixed with salt from the body. This is also called perspiration. Perspiring is a quick method of cooling off the body. As a little bead of sweat evaporates, it carries away a little heat from the body, and we feel a little cooler.\n\nWhat happens to our body when we feel hot?\nA. Our body perspires\nB. Our body evaporates\nC. Our body burns\nD. Our body dies\n\nWhat is the paragraph about?\nA. It is about maintaining the body temperature.\nB. It is about keeping the body warm.\nC. It is about keeping the body cool.\nD. It is about living a meaningful life.\n\nWhat does the selection explain?\nA. perspiring is not good for the body.\nB. perspiring is good for the body.\nC. perspiring is a sign of illness.\nD. Perspiring can make us tired.',NULL,10,9,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nOur body remains at a certain temperature all the time. When we get very warm, little beads of water called sweat form on our skin. Sweat is mostly water mixed with salt from the body. This is also called perspiration. Perspiring is a quick method of cooling off the body. As a little bead of sweat evaporates, it carries away a little heat from the body, and we feel a little cooler.\n\nWhat happens to our body when we feel hot?\nA. Our body perspires\nB. Our body evaporates\nC. Our body burns\nD. Our body dies\n\nWhat is the paragraph about?\nA. It is about maintaining the body temperature.\nB. It is about keeping the body warm.\nC. It is about keeping the body cool.\nD. It is about living a meaningful life.\n\nWhat does the selection explain?\nA. perspiring is not good for the body.\nB. perspiring is good for the body.\nC. perspiring is a sign of illness.\nD. Perspiring can make us tired.',1,1,'answer'),
(1101,400,92,'pre',3,'Exercise 2','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe body should be kept clean at all times. Plenty of soap and warm water help remove excess oil, dirt, and germs from the skin. Rubbing the body with a towel after bathing stimulates the flow of the oil from oil glands and keep the skin smooth and soft.\n\nDirty hands may not actually look dirty, but it is always safe to wash them before handling food, before and after eating.\n\nThe ears, the eyes, the nose, the mouth and teeth need special cleaning Attention so, with the hair.\n\nThe feet should be washed and dried before putting on one’s shoes or slippers.\n\nA clean body keeps sickness away!\n\nWhat is a good title for the selection?\nA. Keeping the body clean\nB. Dirty hands and feet\nC. How to clean One’s Feet\nD. How to be dirty\n\nWhen should the body be kept clean?\nA. before sleeping\nB. at all times\nC. before and after eating\nD. when we wake up\n\nWhich sentence is true according to the selection?\nA. A clean body keeps sickness away.\nB. Keeping the body clean takes little effort.\nC. Cleaning the body takes a lot of time and effort.\nD. A clean foot can attract other people.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe body should be kept clean at all times. Plenty of soap and warm water help remove excess oil, dirt, and germs from the skin. Rubbing the body with a towel after bathing stimulates the flow of the oil from oil glands and keep the skin smooth and soft.\n\nDirty hands may not actually look dirty, but it is always safe to wash them before handling food, before and after eating.\n\nThe ears, the eyes, the nose, the mouth and teeth need special cleaning Attention so, with the hair.\n\nThe feet should be washed and dried before putting on one’s shoes or slippers.\n\nA clean body keeps sickness away!\n\nWhat is a good title for the selection?\nA. Keeping the body clean\nB. Dirty hands and feet\nC. How to clean One’s Feet\nD. How to be dirty\n\nWhen should the body be kept clean?\nA. before sleeping\nB. at all times\nC. before and after eating\nD. when we wake up\n\nWhich sentence is true according to the selection?\nA. A clean body keeps sickness away.\nB. Keeping the body clean takes little effort.\nC. Cleaning the body takes a lot of time and effort.\nD. A clean foot can attract other people.',NULL,10,10,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe body should be kept clean at all times. Plenty of soap and warm water help remove excess oil, dirt, and germs from the skin. Rubbing the body with a towel after bathing stimulates the flow of the oil from oil glands and keep the skin smooth and soft.\n\nDirty hands may not actually look dirty, but it is always safe to wash them before handling food, before and after eating.\n\nThe ears, the eyes, the nose, the mouth and teeth need special cleaning Attention so, with the hair.\n\nThe feet should be washed and dried before putting on one’s shoes or slippers.\n\nA clean body keeps sickness away!\n\nWhat is a good title for the selection?\nA. Keeping the body clean\nB. Dirty hands and feet\nC. How to clean One’s Feet\nD. How to be dirty\n\nWhen should the body be kept clean?\nA. before sleeping\nB. at all times\nC. before and after eating\nD. when we wake up\n\nWhich sentence is true according to the selection?\nA. A clean body keeps sickness away.\nB. Keeping the body clean takes little effort.\nC. Cleaning the body takes a lot of time and effort.\nD. A clean foot can attract other people.',1,1,'answer'),
(1102,400,92,'pre',4,'Anti-Decay Vaccine','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAnti-Decay Vaccine\nMost people have had dental problems which start with a simple toothache. No matter how well one brushes his teeth, sooner or later cavities are formed which later cause tooth decay.\n\nToday, scientists are busy experimenting to discover a vaccine that would make people immune to tooth decay.\n\nWhy do scientists want to discover a vaccine for tooth decay?\nA. To help people avoid tooth decay.\nB. To help babies grow stronger.\nC. To improve people\'s eyesight.\nD. To help medicine companies earn money.\n\nWhat is the vaccine for?\nA. To prevent bad breath\nB. To prevent deformed teeth\nC. To prevent tooth decay\nD. To prevent skin diseases\n\nWhat will be the effect of the vaccine?\nA. Many people will be saved from the pain of having tooth decay.\nB. People will not brush their teeth anymore.\nC. There will be no more need for dentists.\nD. Many people will have skin allergies.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAnti-Decay Vaccine\nMost people have had dental problems which start with a simple toothache. No matter how well one brushes his teeth, sooner or later cavities are formed which later cause tooth decay.\n\nToday, scientists are busy experimenting to discover a vaccine that would make people immune to tooth decay.\n\nWhy do scientists want to discover a vaccine for tooth decay?\nA. To help people avoid tooth decay.\nB. To help babies grow stronger.\nC. To improve people\'s eyesight.\nD. To help medicine companies earn money.\n\nWhat is the vaccine for?\nA. To prevent bad breath\nB. To prevent deformed teeth\nC. To prevent tooth decay\nD. To prevent skin diseases\n\nWhat will be the effect of the vaccine?\nA. Many people will be saved from the pain of having tooth decay.\nB. People will not brush their teeth anymore.\nC. There will be no more need for dentists.\nD. Many people will have skin allergies.',NULL,10,11,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAnti-Decay Vaccine\nMost people have had dental problems which start with a simple toothache. No matter how well one brushes his teeth, sooner or later cavities are formed which later cause tooth decay.\n\nToday, scientists are busy experimenting to discover a vaccine that would make people immune to tooth decay.\n\nWhy do scientists want to discover a vaccine for tooth decay?\nA. To help people avoid tooth decay.\nB. To help babies grow stronger.\nC. To improve people\'s eyesight.\nD. To help medicine companies earn money.\n\nWhat is the vaccine for?\nA. To prevent bad breath\nB. To prevent deformed teeth\nC. To prevent tooth decay\nD. To prevent skin diseases\n\nWhat will be the effect of the vaccine?\nA. Many people will be saved from the pain of having tooth decay.\nB. People will not brush their teeth anymore.\nC. There will be no more need for dentists.\nD. Many people will have skin allergies.',1,1,'answer'),
(1103,400,92,'pre',5,'When Rizal Was a Boy','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nWhen Rizal Was a Boy\nOne Monday morning, Jose woke up early to get ready for school. His mother told him to wear his new “camisa” made of abaca. Jose looked quiet and sad. He didn’t like to wear camisa.\n\n“But I want you to wear it,” his mother insisted.\n\nJose looked at his mother and politely answered, “Yes Mother”.\n\nBox the word that described Jose.\nA. Intelligent\nB. Obedient\nC. Helpful\n\nBox the phrase that tells when the story happened.\nA. when Rizal was a boy\nB. when Rizal was a grown-up man\nC. when Rizal was dead\nD. when he was a teenager\n\nWhat word that starts with letter P that tells how Jose answered his mother?\n\nCopy the name of the plant mentioned in the selection and draw a box around it.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nWhen Rizal Was a Boy\nOne Monday morning, Jose woke up early to get ready for school. His mother told him to wear his new “camisa” made of abaca. Jose looked quiet and sad. He didn’t like to wear camisa.\n\n“But I want you to wear it,” his mother insisted.\n\nJose looked at his mother and politely answered, “Yes Mother”.\n\nBox the word that described Jose.\nA. Intelligent\nB. Obedient\nC. Helpful\n\nBox the phrase that tells when the story happened.\nA. when Rizal was a boy\nB. when Rizal was a grown-up man\nC. when Rizal was dead\nD. when he was a teenager\n\nWhat word that starts with letter P that tells how Jose answered his mother?\n\nCopy the name of the plant mentioned in the selection and draw a box around it.',NULL,10,12,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nWhen Rizal Was a Boy\nOne Monday morning, Jose woke up early to get ready for school. His mother told him to wear his new “camisa” made of abaca. Jose looked quiet and sad. He didn’t like to wear camisa.\n\n“But I want you to wear it,” his mother insisted.\n\nJose looked at his mother and politely answered, “Yes Mother”.\n\nBox the word that described Jose.\nA. Intelligent\nB. Obedient\nC. Helpful\n\nBox the phrase that tells when the story happened.\nA. when Rizal was a boy\nB. when Rizal was a grown-up man\nC. when Rizal was dead\nD. when he was a teenager\n\nWhat word that starts with letter P that tells how Jose answered his mother?\n\nCopy the name of the plant mentioned in the selection and draw a box around it.',1,1,'answer'),
(1104,400,92,'pre',6,'Insects','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nInsects\nThere are more than half a million kinds of insects. The kinds of insects outnumber the kinds of all animals put together.\n\nInsects live in almost any kind of habitat. There are many in the sea, but they are found almost everywhere in freshwater and on land.\n\nAll insects have six legs and one pair of feelers. All insects are covered with a waterproof substance called chitin. Most insects have wings. Their bodies are divided into three parts: the head, the thorax, and the abdomen.\n\nMost insects crawl, hop, swim, jump or walk. But flying is their usual way of getting about. Some can fly very fast. Dragonflies one are among the fastest fliers.\n\nSome insects have two pairs of wings. Some have one pair. Some have none at all. It is safe, therefore, to think that insects differ in shape, size and color.\n\nThere are more than ____________ kinds of insects.\nA. thousand\nB. half a million\nC. hundred\nD. millions\n\nIn what ways do insects differ?\nA. In form\nB. in height\nC. in shape, size and color\nD. in movement\n\nWhy can insects fly?\nA. they have legs\nB. they have antenna\nC. they have wings\nD. they have feelers','assets/images/level6/g5/p013-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g5/p013-1.webp\"]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nInsects\nThere are more than half a million kinds of insects. The kinds of insects outnumber the kinds of all animals put together.\n\nInsects live in almost any kind of habitat. There are many in the sea, but they are found almost everywhere in freshwater and on land.\n\nAll insects have six legs and one pair of feelers. All insects are covered with a waterproof substance called chitin. Most insects have wings. Their bodies are divided into three parts: the head, the thorax, and the abdomen.\n\nMost insects crawl, hop, swim, jump or walk. But flying is their usual way of getting about. Some can fly very fast. Dragonflies one are among the fastest fliers.\n\nSome insects have two pairs of wings. Some have one pair. Some have none at all. It is safe, therefore, to think that insects differ in shape, size and color.\n\nThere are more than ____________ kinds of insects.\nA. thousand\nB. half a million\nC. hundred\nD. millions\n\nIn what ways do insects differ?\nA. In form\nB. in height\nC. in shape, size and color\nD. in movement\n\nWhy can insects fly?\nA. they have legs\nB. they have antenna\nC. they have wings\nD. they have feelers',NULL,10,13,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nInsects\nThere are more than half a million kinds of insects. The kinds of insects outnumber the kinds of all animals put together.\n\nInsects live in almost any kind of habitat. There are many in the sea, but they are found almost everywhere in freshwater and on land.\n\nAll insects have six legs and one pair of feelers. All insects are covered with a waterproof substance called chitin. Most insects have wings. Their bodies are divided into three parts: the head, the thorax, and the abdomen.\n\nMost insects crawl, hop, swim, jump or walk. But flying is their usual way of getting about. Some can fly very fast. Dragonflies one are among the fastest fliers.\n\nSome insects have two pairs of wings. Some have one pair. Some have none at all. It is safe, therefore, to think that insects differ in shape, size and color.\n\nThere are more than ____________ kinds of insects.\nA. thousand\nB. half a million\nC. hundred\nD. millions\n\nIn what ways do insects differ?\nA. In form\nB. in height\nC. in shape, size and color\nD. in movement\n\nWhy can insects fly?\nA. they have legs\nB. they have antenna\nC. they have wings\nD. they have feelers',1,1,'answer'),
(1105,401,NULL,'learn',1,'The Eyebrows','open','Choose the letter of the correct answer:','Choose the letter of the correct answer:\n\nThe Eyebrows\nEyebrows are part of the face which serve two purposes--for beauty and protection.\n\nEyebrows make the face look more beautiful by calling attention to the eyes. They make the eyes look healthier and brighter.\n\nEyebrows not only beautify the face but also protect the eyes from sweat. Without the eyebrows, drops of sweat may run into the eyes and blur the sight. Sweat itself is a waste product and should be gotten rid of.\n\nThe part of the body mentioned in the selection is the ______________.\nA. eyelashes\nB. eyelids\nC. eyebrows\nD. eyeliner\n\nThis part makes the face look ____________.\nA. beautiful\nB. sad\nC. sleepy\nD. happy\n\nAside from beauty, they also serve the purpose of _______.\nA. communication\nB. conservation\nC. protection\nD. transportation\n\nThe eyebrows call attention to the ___________.\nA. nose\nB. eye s\nC. cheeks\nD. lips\n\nThe eyebrows make the face look _________.\nA. uglier\nB. healthier\nC. funnier\nD. younger\n\nHow do eyebrows serve its purpose for the eyes?\nA. The eyebrows protect the eyes from sweat.\nB. The eyebrows protect the eyes from glare.\nC. The eyebrows protect the eyes from diseases.\nD. The eyebrows protect the eyes from enemies.\n\nSweat is ________.\nA. sweet\nB. useful\nC. poisonous\nD. useless\n\nSweat can blur the sense of __________.\nA. sight\nB. smell\nC. taste\nD. touch\n\nSweat should be__________.\nA. conserved\nB. gotten rid of\nC. licked\nD. saved\n\nWhy do we have eyebrows?\nA. They make the face beautiful.\nB. They protect the eyes from sweat.\nC. They make the eyes look brighter.\nD. They help the face look healthier.','assets/images/level6/g5/p016-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level6/g5/p016-1.webp\"]','Choose the letter of the correct answer:\n\nThe Eyebrows\nEyebrows are part of the face which serve two purposes--for beauty and protection.\n\nEyebrows ma