(1194,474,NULL,'learn',1,'Danilo’s School Things','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nDanilo’s School Things\n“It is almost about time, Danilo. What is keeping you so long?” Mother called. “You should have placed them in your bag last night. I always tell you that.” Then she helped Danilo look for his ballpen and notebook.\n\nJust then the school bell rang. “There is the bell.” Mother said, “And you have not found your ballpen yet.”\n\nWhich of these was Danilo not able to find?\nA. His ballpen\nB. His notebook\nC. His ballpen and notebook\n\nWhich happened to Danilo?\nA. He was late in school.\nB. He did not go to school.\nC. He came to school on time.\n\nWhat lessen does the story teach?\nA. To be clean.\nB. To wake up early.\nC. To have school things ready at night.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nDanilo’s School Things\n“It is almost about time, Danilo. What is keeping you so long?” Mother called. “You should have placed them in your bag last night. I always tell you that.” Then she helped Danilo look for his ballpen and notebook.\n\nJust then the school bell rang. “There is the bell.” Mother said, “And you have not found your ballpen yet.”\n\nWhich of these was Danilo not able to find?\nA. His ballpen\nB. His notebook\nC. His ballpen and notebook\n\nWhich happened to Danilo?\nA. He was late in school.\nB. He did not go to school.\nC. He came to school on time.\n\nWhat lessen does the story teach?\nA. To be clean.\nB. To wake up early.\nC. To have school things ready at night.',NULL,10,35,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nDanilo’s School Things\n“It is almost about time, Danilo. What is keeping you so long?” Mother called. “You should have placed them in your bag last night. I always tell you that.” Then she helped Danilo look for his ballpen and notebook.\n\nJust then the school bell rang. “There is the bell.” Mother said, “And you have not found your ballpen yet.”\n\nWhich of these was Danilo not able to find?\nA. His ballpen\nB. His notebook\nC. His ballpen and notebook\n\nWhich happened to Danilo?\nA. He was late in school.\nB. He did not go to school.\nC. He came to school on time.\n\nWhat lessen does the story teach?\nA. To be clean.\nB. To wake up early.\nC. To have school things ready at night.',1,1,'answer'),
(1195,475,NULL,'learn',1,'A Tree','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Tree\nFather came home with a pretty pine tree. “Let us put the tree in this corner,” Mother said.\n\nWhen the tree was put in place, Lilia and Remy started to put decorations on it. Lilia placed a big silver star on top of the tree. Remy placed bells and little stars on its branches. Cards with pictures of angels, flowers, candles, and bells were also hung on its branches.\n\nAt the base of the tree were beautiful boxes. There were gifts for everyone in the family.\n\nWhat do you think was the tree used for?\nA. Tree house\nB. Family tree\nC. Christmas tree\n\nWhat month of the year was it?\nA. June\nB. November\nC. December\n\nWhich is the best ending for the story?\nA. The tree was not beautiful.\nB. The family did not like the gift.\nC. The tree made everyone happy.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Tree\nFather came home with a pretty pine tree. “Let us put the tree in this corner,” Mother said.\n\nWhen the tree was put in place, Lilia and Remy started to put decorations on it. Lilia placed a big silver star on top of the tree. Remy placed bells and little stars on its branches. Cards with pictures of angels, flowers, candles, and bells were also hung on its branches.\n\nAt the base of the tree were beautiful boxes. There were gifts for everyone in the family.\n\nWhat do you think was the tree used for?\nA. Tree house\nB. Family tree\nC. Christmas tree\n\nWhat month of the year was it?\nA. June\nB. November\nC. December\n\nWhich is the best ending for the story?\nA. The tree was not beautiful.\nB. The family did not like the gift.\nC. The tree made everyone happy.',NULL,10,36,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Tree\nFather came home with a pretty pine tree. “Let us put the tree in this corner,” Mother said.\n\nWhen the tree was put in place, Lilia and Remy started to put decorations on it. Lilia placed a big silver star on top of the tree. Remy placed bells and little stars on its branches. Cards with pictures of angels, flowers, candles, and bells were also hung on its branches.\n\nAt the base of the tree were beautiful boxes. There were gifts for everyone in the family.\n\nWhat do you think was the tree used for?\nA. Tree house\nB. Family tree\nC. Christmas tree\n\nWhat month of the year was it?\nA. June\nB. November\nC. December\n\nWhich is the best ending for the story?\nA. The tree was not beautiful.\nB. The family did not like the gift.\nC. The tree made everyone happy.',1,1,'answer'),
(1196,476,NULL,'learn',1,'Playing at Night','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPlaying at Night\nMany children were playing on the street. They were happy. It was night but they did not need any lamp. They could see each other very well.\n\nWhen the children got tired playing, they counted the stars. There were so many of them. An airplane passed by. It had beautiful lights. Later on, the children felt something fall.\n\n“Let us go home before we get wet,” Melinda said.\n\nWhat kind of a night was it?\nA. Dark night\nB. Bright night\nC. Cloudy night\n\nWhat do you think were falling?\nA. Stars\nB. Leaves\nC. Raindrops\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. The children went home.\nB. The children played in the rain.\nC. The children ran to their school.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPlaying at Night\nMany children were playing on the street. They were happy. It was night but they did not need any lamp. They could see each other very well.\n\nWhen the children got tired playing, they counted the stars. There were so many of them. An airplane passed by. It had beautiful lights. Later on, the children felt something fall.\n\n“Let us go home before we get wet,” Melinda said.\n\nWhat kind of a night was it?\nA. Dark night\nB. Bright night\nC. Cloudy night\n\nWhat do you think were falling?\nA. Stars\nB. Leaves\nC. Raindrops\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. The children went home.\nB. The children played in the rain.\nC. The children ran to their school.',NULL,10,37,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPlaying at Night\nMany children were playing on the street. They were happy. It was night but they did not need any lamp. They could see each other very well.\n\nWhen the children got tired playing, they counted the stars. There were so many of them. An airplane passed by. It had beautiful lights. Later on, the children felt something fall.\n\n“Let us go home before we get wet,” Melinda said.\n\nWhat kind of a night was it?\nA. Dark night\nB. Bright night\nC. Cloudy night\n\nWhat do you think were falling?\nA. Stars\nB. Leaves\nC. Raindrops\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. The children went home.\nB. The children played in the rain.\nC. The children ran to their school.',1,1,'answer'),
(1197,477,NULL,'learn',1,'Flowers','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nFlowers\nMarina brought flowers to school. She picked them their garden. She gave each of her classmates a flower.\n\n“How sweet these sampaguita flowers smell! Edna said.\n\n“Roses smell sweet and are pretty, too, “Tina said showing the rose Marina gave her.\n\nMarina’s classmates wanted to see Marina’s flower garden. They wanted to see the roses, dahlias, sampaguitas and gumamelas.\n\nWhy did Marina have a beautiful garden?\nA. She picks flowers every day.\nB. She takes good care of her plants.\nC. She waters her plants once a week.\n\nWhat will the children do one day?\nA. Visit Marina’s Garden.\nB. Buy flowers from Marina.\nC. Ask Marina for a picture of the garden.\n\nWhat did the children do?\nA. They helped Marina water the plants.\nB. They gave a party in school for Marina.\nC. They asked some flowers from Marina.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nFlowers\nMarina brought flowers to school. She picked them their garden. She gave each of her classmates a flower.\n\n“How sweet these sampaguita flowers smell! Edna said.\n\n“Roses smell sweet and are pretty, too, “Tina said showing the rose Marina gave her.\n\nMarina’s classmates wanted to see Marina’s flower garden. They wanted to see the roses, dahlias, sampaguitas and gumamelas.\n\nWhy did Marina have a beautiful garden?\nA. She picks flowers every day.\nB. She takes good care of her plants.\nC. She waters her plants once a week.\n\nWhat will the children do one day?\nA. Visit Marina’s Garden.\nB. Buy flowers from Marina.\nC. Ask Marina for a picture of the garden.\n\nWhat did the children do?\nA. They helped Marina water the plants.\nB. They gave a party in school for Marina.\nC. They asked some flowers from Marina.',NULL,10,38,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nFlowers\nMarina brought flowers to school. She picked them their garden. She gave each of her classmates a flower.\n\n“How sweet these sampaguita flowers smell! Edna said.\n\n“Roses smell sweet and are pretty, too, “Tina said showing the rose Marina gave her.\n\nMarina’s classmates wanted to see Marina’s flower garden. They wanted to see the roses, dahlias, sampaguitas and gumamelas.\n\nWhy did Marina have a beautiful garden?\nA. She picks flowers every day.\nB. She takes good care of her plants.\nC. She waters her plants once a week.\n\nWhat will the children do one day?\nA. Visit Marina’s Garden.\nB. Buy flowers from Marina.\nC. Ask Marina for a picture of the garden.\n\nWhat did the children do?\nA. They helped Marina water the plants.\nB. They gave a party in school for Marina.\nC. They asked some flowers from Marina.',1,1,'answer'),
(1198,478,NULL,'learn',1,'A Christmas Gift','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Christmas Gift\nIt was Christmas Day in school. All the children were happy except Nora. All her classmates had new dress. She wanted very much to have a new dress but her mother had no money to buy one for her. She no longer has a father.\n\nMiss Lozano said, “Before we begin our program, I am going to ask all those who have no mothers and Fathers to write what Christmas gifts they want. A rich man will give you the gift you will write down.”\n\nWhat do you think did Nora write down?\nA. A doll\nB. A book\nC. A dress\n\nHow did Nora feel after writing down the gift she wanted?\nA. Happy\nB. Sad\nC. Angry\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Nora got a doll.\nB. Nora got a book\nC. Nora got a dress',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Christmas Gift\nIt was Christmas Day in school. All the children were happy except Nora. All her classmates had new dress. She wanted very much to have a new dress but her mother had no money to buy one for her. She no longer has a father.\n\nMiss Lozano said, “Before we begin our program, I am going to ask all those who have no mothers and Fathers to write what Christmas gifts they want. A rich man will give you the gift you will write down.”\n\nWhat do you think did Nora write down?\nA. A doll\nB. A book\nC. A dress\n\nHow did Nora feel after writing down the gift she wanted?\nA. Happy\nB. Sad\nC. Angry\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Nora got a doll.\nB. Nora got a book\nC. Nora got a dress',NULL,10,39,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Christmas Gift\nIt was Christmas Day in school. All the children were happy except Nora. All her classmates had new dress. She wanted very much to have a new dress but her mother had no money to buy one for her. She no longer has a father.\n\nMiss Lozano said, “Before we begin our program, I am going to ask all those who have no mothers and Fathers to write what Christmas gifts they want. A rich man will give you the gift you will write down.”\n\nWhat do you think did Nora write down?\nA. A doll\nB. A book\nC. A dress\n\nHow did Nora feel after writing down the gift she wanted?\nA. Happy\nB. Sad\nC. Angry\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Nora got a doll.\nB. Nora got a book\nC. Nora got a dress',1,1,'answer'),
(1199,479,NULL,'learn',1,'Playing Soldiers','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPlaying Soldiers\nIt was Saturday. Jun, Gerry, Samy, Ismael and Dindo were playing happily under a mango tree. Samy had a drum. As he beat the drum, Jun, Gerry and Dindo marched.\n\nIsmael was the leader. He gave the orders.\n\n“Left, left, left, right, left,” Ismael called aloud. To stop them he said, “Halt! One, two.”\n\nWrite the day when they were playing.\n\nDraw what Samy had.\n\nWrite the names of the boys who marched.\n\nWrite the name of the leader.\n\nCopy what Ismael said when he ordered the boys to stop.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPlaying Soldiers\nIt was Saturday. Jun, Gerry, Samy, Ismael and Dindo were playing happily under a mango tree. Samy had a drum. As he beat the drum, Jun, Gerry and Dindo marched.\n\nIsmael was the leader. He gave the orders.\n\n“Left, left, left, right, left,” Ismael called aloud. To stop them he said, “Halt! One, two.”\n\nWrite the day when they were playing.\n\nDraw what Samy had.\n\nWrite the names of the boys who marched.\n\nWrite the name of the leader.\n\nCopy what Ismael said when he ordered the boys to stop.',NULL,10,40,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPlaying Soldiers\nIt was Saturday. Jun, Gerry, Samy, Ismael and Dindo were playing happily under a mango tree. Samy had a drum. As he beat the drum, Jun, Gerry and Dindo marched.\n\nIsmael was the leader. He gave the orders.\n\n“Left, left, left, right, left,” Ismael called aloud. To stop them he said, “Halt! One, two.”\n\nWrite the day when they were playing.\n\nDraw what Samy had.\n\nWrite the names of the boys who marched.\n\nWrite the name of the leader.\n\nCopy what Ismael said when he ordered the boys to stop.',1,1,'answer'),
(1200,480,NULL,'learn',1,'Paper Boats','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPaper Boats\nLito, Jose and Dario were playing in the rain. They were sailing paper boats. Lito’s boat was red and Jose’s was blue, Dario’s boat was green. They made their boats race. After thirty minutes the green boat was the first. The last was the blue boat. It was fun looking at the paper boats.\n\nCopy all the names of the boys in the story.\n\nDraw three boats and color them.\n\nWrite inside a box the number of minutes the boats ran.\n\nWhose boat was red? Copy and underline his name.\n\nWas Dario’s boat red? Answer with Yes or No.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPaper Boats\nLito, Jose and Dario were playing in the rain. They were sailing paper boats. Lito’s boat was red and Jose’s was blue, Dario’s boat was green. They made their boats race. After thirty minutes the green boat was the first. The last was the blue boat. It was fun looking at the paper boats.\n\nCopy all the names of the boys in the story.\n\nDraw three boats and color them.\n\nWrite inside a box the number of minutes the boats ran.\n\nWhose boat was red? Copy and underline his name.\n\nWas Dario’s boat red? Answer with Yes or No.',NULL,10,41,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nPaper Boats\nLito, Jose and Dario were playing in the rain. They were sailing paper boats. Lito’s boat was red and Jose’s was blue, Dario’s boat was green. They made their boats race. After thirty minutes the green boat was the first. The last was the blue boat. It was fun looking at the paper boats.\n\nCopy all the names of the boys in the story.\n\nDraw three boats and color them.\n\nWrite inside a box the number of minutes the boats ran.\n\nWhose boat was red? Copy and underline his name.\n\nWas Dario’s boat red? Answer with Yes or No.',1,1,'answer'),
(1201,481,NULL,'learn',1,'At the School Canteen','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAt the School Canteen\nMarita had twenty pesos. She went to the school canteen to buy something to eat. Below was a list of the food sold at the canteen.\n\nBananas ....................... P3. 00\nSoup ........................... P5.00\nCookies ....................... P2. 00\nGinataan ...................... P5. 00\nBoiled corn ................... P5. 00\n\nWhich of the foods below are not sold at the school canteen? Copy them on your paper.\nbananas\nice drop\negg soup\n\nList down the foods that are sold in cups.\n\nCopy the name of the cheapest food.\n\nCopy the name of the fruit.\n\nWhere did Marita see the foods? Write your answer and underline it.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAt the School Canteen\nMarita had twenty pesos. She went to the school canteen to buy something to eat. Below was a list of the food sold at the canteen.\n\nBananas ....................... P3. 00\nSoup ........................... P5.00\nCookies ....................... P2. 00\nGinataan ...................... P5. 00\nBoiled corn ................... P5. 00\n\nWhich of the foods below are not sold at the school canteen? Copy them on your paper.\nbananas\nice drop\negg soup\n\nList down the foods that are sold in cups.\n\nCopy the name of the cheapest food.\n\nCopy the name of the fruit.\n\nWhere did Marita see the foods? Write your answer and underline it.',NULL,10,42,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAt the School Canteen\nMarita had twenty pesos. She went to the school canteen to buy something to eat. Below was a list of the food sold at the canteen.\n\nBananas ....................... P3. 00\nSoup ........................... P5.00\nCookies ....................... P2. 00\nGinataan ...................... P5. 00\nBoiled corn ................... P5. 00\n\nWhich of the foods below are not sold at the school canteen? Copy them on your paper.\nbananas\nice drop\negg soup\n\nList down the foods that are sold in cups.\n\nCopy the name of the cheapest food.\n\nCopy the name of the fruit.\n\nWhere did Marita see the foods? Write your answer and underline it.',1,1,'answer'),
(1202,482,NULL,'learn',1,'Antonyms','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAntonyms\nPlaying with words is fun. Jose and Lito enjoy playing with words.\n\nOne day the game they played was. “Giving the Opposite of Words.”\n\nLito said, “Boy.”\n\nJose replied “Girl” Words that have opposite meaning are antonyms. You can play the game with your pencil and paper. Just do what the directions tell.\n\nWrite inside a circle the opposite of in.\n\nWrite inside a box the opposite of night.\n\nWrite and underline the opposite of small.\n\nWrite the word down then write its opposite after it.\n\nWrite the opposite of father in capital letters.',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAntonyms\nPlaying with words is fun. Jose and Lito enjoy playing with words.\n\nOne day the game they played was. “Giving the Opposite of Words.”\n\nLito said, “Boy.”\n\nJose replied “Girl” Words that have opposite meaning are antonyms. You can play the game with your pencil and paper. Just do what the directions tell.\n\nWrite inside a circle the opposite of in.\n\nWrite inside a box the opposite of night.\n\nWrite and underline the opposite of small.\n\nWrite the word down then write its opposite after it.\n\nWrite the opposite of father in capital letters.',NULL,10,43,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nAntonyms\nPlaying with words is fun. Jose and Lito enjoy playing with words.\n\nOne day the game they played was. “Giving the Opposite of Words.”\n\nLito said, “Boy.”\n\nJose replied “Girl” Words that have opposite meaning are antonyms. You can play the game with your pencil and paper. Just do what the directions tell.\n\nWrite inside a circle the opposite of in.\n\nWrite inside a box the opposite of night.\n\nWrite and underline the opposite of small.\n\nWrite the word down then write its opposite after it.\n\nWrite the opposite of father in capital letters.',1,1,'answer'),
(1203,483,NULL,'learn',1,'A Happy Family','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Happy Family\nNorma and Cielo are Mr. and Mrs. Villa’s children. They study at Gomez Elementary School. Norma is seven years old and Cielo is ten.\n\nEvery night, Mrs. Villa plays the piano. Norma and Cielo sing. Mr. Villa just listens. Sometimes Norma and Cielo dance as their mother plays the piano. They are a happy family.\n\nCopy the word that tells about the family.\n\nWrite the name of the children.\n\nDraw two triangles like these.\n\nWrite Norma’s age in the first triangle and Cielo’s age in the second.\n\nWrite two things that Norma and Cielo do as their mother plays the piano.\n\nCopy the name of the school in the story.','assets/images/level7/g1/c044-90-386.webp','[\"assets/images/level7/g1/c044-90-386.webp\"]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Happy Family\nNorma and Cielo are Mr. and Mrs. Villa’s children. They study at Gomez Elementary School. Norma is seven years old and Cielo is ten.\n\nEvery night, Mrs. Villa plays the piano. Norma and Cielo sing. Mr. Villa just listens. Sometimes Norma and Cielo dance as their mother plays the piano. They are a happy family.\n\nCopy the word that tells about the family.\n\nWrite the name of the children.\n\nDraw two triangles like these.\n\nWrite Norma’s age in the first triangle and Cielo’s age in the second.\n\nWrite two things that Norma and Cielo do as their mother plays the piano.\n\nCopy the name of the school in the story.',NULL,10,44,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nA Happy Family\nNorma and Cielo are Mr. and Mrs. Villa’s children. They study at Gomez Elementary School. Norma is seven years old and Cielo is ten.\n\nEvery night, Mrs. Villa plays the piano. Norma and Cielo sing. Mr. Villa just listens. Sometimes Norma and Cielo dance as their mother plays the piano. They are a happy family.\n\nCopy the