(1216,496,NULL,'learn',1,'Keeping Healthy','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nKeeping Healthy\nNestor was not a healthy boy. He was pale and thin. His parents were worried about him. One day, Mother took him to the doctor. The doctor examined him.\n\nHe said, “You are not sick, Nestor. But you are not strong and healthy. You will be strong and healthy if you follow the health rules. Do you know the health rules?”\n\n“Yes, Doctor,” said Nestor. “I learned them in school. But I do not follow them.”\n\n“It is easy to follow them,” said the doctor.\n\nAt home Mother said, “What will you do to become healthy? Let’s see if you know.”\n\nNestor said, “I will drink milk. I will sleep ten hours every night. I will eat fruits and vegetables. I will play under the sun. Then I will be healthy.”\n\nWhich describes Nestor?\na. a weak boy\nb. a strong boy\nc. a healthy boy\n\nWho were worried about him?\na. his sister\nb. his parents\nc. his friends\n\nWho took him to a doctor?\na. father\nb. mother\nc. teacher\n\nWho examined Nestor?\na. Mother\nb. the doctor\nc. the teacher\n\nWas Nestor sick?\na. yes\nb. no\nc. Not stated in the story\n\nWhere did Nestor learn the health rules?\na. at home\nb. in school\nc. in the clinic\n\nWho knew that Nestor did not follow the health rules?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. the doctor\n\nWhat will he drink?\na. milk\nb. coffee\nc. soft drink\n\nHow many hours will he sleep?\na. six\nb. eight\nc. ten\n\nWhere will he play?\na. in the house\nb. in the school\nc. under the sun',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nKeeping Healthy\nNestor was not a healthy boy. He was pale and thin. His parents were worried about him. One day, Mother took him to the doctor. The doctor examined him.\n\nHe said, “You are not sick, Nestor. But you are not strong and healthy. You will be strong and healthy if you follow the health rules. Do you know the health r