(1218,498,NULL,'learn',1,'The Lantern Show','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe Lantern Show\nChristmas was soon coming. The school was going to have a lantern show on Christmas Eve.\n\nOne day, Miss Villa brought to class a beautiful lantern. “This is a Christmas lantern,” said Miss Villa. “It is like a star. It is made of paper and bamboo. It can hold a candle. I made this lantern.”\n\n“Let us make lanterns like that for the lantern show,” said Pedro.\n\n“Let us make them of different colors,” Paz said.\n\n“My lantern will be red,” said Pedro.\n\n“Mine will be green,” said Paz.\n\n“Mine will be orange,” said Rene.\n\nEveryone wanted a different color. The children worked and worked. Then the lanterns were finished. How happy the children were to see their lanterns in the lantern show.\n\nWhat was the school going to have?\na. a lantern show\nb. a Christmas show\nc. a Christmas program\n\nWhat did Miss Villa bring to class?\na. a lantern\nb. a book\nc. a bag\n\nWhat does the lantern look like?\na. a star\nb. a moon\nc. a fruit\n\nWhat was the lantern made of?\na. wood and paper\nb. bamboo and cloth\nc. paper and bamboo\n\nWhat can the lantern hold?\na. a bulb\nb. a lamp\nc. a candle\n\nWho made the lantern?\na. a boy\nb. a girl\nc. Miss villa\n\nWhen will the lantern show be?\na. on Christmas day\nb. on Christmas Eve\nc. on the last day of school\n\nWho will make a red lantern?\na. Paz\nb. Pedro\nc. Rene\n\nWhose lantern will be green?\na. Paz’s\nb. Rene’s\nc. Pedro’s\n\nWhose lantern will be orange?\na. Paz’s\nb. Rene’s\nc. Pedro’s',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe Lantern Show\nChristmas was soon coming. The school was going to have a lantern show on Christmas Eve.\n\nOne day, Miss Villa brought to class a beautiful lantern. “This is a Christmas lantern,” said Miss Villa. “It is like a star. It is made of paper and bamboo. It can hold a candle. I made this lantern.”\n\n“Let us make lanterns like that for the lantern show,” said Pedro.\n\n“Let us make them of different colors,” Paz said.\n\n“My lantern will be red,” said Pedro.\n\n“Mine will be green,” said Paz.\n\n“Mine will be orange,” said Rene.\n\nEveryone wanted a different color. The children worked and worked. Then the lanterns were finished. How happy the children were to see their lanterns in the lantern show.\n\nWhat was the school going to have?\na. a lantern show\nb. a Christmas show\nc. a Christmas program\n\nWhat did Miss Villa bring to class?\na. a lantern\nb. a book\nc. a bag\n\nWhat does the lantern look like?\na. a star\nb. a moon\nc. a fruit\n\nWhat was the lantern made of?\na. wood and paper\nb. bamboo and cloth\nc. paper and bamboo\n\nWhat can the lantern hold?\na. a bulb\nb. a lamp\nc. a candle\n\nWho made the lantern?\na. a boy\nb. a girl\nc. Miss villa\n\nWhen will the lantern show be?\na. on Christmas day\nb. on Christmas Eve\nc. on the last day of school\n\nWho will make a red lantern?\na. Paz\nb. Pedro\nc. Rene\n\nWhose lantern will be green?\na. Paz’s\nb. Rene’s\nc. Pedro’s\n\nWhose lantern will be orange?\na. Paz’s\nb. Rene’s\nc. Pedro’s',NULL,10,13,'Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe Lantern Show\nChristmas was soon coming. The school was going to have a lantern show on Christmas Eve.\n\nOne day, Miss Villa brought to class a beautiful lantern. “This is a Christmas lantern,” said Miss Villa. “It is like a star. It is made of paper and bamboo. It can hold a candle. I made this lantern.”\n\n“Let us make lanterns like that for the lantern show,” said Pedro.\n\n“Let us make them of different colors,” Paz said.\n\n“My lantern will be red,” said Pedro.\n\n“Mine will be green,” said Paz.\n\n“Mine will be orange,” said Rene.\n\nEveryone wanted a different color. The children worked and worked. Then the lanterns were finished. How happy the children were to see their lanterns in the lantern show.\n\nWhat was the school going to have?\na. a lantern show\nb. a Christmas show\nc. a Christmas program\n\nWhat did Miss Villa bring to class?\na. a lantern\nb. a book\nc. a bag\n\nWhat does the lantern look like?\na. a star\nb. a moon\nc. a fruit\n\nWhat was the lantern made of?\na. wood and paper\nb. bamboo and cloth\nc. paper and bamboo\n\nWhat can the lantern hold?\na. a bulb\nb. a lamp\nc. a candle\n\nWho made the lantern?\na. a boy\nb. a girl\nc. Miss villa\n\nWhen will the lantern show be?\na. on Christmas day\nb. on Christmas Eve\nc. on the last day of school\n\nWho will make a red lantern?\na. Paz\nb. Pedro\nc. Rene\n\nWhose lantern will be green?\na. Paz’s\nb. Rene’s\nc. Pedro’s\n\nWhose lantern will be orange?\na. Paz’s\nb. Rene’s\nc. Pedro’s',1,1,'answer'),
(1219,499,NULL,'learn',1,'The Chinese Boy','open','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe Chinese Boy\nMother told Nilo to buy some bananas. So, Nilo went to the market. On his way he saw many children playing. Then he saw his friends, Celso and Ben. They were looking inside a room in Sana’s store. Sana was Chinese. He had a son named Sen Lu. “What are you looking at?” Nilo asked Celso and Ben. “We are watching Sen Lu,” answered Ben. “Why are you watching him?” asked Nilo. “He is eating rice. He is eating with chopsticks,” said Celso. “That is the way Chinese eat. It is clean to eat with chopsticks,” said Nilo. “Why do you say it’s clean?” asked Ben. “Chopsticks can be washed with boiling water. It is like eating with spoons,” said Nilo. Then Nilo went on to buy bananas.\n\nWhere did Nilo go?\na. to the river\nb. to the school\nc. to the market\n\nWhat was he going to buy?\na. rice\nb. fish\nc. bananas\n\nWho told him to buy bananas?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Sister\n\nWho were Nilo’s friends?\na. Ben and Pablo\nb. Pablo and Celso\nc. Ben and Celso\n\nWho was Sana?\na. an African\nb. a Chinese\nc. an American\n\nWho was Sen Lu?\na. Sana’s son\nb. Ben’s friend\nc. Sana’s brother\n\nWhat were Ben and Celso doing?\na. watching Sana\nb. watching Sen Lu\nc. looking at the things for sale\n\nWhat was Sen Lu doing?\na. eating rice\nb. eating cakes\nc. eating candies\n\nWhy is it clean to eat with the chopsticks?\na. They can be kept\nb. They can be thrown away\nc. They can be washed with boiling water\n\nWhat is eating with chopsticks like?\na. eating with forks\nb. eating with hands\nc. eating with spoons',NULL,'[]','Read the story carefully, then answer the questions.\n\nThe Chinese Boy\nMother told Nilo to buy some bananas. So, Nilo went to the market. On his way he saw many children playing. Then he saw his friends, Celso and Ben. They were looking inside a room in Sana’s store. Sana was Chines