(1278,558,NULL,'learn',1,'Find It!','open','Directions: Find and encircle each word related to news values in the puzzle. Words may be written horizontally, vertically or diagonally. They also may be written in reverse order, so you may have to read them from right to left.','Directions: Find and encircle each word related to news values in the puzzle. Words may be written horizontally, vertically or diagonally. They also may be written in reverse order, so you may have to read them from right to left.',NULL,'[]','Directions: Find and encircle each word related to news values in the puzzle. Words may be written horizontally, vertically or diagonally. They also may be written in reverse order, so you may have to read them from right to left.',NULL,10,23,'Directions: Find and encircle each word related to news values in the puzzle. Words may be written horizontally, vertically or diagonally. They also may be written in reverse order, so you may have to read them from right to left.',1,1,'answer'),
(1279,559,NULL,'learn',1,'Arranging the Story','open','Arrange the story in the correct sequence. Label each part: Headline, Byline, Lead, Body, Conclusion.','Arrange the story in the correct sequence. Label each part: Headline, Byline, Lead, Body, Conclusion.\n\nResidents of Barangay Maligaya gathered early Sunday morning for a clean-up drive after heavy rains caused flooding and scattered debris across several streets.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nBy Jericho Dela Cruz, Campus Journalist\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nThe barangay plans to hold monthly clean-ups and educational talks on prop er waste disposal in local schools.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nVolunteers, including students and parents, helped clear garbage from sidewalks and drains. Barangay officials said this is part of a larger campaign to prevent future floods. “We need to keep our surroundings clean to protect our health and homes,” said Barangay Captain Liza Ramos.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nBarangay Holds Clean-Up Drive After Flood\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion',NULL,'[]','Arrange the story in the correct sequence. Label each part: Headline, Byline, Lead, Body, Conclusion.\n\nResidents of Barangay Maligaya gathered early Sunday morning for a clean-up drive after heavy rains caused flooding and scattered debris across several streets.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nBy Jericho Dela Cruz, Campus Journalist\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nThe barangay plans to hold monthly clean-ups and educational talks on prop er waste disposal in local schools.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nVolunteers, including students and parents, helped clear garbage from sidewalks and drains. Barangay officials said this is part of a larger campaign to prevent future floods. “We need to keep our surroundings clean to protect our health and homes,” said Barangay Captain Liza Ramos.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nBarangay Holds Clean-Up Drive After Flood\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion',NULL,10,24,'Arrange the story in the correct sequence. Label each part: Headline, Byline, Lead, Body, Conclusion.\n\nResidents of Barangay Maligaya gathered early Sunday morning for a clean-up drive after heavy rains caused flooding and scattered debris across several streets.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nBy Jericho Dela Cruz, Campus Journalist\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nThe barangay plans to hold monthly clean-ups and educational talks on prop er waste disposal in local schools.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nVolunteers, including students and parents, helped clear garbage from sidewalks and drains. Barangay officials said this is part of a larger campaign to prevent future floods. “We need to keep our surroundings clean to protect our health and homes,” said Barangay Captain Liza Ramos.\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion\n\nBarangay Holds Clean-Up Drive After Flood\nHeadline\nByline\nLead\nBody\nConclusion',1,1,'answer'),
(1280,560,NULL,'learn',1,'Sports Writing','open','DIRECTIONS : Write a sports coverage using the following facts.','DIRECTIONS : Write a sports coverage using the following facts.\n\nThe Facts\nWhat: Municipal Meet volleyball eliminations\nWhere: Arayata Sports Complex, Tanza, Cavite\nWhen : September 9 at 2 p.m.\nBetween : Saint John School (SJS) and Saint Mark Academy (SMA)\nScores: 25-19, 23-25, 25-20, 25-20\n\nSignificance of the game:\nSJS on 2-0 lead; routed Saint Joseph Institute (SJI) in previous outing\n\nHeroes of the game:\nJerome Arbis and Noli Cruz combined for 17 points in last set\n\nQuotes from SJS coach Rody Santos:\n“My boys are pumped up from their victory over the Saint Joseph Institute Tossers.”\n“This is a good start as we are gunning for the championship like our basketball varsity posting a 6-0 winning streak.”\n\nWeather condition:\nHeavy rains and thunderstorms brought by Typhoon Maring but the Arayata gym was filled to the rafter.\n\nSpectators’ attitude:\nSJS crowd favorite, predominately SJS crowd chanting cheers; SJS red and white clad mascot dancing in front of SJS contingent\n\nReported injury:\nSMA’s Jin Rivas sprained ankle after a bad fall in the second set; carried out of playing court and brought to Family General Hospital\n\nHighlights of the game:\nSMA came on strong in second set with Joseph Rom’s mounting strong wallops\nRom’s heroics aided by Dan Sibal’s stopping ball on a service by SJS Richard Montes, also in second set.\n\nWrite your sports coverage using the facts.',NULL,'[]','DIRECTIONS : Write a sports coverage using the following facts.\n\nThe Facts\nWhat: Municipal Meet volleyball eliminations\nWhere: Arayata Sports Complex, Tanza, Cavite\nWhen : September 9 at 2 p.m.\nBetween : Saint John School (SJS) and Saint Mark Academy (SMA)\nScores: 25-19, 23-25, 25-20, 25-20\n\nSignificance of the game:\nSJS on 2-0 lead; routed Saint Joseph Institute (SJI) in previous outing\n\nHeroes of the game:\nJerome Arbis and Noli Cruz combined for 17 points in last set\n\nQuotes from SJS coach Rody Santos:\n“My boys are pumped up from their victory over the Saint Joseph Institute Tossers.”\n“This is a good start as we are gunning for the championship like our basketball varsity posting a 6-0 winning streak.”\n\nWeather condition:\nHeavy rains and thunderstorms brought by Typhoon Maring but the Arayata gym was filled to the rafter.\n\nSpectators’ attitude:\nSJS crowd favorite, predominately SJS crowd chanting cheers; SJS red and white clad mascot dancing in front of SJS contingent\n\nReported injury:\nSMA’s Jin Rivas sprained ankle after a bad fall in the second set; carried out of playing court and brought to Family General Hospital\n\nHighlights of the game:\nSMA came on strong in second set with Joseph Rom’s mounting strong wallops\nRom’s heroics aided by Dan Sibal’s stopping ball on a service by SJS Richard Montes, also in second set.\n\nWrite your sports coverage using the facts.',NULL,10,25,'DIRECTIONS : Write a sports coverage using the following facts.\n\nThe Facts\nWhat: Municipal Meet volleyball eliminations\nWhere: Arayata Sports Complex, Tanza, Cavite\nWhen : September 9 at 2 p.m.\nBetween : Saint John School (SJS) and Saint Mark Academy (SMA)\nScores: 25-19, 23-25, 25-20, 25-20\n\nSignificance of the game:\nSJS on 2-0 lead; routed Saint Joseph Institute (SJI) in previous outing\n\nHeroes of the game:\nJerome Arbis and Noli Cruz combined for 17 points in last set\n\nQuotes from SJS coach Rody Santos:\n“My boys are pumped up from their victory over the Saint Joseph Institute Tossers.”\n“This is a good start as we are gunning for the championship like our basketball varsity posting a 6-0 winning streak.”\n\nWeather condition:\nHeavy rains and thunderstorms brought by Typhoon Maring but the Arayata gym was filled to the rafter.\n\nSpectators’ attitude:\nSJS crowd favorite, predominately SJS crowd chanting cheers; SJS red and white clad mascot dancing in front of SJS contingent\n\nReported injury:\nSMA’s Jin Rivas sprained ankle after a bad fall in the second set; carried out of playing court and brought to Family General Hospital\n\nHighlights of the game:\nSMA came on strong in second set with Joseph Rom’s mounting strong wallops\nRom’s heroics aided by Dan Sibal’s stopping ball on a service by SJS Richard Montes, also in second set.\n\nWrite your sports coverage using the facts.',1,1,'answer'),
(1281,561,NULL,'learn',1,'Sports Writing','open','Based on the information presented below, write a sports game story of at least 350 words. Statements as presented on this fact sheet may be treated as direct quotations or paraphrases. You are writing for the Sept. 17 issue of the Hays High Guidon.','Based on the information presented below, write a sports game story of at least 350 words. Statements as presented on this fact sheet may be treated as direct quotations or paraphrases. You are writing for the Sept. 17 issue of the Hays High Guidon.\n\nBackground\nThe Varsity Girls’ Volleyball team began season- Sept. 15- v. Salina South. Hays lost 15-7, 13- 15, 11-15.\nThe next game: Sept. 19, at Junction City.\n\nThe Team\nThe team includes six returners,\nThree returners made all-district last year\nTwo returners advanced to the all-region roster, Amie Roberts and Leah Claycamp, both juniors.\nRhonda Ames, a senior, is predicted to be one of the district’s star players.\n\nSignificant Plays\nFirst game\nAmie Roberts scored the first point of the game, an off-speed spike, after only 10 seconds of play. She scored five points in the first game.\nKenda Von Feldt scored six points. Leah Claycamp scored four points\nThe Salina South team scored seven points.\nSecond game\nRoberts scored six points and blocked 10 spikes.\nClaycamp scored five points. Her most significant play was a dive that set up a point. She also made two fouls.\nVon Feldt scored two points-one after she made a dig to another player who returned it to her for the score.\nHays hit the ball out of bounds four times. The officials called three thrown ball penalties on Hays.\nSalina South won this game.\nThird game\nRhonda Ames scored the first five points of this game. She was injured while making a double block and did not play the rest of the game.\nClaycamp scored four points, one after a spin serve that Salina could not even return.\nVon Feldt scored two points.\nThe score was tied almost the entire way through the game. The winning four points all came within one minute of play when the Hays team looked exhausted.\n\nQuotations\nLarry Schmidt, varsity coach\nThe first game of the season didn’t go as well as I hoped. We didn’t accomplish the team goals that we set. We didn’t serve and pass as well as I hoped to.\nWe need to work on our movement and getting into the right position when it comes to playing defense.\nJessica Bird, sophomore\nI think we were playing very well. We need to work on our fundamentals. Overall, I think that we are playing great and the season should be successful.\nRhonda Ames, senior\nI think if we work hard and use our potential, we’ll do all right in state. Salina just beat us by playing good clean volleyball.\nLori Billinger, senior\nI need to work on my passing, but otherwise, everything is going great for me so far this year. I think that out team should talk more to each other when we are on the courts.\n\nWrite your sports game story (at least 350 words).',NULL,'[]','Based on the information presented below, write a sports game story of at least 350 words. Statements as presented on this fact sheet may be treated as direct quotations or paraphrases. You are writing for the Sept. 17 issue of the Hays High Guidon.\n\nBackground\nThe Varsity Girls’ Volleyball team began season- Sept. 15- v. Salina South. Hays lost 15-7, 13- 15, 11-15.\nThe next game: Sept. 19, at Junction City.\n\nThe Team\nThe team includes six returners,\nThree returners made all-district last year\nTwo returners advanced to the all-region roster, Amie Roberts and Leah Claycamp, both juniors.\nRhonda Ames, a senior, is predicted to be one of the district’s star players.\n\nSignificant Plays\nFirst game\nAmie Roberts scored the first point of the game, an off-speed spike, after only 10 seconds of play. She scored five points in the first game.\nKenda Von Feldt scored six points. Leah Claycamp scored four points\nThe Salina South team scored seven points.\nSecond game\nRoberts scored six points and blocked 10 spikes.\nClaycamp scored five points. Her most significant play was a dive that set up a point. She also made two fouls.\nVon Feldt scored two points-one after she made a dig to another player who returned it to her for the score.\nHays hit the ball out of bounds four times. The officials called three thrown ball penalties on Hays.\nSalina South won this game.\nThird game\nRhonda Ames scored the first five points of this game. She was injured while making a double block and did not play the rest of the game.\nClaycamp scored four points, one after a spin serve that Salina could not even return.\nVon Feldt scored two points.\nThe score was tied almost the entire way through the game. The winning four points all came within one minute of play when the Hays team looked exhausted.\n\nQuotations\nLarry Schmidt, varsity coach\nThe first game of the season didn’t go as well as I hoped. We didn’t accomplish the team goals that we set. We didn’t serve and pass as well as I hoped to.\nWe need to work on our movement and getting into the right position when it comes to playing defense.\nJessica Bird, sophomore\nI think we were playing very well. We need to work on our fundamentals. Overall, I think that we are playing great and the season should be successful.\nRhonda Ames, senior\nI think if we work hard and use our potential, we’ll do all right in state. Salina just beat us by playing good clean volleyball.\nLori Billinger, senior\nI need to work on my passing, but otherwise, everything is going great for me so far this year. I think that out team should talk more to each other when we are on the courts.\n\nWrite your sports game story (at least 350 words).',NULL,10,26,'Based on the information presented below, write a sports game story of at least 350 words. Statements as presented on this fact sheet may be treated as direct quotations or paraphrases. You are writing for the Sept. 17 issue of the Hays High Guidon.\n\nBackground\nThe Varsity Girls’ Volleyball team began season- Sept. 15- v. Salina South. Hays lost 15-7, 13- 15, 11-15.\nThe next game: Sept. 19, at Junction City.\n\nThe Team\nThe team includes six returners,\nThree returners made all-district last year\nTwo returners advanced to the all-region roster, Amie Roberts and Leah Claycamp, both juniors.\nRhonda Ames, a senior, is predicted to be one of the district’s star players.\n\nSignificant Plays\nFirst game\nAmie Roberts scored the first point of the game, an off-speed spike, after only 10 seconds of play. She scored five points in the first game.\nKenda Von Feldt scored six points. Leah Claycamp scored four points\nThe Salina South team scored seven points.\nSecond game\nRoberts scored six points and blocked 10 spikes.\nClaycamp scored five points. Her most significant play was a dive that set up a point. She also made two fouls.\nVon Feldt scored two points-one after she made a dig to another player who returned it to her for the score.\nHays hit the ball out of bounds four times. The officials called three thrown ball penalties on Hays.\nSalina South won this game.\nThird game\nRhonda Ames scored the first five points of this game. She was injured while making a double block and did not play the re',1,1,'answer'),
(1282,562,NULL,'learn',1,'Mystery Matching Type','open','Direction: Match the items on Column B to the items in Column A to answer the mystery question. Write your answers on the space provided for.','Direction: Match the items on Column B to the items in Column A to answer the mystery question. Write your answers on the space provided for.\n\nColumn A\n1. Be precise, choose every word carefully.\n2. A journalist must safeguard his sources.\n3. We speak more slowly on air than in real life, but we need to describe, to tell stories, to create pictures.\n4. Stick to the facts.\n5. The anchor and the editor need to know how you are doing so as to properly work on the broadcast.\n6. Use simple language so the audience can get the focus.\n7. Everybody is owed privacy and respect.\n8. Try to show all sides of the argument.\nA. On-air Delivery – the right tone\nR. Respecting Others\nD. Accuracy\nS. Balance\nW. Clarity\nH. No Commenting\nL. Protect Your Sources\nP. Keep in Touch with Newsroom\n\nMystery Question:\nWho is the American newspaper publisher, known for introducing sensationalism, who cabled this to Frederic Remington in 1898?\n\nWrite the answer to the mystery question.','assets/images/level7/g4/c028-70-557.webp','[\"assets/images/level7/g4/c028-70-557.webp\"]','Direction: Match the items on Column B to the items in Column A to answer the mystery question. Write your answers on the space provided for.\n\nColumn A\n1. Be precise, choose every word carefully.\n2. A journalist must safeguard his sources.\n3. We speak more slowly on air than in real life, but we need to describe, to tell stories, to create pictures.\n4. Stick to the facts.\n5. The anchor and the editor need to know how you are doing so as to properly work on the broadcast.\n6. Use simple language so the audience can get the focus.\n7. Everybody is owed privacy and respect.\n8. Try to show all sides of the argument.\nA. On-air Delivery – the right tone\nR. Respecting Others\nD. Accuracy\nS. Balance\nW. Clarity\nH. No Commenting\nL. Protect Your Sources\nP. Keep in Touch with Newsroom\n\nMystery Question:\nWho is the American newspaper publisher, known for introducing sensationalism, who cabled this to Frederic Remington in 1898?\n\nWrite the answer to the mystery question.',NULL,10,28,'Direction: Match the items on Column B to the items in Column A to answer the mystery question. Write your answers on the space provided for.\n\nColumn A\n1. Be precise, choose every word carefully.\n2. A journalist must safeguard his sources.\n3. We speak more slowly on air than in real life, but we need to describe, to tell stories, to create pictures.\n4. Stick to the facts.\n5. The anchor and the editor need to know how you are doing so as to properly work on the broadcast.\n6. Use simple language so the audience can get the focus.\n7. Everybody is owed privacy and respect.\n8. Try to show all sides of the argument.\nA. On-air Delivery – the right tone\nR. Respecting Others\nD. Accuracy\nS. Balance\nW. Clarity\nH. No Commenting\nL. Protect Your Sources\nP. Keep in Touch with Newsroom\n\nMystery Question:\nWho is the American newspaper publisher, known for introducing sensationalism, who cabled this to Frederic Remington in 1898?\n\nWrite the answer to the mystery question.',1,1,'answer'),
(1283,563,NULL,'learn',1,'Editorial Cartooning','open','Given the editorial cartoon below. Discuss the different characters and how does it symbolize.','Given the editorial cartoon below. Discuss the different characters and how does it symbolize.\n\nDiscuss the different characters and how does it symbolize.','assets/images/level7/g4/p029-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level7/g4/p029-1.webp\"]','Given the editorial cartoon below. Discuss the different characters and how does it symbolize.\n\nDiscuss the different characters and how does it symbolize.',NULL,10,29,'Given the editorial cartoon below. Discuss the different characters and how does it symbolize.\n\nDiscuss the different characters and how does it symbolize.',1,1,'answer'),
(1284,564,NULL,'learn',1,'Writing a News Article','open','Write a news article · Choose an interesting school club and write an article describing its activities, members, goals and achievements.','Write a news article · Choose an interesting school club and write an article describing its activities, members, goals and achievements.\n\nBackground Information for Learners\nNews is an account of an event, a fact or an opinion that interests people. It is a presentation of current events.\n\nThe Inverted Pyramid Style\nLead: The “key” to the story. One to no more than two sentences. Includes the most important of the five Ws and H.\nSecondary information: Vital statistics and description. Extend on five Ws and H.\nBackground information: Incidents leading up to or following the event.\nAdditional information\n\nInverted Pyramid Format\nWhen you write a story in inverted pyramid format, you put the most newsworthy information at the beginning and the least newsworthy information at the end. The inverted pyramid helps readers scan news stories quickly and efficiently, and it also helps you write them with ease. Once you train yourself to organize facts this way, you can apply the formula to almost any breaking news event—this is why the inverted pyramid has been a cornerstone of news writing for the past century.\n\nWho\n\nWhat\n\nWhen\n\nWhere\n\nWhy\n\nHow\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nWrite your newspaper article with a headline.','assets/images/level7/g5/p005-1.webp','[\"assets/images/level7/g5/p005-1.webp\"]','Write a news article · Choose an interesting school club and write an article describing its activities, members, goals and achievements.\n\nBackground Information for Learners\nNews is an account of an event, a fact or an opinion that interests people. It is a presentation of current events.\n\nThe Inverted Pyramid Style\nLead: The “key” to the story. One to no more than two sentences. Includes the most important of the five Ws and H.\nSecondary information: Vital statistics and description. Extend on five Ws and H.\nBackground information: Incidents leading up to or following the event.\nAdditional information\n\nInverted Pyramid Format\nWhen you write a story in inverted pyramid format, you put the most newsworthy information at the beginning and the least newsworthy information at the end. The inverted pyramid helps readers scan news stories quickly and efficiently, and it also helps you write them with ease. Once you train yourself to organize facts this way, you can apply the formula to almost any breaking news event—this is why the inverted pyramid has been a cornerstone of news writing for the past century.\n\nWho\n\nWhat\n\nWhen\n\nWhere\n\nWhy\n\nHow\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nWrite your newspaper article with a headline.',NULL,10,5,'Write a news article · Choose an interesting school club and write an article describing its activities, members, goals and achievements.\n\nBackground Information for Learners\nNews is an account of an event, a fact or an opinion that interests people. It is a presentation of current events.\n\nThe Inverted Pyramid Style\nLead: The “key” to the story. One to no more than two sentences. Includes the most important of the five Ws and H.\nSecondary information: Vital statistics and description. Extend on five Ws and H.\nBackground information: Incidents leading up to or following the event.\nAdditional information\n\nInverted Pyramid Format\nWhen you write a story in inverted pyramid format, you put the most newsworthy information at the beginning and the least newsworthy information at the end. The inverted pyramid helps readers scan news stories quickly and efficiently, and it also helps you write them with ease. Once you train yourself to organize facts this way, you can apply the formula to almost any breaking news event—this is why the inverted pyramid has been a cornerstone of news writing for the past century.\n\nWho\n\nWhat\n\nWhen\n\nWhere\n\nWhy\n\nHow\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nQuestion: · Interviewee: · Response:\n\nWrite your newspaper article with a headline.',1,1,'answer'),
(1285,565,NULL,'learn',1,'Journalistic Writing','open','Directions: Read the following examples of journalistic writing, then identify whether each one is News, Opinion, Feature or Sports news.','Directions: Read the following examples of journalistic writing, then identify whether each one is News, Opinion, Feature or Sports news.\n\nEating chocolates not only satisfies your taste buds, it also improves your brain function. The flavonoids found in chocolate have been proven to increase blood flow to the brain. They can help boost memory and attention span, and it also inhance problem-solving skills.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nA retired police colonel died after being trapped inside one of the structures that collapsed in his family’s resort, as the town of Cataingan in Masbate bore the brunt of a 6.6 magnitude earthquake that suck the province on Tuesday morning. By: Nino Luces\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nManny Pacquiao scored a unanimous decision over the no. 1 pound-for-pound fighter, Floyd Mayweather Jr., in an epic boxing rematch on Sunday in Philippine Arena.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nIndeed, frontliners must be regarded as modern-day heroes. From battling the dreaded COVID-19 in the hospitals to ensuring safety in public spaces, our brave frontliners deserve commendation and respect from the people.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nThe Magician, Efren “Bata” Reyes, has once again proven his magic on the pool table. Reyes captured the gold medal in the men’s 9-ball singles event at the 2020 Manila Billiard Tournament.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news',NULL,'[]','Directions: Read the following examples of journalistic writing, then identify whether each one is News, Opinion, Feature or Sports news.\n\nEating chocolates not only satisfies your taste buds, it also improves your brain function. The flavonoids found in chocolate have been proven to increase blood flow to the brain. They can help boost memory and attention span, and it also inhance problem-solving skills.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nA retired police colonel died after being trapped inside one of the structures that collapsed in his family’s resort, as the town of Cataingan in Masbate bore the brunt of a 6.6 magnitude earthquake that suck the province on Tuesday morning. By: Nino Luces\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nManny Pacquiao scored a unanimous decision over the no. 1 pound-for-pound fighter, Floyd Mayweather Jr., in an epic boxing rematch on Sunday in Philippine Arena.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nIndeed, frontliners must be regarded as modern-day heroes. From battling the dreaded COVID-19 in the hospitals to ensuring safety in public spaces, our brave frontliners deserve commendation and respect from the people.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nThe Magician, Efren “Bata” Reyes, has once again proven his magic on the pool table. Reyes captured the gold medal in the men’s 9-ball singles event at the 2020 Manila Billiard Tournament.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news',NULL,10,10,'Directions: Read the following examples of journalistic writing, then identify whether each one is News, Opinion, Feature or Sports news.\n\nEating chocolates not only satisfies your taste buds, it also improves your brain function. The flavonoids found in chocolate have been proven to increase blood flow to the brain. They can help boost memory and attention span, and it also inhance problem-solving skills.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nA retired police colonel died after being trapped inside one of the structures that collapsed in his family’s resort, as the town of Cataingan in Masbate bore the brunt of a 6.6 magnitude earthquake that suck the province on Tuesday morning. By: Nino Luces\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nManny Pacquiao scored a unanimous decision over the no. 1 pound-for-pound fighter, Floyd Mayweather Jr., in an epic boxing rematch on Sunday in Philippine Arena.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nIndeed, frontliners must be regarded as modern-day heroes. From battling the dreaded COVID-19 in the hospitals to ensuring safety in public spaces, our brave frontliners deserve commendation and respect from the people.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news\n\nThe Magician, Efren “Bata” Reyes, has once again proven his magic on the pool table. Reyes captured the gold medal in the men’s 9-ball singles event at the 2020 Manila Billiard Tournament.\nNews\nOpinion\nFeature\nSports news',1,1,'answer'),
(1286,566,NULL,'learn',1,'Matching Type','open','Direction: Match the types of journalistic writing in Column A with their corresponding contents in Column B.','Direction: Match the types of journalistic writing in Column A with their corresponding contents in Column B.\n\nColumn A\n1. News\n2. Feature\n3. Sports News\n4. Opinion\nA. sporting topics or competition\nB. editorial\nC. current or recent events\nD. in-depth about a certain topic',NULL,'[]','Direction: Match the types of journalistic writing in Column A with their corresponding contents in Column B.\n\nColumn A\n1. News\n2. Feature\n3. Sports News\n4. Opinion\nA. sporting topics or competition\nB. editorial\nC. current or recent events\nD. in-depth about a certain topic',NULL,10,11,'Direction: Match the types of journalistic writing in Column A with their corresponding contents in Column B.\n\nColumn A\n1. News\n2. Feature\n3. Sports News\n4. Opinion\nA. sporting topics or competition\nB. editorial\nC. current or recent events\nD. in-depth about a certain topic',1,1,'answer'),
(1287,567,NULL,'learn',1,'Writing Activity','open','Directions: Find any of the following: News, Features, Opinion and Sports News. Copy the first paragraph in your notebook, then identify its type.','Directions: Find any of the following: News, Features, Opinion and Sports News. Copy the first paragraph in your notebook, then identify its type.\n\nCopy the first paragraph, then identify its type (News, Feature, Opinion or Sports News).',NULL,'[]','Directions: Find any of the following: News, Features, Opinion and Sports News. Copy the first paragraph in your notebook, then identify its type.\n\nCopy the first paragraph, then identify its type (News, Feature, Opinion or Sports News).',NULL,10,12,'Directions: Find any of the following: News, Features, Opinion and Sports News. Copy the first paragraph in your notebook, then identify its type.\n\nCopy the first paragraph, then identify its type (News, Feature, Opinion or Sports News).',1,1,'answer'),
(1288,568,NULL,'learn',1,'Mix Exercises','open','I. Identifying the 5 Ws · Instruction/s: Read the scrambled information, identify the WHO, WHAT, WHY, WHEN, WHERE. Write your answers on the space provided. A sample is given for your guidance.','I. Identifying the 5 Ws · Instruction/s: Read the scrambled information, identify the WHO, WHAT, WHY, WHEN, WHERE. Write your answers on the space provided. A sample is given for your guidance.\n\nExercise No. 1 Scrambled Information\nin preparation for the barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) elections next year.\nwill resume in the voter’s registration at the City Hall\nCommission of Election on Monday\n\nExercise No. 1 · WHO: · WHAT: · WHEN: · WHY: · WHERE:\n\nExercise No. 2\nyesterday.\nThree people riding on a motorcycle\nalong Maharlika Highway, Barangay San Nicolas\nafter their vehicle collided head-on with a passenger bus were killed\n\nExercise No. 2 · WHO: · WHAT: · WHEN: · WHY: · WHERE:',NULL,'[]','I. Identifying the 5 Ws · Instruction/s: Read the scrambled information, identify the WHO, WHAT, WHY, WHEN, WHERE. Write your answers on the space provided. A sample is given for your guidance.\n\nExercise No. 1 Scrambled Information\nin preparation for the barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) elections next year.\nwill resume in the voter’s registration at the City Hall\nCommission of Election on Monday\n\nExercise No. 1 · WHO: · WHAT: · WHEN: · WHY: · WHERE:\n\nExercise No. 2\nyesterday.\nThree people riding on a motorcycle\nalong Maharlika Highway, Barangay San Nicolas\nafter their vehicle collided head-on with a passenger bus were killed\n\nExercise No. 2 · WHO: · WHAT: · WHEN: · WHY: · WHERE:',NULL,10,12,'I. Identifying the 5 Ws · Instruction/s: Read the scrambled information, identify the WHO, WHAT, WHY, WHEN, WHERE. Write your answers on the space provided. A sample is given for your guidance.\n\nExercise No. 1 Scrambled Information\nin preparation for the barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan (SK) elections next 