(1322,602,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: The Voice Within','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: The Voice Within\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 146\n\nThere is a quiet voice inside,\nA faithful friend, a trusted guide.\nIt tells us when to stand up tall,\nTo help someone who starts to fall.\nIt whispers, \"Choose the path that\'s right,\nEven when it\'s out of sight.\"\nIt gives us courage, calm, and grace\nTo meet each challenge that we face.\nSometimes storms may cloud the day,\nAnd doubts may try to block the way.\nYet deep within, that gentle light\nStill shines to guide us through the night.\nA dream begins with one small step,\nWith every promise wisely kept.\nSuccess is built on what we do,\nOn honest hearts that stay sincere and true.\nListen well when choices call.\nYour inner voice can conquer all.\nWith hope and faith beside your way,\nYou\'ll grow much stronger every day.\nBelieve your voice.\nBelieve your dream.\nBecome much more\nThan you may seem.',NULL,'[]','The Voice Within. There is a quiet voice inside, A faithful friend, a trusted guide. It tells us when to stand up tall, To help someone who starts to fall. It whispers, \"Choose the path that\'s right, Even when it\'s out of sight.\" It gives us courage, calm, and grace To meet each challenge that we face. Sometimes storms may cloud the day, And doubts may try to block the way. Yet deep within, that gentle light Still shines to guide us through the night. A dream begins with one small step, With every promise wisely kept. Success is built on what we do, On honest hearts that stay sincere and true. Listen well when choices call. Your inner voice can conquer all. With hope and faith beside your way, You\'ll grow much stronger every day. Believe your voice. Believe your dream. Become much more Than you may seem.','There is a quiet voice inside, A faithful friend, a trusted guide. It tells us when to stand up tall, To help someone who starts to fall. It whispers, \"Choose the path that\'s right, Even when it\'s out of sight.\" It gives us courage, calm, and grace To meet each challenge that we face. Sometimes storms may cloud the day, And doubts may try to block the way. Yet deep within, that gentle light Still shines to guide us through the night. A dream begins with one small step, With every promise wisely kept. Success is built on what we do, On honest hearts that stay sincere and true. Listen well when choices call. Your inner voice can conquer all. With hope and faith beside your way, You\'ll grow much stronger every day. Believe your voice. Believe your dream. Become much more Than you may seem.',20,9,'9 \n \nPART I \nFLUENCY POEMS \n \nActivity 1 \nThe Voice Within \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nThere is a quiet voice inside, \nA faithful friend, a trusted guide. \nIt tells us when to stand up tall, \nTo help someone who starts to fall. \nIt whispers, \"Choose the path that\'s right, \nEven when it\'s out of sight.\" \nIt gives us courage, calm, and grace \nTo meet each challenge that we face. \nSometimes storms may cloud the day, \nAnd doubts may try to block the way. \nYet deep within, that gentle light \nStill shines to guide us through the night. \nA dream begins with one small step, \nWith every promise wisely kept. \nSuccess is built on what we do, \nOn honest hearts that stay sincere and true. \nListen well when choices call. \nYour inner voice can conquer all. \nWith hope and faith beside your way, \nYou\'ll grow much stronger every day. \nBelieve your voice. \nBelieve your dream. \nBecome much more \nThan you may seem.',1,1,'answer'),
(1323,603,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: Tomorrow Begins Today','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: Tomorrow Begins Today\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 103\n\nTomorrow waits beyond the hill,\nPrepared for those with strength and will.\nIt does not ask how rich you are,\nNor where you live, nor near nor far.\nIt simply asks,\n\"Will you prepare?\nWill you keep learning everywhere?\"\nA page today,\nA book tonight,\nCan help your future shine more bright.\nMistakes may come,\nAnd plans may bend,\nYet every challenge has an end.\nEach sunrise brings another chance\nTo learn,\nTo lead,\nTo dream,\nTo dance.\nSo build your future,\nBrick by brick,\nWith patient hands that never quit.\nTomorrow starts\nWith what you do—\nAnd all tomorrow\nStarts with you.',NULL,'[]','Tomorrow Begins Today. Tomorrow waits beyond the hill, Prepared for those with strength and will. It does not ask how rich you are, Nor where you live, nor near nor far. It simply asks, \"Will you prepare? Will you keep learning everywhere?\" A page today, A book tonight, Can help your future shine more bright. Mistakes may come, And plans may bend, Yet every challenge has an end. Each sunrise brings another chance To learn, To lead, To dream, To dance. So build your future, Brick by brick, With patient hands that never quit. Tomorrow starts With what you do— And all tomorrow Starts with you.','Tomorrow waits beyond the hill, Prepared for those with strength and will. It does not ask how rich you are, Nor where you live, nor near nor far. It simply asks, \"Will you prepare? Will you keep learning everywhere?\" A page today, A book tonight, Can help your future shine more bright. Mistakes may come, And plans may bend, Yet every challenge has an end. Each sunrise brings another chance To learn, To lead, To dream, To dance. So build your future, Brick by brick, With patient hands that never quit. Tomorrow starts With what you do— And all tomorrow Starts with you.',20,11,'11 \n \n \nActivity 2 \nTomorrow Begins Today \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nTomorrow waits beyond the hill, \nPrepared for those with strength and will. \nIt does not ask how rich you are, \nNor where you live, nor near nor far. \nIt simply asks, \n\"Will you prepare? \nWill you keep learning everywhere?\" \nA page today, \nA book tonight, \nCan help your future shine more bright. \nMistakes may come, \nAnd plans may bend, \nYet every challenge has an end. \nEach sunrise brings another chance \nTo learn, \nTo lead, \nTo dream, \nTo dance. \nSo build your future, \nBrick by brick, \nWith patient hands that never quit. \nTomorrow starts \nWith what you do— \nAnd all tomorrow \nStarts with you.',1,1,'answer'),
(1324,604,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: Beyond the Mountain','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: Beyond the Mountain\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 96\n\nBeyond the mountain stands a dream,\nBrighter than the morning gleam.\nMany travelers lose their way,\nYet hopeful hearts decide to stay.\nThey climb through rain,\nThey climb through heat,\nWith tired hands and aching feet.\nEach rocky trail,\nEach winding road,\nMakes lighter every heavy load.\nThe summit waits for those who try,\nWho never fear to ask, \"Why?\"\nFor every step, though small it seems,\nLeads us closer to our dreams.\nSo if the journey feels too long,\nRemember this encouraging song:\nNo mountain stands forever high—\nThe brave will always reach the sky.',NULL,'[]','Beyond the Mountain. Beyond the mountain stands a dream, Brighter than the morning gleam. Many travelers lose their way, Yet hopeful hearts decide to stay. They climb through rain, They climb through heat, With tired hands and aching feet. Each rocky trail, Each winding road, Makes lighter every heavy load. The summit waits for those who try, Who never fear to ask, \"Why?\" For every step, though small it seems, Leads us closer to our dreams. So if the journey feels too long, Remember this encouraging song: No mountain stands forever high— The brave will always reach the sky.','Beyond the mountain stands a dream, Brighter than the morning gleam. Many travelers lose their way, Yet hopeful hearts decide to stay. They climb through rain, They climb through heat, With tired hands and aching feet. Each rocky trail, Each winding road, Makes lighter every heavy load. The summit waits for those who try, Who never fear to ask, \"Why?\" For every step, though small it seems, Leads us closer to our dreams. So if the journey feels too long, Remember this encouraging song: No mountain stands forever high— The brave will always reach the sky.',20,13,'13 \n \n \nActivity 3 \nBeyond the Mountain \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nBeyond the mountain stands a dream, \nBrighter than the morning gleam. \nMany travelers lose their way, \nYet hopeful hearts decide to stay. \nThey climb through rain, \nThey climb through heat, \nWith tired hands and aching feet. \nEach rocky trail, \nEach winding road, \nMakes lighter every heavy load. \nThe summit waits for those who try, \nWho never fear to ask, \"Why?\" \nFor every step, though small it seems, \nLeads us closer to our dreams. \nSo if the journey feels too long, \nRemember this encouraging song: \nNo mountain stands forever high— \nThe brave will always reach the sky. \nWord Count: 96 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n96 \nOral Reading Score = 96__________/96 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1325,605,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: Digital Footprints','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: Digital Footprints\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 85\n\nEvery message that we send,\nEvery photo that we lend,\nLeaves a mark upon the way,\nLong beyond the passing day.\nKindness posted,\nTruth expressed,\nMakes the internet its best.\nWords can heal,\nOr words can harm,\nHolding either peace or alarm.\nThink before you click \"Send,\"\nChoose the message you defend.\nBuild a world that\'s safe and bright,\nGuided always by what\'s right.\nThough our screens may glow each night,\nCharacter remains our light.\nLet our footprints clearly show\nRespect wherever we may go.',NULL,'[]','Digital Footprints. Every message that we send, Every photo that we lend, Leaves a mark upon the way, Long beyond the passing day. Kindness posted, Truth expressed, Makes the internet its best. Words can heal, Or words can harm, Holding either peace or alarm. Think before you click \"Send,\" Choose the message you defend. Build a world that\'s safe and bright, Guided always by what\'s right. Though our screens may glow each night, Character remains our light. Let our footprints clearly show Respect wherever we may go.','Every message that we send, Every photo that we lend, Leaves a mark upon the way, Long beyond the passing day. Kindness posted, Truth expressed, Makes the internet its best. Words can heal, Or words can harm, Holding either peace or alarm. Think before you click \"Send,\" Choose the message you defend. Build a world that\'s safe and bright, Guided always by what\'s right. Though our screens may glow each night, Character remains our light. Let our footprints clearly show Respect wherever we may go.',20,14,'14 \n \n \nActivity 4 \nDigital Footprints \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nEvery message that we send, \nEvery photo that we lend, \nLeaves a mark upon the way, \nLong beyond the passing day. \nKindness posted, \nTruth expressed, \nMakes the internet its best. \nWords can heal, \nOr words can harm, \nHolding either peace or alarm. \nThink before you click \"Send,\" \nChoose the message you defend. \nBuild a world that\'s safe and bright, \nGuided always by what\'s right. \nThough our screens may glow each night, \nCharacter remains our light. \nLet our footprints clearly show \nRespect wherever we may go. \nWord Count: 85 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n85 \nOral Reading Score = 85__________/85 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1326,606,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: The Library Window','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: The Library Window\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 85\n\nBeside the library window wide,\nCountless worlds are found inside.\nHeroes, oceans, stars, and kings,\nLive among the printed things.\nEvery shelf contains a door,\nOpening to something more.\nHistory whispers,\nScience sings,\nAdventure spreads its eager wings.\nA single book can change a mind,\nLeaving fear and doubt behind.\nReaders travel far each day\nThough they never move away.\nTurn each page with eager eyes,\nSeek the truth,\nBe brave,\nBe wise.\nFor every reader soon will find\nA stronger heart,\nA brighter mind.',NULL,'[]','The Library Window. Beside the library window wide, Countless worlds are found inside. Heroes, oceans, stars, and kings, Live among the printed things. Every shelf contains a door, Opening to something more. History whispers, Science sings, Adventure spreads its eager wings. A single book can change a mind, Leaving fear and doubt behind. Readers travel far each day Though they never move away. Turn each page with eager eyes, Seek the truth, Be brave, Be wise. For every reader soon will find A stronger heart, A brighter mind.','Beside the library window wide, Countless worlds are found inside. Heroes, oceans, stars, and kings, Live among the printed things. Every shelf contains a door, Opening to something more. History whispers, Science sings, Adventure spreads its eager wings. A single book can change a mind, Leaving fear and doubt behind. Readers travel far each day Though they never move away. Turn each page with eager eyes, Seek the truth, Be brave, Be wise. For every reader soon will find A stronger heart, A brighter mind.',20,15,'15 \n \n \nActivity 5 \nThe Library Window \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nBeside the library window wide, \nCountless worlds are found inside. \nHeroes, oceans, stars, and kings, \nLive among the printed things. \nEvery shelf contains a door, \nOpening to something more. \nHistory whispers, \nScience sings, \nAdventure spreads its eager wings. \nA single book can change a mind, \nLeaving fear and doubt behind. \nReaders travel far each day \nThough they never move away. \nTurn each page with eager eyes, \nSeek the truth, \nBe brave, \nBe wise. \nFor every reader soon will find \nA stronger heart, \nA brighter mind. \nWord Count: 85 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n85 \nOral Reading Score = 85__________/85 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1327,607,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: A Teacher\'s Gift','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: A Teacher\'s Gift\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 97\n\nA teacher plants a tiny seed,\nWith every lesson, thought, and deed.\nNot made of gold or precious stone,\nBut wisdom learners call their own.\nA word of praise, a guiding hand,\nCan help a fearful learner stand.\nA patient smile, a simple cheer,\nCan chase away uncertainty and fear.\nEach question asked, each answer found,\nMakes knowledge grow on fertile ground.\nThough years may pass and seasons shift,\nLearning remains a lasting gift.\nOne day the learner leads the way,\nHelping others every day.\nThe greatest treasure we can give\nIs teaching others how to live.',NULL,'[]','A Teacher\'s Gift. A teacher plants a tiny seed, With every lesson, thought, and deed. Not made of gold or precious stone, But wisdom learners call their own. A word of praise, a guiding hand, Can help a fearful learner stand. A patient smile, a simple cheer, Can chase away uncertainty and fear. Each question asked, each answer found, Makes knowledge grow on fertile ground. Though years may pass and seasons shift, Learning remains a lasting gift. One day the learner leads the way, Helping others every day. The greatest treasure we can give Is teaching others how to live.','A teacher plants a tiny seed, With every lesson, thought, and deed. Not made of gold or precious stone, But wisdom learners call their own. A word of praise, a guiding hand, Can help a fearful learner stand. A patient smile, a simple cheer, Can chase away uncertainty and fear. Each question asked, each answer found, Makes knowledge grow on fertile ground. Though years may pass and seasons shift, Learning remains a lasting gift. One day the learner leads the way, Helping others every day. The greatest treasure we can give Is teaching others how to live.',20,16,'16 \n \n \nActivity 6 \nA Teacher\'s Gift \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nA teacher plants a tiny seed, \nWith every lesson, thought, and deed. \nNot made of gold or precious stone, \nBut wisdom learners call their own. \nA word of praise, a guiding hand, \nCan help a fearful learner stand. \nA patient smile, a simple cheer, \nCan chase away uncertainty and fear. \nEach question asked, each answer found, \nMakes knowledge grow on fertile ground. \nThough years may pass and seasons shift, \nLearning remains a lasting gift. \nOne day the learner leads the way, \nHelping others every day. \nThe greatest treasure we can give \nIs teaching others how to live. \n \nWord Count: 97 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n97 \nOral Reading Score = 97__________/97 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1328,608,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: The Silent River','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: The Silent River\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 95\n\nThe river never boasts aloud,\nNor seeks applause from any crowd.\nYet day by day it shapes the land\nWith quiet strength and patient hand.\nIt bends around the hardest stone,\nStill finding pathways of its own.\nIts waters teach us not to fight,\nBut gently choose the wiser right.\nThough storms may darken overhead,\nThe river steadily moves ahead.\nIt never stops because of fear;\nIts destination still is clear.\nLike rivers flowing to the sea,\nOur dreams become reality\nWhen steady hearts refuse to stray\nAnd choose to grow a little each day.',NULL,'[]','The Silent River. The river never boasts aloud, Nor seeks applause from any crowd. Yet day by day it shapes the land With quiet strength and patient hand. It bends around the hardest stone, Still finding pathways of its own. Its waters teach us not to fight, But gently choose the wiser right. Though storms may darken overhead, The river steadily moves ahead. It never stops because of fear; Its destination still is clear. Like rivers flowing to the sea, Our dreams become reality When steady hearts refuse to stray And choose to grow a little each day.','The river never boasts aloud, Nor seeks applause from any crowd. Yet day by day it shapes the land With quiet strength and patient hand. It bends around the hardest stone, Still finding pathways of its own. Its waters teach us not to fight, But gently choose the wiser right. Though storms may darken overhead, The river steadily moves ahead. It never stops because of fear; Its destination still is clear. Like rivers flowing to the sea, Our dreams become reality When steady hearts refuse to stray And choose to grow a little each day.',20,17,'17 \n \n \nActivity 7 \nThe Silent River \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nThe river never boasts aloud, \nNor seeks applause from any crowd. \nYet day by day it shapes the land \nWith quiet strength and patient hand. \nIt bends around the hardest stone, \nStill finding pathways of its own. \nIts waters teach us not to fight, \nBut gently choose the wiser right. \nThough storms may darken overhead, \nThe river steadily moves ahead. \nIt never stops because of fear; \nIts destination still is clear. \nLike rivers flowing to the sea, \nOur dreams become reality \nWhen steady hearts refuse to stray \nAnd choose to grow a little each day. \n \nWord Count: 95 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n95 \nOral Reading Score = 95__________/95 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1329,609,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: Hope in the Storm','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: Hope in the Storm\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 85\n\nDark clouds gather in the sky,\nThunder rumbles rolling by.\nBranches bend beneath the rain,\nYet flowers bloom once more again.\nEvery storm will someday cease,\nGiving way to light and peace.\nCourage grows through every trial,\nOften hidden for a while.\nThough the winds may shake the trees,\nHope remains within the breeze.\nMorning always follows night,\nBringing warmth and golden light.\nSo when life seems hard to bear,\nKeep believing, keep your care.\nEven storms that make us strong\nCannot last forever long.',NULL,'[]','Hope in the Storm. Dark clouds gather in the sky, Thunder rumbles rolling by. Branches bend beneath the rain, Yet flowers bloom once more again. Every storm will someday cease, Giving way to light and peace. Courage grows through every trial, Often hidden for a while. Though the winds may shake the trees, Hope remains within the breeze. Morning always follows night, Bringing warmth and golden light. So when life seems hard to bear, Keep believing, keep your care. Even storms that make us strong Cannot last forever long.','Dark clouds gather in the sky, Thunder rumbles rolling by. Branches bend beneath the rain, Yet flowers bloom once more again. Every storm will someday cease, Giving way to light and peace. Courage grows through every trial, Often hidden for a while. Though the winds may shake the trees, Hope remains within the breeze. Morning always follows night, Bringing warmth and golden light. So when life seems hard to bear, Keep believing, keep your care. Even storms that make us strong Cannot last forever long.',20,18,'18 \n \n \nActivity 8 \nHope in the Storm \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nDark clouds gather in the sky, \nThunder rumbles rolling by. \nBranches bend beneath the rain, \nYet flowers bloom once more again. \nEvery storm will someday cease, \nGiving way to light and peace. \nCourage grows through every trial, \nOften hidden for a while. \nThough the winds may shake the trees, \nHope remains within the breeze. \nMorning always follows night, \nBringing warmth and golden light. \nSo when life seems hard to bear, \nKeep believing, keep your care. \nEven storms that make us strong \nCannot last forever long. \n \nWord Count: 85 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n85 \nOral Reading Score = 85__________/85 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1330,610,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: Every Dream Matters','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: Every Dream Matters\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 84\n\nSome dream high among the stars,\nOthers heal invisible scars.\nSome create amazing art,\nOthers serve with faithful heart.\nEvery dream deserves its place,\nEvery goal its patient race.\nGreat achievements always start\nFrom hope inside a willing heart.\nDreams are built through daily choice,\nThrough discipline and honest voice.\nStep by step the future grows,\nMore than anyone yet knows.\nHold your dream with courage true.\nLet determination carry you.\nFor every dream that lights the night\nCan change tomorrow with its light.',NULL,'[]','Every Dream Matters. Some dream high among the stars, Others heal invisible scars. Some create amazing art, Others serve with faithful heart. Every dream deserves its place, Every goal its patient race. Great achievements always start From hope inside a willing heart. Dreams are built through daily choice, Through discipline and honest voice. Step by step the future grows, More than anyone yet knows. Hold your dream with courage true. Let determination carry you. For every dream that lights the night Can change tomorrow with its light.','Some dream high among the stars, Others heal invisible scars. Some create amazing art, Others serve with faithful heart. Every dream deserves its place, Every goal its patient race. Great achievements always start From hope inside a willing heart. Dreams are built through daily choice, Through discipline and honest voice. Step by step the future grows, More than anyone yet knows. Hold your dream with courage true. Let determination carry you. For every dream that lights the night Can change tomorrow with its light.',20,19,'19 \n \n \nActivity 9 \nEvery Dream Matters \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nSome dream high among the stars, \nOthers heal invisible scars. \nSome create amazing art, \nOthers serve with faithful heart. \nEvery dream deserves its place, \nEvery goal its patient race. \nGreat achievements always start \nFrom hope inside a willing heart. \nDreams are built through daily choice, \nThrough discipline and honest voice. \nStep by step the future grows, \nMore than anyone yet knows. \nHold your dream with courage true. \nLet determination carry you. \nFor every dream that lights the night \nCan change tomorrow with its light. \n \nWord Count: 84 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n84 \nOral Reading Score = 84__________/844 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1331,611,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: We Rise Together','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: We Rise Together\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 85\n\nOne small hand can plant a tree,\nTwo can build community.\nMany hearts that work as one\nFinish what cannot be done.\nDifferent voices, different minds,\nEach unique in countless kinds.\nYet together we become\nStronger than we are alone.\nHelping others makes us grow.\nSharing all the things we know.\nKindness spreads from friend to friend,\nWith no limit, with no end.\nLet us build a brighter day,\nChoosing hope in every way.\nWhen we stand through every weather,\nWe discover—\nWe rise together.',NULL,'[]','We Rise Together. One small hand can plant a tree, Two can build community. Many hearts that work as one Finish what cannot be done. Different voices, different minds, Each unique in countless kinds. Yet together we become Stronger than we are alone. Helping others makes us grow. Sharing all the things we know. Kindness spreads from friend to friend, With no limit, with no end. Let us build a brighter day, Choosing hope in every way. When we stand through every weather, We discover— We rise together.','One small hand can plant a tree, Two can build community. Many hearts that work as one Finish what cannot be done. Different voices, different minds, Each unique in countless kinds. Yet together we become Stronger than we are alone. Helping others makes us grow. Sharing all the things we know. Kindness spreads from friend to friend, With no limit, with no end. Let us build a brighter day, Choosing hope in every way. When we stand through every weather, We discover— We rise together.',20,20,'20 \n \nActivity 10 \nWe Rise Together \nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original) \nOne small hand can plant a tree, \nTwo can build community. \nMany hearts that work as one \nFinish what cannot be done. \nDifferent voices, different minds, \nEach unique in countless kinds. \nYet together we become \nStronger than we are alone. \nHelping others makes us grow. \nSharing all the things we know. \nKindness spreads from friend to friend, \nWith no limit, with no end. \nLet us build a brighter day, \nChoosing hope in every way. \nWhen we stand through every weather, \nWe discover— \nWe rise together. \nWord Count: 85 \nOral Reading Record \nTypes of Mis- \ncues \nMispronun- \nciation \nOmis- \nsion \nSubsti- \ntution \nInser- \ntion \nRepe- \ntition \nTranspo- \nsition \nRever- \nsal \nTotal \nNumber of \nMiscues \nNumber of Words in the Passage \n85 \nOral Reading Score = 85__________/85 X 100 \nReading Level (Ind-98-100, Ins-90-96, Frus– 89 below) \nReading Speed = Words Read/Reading time in seconds X 60 \nwords per Minute',1,1,'answer'),
(1332,612,NULL,'learn',1,'Read aloud: The Last Seat in the Classroom','reading','Tap Start reading and read the whole passage aloud. Tap I’m done when you finish. Your teacher listens for accuracy, speed and expression.','Title: The Last Seat in the Classroom\nAuthor: BULIG Development Team (Original)\nWords: 260\n\nThe last seat in Room Seven was always empty until the second week of classes. On Monday morning, a quiet boy named Adrian entered the room carrying an old backpack and a neatly folded notebook. He smiled politely as the teacher introduced him to the class.\n\nSince all the front seats were already occupied, Adrian sat at the back. During lessons, he listened carefully and wrote detailed notes, but he rarely spoke. Some classmates assumed he was shy, while others simply forgot he was there.\n\nOne afternoon, the class was assigned a group science project. Adrian\'s group struggled to organize their ideas. They argued over the experiment and could not agree on who would present.\n\nAfter listening quietly, Adrian finally raised his hand. \"May I suggest something?\" he asked.\n\nHis classmates nodded.\n\nHe explained how they could divide the work fairly. He also showed them a simple experiment he had learned in his previous school. Everyone agreed to follow his plan.\n\nPresentation day arrived. Their experiment worked perfectly, and the class applauded their teamwork. Their teacher praised not only the project but also the way everyone cooperated.\n\nDuring recess, Adrian no longer sat alone. His classmates invited him to eat with them, asking questions about his old school and sharing stories about their own experiences.\n\nAdrian realized that sometimes people are not noticed because they remain silent. Yet kindness, preparation, and willingness to help often speak louder than words. From that day forward, the last seat in the classroom became known as the place where a quiet leader once sat.',NULL,'[]','The Last Seat in the Classroom. The last seat i