(1518,770,NULL,'learn',1,'Day 12 · Part 1','open','Read the passage, then answer the questions.','A FRIEND IN NEED IS A FRIEND INDEED\nOnce upon a time two very close friends lived in a village. As time passed their friendship grew thicker. Now they were grown up men.\n\nOne day they decided to go and find work. They set off.\nBefore leaving their village, they promised to stand by each other through thick and thin. They took oath of sincerity and assured each other of help in the hour of need. They had to pass through a jungle. They had not gone far into the thick forest when they found themselves face to face with a big bear.\nThe bear began to move towards them. They felt helpless and terrified.\nOne of them knew how to climb a tree. He at once caught hold of a strong branch and swung up the tree. The other could not climb. He had heard that the bear does not eat the dead. So, he lay down on the ground and held his breath pretending to be dead. Meanwhile, the bear came to him and shifted him. The bear left him.\nWhen the bear had gone out of sight, the friend on the tree came down. He asked his friend, \"Dear friend, what did the bear whisper in your ear?\"\nThe other replied quickly, \"The bear advised me not to trust a selfish friend.\"\nSaying this he left him and went away.\nMoral: A Friend in Need is a Friend Indeed\n\nA FRIEND IN NEED IS A FRIEND INDEED VOCABULARY\n\nVocabulary\n1. village -a small town in the country; a settlement usually larger than a hamlet and smaller than a town. Example:       1. The entire villages come to see the parade. 2.We stayed in a charming bed-and-breakfast in a lakeside village.\n2. oath -a formal and serious promise to tell the truth or to do something. Example:       1. It is an oath to defend the nation. 2.He uttered an oath and walk away.\n3. jungle -an impenetrable thicket or tangled mass of tropical vegetation. Example:       1. That is their way of living in the corporate jungle. 2.Wild animals live in a jungle.\n4. sincerity -the quality or state of being sincere; honesty of mind. Example:      1. His sincerity is the cause of their friendship. 2.Your sincerity will be measured in times of needs.\n5. selfish -having or showing concern only for yourself and not for the needs or feelings of other people. Example:      1. She is interested only in her own selfish concern. 2.Her selfishness could bring her down. A FRIEND IN NEED IS A FRIEND INDEED ASSESSMENT\n\nWrite your answer.',NULL,'[]','Read the passage, then answer the questions.',NULL,10,52,'',1,1,'answer'),
(1519,770,NULL,'learn',2,'Day 12 · Part 2','open','Carefully read the sentences. Look for the synonym of the underlined words. Encircle the letter of the correct answer.','1. We stayed in a small house in the village.\n\n2. After the oath taking ceremony, I will go home.\n\n3. This is the entry way to the jungle.\n\n4. His sincerity was measured during the times of his friend’s failures.\n\n5. Her selfishness is the reason why she failed.',NULL,'[]','Carefully read the sentences. Look for the synonym of the underlined words. Encircle the letter of the correct answer.',NULL,10,52,'',1,1,'answer'),
