(1675,882,NULL,'learn',1,'Activity 2','open','Read the passage, then answer the questions.','Write a news article based on the following facts which are given at random.\n\n➢     Roxana Saberi – US –Iranian journalist. She was sentenced to eight years in jail by an Iranian revolutionary court. This was according to Saberi’s lawyer.\n\n➢     Saberi was charged with spying for the United States.\n\n➢     Saberi is 31 years old. She has been detained in Tehran’s notorious Evin Prison since January.\n\n➢     The verdict was the harshest sentence ever meted out to a dual national on security charges.\n\n➢     Abdulsamad Koramshahi – Saberi’s lawyer. According to him, Saberi has been sentenced to eight years in jail, and he’s going to appeal, because according to Iranian law the verdict can be appealed within 20 days.\n\n➢     Saberi’s father was greeted with shock and said that her daughter had been “tricked” into confessing. She was initially reported to have been detained for buying alcohol, an illegal act in the Islamic Republic.\n\n➢      Saberi went on trial behind closed doors on Monday accused of spying for the US.\n\n➢     The case against Saberi has raised deep concerns in Washington and among the right groups.\n\n➢     According to ISNA news agency, as it quotes unnamed judiciary source- a revolutionary court had sentenced Saberi for espionage – a charge that could have risked the death sentence.\n\n➢      Hillary R. Clinton- US Secretary of State. She was deeply disappointed over the sentence. She also said that Washington would “vigorously raise” its concerns with Tehran. No date yet has been given to the verdict.\n\n___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ____________________________________________