(1685,892,NULL,'learn',1,'Activity 12','open','Copyread the news below using appropriate copy reading symbols, write the slug and instructions with two headlines and unit counts using flush left and flush right. This article was taken last 2020 in the Philippine Star.','manila, Philippines — mount bulusan in sorsogon province has contined to show an increase in volcanic earthquakes, state seism ologists said on Tuesday\n\naA total of ninety-one volcano-tectonic earth qakes “associated with rock fracturing” with a depth of 2 to 4 kilometers have been recorded since 1:38 a.m. on monday,\n\nacording the philippine institute of volcanology and Seismology (Phivolcs).\n\nincreased seismic activity and pres surization of the volcano edifice may endicated that hydrothermal processes may be occurring beneath the vol cano and may lead to\n\nsteam-driven eruptions at any of th e summit vents, Phivolcs said in a statement\n\nAlso, the volcano’s southwestern andsouth eastern flanks have been inflated since Feb. 2023 based on Phivolcs’ grounddeformation data from con tinuous GPS and electronic tilt monit oring\n\nOn the hand other, Phivolcs said degassing activity from the summit crater and active vents has been very weak to modirate when the\n\nvolcanosummit has been visibleble\n\nConsidering these fac tors, the statevolcanologist said bulusan volcano remains alert under level 1, meaning it is still at a low level ofunrest.\n\n___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ______________________________