                  12\n\nPDF page 22\n12\n\n\nActivity No. 2-Direction: Read the sentence and color the star as\nyou read each word.\n\n        I see the pen.\n        I see the vet.\n        I see the hen.\n        I see the men.\n\n\n\n\n                         Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                 13\n\nPDF page 23\n13\n\n\n\n                       Rhyming and Rhyming Songs\n\n\nName                                            Grade\n\nDirection: Encircle the word inside the parenthesis that\n        rhymes on the underlined words in the\n        sentence.\n\n   1. The old man’s cane is on the ( mat, box, lane).\n\n   2. Dad came home late and mom closed the ( pen, gate,\n\n   bag).\n\n   3. Dan pulled the weed and planted the ( seed, cap, bun).\n\n   4. Pam gave a toy to the ( man, lady, boy).\n\n   5. I saw a mouse in the( car, pin, house).\n\n   6. We can’t see a moon at ( room, noon, hoop).\n\n   7. Mothers love to bake a ( cake, day, pine).\n\n   8. Roy heard a boom from his ( line, room, game).\n\n   9. Ana went to the bay the other ( day, pit, log).\n\n\n   10. 10. Rob bought a ball in the (mask, mall, home).\n\n\n\n\n                         Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                 14\n\nPDF page 24\nPre-Test: Phonological Awareness (Oral Assessment )\n\nInstructions for Teacher:\n\nAdminister one-on-one. Read each item clearly and allow the pupil to respond\nimmediately. Complete all 30 items in **approximately 60 seconds**. Encourage quick\nresponses. Record answers on the scoring sheet. No repetition allowed to maintain speed.\nTime Limit: 60 seconds total\nSkills Covered: Rhyming, Onset-Rime, Blending, Alliteration, Segmentation\nPart 1: Rhyming – Yes/No (6 items, 12 seconds)\n\n*Teacher says quickly:* “Rhyme? Yes or no: cat – hat.”\n\n1. cat – hat\n\n2. dog – log\n\n3. sun – bed\n\n4. hop – top\n\n5. pen – hen\n\n6. book – look\n\nPart 2: Onset-Rime – First Sound (6 items, 12 seconds)\n\n*Teacher says:* “First sound in:”\n\n7. man\n\n8. fish\n\n9. dog\n\n10. cup\n\n11. sun\n\n12. zip\n\nPart 3: Blending Syllables (6 items, 12 seconds)\n\n*Teacher says:* “Put together: rain – bow”\n\n13. rain – bow\n                                    Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                            15\n\nPDF page 25\n14. cup – cake\n\n15. wa – ter\n\n16. air – plane\n\n17. el – e – phant\n\n18. ham – bur – ger\n\nPart 4: Alliteration – Same Sound? (6 items, 12 seconds)\n\n*Teacher says:* “Same sound? Yes or no: bat, ball, boy”\n\n19. bat, ball, boy\n\n20. cat, sun, cup\n\n21. fish, fan, fun\n\n22. moon, star, sun\n\n23. pen, pig, pan\n\n24. red, run, rag\n\nPart 5: Sentence Segmentation (6 items, 12 seconds)\n\n*Teacher says:* “How many words? ‘I run.’”\n\n25. I run.\n\n26. She sits.\n\n27. The cat jumps.\n\n28. We eat cake.\n\n29. My mom reads.\n\n30. The big dog barks.\n\n\n\n\n                                Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                        16\n\nPDF page 26\nAnswer Key & Scoring Guide\n\nPart 1: Rhyming\n\n1. Yes\n\n2. Yes\n\n3. No\n\n4. Yes\n\n5. Yes\n\n6. Yes\n\nPart 2: Onset-Rime (accept correct phoneme)\n\n7. /m/\n\n8. /f/\n\n9. /d/\n\n10. /k/\n\n11. /s/\n\n12. /z/\n\nPart 3: Blending Syllables\n\n13. rainbow\n\n14. cupcake\n\n15. water\n\n16. airplane\n\n17. elephant\n\n18. hamburger\n\n\n\n\n                             Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                     17\n\nPDF page 27\nPart 4: Alliteration\n\n19. Yes\n\n20. No\n\n21. Yes\n\n22. No\n\n23. Yes\n\n24. Yes\n\nPart 5: Sentence Segmentation\n\n25. 2\n\n26. 2\n\n27. 3\n\n28. 3\n\n29. 3\n\n30. 4\n\n\n\n\n                                Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                        18\n\nPDF page 28\nRapid Scoring Sheet\n\n\n\nPupil: _______________ Date: _______________ Time: _______________\n\n        Skill                      Items                   Score (/6)\n\nRhyming                              1–6                   _____\n\nOnset-Rime                           7–12                  _____\n\nBlending                            13–18                  _____\n\nAlliteration                        19–24                  _____\n\nSegmentation                        25–30                  _____\n\nTotal                                ____/30               _____\n\n\n\n\n                                Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                        19\n\nPDF page 29\nInterpretation – 60-Second Diagnostic\n\n- 25–30: Strong PA – ready for advanced phonics\n\n- 18–24: Moderate PA – needs group practice\n\n- 12–17: Low PA – requires targeted intervention\n\n- Below 12: Very low PA – intensive one-on-one support\n\n**Teacher’s Notes for Rapid Administration**\n\n- Use a stopwatch or timer.\n\n- If a student hesitates >2 seconds, mark incorrect and move on.\n\n- Accept phonemes (sounds) for onset-rime, not letter names.\n\n- For sentence segmentation, accept number words or fingers shown.\n\n- This test is **speed-sensitive** to assess automaticity.\n\n\n\n\n                                   Department of Education ● Republic of the Philippines\n                                                                                           20',12,'Untimed digital worksheet adaptation. Teacher observation is optional and does not gate progress; do not treat completion as a standardized assessment score.',NULL),
