          2. I saw a big pig.\n               3. There was a bug on the rug.\n               4. The pot is hot.\n               5. The net is wet.\n               6. They had fun under the sun.\n               7. The hen is in the pen.\n               8. A frog hid under the log.\n               9. It is dark in the park.\n               10. A goat is in the boat.\n               11. The man is in the van.\n               12. The lad is mad.\n               13. Tam’s top is on the mop.\n               14. She lost the pill on the hill.\n               15. The well has a bell.\n               16. Puss foot fits in the boat.\n               17. A cock stays on the rock.\n               18. The mice eat the rice.\n               19. They got a wine from the vine.\n               20. The children hike to the dike.\n\nPDF page 62\n48\n\n\n\n\n                 Post-Test: Phonological Awareness (Oral Assessment)\n**Instructions for Teacher:**\nAdminister one-on-one. Read each item clearly and allow the pupil to respond\nimmediately. Complete all 30 items in **approximately 60 seconds**.\nEncourage quick, automatic responses. Record answers on the scoring sheet.\nNo repetition allowed to assess fluency and mastery.\n\n\n**Time Limit:** 60 seconds total\n**Skills Covered:** Rhyming, Onset-Rime, Blending, Alliteration, Segmentation\nPart 1: Rhyming – Yes/No (6 items, 12 seconds)\nTeacher says quickly: “Rhyme? Yes or no: boat – coat.”\n1. boat – coat\n2. fish – dish\n3. bed – head\n4. run – sun\n5. cake – lake\n6. moon – spoon\nPart 2: Onset-Rime – First Sound (6 items, 12 seconds)\n*Teacher says:* “First sound in:”\n7. pig\n8. kite\n9. van\n10. goat\n11. zebra\n12. chair\nPart 3: Blending Syllables (6 items, 12 seconds)\n*Teacher says:* “Put together: sun – shine”\n13. sun – shine\n14. tooth – brush\n15. but – ter – fly\n\nPDF page 63\n16. wa – ter – mel – on\n17. bas – ket – ball\n18. ham – bur – ger\nPart 4: Alliteration – Same Sound? (6 items, 12 seconds)\nTeacher says: “Same sound? Yes or no: dog, door, duck”\n19. dog, door, duck\n20. cat, cup, sun\n21. snake, sock, sand\n22. moon, mouse, house\n23. fish, frog, fox\n24. red, rat, rug\nPart 5: Sentence Segmentation (6 items, 12 seconds)\n*Teacher says:* “How many words? ‘She eats.’”\n25. She eats.\n26. The dog runs.\n27. My mom reads books.\n28. We play in the park.\n29. The little bird sings.\n30. I like to read stories.\n\nPDF page 64\nAnswer Key & Scoring Guide\nPart 1: Rhyming\n\n1. Yes\n2. Yes\n3. Yes\n4. Yes\n5. Yes\n6. Yes\nPart 2: Onset-Rime (accept correct phoneme)\n\n7. /p/\n8. /k/\n9. /v/\n10. /g/\n11. /z/\n12. /ch/\nPart 3: Blending Syllables\n\n13. sunshine\n14. toothbrush\n15. butterfly\n16. watermelon\n17. basketball\n18. hamburger\nPart 4: Alliteration\n\n19. Yes\n20. No\n21. Yes\n22. No\n23. Yes\n24. Yes\n\nPDF page 65\nPart 5: Sentence Segmentation\n\n25. 2\n26. 3\n27. 4\n28. 5\n29. 4\n30. 5\n\nPDF page 66\nRapid Scoring Sheet\n\n\nPupil: _____________ Date: _______________ | Time: _______________\n\n\n     Skill          Items               Score (/6)\nRhyming            1–6                   _____\nOnset-Rime         7–12                  _____\nBlending          13–18                  _____\nAlliteration      19–24                  _____\nSegmentation      25–30                  _____\n     Total        ____/30               _____\n\nPDF page 67\nInterpretation – 60-Second Post-Test\n- 28–30: Mastery – Advanced phonological awareness - Remarks - Passed\n- 24–27: Proficient – Strong skills, ready for phonics application - Remarks -\nPassed\n- 18–23: Developing – Needs continued practice - Remarks – Not Ready\n- Below 18: Intervention Required – Significant gaps in phonological awareness\n\n\nInterpretation – 30 items test\n24 – 30 – Remarks - Passed and recommended for the next Reading Level\n23 and below – Remarks- Not Ready and will continue the intervention for the\nnext cycle\n\n\n\n\n**Teacher’s Notes for Post-Test Administration**\n- Use a stopwatch – true measure of automaticity.\n- If hesitation >2 seconds, mark incorrect and proceed.\n- For onset-rime, accept clear phoneme production (not letter names).\n- Sentence segmentation: accept number words or fingers.\n- Compare with pre-test scores to measure growth.',54,'Untimed digital worksheet adaptation. Teacher observation is optional and does not gate progress; do not treat completion as a standardized assessment score.',NULL),
