(166,11,12211,'Activity 11','Me and My School','Listen, learn and use new words about me and my school.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nMe and My School · module PDF pages 49, 50, 51, 52\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 49\nMe and My School\nIn my school.\n| can learn.\nTo read and write.\n| can learn.\nTo dance and sing.\n\nPDF page 50\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the word in Column A with its\nmeaning in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Learn\na. To make words with a pen\nor pencil\n2. Read\nb. To make your body to\nmusic\n3. Write\nc. †o say words out loud from\na book\n4. Dance\nd. To get new knowledge or\nskills\n5. Sing\ne. To make music with your\nvoice\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully to the following sentences\nand choose the best answer for each question.\nSentence 1: “In my school”\nSentence 2.:“I can learn”\nSentence 3: “To read and write”\nSentence 4: “To dance and sing”\n\nPDF page 51\nQuestions:\n1. What place are we talking about?\na. Home\nb. School\nc. Park\nd. Store\n2. What can you do at school?\na. Sleep\nb. Learn\nc. Eat\nd. Play\n3. What can you do with words at school?\na. Read and sing\nb. Dance and write\nc. Read and write\nd. Sing and dance\n4. What can you do with music at school?\na. Dance and sing\nb. Read and write\nc. Learn and play\nd. Eat and sleep\n\nPDF page 52\n5. What is something you CANNOT do according to\nthe sentences?\na. Read\nb. Write\nc. Play\nd. Sing\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[49, 50, 51, 52]','assets/images/level5/g1/p049-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(167,11,13212,'Activity 12','In the Classroom','Listen, learn and use new words about in the classroom.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nIn the Classroom · module PDF pages 53, 54, 55, 56\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 53\nIn The Classroom\nThis is our classroom.\n| can name the things in our classroom.\nruler\ntable i\nsharpener SS\ncicero\n(eaalfoery\nblackboard\ncolor pen\neraser book\n\nPDF page 54\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the classroom item in Column A\nwith the use in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Pencil\na. Used to carrying things\n2. Book.\nb. Used for drawing\nstraight lines\n3. Eraser.\nc. Used for writing\n4. Ruler\nd. Used for reading\nstories\n5. Bag\ne. Used for removing\nmistakes\n\nPDF page 55\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully to the following sentences\nand choose the best answer for each question.\nSentence 1: “This is our classroom”\nSentence 2:“I can name the things in our classroom”\nQuestions:\n1. Where are we?\na. Home\nb. Classroom\nc. Park\nd. Store\n2. What can you do in the classroom?\na. Eat\nb. Sleep\nc. Name things\nd. Play\n3. What is something you might find in the classroom?\na. Bed\nb. Table\nc. Car\nd. Tree\n\nPDF page 56\n4. What do you the place where we learn?\na.Kitchen\nb. Bedroom\nc. Classroom\nd. Garden\n5. What is the main idea of the sentences?\na. Playing outside\nb. Being in the classroom\nc. Eating lunch\nd. Sleeping at home\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[53, 54, 55, 56]','assets/images/level5/g1/p053-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(168,11,14213,'Activity 13','In the Garden','Listen, learn and use new words about in the garden.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nIn the Garden · module PDF pages 57, 58, 59, 60\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 57\nIn The Garden\nThis is our school garden.\nWe have vegetables in our garden.\n| plant vegetables in our garden\nDED ge\nsquash tomato pechay eggplant\ncarrots bitter gourd pepper cabbage\n\nPDF page 58\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the vegetable in Column A with\nits color in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Carrot\na. Purple\n2. Tomato\nb. Green\n3. Eggplant\nc. Orange\n4. Pechay\nd. Red\n\nPDF page 59\n5. Squash\ne. Green with stripes\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully to the following sentences\nand choose the best answer for each question.\nSentence 1: “This is our school garden”\nSentence 2:“We have vegetables in our garden”\nSentence 3: “I plant vegetable in our garden”\nQuestions:\n1. Where are we?\na. Home\nb. School garden\nc. Park\nd. Store\n2. What do we have in the garden?\na. Flowers\nb. Vegetables\nc. Fruits\nd. Trees\n\nPDF page 60\n3. What do we do in the garden?\na. Play games\nb. Plant vegetables\nc. Read books\nd. Sing songs\n4. What is something you might find in the garden?\na. Car\nb. Table\nc. Tomato\nd. Bed\n5. What is the main idea of the sentences?\na. Playing inside\nb. Being in the school garden\nc. Eating lunch\nd. Sleeping at home\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[57, 58, 59, 60]','assets/images/level5/g1/p057-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(169,11,15214,'Activity 14','In the Canteen','Listen, learn and use new words about in the canteen.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nIn the Canteen · module PDF pages 61, 62, 63, 64\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 61\nIn The Canteen\nThis is our school canteen.\n| buy food in our school canteen.\nsales lady\nWW\nice drop banana Cue sandwich\nBy . &\nbiscuits juice sweet potato\n\nPDF page 62\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Choose the best answer for each\nquestion. Encircle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What is a “sandwich”?\na. A cold treat\nb. Food between two slices of bread\nc. A sweet snack on the stick\nd. A yellow drink\n2. What is “juice”\na. A frozen dessert\nb. Cooked bananas on a stick\nc. A sweet drink made from fruits\nd. A baked treat\n3. What is “banana cue”?\na. A frozen treat\nb. Cooked bananas on a stick\nc. A sweet baked treat\nd. A cold drink\n4. What is an “ice drop”?\na. A cold frozen treat\nb. A hot snack\nc. A baked treat\nd. A drink\n\nPDF page 63\n5. What are “biscuits”?\na. A frozen treat\nb. Small baked treats\nc. Cooked bananas\nd. A sweet drink\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully to the following sentences\nand choose the best answer for each question.\nSentence 1: “This is our school canteen”\nSentence 2:“I buy foods in our school canteen”\nQuestions:\n1. Where are we?\na. Home\nb. School canteen\nc. Park\nd. Store\n2. What do we do in the school canteen?\na. Play games\nb. Buy foods\nc. Read books\nd. Sing songs\n3. Who helps us in the canteen?\na. Teacher\nb. Sales lady\nc. Doctor\nd. Policeman\n\nPDF page 64\n4. What is something you might find in the canteen?\na. Car\nb. Table\nc. Sandwich\nd. Bed\n5. What is the main idea of the sentences?\na. Playing outside\nb. Being in the school canteen\nc. Eating lunch at home\nd. Sleeping at home\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[61, 62, 63, 64]','assets/images/level5/g1/p061-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(170,11,16215,'Activity 15','In the Library','Listen, learn and use new words about in the library.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nIn the Library · module PDF pages 65, 66, 67, 68\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 65\nIn The Library\nThis is our school library.\n| read books in the library.\ndictionary magazine rock books\nnewspaper\nlibrarian book shelves magazine\n\nPDF page 66\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\nmeanings in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on\nthe line before each number.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nBooks\na. A person who works in a library\n2. ______\nMagazine\nb. A daily or weekly publication\nwith news\n3. ______\nNewspaper\nc. A collection of printed pages\n\nPDF page 67\n4. ______\nLibrarian\nd. A book that list words and their\nmeanings\n5. ______\nDictionary\ne. A periodical publication with\narticles\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. Where does the story take place?\na. At a park\nb. In a school library\nc. In a classroom\nd. At a bookstore\n\nPDF page 68\n2. Who does the library belong to?\na. The speaker and their friends\nb. The teacher\nc. The public\nd. A bookstore owner\n3. What is the main activity the speaker does in this\nplace?\na. They play games.\nb. They read books.\nc. They draw pictures.\nd. They eat lunch.\n4. What kind of items are found in this place?\na. Computers and toys\nb. Food and drinks\nc. Balls and sports equipment\nd. Books\n5. What is the best title for this passage?\na. My Favorite Teacher\nb. Playing at School\nc. The School Library\nd. Buying New Books\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[65, 66, 67, 68]','assets/images/level5/g1/p065-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(171,11,17216,'Activity 16','Keeping Our School Clean','Listen, learn and use new words about keeping our school clean.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nKeeping Our School Clean · module PDF pages 69, 70, 71, 72\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 69\nKeeping Our School Clean\nWe take care of our school.\nWe keep our school clean.\nyoul\nS | coconut husk brooms\nJ hh\nwT cleaning mop trash can\njanitor brush\n\nPDF page 70\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\nmeanings in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on\nthe line before each number.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nJanitor.\na. A container for waste\n2. ______\nBroom\nb. A tool for bristles used for\ncleaning\n3. ______\nTrash Can\nc. A floor covering\n\nPDF page 71\n4. ______\nRug\nd. A person who cleans\nbuildings\n5. ______\nBrush\ne. A tool used for sweeping\nA. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage.\nThen, answer the Questions below.\nPassage:\n“Every morning, the janitor, Mang Tomas, clans our\nschool. He uses a broom to sweep the floors and a\nbrush to scrub the walls. He throws all the trash into the\ntrash can. Sometimes, he uses a cleaning mop to\nwipe the spills. Our school is clean because of Mang\nTomas”.\nQuestions:\n1. Who cleans the school every morning?\na. Mang Andoy\nb. Mang Tomas\nc. Mang Pedro\n\nPDF page 72\n2. What does he use to sweep the floors?\na. Cleaning mop\nb. Broom\nc. Brush\n3. What does he use to scrub the walls?\na. Broom\nb. Cleaning mop\nc. Brush\n4. Where does he throw the trash?\na. On the floor\nb. In the trash can\nc. Under the rug\n5. Why is the school clean?\na. Because of the students\nb. Because of Mang Tomas\nc. Because of the teachers\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[69, 70, 71, 72]','assets/images/level5/g1/p069-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(172,11,18217,'Activity 17','The Community Helpers','Listen, learn and use new words about the community helpers.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nThe Community Helpers · module PDF pages 73, 74, 75, 76, 77\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 73\nMe and My Community\n| stay ina place.\nSafe and with peace.\nSurrounded with love.\nev A gift noeneve.\nSm\n\nPDF page 74\nThe Community Helpers\nIN our community there are many helpers.\nWe love our community helpers.\nEls he\nteacher policeman _ me a Salpeter\nfarmer fisherman doctor\n“a> on\nie. eeper\nx ae\nk Borer driver fireman nurse\n\nPDF page 75\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\nmeanings in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on\nthe line before each number.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nFarmer\na. Catches fish from the sea or river\n2. ______\nCarpenter\nb. Grows crops and raises animals\nfor food\n3. ______\nNurse\nc. Sells goods and items in a shop\n\nPDF page 76\n4. ______\nFisherman\nd. Takes care of sick or injured\npeople in a hospital or clinic\n5. ______\nStorekeeper\ne. Builds and repairs things made of\nwood\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main idea of the passage?\na. Helpers work in a hospital.\nb. There are many different kinds of community\nhelpers.\nc. Teachers are the most important helpers.\nd. Helpers are very busy.\n\nPDF page 77\n2. According to the passage, how do the people feel\nabout their community helpers?\na. They are afraid of them.\nb. They love them.\nc. They do not know them.\nd. They are angry with them.\n3. Which helper is most likely to help you if you are sick?\na. A policeman and a security guard\nb. A doctor and a nurse\nc. A fireman and a driver\nd. A carpenter and a laborer\n4. Which of the following helpers is NOT mentioned in the\npassage?\na. Fisherman\nb. Pilot\nc. Teacher\nd. Storekeeper\n5. Based on the passage, a community helper is\nsomeone who...\na. works only for money.\nb. lives in a big house.\nc. does a job that helps people in the area.\nd. travels to different countries.\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[73, 74, 75, 76, 77]','assets/images/level5/g1/p073-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(173,11,19218,'Activity 18','In the Plaza','Listen, learn and use new words about in the plaza.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nIn the Plaza · module PDF pages 78, 79, 80, 81\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 78\nIn The Plaza\nThis is our plaza.\nWe play in our plaza.\nOur plaza is very clean and beautiful.\nseesaw monkey bar\n\nPDF page 79\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect descriptions or functions in Column B. Write\nthe letter of your answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______ Plaza\na. A place of playground\nequipment you down\nsitting or lying\n2. ______\nStatue\nb. A public open space\nin a city or town, often for\npeople to walk and play\n3. ______ Swing\nc. A structure of bars you\ncan swing across using\nyour hands\n\nPDF page 80\n4. ______\nSlide\nd. A seat hanging from\nropes or chains that\nmoves back and forth\n5. ______\nMonkey bar\ne. A model of a person or\nanimal, made of stone\nor metal\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A plaza\nc. A garden\nd. A park\n\nPDF page 81\n2. What do the children do in the plaza?\na. They study.\nb. They play.\nc. They work.\nd. They sleep.\n3. How is the plaza described?\na. Very big and busy\nb. Clean and beautiful\nc. Old and quiet\nd. Dark and scary\n4. Which of the following items is mentioned as being in\nthe plaza?\na. A swimming pool\nb. A basketball court\nc. A statue\nd. A fountain\n5. The word \"our\" in the passage suggests that the\nplaza...\na. is very far away.\nb. belongs to or is used by the speaker and their\ncommunity.\nc. is new.\nd. is only for children.\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[78, 79, 80, 81]','assets/images/level5/g1/p078-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(174,11,20219,'Activity 19','In the Market','Listen, learn and use new words about in the market.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nIn the Market · module PDF pages 82, 83, 84, 85\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 82\nIn The Market\nThis is OUr market.\nWe can buy our food in the market.\nbutchers weighing scale\nknife\nchopping board\nbutcher\n\nPDF page 83\nA. Vocabulary\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect meanings or uses in Column B. Write the letter of\nyour answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nButcher\na. A tool used to measure how\nheavy something is\n2. ______\nWeighing Scale\nb. A person whose job is to cut\nand sell meat\n3. ______\nChopping board\nc. Vegetables that grow\nunderground, like potatoes\nor carrots.\n4. ______\nGrains\nd. A hard board used for\ncutting good on.\n5. ______\nRoot crops\ne. Small hard seeds from plants\nlike rice or wheat, used for food.\n\nPDF page 84\nA. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a short\npassage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A market\nc. A farm\nd. A restaurant\n2. What is the main purpose of going to this place?\na. To play and have fun\nb. To study and learn\nc. To buy food\nd. To cook meals\n3. Which of the following is an example of a food you\ncan buy there?\na. A toy car\nb. A storybook\nc. A chair\nd. Fruits\n\nPDF page 85\n4. Who is the person you would find working with meat\nin this place?\na. The fisherman\nb. The butcher\nc. The farmer\nd. The driver\n5. Which tool would a seller use to tell you the weight\nof your fruits?\na. A chopping board\nb. A butcher\'s knife\nc. A weighing scale\nd. A shopping cart\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[82, 83, 84, 85]','assets/images/level5/g1/p082-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(175,11,21220,'Activity 20','In the Farm','Listen, learn and use new words about in the farm.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nIn the Farm · module PDF pages 86, 87, 88, 89\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 86\nIn The Farm\nThis is our farm.\nWe grow plants on our farm.\nWe have animals on our farm to\ncoconut banana cassava guava\nbottle guard cashew\n\nPDF page 87\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle the\nletter of the best answer.\n1. What is a farm?\na. A place where people go to work in offices.\nb. A place where animals are kept for display.\nc. An area of land used for growing crops and\nraising animals.\nd. A large building where machines make cars.\n2. Which word describes a large animal often used for\npulling plows in some countries?\na. Goat\nb. Carabao\nc. Chicken\nd. Bird\n3. What does it mean to grow plants?\na. To cook and eat them.\nb. To draw pictures of them.\nc. To cultivate and help them develop from seeds.\nd. To collect them from the forest.\n4. Which of the following is most likely a plant with a\nlarge, hard-shelled nut that grows on trees?\na. Cassava\nb. Pineapple\nc. Coconut\nd. Banana\n\nPDF page 88\n5. If you see a bottle gourd on a farm, what are you\nlooking at?\na. A type of animal\nb. A tool for feeding animals\nc. A building for storing tools\nd. A type of vegetable that grows on a vine\nB Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main topic of the passage?\na. A family home\nb. A school playground\nc. A farm and what is on it\nd. A zoo with many animals\n2. What are the two main types of things found on this\nfarm?\na. Buildings and roads\nb. Toys and games\nc. Plants and animals\nd. Rivers and mountains\n\nPDF page 89\n3. Which of these animals is NOT mentioned as living on\nthe farm?\na. Goat\nb. Sheep\nc. Pig\nd. Chicken\n4. Based on the passage, which activity do the people\nmost likely do on this farm?\na. They go swimming.\nb. They grow fruits and raise animals.\nc. They build cars and machines.\nd. They buy and sell clothes.\n5. The passage says, \"This is our farm.\" What does this\nmost likely mean?\na. The farm belongs to someone else.\nb. The farm is a public park for everyone.\nc. The speaker and their family or community own or\nwork on the farm.\nd. The farm is very old\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[86, 87, 88, 89]','assets/images/level5/g1/p086-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(176,11,22221,'Activity 21','Buildings Around Me','Listen, learn and use new words about buildings around me.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nBuildings Around Me · module PDF pages 90, 91, 92, 93\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 90\nBuildings Around Me\nThere are many building in our place.\nEach building is very useful for us.\nWe keep our building safe and clean.\nchurch\n<a@iane SHOP>| [Ml [i\nfire station\n\nPDF page 91\nA. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle\nthe letter of the best answer.\n1. What is a building?\na. A natural formation like a mountain or a river.\nb. A vehicle used for transportation.\nc. A structure with a roof and walls, such as a\nhouse or school.\nd. A type of animal that lives in a forest.\n2. If you need to buy medicine,\nwhich building should you go to?\na. A bakery\nb. A pharmacy\nc. a bank\nd. a restaurant\n3. What does useful mean?\na. Old and beautiful\nb. Able to be used for a purpose; helpful.\nc. Very large and expensive\nd. New and modern\n4. The barangay hall is most likely a building that\nserves as what?\na. A place for local government and community\nmeetings.\nb. A place to watch movies.\nc. A place to buy fresh fish and vegetables.\nd. A place to repair cars.\n\nPDF page 92\n5. What does it mean to keep our buildings safe\nand clean?\na. To forget about them.\nb. To destroy them and build new ones.\nc. To maintain or preserve them in that condition.\nd. To paint them all the same color.\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main idea of the passage?\na. There are many useful buildings in the community.\nb. Houses are the most important buildings.\nc. Buildings are very expensive to build.\nd. All buildings look the same.\n2. How do the people feel about the buildings in their\nplace?\na. They find them useless.\nb. They think they are ugly.\nc. They find them very useful.\nd. They are afraid of them.\n\nPDF page 93\n3. If someone needs to put out a fire, which building\nshould they call for help?\na. The hospital\nb. The barangay hall\nc. The fire station\nd. The market\n4. Which of the following is a building where you can\nbuy bread and pastries?\na. The restaurant\nb. The pharmacy\nc. The bakery\nd. The store\n5. What do the people do for their buildings?\na. They keep them safe and clean.\nb. They ignore them.\nc. They paint them every year.\nd. They sell them to other people.\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[90, 91, 92, 93]','assets/images/level5/g1/p090-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(177,11,23300,'Post-test','Post-assessment','Show how much your listening and vocabulary have grown.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 1\nPost-assessment · module PDF pages 95, 96, 97, 98, 99, 100, 101, 102, 103\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 95\nPOST TEST (Activity 1-10)\nVocabulary Development (1-10)\nA. Instructions: Draw a line to match the word to the\ncorrect picture.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Shovel\na.\n2. Nose\nb.\n3. Chair\nc.\n4. Teddy Bear\nd.\n5. Mother\ne.\n\nPDF page 96\nB. Instructions: Draw a line to match the meaning to\nthe correct picture.\n1. An animal that barks\na.\n2. Used for writing\nb.\n3. Comes from chicken\nc.\n4. The father of your mother\nd.\nor father\n5. A dish used for holding\ne.\nliquids often with handle\n\nPDF page 97\nA. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\nsentences/passage. Then, answer the questions below.\nChoose the letter of the correct answer.\n1. (Read Aloud) “My Home” This is my home. We have\ntables and chairs in our home. We have rooms and beds\ninn our home. We have the kitchen and the comfort rooms\ntoo. What is the story about?\na. My Garden\nb. My Home\nc. My Kitchen\n2. (Read Aloud) “My Toys” These are my toys. My mother\nand father gives it to me! I can name my favorite toys. “My\nparents gave me something I can throw and catch. It’s\nround and bouncy. What is it?”\na. Kite\nb. Ball\nc. Doll\nd. Teddy Bear\n\nPDF page 98\n3. (Read Aloud) “Our Tools” This is our tools. We have\nshovel and rake. We have to take care of our tools. Tools\nare very important for us. What is the main idea of the\nstory?\na. Tools are fun\nb. Tools are useful and we should take care of\nthem\nc. Tools are expensive\n4. (Read Aloud) “My Pets” These are my pets. I will take\ncare of my pets. I will give them food. I love my pets.\nWrite T if it is true and F if it is false.\n______ A dog can bark.\n______ A fish can fly in the sky\n5. (Read Aloud) “My Things” These are my things. I will take\ncare of my things. I will keep it clean.\nWhat should you do with your things?\na. Break them\nb. Take care of them\nc. Make it tidy\nWhat does “keep it clean” mean?\na. Make it dirty\nb. Make it new\nc. Make it tidy\n\nPDF page 99\n6. (Read Aloud) “My Family” This is my family. My mother\nand my father. My brother and my sister. And our baby\nboy. Who is in the family?\na. Friends\nb. Relatives\nc. Mother, Father, Brother, Sister, and Baby\n7. (Read Aloud) “My Food” These are the foods I eat.\nMy father buys them for me. My mother cook these for\nme. Who cooks the food in the story?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Friend\n8. “I love to play with my toy on the water. It has a sail\nand helps me pretend I’m a sailor. What am I playing\nwith?\na. Car\nb. Train\nc. Boat\nd. Yoyo\n\nPDF page 100\nPOST TEST (Activity 1-15)\nA. Vocabulary Development\nInstructions: Draw a line to match the words in Column A\nwith their meanings/uses /color in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Librarian\na. Its color is orange\n2. Swing\nb. A container for waste\n3. Trash can\nc. Takes care of sick or\ninjured people in a\nhospital or clinic\n\nPDF page 101\nd. A seat hanging from c\n4. Nurse\nropes or chains that\nmoves back and forth\n5. Building\ne. A hard board used for\ncutting\ngoods\n6. . Chopping board\nf. A structure with a roof\nand walls, such as a house\nor\nSchool.\n7. Pencil\ng. Used to carrying things.\n8. Bag\nh. Cooked bananas\non a stick\n9. Carrot\ni. Used for writing.\n\nPDF page 102\n10. Banana cue\nj. A person who\nworks in a library\nA. Listening Comprehension\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\nsentences/passage.. Then, answer the questions below.\nCircle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. (Read Aloud) “Our Tools” This is our tools. We have\nshovel and rake. We have to take care of our tools. Tools\nare very important for us. What is the main idea of the\nstory?\na. Tools are fun\nb. Tools are useful and we should take care of\nthem\nc. Tools are expensive\n2. (Read Aloud) “My Toys” These are my toys. My mother\nand father gives it to me! I can name my favorite toys. “My\nparents gave me something I can throw and catch. It’s\nround and bouncy. What is it?”\na. Kite\nb. Ball\nc. Doll\nd. Teddy Bear\n\nPDF page 103\n3. (Read Aloud) “My Home” This is my home. We have\ntables and chairs in our home. We have rooms and beds\nin our home. We have the kitchen and the comfort rooms\ntoo. What is the story about?\na. My Garden\nb. My Home\nc. My Kitchen\n4. (Read Aloud) “My Food” These are the foods I eat. My\nfather buys them for me. My mother cook these for me.\nWho cooks the food in the story?\na. Father\nb, Mother\nc. Friend\n5. (Read Aloud) “My Things” These are my things. I will take\ncare of my things. I will keep it clean. What should you do\nwith your things?\na. Break them\nb. Take care of them\nc. Make it tidy\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[95, 96, 97, 98, 99, 100, 101, 102, 103]','assets/images/level5/g1/p095-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(178,12,1100,'Pre-test','Pre-test (Lessons 1–10)','Show what you already know about these words and stories.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nPre-test (Lessons 1–10) · module PDF pages 5, 6, 7, 8, 9\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 5\nPretest: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nVOCABULARY PRETEST (15 ITEMS)\nDirections: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the underlined word.\n1. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n2. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To fall to the ground\nc) To hide\n3. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Bad smell\nb) No smell\nc) Good smell\n4. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Harmful things\nb) Things that help us grow\nc) Toys for us to play\n5. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Feeling sleepy\nc) Full of energy\n6. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n7. Fruits can taste sour or sweet. What does sour mean?\na) Not sweet\nb) Too salty\nc) Very cold\n\nPDF page 6\n8. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n9. Herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Ordinary\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Special or amazing\n10. Herbs can cure much illness. What does illness mean?\na) A sickness\nb) A birthday\nc) A school subject\n11. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that are broken\nc) Things that disappear\n12. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?\na) To ignore\nb) To look and listen carefully\nc) To run away\n13. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Helping nicely\nb) Playing in a mean or silly way\nc) Sleeping quietly\n14. The animals swim under the deep blue sea. What does deep mean?\na) Very shallow\nb) Very far down\nc) Very noisy\n15. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) Only in one place\nb) Not in many places\nc) In many places all around\n\nPDF page 7\nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nonly )\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because\nthey make places look bright and lovely.”\n1. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they are loud\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they taste sweet\n2. What do flowers give?\na) A good smell\nb) A loud noise\nc) A sour taste\n\nPDF page 8\nTeacher reads:\n“Vegetables help our body because they have nutrients. They keep us strong, active, and\nhealthy.”\n3. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Toys\nb) Nutrients\nc) Smoke\n4. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us sleepy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us noisy\nTeacher reads:\n“Fruits can taste sweet or sour. They help us stay healthy and give us vitamins.”\n5. How do fruits taste?\na) Sweet or sour\nb) Salty\nc) Bitter\n6. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\nTeacher reads:\n“Trees give us clean air. Birds live in trees because they are safe and high.”\n7. What do trees give us?\na) Dirty air\nb) Clean air\nc) Hot air\n8. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are noisy\nc) Trees are cold\nTeacher reads:\n“Some herbs are used to help sick people feel better. Herbs can cure small illnesses.”\n9. What can herbs do?\na) Make cars move\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make people laugh\n\nPDF page 9\n10. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people\nb) Robots\nc) Trees\nTeacher reads:\n“Many animals live on land. Some help farmers by carrying heavy loads or guarding the farm.”\n11. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Horse\nb) Whale\nc) Lobster\n12. Where do these animals live?\na) In the sea\nb) On land\nc) In the sky\nTeacher reads:\n“Woodland animals like squirrels and tarsiers live among trees. Some hide when they see people.”\n13. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They swim\nc) They fly to the sea\nTeacher reads:\n“In the meadow, we see butterflies, bees, and birds. They fly around flowers.”\n14. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They swim\nb) They fly around flowers\nc) They dig tunnels\nTeacher reads:\n“In the forest, animals like monkeys and deer hide among the trees. In the sea, animals like\ndolphins and whales swim together.”\n15. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Deer and monkeys\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Pigs and cows\nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[5, 6, 7, 8, 9]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(179,12,2100,'Pre-test','Comprehensive Pre-test (Lessons 11–20)','Show what you already know about these words and stories.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nComprehensive Pre-test (Lessons 11–20) · module PDF pages 10, 11, 12, 13, 14\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 10\nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20)\nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct answer.\n1. We use a blender to:\na) Wash plates\nb) Make juice\nc) Cook rice\n2. A television is used for:\na) Baking\nb) Watching shows\nc) Watering plants\n3. A pillow is used for:\na) Sleeping comfortably\nb) Cooking food\nc) Writing letters\n\nPDF page 11\n4. Soap is used for:\na) Cleaning the body\nb) Sweeping the floor\nc) Cutting paper\n5. A car is found in the:\na) Garden\nb) Garage\nc) Bedroom\n6. A mountain is:\na) A tall landform\nb) A body of water\nc) A type of house\n7. A pond is:\na) A small body of water\nb) A large sea\nc) A mountain\n8. Gold is a type of:\na) Clothing\nb) Mineral\nc) Food\n9. A truck is used to:\na) Fly in the sky\nb) Carry heavy goods\nc) Swim in water\n10. Boracay Island is famous for its:\na) Snow\nb) White sand beach\nc) Tall buildings\n11. A soap dish is used to:\na) Store soap\nb) Plant flowers\nc) Keep toys\n12. A wardrobe is used to store:\na) Clothes\nb) Food\nc) Books\n13. A plateau is:\na) A flat land higher than the land around it\nb) A body of water\nc) A small hill\n\nPDF page 12\n14. A funnel is used for:\na) Pouring liquids easily\nb) Playing music\nc) Carrying books\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Land\nb) Water\nc) Rails\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION (15 items)\nTeacher reads the passages assigned to each lesson.\nBased on Lesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The stove cooks\nvegetables and the rice cooker cooks’ rice. Plates and utensils are for eating.”\n16. What should we do in the kitchen?\na) Make it messy\nb) Keep it clean\nc) Leave water everywhere\n17. What do we put in the blender?\na) Rice\nb) Fruits\nc) Plates\nBased on Lesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the windows and a\nbookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do we sit?\na) Bookshelf\nb) Sofa\nc) Table\nBased on Lesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net protects from\ninsects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”\n\nPDF page 13\n19. What protects us from insects?\na) Blanket\nb) Mosquito net\nc) Curtain\n20. Where do we keep clothes?\na) Wardrobe\nb) Table\nc) Floor\nBased on Lesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and poured into a\nbucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What do we use to wash hair?\na) Soap\nb) Shampoo\nc) Comb\n22. What do we step on after bathing?\na) Carpet\nb) Bath mat\nc) Soap dish\nBased on Lesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer help fix small\nparts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What lifts the car?\na) Hammer\nb) Trolley jack\nc) Wheel\n24. What tool is used to fix screws?\na) Screwdriver\nb) Funnel\nc) Pliers\nBased on Lesson 16 – Landforms\nTeacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide and flat. A\nshoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. What landform is tall?\na) Mountain\n\nPDF page 14\nb) Hill\nc) Basin\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Desert\nb) Shoreline\nc) Glacier\nBased on Lesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) Lake and pond\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) River and spring\n28. What should we keep clean?\na) Land\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Cars\nBased on Lesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Toys\nb) Treasure\nc) Houses\n30. Which mineral is mentioned?\na) Plastic\nb) Gold\nc) Wood\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[10, 11, 12, 13, 14]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(180,12,3201,'Activity 1','Flowers','Listen, learn and use new words about flowers.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nFlowers · module PDF pages 18, 19, 20\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 18\nPlants around Me\nThis is my garden.\nI\'ll plant flowers, vegetables, and grains.\nHere are the seeds of trees and herbs.\nThe sun will shine; the rain will fall.\nThe seeds will sprout, up tall.\n\nPDF page 19\nActivity 1- Flowers\nFlowers\nFlowers are the beauty of nature.\nThey grow and bloom in different colors.\nThey gave us fragrant odor.\nFlowers are wonderful.\nOrchids\nDahlia\nRose\nSampaguita\nSunflower Sampaguita Tulips\nYellow Plumeria\nChrysanthemum\nAster\n\nPDF page 20\nActivity 1A: Assessment\nA. Vocabulary (5 items)\nLesson 1A: Assessment\nDirections: Match the word with its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud the\nwords and meanings.)\n1. Beauty\na. Smells good\n2. Bloom\nb. Something nice to see\n3. Color\nc. To open like a flower\n4. Fragrant\nd. A shade like red, blue, or yellow\n5. Wonderful\ne. Very nice or amazing\nLesson 1B: Assessment\nB. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully to the teacher as the story is read aloud. Then\nanswer the questions.\n1. What is the beauty of nature in the story?\na. Trees\nb. flowers\nc. clouds\n2. What do flowers do?\na. They sleep\nb. They grow and bloom\nc. They jump\n3. Flowers bloom in different ______\n.\na. Colors\nb. sizes\nc. sounds\n4. What do flowers give us?\na. A fragrant odor\nb. A loud noise\nc. A bright light\n5. How does the story describe flowers?\na. Ugly\nb. wonderful\nc. scary\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[18, 19, 20]','assets/images/level5/g2/p018-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(181,12,4202,'Activity 2','Vegetables','Listen, learn and use new words about vegetables.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nVegetables · module PDF pages 21, 22\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 21\nActivity 2- Vegetables\nVegetables in our garden.\nLegumes, leafy vegetables and grains\nThey give nutrients to our body and brains,\nTo keep us active and healthy mind\ncarrots\ncabbage\nradish\nlettuce\nbroccoli\ncauliflower\npotatoes\ntomato\nbean\nstring bean\n\nPDF page 22\nActivity 2 A: Assessment\nA. Matching Type: In column A is the picture of vegetables. In column B\nis the name of the vegetables. Match column A and B by\nconnecting it with a line.\nA. Picture of vegetables\nB. Name of vegetables\n1.\na. carrots\n2.\nb. stringbeans\n3.\nc. tomato\n4.\nd. potato\n5.\ne. cabbage\nActivity 2B: Assessment\nStory for the teacher to read:\nVegetables\nVegetables in our garden. Legumes, leafy and grains. They give nutrients to\nour body and brains, to keep us active and healthy mind.\nDirections: Listen carefully to the story. Then answer the questions.\nA. Listening and Vocabulary Questions (5 items)\n1. Where can we find the vegetables in the story?\na. in the garden\nb. in the store\nc. in the forest\n2. Which of the following is a kind of vegetable mentioned in the story?\na. Fruits b. legumes c. candies\n3. What do vegetables give to our body and brain?\na. Toys\nb. nutrients\nc. noise\n4. Why are nutrients important for us?\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[21, 22]','assets/images/level5/g2/p021-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
