(189,12,12210,'Activity 10','Animals in the Sea','Listen, learn and use new words about animals in the sea.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nAnimals in the Sea · module PDF pages 38, 39\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 38\nActivity 10- Animals in the Sea\nAnimals in the Sea\nThe fish in the sea.\nGo swimming and swimming.\nUnder the deep blue sea.\nDolphins and whales are friends of me.\nshark\nwhale\ndolphin\nlobster\nsquid\ncrab\nstarfish\nshrimps\nshells\n\nPDF page 39\nActivity 10 Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson: Animals in the Sea\nInstructions for Teacher:\n1. Read the story aloud slowly to the students.\n2. Ask the students to listen carefully.\n3. Complete the tasks below based on what they hear.\nPart 1: Vocabulary Matching\nDirections: Match the animal with the correct picture or word. Draw a line to\nmatch.\nWord\nPicture/Option\n1. dolphin\ndolphin / whale / shark\n2. whale\nwhale /\nfish /\ncrab\n3. shark\nshark /\ndolphin / lobster\n4. lobster\nlobster / crab /\nsquid\nsquid /\nlobster / crab\n5. squid\ncrab /\nsquid /\nfish\n6. crab\nstarfish / shells / shrimps\n7. starfish\nshrimps / starfish / shells\n8. shrimps\nshells /\nshrimps / starfish\n9. shells\nPart 2: Listening Comprehension Questions\nDirections: Listen to the story and answer the questions.\n1. Which animals are friends of the speaker?\na)\na) Shark and whale\nb)\nb) Dolphins and whale\nc) Fish and crab\n2. c) Fish and crab Where do the animals in the story live?\na) In the sky\nb)\na) In the sky b) On the land\nc)\nc) Under the deep blue sea\nWhich animals did you hear in the story? Circle all that apply.\nfish, dolphin, whale, shark, lobster, squid, crab, starfish, shrimps, shells\nPart 3: Fillin the Blanks\nDirections: Fill in the missing words from the story.\n1. Directions: The on the sea. Fill in the missing words from the story.\n2. Go and swim.\n3. Under the deep sea.\n4. and are friends of me.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & 