(193,12,16214,'Activity 14','Things Found in the Bathroom','Listen, learn and use new words about things found in the bathroom.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nThings Found in the Bathroom · module PDF pages 47, 48\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 47\n14:\nLesson 14:\nThings Found in the Bath Room\nIf you want to shower\nDon’t forget to bring towel.\nUse soap and shampoo\nBrush and comb are set for you.\nbath mat\npaper\nshampoo\ntoilet paper\nbucket\nsoap dish\nsoap\nbath cup\ncomb bath cup brush\n\nPDF page 48\nFormative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 14: Things Found in the Bathroom\nPart |: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: bath mat, toilet paper, shampoo, soap, comb, brush, bucket,\nbath cup, soap dish\n1. bath cup, soap dish We use to wash our hair.\na)\na) shampoo b) comb c) bucket\n2. We place the soap ona .\na)\na) brush b) soap dish c) bath mat\n3. After taking a bath, we stand on the SO We will not slip.\na)\nb) toilet paper\na) bath mat b) toilet paper c) soap\n4. We use a to comb and fix our hair.\na)\na) brush b) comb c) bath cup\nfill\n______.\n5. When we need water for bathing, we can fill a\na)\nc) toilet paper\na) bucket b) shampoo c) toilet paper\nPart Il: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n\"If\ntowel.\n\"If you want to shower, don\'t forget to bring your towel. Use soap and\nhair.\nis\nin\nbathing, you may step on the bath mat so the floor will not get wet. You\nis\nWater is scooped using a bath cup and poured into the bucket. After\nwill\nbathing, you may step on the bath mat so the floor will not get wet. You\nToilet\nis\nin\ncan brush your hair using a brush or a comb. Toilet paper is also found in the\nyourself\nbathroom for keeping yourself clean.\"\nWhere do we keep the soap?\na) In the bucket b) On the soap dish c) In the bath cup\n7. What do we use to clean our hair?\na)\nc) toilet paper\na) shampoo b) brush c) toilet paper\n8. What helps keep the floor from getting wet?\na)\na) bath cup b) bath mat c) comb\n9. What can we use fo fix our hair after bathing?\na)\na) blanket b) towel c) brush or comb\n10. What do we use for cleaning ourselves in the bathroom?\na)\na) toilet paper b) bath mat c) bucket\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[47, 48]','assets/images/level5/g2/p047-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(194,12,17215,'Activity 15','Things Found in the Garage','Listen, learn and use new words about things found in the garage.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nThings Found in the Garage · module PDF pages 49, 50\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 49\nLesson 15- Things Found in the Garage\nThings Found in the Garage\nDo you really want to shop?\nOn the garage you can stop.\nPark there safely.\nTo keep you and your car safety.\ncar\nengine oil\nwheel\ncan\npliers screw driver\nfunnel\nhammer\ntrolley jack\n\nPDF page 50\nFormative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 15: Things Found in the Garage\nPart |: Vocabulary (5 items)\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: car, engine oil, wheel, petrol can, pliers, screwdriver, trolley\njack, funnel, hammer\nA ______\nis used for fixing or turning screws.\na)\nA is used for fixing or turning screws. a) wheel lb) screwdriver c) funnel\n2. The helps the car move on the road.\na)\na) wheel b) hammer C) pliers\n3. A holds fuel that can be used for a car.\na) petrol can\nb) trolley jack\nc) engine oil\na) petrol can b) trolley jack c) engine oil We use a to make pouring liquid easier.\na)\na) funnel b) car c) hammer\n______ lift\ntire.\n5. A helps liff a car when changing a tire.\na) pliers\nb) trolley jack\nc) engine oil\nPart Il: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\nis\n\"In the garage, we can find many tools and things for the car. A car is parked\noil\nsafely inside the garage. Wheels help the car move, while engine oil keeps\nis\nfuel.\nlike\nthe engine running smoothly. There is a petrol can for storing fuel. Tools like a\npliers,\nhammer, pliers, and a screwdriver are used for fixing small parts. A funnel\noil\nspilling. trolley\nis\nlift\nhelps pour oil or petrol without spilling. A trolley jack is used fo lift the car when\nis\nchanging a wheel. The garage is a safe place for both the car and the\nit.\"\na) hammer b) petrol can c) funnel\na)\na) engine oil __b) petrol can c) funnel\nWhat is used to fix small parts?\na)\na) wheel 6b) hammer, pliers, and screwdriver = c) car\nlift\n8. What helps lift the car?\na) petrol can\nb) trolley jack\nc) engine oil\na) petrolcan _b) trolley jack c) engine oil What is used to store fuel?\na)\na) hammer b) petrol can c) funnel\n10. Where is the car parked safely?\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[49, 50]','assets/images/level5/g2/p049-4.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(195,12,18216,'Activity 16','Landforms','Listen, learn and use new words about landforms.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nLandforms · module PDF pages 51, 52, 53\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 51\nMe and My\nMe and My Surroundings\nGod created heaven and Earth.\nBeautiful surrounding with fresh air to breath.\nKeep our environment clean and green.\nMake our place safe to live in.\n\nPDF page 52\nLesson 16- Landforms\nLandforms\nBeyond your imagination.\nLand has different forms.\nExperience the beauty of nature.\nmountain\nvalley\nplateau\nglacier\ndesert\nhill\nbasin\nshoreline\nplain\n\nPDF page 53\nFormative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 16: Landforms\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: mountain, valley, plateau, glacier, hill, desert, basin, shoreline,\nplain\n1. A ______\nis a high landform with steep sides that is taller than a hill.\na) mountain\nb) plain\nc) shoreline\n2. A ______\nis a wide, flat area of land.\na) hill\nb) plain\nc) glacier\n3. A ______\nis a low area between mountains or hills.\na) valley\nb) plateau\nc) desert\n4. A ______\nis a large area of flat land that is higher than the land\naround it.\na) shoreline\nb) plateau\nc) basin\n5. A ______\nis a very dry place with lots of sand.\na) desert\nb) glacier\nc) hill\nPart II: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n\"The Earth has many different landforms. A mountain is tall and reaches\nhigh into the sky, while a hill is smaller and gently rounded. A valley lies\nbetween mountains and hills. A plain is a wide, flat area where many\npeople build houses and farms. A plateau is also flat but stands higher than\nthe land around it. Some places have glaciers, which are large, slow-\nmoving ice. A desert is hot and dry with very little water. The shoreline is the\nplace where land meets the water. A basin is a low area that can hold\nwater. These landforms make the Earth beautiful and exciting to explore.\"\nWhich landform is tall and reaches high into the sky?\na) hill\nb) mountain\nc) basin\n7. What landform is a low area between mountains or hills?\na)\na) valley b) shoreline c) plateau\n8. Which landform is flat and good for farms and houses?\na)\na) glacier b) plain c) desert\n9. What landform is made of slow-moving ice?\na) basin\nb) glacier\nc) hill\nWhere does the land meet the water?\na)\na) shoreline b) desert c) plateau\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[51, 52, 53]','assets/images/level5/g2/p051-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(196,12,19217,'Activity 17','Bodies of Water','Listen, learn and use new words about bodies of water.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nBodies of Water · module PDF pages 54, 55\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 54\nLesson 17- Body of Water\nBody of Water\nThe spring, falls, pond, lake and river.\nEnhancing the beauty on Earth forever.\nOcean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean and garbage free.\nocean\nsea\nriver\nstream\nspring\nfalls\nlake\npond\nditch\n\nPDF page 55\nLesson 17: Body of Water\nPart I: Vocabulary (5 items)\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct body of water that fits.\n(Teacher may show pictures of each body of water while reading.)\n1. A small body of water where frogs and fish can live is a ______\n.\na) pond\nb) ocean\nc) river\n2. A very big body of water with big waves is called the\n______.\na) sea\nb) ocean\nc) lake\n3. Water that comes from a high place and falls down is called\n______.\na) spring\nb) falls\nc) river\n4. A long body of water that flows from one place to another is a ______\n.\na) river\nb) lake\nc) pond\n5. A large body of water that is bigger than a pond but calmer than the\nsea is a ______\n.\na) lake\nb) falls\nc) ocean c) ocean\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short poem. Then answer\nthe questions.\nTeacher Reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake and river, Enhancing the beauty on Earth\nforever. Ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean and garbage\nfree.”\nQuestions:\n6. What are named in the poem that make Earth beautiful?\na) mountains\nb) bodies of water\nc) animals\n7. Which two bodies of water are described as “nice to see”?\na) lake and pond\nb) ocean and sea\nc) river and spring\n8. What should we keep clean and garbage-free?\na) the ocean and sea b) the classroom c) the trees\n9. Which body of water flows from place to place?\na) river\nb) pond c) lake\n10. Which body of water comes from the ground and is mentioned first in\nthe poem?\na) pond b) spring\nc) sea\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n