(197,12,20218,'Activity 18','Mineral Resources','Listen, learn and use new words about mineral resources.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nMineral Resources · module PDF pages 56, 57\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 56\nLesson 18- Mineral Resources\nMineral Resources\nEarth is rich in treasure.\nMore than we could ever measure.\nCoal, copper, gold and silver.\nElements on Earth layer upon layer.\ngold\nsilver\ncopper\nsalt\nlimestone\ncoal\naluminum\nsand and\nphosphate\ngravel\n\nPDF page 57\nPART A — VOCABULARY WITH PICTURES\nDirections:\nMatch the picture to the correct word. Write the letter of the correct\nanswer.\nPicture Icons\n– gold\n– silver\n– copper (use magnet icon to represent metal)\n– coal\n– salt\n– limestone\n– phosphate (fertilizer symbol\nsubstitute)\n– aluminium (aluminum can)\n– sand & gravel\nItems:\nWord List:\n1. ______\nA. Coal\n2. ______\nB. Silver\n3. ______\nC. Sand & Gravel\n4. ______\nD. Limestone\n5. ______\nE. Aluminium\n6. ______\nF. Gold\n7. ______\nG. Salt\n8. ______\nH. Phosphate\n9. ______\nI. Copper\nPART B — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the short story aloud. Story: Mineral Resources\nEarth is rich of treasure. More than we could ever measure. Coal, copper,\ngold and silver. Elements on Earth layer upon layer.\nDirections:\nListen to the story. Then answer the questions.\n1. What is the story talking about?\na. Animals\nb. Mineral resources\nc. Weather\n2. Which of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\na. Silver\nb. Coal\nc. Plastic\n3. Name one mineral you heard from the story.\na. Gold\nb. Tree\nc. Water\n4. What word in the poem means “precious things found on Earth”?\na. Treasure\nb. Rock\nc. Soil\nd. Sand\n5. What does the poem say Earth is full of?\na. Treasure\nb. Food\nc. Water only\nPART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections: Use the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: gold • coal • silver • copper\nPeople use to make jewelry.\nto make jewelry.\n2. Many machines use wires.\nis black and used for fuel.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[56, 57]','assets/images/level5/g2/p056-5.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(198,12,21219,'Activity 19','Transportation','Listen, learn and use new words about transportation.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nTransportation · module PDF pages 58, 59\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 58\nTransportation\nLesson 19- Transportation\nIn the street you can see.\nBuses, cars and taxi.\nIn the air there is a plane.\nOn the rails there is a train.\ntruck\nvan\nambulance\ntrain\ntaxi\nbicycle\nboat\nairplane\nship\n\nPDF page 59\nGRADE 2 FORMATIVE ASSESSMENT\nLesson 19 —- Transportation\nPART A — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the short story aloud. Story: Transportation\nIn the street you can see. Buses, cars and taxi. In the air there is a plane. On\nthe rails there is a train.\nDirections:\nListen carefully to the story and answer the questions.\nWhere can you see buses, cars, and taxis?\na. In the street\nb. In the air\nc. On the rails\na. In the street b. In the air c. On the rails What travels in the air?\na. Train\nb. Plane\nc. Boat\nWhat moves on the rails?\na. Car b. Train c. Truck What moves on the rails?\nWhich of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\na. Bicycle b. Taxi c. Plane\nName one vehicle you heard in the story.\na. Car b. Tree c. Flower d.Sand Name one vehicle you heard in the story.\nPART B — VOCABULARY WITH PICTURES\nDirections: Match the picture to the correct word. Write the letter of the\ncorrect answer.\nPicture Icons :\n– truck\n– van\n– ambulance\n– bicycle\n— truck — ambulance — bicycle\n— train — taxi — boat — ship\n– train\n– taxi\n– boat\n– ship\n– airplane\nItems:\nWord List:\n1. ______\nA. Truck\n2. ______\nB. Van\n3. ______\nC. Ambulance\n4. ______\nD. Bicycle\n5. ______\nE. Train\n6. ______\nF. Taxi\n7. ______\nG. Boat\n8. ______\nH. Ship\n9. ______\nI. Airplane\nPART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections: Use the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: bicycle • train • airplane • truck\n1. People ride a to move around short distances.\n2. A travels on tracks.\nAn ______\nflies in the sky.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a