oking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[60, 61, 62]','assets/images/level5/g2/p060-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(200,12,23300,'Post-test','Post-test (Lessons 1–10)','Show how much your listening and vocabulary have grown.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nPost-test (Lessons 1–10) · module PDF pages 64, 65, 66, 67\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 64\nPOSTTEST: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nPart I: Vocabulary (15 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the\nunderlined word.\n1. Herbs can cure many illness. What does illness mean?\na) Birthday\nb) A sickness\nc) School subject\n2. Fruits can taste sweet or sour. What does sour mean?\na) Very cold\nb) Not sweet\nc) Too salty\n3. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n4. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) In many places all around\nb) Only in one place\nc) Not in many places\n5. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n6. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Full of energy\nc) Feeling sleepy\n7. Some herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Special or amazing\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Ordinary\n8. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?\n\nPDF page 65\na) To look and listen carefully\nb) To run away\nc) To ignore\n9. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that disappear\nc) Things that are broken\n10. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n11. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Things that help us grow\nb) Toys for us to play\nc) Harmful things\n12. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Playing in a mean or silly way\nb) Helping nicely\nc) Sleeping quietly\n13. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Good smell\nb) Bad smell\nc) No smell\n14. Fruits give vitamins that help us grow strong.\na) Weak\nb) Full of energy and healthy\nc) Sleepy\n15. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To hide\nc) To fall to the ground\n( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (15 items)\nonly)\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads the passage or question.\nChoose the correct answer.\n\nPDF page 66\n16. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they taste sweet\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they are loud\n17. What do flowers give?\na) A loud noise\nb) A good smell\nc) A sour taste\n18. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us noisy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us sleepy\n19. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Smoke\nb) Toys\nc) Nutrients\n20. How do fruits taste?\na) Salty\nb) Bitter\nc) Sweet or sour\n21. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\n22. What do trees give us?\na) Hot air\nb) Clean air\nc) Dirty air\n23. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are cold\nc) Trees are noise\nLesson 5 – Herbs (Items 24–25)\n24. What can herbs do?\na) Make people laugh\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make cars move\n25. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people\n\nPDF page 67\nb) Robots\nc) Trees\n26. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Whale\nb) Lobster\nc) Horse\n27. Where do these animals live?\na) On land\nb) In the sea\nc) In the sky\n28. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They fly to the sea\nc) They swim\n29. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They fly around flowers\nb) They dig tunnels\nc) They swim\n30. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Pigs and cows\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Deer and monkeys\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[64, 65, 66, 67]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(201,12,24300,'Post-test','Comprehensive Post-test (Lessons 11–20)','Show how much your listening and vocabulary have grown.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 2\nComprehensive Post-test (Lessons 11–20) · module PDF pages 68, 69, 70, 71, 72\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 68\nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20)\nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct answer.\n1. A blender is used to:\na) Cook rice\nb) Wash plates\nc) Make juice\n2. We use a television to:\na) Water plants\nb) Watch shows\nc) Bake food\n3. A pillow is mainly for:\na) Writing letters\nb) Sleeping comfortably\nc) Cooking meals\n\nPDF page 69\n4. Soap is used to:\na) Cut paper\nb) Sweep the floor\nc) Clean the body\n5. You can find a car in the:\na) Bedroom\nb) Garage\nc) Garden\n6. A mountain is:\na) A body of water\nb) A type of house\nc) A tall landform\n7. A pond is:\na) A mountain\nb) A large sea\nc) A small body of water\n8. Gold is an example of a:\na) Mineral\nb) Food\nc) Clothing\n9. A truck is helpful for:\na) Flying in the sky\nb) Swimming in the ocean\nc) Carrying heavy goods\n10. Boracay Island is known for its:\na) Tall buildings\nb) White sand beach\nc) Snow\n11. A soap dish is used to:\na) Keep toys\nb) Store soap\nc) Grow plants\n12. We keep our clothes in the:\na) Bookshelf\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Refrigerator\n13. A plateau is:\na) A body of water\nb) A flat land higher than the land around it\nc) A small hill\n\nPDF page 70\n14. A funnel helps us:\na) Carry books\nb) Pour liquids easily\nc) Play music\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Rails\nb) Land\nc) Water\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the passages before learner’s answer.\nLesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The\nstove cooks vegetables, and the rice cooker cooks rice. Plates and utensils are for\neating.”\n16. What must we do in the kitchen?\na) Keep it clean\nb) Spill water everywhere\nc) Make it messy\n17. What do we put inside the blender?\na) Plates\nb) Rice\nc) Fruits\nLesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the\nwindows and a bookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do people sit in the living room?\na) Sofa\nb) Table\nc) Bookshelf\nLesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net\nprotects from insects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”\n\nPDF page 71\n19. What protects us from insects?\na) Curtain\nb) Blanket\nc) Mosquito net\n20. Where are clothes stored?\na) Floor\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Table\nLesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and\npoured into a bucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What is used to wash the hair?\na) Comb\nb) Shampoo\nc) Soap\n22. What do we step on after taking a bath?\na) Soap dish\nb) Carpet\nc) Bathmat\nLesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer\nhelp fix small parts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What tool lifts the car?\na) Wheel\nb) Hammer\nc) Trolley jack\n24. Which tool fixes screws?\na) Pliers\nb) Screwdriver\nc) Funnel\nLesson 16 – Landforms\n\nPDF page 72\nTeacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide\nand flat. A shoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. Which landform is tall?\na) Basin\nb) Hill\nc) Mountain\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Glacier\nb) Shoreline\nc) Desert\nLesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are\nnice to see. Keep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) River and spring\nb) Lake and pond\nc) Ocean and sea\n28. What should be kept clean?\na) Cars\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Land\nLesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Treasure\nb) Houses\nc) Toys\n30. Which mineral is mentioned in the poem?\na) Wood\nb) Gold\nc) Plastic\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 7\n7 \n \n \n \nVOCABULARY PRETEST ( ANSWER KEY) \n1. b \n2. a \n3. c \n4. b \n5. c \n6. a \n7. a \n8. a \n9. c \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. b \n14. b \n15. c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 \nonly ) \nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then \nchoose the correct answer. \nTeacher reads: \n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because \nthey make places look bright and lovely.” \n1. Why do people like flowers? \na) Because they are loud \nb) Because they look bright and lovely \nc) Because they taste sweet \n2. What do flowers give? \na) A good smell \nb) A loud noise \nc) A sour taste\nPDF page 10\n10 \n \n \n \nANSWER KEY \n1. b \n2. a \n3. b \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. a \n9. b \n10. a \n11. a \n12. b \n13. a \n14. b \n15. b \nCOMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. We use a blender to: \na) Wash plates \nb) Make juice \nc) Cook rice \n2. A television is used for: \na) Baking \nb) Watching shows \nc) Watering plants \n3. A pillow is used for: \na) Sleeping comfortably \nb) Cooking food \nc) Writing letters\nPDF page 15\n15 \n \n \n \n10-b \n11-a \n12-a \n13-a \n14-a \n15-b \nListening Comprehension \n16-b \n17-b \n18-b \n19-b \n20-a \n21-b \n22-b \n23-b \n24-a \n25-a \n26-b \n27-b \n28-b \n29-b \n30-b\nPDF page 68\n68 \n \n \n \n11. a \n12. a \n13. a \n14. b \n15. a \nListening Comprehension: \n16. b \n17. b \n18. b \n19. c \n20. c \n21. a \n22. b \n23. a \n24. b \n25. a \n26. c \n27. a \n28. a \n29. a \n30. b \n \nCOMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20) \nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension \nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items) \nDirections: Choose the correct answer. \n1. A blender is used to: \na) Cook rice \nb) Wash plates \nc) Make juice \n2. We use a television to: \na) Water plants \nb) Watch shows \nc) Bake food \n3. A pillow is mainly for: \na) Writing letters \nb) Sleeping comfortably \nc) Cooking meals\nPDF page 73\n73 \n \n \n \n⬛\n   ANSWER KEY \nVOCABULARY \n1-c \n2-b \n3-b \n4-c \n5-b \n6-c \n7-c \n8-a \n9-c \n10-b \n11-b \n12-b \n13-b \n14-b \n15-c \nLISTENING COMPREHENSION \n16-a \n17-c \n18-a \n19-c \n20-b \n21-b \n22-c \n23-c \n24-b \n25-c \n26-b \n27-c \n28-b \n29-a \n30-b','[68, 69, 70, 71, 72]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(202,13,1100,'Pre-test','Pre-test','Show what you already know about these words and stories.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nPre-test · module PDF pages 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 6\nSET A\nPRE-TEST Day 1-10 grade 9 to 10\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write its\nletter on the line.\nSection 1: Reading Comprehension\n______ 1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n______ 2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n______ 3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n______ 4. Where did the magical treehouse take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n______ 5. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n______ 6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house\n\nPDF page 7\n______ 7. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n______ 8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n______ 9. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n______ 10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n______ 11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n______ 12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\n______ 13. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n______ 14. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n\nPDF page 8\n______ 15. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n______ 16. Who was talking to each other in \"Summer Fun\"?\na. Lita and Lito\nb. Lina and Lino\nc. Lina and Leo\n______ 17. What were they talking about?\na. what to do during the summer\nb. what to have during the summer\nc. what to wear during the summer\n______ 18. The children in the story could be ______\na. brother and sister\nb. neighbors\nc. cousins\n______ 19. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na. pick flowers\nb. pick star apples\nc. go swimming\n______ 20. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na. doing something in the summer\nb. doing something in the house\nc. doing something that we like\n______ 21. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na. picking flowers\nb. cleaning up\nc. swimming\n______ 22. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain\n\nPDF page 9\n______ 23. What does Nina want to do?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain\n______ 24. Who wants to play tag?\na. Ria\nb. Nina\nc. Ria and Nina\n______ 25. What is \"tag?\"\na. a card game\nb. a video game\nc. a running game\n______ 26. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na. Something might break\nb. Someone might get tired\nc. Something might get lost\n______ 27. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na. careless\nb. careful\nc. curious\n______ 28. Who was Curly?\na. a dog\nb. a doll\nc. a cat\n______ 29. Who gave Curly to Miriam?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n______ 30. Where does Uncle Max live?\na. Cebu\nb. Manila\nc. New York\n______ 31. On what occasion was Curly given?\na. birthday\nb. Christmas\nc. graduation\n\nPDF page 10\n______ 32. Who helped Miriam open the box?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n______ 33. What words talk about the box?\na. big and light\nb. big and heavy\nc. small and light\n______ 34. What words talk about Curly’s mouth?\na. red\nb. pink\nc. yellow\n______ 35. What was Curly’s dress made of?\na. silk\nb. lace\nc. cotton\n______ 36. What word talks about her hair?\na. curly\nb. brown\nc. straight\n______ 37. What can Curly do?\na. talk\nb. sing\nc. walk\n______ 38. Where does Victor live?\na. in the city\nb. on a farm\nc. near the sea\n______ 39. Which word tells about their house?\na. nipa\nb. cement\nc. wooden\n______ 40. Who is Victor’s sister?\na. Nina\nb. Nora\nc. Nida\n\nPDF page 11\n______ 41. Who is older, Victor or Nora?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Cannot be determined\n______ 42. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na. 3\nb. 4\nc. 5\n______ 43. Which one do they NOT have?\na. cow\nb. horse\nc. carabao\n______ 44. Who takes care of the horse?\na. Victor\nb. Father\nc. Mother\n______ 45. Who takes care of the carabao?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Father\n______ 46. Who takes care of the chickens?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Mother\n______ 47. Which one does Nora take care of?\na. goat\nb. chickens\nc. carabao\nSection 2: Vocabulary\n______ 48. In \"The Story of the First Thanksgiving,\" what does the word harvest mean?\na) a big ship\nb) the food that is gathered from crops\nc) a type of celebration\nd) a difficult time\n______ 49. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word nectar mean?\na) a sweet liquid found in flowers\n\nPDF page 12\nb) the stem of a plant\nc) the journey a seed takes\nd) the roots of a flower\n______ 50. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word sprouted mean?\na) to be blown by the wind\nb) to be planted in a field\nc) to start to grow\nd) to collect food\n\nPDF page 14\nSET B\nPRE-TEST Day 11-20 Grade 3-4\nInstructions: Read each question carefully and choose the best answer. Encircle the\nletter of your choice.\nVocabulary\n1. What is the best definition for coax?\na. to force someone\nb. to persuade gently\nc. to ignore someone\nd. to argue with someone\n2. If someone is distrustful, they are:\na. Very confident\nb. Lacking trust\nc. Extremely happy\nd. Easily persuaded\n3. The word despise most nearly means:\na. To admire greatly\nb. To dislike very much\nc. To feel sorry for\nd. To be jealous of\n4. A person who is arrogant:\na. Thinks they are better than others\nb. Is very shy and quiet\nc. Is kind to everyone\nd. Works very hard\n5. To apologize means to:\na. Express regret for a mistake\nb. Celebrate a victory\nc. Make a formal promise\nd. Give someone a gift\nGrammar and Writing\n6. Which sentence is punctuated correctly?\na. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\n\nPDF page 15\nb. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nc. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nd. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice\".\n7. What is the simple predicate (verb) in this sentence: \"The greedy lion chased the\ndeer.\"\na. The greedy lion\nb. chased\nc. the deer\nd. chased the deer\n8. Which word is an antonym for sincerity?\na. Honesty\nb. Dishonesty\nc. Friendship\nd. Kindness\n9. What part of speech is the word huge in this sentence: \"The elephant had a huge\nbody.\"?\na. Noun\nb. Verb\nc. Adjective\nd. Adverb\n10. Which sentence is written in the future tense?\na. The farmer calls his sons.\nb. The farmer called his sons.\nc. The farmer is calling his sons.\nd. The farmer will call his sons.\nReading Comprehension\nRead the short passage and answer questions 11-13.\n\"The ants were angry at the elephant for spraying them with water. They decided to\nteach him a lesson. They crept into his ears and started biting him. The elephant\ncried and apologized, learning never to trouble others again.\"\n11. Why were the ants angry?\na. The elephant stepped on their home.\nb. The elephant sprayed them with water.\nc. The elephant ate their food.\nd. The elephant ignored them.\n12. How did the ants teach the elephant a lesson?\na. They told the other animals.\nb. They bit him inside his ears.\nc. They stole his food.\nd. They sprayed him with water.\n\nPDF page 16\n13. What was the result of the ants\' action?\na. The elephant became angrier.\nb. The elephant never troubled anyone again.\nc. The elephant chased the ants away.\nd. The elephant became friends with the ants.\nLiterary Concepts\n14. The central lesson or message of a story is called the:\na. Plot\nb. Moral\nc. Setting\nd. Conflict\n15. The main problem that characters face in a story is the:\na. Solution\nb. Climax\nc. Conflict\nd. Theme\n16. \"The wind whispered through the trees\" is an example of:\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole\n17. A story that uses animals as characters to teach a lesson is called a:\na. Biography\nb. Fable\nc. Mystery\nd. Fantasy\n18. The high point or most exciting part of a story is the:\na. Exposition\nb. Rising Action\nc. Climax\nd. Falling Action\nGeneral Knowledge & Inference\n19. What is the primary purpose of a fable?\na. To explain historical events\nb. To teach a moral lesson\nc. To describe a scientific process\nd. To tell a funny story with no lesson\n20. If a character is described as \"cunning,\" they are most likely to be:\na. Honest and kind\nb. Shy and quiet\n\nPDF page 17\nc. Clever and tricky\nd. Strong and brave\n21. What is the best source to find a synonym for the word \"huge\"?\na. A dictionary\nb. A thesaurus\nc. An encyclopedia\nd. An atlas\n22. What is the term for the feeling of sadness or pity you feel for a character?\na. Empathy\nb. Sympathy\nc. Anger\nd. Joy\n23. Which of these is a complete sentence?\na. The old tortoise slowly.\nb. Challenged the hare for a race.\nc. The hare ran very fast.\nd. Under the tree for some time.\n24. What do we call the narrator of a story who is also a character in the story?\na. First-person narrator\nb. Second-person narrator\nc. Third-person narrator\nd. Omniscient narrator\n25. What is the term for a word that means the opposite of another word?\na. Synonym\nb. Antonym\nc. Homophone\nd. Homonym\nContinuing with more general items...\n26. What is the opposite meaning of the word victory?\na. Success\nb. Defeat\nc. Contest\nd. Race\n27. Which word is a noun?\na. Run\nb. Beautiful\nc. Peace\nd. Quickly\n28. The phrase \"as slow as a tortoise\" is an example of a:\na. Metaphor\nb. Simile\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole\n\nPDF page 18\n29. What is the purpose of the beginning of a story (exposition)?\na. To solve the problem\nb. To introduce characters and setting\nc. To present the most exciting action\nd. To provide the moral lesson\n30. Which of these is a theme that might be found in a fable?\na. The chemical process of photosynthesis\nb. The importance of honesty\nc. The history of ancient Rome\nd. The rules of a board game\n31. What does the prefix \"re-\" mean in the word \"rewrite\"?\na. Not\nb. Again\nc. Before\nd. After\n32. Which sentence uses correct subject-verb agreement?\na. The four sons argues.\nb. The four sons argue.\nc. The four sons is arguing.\nd. The four sons was arguing.\n33. What is the term for the actual, dictionary definition of a word?\na. Connotation\nb. Denotation\nc. Synonym\nd. Acronym\n34. In the story \"The Farmer and His Four Sons,\" what does the bundle of sticks\nsymbolize?\na. Individual strength\nb. Family quarrels\nc. Unity and strength\nd. Old age and weakness\n35. Which part of a story comes after the climax?\na. Exposition\nb. Rising Action\nc. Falling Action\nd. Introduction\n36. What is the term for a conversation between two or more characters?\na. Monologue\nb. Dialogue\nc. Narration\nd. Description\n\nPDF page 19\n37. Which word best describes the fox in \"The Fox and the Crow\"?\na. Honest\nb. Generous\nc. Cunning\nd. Brave\n38. What is the best way to identify the moral of a fable?\na. Look at the title.\nb. Find the lesson the characters learn.\nc. Identify the main character.\nd. Count the number of animals.\n39. \"He was a lion in battle.\" This is an example of a:\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Onomatopoeia\n40. Which word is a verb?\na. Decision\nb. Decisive\nc. Decide\nd. Decisively\n41. What is the term for an exaggerated statement used for effect?\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole\n42. Which of these is a compound word?\na. Therefore\nb. Sunshine\nc. Elephant\nd. Together\n43. What is the primary purpose of narrative writing?\na. To convince the reader\nb. To tell a story\nc. to explain how to do something\nd. To describe a person or place\n44. Which sentence is an opinion?\na. The hare lost the race.\nb. The tortoise has a shell.\nc. The hare is the fastest animal.\nd. The race was to the riverbank.\n45. What is the term for the feelings and ideas associated with a word (beyond its\ndictionary definition)?\na. Denotation\nb. Connotation\nc. Definition\nd. Pronunciation\n\nPDF page 20\n46. What do you call the perspective from which a story is told?\na. Plot\nb. Setting\nc. Point of View\nd. Theme\n47. Which of these is a proper noun?\na. jungle\nb. farmer\nc. Birbal\nd. son\n48. What is the best way to understand a character\'s traits?\na. Look only at their name.\nb. See what they say, do, and what others say about them.\nc. Focus only on the story\'s setting.\nd. Read the first paragraph only.\n49. What is the name for a word that describes a verb (e.g., slowly, quickly)?\na. Adjective\nb. Adverb\nc. Noun\nd. Preposition\n50. The final part of a story where the conflict is resolved is called the:\na. Climax\nb. Rising Action\nc. Resolution\nd. Introduction\nPRE-TEST ANSWER KEY\n1.B\n11.B\n21.B\n31.B\n41.D\n2. B\n12.B\n22.B\n32.B\n42.B\n3. B\n13.B\n23.C\n33.B\n43.B\n4. A\n14.B\n24.A\n34.C\n44.C\n5. A\n15.C\n25.B\n35.C\n45.B\n6. B\n16.C\n26.B\n36.B\n46.C\n7. B\n17.B\n27.C\n37.C\n47.C\n8. B\n18.C\n28.B\n38.B\n48.B\n9. C\n19.B\n29.B\n39.B\n49.B\n10. D\n20.C\n30.B\n40.C\n50.C\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. A\n42. B \n43. A \n44. B \n45. B \n46. C \n47. A \n48. B \n49. A \n50. C\nPDF page 43\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nAnswer Keys \nActivity 1: \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n \nActivity 2: \n1. c \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 3: \n1. b \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 4: \n1. b \n2. d \n3. c \n \nActivity 5: \n1.c \n2.b \n3.b \n \nActivity 6: Set A \n1. c \n2. a \n3. a \n4. b \n5. c \n6. b \n \nActivity 7: Set B \n1. a \n2. b \n3. a \n4. c \n5. a \n6. b \n \n \nActivity 9 – Set B (A Gift from Uncle) \n \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n4. b \n5. a \n6. b \n7. a \n8. b \n9. a\nPDF page 44\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \n10. c \nActivity 10 – Set A (Taking Care of Animals) \n \n1. b  \n2. a  \n3. b \n4. a \n5. b \n6. a \n7. b \n8. b \n \n9. \nC \n10. A \n \nActivity 10- Set B ( Lost and Found) \n \n1. b \n2. b \n3. c \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. c \n9. c \n10. c \n \nActivity 11 (The Banana Peeling) \n \n1. b \n2. b \n3. c \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. c \n9. c \n10. c\nPDF page 45\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nActivity 12 (The News Boy) \n \n1. b \n2. b \n3. c \n4. a \n5. c \n6. b \n7. c \n8. c \n9. c \n10. b \n \nActivity 13 (Sick Classmate) \n \n1. c \n2. a \n3. b \n4. a \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. c \n9. c \n10. b \nActivity 14 – Set A (The Kitten) \n \n1. c \n2. a \n3. a \n4. c 