(203,13,2201,'Activity 1','The Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox','Listen, learn and use new words about the mystery of the missing lunchbox.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nThe Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox · module PDF page 22\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 22\nGRADE 3 Intervention Activities\nActivity 1:\n\"The Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox\"\nSarah opened her backpack, but her lunchbox was gone! She looked\neverywhere. \"Where could it be?\" she wondered. She asked\nher friends, but no one had seen it. Suddenly, she remembered\nleaving it in the library after reading a book\nabout archaeology. She raced to the library and found it right where she left it.\nQuestions:\n1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. A\n42. B \n43. A \n44. B \n45. B \n46. C \n47. A \n48. B \n49. A \n50. C\nPDF page 43\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nAnswer Keys \nActivity 1: \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n \nActivity 2: \n1. c \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 3: \n1. b \n2. b \n3. b \n \nA