(205,13,4203,'Activity 3','The Inventor\'s Workshop','Listen, learn and use new words about the inventor\'s workshop.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nThe Inventor\'s Workshop · module PDF page 24\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 24\nActivity 3:\n\"The Inventor\'s Workshop\"\nEmily loved inventing new things. Her workshop was filled\nwith tools, wires, and gadgets. One day, she decided to\nbuild a robot that could help her with her chores. After\nmany\nattempts, she finally created a robot that could sweep, dust, and even make her\nbed. She called it \"Handy Helper.\"\nQuestions:\n1. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n2. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n3. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. A\n42. B \n43. A \n44. B \n45. B \n46. C \n47. A \n48. B \n49. A \n50. C\nPDF page 43\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nAnswer Keys \nActivity 1: \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n \nActivity 2: \n1. c \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 3: \n1. b \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 4: \n1. b \n2. d \n3. c \n \nActivity 5: \n1.c \n2.b \n3.b \n \nActivity 6: Set A \n1. c \n2. a \n3. a \n4. b \n5. c \n6. b \n \nActi