(206,13,5204,'Activity 4','The Story of the First Thanksgiving','Listen, learn and use new words about the story of the first thanksgiving.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nThe Story of the First Thanksgiving · module PDF page 25\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 25\nActivity 4:\n“The Story of the First Thanksgiving”\nLong ago, the Pilgrims came to America on a ship called the Mayflower. They\nhad a difficult time finding food. The Native Americans, like the\nWampanoag tribe, helped them learn how to grow corn\nand other crops. The next year, they had a big feast to\ncelebrate their harvest. This feast is now known as\nThanksgiving.\nVocabulary Focus: Pilgrims, Mayflower, harvest, crops, tribe\nARAL Connection: Social studies vocabulary and understanding historical events.\nQuestions:\n1. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n2. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n4. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. A\n42. B \n43. A \n44. B \n45. B \n46. C \n47. A \n48. B \n49. A \n50. C\nPDF page 43\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nAnswer Keys \nActivity 1: \n1. b \n2.