(207,13,6205,'Activity 5','The Little Seed\'s Journey','Listen, learn and use new words about the little seed\'s journey.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nThe Little Seed\'s Journey · module PDF page 26\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 26\nActivity 5:\n\"The Little Seed\'s Journey\"\nOnce upon a time, there was a little seed. The wind blew it far away from its\nparent plant. The seed landed in a field. Rain fell, and\nthe seed began to grow. It sprouted roots and a tiny\nstem.\nSoon, it became a beautiful flower. Bees came to collect\nnectar from the flower, helping it make more seeds.\nVocabulary Focus: parent, nectar, sprouted, stem, journey\nARAL Connection: Science-related vocabulary and understanding plant life cycles.\nQuestions:\n1. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n2. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n3. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. A\n42. B \n43. A \n44. B \n45. B \n46. C \n47. A \n48. B \n49. A \n50. C\nPDF page 43\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nAnswer Keys \nActivity 1: \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n \nActivity 2: \n1. c \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 3: \n1. b \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 4: \n1. b \n2. d \n3. c \n \