(209,13,8207,'Activity 7','A Rainy Day','Listen, learn and use new words about a rainy day.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nA Rainy Day · module PDF page 29\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 29\nActivity 7:\nSET B\nA RAINY DAY\nNina and Ria are looking out the window.\n“I do not like getting wet in the rain,” says Nina.\n“What can we do?” asks Ria.\n“We can play house,” says Nina.\n“Or we can play tag,” says Ria.\n“Okay, let’s play tag. You’re it!” says Nina.\nNina runs from Ria and bumps a lamp.\n“Oh no!” says Nina.\n“We must not play tag in the house.”\nQuestions\n1. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain\n2. What does Nina want to do?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. gets wet in the rain\n3. Who wants to play tag?\na. Ria\nb. Nina\nc. Ria and Nina\n4. What is \"tag?\"\na. a card game\nb. a video game\nc. a running game\n5. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na. Something might break\nb. Someone might get tired\nc. Something might get lost\n6. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na. careless\nb. careful\nc. curious\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. A\n42. B \n43. A \n44. B \n45. B \n46. C \n47. A \n48. B \n49. A \n50. C\nPDF page 43\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nAnswer Keys \nActivity 1: \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n \nActivity 2: \n1. c \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActiv