(214,13,13213,'Activity 13','A Sick Classmate','Listen, learn and use new words about a sick classmate.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nA Sick Classmate · module PDF page 34\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 34\nActivity 13:\nA SICK CLASSMATE\nOne morning, Miss Luna said to her Grade 3 class, “I got a letter\nfrom Teresa’s mother. Teresa cannot come to school. She is sick. The doctor\ntold her to stay in bed for a few days. What shall we do for Teresa?” “Let\nus visit her this afternoon,” said Linda.\n“Yes, let us visit her,” said the other children. That afternoon, the\nchildren went to visit Teresa. The girls brought her some fruits. The boys\nbrought her a can of biscuits. Miss Luna brought her some roses. Teresa was sleeping when\nthey arrived. Soon, she woke up. She was happy to see her teacher and classmates.\n1. Who is Miss Luna?\na. A nurse\nb. A mother\nc. A teacher\n2. What did she get one morning?\na. A letter\nb. A telegram\nc. A newspaper\n3. Who sent a letter?\na. Teresa\nb. Teresa’s mother\nc. Teresa’s father\n4. Why was Teresa absent?\na. She was sick.\nb. She was busy.\nc. She was away.\n5. Did a doctor treat her?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell.\n6. What did the children do?\na. They visited her.\nb. They sent flowers.\nc. They sent her letter.\n7. What did the girls bring?\na. Milk\nb. Fruits\nc. flowers\n8. What did the boys bring?\na. Fruits\nb. Roses\nc. biscuits\n9. Who brought some roses?\na. The girls\nb. The boys\nc. Miss Luna\n10. When did they visit Teresa?\na. Morning\nb. Afternoon\nc. evening\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. 