(222,13,21220,'Activity 20','The First Monkey','Listen, learn and use new words about the first monkey.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nThe First Monkey · module PDF page 42\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 42\nActivity 20:\nTHE FIRST MONKEY\nLong time ago, there was a farmer who had a wide corn field.\nHe grew big and sweet corn. One day he saw some of his corn gone.\nMany corn plants had no more fruits. He wanted to catch whoever\nstole his corn.\nThe next day he hid behind a big mango tree. He carried a\nstick. He watched and watched until he saw a man coming.\nThe man passed through a broken part of the fence. The man began to pick some corn.\nThe farmer went from behind the mango tree and walked towards the man. The man\nsaw the farmer and started to run. The farmer ran after him but he could not catch him.\nThen he threw the stick at the man’s back and became a tail. The\nman went up the tree. He became smaller and smaller until he became the monkey.\n1. When did the story happen?\na. Last year\nb. A few years ago c. a long time ago\n2. What did the farmer have?\na. A rice field\nb. a camote field\nc. a corn field\n3. What words will tell about his corn?\na. Big and sweet\nb. small and sweet c. sweet and yellow\n4. What happened to his corn?\na. was stolen\nb. destroyed by insects\nc. destroyed by the\nwind\n5. Where did the farmer hide one day?\na. up the mango tree\nb. behind the guava tree c. behind the mango\ntree\n6. What did he carry?\na. A stick\nb. Some fruits\nc. some stones\n7. Who did he see come into the corn field?\na. A dog\nb. A man\nc. a monkey\n8. What did the farmer do to the man?\na. caught him\nb. threw the stick at him\nc. beat him with\nthe stick\n9. What happened with the stick?\na. was lost\nb. was broken\nc. became a tail\n10. What happened to the man?\na. became sick\nb. became a monkey\nc. became a corn\nplant\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. A\n42. B \n43. A \n44. B \n45. B \n46. C \n47. A \n48. B \n49. A \n50. C\nPDF page 43\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nAnswer Keys \nActivity 1: \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n \nActivity 2: \n1. c \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 3: \n1. b \n2. b \n3. b \n \nActivity 4: \n1. b \n2. d \n3. c \n \nActivity 5: \n1.c \n2.b \n3.b \n \nActivity 6: Set A \n1. c \n2. a \n3. a \n4. b \n5. c \n6. b \n \nActivity 7: Set B \n1. a \n2. b \n3. a \n4. c \n5. a \n6. b \n \n \nActivity 9 – Set B (A Gift from Uncle) \n \n1. b \n2. c \n3. c \n4. b \n5. a \n6. b \n7. a \n8. b \n9. a\nPDF page 44\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \n10. c \nActivity 10 – Set A (Taking Care of Animals) \n \n1. b  \n2. a  \n3. b \n4. a \n5. b \n6. a \n7. b \n8. b \n \n9. \nC \n10. A \n \nActivity 10- Set B ( Lost and Found) \n \n1. b \n2. b \n3. c \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. c \n9. c \n10. c \n \nActivity 11 (The Banana Peeling) \n \n1. b \n2. b \n3. c \n4. b \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. c \n9. c \n10. c\nPDF page 45\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \nActivity 12 (The News Boy) \n \n1. b \n2. b \n3. c \n4. a \n5. c \n6. b \n7. c \n8. c \n9. c \n10. b \n \nActivity 13 (Sick Classmate) \n \n1. c \n2. a \n3. b \n4. a \n5. a \n6. a \n7. b \n8. c \n9. c \n10. b \nActivity 14 – Set A (The Kitten) \n \n1. c \n2. a \n3. a \n4. c \n5. b \n6. b \n7. a \n8. a \n9. a \n10. a \nActivity 14 – Set B (The Coconut) \n \n1. b \n2. b \n3. a \n4. b \n5. c \n6. b \n7. b \n8. c\nPDF page 46\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 20 \n9. b \