(223,13,22300,'Post-test','Post-test','Show how much your listening and vocabulary have grown.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 3\nPost-test · module PDF pages 48, 49, 50, 51, 52, 54, 55, 56, 57\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 48\nSET A\nPOST-TEST (Based on Days 1-10)\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write the\ncorresponding letter on your answer sheet.\n1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n4. Where did the magical tree house take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n5. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house\n7. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n9. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\n\nPDF page 49\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\nActivity 5: The Little Seed\'s Journey\n13. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n14. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n15. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n16. Who were talking to each other?\na) Lita and Lito\nb) Lina and Lino\nc) Lina and Leo\n17. What were they talking about?\na) what to do during the summer\nb) what to have during the summer\nc) what to wear during the summer\n18. The children in the story could be ______\na) brother and sister\nb) neighbors\nc) cousins\n\nPDF page 50\n19. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na) pick flowers\nb) pick star apples\nc) go swimming\n20. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na) doing something in the summer\nb) doing something in the house\nc) doing something that we like\n21. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na) picking flowers\nb) cleaning up\nc) swimming\n22. What is it that Nina does not like?\na) playing tag\nb) playing house\nc) getting wet in the rain\n23. What does Nina want to do?\na) play tag\nb) play house\nc) get wet in the rain\n24. Who wants to play tag?\na) Ria\nb) Nina\nc) Ria and Nina\n25. What is \"tag?\"\na) a card game\nb) a video game\nc) a running game\n26. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na) Something might break.\nb) Someone might get tired.\nc) Something might get lost.\n27. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na) careless\nb) careful\nc) curious\n28. Who was Curly?\na) a dog\nb) a doll\nc) a cat\n29. Who gave Curly to Miriam?\na) Father\nb) Mother\nc) Uncle Max\n30. Where does Uncle Max live?\na) Cebu\n\nPDF page 51\nb) Manila\nc) New York\n31. On what occasion was Curly given?\na) birthday\nb) Christmas\nc) graduation\n32. Who helped Miriam open the box?\na) Father\nb) Mother\nc) Uncle Max\n33. What words talk about the box?\na) big and light\nb) big and heavy\nc) small and light\n34. What words talk about Curly’s mouth?\na) red\nb) pink\nc) yellow\n35. What was Curly’s dress made of?\na) silk\nb) lace\nc) cotton\n36. What word talks about her hair?\na) curly\nb) brown\nc) straight\n37. What can Curly do?\na) talk\nb) sing\nc) walk\nActivity 10: SET A - TAKING CARE OF ANIMALS\n38. Where does Victor live?\na) in the city\nb) on a farm\nc) near the sea\n39. Which word tells about their house?\na) nipa\nb) cement\nc) wooden\n40. Who is Victor’s sister?\na) Nina\nb) Nora\nc) Nida\n41. Who is older, Victor or Nora?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Does not tell\n\nPDF page 52\n42. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na) 3\nb) 4\nc) 5\n43. Which one do they NOT have?\na) cow\nb) horse\nc) carabao\n44. Who takes care of the horse?\na) Victor\nb) Father\nc) Mother\n45. Who takes care of the carabao?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Father\n46. Who takes care of the chickens?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Mother\n47. Which one does Nora take care of?\na) goat\nb) chickens\nc) carabao\nVocabulary Focus\n48. In \"The Story of the First Thanksgiving,\" what does the\nword harvest mean?\na) a big ship\nb) a large feast\nc) the time when crops are gathered\n49. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word nectar mean?\na) a sweet liquid in flowers that bees collect\nb) the stem of a plant\nc) the journey a seed takes\n50. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word sprouted mean?\na) to be blown by the wind\nb) to be watered by the rain\nc) to start to grow\n\nPDF page 54\nSET B\nPOST-TEST (Based on Days 11-20)\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write\nthe corresponding letter on your answer sheet.\n1. What did Celso eat?\na) bananas b) mangoes c) oranges\n2. When did he eat the fruit?\na) last night b) that morning c) last week\n3. Where did he throw the peelings?\na) into the basket b) out of the window c) into the garbage can\n4. Where was Celso going?\na) to church b) to market c) to school\n5. What sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late?\na) He walked fast b) He walked slowly c) He played on the way\n6. Who stepped on the banana peelings?\na) Father b) Mother c) Celso\n7. Who saw Celso fall?\na) Father b) Mother c) Sister\n8. Who did not use the garbage can?\na) Mother b) Celso c) Sister\n9. Was Celso hurt?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n10. Which word tells about Celso?\na) polite b) kind c) truthful\n11. Where does Alfredo live?\na) in Manila b) in Naga City c) on a farm\n12. What time does the train arrive?\na) 4 o’clock b) 5 o’clock c) 6 o’clock\n13. What carries the newspapers to Naga City?\na) a car b) a truck c) a train\n14. Where do the newspapers come from?\na) Manila b) Cebu City c) Pasay City\n15. What does Alfredo do?\na) sells fruit b) sells candies c) sells newspapers\n16. How long does Alfredo sell newspapers?\na) one hour b) two hours c) three hours\n17. How much does he earn per day?\na) 5 pesos b) 75 pesos c) 100 pesos\n18. What does he do with the money?\na) gives it to mother b) buys cakes and candies c) keeps it in his piggy bank\n19. What kind of a boy is Alfredo?\na) clean b) polite c) industrious\n\nPDF page 55\n20. Are his parents poor?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n21. Who is Miss Luna?\na) nurse b) mother c) teacher\n22. What did she get one morning?\na) a letter b) a telegram c) a newspaper\n23. Who sent the letter?\na) Teresa b) Teresa’s mother c) Teresa’s father\n24. Why was Teresa absent?\na) She was sick b) She was busy c) She was away\n25. Did a doctor treat her?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n26. What did the children do?\na) visited her b) sent flowers c) sent her a letter\n27. What did the girls bring?\na) milk b) fruits c) flowers\n28. What did the boys bring?\na) fruits b) roses c) biscuits\n29. Who brought some roses?\na) girls b) boys c) Miss Luna\n30. When did they visit Teresa?\na) morning b) afternoon c) evening\n31. What time of the day was it?\na) morning b) noon c) afternoon\n32. What kind of afternoon was it?\na) rainy b) sunny c) cloudy\n33. Where was Juan going?\na) home b) school c) church\n34. What was Juan wearing?\na) hat b) sweater c) raincoat\n35. What did Juan see on the way?\na) dog b) kitten c) chick\n36. How did the kitten feel?\na) hot b) cold c) warm\n37. What did Juan feel for the kitten?\na) pity b) gladness c) happiness\n38. Where did he bring it?\na) home b) school c) in the shade\n39. Where did he put the kitten?\na) near the fire b) the table c) near the bed\n40. Did the kitten like to stay near the fire?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n41. What word tells about the coconut tree?\na) short b) tall c) small\n42. Does the coconut tree have branches?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n43. What part of the coconut tree is good for a post?\n\nPDF page 56\na) trunk b) roots c) fruits\n44. From where can we get oil?\na) coconut husk b) ripe coconut milk c) young coconut meat\n\nPDF page 57\n45. Which is good to eat?\na) coconut husk b) coconut shell c) coconut meat\n46. What part is made into doormats?\na) shell b) husk c) midribs\n47. What can be made from the midribs?\na) buttons b) brooms c) candies\n48. What part is woven into baskets?\na) husk b) shell c) leaves\n49. Which part can be made into buttons?\na) husk b) shell c) midribs\n50. What is the use of the stalk of the leaves?\na) for fuel b) for post c) for food\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 13\nPAGE  \\* MERGEFORMAT 1 \nANSWER KEY \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. C \n5. B \n6. B \n7. B \n8. B \n9. B \n10. B \n11. D \n12. C \n13. C \n14. B \n15. B \n16. C \n17. A \n18. A \n19. B \n20. C \n21. B \n22. C \n23. B \n24. A \n25. C \n26. A \n27. B \n28. B \n29. C \n30. C \n31. B \n32. A \n33. B \n34. A \n35. B \n36. A \n37. C \n38. B \n39. A \n40. B \n41. 