ie \nKill \nstart \nneglect \nKick \naccept \nLoosen \nBorn \ndie \nHalt \nCare \nneglect \nRise \nDream \ndislike \nUproot \nPress \nloosen \naccept \nMarch \nhalt \nStart \nLead \nfollow \nIdle \nHang \nrise \nMoist \nDry \nmoist \nDislike \nBusy \nidle \nFollow \n \n \n \nActivity 10: Prep Paired \n \n1. Above \n2. Across \n3. Ago \n4. Almost \n5. Outside \n6. Front \n7. East \n8. Between \n9. Center \n10. Under \n11. Beside \n12. Began\nPDF page 65\nPre Test(Activity 1-10) \nPre Test Activity (1-10) \n1. huge \n11. c \n2. clean \n12. b \n3. beach \n13. b \n4. friend \n14. c \n5. desk \n15. c \n6. pie \n16. b \n7. gift \n17. c \n8. learn \n18. b \n9. dead \n19. c \n10. above \n20. C \nPost- Test Assessment (Activity 1-10) \n1. beach \n11. b \n2. desk \n12. c \n3. gift \n13. c \n4. huge \n14. c \n5. pie \n15. b \n6. friend \n16. b \n7. dead \n17. c \n8. above \n18. c \n9. clean \n19. c \n10. learn \n20. b \nActivity 11: Fill in the Blank \n1. Body \n6. skin \n11. mouth \n2. Bill \n7. lap \n12. meat \n3. Feather \n8. eye \n4. Fingers \n9. bone \n5. Hair \n10. foot \n13. chin\nPDF page 66\nActivity 12: Synonyms \n \nBelt \nStrap \nshield \nPicture \nImage \ncash \nCover \nShield \nimage \nPull \nTug \nstrap \nMoney \nCash \nsource \nPaint \nTint \nattempt \nMovie \nShow \ndinner \nTry \nAttempt \ntime \nSupper \nDinner \ntug \nCause \nSource \nshow \nWhen \nTime \ntint \nCrop \nYield \nyield \n \n \n \nActivity 13: Antonyms \n \nSet A \nSet B \nalways \nthrough \nsometimes \nconstantly \nmorning \nthe past \nafternoon \nsunrise \neveryday \nby-and-by \nfinally \ndaily \ntomorrow \nlastly \nStart \noccasionally \nyesterday \nafter lunch \nlater \nfuture \nmorning \nadvanced \n5\nPDF page 67\nActivity 14: Word Puzzle \n \nP \nC \nW \nA \nN \nS \nW \nE \nR \nA \nR \nH \nA \nM \nO\nU \nN \nT \nR \nM \nO \nS \nQ \nU \nA \nR \nE \nT \nE \nL \nB \nX \nT \nZ \nW \nV \nL \nD \nE \nG \nL\nH \nU \nG \nE \nC \nI \nR \nC \nL \nE \nJ \nI \nQ \nO \nU \nC \nO \nE \nH \nM \nK \nU \nI \nM \nF \nS \nL \nO \nD \nS \nA \nN \nO \nI \nT \nC \nA \nR \nF \nL \n \nActivity 15: Arranging Letters \n \n1 \nr e s f o t \nforest \n2 \nr e r o c t c \ncorrect \n3 \ns o w d r \nwords \n4 \nk r i d n \ndrink \n5 \nr a g r p h a p a \nparagraph \n6 \ne n s t e n e c \nsentence \n7 \ne d a r a p \nparade \n8 \nt h r a e \nearth \n9 \nt a c h \nchat \n10 \nw r a d \ndraw \n11 \nn o s e ra \nreason \n12 \ny o s t r \nstory \n \nActivity 16: Correctly Spelled \n \n1. Ant \n6. animal \n2. Bug \n7. world \nDuring \nbegin\nPDF page 68\n3. kitten \n8. home \n4. everybody \n9. teeth \n5. deer \n10. Tongue \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nActivity 20: Sentence Completion \n \n \nfavorite \nbeautiful \nnotice \nsince \nnecessary \npleasure \nthought \nbetter \nsuppose \nwritten \nperhaps \ngeneral \n \n1. My favorite fruit is mango. \n2. Teachers notice to the parents about the meeting. \n3. It is better to take care of ourselves. \n4. Watching a game gave me a great pleasure \n5. He has two works since he graduated. \n6. You’d better back off. \n7. The book provide general information of the subject. \n8. Farmers perhaps not interested in the new Farming. \n9. My name is written on the blackboard. \n10. I suppose that they are not ready for the class. \n11. Do you have any thought for the lesson? \n12. She has the most beautiful  smile. \n \n \nPre - Assessment (Activity 11-20) \n \nVocabulary Development \nListening Comprehension \n \n1. Body \n11. lap \n2. feather \n12. hand \n3. Bill \n13. east \n4. eye \n14. pie \n5. finger \n15. tail \n \nB. \nContext Clues \nListening Comprehension(Passage) \n \n6. ant \n16. Lila goes to the park with her dog, Max . \n \n7. kitten \n17. Max is brown. \n \n8. everybody \n18. Lila swings on the swings and plays on \nthe slide.\nPDF page 69\n9. deer \n19. She brings a small snack and a bottle of \nwater. \n10. umbrella \n20. She watches birds in the trees and feeds \nthe ducks near the pond . \n \n \n \n \nPost - Assessment (Activity 11-20) \n 