p.\") \na. N (noun - captain) \n(Teacher reads: \"The dark shape that is made \nwhen something blocks light.\") \na. N (noun - shadow) \n \nPart A: Noun (N) or Verb (V) Your teacher will read a word aloud. Listen \ncarefully and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V). \n \n \n1.N \n2.V \n3.V \n4.N \n5.N \nPart B: Context Clues Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen \ncarefully and write the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the \nline. \n1. napkin \n2. Mirror \n3. Medicine \n4. lips \n5. Lesson \n6. Juice \n7. office \n8. Grocery \n9. Hammer \n10. gate \n11. Curtain \n12. Cupboard \n13. crown \n14. Crayons \n15. cocoa\nPDF page 67\n62 \n \n \n \nActivity 1: Multiple Choice Vocabulary Review \nActivity 2: Fill in the Blank Puzzle \n \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. \nB \n5. C \n1. ROSE \n2. SOLDIER \n3. CUPBOARD \n6. B \n7. C \n8. C \n9. B \n10. C \n4. VISIT \n5. TWENTY \n6. CHURCH \n \nActivity 3: Short Answer and Categorization \n \nTissue, Child, Tomorrow, Size, Quarter \nScissors, Shirt, Bag (or suitcase), Pharmacy \nDeposit \n7. STOVE \n8. NAPKIN \n9. NOON \n10. THOUSAND \nActivity 5: Matching Activity: Vocabulary Definitions \n \nActivity 6: Fill in the Blank Definitions \n \n \nActivity 7: Multiple Choice Questions \n \n \n1. A \n2. B \n3. A \n4. A \n5. A \n6. A \n7. A \n8. B \n9. A \n10. A \n1. Sugar - D. A sweet substance used to flavor food \n2. Umbrella - A. An object carried to protect from rain \n3. Finish - H. The opposite of starting or beginning \n4. Skirt - C. A short garment worn by women \n5. Doctor - B. A profession treating sick individuals \n6. Tear - E. A drop of liquid from the eye when crying \n7. Fork - F. An eating utensil with prongs \n8. Market - G. A type of public area for buying and selling goods \n9. Train - I. A type of transportation that travels on tracks \n10. Leather - J. A fabric made from the skin of an animal \n \n5. follow. \n8. clarify. \n2. thumb. \n3. captain. \n \n6. thermometer. \n \n9. Pilot \n10. oil.\nPDF page 68\n63 \n \n \n \nActivity 8: Match the Definitions \nActivity 9: Crossword Puzzle \n \n1. D \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. E \nACROSS: \nActivity 10. True or false \n1. SHADOW \n2. FOLLOW \n3. CAPTAIN \n1. true 2. False \n3. True \n4. false \n5. False \nDOWN: \n1. GARAGE \n2. THUMB \nActivity 11: Short Answer Questions \nActivity 12: Create a Sentence \n \n1. A garage is used for parking and \nstoring vehicles, as well as for storage \nof tools and equipment. \n2. A captain is responsible for the \ncommand and navigation of a ship, \nensuring the safety of the crew and \npassengers. \n3. A shadow is caused when an object \nblocks light, creating a dark shape on \na surface behind it. \n4. To follow someone means to move in \nthe same direction as that person, \noften by walking or traveling closely \nbehind them. \n5. The thumb is considered the thickest \nfinger because it has a larger bone \nstructure, is more muscular, and is \nopposable, allowing for a stronger grip. \n \nActivity 14: Sorting Activity \n \nPeople: captain \nObjects: garage, thumb, shadow, \nfollow \nActivity 16: Vocabulary Riddles \n \n1. beauty \n2. Calculator  3. Environment \n1 Garage: I park my car in the garage to protect it \nfrom the weather. \n2. Thumb: I injured my thumb while trying to open a jar. \n3. Captain: The captain gave clear instructions to the \ncrew before setting sail. \n4. Shadow: The tall tree cast a long shadow on the \nground in the late afternoon sun. \n5. Follow: If you want to know where to go, just follow \nme to the park. \n \nActivity 13: Vocabulary Riddles \n1. garage \n2. Thumb \n3. Shadow \n4. Captain \n5. follow \n \nActivity 15: Word Search \n \nGarage (Row 1, Left to Right) \nThumb (Row 6, Column 4, Up to Down) \nCaptain (Row 3, Left to Right) \nShadow (Row 6, Right to Left) \nFollow (Row 5, Column 4, Up to Down) \n \nActivity 17: Word Search \n4. journey \n5. Inspiration \nBeautiful (Row 1, Left to Right) \nCalculate (Row 3, Left to Right)