ing sick individuals \n6. Tear - E. A drop of liquid from the eye when crying \n7. Fork - F. An eating utensil with prongs \n8. Market - G. A type of public area for buying and selling goods \n9. Train - I. A type of transportation that travels on tracks \n10. Leather - J. A fabric made from the skin of an animal \n \n5. follow. \n8. clarify. \n2. thumb. \n3. captain. \n \n6. thermometer. \n \n9. Pilot \n10. oil.\nPDF page 68\n63 \n \n \n \nActivity 8: Match the Definitions \nActivity 9: Crossword Puzzle \n \n1. D \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. E \nACROSS: \nActivity 10. True or false \n1. SHADOW \n2. FOLLOW \n3. CAPTAIN \n1. true 2. False \n3. True \n4. false \n5. False \nDOWN: \n1. GARAGE \n2. THUMB \nActivity 11: Short Answer Questions \nActivity 12: Create a Sentence \n \n1. A garage is used for parking and \nstoring vehicles, as well as for storage \nof tools and equipment. \n2. A captain is responsible for the \ncommand and navigation of a ship, \nensuring the safety of the crew and \npassengers. \n3. A shadow is caused when an object \nblocks light, creating a dark shape on \na surface behind it. \n4. To follow someone means to move in \nthe same direction as that person, \noften by walking or traveling closely \nbehind them. \n5. The thumb is considered the thickest \nfinger because it has a larger bone \nstructure, is more muscular, and is \nopposable, allowing for a stronger grip. \n \nActivity 14: Sorting Activity \n \nPeople: captain \nObjects: garage, thumb, shadow, \nfollow \nActivity 16: Vocabulary Riddles \n \n1. beauty \n2. Calculator  3. Environment \n1 Garage: I park my car in the garage to protect it \nfrom the weather. \n2. Thumb: I injured my thumb while trying to open a jar. \n3. Captain: The captain gave clear instructions to the \ncrew before setting sail. \n4. Shadow: The tall tree cast a long shadow on the \nground in the late afternoon sun. \n5. Follow: If you want to know where to go, just follow \nme to the park. \n \nActivity 13: Vocabulary Riddles \n1. garage \n2. Thumb \n3. Shadow \n4. Captain \n5. follow \n \nActivity 15: Word Search \n \nGarage (Row 1, Left to Right) \nThumb (Row 6, Column 4, Up to Down) \nCaptain (Row 3, Left to Right) \nShadow (Row 6, Right to Left) \nFollow (Row 5, Column 4, Up to Down) \n \nActivity 17: Word Search \n4. journey \n5. Inspiration \nBeautiful (Row 1, Left to Right) \nCalculate (Row 3, Left to Right) \nEnvironment (Row 5, Left to Right) \nJourney (Row 4, Column 6, Down to Up) \nInspire (Diagonal from Row 1, Column 1 to Row 7, Col\nPDF page 69\n64 \n \n \nActivity 18: Fill in the Blank Definitions \nActivity 19: Fill in the Blanks \n1. mysterious \n2. Respect \n3. Discover \n4. challenge \n5. creative \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nActivity 20: Multiple Choice \n1. b \n2. B \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \n1. beautiful \n2. Calculate \n3. Environment \n4. journey \n5. Inspire \n6. Confusing \n7. praise \n8. Discover \n9. Challenge \n10. creative','[21]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(260,15,13212,'Activity 12','Match to Complete the Sentence','Listen, learn and use new words about match to complete the sentence.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 5\nMatch to Complete the Sentence · module PDF page 22\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 22\nMatching Meanings\nActivity 12- Match to Complete the Sentence\nDirection: In column A are the phrases. In column B are the words.\nMatch column A with column B by drawing a line.\nA\nB\n1. Save your money and deposit it in your ______\n.\na. market\n2. Every ______\nI take a nap.\nb. ought\n3. I ______\nhave my vitamins.\nc. cousin\n4. I ran five kilometres, and now I am ______\n.\nd. tub\n5. Give me one ______\npesos to buy a cake.\ne. thirsty\n6. ______\nis the number after nineteen.\nf. already\n7. Please get water from the ______\n.\ng. note\n8. You ______\nto try it sometimes.\nh. afternoon\n9. A ______\nis a silvery white metal.\ni. tomatoes\n10. Kindly take ______\nof the important events.\nj. thousand\n11. He used a knife ______\nof chopsticks.\nk. nickel\n12. My ______\nAna is the only relative I have.\nl. twenty\n13. Let us climb the ______\nto have an adventure.\nm. instead\n14. Maria goes to the ______\nto buy fruits.\nn. mountain\n15. ______\nare glossy red edible fruit.\no. bank\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 63\n58 \n \nI- Pre-test Assessment \nIV. Listening Comprehension & \nVocabulary: Homophones \n \n26. b \nVocabulary Development: Synonyms \n27. a \n1. b. crash \n28. b \n2. c. pretty \n29. b \n3. c. reply \n30. a \n4. c. wash \n31. a \n5. c. leader \n32. a \n6. c. select \n33. a \n7. c. twin \n34. b \n8. b. disagree \n35. b \n9. b. move \nV. Listening Comprehension: Context Clues \n10. b. sea \n36. friend \nII- Vocabulary De