(261,15,14213,'Activity 13','Context Clue','Listen, learn and use new words about context clue.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 5\nContext Clue · module PDF pages 23, 24\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 23\nGiving Hints\nActivity 13- Context Clue\nDirection: Read the context clues to identify the correct meaning\nof the underlined word below.\n1. An automobile is a road vehicle, typically with four wheels,\npowered by an engine and able to carry a small number of\npeople.\na. bicycle\nb. car\nc. carriage\nd. truck\n2. A strip of material used to bind a wound or to protect an injured\npart of the body is called a bandage.\na. cloth\nb. plaster\nc. ribbon\nd. string\n3. The wound is bleeding, losing more blood and it’s scary.\na.\nclosing\nb. fine\nc. healing\nd. hemorrhaging\n4. I like to write on the blackboard because I have plenty of\nchalk, it’s mounted on the wall and it’s smooth.\na. bond paper b. cardboard\nc. chalkboard\nd. colored paper\n5. Our classroom is dusty, please bring me a broom, that is long,\nhandle for sweeping.\na. brush\nb. rag\nc. scrub\nd. sweeper\n6. The stomach is an internal organ where digestion of food occurs\na. abdomen\nb. brain\nc. heart\nd. lung\n7. Sandro speaks wisely as he expresses his ideas to the public with\npride.\na. dream\nb. rejoice\nc. shout\nd. talk\n\nPDF page 24\n8. I love to drink lemonade because it quenches my thirst.\na. coffee\nb. lemon juice\nc. milk\nd. water\n9. Kindly use a ruler to measure his height.\na. calculate\nb. guess c. see d. write\n10. Please erase the writings to remove the prints on the wall.\na. wipe off\nb. write\nc. litter\nd. loiter\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 63\n58 \n \nI- Pre-test Assessment \nIV. Listening Comprehen