nk Definitions \n \n \nActivity 7: Multiple Choice Questions \n \n \n1. A \n2. B \n3. A \n4. A \n5. A \n6. A \n7. A \n8. B \n9. A \n10. A \n1. Sugar - D. A sweet substance used to flavor food \n2. Umbrella - A. An object carried to protect from rain \n3. Finish - H. The opposite of starting or beginning \n4. Skirt - C. A short garment worn by women \n5. Doctor - B. A profession treating sick individuals \n6. Tear - E. A drop of liquid from the eye when crying \n7. Fork - F. An eating utensil with prongs \n8. Market - G. A type of public area for buying and selling goods \n9. Train - I. A type of transportation that travels on tracks \n10. Leather - J. A fabric made from the skin of an animal \n \n5. follow. \n8. clarify. \n2. thumb. \n3. captain. \n \n6. thermometer. \n \n9. Pilot \n10. oil.\nPDF page 68\n63 \n \n \n \nActivity 8: Match the Definitions \nActivity 9: Crossword Puzzle \n \n1. D \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. E \nACROSS: \nActivity 10. True or false \n1. SHADOW \n2. FOLLOW \n3. CAPTAIN \n1. true 2. False \n3. True \n4. false \n5. False \nDOWN: \n1. GARAGE \n2. THUMB \nActivity 11: Short Answer Questions \nActivity 12: Create a Sentence \n \n1. A garage is used for parking and \nstoring vehicles, as well as for storage \nof tools and equipment. \n2. A captain is responsible for the \ncommand and navigation of a ship, \nensuring the safety of the crew and \npassengers. \n3. A shadow is caused when an object \nblocks light, creating a dark shape on \na surface behind it. \n4. To follow someone means to move in \nthe same direction as that person, \noften by walking or traveling closely \nbehind them. \n5. The thumb is considered the thickest \nfinger because it has a larger bone \nstructure, is more muscular, and is \nopposable, allowing for a stronger grip. \n \nActivity 14: Sorting Activity \n \nPeople: captain \nObjects: garage, thumb, shadow, \nfollow \nActivity 16: Vocabulary Riddles \n \n1. beauty \n2. Calculator  3. Environment \n1 Garage: I park my car in the garage to protect it \nfrom the weather. \n2. Thumb: I injured my thumb while trying to open a jar. \n3. Captain: The captain gave clear instructions to the \ncrew before setting sail. \n4. Shadow: The tall tree cast a long shadow on the \nground in the late afternoon sun. \n5. Follow: If you want to know where to go, just follow \nme to the park. \n \nActivity 13: Vocabulary Riddles \n1. garage \n2. Thumb \n3. Shadow \n4. Captain \n5. follow \n \nActivity 15: Word Search \n \nGarage (Row 1, Left to Right) \nThumb (Row 6, Column 4, Up to Down) \nCaptain (Row 3, Left to Right) \nShadow (Row 6, Right to Left) \nFollow (Row 5, Column 4, Up to Down) \n \nActivity 17: Word Search \n4. journey \n5. Inspiration \nBeautiful (Row 1, Left to Right) \nCalculate (Row 3, Left to Right) \nEnvironment (Row 5, Left to Right) \nJourney (Row 4, Column 6, Down to Up) \nInspire (Diagonal from Row 1, Column 1 to Row 7, Col\nPDF page 69\n64 \n \n \nActivity 18: Fill in the Blank Definitions \nActivity 19: Fill in the Blanks \n1. mysterious \n2. Respect \n3. Discover \n4. challenge \n5. creative \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nActivity 20: Multiple Choice \n1. b \n2. B \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \n1. beautiful \n2. Calculate \n3. Environment \n4. journey \n5. Inspire \n6. Confusing \n7. praise \n8. Discover \n9. Challenge \n10. creative','[33, 34]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(269,15,22300,'Post-test','Post-test','Show how much your listening and vocabulary have grown.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 5\nPost-test · module PDF pages 36, 37, 38, 39\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 36\nPost-Test Assessment: (1-10)\nVocabulary and Listening Comprehension (Items 1–40)\nI. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning as\nthe underlined word.\n1. She felt glad when she won the medal.\na. strong\nb. sad\nc. truth\nd. ache\n2. The old photograph is very clear.\na. blurry\nb. light\nc. happy\nd. long\n3. He decided to lie about the broken vase.\na. truth\nb. doubt\nc. rejoice\nd. worry\n4. I will end my presentation with a summary.\na. often\nb. start\nc. tomorrow\nd. sir\n5. You must remember to lock the door.\na. forget\nb. lad\nc. act\nd. weak\n6. The children began to laugh at the funny story.\na. cry\nb. believe\nc. catch\nd. free\n7. He is too weak to lift the box.\na. strong\nb. thin\nc. ugly\nd. bad\n8. They went outdoors to play basketball.\na. north\nb. lady\nc. indoors\nd. sometimes\n9. She is very careful with her school supplies.\na. tomorrow\nb. careless\nc. south\nd. morning\n10. The blanket is too thin for this cold weather.\na. healthy\nb. thick\nc. beautiful\nd. pretty\n\nPDF page 37\nII. Vocabulary Development: Synonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the same meaning as the\nunderlined word.\n1. She is planning to select a new puppy.\na. deny\nb. reply\nc. choose\nd. mind\n2. The two brothers are twin sons.\na. cover\nb. fix\nc. double\nd. risk\n3. Did you reply to her email?\na. select\nb. go\nc. answer\nd. wash\n4. We must obey the chief\'s orders.\na. audience\nb. disagree\nc. leader\nd. day\n5. I need to go to the hospital for a check-up.\na. begin\nb. move\nc. finish\nd. end\n6. Please wash your hands before eating.\na. cover\nb. bathe\nc. fix\nd. glue\n7. The sea is rough today.\na. time\nb. ocean\nc. soil\nd. date\n8. He was against the idea of closing the park.\na. time\nb. disagree\nc. alone\nd. eating\n9. That was a terrible crash involving three cars.\na. answer\nb. bathe\nc. accident\nd. double\n10. What a pretty bouquet of flowers!\na. dirty\nb. noisy\nc. beautiful\nd. short\n\nPDF page 38\nIII. Vocabulary Development: Homophones (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct word inside the parenthesis that fits the\nsentence.\n1. My doctor told me to watch my (wait / weight).\na. wait\nb. weight\n2. What is the total (coast / cost) of the groceries?\na. coast\nb. cost\n3. You can use this color to (die / dye) your shirt.\na. die\nb. dye\n4. She used a needle to mend the (hole / whole) in her sock.\na. hole\nb. whole\n5. We need to hire a boat to (sail / sale) across the lake.\na. sail\nb. sale\n6. I hope we don\'t have another world (war / wore).\na. war\nb. wore\n7. This old furniture is just going to (waist / waste).\na. waist\nb. waste\n8. The (fair / fare) was much higher than expected.\na. fare\nb. fair\n9. The whole family (road / rode) the carousel.\na. road\nb. rode\n10. We went to the summer (fare / fair) yesterday.\na. fare\nb. fair\nIV. Listening Comprehension & Vocabulary: Noun, Verb, and Context Clues\n(10 items)\nDirections: Listen to the word or clue read by your teacher and follow the\ninstructions for each item.\n\nPDF page 39\nPart A: Noun (N) or Verb (V) Your teacher will read a word aloud. Listen\ncarefully and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V).\n1. (Teacher reads: \"chalk\")\na. N\nb. V\n2. (Teacher reads: \"fell\")\na. N\nb. V\n3. (Teacher reads: \"guess\")\na. N\nb. V\n4. (Teacher reads: \"porch\")\na. N\nb. V\n5. (Teacher reads: \"change\")\na. N\nb. V\nPart B: Context Clues Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen\ncarefully and write the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the\nline.\n6. (Teacher reads: \"The place where a car is kept, usually attached to a\nhouse.\")\n7. (Teacher reads: \"The thickest finger of the hand.\")\n8. (Teacher reads: \"A person who is in charge of a ship.\")\n9. (Teacher reads: \"The dark shape that is made when something blocks\nlight.\")\n10. (Teacher reads: \"To move in the same direction or track as someone\nelse.\")\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 63\n58 \n \nI- Pre-test Assessment \nIV. Listening Comprehension & \nVocabulary: Homophones \n \n26. b \nVocabulary Development: Synonyms \n27. a \n1. b. crash \n28. b \n2. c. pretty \n29. b \n3. c. reply \n30. a \n4. c. wash \n31. a \n5. c. leader \n32. a \n6. c. select \n33. a \n7. c. twin \n34. b \n8. b. disagree \n35. b \n9. b. move \nV. Listening Comprehension: Context Clues \n10. b. sea \n36. friend \nII- Vocabulary Development: Antonyms \n37. Dentist \n11. a. rememberDentist \n38. Pants \n12. b. do nothing \n39. Boat \n13. b. careful \n40. Reason \n14. b. clear \nActivity 1- Synonyms \n15. b. morning \n1. Crash \n6. twin \n16. b. glad \n2. Pretty \n7. world \n17. b. truth \n3. Reply \n8. down \n18. a. outdoors \n4. Wash \n9. postman \n19. b. thin \n5. Supper \n10. fix \n20. b. sometimes \nIII- Vocabulary Development: Noun or Verb \nActivity 2- Synonyms \n \n21. b. V (verb) \n1. Go \n2. Sea \n3. time \n22. a. N (noun) \n4. Disagree \n5. Alone \n6. start \n23. a. N (noun) \n7. Leader \n8. Select \n9. round \n24. b. V (verb) \n10. Audience \n11. Risk \n12. day \n25. a. N (noun) \n13. Eating \n14. Dirt \n15. End \nAnswer keys\nPDF page 64\n59 \n \n \n \nActivity 3 \nActivity 4 \n1. do nothing 6. Laugh \n11. Outdoors \n1. Hen \n6. Healthy \n11. men \n2. doubt \n7. Start \n12. Lad \n2. Plenty \n7. Winter \n12. rejoice \n3. careful \n8. Morning \n13. Truth \n3. Gather \n8. Thin \n13. calm \n4. free \n9. Remember \n14. South \n4. F