(275,15,28406,'Activity 6 (second set)','Fill in the Blank Definitions','Listen, learn and use new words about fill in the blank definitions.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 5\nFill in the Blank Definitions · module PDF page 47\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 47\nActivity 6: Fill in the Blank Definitions\nDirections: Complete each sentence with the appropriate\nvocabulary word.\n1. The place where a car is kept, usually attached to a house is\ncalled a ______\n.\n2. The thickest finger of the hand is the ______\n.\n3. A person who is in charge of a ship is known as the ______\n.\n4. The dark shape that is made when something blocks light is\ncalled a ______\n.\n5. To move in the same direction or track as someone else means\nto ______\n.\n6. A measurement of temperature is called ______\n.\n7. The act of deciding what to choose is known as ______\n.\n8. To make something clearer is to ______\n.\n9. The person who flies an airplane is called a ______\n.\n10. The liquid used for cooking food at high temperatures is called\n______.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 63\n58 \n \nI- Pre-test Assessment \nIV. Listening Comprehension & \nVocabulary: Homophones \n \n26. b \nVocabulary Development: Synonyms \n27. a \n1. b. crash \n28. b \n2. c. pretty \n29. b \n3. c. reply \n30. a \n4. c. wash \n31. a \n5. c. leader \n32. a \n6. c. select \n33. a \n7. c. twin \n34. b \n8. b. disagree \n35. b \n9. b. move \nV. Listening Comprehension: Context Clues \n10. b. sea \n36. friend \nII- Vocabulary Development: Antonyms \n37. Dentist \n11. a. rememberDentist \n38. Pants \n12. b. do nothing \n39. Boat \n13. b. careful \n40. Reason \n14. b. clear \nActivity 1- Synonyms \n15. b. morning \n1. Crash \n6. twin \n16. b. gl