(276,15,29407,'Activity 7 (second set)','Multiple Choice Questions','Listen, learn and use new words about multiple choice questions.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 5\nMultiple Choice Questions · module PDF page 48\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 48\nActivity 7: Multiple Choice Questions\nDirections: Choose the letter of the correct answer.\n1. The place where a car is kept, usually attached to a house:\na. Garage\nb. Kitchen\nc. Bedroom\nd. Office\n2. The thickest finger of the hand is called the:\na. Index\nb. Thumb\nc. Pinky\nd. Ring\n3. A person who is in charge of a ship is:\na. Captain b. Sailor c. Mechanic\nd. Diver\n4. The dark shape created when something blocks light is known as:\na. Shadow b. Reflection c. Beam\nd. Glare\n5. To move in the same direction or track as someone else means to:\na. Follow\nb. Lead\nc. Attend\nd. Join\n6. The act of preparing food is called:\na. Cooking b. Arranging c. Eating d. Serving\n7. A tool used for writing:\na. Pencil\nb. Ruler\nc. Brush\nd. Paper\n8. The substance used in cooking that can add flavor:\na. Sugar\nb. Salt c. Pepper\nd. Oil\n9. The position of something in relation to its surroundings:\na. Location b. Direction c. Distance d. Area\n10. The person who makes laws in a government is called a:\na. Senator\nb. Mayor\nc. Judge\nd. Citizen\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 63\n58 \n \nI- Pre-test Assessment \nIV. Listening Comprehension & \nVocabulary: Homophones \n \n26. b \nVocabulary Development: Synonyms \n27. a \n1. b. crash \n28. b \n2. c. pretty \n29. b \n3. c. reply \n30. a \n4. c. wash \n31. a \n5. c. leader \n32. a \n6. c. select \n33. a \n7. c. twin \n34. b \n8. b. disagree \n35. b \n9. b. move \nV. Listening Comprehension: Context C