 thickest finger of the \nhand.\") \na. N (noun - thumb) \n(Teacher reads: \"A person who is in charge of a \nship.\") \na. N (noun - captain) \n(Teacher reads: \"The dark shape that is made \nwhen something blocks light.\") \na. N (noun - shadow) \n \nPart A: Noun (N) or Verb (V) Your teacher will read a word aloud. Listen \ncarefully and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V). \n \n \n1.N \n2.V \n3.V \n4.N \n5.N \nPart B: Context Clues Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen \ncarefully and write the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the \nline. \n1. napkin \n2. Mirror \n3. Medicine \n4. lips \n5. Lesson \n6. Juice \n7. office \n8. Grocery \n9. Hammer \n10. gate \n11. Curtain \n12. Cupboard \n13. crown \n14. Crayons \n15. cocoa\nPDF page 67\n62 \n \n \n \nActivity 1: Multiple Choice Vocabulary Review \nActivity 2: Fill in the Blank Puzzle \n \n1. B \n2. C \n3. C \n4. \nB \n5. C \n1. ROSE \n2. SOLDIER \n3. CUPBOARD \n6. B \n7. C \n8. C \n9. B \n10. C \n4. VISIT \n5. TWENTY \n6. CHURCH \n \nActivity 3: Short Answer and Categorization \n \nTissue, Child, Tomorrow, Size, Quarter \nScissors, Shirt, Bag (or suitcase), Pharmacy \nDeposit \n7. STOVE \n8. NAPKIN \n9. NOON \n10. THOUSAND \nActivity 5: Matching Activity: Vocabulary Definitions \n \nActivity 6: Fill in the Blank Definitions \n \n \nActivity 7: Multiple Choice Questions \n \n \n1. A \n2. B \n3. A \n4. A \n5. A \n6. A \n7. A \n8. B \n9. A \n10. A \n1. Sugar - D. A sweet substance used to flavor food \n2. Umbrella - A. An object carried to protect from rain \n3. Finish - H. The opposite of starting or beginning \n4. Skirt - C. A short garment worn by women \n5. Doctor - B. A profession treating sick individuals \n6. Tear - E. A drop of liquid from the eye when crying \n7. Fork - F. An eating utensil with prongs \n8. Market - G. A type of public area for buying and selling goods \n9. Train - I. A type of transportation that travels on tracks \n10. Leather - J. A fabric made from the skin of an animal \n \n5. follow. \n8. clarify. \n2. thumb. \n3. captain. \n \n6. thermometer. \n \n9. Pilot \n10. oil.\nPDF page 68\n63 \n \n \n \nActivity 8: Match the Definitions \nActivity 9: Crossword Puzzle \n \n1. D \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. E \nACROSS: \nActivity 10. True or false \n1. SHADOW \n2. FOLLOW \n3. CAPTAIN \n1. true 2. False \n3. True \n4. false \n5. False \nDOWN: \n1. GARAGE \n2. THUMB \nActivity 11: Short Answer Questions \nActivity 12: Create a Sentence \n \n1. A garage is used for parking and \nstoring vehicles, as well as for storage \nof tools and equipment. \n2. A captain is responsible for the \ncommand and navigation of a ship, \nensuring the safety of the crew and \npassengers. \n3. A shadow is caused when an object \nblocks light, creating a dark shape on \na surface behind it. \n4. To follow someone means to move in \nthe same direction as that person, \noften by walking or traveling closely \nbehind them. \n5. The thumb is considered the thickest \nfinger because it has a larger bone \nstructure, is more muscular, and is \nopposable, allowing for a stronger grip. \n \nActivity 14: Sorting Activity \n \nPeople: captain \nObjects: garage, thumb, shadow, \nfollow \nActivity 16: Vocabulary Riddles \n \n1. beauty \n2. Calculator  3. Environment \n1 Garage: I park my car in the garage to protect it \nfrom the weather. \n2. Thumb: I injured my thumb while trying to open a jar. \n3. Captain: The captain gave clear instructions to the \ncrew before setting sail. \n4. Shadow: The tall tree cast a long shadow on the \nground in the late afternoon sun. \n5. Follow: If you want to know where to go, just follow \nme to the park. \n \nActivity 13: Vocabulary Riddles \n1. garage \n2. Thumb \n3. Shadow \n4. Captain \n5. follow \n \nActivity 15: Word Search \n \nGarage (Row 1, Left to Right) \nThumb (Row 6, Column 4, Up to Down) \nCaptain (Row 3, Left to Right) \nShadow (Row 6, Right to Left) \nFollow (Row 5, Column 4, Up to Down) \n \nActivity 17: Word Search \n4. journey \n5. Inspiration \nBeautiful (Row 1, Left to Right) \nCalculate (Row 3, Left to Right) \nEnvironment (Row 5, Left to Right) \nJourney (Row 4, Column 6, Down to Up) \nInspire (Diagonal from Row 1, Column 1 to Row 7, Col\nPDF page 69\n64 \n \n \nActivity 18: Fill in the Blank Definitions \nActivity 19: Fill in the Blanks \n1. mysterious \n2. Respect \n3. Discover \n4. challenge \n5. creative \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nActivity 20: Multiple Choice \n1. b \n2. B \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \n1. beautiful \n2. Calculate \n3. Environment \n4. journey \n5. Inspire \n6. Confusing \n7. praise \n8. Discover \n9. Challenge \n10. creative','[61, 62]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(290,16,1100,'Pre-test','Pre-test','Show what you already know about these words and stories.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 6\nPre-test · module PDF pages 6, 7, 8\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 6\nPRETEST\nPart A — Numbers & Colors (1–4)\nInstructions: Read, understand and answer the questions correctly.\n1. Write the number: “seven” → ______\n2. Write the number word: “12 → ______\n”\n3. What color is the sky on a clear day?\na. blue\nb. red\nc. green\n4. Which word is a color?\na. run\nb. yellow\nc. happy\nPart B — Adverbs (5–6)\n5. Choose the adverb:\na. slowly\nb. tiger\nc. table\n6. Choose the sentence that uses an adverb correctly:\na. The cat runs quickly.\nb. The cat quickly.\nc. The quick cat run.\nPart C — Antonyms (7–8)\n7. Find the opposite of “big”:\na. tall\nb. small\nc. long\n8. The antonym of “happy” is ______\n.\na. sad\nb. joyful\nc. glad\n\nPDF page 7\nPart D — Synonyms (9–10)\n9. Which word means the same as “fast”?\na) quick\nb) slow\nc) heavy\n10. A synonym for “begin” is ______\n.\na) start\nb) stop\nc) wait\nPart E — Nouns (11–12)\n11. Which word is a noun?\na) jump\nb) teacher\nc) slowly\n12. Choose the noun that names a place:\na) school\nb) red\nc) eat\nPart F — Human & Animal Body Parts (Matching) (13–15)\nMatch the word to the correct picture/description. Write the letter.\n13. ______\nTail\na) Helps animals balance\n14. ______\nEar\nb) Used for hearing\n15. ______\nHand\nc) Used for holding things\nPart G — Mini Crossword (16–17)\n16. Across (4 letters): Color of sky\n17. Down (5 letters): A number between six and eight\nPart H — Word Hunt (18)\n18. Circle and list three animals hidden in this string:\nXCCATRDTGHDOGASDGFRATZSDGRBIRDZSDGFOXDFHSH\n______, ______\n, ______\n\nPDF page 8\nPart I — Word Pairing (19)\n19. Match the words that go together:\n1. hot\na. milk\n2. cold\nb. tea\nWrite the pairs: ______\n→ ______\n,\n______ → ______\nPart J — Matching Meaning (20)\n20. Match the word with its meaning:\n1. run\na. to move fast\n2. blue\nb. a color\nWrite: 1. ______\n,\n2. ______\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[6, 7, 8]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(291,16,2201,'Activity 1','Act Game','Listen, learn and use new words about act game.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 6\nAct Game · module PDF page 10\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 10\nAct Game\nActivity 1\nDirections: Pick a square word card inside a box or bag. Read the\nword. Find the word inside the classroom. Write them on the\nboard (e.g. half ½, 9, 11, etc.) Do it repeatedly.\nshape\nrecord\nsouth\nobject\nminute\nwhole\nunit\nbigger\ntoday\nnight\nspring\nhow\nwhen\nalways\nlive\ntime\nroad\ndraw\npair\ndress\ncounter\nflow\nmeasure ______\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[10]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
