(309,16,20219,'Activity 19','Sentence Complete','Listen, learn and use new words about sentence complete.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 6\nSentence Complete · module PDF page 28\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 28\nSentence Complete\nActivity 19\nDirections:\nSelect the correct word from the list to complete each\nsentence. Write the correct answer in the blank.\namber\ndominion\nsundry\ncapillary\nimpetuous\nblight\nwrest\nenumerate\ndaunted\ncondescend\nimprison\nadjust\nbacteria\noccurrence\naccess\ncalendar\ndivision\ndevelop\ndirect\ndescribe\n1. My mother bought a ______\noranges.\n2. Ants ______\nis situated in the ground.\n3. It is ______\nto take care of ourselves.\n4. Watching basketball is my great ______\n.\n5. He works using the two ______\n.\n6. You’re so ______\n, it’s better to back off.\n7. The book ______\nhas huge information of the subject\nmatter.\n8. Farmers ______\nthe interested ways in Farming.\n9. I am ______\nwith my name on the blackboard.\n10.\nMy ______\nare not ready doing something.\n11.\nDo you have some ______\nin your body?\n12.\nHer smile can ______\na heart.\n13.\nI have a ______\nin my arm.\n14.\nPlease ______\nthe echo of the sound.\n15.\nOh my! I don’t have ______\nin the net.\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[28]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(310,16,21220,'Activity 20','Paragraph Filling','Listen, learn and use new words about paragraph filling.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 6\nParagraph Filling · module PDF page 29\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 29\nParagraph Filling\nActivity 20\nDirections:\nComplete the paragraph by filling on the blank. The first and\nlast letters of each word are given. Use/Select the words\ninisde the box.\nadvance\ndirection\nchilly\nweird\ngallery\nimpossible\nbridge\ngeneral\nabolish\ntrucker\napparatus comment\nelementary perhaps\nnecessity relativity\ncommercial favorite\nbeautiful\nimprint\nAn a ______\ne used of technolog\nis\nvery w ______ d but c ______\ny\nthings\nhappened nowadays. It gives us good\nd ______\nn in c ______\nl and g ______\ny\nof a ______\ns.\nB ______\ne were a ______\nh in very i\n______ e reasons and in easy way that t\n______ r had no c ______\ns.\nAn e ______\ny learners has lots of\nn ______\ny needed that were b\n______ l and their f ______\ne.\nIn g ______\nl these things needed to i\n______ t and p ______\ns required r\n______ y.\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[29]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(311,16,22300,'Post-test','Post-test','Show how much your listening and vocabulary have grown.','Listening Comprehension and Vocabulary Development · Level 5 · Grade 6\nPost-test · module PDF pages 31, 32\n\nPupils see each module page with its text and pictures. Listen reads the page aloud; for listening items read the passage yourself if you prefer. Pupils type or say their numbered answers; check them with the answer key below and give feedback.\n\nPDF page 31\nPOST TEST\nPart A — Numbers (1–4)\n1. Write the number word: 3 = ______\n2. Write the number: “five” = ______\n3. Which is a number?\na) red b) six c) cat\n4. What number comes after 2? ______\nPart B — Colors (5–6)\n5. Which is a color?\na) blue b) run c) book\n6. The sun is ______\n.\na) yellow b) green c) black\nPart C — Adverbs (7–8)\n7. Choose the adverb:\na) quickly b) dog\nc) chair\n8. “She sings softly.”\nThe adverb is: ______\nPart D — Antonyms (Opposites) (9–10)\n9. Opposite of hot is ______\n.\n10. Opposite of big:\na) small b) tall c) long\nPart E — Synonyms (Same meaning) (11–12)\n11. “Happy” means the same as:\na) sad b) glad\nc) angry\n12. “Start” means the same as ______\n.\na) begin\nb) stop c) sleep\nPart F — Nouns (13–14)\n13. Which is a noun?\na) pencil\nb) run c) quickly\n14. Which is a place?\na) school b) blue c) jump\n\nPDF page 32\nPart G — Body Parts (15–16)\n15 You hear with your ______\na) tail\nb) nose c) wing\n16.An animal has a ______\nto move (example: horse).\nb) tail b) nose c) wing\nPart H — Mini Crossword (17–18)\n17. Across (3 letters): A pet that barks:\n18. Down (5 letters): Color of grass:\nPart I — Word Hunt (19)\n19. Find two animals with wings in this string:\nCATDOGHORSEBIRDSUN\nPart J — Matching (20)\n20. Match:\nc) red\n1. a color\nd) run\n2. to move fast\nWrite: a– ______\n, b– ______\n\nThe module has no answer key for this grade.','[31, 32]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(312,17,1100,'Pre-test','Reading comprehension test','Show how well you understand what you read before the lessons.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nPre-test: Pre-test · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 6, 7, 8\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nPre-test · Reading (PDF pages 6, 7)\nRead the stories. Then read the questions carefully and encircle the correct answer.\n\nPre-test\nI am Miko. I have a friend. His name is Tito.\nTito is a smart cat. I feed him rice and fish.\nTito and I play together.\n\nDana’s father is a farmer. He goes to farm every day.\nHe works on the farm. He plants rice and corn on the farm.\n\nDolly is a doll. She has long and curly hair.\nIsn’t she pretty? She has a nice dress.\nI bring her to school. I love Dolly so much!\n\nTito is a smart ______.\na. cat\nb. dog\nc. pig\n\nTito eats ______.\na. rice and fish\nb. rice and meat\nc. rice and fruits\n\nDana’s father is a ______?\na. farmer\nb. driver\nc. teacher\n\nWhat did he plant on the farm?\na. Ubi and gabi\nb. Rice and corn\nc. Sugar cane\n\nWho is Dolly?\na. a cat\nb. a doll\nc. a rat\n\nPre-test · Reality or Fantasy (PDF page 7)\nDirection: Write R for Reality and F for Fantasy on the space provided.\n\nA cow can give milk.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe baby goats drink milk from their mother goat.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe grass eats the mother goat.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nHorse Lino, goat Lucy and cow Lita are animals.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nCows and goats can give milk and meat too.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nPre-test · Sequencing (PDF page 7)\nDirection: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Write numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 on the blank provided.\n\nItems 11–15. Write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event to show the order.\n11. Bear finds a den.\n12. Bear eats a lot.\n13. Bear eats even more!\n14. Bear fills the den with leaves, so he will stay warm.\n15. Bear needs to get ready for winter.\n\nPre-test · Cause and Effect (PDF page 8)\nDirection: Draw a line to match each cause on the left with its effect on the right.\n\nColumn A\n16. Matt did not study\n17. To ease the pain\n18. Jean went inside her house\n19. Jean was unhappy\n20. Emmy got a wound\nA. because she fell off her bike.\nB. because the wind blows her balloon.\nC. Emmy eats an ice cream.\nD. so he failed the Math test.\nE. because she was tired.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nMy Dolly \n1. B \n2. A \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \nJoy’s Aya \n1. C \n2. A \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nLita the Cow \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nRosa’s Goat \n1. R \n2. F \n3. R \n4. F \n5. R \nBenny’s Happy Day \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nLily’s Magical Pet \n1. R \n2. R \n3. R \n4. F \n5. F \nA Cold Bear \n1. _3  Bear finds a den. \n2.  2  Bear eats a lot. \n3.  5  Bear eats even more. \n4.  4  Bear fills the den with leaves, so \nhe will stay warm. \n5.  1  Bear needs to get ready for winter. \nDessert Time \n1. 3  Jan gets some cake. \n2.  2 Tim gets a cookie. \n3.  4 Ben gets a donut. \n4. 1  It is time for dessert. \n5. 5  Deb gets some pie. \nHarry and the Crayon \n1. 2  He took the bag with crayons. \n2.  3 He sits under the trees. \n3.  1 Harry was dreaming. \n4.  4 He lays his bag and draws. \n5. 5  He uses his crayons in drawing. \nHarry and the Crayon \n1.  2 He took his bag with crayons. \n2. 3  He sits under the trees. \n3.  1 Harry was dreaming. \n4. 4  He lays his bag and draws. \n5. 5  He uses his crayons in drawing. \nMy Pet \n1. 5 I love my pet dog. \n2. 3 He eats fish and bones. \n3. 1 I have a pet. \n4. 2 His name is Whitey. \n5. 4 He likes to play hide and seek.\n\nPDF page 37\n32 \nPre Test/Post Test \n16. Matt did not study \n17. To ease the pain \n18. Jean went inside \nher house \n19. Jean was unhappy \nA. so Emmy got a wound. \nB. because the wind blows \nballoon. \nC. Emmy eats ice cream. \n20. She fell off her bike \nD. therefore he failed the Math \ntest \nE. because she is tired. \n1. B \n9. R \n2. A \n10. R \n3. A \n11. 3 \n4. B \n12. 1 \n5. B \n13. 5 \n6. R \n14. 4 \n7. R \n15. 2 \n8. F \nActivities \nCause \n1. Hector got scared \n2. Letty studied for the next test. \n3. Luis fell off his bike \n4. It rained all night \n5. Mary ran fast to Luis \nEffect \nA. so she slipped. \nB. so his knee got wounded. \nC. so the classes are cancelled. \nD. so she got an A grade. \nE. so he went home. \nFishing \n1. Father and Eric will go fishing. \n2. His dad does not want Eric to get hurt. \n3. They started fishing. \n4. Eric is happy. \n5. Eric’s father will cook the fish they caught. \nGood Ways \nCause \nLino went to the garden \nHe picked malunggay leaves \nLino cooked the vegetables \nHe was walking fast \nTo be able to bring home \nsome vegetables \nEffect \nso they had a \ndelicious viand. \nwhen a branch hit \nhis head. \nand rubbed it on his \nforehead \nhe gathered it. \nto check the \nvegetables. \nSnowball Fight \nJan was hit by a snowball \nMark throws a snowball \nThey saw a bear \nEffect \nthe snowball knocks \nJan down. \nthey ran fast. \nbecause he was not fast \nenough. \nto make snowballs. \nAlex and His Mother \n1. Alex and his mother went to a store. \n2. Alex and his mother were buying. \n3. Alex and his mother were paying for their groceries. \n4. Alex and his mother are at the bus terminal. \n5. Alex and his mother are now inside their house. \nKaren’s Puzzle \n1. The box was full of pictures. \n2. Karen is starting to put the pieces together. \n3. Karen is starting to put together a puzzle. \n4. Karen has completed the puzzle. \n5. Karen liked playing the puzzle. \nHappenings \nCause \n1. Matt did not study \n2. To ease the pain \n3. Jean went inside her house \n4. Jean was unhappy. \n5. She fell off her bike. \nEffect \nA. so Emmy got a wound. \nB. because the wind blows \nher balloon. \nC. Emmy eats ice cream. \nD. there he failed the Math \ntest. \nE. because she is tired. \nWatching a Circus Show \n1. They will watch a circus. \n2. Frankie’s family is at a magic show. \n3. Franlie is enjoying the show. \n4. Frankie’s family is at the circus park. \n5. Frankie is in school.','[6, 7, 8]','assets/images/level6/g1/p006-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
