(319,17,8207,'Activity 7','Benny’s Happy Day','Fantasy or Reality: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nActivity 7: Benny’s Happy Day · skill: Fantasy or Reality · module PDF page 16\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nBenny’s Happy Day (PDF page 16)\nDirection: Read the selection. Write R for Reality and F for Fantasy on the space provided.\n\nBenny’s Happy Day\nBenny the bear loved to play.\nHe played in his backyard.\nHe saw a bright sun shining in the sky.\nBenny picked a colorful flower for his mom.\nHe felt happy and danced with his friends.\nBenny said, “Today is the best day ever”.\n\nBenny was playing in his backyard.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nHe picked a golden crown for his mom.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nHe was playing with animals and fairies.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nPicking flowers for Benny’s mother made him happy.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nFinally, Benny said, “Today is the best day ever”.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nMy Dolly \n1. B \n2. A \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \nJoy’s Aya \n1. C \n2. A \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nLita the Cow \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nRosa’s Goat \n1. R \n2. F \n3. R \n4. F \n5. R \nBenny’s Happy Day \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nLily’s Magical Pet \n1. R \n2. R \n3. R \n4. F \n5. F \nA Cold Bear \n1. _3  Bear finds a den. \n2.  2  Bear eats a lot. \n3.  5  Bear eats even more. \n4.  4  Bear fills the den with leaves, so \nhe will stay warm. \n5.  1  Bear needs to get ready for winter. \nDessert Time \n1. 3  Jan gets some cake. \n2.  2 Tim gets a