nEffect \nthe snowball knocks \nJan down. \nthey ran fast. \nbecause he was not fast \nenough. \nto make snowballs. \nAlex and His Mother \n1. Alex and his mother went to a store. \n2. Alex and his mother were buying. \n3. Alex and his mother were paying for their groceries. \n4. Alex and his mother are at the bus terminal. \n5. Alex and his mother are now inside their house. \nKaren’s Puzzle \n1. The box was full of pictures. \n2. Karen is starting to put the pieces together. \n3. Karen is starting to put together a puzzle. \n4. Karen has completed the puzzle. \n5. Karen liked playing the puzzle. \nHappenings \nCause \n1. Matt did not study \n2. To ease the pain \n3. Jean went inside her house \n4. Jean was unhappy. \n5. She fell off her bike. \nEffect \nA. so Emmy got a wound. \nB. because the wind blows \nher balloon. \nC. Emmy eats ice cream. \nD. there he failed the Math \ntest. \nE. because she is tired. \nWatching a Circus Show \n1. They will watch a circus. \n2. Frankie’s family is at a magic show. \n3. Franlie is enjoying the show. \n4. Frankie’s family is at the circus park. \n5. Frankie is in school.','[16]','assets/images/level6/g1/p016-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(320,17,9208,'Activity 8','Lily’s Magical Pet','Fantasy or Reality: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nActivity 8: Lily’s Magical Pet · skill: Fantasy or Reality · module PDF page 17\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLily’s Magical Pet (PDF page 17)\nDirection: Read the selection. Write R for Reality and F for Fantasy on the space provided.\n\nLily’s Magical Pet\nLily had a stuffed rabbit named Fluffy.\nOne day, she wished Fluffy could talk and play with her.\nSuddenly, in her dream, Fluffy spoke and said, “Let’s play hide-and-seek!”\nThey played together in a magical garden.\nBut when Lily woke up, Fluffy was just a stuffed animal again.\n\nLily had a stuffed rabbit.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nShe wished Fluffy to talk and play with her.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nLily and Fluffy played in a magical garden.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nLily dreamed of playing Fluffy in a magical garden.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nFluffy was talking in real life.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nMy Dolly \n1. B \n2. A \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \nJoy’s Aya \n1. C \n2. A \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nLita the Cow \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nRosa’s Goat \n1. R \n2. F \n3. R \n4. F \n5. R \nBenny’s Happy Day \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nLily’s Magical Pet \n1. R \n2. R \n3. R \n4. F \n5. F \nA Cold Bear \n1. _3  Bear finds a den. \n2.  2  Bear eats a lot. \n3.  5  Bear eats even more. \n4.  4  Bear fills the den with leaves, so \nhe will stay warm. \n5.  1  Bear needs to get ready for winter. \nDessert Time \n1. 3 