(321,17,10209,'Activity 9','A Cold Bear','Sequencing Events: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nActivity 9: A Cold Bear · skill: Sequencing Events · module PDF page 18\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nA Cold Bear (PDF page 18)\nDirection: Write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\n\nA Cold Bear\nBrrrr! It is getting cold.\nBear needs to get ready for winter.\nFirst, he eats a lot.\nNext, he finds a den.\nThen, he fills the den with leaves, so he will stay warm.\nLast, he eats even more.\nIs Bear ready for winter?\nYes, he is. Winter is here!\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nBear finds a den.\nBear eats a lot.\nBear eats even more!\nBear fills the den with leaves, so he will stay warm.\nBear needs to get ready for winter.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nMy Dolly \n1. B \n2. A \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \nJoy’s Aya \n1. C \n2. A \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nLita the Cow \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nRosa’s Goat \n1. R \n2. F \n3. R \n4. F \n5. R \nBenny’s Happy Day \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nLily’s Magical Pet \n1. R \n2. R \n3. R \n4. F \n5. F \nA Cold Bear \n1. _3  Bear finds a den. \n2.  2  Bear eats a lot. \n3.  5  Bear eats even more. \n4.  4  Bear fills the den with leaves, so \nhe will stay warm. \n5.  1  Bear needs to get ready for winter. \nDessert Time \n1. 3  Jan gets some cake. \n2.  2 Tim gets a cookie. \n3.  4 Ben gets a donut. \n4. 1  It is time for dessert. \n5. 5  Deb gets some pie. \nHarry and the Crayon \n1. 2  He took the bag with c