(329,17,18217,'Activity 17','Alex and His Mother','Making Predictions/Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nActivity 17: Alex and His Mother · skill: Making Predictions/Conclusions · module PDF pages 26, 27\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nAlex and His Mother (PDF pages 26, 27)\nRead the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nAlex and His Mother\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nAlex’s mother checked her list while she carried a basket. They went up from one lane to another. This perhaps means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother went to a picnic.\n☐ Alex and his mother went to a store.\n\nThe basket was getting full. They now had vegetables, fruits, and bananas in the basket. They still needed to get milk, bread, eggs, and rice. This perhaps means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother were buying.\n☐ Alex and his mother were eating.\n\nMany people are waiting in a lane, with baskets full of groceries. Then they stood in line and waited from one customer to another. This probably means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother were paying for their groceries.\n☐ Alex and his mother were choosing from the shelves.\n\nAlex hoped they would get home in time as they waited for a ride for him to go outside and play for a while. This probably means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother are at the park.\n☐ Alex and his mother are at the bus terminal.\n\nHis mother put their groceries on top of the table. He went to his room and immediately changed his clothes. This probably means that:\n☐ Alex and his mother are now inside their house.\n☐ Alex and his mother ar