(330,17,19218,'Activity 18','Karen’s Puzzle','Making Predictions/Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nActivity 18: Karen’s Puzzle · skill: Making Predictions/Conclusions · module PDF pages 28, 29\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nKaren’s Puzzle (PDF pages 28, 29)\nRead the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nKaren’s Puzzle\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nKaren opened a puzzle box and put all the pieces out on the table. This perhaps means that:\n☐ the box was full of fruits.\n☐ the box was full of pictures.\n\nAll the pieces would go together to take a picture of a beautiful butterfly. There were 15 different pieces to put together. This perhaps means that:\n☐ Karen is getting annoyed with the puzzle.\n☐ Karen is starting to put together the puzzle.\n\nKaren looked for pieces that looked like the butterfly’s wings. Soon she had four pieces put together. This probably means that:\n☐ Karen is starting to put together a puzzle.\n☐ Karen is coloring a picture with crayons.\n\nShe was very happy with the result. She was proud of herself and she couldn’t wait to show her mom. This probably means that:\n☐ Karen has completed the puzzle.\n☐ Karen did not finish the puzzle.\n\nKaren asked her mother for another puzzle. This time she wants to have a flower. This probably means that:\n☐ Karen liked playing the puzzle.\n☐ Karen does not want to play puzzle again.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nMy Dolly \n1. B \n2. A \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \nJoy’s Aya \n1. C \n2. A \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nLita the Cow \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nRosa’s Goat \n1. R \n2. F \n3. R \n4. F \n5. R \nBenny’s Happy Day \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nLily’s Magical Pet \n1. R \n2. R \n3. R \n4. F \n5. F \nA Cold Bear \n1. _3  Bear finds a den. \n2.  2  Bear eats a lot. \n3.  5  Bear eats even more. \n4.  4  Bear fills the den with leaves, so \nhe will stay warm. \n5.  1  Bear needs to get ready for winter. \nDessert Time \n1. 3  Jan gets some cake. \n2.  2 Tim gets a cookie. \n3.  4 Ben gets a donut. \n4. 1  It is time for dessert. \n5. 5  Deb gets some pie. \nHarry and the Crayon \n1. 2  He took the bag with crayons. \n2.  3 He sits under the trees. \n3.  1 Harry was dreaming. \n4.  4 He lays his bag and draws. \n5. 5  He uses his crayons in drawing. \nHarry and the Crayon \n1.  2 He took his bag with crayons. \n2. 3  He sits under the trees. \n3.  1 Harry was dreaming. \n4. 4  He lays his bag and draws. \n5. 5  He uses his crayons in drawing. \nMy Pet \n1. 5 I love my pet dog. \n2. 3 He eats fish and bones. \n3. 1 I have a pet. \n4. 2 His name is Whitey. \n5. 4 He likes to play hide and seek.\n\nPDF page 37\n32 \nPre Test/Post Test \n16. Matt did not study \n17. To ease the pain \n18. Jean went inside \nher house \n19. Jean was unhappy \nA. so Emmy got a wound. \nB. because the wind blows \nballoon. \nC. Emmy eats ice cream. \n20. She fell off her bike \nD. therefore he failed the Math \ntest \nE. because she is tired. \n1. B \n9. R \n2. A \n10. R \n3. A \n11. 3 \n4. B \n12. 1 \n5. B \n13. 5 \n6. R \n14. 4 \n7. R \n15. 2 \n8. F \nActivities \nCause \n1. Hector got scared \n2. Letty studied for the next test. \n3. Luis fell off his bike \n4. It rained all night \n5. Mary ran fast to Luis \nEffect \nA. so she slipped. \nB. so his knee got wounded. \nC. so the classes are cancelled. \nD. so she got an A grade. \nE. so he went home. \nFishing \n1. Father and Eric wi