(331,17,20219,'Activity 19','Watching a Circus Show','Making Predictions/Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nActivity 19: Watching a Circus Show · skill: Making Predictions/Conclusions · module PDF pages 30, 31\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nWatching a Circus Show (PDF pages 30, 31)\nRead the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nWatching a Circus Show\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nFrankie’s dad bought snacks for everyone before they went in to watch the show. This probably means that:\n☐ They will watch a movie.\n☐ They will watch a circus.\n\nFirst, clowns were running around doing tricks and beeping little horns. This probably means that:\n☐ Frankie’s family is at the birthday party.\n☐ Frankie’s family is at the circus show.\n\nThen there was a parade of elephants, horseback riders, and of course, the clowns. Frankie could not stop clapping his hands. This probably means that:\n☐ Frankie is enjoying the show.\n☐ Frankie is scared.\n\nThen there were men and women walking on high wires far up above the ground. Then came the event that Frankie had been waiting for — the lion tamers! This probably means that:\n☐ Frankie’s family is at the circus park.\n☐ Frankie’s family is at the concert hall.\n\nFrankie told his classmates about his Circus experience. His classmates wanted to watch too. This probably means that:\n☐ Frankie is in school.\n☐ Frankie is in his house.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2.