(332,17,21220,'Activity 20','Fishing','Making Predictions/Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nActivity 20: Fishing · skill: Making Predictions/Conclusions · module PDF page 32\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nFishing (PDF page 32)\nRead the sentence in each number and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nFishing\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nDad and Eric prepare a hook. This probably means that:\n☐ Father and Eric will go farming.\n☐ Father and Eric will go fishing.\n\nEric’s dad helped him put bait on his hook. This probably means that:\n☐ His dad does not want Eric to get hurt.\n☐ His dad does not care about Eric.\n\nHe doesn’t want Eric to be hurt. He showed Eric how to toss his hook out into the water. Then they waited. This probably means that:\n☐ They started fishing.\n☐ They started swimming.\n\nThe hook started to move. When his father took it, it caught a big fish. This probably means that:\n☐ Eric is happy.\n☐ Eric is sad.\n\nWhen they had caught enough fish, Eric’s father started to light a fire. This probably means that:\n☐ Eric’s father will swim.\n☐ Eric’s father will cook the fish they catch.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nMy Dolly \n1. B \n2. A \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \nJoy’s Aya \n1. C \n2. A \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nLita the Cow \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nRosa’s Goat \n1. R \n2. F \n3. R \n4. F \n5. R \nBenny’s Happy Day \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nLily’s Magical Pet \n