(333,17,22300,'Post-test','Reading comprehension test','Show how much your reading comprehension has grown.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 1\nPost-test: Post-test · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 33, 34\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nPost-test · Reading (PDF page 33)\nDirection: Read the questions/sentence carefully and encircle the correct answer.\n\nTito is a smart ______.\na. cat\nb. dog\nc. pig\n\nTito eats ______.\na. rice and fish\nb. rice and meat\nc. rice and fruits\n\nDana’s father is a ______?\na. farmer\nb. driver\nc. teacher\n\nWhat did he plant on the farm?\na. Ubi and gabi\nb. Rice and corn\nc. Sugar cane\n\nWho is Dolly?\na. a cat\nb. a doll\nc. a rat\n\nPost-test · Reality or Fantasy (PDF page 33)\nDirection: Write R for Reality and F for Fantasy on the space provided.\n\nA cow can give milk.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe baby goats drink milk from their mother goat.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe grass eats the mother goat.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nHorse Lino, goat Lucy and cow Lita are animals.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nCows and goats can give milk and meat too.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nPost-test · Sequencing (PDF page 34)\nDirection: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Write numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank provided.\n\nItems 11–15. Write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event to show the order.\n11. Bear finds a den.\n12. Bear eats a lot.\n13. Bear eats even more!\n14. Bear fills the den with leaves, so he will stay warm.\n15. Bear needs to get ready for winter.\n\nPost-test · Cause and Effect (PDF page 34)\nDirection: Draw a line to match each cause on the left with its effect on the right.\n\nColumn A\n16. Matt did not study\n17. To ease the pain\n18. Jean went inside her house\n19. Jean was unhappy\n20. Emmy got a wound\nA. because she fell off her bike.\nB. because the wind blows her balloon.\nC. Emmy eats an ice cream.\nD. so he failed the Math test.\nE. because she was tired.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 36\n31 \nAnswer Key \nPretest \nMy Friend \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. A \n5. B \nThe Farmer \n1. B \n2. C \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nMy Dolly \n1. B \n2. A \n3. B \n4. B \n5. B \nJoy’s Aya \n1. C \n2. A \n3. A \n4. B \n5. B \nLita the Cow \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nRosa’s Goat \n1. R \n2. F \n3. R \n4. F \n5. R \nBenny’s Happy Day \n1. R \n2. F \n3. F \n4. R \n5. R \nLily’s Magical Pet \n1. R \n2. R \n3. R \n4. F \n5. F \nA Cold Bear \n1. _3  Bear finds a den. \n2.  2  Bear eats a lot. \n3.  5  Bear eats even more. \n4.  4  Bear fills the den with leaves, so \nhe will stay warm. \n5.  1  Bear needs to get ready for winter. \nDessert Time \n1. 3  Jan gets some cake. \n2.  2 Tim gets a cookie. \n3.  4 Ben gets a donut. \n4. 1  It is time for dessert. \n5. 5  Deb gets some pie. \nHarry and the Crayon \n1. 2  He took the bag with crayons. \n2.  3 He sits under the trees. \n3.  1 Harry was dreaming. \n4.  4 He lays his bag and draws. \n5. 5  He uses his crayons in drawing. \nHarry and the Crayon \n1.  2 He took his bag with crayons. \n2. 3  He sits under the trees. \n3.  1 Harry was dreaming. \n4. 4  He lays his bag and draws. \n5. 5  He uses his crayons in drawing. \nMy Pet \n1. 5 I love my pet dog. \n2. 3 He eats fish and bones. \n3. 1 I have a pet. \n4. 2 His name is Whitey. \n5. 4 He likes to play hide and seek.\n\nPDF page 37\n32 \nPre Test/Post Test \n16. Matt did not study \n17. To ease the pain \n18. Jean went inside \nher house \n19. Jean was unhappy \nA. so Emmy got a wound. \nB. because the wind blows \nballoon. \nC. Emmy eats ice cream. \n20. She fell off her bike \nD. therefore he failed the Math \ntest \nE. because she is tired. \n1. B \n9. R \n2. A \n10. R \n3. A \n11. 3 \n4. B \n12. 1 \n5. B \n13. 5 \n6. R \n14. 4 \n7. R \n15. 2 \n8. F \nActivities \nCause \n1. Hector got scared \n2. Letty studied for the next test. \n3. Luis fell off his bike \n4. It rained all night \n5. Mary ran fast to Luis \nEffect \nA. so she slipped. \nB. so his knee got wounded. \nC. so the classes are cancelled. \nD. so she got an A grade. \nE. so he went home. \nFishing \n1. Father and Eric will go fishing. \n2. His dad does not want Eric to get hurt. \n3. They started fishing. \n4. Eric is happy. \n5. Eric’s father will cook the fish they caught. \nGood Ways \nCause \nLino went to the garden \nHe picked malunggay leaves \nLino cooked the vegetables \nHe was walking fast \nTo be able to bring home \nsome vegetables \nEffect \nso they had a \ndelicious viand. \nwhen a branch hit \nhis head. \nand rubbed it on his \nforehead \nhe gathered it. \nto check the \nvegetables. \nSnowball Fight \nJan was hit by a snowball \nMark throws a snowball \nThey saw a bear \nEffect \nthe snowball knocks \nJan down. \nthey ran fast. \nbecause he was not fast \nenough. \nto make snowballs. \nAlex and His Mother \n1. Alex and his mother went to a store. \n2. Alex and his mother were buying. \n3. Alex and his mother were paying for their groceries. \n4. Alex and his mother are at the bus terminal. \n5. Alex and his mother are now inside their house. \nKaren’s Puzzle \n1. The box was full of pictures. \n2. Karen is starting to put the pieces together. \n3. Karen is starting to put together a puzzle. \n4. Karen has completed the puzzle. \n5. Karen liked playing the puzzle. \nHappenings \nCause \n1. Matt did not study \n2. To ease the pain \n3. Jean went inside her house \n4. Jean was unhappy. \n5. She fell off her bike. \nEffect \nA. so Emmy got a wound. \nB. because the wind blows \nher balloon. \nC. Emmy eats ice cream. \nD. there he failed the Math \ntest. \nE. because she is tired. \nWatching a Circus Show \n1. They will watch a circus. \n2. Frankie’s family is at a magic show. \n3. Franlie is enjoying the show. \n4. Frankie’s family is at the circus park. \n5. Frankie is in school.','[33, 34]',NULL,1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(334,18,1100,'Pretest','Reading comprehension test','Show how well you understand what you read before the lessons.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nPretest: Pretest · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 45, 46, 47\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nPretest · Reading (PDF page 45)\nDirection: Read carefully and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nI have ______.\na. a car\nb. a friend\nc. a pen\n\nHis name is ______.\na. Ben\nb. Tim\nc. Tom\n\nI went to the ______.\na. farm\nb. park\nc. zoo\n\nWho lived in the palace?\na. King\nb. Princess\nc. Queen\n\nWhere does the king sit to watch people?\na. balcony\nb. inside the palace\nc. office\n\nPretest · Reality or Fantasy (PDF page 45)\nDirection: On the space provided, write R if it is Reality, F if it is Fantasy.\n\nBirds can be seen in the park.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe birds hop in the trees.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds read books in the library.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe birds drive cars to school.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds fluff their feathers.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nPretest · Sequencing (PDF page 45)\nDirection: Arrange the events below in the correct order. Write numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank before each event.\n\nItems 11–15. Write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event to show the order.\n11. They are stories about brave kids.\n12. She loved to read about Sherlock Holmes, who was a brave detective.\n13. She loves to read.\n14. She is a quiet girl.\n15. She loved adventure stories.\n\nPretest · Cause and Effect (PDF page 46)\nDirection: After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed at night so…\n☐ the classes were cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jan studied hard so…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: She fell off her bike so…\n☐ she bruised her arm.\n☐ she ate ice cream.\n\nCause: Amora did not study so…\n☐ she failed the exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.\n\nPretest · In the Barn (PDF pages 46, 47)\nDirection: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIn the Barn\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nThe animals came to the barn. They told each other about their moms. “My mom lay me in the nest,” the chick said. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The chick came out of an egg.\n☐ The chick came out of a shell.\n\n“My mom is a big animal,” the calf said. “She eats plenty of grass to produce milk for me.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him milk.\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him an egg.\n\n“My mother stays in the pen. She says oink, oink, oink,” said the piglet. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also oink, oink, oink.\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also meow, meow, meow.\n\n“My mom loves to eat bones. She guards the master’s house.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ Her mom is a dog who barks at strangers.\n☐ Her mom is a cat who calls at strangers.\n\n“My mother pulls carriages and can be used for transportation,” said the baby horse. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His mother is hardworking.\n☐ His mother just sleeps all day.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                          Rex’s New Dog \n1. B                                                                    1. R \n2. A                                                                   2. F \n3. B                                                                    3. R \n4. A                                                                   4. F \n5. A                                                                   5. F \nMy Pet Dog                                                    My New Pet \n1. C                                                                     1. R \n2. C                                                                     2. F \n3. B                                                                      3. F \n4. A                                                                     4. F \n5. C                                                                     5. R \nAt the Farm                                                Pushing and Pulling \n1. A                                                __3__Engines help to push big and heavy things \n2. B                                                __2__Heavy things are hard to move. \n3. A                                             __4__ Wheels make it easier to push heavy things \n4. B                                              ___5__ Trucks have engines and wheels. \n5.B                                         ___1___ We move things by push them or by pulling them \nThe King                                               Ann \n1. A                                               ___5___ Luis rides the big fast train to work everyday \n2. C                                              ___2____Nina rides the big bus to work.                                   \n3. A                                              ___1____ Ann rides her bicycle. \n4. A                                              ___4____Luis rides the train. \n5. C                                              ___3____Nina rides the big slow bus to work everyday \nAt the Park                                         My Mom \n          1. R                                          ___4___ She takes good care of everyone in the family. \n          2. R                                       ____1 ___Her name is George, and she is her mother, Franklin. \n          3. F                                        ____5 ___She is the best mother in the world. \n          4. F                                       ____2 ___Her mother is a doctor. \n          5. R                                       ____3___ she plays with George and tells her bedtime stories. \n         Molly Reads Stories \n         1. R \n         2. R \n         3. F \n         4. F \n         5. R \n44\n\nPDF page 50\nPearl                                                                                                   Day 17 Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions \n____4____ It is stories about brave kids.                                        1. They must get permission from their parents.                   \n____5____ She loved to read about Sherlock                                 2. Their parents must accompany them. \nHolmes, who was a brave detective.                                                3. They usually like to watch movies. \n____2____She loves to read.                                                             4. They want to eat while watching movie. \n____1 ____She is a quiet girl.                                                              5. They all liked the movie. \n____3 ____She loved adventure stories.                                    Day 18 Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions \nDay 13 Cause and Effect                                                                       1. She ran to the bank to help the dog. \n                                                                                                                   2. She feels sorry for the dog. \n      1. it barked and chased it.                                                               3. The boys only followed their father’s                               \n      2. her mom baked a cake.                                                                            C