(341,18,8207,'Activity 7','Rex’s New Dog','Fantasy and Reality: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nActivity 7: Rex’s New Dog · skill: Fantasy and Reality · module PDF page 18\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLESSON GUIDE (module PDF page 17)\nLesson Guide \nTitle: Rex’s New Dog \nActivity 2.3 Fantasy and Reality \nA Fantasy is something that is imaginary and not real. \nReality is something that is real and can happen in everyday \nlife. \nObjectives: \nLearners will be able to distinguish between reality and \nfantasy. \nMaterials: \n1. Storybook \n2. Printed pictures \nDirection:  \nWrite R for reality and F for fantasy on the space \nprovided.  \n12\n\nRex’s New Dog (PDF page 18)\nActivity 2.3 · Fantasy or Reality tells if the events in the story are real or not. Direction: Write R for reality and F for fantasy on the space provided.\n\nRex’s New Dog\nRex got a new dog.\nHe loves to play with his dog.\nSometimes Rex takes his dog to the park.\nThey run and jump and chase each other.\nRex throws a ball for his dog.\nRex has fun with his new dog.\n\nRex got a new dog.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nHis dog could fly over the clouds.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nRex takes his dog to the park.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nRex and his dog barked each other.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe dog went shopping at the mall.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                          Rex’s New Dog \n1. B                                                                    1. R \n2. A                                                     