(343,18,10209,'Activity 9','Pushing and Pulling','Sequencing Events: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nActivity 9: Pushing and Pulling · skill: Sequencing Events · module PDF page 22\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLESSON GUIDE (module PDF page 21)\nLesson Guide \nTitle: Pushing and Pulling \nActivity 3.1 Sequencing/Arranging Events \nIt is the identification of the components of the story-the \nbeginning, middle and end-the ability to retell the events within \na given text in the order in which they occurred. \nObjectives: \nLearners will be able to correctly arrange  \n               the events in order. \nMaterials: \n1. Storybook \n2. Printed pictures \n3. Real object \nDirection:  \nPut the sentences in order by arranging the events \nlisted below. Before each event, write the numbers 1,2,3,4, and \n5 in the blank. \n16\n\nPushing and Pulling (PDF page 22)\nActivity 3.1 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nPushing and Pulling\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them. Heavy things are hard to move. We want to move things; we push them and move them away from us. Wheels make it easier to push heavy things. Engines help to push big and heavy things. When we want to move things, we pull them, we move them towards us. Wheels made it easier to pull heavy things. A cart has wheels to make it easier to pull the cart. Trucks have engines and wheels.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nEngines help to push big and heavy things.\nHeavy things are hard to move.\nWheels make it easier to push heavy things.\nTrucks have engines and wheels.\nWe move things by pushing them or by pulling them.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                          Rex’s New Dog \n1. B                                                                    1. R \n2. A                                                                   2. F \n3. B                                                                    3. R \n4. A                                                                   4. F \n5. A                                                                   5. F \nMy Pet Dog                                                    My New Pet \n1. C                                                                     1. R \n2. C                                                                     2. F \n3. B                                                                      3. F \n4. A                                                                     4. F \n5. C                                                                     5. R \nAt the Farm                                                Pushing and Pulling \n1. A                                                __3__Engines help to push big and heavy things \n2. B                                                __2__Heavy things are hard to move. \n3. A                                             __4__ Wheels make it easier to push heavy things \n4. B                                              ___5__ Trucks have engines and wheels. \n5.B                                         ___1___ We move things by push them or by pulling them \nThe King                                               Ann \n1. A                                               ___5___ Luis rides the big fast train to work everyday \n2. C                                              ___2____Nina rides the big bus to work.           