(345,18,12211,'Activity 11','My Mom','Sequencing Events: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nActivity 11: My Mom · skill: Sequencing Events · module PDF page 26\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLESSON GUIDE (module PDF page 25)\nLesson Guide \nTitle: My Mom \nActivity 3.3 Sequencing/Arranging Events \nIt is the identification of the components of a story-the \nbeginning, middle and end-and the ability to retell the events \nwithin  a given text in the order in which they occurred. \nObjectives: \nLearners will be able to correctly arrange the events in      \n                order. \nMaterials: \n1. Storybook \n2. Printed pictures \n3. Real object \nDirection:  \nPut the sentences in order by arranging the events \nlisted below. Before each event, write the numbers 1,2,3,4,and \n5 in the blank. \n20\n\nMy Mom (PDF page 26)\nActivity 3.3 · Sequencing/Arranging Events. Direction: Put the sentences in order by arranging the events listed below. Before each event, write the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank.\n\nMy Mom\nI am George and she is my mother Franklin. My mother is a doctor. She plays with me and tells me bedtime stories. She takes good care of everyone in the family. She is the best mother in the world.\n\nWrite 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event as they happen in the story.\nShe takes good care of everyone in the family.\nHer name is George, and she is her mother, Franklin.\nShe is the best mother in the world.\nMy mother is a doctor.\nShe plays with George and tells her bedtime stories.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                     