(347,18,14213,'Activity 13','Cause and Effect 1','Cause and Effect: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nActivity 13: Cause and Effect 1 · skill: Cause and Effect · module PDF page 30\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLESSON GUIDE (module PDF page 29)\nLesson Guide \nTitle:  \nActivity 4.1 Cause and Effect \nA cause is WHY something happens. \nThe effect is WHAT happens as a result. \nObjectives: \nLearners will be able to identify the cause and effect  \n                 of the story. \nMaterials: \n1. Storybook \n2. Printed pictures \n3. Real object \nDirection:  \n             After reading through each cause, put a check \n        (/) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.  \n24\n\nCause and Effect 1 (PDF page 30)\nActivity 4.1 · Cause and Effect. A cause is WHY something happens. The effect is WHAT happens as a result. Read and check the most likely effect of each cause.\n\nCause: The dog saw a squirrel…\n☐ it barked and chased it.\n☐ it fell asleep.\n\nCause: It’s Gab’s birthday so…\n☐ her mom baked a cake.\n☐ Her mom scolded him.\n\nCause: The kids are on a field trip at the zoo so…\n☐ they took a Math test.\n☐ they saw a crocodile.\n\nCause: When Ana was little, she was afraid of the chickens on her grandpa’s farm. Because Ana was afraid of the chickens,…\n☐ Her grandpa no longer brings her to the farm.\n☐ Her grandpa showed him how to shoo the chickens away.\n\nCause: Ana learned to shoo the chickens away by waving her hand, saying “Shoo chicks, shoo chicks!” Because Ana learned to shoo the chickens away,…\n☐ She’s no longer afraid of the chickens anymore.\n☐ she played with his grandpa’s dog.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer 