(351,18,18217,'Activity 17','Going to the Movies','Making Predictions/Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nActivity 17: Going to the Movies · skill: Making Predictions/Conclusions · module PDF page 38\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLESSON GUIDE (module PDF page 37)\nLesson Guide \nTitle:  \nActivity 5.1 Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions \nConcluding means figuring something out for yourself.  \nTo draw conclusions, you need to think about what makes the \nmost sense. \nObjectives: \nLearners will be able to be able to make predictions or \ndraw conclusions to complete the meaning of the sentences. \nMaterials: \n1. Storybook \n2. Printed pictures \n3. Real object \nDirection: \nRead the selection and put a check (/) in the box for the \nconclusion that makes the most sense. \n32\n\nGoing to the Movies (PDF page 38)\nActivity 5.1 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. To draw conclusions, you need to think about what makes the most sense. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nGoing to the Movies\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nMy class is going to the movies on the field trip next week. We have to get permission slips signed before we go. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They must get permission from their parents.\n☐ They must ride a bus to go to movies.\n\nWe also need to ask our parents to drive us to the movie theater. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Their parents should not mind them.\n☐ Their parents should accompany them.\n\nWe love it when movies are made from books. It is fun to compare the movie to the book. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They usually like to watch movies based on books.\n☐ They usually liked to read books based on movies.\n\nWe get the movie early so we can buy popcorn. Some of us buy candy too. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They want to eat while watching movie.\n☐ They want to play.\n\nThe movie ended and everyone in the audience clapped. This perhaps means that…\n☐ They wanted to see another movie.\n☐ They all liked the movie.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                          Rex’s New Dog \n1. B                                                                    1. R \n2. A                                                                   2. F \n3. B                                                                    3. R \n4. A                                                                   4. F \n5. A                                                                   5. F \nMy Pet Dog                                                    My New Pet \n1. C                                                                     1. R \n2. C                                                                     2. F \n3. B                                                                      3. F \n4. A                                                                     4. F \n5. C                                                                     5. R \nAt the Farm                                                Pushing and Pulling \n1. A                                                __3__Engines help to push big and heavy things \n2. B                                                __2__Heavy things are hard to move. \n3. A                                             __4__ Wheels make it easier to push heavy things \n4. B                                              ___5__ Trucks have engines and wheels. \n5.B                                         ___1___ We move things by push them or by pulling them \nThe King                                               Ann \n1. A                                               ___5___ Luis rides the big fast train to work everyday \n2. C                                              ___2____Nina rides the big bus to work.                                   \n3. A                                              ___1____ Ann rides her bicycle. \n4. A                                              ___4____Luis rides the train. \n5. C                                              ___3____Nina rides the big slow bus to work everyday \nAt the Park                                         My Mom \n          1. R                                          ___4___ She takes good care of everyone in the family. \n          2. R                                       ____1 ___Her name is George, and she is her mother, Franklin. \n          3. F                                        ____5 ___She is the best mother in the world. \n          4. F                                       ____2 ___Her mother is a doctor. \n          5. R                                       ____3___ she plays with George and tells her bedtime stories. \n         Molly Reads Stories \n         1. R \n         2. R \n         3. F \n         4. F \n         5. R \n44\n\nPDF page 50\nPearl                                                                                                   Day 17 Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions \n____4____ It is stories about brave kids.                                        1. They must get permission from their parents.                   \n____5____ She loved to read about Sherlock                                 2. Their parents must accompany them. \nHolmes, who was a brave detective.                                                3. They usually like to watch movies. \n____2____She loves to read.                                      