(352,18,19218,'Activity 18','Reward','Making Predictions/Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nActivity 18: Reward · skill: Making Predictions/Conclusions · module PDF page 40\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLESSON GUIDE (module PDF page 39)\nLesson Guide \nTitle:  \nActivity 5.2 - Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions \nDrawing conclusions means figuring something out \n for yourself. To draw conclusions, you need to think  \nabout what makes the most sense. \nObjectives: \nLearners will be able to be able to make predictions or \ndraw conclusions to complete the meaning of the \n sentences. \nMaterials: \n1. Storybook \n2. Printed picture \n3. Real object \nDirection: \nRead the selection and put a (/) in the box for the \nconclusion that makes the most sense. \n34\n\nReward (PDF page 40)\nActivity 5.2 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nReward\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIda was a kind-hearted girl. One day when she’s crossing a bridge, she saw two boys on the stream, trying to drown a little dog. This perhaps means that…\n☐ She wanted to join the boys in drowning the dog.\n☐ She ran to the bank to help the dog.\n\nIda was crying loudly, “Oh! How can you be so cruel to that poor little dog?” This perhaps means that…\n☐ She feels sorry for the dog.\n☐ She wants to hit the boys.\n\nOne of the boys said, “Father told us to drown it.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The boys only followed their father.\n☐ The boys willingly wants to drown the dog.\n\nThe dog reached the bank and crept toward Ida. “Poor little fellow,” she said, patting him. This perhaps means that…\n☐ She wants to throw the dog away.\n☐ She wants to adopt the dog.\n\n“Yes,” said the boys, “You may have him.” Ida thanked the boys and ran home. This perhaps means that…\n☐ Ida is going home happy.\n☐ Ida is going home sad.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                          Rex’s New Dog \n1. B                                                                    1. R \n2. A                                                                   2. F \n3. B                                                                    3. R \n4. A                                                                   4. F \n5. A                                                                   5. F \nMy Pet Dog                                                    My New Pet \n1. C                                                                     1. R \n2. C                                                                     2. F \n3. B                                                                      3. F \n4. A                                                                     4. F \n5. C                                                                     5. R \nAt the Farm                                                Pushing and Pulling \n1. A                                                __3__Engines help to push big and heavy things \n2. B                                                __2__Heavy things are hard to move. \n3. A                                             __4__ Wheels make it easier to push heavy things \n4. B                                              ___5__ Trucks have engines and wheels. \n5.B                                         ___1___ We move things by push them or by pulling them \nThe King               