(353,18,20219,'Activity 19','In the Barn','Making Predictions/Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nActivity 19: In the Barn · skill: Making Predictions/Conclusions · module PDF page 42\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLESSON GUIDE (module PDF page 41)\nLesson Guide \nTitle:  \nActivity 5.3 Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions  \nDrawing Conclusions means figuring something out  \nfor yourself. To draw conclusions, you need to think about  \nwhat makes the most sense. \nObjectives: \nLearners will be able to make predictions or draw \nconclusions to complete the meaning of the sentences. \nMaterials: \n1. Storybook \n2. Printed pictures \n3. Real object \nDirection: \nRead the selection and put a (/) in the box for the \nconclusion that makes the most sense. \n36\n\nIn the Barn (PDF page 42)\nActivity 5.3 · Drawing conclusions means figuring something out for yourself. Direction: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIn the Barn\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nThe animals came to the barn. They told each other about their moms. “My mom laid me in the nest,” the chick said. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The chick came out of an egg.\n☐ The chick came out of a shell.\n\n“My mom is a big animal,” the calf said. “She eats plenty of grass to produce milk for me.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him milk.\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him an egg.\n\n“My mother stays in the pen. She says oink, oink, oink,” said the piglet. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also oink, oink, oink.\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is meow, meow, meow.\n\n“My mom loves to eat bones. She guards the master’s house.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ Her mom is a dog who barks at strangers.\n☐ Her mom is a cat who calls at strangers.\n\n“My mother pulls carriages and can be used for transportation,” said the baby horse. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His mom is hardworking.\n☐ His mother just sleeps all day.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                          Rex’s New Dog \n1. B                                                                    1. R \n2. A                                                                   2. F \n3. B                                                                    3. R \n4. A                                                                   4. F \n5. A                                                                   5. F \nMy Pet Dog                                                    My New Pet \n1. C                                                                     1. R \n2. C                                                                     2. F \n3. B                                                                      3. F \n4. A                                                                     4. F \n5. C                                                                     5. R \nAt the Farm                                                Pushing and Pulling \n1. A                                                __3__Engines help to push big and heavy things \n2. B                                                __2__Heavy things are hard to move. \n3. A                                             __4__ Wheels make it easier to push heavy things \n4. B                                              ___5__ Trucks have engines and wheels. \n5.B                                         ___1___ We move things by push them or by pulling them \nThe King                                               Ann \n1. A                                               ___5___ Luis rides the big fast train to work everyday \n2. C                                              ___2____Nina rides the big bus to work.                                   \n3. A                                              ___1____ Ann rides her bicycle. \n4. A                                              ___4____Luis rides the train. \n5. C                                              ___3____Nina rides the big slow bus to work everyday \nAt the Park                                         My Mom \n          1. R                                          ___4___ She takes good care of everyone in the family. \n          2. R                                       ____1 ___Her name is George, and she is her mother, Franklin. \n          3. F                                        ____5 ___She is the best mother in the world. \n          4. F                                       ____2 ___Her mother is a doctor. \n          5. R                                       ____3___ she plays with George and tells her bedtime stories. \n         Molly Reads Stories \n         1. R \n         2. R \n         3. F \n         4. F \n         5. R \n44\n\nPDF page 50\nPearl                                                                                                   Day 17 Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions \n____4____ It is stories about brave kids.                                        1. They must get permission from their parents.                   \n____5____ She loved to read about Sherlock                                 2. Their parents must accompany them. \nHolmes, who was a brave detective.                                                3. They usually like to watch movies. \n____2____She loves to read.                                                             4. They want to eat while watching movie. \n____1 ____She is a quiet girl.                                                              5. They all liked the movie. \n____3 ____She loved adventure stories.                                    Day 18 Making Predictions/ Drawing Conclusions \nDay 13 Cause and Effect                                                                       1. She ran to the bank to help the dog. \n                                                                                                                   2. She feels sorry for the dog. \n      1. it barked and chased it.                                                               3. The boys only followed their father’s                               \n      2. her mom baked a cake.                                                                            Command.                                                           \n      3. they saw a crocodile.                                                                    4. She wants to adopt the dog. \n      4. her grandpa showed him how to                                                5. Ida is going home happy. \n            Shoo the chickens away. \n      5. she’s no longer afraid of the chickens anymore.                 Day 19 Making Predictions/ Drawing                                  \n                                                                                                                                Conclusions \n   Day 14 Cause and Effect                                                                              1. The chick came out of an egg \n                                                                                                                            2. The calf’s mom give him milk \n        1. he got wounds on his knee.                                                               3. The sound the piglet makes is also \n        2. the classes are cancelled.                                                                      Oink, oink, oink.    \n        3.