(355,18,22300,'Post Test','Reading comprehension test','Show how much your reading comprehension has grown.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 2\nPost Test: Post Test · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 45, 46, 47\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nPost Test · Reading (PDF page 45)\nDirection: Read carefully and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nI have ______.\na. a car\nb. a friend\nc. a pen\n\nHis name is ______.\na. Ben\nb. Tim\nc. Tom\n\nI went to the ______.\na. farm\nb. park\nc. zoo\n\nWho lived in the palace?\na. King\nb. Princess\nc. Queen\n\nWhere does the king sit to watch people?\na. balcony\nb. inside the palace\nc. office\n\nPost Test · Reality or Fantasy (PDF page 45)\nDirection: On the space provided, write R if it is Reality, F if it is Fantasy.\n\nBirds can be seen in the park.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe birds hop in the trees.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds read books in the library.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nThe birds drive cars to school.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nBirds fluff their feathers.\nR – Reality\nF – Fantasy\n\nPost Test · Sequencing (PDF page 45)\nDirection: Arrange the events below in the correct order. Write numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 in the blank before each event.\n\nItems 11–15. Write 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 before each event to show the order.\n11. They are stories about brave kids.\n12. She loved to read about Sherlock Holmes, who was a brave detective.\n13. She loves to read.\n14. She is a quiet girl.\n15. She loved adventure stories.\n\nPost Test · Cause and Effect (PDF page 46)\nDirection: After reading through each cause, put a check (✓) on the effect that appears most likely to happen.\n\nCause: A boy fell off his bike so…\n☐ he rode his bike again.\n☐ he got wounds on his knee.\n\nCause: It snowed at night so…\n☐ the classes were cancelled.\n☐ they had a picnic.\n\nCause: Jan studied hard so…\n☐ she passed the test.\n☐ she failed the test.\n\nCause: She fell off her bike so…\n☐ she bruised her arm.\n☐ she ate ice cream.\n\nCause: Amora did not study so…\n☐ she failed the exam.\n☐ she got the highest score.\n\nPost Test · In the Barn (PDF pages 46, 47)\nDirection: Read the selection and put a check (✓) in the box for the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nIn the Barn\nRead each part of the story on the next cards. Then check (✓) the conclusion that makes the most sense.\n\nThe animals came to the barn. They told each other about their moms. “My mom lay me in the nest,” the chick said. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The chick came out of an egg.\n☐ The chick came out of a shell.\n\n“My mom is a big animal,” the calf said. “She eats plenty of grass to produce milk for me.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him milk.\n☐ The calf’s mom gives him an egg.\n\n“My mother stays in the pen. She says oink, oink, oink,” said the piglet. This perhaps means that…\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also oink, oink, oink.\n☐ The sound the piglet makes is also meow, meow, meow.\n\n“My mom loves to eat bones. She guards the master’s house.” This perhaps means that…\n☐ Her mom is a dog who barks at strangers.\n☐ Her mom is a cat who calls at strangers.\n\n“My mother pulls carriages and can be used for transportation,” said the baby horse. This perhaps means that…\n☐ His mother is hardworking.\n☐ His mother just sleeps all day.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 49\nAnswer Key:                                                  \nA Friend                                                          Rex’s New Dog \n1. B                                                                    1. R \n2. A                                                                   2. F \n3. B                                                                    3. R \n4. A                                                                   4. F \n5. A                                                                   5. F \nMy Pet Dog                                                    My New Pet \n1. C                                                                     1. R \n2. C                                                                     2. F \n3. B                                                                      3. F \n4. A                                                                     4. F \n5. C                                                                     5. R \nAt the Farm                                                Pushing and Pulling \n1. A                                                __3__Engines help to push big and heavy things \n2. B                                                __2__Heavy things are hard to move. \n3. A                                             __4__ Wheels make it easier to push heavy things \n4. B                                              ___5__ Trucks have engines and wheels. \n5.B                                         ___1___ We move things by push them or by pulling them \nThe King                                               Ann \n1. A                                               ___5___ Luis rides the big fast train to work everyday \n2. C                                              ___2____Nina rides the big bus to work.                                   \n3. A                                              ___1____ Ann rides her bicycle. \n4. A                                              ___4____Luis rides the train. \n5. C                                              ___3____Nina rides the big slow bus to work everyday \nAt the Park                                         My Mom \n          1. R                                          ___4___ She takes good care of everyone in the family. \n          2. R            