(357,19,2201,'Activity 1','A Rainy Day','Noting Details: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 1: A Rainy Day · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 15, 16\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nA Rainy Day (PDF pages 15, 16)\nDirection: Read the story below and encircle the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Rainy Day\nIt was a rainy day. The children could not go out to play. So Lucy, Zeny and Perla stayed in the house.\n\n“Let’s cut out paper fruits for our store,” said Lucy.\n\nSo, the girls got their papers, scissors and crayons. Lucy cut out 5 apples. She colored them red. Zeny cut out 6 mangoes. She colored them yellow. Perla cut out 4 guavas. She colored them green. Then they counted their paper fruits.\n\n“Now we have many pretty paper fruits for our store,” said Perla.\n\nWhat kind of day was it?\nA. Sunny\nB. rainy\nC. bright\n\nHow many girls are in the story?\nA. two\nB. three\nC. four\n\nWhere did the girls stay?\nA. In school\nB. In the yard\nC. In the house\n\nWhat did Lucy cut out?\nA. 5 apples\nB. 6 mangoes\nC. 4 guavas\n\nWhat color were the apples?\nA. Green\nB. yellow\nC. red\n\nWhy did the girls couldn’t go out?\nA. Because it’s raining.\nB. Because it’s so hot .\nC. Because it’s stormy.\n\nHow did the girls make use of their time on a rainy day?\nA. cut out paper fruits\nB. played hide-and-seek\nC. cooked soup\n\nIf you were the girls, how would you spend a rainy day?\nA. play under the rain\nB. sleep\nC. read stories\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5lea