(360,19,5204,'Activity 4','Lost and Found','Noting Details: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 4: Lost and Found · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 21, 22\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nLost and Found (PDF pages 21, 22)\nDirection: Read the story below and encircle the letter of the correct answer.\n\nLost and Found\nPedro and Jose came to school early. There were no other pupils in the school yet.\n\n“Look,” said Pedro. “There is a handbag under the stairs. It is a girl’s handbag.”\n\nJose got the handbag. He opened it. There was a red pencil, a pink handkerchief and fifty centavos in it.\n\n“Let’s look for the owner of this handbag.”\n\n“Good morning, Mr. Cruz. We found this bag under the stairs,” said Jose.\n\nMr. Cruz smiled and said, “Thank you boys. I shall help you find the owner.”\n\nWhat time was it?\nA. Morning\nB. afternoon\nC. noon\n\nWho are the boys in the story?\nA. Pedro and Juan\nB. Juan and Jose\nC. Pedro and Jose\n\nWhat did the boys find?\nA. a book\nB. a handbag\nC. a box\n\nWhere was the handbag found?\nA. Under the building\nB. Under the tree\nC. Under the stairs\n\nWhat kind of handbag was it?\nA. A girl’s handbag\nB. A man’s handbag\nC. A teacher’s hand bag\n\nWhy do you think finding it was so important to Jose and Pedro?\nA. to show greediness\nB. to show honesty\nC. to show dishonesty\n\nWhat would you do if you found something that was lost?\nA. Keep it.\nB. Tell nobody about it.\nC. Return it to the owner.\n\nWhat other way can they do to find the owner of the bag?\nA. announce it during flag ceremony\nB. keep it\nC. do nothing\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B \n62  \nPre Test Answer Key (   \nPre and Post Answer   \nNothing Details)  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. C  \n5. B  \n