(361,19,6205,'Activity 5','The Banana Peelings','Noting Details: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 5: The Banana Peelings · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 23, 24\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe Banana Peelings (PDF pages 23, 24)\nDirection: Read the story below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nThe Banana Peelings\nCelso was eating bananas one evening. He threw the peelings out of the window. In the morning, Celso got ready for school. He did not want to be late for school. He walked fast.\n\n“Ouch!” Celso cried as he stepped on some banana peelings. Down he fell. His clothes became dirty. His books dropped. “Are you hurt?” Mother asked running to him.\n\n“No, Mother, I’m not hurt,” Celso said as he got up. He looked at the banana peelings.\n\n“Somebody did not use the garbage can,” Mother said. “I threw these peelings last night, Mother. Next time I’ll use the garbage can,” said Celso.\n\nWhat did Celso eat?\nA. Mango\nB. bananas\nC. oranges\n\nWhen did he eat the fruit?\nA. One evening\nB. One morning\nC. One afternoon\n\nWho stepped on the banana peelings?\nA. Father\nB. Mother\nC. Celso\n\nWhere was Celso going?\nA. to church\nB. to market\nC. to school\n\nWho saw Celso fall?\nA. Father\nB. Mother\nC. Sister\n\nHow did Celso feel when he stepped the banana peelings and fell?\nA. regretful\nB. happy\nC. angry\n\nIf you saw banana peelings on the floor, what would you do?\nA. Ignore it .\nB. Call someone to pick it up\nC. Put it in the trash bin\n\nWhat could Celso do next time after eating a banana?\nA. throw it anywhere\nB. put it under the chair\nC. put it in the trash bin\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B \n62  \nPre Test Answer Key (   \nPre and Post Answer   \nNothing Details)  \