(362,19,7206,'Activity 6','Getting the General Significance','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 6: Getting the General Significance · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF pages 25, 26\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 25)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFather who was sitting near the children, stopped reading the newspaper. “Today is Sunday. Two days from now your Uncle Fred will arrive from America. What day will it be?” Father asked.\n\n“It will be Wednesday,” Nestor said.\n\n“No, it will be Friday,” little Nenita said.\n\n“That will be on Tuesday,” ten-year-old Vita said.\n\nWho had the correct answer?\nA. Nestor\nB. Nenita\nC. Vita\n\nWhat is the story about?\nA. the coming of Uncle Fred\nB. the days of the week\nC. on a Sunday\n\nWhich sentence is correct?\nA. All the children have the same answer.\nB. Uncle Fred will come home soon\nC. The children do not like to see Uncle Fred.\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 26)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nNida combed her hair and tied it with a ribbon. She changed her sleeping clothes with working clothes. She got a bolo and went to the garden.\n\n“Are you going to help me today?” Father asked.\n\n“Yes, Father. It’s Saturday and I have nothing to do. Lilia is helping Mother. I would like to help you, too.”\n\nWhat time of the day was it?\nA. night\nB. afternoon\nC. morning\n\nWhich is the best title for the story?\nA. Saturday morning\nB. Helping at home\nC. How to Comb\n\nWhy were Nida and Lilia at home?\nA. It was Saturday\nB. They were sick\nC. To play all day\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  