(363,19,8207,'Activity 7','Getting the General Significance','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 7: Getting the General Significance · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF pages 27, 28\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 27)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nCarling and his baby brother were by the window. They were watching Father get ready for the market.\n\nFather put a big basket of camote and a sack of corn in the calesa. There was also another basket of fresh vegetables and fruits. “Father, please buy us something to eat when you come home,” Carling said.\n\n“Take good care of your brother and I’ll buy you some.” Father said as he got into his calesa.\n\nWhat was Father’s work?\nA. a carpenter\nB. a fisherman\nC. a farmer\n\nHow did Carling help at home?\nA. by raising chickens\nB. by taking care of his brother\nC. by raising vegetables\n\nWhich sentence is true?\nA. Father got ready for the market in a jeep.\nB. Carling and his baby brother were by the window.\nC. Carling helped Father get ready for the market.\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 28)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“All flowers are red,” six-year-old Rosa said.\n\n“No, all flowers are yellow,” four-year-old Jose said.\n\n“Come here, you two,” ten-year-old Tina said. “There are white, red, yellow, pink, violet, orange and green flowers. Sampaguita, our national flower is white. Ilang-ilang is green and some daisies are orange. There are red and yellow roses.\n\n“Now I know why flowers are beautiful,” Rosa said. “They are not of the same color.”\n\nWhich is a good title for the story?\nA. Our National Flower\nB. Colors of Flowers\nC. Care of Flowers\n\nWhich is true about flowers?\nA. They have the same color.\nB. They have different colors.\nC. All are white.\n\nWho knows best about flowers?\nA. Jose\nB. Tina\nC. Rosa\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  