(364,19,9208,'Activity 8','Getting the General Significance','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 8: Getting the General Significance · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF pages 29, 30\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 29)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“My pet can bark. It guards our house,” Pablo said.\n\n“My pet lives in a cage. It has brightly colored feathers. It can sing and dance,” Paula said.\n\n“Mine has soft hair. It walks lightly. It catches mice,” Nena said. “I have three pets. One barks, another catches mice and the other lives in a cage,” Merla said.\n\nWhat is the story about?\nA. pets\nB. mouse\nC. dogs\n\nWhat is Pablo’s pet?\nA. dog\nB. cat\nC. bird\n\nWhat are Merla’s pets?\nA. dog, bird, cat\nB. fish, bird, hen\nC. cat, carabao, goat\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 30)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMarina got out of her bed in the middle of the night. She went near mother and said, “Mother, please get up. Let’s go to the toilet.\n\nMother, got up and saw Marina holding her stomach. “I told you not to eat much ice cream yesterday. Did you eat santol and guavas, too?\n\nI did, Mother,” Marina replied.\n\nWhat did Marina do the day before?\nA. ate cake and candies\nB. ate fruits and ice cream\nC. ate peanuts and chicos\n\nWhat does the story tell about Marina?\nA. She got up to study.\nB. She got up to eat santol\nC. She got up to go to the toilet.\n\nWhy was Marina holding her stomach?\nA. It was painful.\nB. She was hungry.\nC. It was full\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B \n62  \nPre 