(365,19,10209,'Activity 9','Getting the General Significance','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 9: Getting the General Significance · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF pages 31, 32\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 31)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nPr---r---r a k !\n\nMother went running to the sala. She saw Pina very pale and trembling. She was holding a broom. On the floor was a broken vase. “I am very sorry, Mother. The vase fell when I moved the table,” Pina said.\n\n“It’s all right. Now be careful in sweeping all the broken pieces away,” Mother said. “Be sure not a piece is left.”\n\nWhich is a good title for the story?\nA. An Honest Girl\nB. Helping At Home\nC. How Pina Trembled\n\nWhat word best describes Pina?\nA. honest\nB. kind\nC. bright\n\nWhat was Pina doing in the house?\nA. playing\nB. cleaning\nC. sleeping\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 32)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\n“I will buy an ice cream cone for the one who can tell the name of the fruit I will describe.” Father said to two-year-old Ofelia and Malu. “Go ahead and describe it,” his daughters replied.\n\n“It’s a fruit and seed at the same time. It has water inside surrounded by white meat,” Father described.\n\n“I don’t know,” Lety and Ofelia replied almost at the same time. “It’s coconut,” Malu, the eldest of the three, replied.\n\nWho got an ice cream cone?\nA. Lety\nB. Ofelia\nC. Malu\n\nWhat game was Father and his daughters playing?\nA. fruit game\nB. guessing game\nC. story game\n\nWhy did Lety and Ofelia not know the answer?\nA. They were still small.\nB. They were old.\nC. They were as old as Malu\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B