(366,19,11210,'Activity 10','Getting the General Significance','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 10: Getting the General Significance · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF pages 33, 34\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 33)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nNardo stopped in front of a small store and counted his money. “Five pesos and thirty centavos!” he said with a smile. He rested for a while. Soon he was on the streets again. “Journal, Bulletin, Inquirer!” he shouted. As he walked calling out his sales, he thought of the birthday gift he would buy his mother. “I will bring home a box of chocolate for her,” he thought.\n\nWhat does Nardo sell?\nA. chocolate\nB. newspapers\nC. cakes\n\nWhy does Nardo want to give his mother a gift?\nA. It was her birthday\nB. It was Mother’s Day\nC. It was Christmas Day\n\nWhat was Nardo’s work?\nA. a newsboy\nB. a bootblack\nC. a janitor\n\nGetting the General Significance (PDF page 34)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nAling Ines was very happy watching her children. Rosita was cleaning the house. Anita was taking care of her baby sister. Lino was watering the plants in the garden. Petra went to the market.\n\n“I told the doctor that you have fever, Mother. He will be here soon,” Petra said when she came from the market.\n\n“Thank you, Petra. You’re a good girl,” Mother said.\n\nWhy was Aling Ines not working?\nA. She was lazy.\nB. She had a visitor.\nC. She was sick.\n\nWhat was the story about?\nA. helpful children\nB. how to clean the house\nC. how to go to market\n\nWhat lesson does the story teach?\nA. Love your neighbor\nB. Love you pets\nC. Love your family\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B 