(367,19,12211,'Activity 11','Hearing Mass · The Big, Pink Bundle of Joy','Drawing Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 11: Hearing Mass · The Big, Pink Bundle of Joy · skill: Drawing Conclusions · module PDF pages 35, 36\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nHearing Mass (PDF page 35)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nHearing Mass\nOne Sunday morning, Father, Mother, Teresita and Marivic were attending mass. They could not wait any longer for the mass to end. During consecration, Marivic began to cry loudly. Everybody turned to look at her.\n\nHow did Mother feel when Marivic started to cry in the church?\nA. excited\nB. angry\nC. embarrassed\n\nIf you were Mother and Father, what would you do?\nA. Spank Marivic\nB. Take Marivic out of the church\nC. Scold Marivic and finish the mass\n\nWhat should Father and Mother do with Marivic next time they go to mass?\nA. Remind Marivic to behave well at church\nB. Let her play in the church patio\nC. Bring her along and not mind if she annoys the other people in the church\n\nThe Big, Pink Bundle of Joy (PDF page 36)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nThe Big, Pink Bundle of Joy\nMother had been in the hospital for five days. She could hardly wait to bring the big, pink bundle of joy to the children. Mother held the pink bundle lovingly to her bosom while Father called for a taxi.\n\nWhere were Father and Mother?\nA. in the hospital\nB. in the supermarket\nC. in the store\n\nWhy were they there?\nA. Mother was sick\nB. Mother delivered a baby\nC. Mother met an accident\n\nWhere were they going?\nA. home\nB. to the hospital\nC. to the park\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3