(368,19,13212,'Activity 12','A Bookworm · The Ferris Wheel Ride','Drawing Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 12: A Bookworm · The Ferris Wheel Ride · skill: Drawing Conclusions · module PDF pages 37, 38\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nA Bookworm (PDF page 37)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Bookworm\nVicente is a bookworm. He likes to read about almost everything. He likes to read adventure stories, nature stories, fairy tales, and biographies. Whenever he gets hold of a book, nothing could stop him from finishing it. He overworks his eyes by reading. He reads even when light is dim.\n\nWhat do you think will happen to Vicente?\nA. He will get tired of reading\nB. He will lose interest in books\nC. His eyes will become poor so he will soon need eyeglasses\n\nWhat should Vicente do to save his eyes?\nA. He should not read at all\nB. He should read with a good light on\nC. He should read only books with big letters.\n\nDoes Vicente know how to take care of his eyes?\nA. Yes\nB. No\nC. Maybe\n\nThe Ferris Wheel Ride (PDF page 38)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nThe Ferris Wheel Ride\nMyrna was scared to ride on the Ferris wheel. One fiesta day, her cousin asked her to ride on the Ferris wheel. When the Ferris wheel turned around, Myrna felt dizzy. She couldn’t look down. She felt as if she was falling.\n\nWhat do you think Myrna wished for?\nA. She wished the ferris wheel would soon stop turning.\nB. She wished that the ferris wheel would never stop turning.\nC. She wished that she had not ridden on a ferris wheel.\n\nDid Myrna enjoy her ride on the ferris wheel?\nA. Yes\nB. No\nC. Maybe\n\nWhat would Myrna do next time?\nA. She would ride on a ferris wheel again.\nB. She would not go to the carnival again.\nC. She would never ride on a ferris wheel again.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \