(369,19,14213,'Activity 13','Anti-Decay Vaccine · Scared Stiff','Drawing Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 13: Anti-Decay Vaccine · Scared Stiff · skill: Drawing Conclusions · module PDF pages 39, 40\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nAnti-Decay Vaccine (PDF page 39)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nAnti-Decay Vaccine\nMost people have had dental problems which start with simple toothache. No matter how well one brushes his teeth, sooner or later cavities are formed which later cause tooth decay.\n\nToday, scientists are busy experimenting to discover a vaccine that would make people immune to tooth decay.\n\nWhy do you think do scientists want to develop the vaccine?\nA. to help children and youth\nB. to help babies\nC. to help people, young and old alike\n\nWhat is the vaccine for?\nA. to prevent bad breath\nB. to prevent deformed teeth\nC. to prevent tooth decay\n\nWhat will be the effect of the vaccine?\nA. Many people will no longer need dentists\nB. People will not brush their teeth anymore\nC. Many people will be saved from pain of having tooth decay\n\nScared Stiff (PDF page 40)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nScared Stiff\nMario watched a horror movie that afternoon. That night when he turned off the light to sleep, he suddenly remembered the ghost in the movie. The ghost seemed to be in every corner of his room. It seemed to be peeping at him from the ceiling from the wall, from the door lock, or from the broken windowpane.\n\nSuddenly, he heard something go clink-clank! Then there was a loud “CRUSH” sound from the kitchen.\n\nWhat could it be?\nA. A real ghost\nB. A robber\nC. A glass shaved by the cat\n\nHow did Mario feel?\nA. thrilled\nB. surprised\nC. scared\n\nWhat was Mario likely to do?\nA. watch another horror movie\nB. read a book\nC. sleep with his brother\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes