(370,19,15214,'Activity 14','Caught in the Rain · A Visit to the City','Drawing Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 14: Caught in the Rain · A Visit to the City · skill: Drawing Conclusions · module PDF pages 41, 42\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nCaught in the Rain (PDF page 41)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nCaught in the Rain\nThe sky was very dark. With his books, Jose ran as fast as he could. He was panting and perspiring. He was only about three blocks away from home when the rain fell. That night, Jose lay shivering on his bed. He was wrapped in thick blankets with a thermometer in his mouth.\n\nWhat happened to Jose?\nA. He was scared of ghosts.\nB. He caught a cold and developed a fever.\nC. He ate an ice\n\nWhen did the story happen?\nA. on a Sunday\nB. on a holiday\nC. on a school day\n\nWhere did Jose come from?\nA. from school\nB. from church\nC. from the market\n\nA Visit to the City (PDF page 42)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Visit to the City\nMang Tibo had not visited the city lately. Every time he came to the city, he would write his son to pick him up at the station. Because he wanted to surprise his son, he did not write him about his coming this time.\n\nMang Tibo was surprised to see the many changes in the city. When he got down the bus, he did not know where to go.\n\nWhat happened to Mang Tibo?\nA. He got lost.\nB. He enjoyed looking around\nC. He took a walk around the place\n\nWhat should Mang Tibo have done?\nA. gone to the nearest radio and TV station\nB. gone back to the province at once\nC. looked for a policeman and asked for help\n\nWhat was Mang Tibo likely to decide?\nA. Never come to the city again\nB. Never leave the province\nC. Never come to the city without asking his son to meet him\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B