(371,19,16215,'Activity 15','First Elevator Ride · Falling in Line','Drawing Conclusions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 15: First Elevator Ride · Falling in Line · skill: Drawing Conclusions · module PDF pages 43, 44\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nFirst Elevator Ride (PDF page 43)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFirst Elevator Ride\nIt was Marcelo’s first trip to Manila. It was his first time to see a train, an electric light, a telephone, a television set and big buildings. It was his first time to ride in a car, an elevator and on an escalator. Marcelo rode in an elevator on his third day in the city. His mother took him to the office of his eldest brother. His brother’s office was in the seventh floor so they rode in the elevator. Inside the elevator Marcelo cried and said, “Let me out of this box!”\n\nWhat do you think did the people in the elevator do?\nA. They did nothing.\nB. They laughed at him.\nC. They told him not to be afraid.\n\nWhy did Marcelo want to go out?\nA. he could not breathe inside.\nB. He was afraid.\nC. He wanted to play.\n\nHow did Marcelo’s mother feel?\nA. proud of Marcelo\nB. ashamed of Marcelo\nC. happy about Marcelo\n\nFalling in Line (PDF page 44)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nFalling in Line\nA little boy was walking on the street. He was holding a pail. Also walking were an old man who was holding a can and a little girl holding a bottle. They would all join a line with people at the corner of the street. Some of the people were holding cans, others, pails and still others, bottles and pitchers. They seemed to be waiting for something.\n\nThen a big red truck was seen coming. How happy the people were! They would hardly keep still on the line.\n\nWhat was the content of the truck?\nA. rice\nB. water\nC. fish\n\nWhat would happen if the truck did not come?\na. the people would have nothing to drink\nb. the people would have nothing to eat\nc. the people would have nothing to sell\n\nHow did the people feel afterwards?\nA. angry\nB. happy\nC. proud\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B \n62  \nPre Test Answer Key (   \nPre and Post Answer   \nNothing Details)  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. C  \n5. B  \nPre test SKILL B- Getting the  \nGeneral Significance  \nAnswer Key  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre test SKILL C- Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre test SKILL D  \nPredicting Outcomes   \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nKey ( Nothing Details) \n1.B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. C  \n5. B  \nPre and Post test SKILL B\n\nPDF page 66\nGetting the General   \nSignificance  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre and Post test SKILL C \nDrawing Conclusion  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre and Post test SKILL D \nPredicting Outcomes   \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A','[43, 44]','assets/images/level6/g3/p043-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(372,19,17216,'Activity 16','An Accident · A Surprise Gift','Predicting Outcomes: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 16: An Accident · A Surprise Gift · skill: Predicting Outcomes · module PDF pages 45, 46\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nAn Accident (PDF page 45)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nAn Accident\nLety heard a jeep stopped very suddenly in front of their house. Then there was a loud cry. She ran to the window to see what happened.\n\nThere was already a crowd of people. Many more people were running to see what happened. Someone was crying loudly.\n\nWhat do you think happened?\nA. The jeep picked up a passenger.\nB. The jeep bumped somebody.\nC. A child got into the jeep.\n\nWhy was an ambulance needed?\nA. Somebody was dead.\nB. Somebody was hurt.\nC. For a joy ride\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Nobody got an ambulance.\nB. the people did not help at all.\nC. An ambulance came to help.\n\nA Surprise Gift (PDF page 46)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Surprise Gift\nNorma’s fever was very high. She kept tossing in bed. After a while, she fell asleep. Then she began talking in her sleep.\n\n“Oh, Mother, please buy me a box of chocolate,” she said. Mother heard her. She went to the store as fast as she could. She was back before Norma woke up.\n\n“Is this mine, Mother?” Norma asked when she woke up. She was holding something.\n\nWhat was Norma holding?\nA. a bunch of flowers\nB. a box of chocolate\nC. a beautiful dress\n\nWhat was she likely to do with it?\nA. keep it\nB. eat it\nC. play with it\n\nHow do you think did Norma feel?\nA. She felt happy.\nB. She felt angry.\nC. She felt sad.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  \n2. A  \n3. B  \