(373,19,18217,'Activity 17','Rico · Why Lina Cried','Predicting Outcomes: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 17: Rico · Why Lina Cried · skill: Predicting Outcomes · module PDF pages 47, 48\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nRico (PDF page 47)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nRico\nRico is in the third grade. He goes to school every day. He listens well to his teacher. He tries to answer all questions asked of him. He works well with his classmates. He finished his school projects on time. At home he studies his lessons before going to bed. He dies his homework neatly and well. When he finishes all his school assignments he tries to help his mother. In this way he makes his mother happy.\n\nWhat grade will Rico likely receive?\nA. poor grades\nB. high grades\nC. failing grades\n\nWhat is likely to happen to Rico?\nA. will not finish his studies\nB. graduate with honors\nC. stop going to school\n\nWhat else will likely happen to Rico?\nA. becomes successful\nB. become lazy\nC. become sickly\n\nWhy Lina Cried (PDF page 48)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nWhy Lina Cried\nFour-year-old Lina came out of the room crying. She just woke up.\n\nMother, still holding needle and thread asked, “What do you want Lina?” Lina did not answer but continued crying.\n\nMother touched Lina. Her hands were hot. Her cheeks were red. Her eyes were red too.\n\n“Call a taxi at once,” Mother told father as she was changing Lina’s clothes.\n\nWhat was Mother doing when Lina woke up?\nA. cooking\nB. reading\nC. sewing\n\nWhy was Lina crying?\nA. She lost her money.\nB. She was sick.\nC. She was hungry.\n\nWhy did Mother need a taxi?\nA. She was taking Lina to a doctor.\nB. She was going to party with Lina.\nC. She was going to the market with Lina.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting