(374,19,19218,'Activity 18','A Letter from Father · A Boy’s Wish','Predicting Outcomes: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 18: A Letter from Father · A Boy’s Wish · skill: Predicting Outcomes · module PDF pages 49, 50\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nA Letter from Father (PDF page 49)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Letter from Father\n“Come, Leah, come, eric,” Mrs. Mislang said. “I have here a letter from your father.”\n\n“What does it say, Mother?” little Eric asked.\n\n“He says that Mindanao is really a land of promise. He wants us to go there soon.” Mrs. Mislang said. We will build our house there and stay there for some years.\n\n“Why did father go there?” Leah asked.\n\n“To earn money for us. He loves us that’s why,” Mrs. Mislang explained.\n\nWhere do you think the father is?\nA. Philippines\nB. America\nC. China\n\nWhat will Mrs. Mislang do?\nA. stay in Manila\nB. plan to go abroad\nC. prepare to live in Mindanao\n\nHow will this story end?\nA. Mrs. Mislang and her children went to Mindanao\nB. Mrs. Mislang and her children stayed in Manila\nC. Mrs. Mislang and her children went to Japan.\n\nA Boy’s Wish (PDF page 50)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nA Boy’s Wish\nAngel has been sick for a week. He is not getting any better. A good doctor visits him every day but he is still very ill. His mother is always near him.\n\nShe is not happy. The doctor said that angel’s sickness cannot be cured. In a few days he will die.\n\n“I want a beautiful schoolbag,” Angel said in his sleep one time. Mother heard it. While angel was still sleeping Mother went to the nearest store. She went to buy something for Angel.\n\nWhat do you think did Mother buy?\nA. ice cream for Angel\nB. schoolbag for Angel\nC. shirt for Angel\n\nHow did Angel feel about it?\nA. happy\nB. angry\nC. sad\n\nHow did this story end?\nA. Angel got mad at Mother.\nB. Angel died.\nC. Angel was happy\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C  \nDay 17 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. A  \nOutcomes  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 19 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \nDay 20 - Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. A  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B \n62  \nPre Test Answer Key (   \nPre and Post Answer   \nNothing Details)  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. C  \n5. B  \nPre test SKILL B- Getting the  \nGeneral Significance  \nAnswer Key  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre test SKILL C- Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre test SKILL D  \nPredicting Outcomes   \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nKey ( Nothing Details) \n1.B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. C  \n5. B  \nPre and Post test SKILL B\n\nPDF page 66\nGetting the General   \nSignificance  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre and Post test SKILL C \nDrawing Conclusion  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nPre and Post test SKILL D \nPredicting Outcomes   \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n4. B  \n5. A','[49, 50]','assets/images/level6/g3/p049-1.webp',1,'2026-11-15 11:14:45'),
(375,19,20219,'Activity 19','Mina’s Father · Getting Ready','Predicting Outcomes: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 3\nActivity 19: Mina’s Father · Getting Ready · skill: Predicting Outcomes · module PDF pages 51, 52\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nMina’s Father (PDF page 51)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nMina’s Father\nMina and mother were on their way to the bank. “What shall we do at the bank, Mother?” Mina asked.\n\n“We’ll deposit the money your father sent us,” Mother said.\n\n“What does father do to earn money?” Mina asked.\n\n“He checks if all letters mailed have correct stamps. He says that he works with friendly Arabs. He said, too, that he is the only Filipino in the office where he works.\n\nWhat is the work of Mina’s father?\nA. teacher\nB. doctor\nC. office worker\n\nWhere do you think does Mina’s father work?\nA. school\nB. post office\nC. hospital\n\nWhat will Mother likely do after depositing the money?\nA. write Father she received the money\nB. write Father she is sick\nC. write Father that she did not receive the money.\n\nGetting Ready (PDF page 52)\nDirection: Read the selections below and choose the letter of the correct answer.\n\nGetting Ready\nHow busy they were! Liza was wiping pieces of furniture. Maya was hanging new curtains. Nilo was sweeping the yard and Pepe was busy borrowing chairs from their neighbors. Mother with three other women were cooking in the kitchen. Father was roasting a pig at the backyard. “How delicious the litson smells!” Pepe said.\n\n“Your friends will enjoy your party, Maya,” Nilo said.\n\n“When I’ll be eighteen years old, will I have a big party like this, Ate Maya?” Liza asked.\n\nWhat was the family preparing for?\nA. a fiesta\nB. a birthday party\nC. a family reunion\n\nWhat is likely to happen?\nA. Many visitors would come.\nB. No visitor would come.\nC. Only father’s friends would come.\n\nHow did the story end?\nA. Liza received many gifts.\nB. Maya received many gifts\nC. father received many gifts.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 64\n60  \nReferences:  \nDeveloping Reading Power 3  \nJack\'s Birdhouse - Level D Children\'s Story | K5 Learning The \nMissing Doll (k5learning.com)  \nMarty the Clownfish (k5learning.com)  \nlevel-g-childrens-story.pdf (k5learning.com) \nAnswer Key:  \nA Rainy Day  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nA Gift from Uncle \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. B  \nTaking Care of  \nAnimals  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. C  \nLost and Found \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n4. B  \n5. A  \nThe Banana   \nPeelings  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n4. C  \n5. C  \nDay 6 – Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 7 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 8 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 9 - Getting  \nthe General  \nSignificance  \n1. A   \n1. B  \n2. B   \n2. B  \n3. A   \n4. B  \nDay 10 - Getting  \nthe General   \nSignificance  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. C  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B\n61  \nDay 14- Drawing   \nDay 18- Predicting  \nDay 11 – Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. A  \n1. A  \n2. B\n\nPDF page 65\n3. A  \nDay 12 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. B  \n3. C  \nDay 13 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. B  \n3. C  \n3. B  \n1. B  \n2. A  \n3. C \nConclusion  \n1. B  \n2. C  \n3. B  \n1. A  \n2. C  \n3. C  \nDay 15 - Drawing  \nConclusion  \n1. C  \n2. A  \n3. B  \n1. C  \n2. C  \n3. B  \nDay 16 – Predicting  \nOutcomes  \n1. B  \n2. B  \n3. B  \n1.