(385,20,8207,'Activity 7','Pal Is Sick','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 4\nActivity 7: Pal Is Sick · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF pages 27, 28\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nPal Is Sick (PDF pages 27, 28)\nInstructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nPal Is Sick\nPal was crying in his bed. He did not like the things that happened that day. “You will have to take this with a glass of water. It tastes fine, like candy.” Said a nurse by his bedside. “Take it and you’ll see that you’ll start feeling fine.” “No! No! I don’t want anything, I don’t even want to stay here. I want to go home,” cried Pal.\n\n“I will stay with you here, Pal,” said mother. “We shall go home as soon as you get well. Take what the nurse is giving you so you will get well soon. Then we can go home.\n\nWho is in the bed crying?\nA. Dante\nB. Carlo\nC. Pal\n\nWhat do you think happened to the boy?\nA. Sick\nB. Fine\nC. Playing\n\nDoes the boy like to stay in that place?\nA. Yes\nB. No\nC. I don’t know\n\nWhere was Pal?\nA. In the school\nB. In the church.\nC. In the hospital\n\nWhat was the matter with him?\nA. He was sick.\nB. He was playing.\nC. He was studying\n\nWhat was the nurse giving him?\nA. Toys\nB. Books\nC. Medicine\n\nwhom you will ask help if you are sick?\nA. Teacher\nB. Friend\nC. Doctor\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 51\n51 \nPre-Assessment/Post-Assessment Answer Key \nANSWER KEY \nANA’S PET \nEXERCISE \nGUAVA JAM