(388,20,11210,'Activity 10','The Birdlings','Predicting Outcomes and Making Inferences: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 4\nActivity 10: The Birdlings · skill: Predicting Outcomes and Making Inferences · module PDF page 31\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe Birdlings (PDF page 31)\nInstructions: Read the given story carefully and silently. After reading, answer the questions based on what you understood. Write only the letter of the correct answer on your answer sheet. Make sure to read each question before answering.\n\nThe Birdlings\nHigh on the tree top, four hungry bird lings lay chirping in their nest.\n\nMother bird was hunting food for its young ones. It was in the wide-open yard looking for fat worms.\n\nA boy with a slingshot came along. Slowly he went near mother bird and shot at it.\n\nWhat a good aim! Mother bird lay on the ground with a broken wing. “I’ll have my catch fried for my supper,” said the boy to himself as he went home whistling with the bird on his hand.\n\nWhat do you think happened to the birdlings?\nA. They learned to look for their own food.\nB. They died of hunger.\nC. The boy took care of them.\n\nWhat happened with Mother bird?\nA. It’s broken wing was treated and it was returned to the birdlings.\nB. It was killed and fried for supper.\nC. It was thrown away.\n\nWhat do you think did the boy have for his supper that evening?\nA. Fried bird\nB. Fried fish\nC. Pancit and soup\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 51\n51 \nPre-Assessment/Post-Assessment Answer Key \nANSWER KEY \nANA’S PET \nEXERCISE \nGUAVA JAM \n1. A \n1.C \n1.B \n2. B \n2. B \n2. A \n3. A \n3.A \n3. C \n4. A \n4.C \n4. C \n5. C \n5.C \n5. A \n6. A \n6.B \n6. B