(391,20,14213,'Activity 13','Months of the Year','Following Precise Directions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 4\nActivity 13: Months of the Year · skill: Following Precise Directions · module PDF page 34\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nMonths of the Year (PDF page 34)\nInstructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.\n\nMonths of the Year\nDo you know the months of the year in their proper order? You may use a scratch paper if you like, in following the directions below.\n\nWrite the first month of the year.\n\nWhat month has the shortest name? Write it down.\n\nWrite the month which comes after July.\n\nWrite the month which comes before September?\n\nWrite the name of the month when Christmas is celebrated.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 51\n51 \nPre-Assessment/Post-Assessment Answer Key \nANSWER KEY \nANA’S PET \nEXERCISE \nGUAVA JAM \n1. A \n1.C \n1.B \n2. B \n2. B \n2. A \n3. A \n3.A \n3. C \n4. A \n4.C \n4. C \n5. C \n5.C \n5. A \n6. A \n6.B \n6. B \n7. A \n7.A \n7. C \n8. C \n9. B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nPEPE \nAND \nTHE GUAVA \nAT THE PUBLIC \nPLAYGROUND \nA FAMILY OF \nMUSICLOVERS \nTHE ARTESIAN \nWELL \n1. A \n1.C \n1.A \n1.A \n2. A \n2.A \n2.C \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.A \n3.B \n4. C \n4.B \n4.C \n4.A \n5. C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.A \n6. B \n6.C \n6.C \n6.B \n7. A \n7.A \n7.C \n7.B \n8.B \n8.B \n8.A \n9.A \n9.B \n9.A \n10.C \n10.B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nRAINDROPS \nCARLOS \nPAL IS SICK \nFLAG \n1. B \n1.A \n1.C \n1.A \n2. B \n2.C \n2.A \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.B \n3.B \n4.B \n4.C \n4.C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.B \n6.A \n6.C \n7.B \n7.C\n\nPDF page 52\n52 \nA JOKE \nTHE BIRDLINGS \nTHE PET BIRD \nBANANA \nPEELING \n1. B \n1.B \n1