(392,20,15214,'Activity 14','The English Alphabet','Following Precise Directions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 4\nActivity 14: The English Alphabet · skill: Following Precise Directions · module PDF page 35\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe English Alphabet (PDF page 35)\nInstructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.\n\nThe English Alphabet\nHow well do you know the English alphabet? Use a scratch paper if you think you need one in following these directions.\n\nWrite down the first letter in the English alphabet.\n\nWrite down the last letter in the English alphabet and encircle it.\n\nDraw a square. Inside it, write the third letter of the alphabet.\n\nWrite the word “boil”. Cross out its, first letter. In its place, write the third letter of the alphabet.\n\nWrite the letter in the alphabet that comes after “m”.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 51\n51 \nPre-Assessment/Post-Assessment Answer Key \nANSWER KEY \nANA’S PET \nEXERCISE \nGUAVA JAM \n1. A \n1.C \n1.B \n2. B \n2. B \n2. A \n3. A \n3.A \n3. C \n4. A \n4.C \n4. C \n5. C \n5.C \n5. A \n6. A \n6.B \n6. B \n7. A \n7.A \n7. C \n8. C \n9. B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nPEPE \nAND \nTHE GUAVA \nAT THE PUBLIC \nPLAYGROUND \nA FAMILY OF \nMUSICLOVERS \nTHE ARTESIAN \nWELL \n1. A \n1.C \n1.A \n1.A \n2. A \n2.A \n2.C \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.A \n3.B \n4. C \n4.B \n4.C \n4.A \n5. C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.A \n6. B \n6.C \n6.C \n6.B \n7. A \n7.A \n7.C \n7.B \n8.B \n8.B \n8.A \n9.A \n9.B \n9.A \n10.C \n10.B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nRAINDROPS \nCARLOS \nPAL IS SICK \nFLAG \n1. B \n1.A \n1.C \n1.A \n2. B \n2.C \n2.A \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.B \n3.B \n4.B \n4.C \n4.C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.B \n6.