(393,20,16215,'Activity 15','Our Nipa Hut','Following Precise Directions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 4\nActivity 15: Our Nipa Hut · skill: Following Precise Directions · module PDF page 36\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nOur Nipa Hut (PDF page 36)\nInstructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.\n\nOur Nipa Hut\nSee our nipa hut, It’s home to all of us; It’s here that we live, Father, Mother and I. Inside our nipa hut, There’s not much to see; A chair, a table, a bed, Which to visitors we give. Behind our nipa hut, Are fruit trees big and small; Duhat, santol, balimbing, Guava, chico, and atis too.\n\nDraw a nipa hut.\n\nCopy the title of the poem in printed form.\n\nCopy the line that tells who lives in the nipa hut.\n\nDraw one of the things that can be seen inside the nipa hut.\n\nWrite at least 3 fruit trees that can be found behind the nipa hut.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 51\n51 \nPre-Assessment/Post-Assessment Answer Key \nANSWER KEY \nANA’S PET \nEXERCISE \nGUAVA JAM \n1. A \n1.C \n1.B \n2. B \n2. B \n2. A \n3. A \n3.A \n3. C \n4. A \n4.C \n4. C \n5. C \n5.C \n5. A \n6. A \n6.B \n6. B \n7. A \n7.A \n7. C \n8. C \n9. B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nPEPE \nAND \nTHE GUAVA \nAT THE PUBLIC \nPLAYGROUND \nA FAMILY OF \nMUSICLOVERS \nTHE ARTESIAN \nWELL \n1. A \n1.C \n1.A \n1.A \n2. A \n2.A \n2.C \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.A \n3.B \n4. C \n4.B \n4.C \n4.A \n5. C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.A \n6. B \n6.C \n6.C \n6.B \n7. A \n7.A \n7.C \n7.B \n8.B \n8.B \n8.A \n9.A \n9.B \n9.A \n10.C \n10.B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nRAINDROPS \nCARLOS \nPAL IS SICK \nFLAG \n1. B \n1.A \n1.C \n1.A \n2. B \n2.C \n2.A \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.B \n3.B \n4.B 