(394,20,17216,'Activity 16','Understanding Directions','Following Precise Directions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 4\nActivity 16: Understanding Directions · skill: Following Precise Directions · module PDF page 37\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nUnderstanding Directions (PDF page 37)\nInstructions: Read each direction carefully and follow the instructions exactly.\n\nUnderstanding Directions\n\nWrite the name of the place in your school where children borrow and read books, newspapers and magazines.\n\nCopy the three words in the list below that refer to animals. Words in the list: vegetable, kitchen, cat, bark, fruit, kettle, tiger, elephant, bag, castle\n\nCopy the word below and write its opposite. Clean-\n\nWrite the word “boil”. Cross out its first letter.\n\nWrite down the name of our country. Underline its first letter.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 51\n51 \nPre-Assessment/Post-Assessment Answer Key \nANSWER KEY \nANA’S PET \nEXERCISE \nGUAVA JAM \n1. A \n1.C \n1.B \n2. B \n2. B \n2. A \n3. A \n3.A \n3. C \n4. A \n4.C \n4. C \n5. C \n5.C \n5. A \n6. A \n6.B \n6. B \n7. A \n7.A \n7. C \n8. C \n9. B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nPEPE \nAND \nTHE GUAVA \nAT THE PUBLIC \nPLAYGROUND \nA FAMILY OF \nMUSICLOVERS \nTHE ARTESIAN \nWELL \n1. A \n1.C \n1.A \n1.A \n2. A \n2.A \n2.C \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.A \n3.B \n4. C \n4.B \n4.C \n4.A \n5. C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.A \n6. B \n6.C \n6.C \n6.B \n7. A \n7.A \n7.C \n7.B \n8.B \n8.B \n8.A \n9.A \n9.B \n9.A \n10.C \n10.B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nRAINDROPS \nCARLOS \nPAL IS SICK \nFLAG \n1. B \n1.A \n1.C \n1.A \n2. B \n2.C \n2.A \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.B \n3.B \n4.B \n4.C \n4.C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.B \n6.A \n6.C \n7.B \n7.C\n\nP