(395,20,18217,'Activity 17','The Kingfisher and the Cat','Reading Exercises for Speed: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 4\nActivity 17: The Kingfisher and the Cat · skill: Reading Exercises for Speed · module PDF page 38\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe Kingfisher and the Cat (PDF page 38)\nInstructions: Read the words or sentences aloud as quickly and correctly as you can. Start when your teacher says “Go.” Read clearly and do not skip any word.\n\nThe Kingfisher and the Cat\nOne fine morning, a kingfisher sat on a branch of a tree. She was busy eating a fresh fish which she caught in the river. A hungry cat ran under the tree and asked a piece of it. The kingfisher did not want to share the fish.\n\nThe cat was very hungry so she thought of a way to get the fish from the kingfisher. She asked the kingfisher to sing.\n\nThe silly kingfisher could not sing at all. But she was so flattered that she opened her mouth and tried. Of course, she dropped the fish.\n\nThe cat gulped it down hurriedly. Then she ran away laughing.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 51\n51 \nPre-Assessment/Post-Assessment Answer Key \nANSWER KEY \nANA’S PET \nEXERCISE \nGUAVA JAM \n1. A \n1.C \n1.B \n2. B \n2. B \n2. A \n3. A \n3.A \n3. C \n4. A \n4.C \n4. C \n5. C \n5.C \n5. A \n6. A \n6.B \n6. B \n7. A \n7.A \n7. C \n8. C \n9. B \n10. C \nANSWER KEY \nPEPE \nAND \nTHE GUAVA \nAT THE PUBLIC \nPLAYGROUND \nA FAMILY OF \nMUSICLOVERS \nTHE ARTESIAN \nWELL \n1. A \n1.C \n1.A \n1.A \n2. A \n2.A \n2.C \n2.A \n3. A \n3.C \n3.A \n3.B \n4. C \n4.B \n4.C \n4.A \n5. C \n5.C \n5.A \n5.A \n6. B \n6.C \n6.C \n6.B \n7. A \n7.A \n7.C \n7.B \n8.B \n8.B \n8.A \n9.A \n9.B \n9.A \n10.C \n10.B \n10. 