(425,22,3202,'Activity 2','Daphne','Noting Details: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 6\nActivity 2: Daphne · skill: Noting Details · module PDF pages 20, 21\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nDaphne (PDF pages 20, 21)\nDirections: Read the passages and answer the questions.\n\nDaphne\nDaphne was a beautiful nymph. The sun god, Apollo, fell in love with her but she rejected him. Once, Apollo saw here and pursued her. Daphne sought shelter behind a big tree. She was out of breath from running. Now, as she leaned on the tree, she looked back with threw herself upon her knees and prayed to be saved from her pursuer. She rose with outstretched arms. Then her fingers fluttered gently, as if blown by a gentle breeze. Little by little she was changed from a beautiful nymph to a laurel tree. Slowly she broke into a smile. Now, she was safe. Apollo could not carry her away anymore.\n\nDaphne sought shelter behind ____.\nA. a big tree\nB. a laurel tree\nC. a large tree\n\nAs she leaned on the tree, she looked back with ____.\nA. round eyes\nB. smiling eyes\nC. frightened eyes\n\nShe was out of breath from ____.\nA. talking\nB. running\nC. laughing\n\nShe prayed to be saved from her ____.\nA. father\nB. pursuer\nC. husband\n\nSlowly she stretched out her ____.\nA. feet\nB. arms\nC. hands\n\nShe threw herself upon her ____.\nA. bed\nB. knees\nC. pillow\n\nShe was changed from a beautiful nymph into ____.\nA. an oak tree\nB. a narra tree\nC. a laurel tree\n\nHer fingers fluttered ____.\nA. slowly\nB. gently\nC. rapidly\n\nShe felt safe, after she became a ____.\nA. tree\nB. nymph\nC. goddess\n\nShe could not be carried away anymore by ____.\nA. Theus\nB. Midas\nC. Apollo\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 58\n51 \nAnswer Key: \nPre-Test \nSkill-A  \nNoting \nDetails \nSkill-B \nGetting \nSignificance \nof a \nSelection \nSkill-C \nPredicting \nOutcomes \nof a given \nevent \nSkill-D \nReading to \nFollow \nPrecise \nDirections \nSkill-E \nReading for \nSpeed and \nComprehension \nThe Face \nin the \nPool1 \nJay’s \nCuriosity \nRice \nWally’s Kite \nA Fairy Tale \nfrom Japan \n1. A \n1. B \n1. C \n1. answers \nmay vary \n1. B \n2. B \n2. C \n2. C \n2. A \n2. A \n3. A \n3. C \n3. A \n3. answers \nmay vary \n3. C \n4. A \n4. \n4.  \n4. \n4. C \n5. B \n5. \n5. \n5. \n5. A \n6. \n6. \n6. \n6. \n6. B \n7. \n7. \n7. \n7. \n7. C \n8. \n8. \n8. \n8. \n8. A \n9. \n9. \n9. \n9. \n9. B \n10. \n10. \n10. \n10. \n10. A \nSkill-A Noting Details \nRules to Follow \nDaphne \nHow the \nRomans \nCooked their \nFood \nFirst Night in the \nCity \n1. A \n1. A \n1. C \n1. A \n2. B \n2. C \n2. C \n2. A \n3. A \n3. B \n3. B \n3. B \n4. C \n4. B \n4. A \n4. B \n5. A \n5. B \n5. B \n5. B \n6. A \n6. B \n6. C \n6. C \n7. A \n7. C \n7. C \n7. C \n8. C \n8. B \n8. C \n8. B \n9. C \n9. A \n9. B \n9. B \n10. B \n10. C \n10. C \n10. A\n\nPDF page 59\n52 \nSkill- B Getting the General Significance of a Selection \nExercise 5 \nExercise 6 \nExercise 7 \nExercise 8 \n1. B \n1. B \n1. C \n1. C \n2. B \n2. C \n2. C \n2. B \n3. C \n3. B \n3. B \n3. C \nSkill-C Predicting Outcome of a Given Event and Making Inferences \nExer \nExercise 10 \nExercise 11 \nExercise 12 \n1. anwers may \nvary \n1. anwers may \nvary \n1. anwers may \nvary \n1.anwers may \nvary \n2. anwers may \nvary \n2. anwers may \nvary \n2. anwers may \nvary \n2. anwers may \nvary \n3. anwers may \nvary \n3. anwers may \nvary \n3. anwers may \nvary \n3.. anwers may \nvary \nSkill-D Reading to Follow Precise Directions \nThe Earthworm \nRizal and the \nFilipino Youth \nChristmas Eve \nHints for \nKeeping Friends \n1. \n1. \n1. anwers may \nvary \n1. B \n2. \n2. B \n2. \n2. C \n3. \n3. \n3. A \n3. A \n4. \n4. 