(429,22,7206,'Activity 6','The Crayfish','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 6\nActivity 6: The Crayfish · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF page 28\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe Crayfish (PDF page 28)\nDirections: Read the passages and answer the questions.\n\nThe Crayfish\nThe most striking thing in the appearance of the crayfish is the pair of nippers at the tips of its front legs. Joined together are its “thumb and finger”. The “thumb” is jointed so that it can move back and forth freely. Both nippers are armed with saw teeth and a sharp claw at the tip so that they can get a firm grip of any object. The claws can be bent in any direction.\n\nWhat is the story about?\na. the crab\nb. the crayfish\nc. a water animal\n\nWhich is true about the animal described?\na. It has a great pair of nippers on its sides.\nb. It has a great pair of nippers on its hind legs.\nc. It has a great pair of nippers on each tip of his front legs.\n\nWhich sentence describes their claws?\na. It can be bent sideways.\nb. It can be bent in any direction.\nc. It can be bent forward and back\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 58\n51 \nAnswer Key: \nPre-Test \nSkill-A  \nNoting \nDetails \nSkill-B \nGetting \nSignificance \nof a \nSelection \nSkill-C \nPredicting \nOutcomes \nof a given \nevent \nSkill-D \nReading to \nFollow \nPrecise \nDirections \nSkill-E \nReading for \nSpeed and \nComprehension \nThe Face \nin the \nPool1 \nJay’s \nCuriosity \nRice \nWally’s Kite \nA Fairy Tale \nfrom Japan \n1. A \n1. B \n1. C \n1. answers \nmay vary \n1. B \n2. B \n2. C \n2. C \n2. A \n2. A \n3. A \n3. C \n3. A \n3. answers \nmay vary