(431,22,9208,'Activity 8','The Bible','Getting the General Significance: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 6\nActivity 8: The Bible · skill: Getting the General Significance · module PDF page 30\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe Bible (PDF page 30)\nDirections: Read the passages and answer the questions.\n\nThe Bible\nThe Bible is the word of God. The evangelists who wrote the Bible did so at the command and inspiration of God Himself. What God wants to say to us, He has indicated in the Bible, in the Old and New Testament, we learn what God wants of us: to make us know Him, love Him, serve Him and be forever happy with Him in heaven. It is in the Bible where we learn His exact will for us, His commandments, His love and reward for us, and the Last Judgment.\n\nWhat is the selection about?\nA. God’s physical appearance\nB. The Old and New Testaments\nC. The Bible as the Word of God\n\nWhich sentence is true?\nA. It is man’s word that is written in the Bible.\nB. We learn the exact will of God for us from the Bible.\nC. God will appear to us so that we may know what He expects of us\n\nWhat is the ultimate goal of God’s wishes for us?\nA. to punish us\nB. to appear before us\nC. to be forever happy with Him in heaven\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 58\n51 \nAnswer Key: \nPre-Test \nSkill-A  \nNoting \nDetails \nSkill-B \nGetting \nSignificance \nof a \nSelection \nSkill-C \nPredicting \nOutcomes \nof a given \nevent \nSkill-D \nReading to \nFollow \nPrecise \nDirections \nSkill-E \nReading for \nSpeed and \nComprehension \nThe Face \nin the \nPool1 \nJay’s \nCuriosity \nRice \nWally’s Kite \nA Fairy Tale \nfrom Japan \n1. A \n1. B \n1. C \n1. answers \n