(433,22,11210,'Activity 10','Pete’s Catch','Predicting Outcomes and Making Inferences: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 6\nActivity 10: Pete’s Catch · skill: Predicting Outcomes and Making Inferences · module PDF page 32\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nPete’s Catch (PDF page 32)\nDirections: Read the passages and answer the questions.\n\nPete’s Catch\nPete considered himself a fine fisherman. He stood on the riverbank as he held his fishing line with the patience only a fisherman knew. His heart beat faster as he felt a tug on the line. He was excited as he planted his feet firmly on the ground. He gave a big pull expecting to find a big fish at the hook of his fishing line. Disappointment clouded his face as he stared at his catch.\n\nWhat do you think did Pete catch?\nA. a big fish\nB. a big turtle\nC. a boot\n\nWhat kind of fisherman was Pete?\nA. He was an old fisherman.\nB. He was a good fisherman.\nC. He was an impatient fisherman.\n\nWhat did Pete do?\nA. went away\nB. sat on the riverbank\nC. threw his fishing line again into the water\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 58\n51 \nAnswer Key: \nPre-Test \nSkill-A  \nNoting \nDetails \nSkill-B \nGetting \nSignificance \nof a \nSelection \nSkill-C \nPredicting \nOutcomes \nof a given \nevent \nSkill-D \nReading to \nFollow \nPrecise \nDirections \nSkill-E \nReading for \nSpeed and \nComprehension \nThe Face \nin the \nPool1 \nJay’s \nCuriosity \nRice \nWally’s Kite \nA Fairy Tale \nfrom Japan \n1. A \n1. B \n1. C \n1. answers \nmay vary \n1. B \n2. B \n2. C \n2. C \n2. A \n2. A \n3. A \n3. C \n3. A \n3. answers \nmay vary \n3. C \n4. A \n4. \n4.  \n4. \n4. C \n5. B \n5. \n5. \n5. \n5. A \n6. \n6. \n6. 