(434,22,12211,'Activity 11','The Red Sweater','Predicting Outcomes and Making Inferences: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 6\nActivity 11: The Red Sweater · skill: Predicting Outcomes and Making Inferences · module PDF page 33\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe Red Sweater (PDF page 33)\nDirections: Read the passages and answer the questions.\n\nThe Red Sweater\nLourdes opened her piggy bank. She counted her money carefully and went straight to a downtown store. She looked with longing at the bright new sweater on display at the store window. She wanted to inquire about the price but as she was about to go in, she stopped and hesitated. She counted her money again, then shook her head. At last, she looked at the sweater with regret and returned the money into her pocket.\n\nHow did Lourdes feel about the sweater?\nA. She disliked it.\nB. She liked it very much.\nC. She just wanted to look at it.\n\nWhat did she intended to do?\nA. She wanted to buy it.\nB. She wanted to ask for it.\nC. She wanted to ask Mother to buy it for her.\n\nDid she finally get the sweater?\nA. Yes\nB. No\nC. Maybe\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 58\n51 \nAnswer Key: \nPre-Test \nSkill-A  \nNoting \nDetails \nSkill-B \nGetting \nSignificance \nof a \nSelection \nSkill-C \nPredicting \nOutcomes \nof a given \nevent \nSkill-D \nReading to \nFollow \nPrecise \nDirections \nSkill-E \nReading for \nSpeed and \nComprehension \nThe Face \nin the \nPool1 \nJay’s \nCuriosity \nRice \nWally’s Kite \nA Fairy Tale \nfrom Japan \n1. A \n1. B \n1. C \n1. answers \nmay vary \n1. B \n2. B \n2. C \n2. C \n2. A \n2. A \n3. A \n3. C \n3. A \n3. answers \nmay vary \n3. C \n4. A \n4. \n4.  \n4. \n4.