(436,22,14213,'Activity 13','The Earthworm','Reading to Follow Precise Directions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 6\nActivity 13: The Earthworm · skill: Reading to Follow Precise Directions · module PDF page 36\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nThe Earthworm (PDF page 36)\nDirections: Read the passages and answer the questions.\n\nThe Earthworm\nHave you seen an earthworm? Children are afraid of the earthworm. It lives in moist soil. It has no distinct head and it breathes through its skin. If you cut an earthworm in two, the parts will still live.\n\nThe earthworm is harmless. It helps the farmers and plant growers. The earthworm bores many holes in the soil. This way the soil becomes soft and well- mixed. Then more air goes into the soil. Soft, well-mixed and airy soil is good for the plants. Earthworms help the plants grow well.\n\nIn what kind of soil does the earthworm live?\n\nDoes the earthworm have a head? Write Yes or No.\n\nWrite the word that tells where the earthworm breathes through.\n\nWrite the earthworm have a head? Write Yes or No.\n\nCopy the correct sentence.\nA. The earthworm is harmful\nB. The earthworm kills the plants\nC. The earthworm helps the plants\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 58\n51 \nAnswer Key: \nPre-Test \nSkill-A  \nNoting \nDetails \nSkill-B \nGetting \nSignificance \nof a \nSelection \nSkill-C \nPredicting \nOutcomes \nof a given \nevent \nSkill-D \nReading to \nFollow \nPrecise \nDirections \nSkill-E \nReading for \nSpeed and \nComprehension \nThe Face \nin the \nPool1 \nJay’s \nCuriosity \nRice \nWally’s Kite \nA Fairy Tale \nfrom Japan \n1. A \n1. B \n1. C \n1. answers \nmay vary \n1. B \n2. B \n2. C \n2. C \n2. A