(438,22,16215,'Activity 15','Christmas Eve','Reading to Follow Precise Directions: read the story and answer the questions.','Graded Reading Comprehension · Level 6 · Grade 6\nActivity 15: Christmas Eve · skill: Reading to Follow Precise Directions · module PDF page 38\n\nPupils read the story on its own card (Listen reads it aloud), then answer one question per card. Choices, Reality/Fantasy, ordering of events and cause-and-effect matching follow the module. Speed-reading stories have a timer that records the reading time and words per minute.\n\nChristmas Eve (PDF page 38)\nDirections: Read the passages and answer the questions.\n\nChristmas Eve\nIt was Christmas Eve. Mr. Cruz’s family had finished their Noche Buena. “Come on children,” Mother called. “Hang your stockings and go to bed.” Sonia hung one for her mother, one for her father and a very small one for her baby brother. Tess put hers on one corner of her mirror. Dennis pinned his on the curtain of his bedroom window and Edmer found a place near his Cabinet.\n\nWrite the name of the holiday that the children were preparing for.\n\nWhat did the children do before going to bed? Copy the answer.\n\nCopy the phrase that tells what the family would do.\nA. go to bed\nB. go to a party\nC. go to the movies\n\nCopy the sentence that is true.\nA. Sonia hung one stocking for herself.\nB. Sonia hung stockings for herself and her mother.\nC. Sonia hung stockings for her mother, father and for her baby brother.\n\nWrite the name of the boy who pinned his stockings on the curtain of his bedroom.\n\nANSWER KEY (teacher only)\n\nPDF page 58\n51 \nAnswer Key: \nPre-Test \nSkill-A  \nNoting \nDetails \nSkill-B \nGetting \nSignificance \nof a \nSelection \nSkill-C \nPredicting \nOutcomes \nof a given \nevent \nSkill-D \nReading to \nFollow \nPrecise \nDirections \nSkill-E \nReading for \nSpeed and \nComprehension \nThe Face \nin the \nPool1 \nJay’s \nCuriosity \nRice \nWally’s Kite \nA Fairy Tale \nfrom Japan \n1. A \n1. B 