(536,536,'These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s First 100 list:\nsaid   were   one   come   does   two   they   their   what   where\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.','teacher'),
(537,537,'Pick a fish from the basin and read the word on it aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a big basin with fish cutouts that have words on them (e.g., said, were, one, come, does, two, they, their, what, where, when, why).\n2. The learners gather around the basin.\n3. Each learner takes a turn to pick one fish.\n4. The learner reads the word written on the fish aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.','teacher'),
(538,538,'what they said\nwhere they were\ndoes it come\none or two\nwhy they went','teacher'),
(539,539,'They said it was fun.\nWhere were you yesterday?\nDoes she come every day?\nI saw one dog and two cats.\nWhy is their bag on the floor?','teacher'),
(540,540,'said   two   were   they   one   their   come   what   does   where','teacher'),
(541,541,'These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 2nd 100 list:\nagain   because   around   every   know   only   people   right   their   would\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.','teacher'),
(542,542,'Roll the dice, move to the number, and read the word on that space aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a snake and ladder board with words and a dice.\n2. The learners line up and take turns rolling the dice.\n3. The learner moves to the correct number on the board.\n4. The learner reads the word on that space aloud.\n5. The class listens and claps after each turn.','teacher'),
(543,543,'again and again\nbecause they know\naround the corner\nonly the right answer\nevery people’s story','teacher'),
(544,544,'I would go again tomorrow.\nThey walked around the park.\nShe knows every word.\nPeople only want the truth.\nTheir answer was right.','teacher'),
(545,545,'again   only   because   people   around   right   every   their   know   would','teacher'),
(546,546,'These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 3rd 100 list:\nabove   enough   through   though   young   laugh   once   both   always   together\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.','teacher'),
(547,547,'Spin the wheel and read the word it points to aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a Spin Wheel with sight words.\n2. The learners line up and take turns spinning the wheel.\n3. The learner reads the word the arrow points to aloud.\n4. The class listens and claps after each turn.','teacher'),
(548,548,'above the clouds\nenough for everyone\nthrough the door\nyoung and strong\nalways together','teacher'),
(549,549,'She climbed above the hill.\nI have enough food for lunch.\nWe walked through the park.\nThe young boy can laugh loudly.\nThey always work together.','teacher'),
(550,550,'above   laugh   enough   once   through   both   though   always   young   together','teacher'),
(551,551,'These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 4th 100 list:\nbeautiful   country   different   important   against   enough   write   without   second   water\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.','teacher'),
(552,552,'Take turns drawing a word card from the decorated Mystery Box and read it aloud.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares a decorated Mystery Box.\n2. The teacher prints the selected sight words and places them inside the box.\n3. Learners form a line, take turns drawing one word card from the Mystery Box, and read the word aloud.','teacher'),
(553,553,'beautiful country\ndifferent people\nimportant work\nagainst the wall\nsecond water bottle','teacher'),
(554,554,'The beautiful flower is in the garden.\nOur country is big and strong.\nShe has a different idea.\nIt is important to read every day.\nHe drank enough water after the game.','teacher'),
(555,555,'beautiful   enough   country   write   different   without   important   second   against   water','teacher'),
(556,556,'These are 10 difficult words to read from Fry’s 5th 100 list:\nalready   certain   early   family   mountain   sentence   special   sure   toward   usually\n\nFirst, review the words you learned before.','teacher'),
(557,557,'Take turns selecting a leaf from the Word Hunt Table and read aloud the word written on it. You can also hunt for the words in the letter grid.\n\nHow to play:\n1. The teacher prepares the Word Hunt Table and posts it on the board, with the target words written on the leaf.\n2. Learners form a line in front of the board and take turns finding or hunting a word from the leaf.\n3. After selecting, the learner reads aloud the word he or she has found.','teacher'),
(558,558,'already finished work\ncertain answer\nearly morning\nfamily dinner\nspecial gift','teacher'),
(559,559,'already sure\ntowards the mountain\nspecial family\nearly today\nusually certain','teacher'),
(560,560,'She already knows the way.\nI am certain this is right.\nWe woke up early today.\nThe family went to the park.\nHe climbed the mountain with friends.','teacher'),
