(698,698,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the vegetable in Column A with\nits color in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Carrot\na. Purple\n2. Tomato\nb. Green\n3. Eggplant\nc. Orange\n4. Pechay\nd. Red','teacher'),
(699,699,'5. Squash\ne. Green with stripes\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully to the following sentences\nand choose the best answer for each question.\nSentence 1: “This is our school garden”\nSentence 2:“We have vegetables in our garden”\nSentence 3: “I plant vegetable in our garden”\nQuestions:\n1. Where are we?\na. Home\nb. School garden\nc. Park\nd. Store\n2. What do we have in the garden?\na. Flowers\nb. Vegetables\nc. Fruits\nd. Trees','teacher'),
(700,700,'3. What do we do in the garden?\na. Play games\nb. Plant vegetables\nc. Read books\nd. Sing songs\n4. What is something you might find in the garden?\na. Car\nb. Table\nc. Tomato\nd. Bed\n5. What is the main idea of the sentences?\na. Playing inside\nb. Being in the school garden\nc. Eating lunch\nd. Sleeping at home','teacher'),
(701,701,'In The Canteen\nThis is our school canteen.\n| buy food in our school canteen.\nsales lady\nWW\nice drop banana Cue sandwich\nBy . &\nbiscuits juice sweet potato','teacher'),
(702,702,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Choose the best answer for each\nquestion. Encircle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. What is a “sandwich”?\na. A cold treat\nb. Food between two slices of bread\nc. A sweet snack on the stick\nd. A yellow drink\n2. What is “juice”\na. A frozen dessert\nb. Cooked bananas on a stick\nc. A sweet drink made from fruits\nd. A baked treat\n3. What is “banana cue”?\na. A frozen treat\nb. Cooked bananas on a stick\nc. A sweet baked treat\nd. A cold drink\n4. What is an “ice drop”?\na. A cold frozen treat\nb. A hot snack\nc. A baked treat\nd. A drink','teacher'),
(703,703,'5. What are “biscuits”?\na. A frozen treat\nb. Small baked treats\nc. Cooked bananas\nd. A sweet drink\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully to the following sentences\nand choose the best answer for each question.\nSentence 1: “This is our school canteen”\nSentence 2:“I buy foods in our school canteen”\nQuestions:\n1. Where are we?\na. Home\nb. School canteen\nc. Park\nd. Store\n2. What do we do in the school canteen?\na. Play games\nb. Buy foods\nc. Read books\nd. Sing songs\n3. Who helps us in the canteen?\na. Teacher\nb. Sales lady\nc. Doctor\nd. Policeman','teacher'),
(704,704,'4. What is something you might find in the canteen?\na. Car\nb. Table\nc. Sandwich\nd. Bed\n5. What is the main idea of the sentences?\na. Playing outside\nb. Being in the school canteen\nc. Eating lunch at home\nd. Sleeping at home','teacher'),
(705,705,'In The Library\nThis is our school library.\n| read books in the library.\ndictionary magazine rock books\nnewspaper\nlibrarian book shelves magazine','teacher'),
(706,706,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\nmeanings in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on\nthe line before each number.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nBooks\na. A person who works in a library\n2. ______\nMagazine\nb. A daily or weekly publication\nwith news\n3. ______\nNewspaper\nc. A collection of printed pages','teacher'),
(707,707,'4. ______\nLibrarian\nd. A book that list words and their\nmeanings\n5. ______\nDictionary\ne. A periodical publication with\narticles\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. Where does the story take place?\na. At a park\nb. In a school library\nc. In a classroom\nd. At a bookstore','teacher'),
(708,708,'2. Who does the library belong to?\na. The speaker and their friends\nb. The teacher\nc. The public\nd. A bookstore owner\n3. What is the main activity the speaker does in this\nplace?\na. They play games.\nb. They read books.\nc. They draw pictures.\nd. They eat lunch.\n4. What kind of items are found in this place?\na. Computers and toys\nb. Food and drinks\nc. Balls and sports equipment\nd. Books\n5. What is the best title for this passage?\na. My Favorite Teacher\nb. Playing at School\nc. The School Library\nd. Buying New Books','teacher'),
(709,709,'Keeping Our School Clean\nWe take care of our school.\nWe keep our school clean.\nyoul\nS | coconut husk brooms\nJ hh\nwT cleaning mop trash can\njanitor brush','teacher'),
(710,710,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\nmeanings in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on\nthe line before each number.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nJanitor.\na. A container for waste\n2. ______\nBroom\nb. A tool for bristles used for\ncleaning\n3. ______\nTrash Can\nc. A floor covering','teacher'),
(711,711,'4. ______\nRug\nd. A person who cleans\nbuildings\n5. ______\nBrush\ne. A tool used for sweeping\nA. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage.\nThen, answer the Questions below.\nPassage:\n“Every morning, the janitor, Mang Tomas, clans our\nschool. He uses a broom to sweep the floors and a\nbrush to scrub the walls. He throws all the trash into the\ntrash can. Sometimes, he uses a cleaning mop to\nwipe the spills. Our school is clean because of Mang\nTomas”.\nQuestions:\n1. Who cleans the school every morning?\na. Mang Andoy\nb. Mang Tomas\nc. Mang Pedro','teacher'),
(712,712,'2. What does he use to sweep the floors?\na. Cleaning mop\nb. Broom\nc. Brush\n3. What does he use to scrub the walls?\na. Broom\nb. Cleaning mop\nc. Brush\n4. Where does he throw the trash?\na. On the floor\nb. In the trash can\nc. Under the rug\n5. Why is the school clean?\na. Because of the students\nb. Because of Mang Tomas\nc. Because of the teachers','teacher'),
(713,713,'Me and My Community\n| stay ina place.\nSafe and with peace.\nSurrounded with love.\nev A gift noeneve.\nSm','teacher'),
(714,714,'The Community Helpers\nIN our community there are many helpers.\nWe love our community helpers.\nEls he\nteacher policeman _ me a Salpeter\nfarmer fisherman doctor\n“a> on\nie. eeper\nx ae\nk Borer driver fireman nurse','teacher'),
(715,715,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\nmeanings in Column B. Write the letter of your answer on\nthe line before each number.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nFarmer\na. Catches fish from the sea or river\n2. ______\nCarpenter\nb. Grows crops and raises animals\nfor food\n3. ______\nNurse\nc. Sells goods and items in a shop','teacher'),
(716,716,'4. ______\nFisherman\nd. Takes care of sick or injured\npeople in a hospital or clinic\n5. ______\nStorekeeper\ne. Builds and repairs things made of\nwood\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main idea of the passage?\na. Helpers work in a hospital.\nb. There are many different kinds of community\nhelpers.\nc. Teachers are the most important helpers.\nd. Helpers are very busy.','teacher'),
(717,717,'2. According to the passage, how do the people feel\nabout their community helpers?\na. They are afraid of them.\nb. They love them.\nc. They do not know them.\nd. They are angry with them.\n3. Which helper is most likely to help you if you are sick?\na. A policeman and a security guard\nb. A doctor and a nurse\nc. A fireman and a driver\nd. A carpenter and a laborer\n4. Which of the following helpers is NOT mentioned in the\npassage?\na. Fisherman\nb. Pilot\nc. Teacher\nd. Storekeeper\n5. Based on the passage, a community helper is\nsomeone who...\na. works only for money.\nb. lives in a big house.\nc. does a job that helps people in the area.\nd. travels to different countries.','teacher'),
(718,718,'In The Plaza\nThis is our plaza.\nWe play in our plaza.\nOur plaza is very clean and beautiful.\nseesaw monkey bar','teacher'),
(719,719,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect descriptions or functions in Column B. Write\nthe letter of your answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______ Plaza\na. A place of playground\nequipment you down\nsitting or lying\n2. ______\nStatue\nb. A public open space\nin a city or town, often for\npeople to walk and play\n3. ______ Swing\nc. A structure of bars you\ncan swing across using\nyour hands','teacher'),
(720,720,'4. ______\nSlide\nd. A seat hanging from\nropes or chains that\nmoves back and forth\n5. ______\nMonkey bar\ne. A model of a person or\nanimal, made of stone\nor metal\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a\nshort passage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A plaza\nc. A garden\nd. A park','teacher'),
(721,721,'2. What do the children do in the plaza?\na. They study.\nb. They play.\nc. They work.\nd. They sleep.\n3. How is the plaza described?\na. Very big and busy\nb. Clean and beautiful\nc. Old and quiet\nd. Dark and scary\n4. Which of the following items is mentioned as being in\nthe plaza?\na. A swimming pool\nb. A basketball court\nc. A statue\nd. A fountain\n5. The word \"our\" in the passage suggests that the\nplaza...\na. is very far away.\nb. belongs to or is used by the speaker and their\ncommunity.\nc. is new.\nd. is only for children.','teacher'),
(722,722,'In The Market\nThis is OUr market.\nWe can buy our food in the market.\nbutchers weighing scale\nknife\nchopping board\nbutcher','teacher'),
(723,723,'A. Vocabulary\nInstructions: Match the words in Column A with their\ncorrect meanings or uses in Column B. Write the letter of\nyour answer on the line provided.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. ______\nButcher\na. A tool used to measure how\nheavy something is\n2. ______\nWeighing Scale\nb. A person whose job is to cut\nand sell meat\n3. ______\nChopping board\nc. Vegetables that grow\nunderground, like potatoes\nor carrots.\n4. ______\nGrains\nd. A hard board used for\ncutting good on.\n5. ______\nRoot crops\ne. Small hard seeds from plants\nlike rice or wheat, used for food.','teacher'),
(724,724,'A. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads a short\npassage. Then, answer the questions below.\n1. What is the main place described in the passage?\na. A school\nb. A market\nc. A farm\nd. A restaurant\n2. What is the main purpose of going to this place?\na. To play and have fun\nb. To study and learn\nc. To buy food\nd. To cook meals\n3. Which of the following is an example of a food you\ncan buy there?\na. A toy car\nb. A storybook\nc. A chair\nd. Fruits','teacher'),
(725,725,'4. Who is the person you would find working with meat\nin this place?\na. The fisherman\nb. The butcher\nc. The farmer\nd. The driver\n5. Which tool would a seller use to tell you the weight\nof your fruits?\na. A chopping board\nb. A butcher\'s knife\nc. A weighing scale\nd. A shopping cart','teacher'),
(726,726,'In The Farm\nThis is our farm.\nWe grow plants on our farm.\nWe have animals on our farm to\ncoconut banana cassava guava\nbottle guard cashew','teacher'),
(727,727,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle the\nletter of the best answer.\n1. What is a farm?\na. A place where people go to work in offices.\nb. A place where animals are kept for display.\nc. An area of land used for growing crops and\nraising animals.\nd. A large building where machines make cars.\n2. Which word describes a large animal often used for\npulling plows in some countries?\na. Goat\nb. Carabao\nc. Chicken\nd. Bird\n3. What does it mean to grow plants?\na. To cook and eat them.\nb. To draw pictures of them.\nc. To cultivate and help them develop from seeds.\nd. To collect them from the forest.\n4. Which of the following is most likely a plant with a\nlarge, hard-shelled nut that grows on trees?\na. Cassava\nb. Pineapple\nc. Coconut\nd. Banana','teacher'),
(728,728,'5. If you see a bottle gourd on a farm, what are you\nlooking at?\na. A type of animal\nb. A tool for feeding animals\nc. A building for storing tools\nd. A type of vegetable that grows on a vine\nB Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main topic of the passage?\na. A family home\nb. A school playground\nc. A farm and what is on it\nd. A zoo with many animals\n2. What are the two main types of things found on this\nfarm?\na. Buildings and roads\nb. Toys and games\nc. Plants and animals\nd. Rivers and mountains','teacher'),
(729,729,'3. Which of these animals is NOT mentioned as living on\nthe farm?\na. Goat\nb. Sheep\nc. Pig\nd. Chicken\n4. Based on the passage, which activity do the people\nmost likely do on this farm?\na. They go swimming.\nb. They grow fruits and raise animals.\nc. They build cars and machines.\nd. They buy and sell clothes.\n5. The passage says, \"This is our farm.\" What does this\nmost likely mean?\na. The farm belongs to someone else.\nb. The farm is a public park for everyone.\nc. The speaker and their family or community own or\nwork on the farm.\nd. The farm is very old','teacher'),
(730,730,'Buildings Around Me\nThere are many building in our place.\nEach building is very useful for us.\nWe keep our building safe and clean.\nchurch\n<a@iane SHOP>| [Ml [i\nfire station','teacher'),
(731,731,'A. Vocabulary:\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Circle\nthe letter of the best answer.\n1. What is a building?\na. A natural formation like a mountain or a river.\nb. A vehicle used for transportation.\nc. A structure with a roof and walls, such as a\nhouse or school.\nd. A type of animal that lives in a forest.\n2. If you need to buy medicine,\nwhich building should you go to?\na. A bakery\nb. A pharmacy\nc. a bank\nd. a restaurant\n3. What does useful mean?\na. Old and beautiful\nb. Able to be used for a purpose; helpful.\nc. Very large and expensive\nd. New and modern\n4. The barangay hall is most likely a building that\nserves as what?\na. A place for local government and community\nmeetings.\nb. A place to watch movies.\nc. A place to buy fresh fish and vegetables.\nd. A place to repair cars.','teacher'),
(732,732,'5. What does it mean to keep our buildings safe\nand clean?\na. To forget about them.\nb. To destroy them and build new ones.\nc. To maintain or preserve them in that condition.\nd. To paint them all the same color.\nB. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\npassage twice. Then, circle the letter of the best answer for\neach question below.\n1. What is the main idea of the passage?\na. There are many useful buildings in the community.\nb. Houses are the most important buildings.\nc. Buildings are very expensive to build.\nd. All buildings look the same.\n2. How do the people feel about the buildings in their\nplace?\na. They find them useless.\nb. They think they are ugly.\nc. They find them very useful.\nd. They are afraid of them.','teacher'),
(733,733,'3. If someone needs to put out a fire, which building\nshould they call for help?\na. The hospital\nb. The barangay hall\nc. The fire station\nd. The market\n4. Which of the following is a building where you can\nbuy bread and pastries?\na. The restaurant\nb. The pharmacy\nc. The bakery\nd. The store\n5. What do the people do for their buildings?\na. They keep them safe and clean.\nb. They ignore them.\nc. They paint them every year.\nd. They sell them to other people.','teacher'),
(734,734,'POST TEST (Activity 1-10)\nVocabulary Development (1-10)\nA. Instructions: Draw a line to match the word to the\ncorrect picture.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Shovel\na.\n2. Nose\nb.\n3. Chair\nc.\n4. Teddy Bear\nd.\n5. Mother\ne.','teacher'),
(735,735,'B. Instructions: Draw a line to match the meaning to\nthe correct picture.\n1. An animal that barks\na.\n2. Used for writing\nb.\n3. Comes from chicken\nc.\n4. The father of your mother\nd.\nor father\n5. A dish used for holding\ne.\nliquids often with handle','teacher'),
(736,736,'A. Listening Comprehension:\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\nsentences/passage. Then, answer the questions below.\nChoose the letter of the correct answer.\n1. (Read Aloud) “My Home” This is my home. We have\ntables and chairs in our home. We have rooms and beds\ninn our home. We have the kitchen and the comfort rooms\ntoo. What is the story about?\na. My Garden\nb. My Home\nc. My Kitchen\n2. (Read Aloud) “My Toys” These are my toys. My mother\nand father gives it to me! I can name my favorite toys. “My\nparents gave me something I can throw and catch. It’s\nround and bouncy. What is it?”\na. Kite\nb. Ball\nc. Doll\nd. Teddy Bear','teacher'),
(737,737,'3. (Read Aloud) “Our Tools” This is our tools. We have\nshovel and rake. We have to take care of our tools. Tools\nare very important for us. What is the main idea of the\nstory?\na. Tools are fun\nb. Tools are useful and we should take care of\nthem\nc. Tools are expensive\n4. (Read Aloud) “My Pets” These are my pets. I will take\ncare of my pets. I will give them food. I love my pets.\nWrite T if it is true and F if it is false.\n______ A dog can bark.\n______ A fish can fly in the sky\n5. (Read Aloud) “My Things” These are my things. I will take\ncare of my things. I will keep it clean.\nWhat should you do with your things?\na. Break them\nb. Take care of them\nc. Make it tidy\nWhat does “keep it clean” mean?\na. Make it dirty\nb. Make it new\nc. Make it tidy','teacher'),
(738,738,'6. (Read Aloud) “My Family” This is my family. My mother\nand my father. My brother and my sister. And our baby\nboy. Who is in the family?\na. Friends\nb. Relatives\nc. Mother, Father, Brother, Sister, and Baby\n7. (Read Aloud) “My Food” These are the foods I eat.\nMy father buys them for me. My mother cook these for\nme. Who cooks the food in the story?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Friend\n8. “I love to play with my toy on the water. It has a sail\nand helps me pretend I’m a sailor. What am I playing\nwith?\na. Car\nb. Train\nc. Boat\nd. Yoyo','teacher'),
(739,739,'POST TEST (Activity 1-15)\nA. Vocabulary Development\nInstructions: Draw a line to match the words in Column A\nwith their meanings/uses /color in Column B.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. Librarian\na. Its color is orange\n2. Swing\nb. A container for waste\n3. Trash can\nc. Takes care of sick or\ninjured people in a\nhospital or clinic','teacher'),
(740,740,'d. A seat hanging from c\n4. Nurse\nropes or chains that\nmoves back and forth\n5. Building\ne. A hard board used for\ncutting\ngoods\n6. . Chopping board\nf. A structure with a roof\nand walls, such as a house\nor\nSchool.\n7. Pencil\ng. Used to carrying things.\n8. Bag\nh. Cooked bananas\non a stick\n9. Carrot\ni. Used for writing.','teacher'),
(741,741,'10. Banana cue\nj. A person who\nworks in a library\nA. Listening Comprehension\nInstructions: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the\nsentences/passage.. Then, answer the questions below.\nCircle the letter of the correct answer.\n1. (Read Aloud) “Our Tools” This is our tools. We have\nshovel and rake. We have to take care of our tools. Tools\nare very important for us. What is the main idea of the\nstory?\na. Tools are fun\nb. Tools are useful and we should take care of\nthem\nc. Tools are expensive\n2. (Read Aloud) “My Toys” These are my toys. My mother\nand father gives it to me! I can name my favorite toys. “My\nparents gave me something I can throw and catch. It’s\nround and bouncy. What is it?”\na. Kite\nb. Ball\nc. Doll\nd. Teddy Bear','teacher'),
(742,742,'3. (Read Aloud) “My Home” This is my home. We have\ntables and chairs in our home. We have rooms and beds\nin our home. We have the kitchen and the comfort rooms\ntoo. What is the story about?\na. My Garden\nb. My Home\nc. My Kitchen\n4. (Read Aloud) “My Food” These are the foods I eat. My\nfather buys them for me. My mother cook these for me.\nWho cooks the food in the story?\na. Father\nb, Mother\nc. Friend\n5. (Read Aloud) “My Things” These are my things. I will take\ncare of my things. I will keep it clean. What should you do\nwith your things?\na. Break them\nb. Take care of them\nc. Make it tidy','teacher'),
(743,743,'Pretest: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nVOCABULARY PRETEST (15 ITEMS)\nDirections: Read each question carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the underlined word.\n1. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n2. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To fall to the ground\nc) To hide\n3. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Bad smell\nb) No smell\nc) Good smell\n4. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Harmful things\nb) Things that help us grow\nc) Toys for us to play\n5. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Feeling sleepy\nc) Full of energy\n6. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n7. Fruits can taste sour or sweet. What does sour mean?\na) Not sweet\nb) Too salty\nc) Very cold','teacher'),
(744,744,'8. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n9. Herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Ordinary\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Special or amazing\n10. Herbs can cure much illness. What does illness mean?\na) A sickness\nb) A birthday\nc) A school subject\n11. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that are broken\nc) Things that disappear\n12. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?\na) To ignore\nb) To look and listen carefully\nc) To run away\n13. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Helping nicely\nb) Playing in a mean or silly way\nc) Sleeping quietly\n14. The animals swim under the deep blue sea. What does deep mean?\na) Very shallow\nb) Very far down\nc) Very noisy\n15. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) Only in one place\nb) Not in many places\nc) In many places all around','teacher'),
(745,745,'LISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST (15 ITEMS) ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nonly )\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads each short passage or question. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“Flowers are beautiful. They grow in many colors and smell good. People like flowers because\nthey make places look bright and lovely.”\n1. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they are loud\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they taste sweet\n2. What do flowers give?\na) A good smell\nb) A loud noise\nc) A sour taste','teacher'),
(746,746,'Teacher reads:\n“Vegetables help our body because they have nutrients. They keep us strong, active, and\nhealthy.”\n3. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Toys\nb) Nutrients\nc) Smoke\n4. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us sleepy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us noisy\nTeacher reads:\n“Fruits can taste sweet or sour. They help us stay healthy and give us vitamins.”\n5. How do fruits taste?\na) Sweet or sour\nb) Salty\nc) Bitter\n6. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\nTeacher reads:\n“Trees give us clean air. Birds live in trees because they are safe and high.”\n7. What do trees give us?\na) Dirty air\nb) Clean air\nc) Hot air\n8. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are noisy\nc) Trees are cold\nTeacher reads:\n“Some herbs are used to help sick people feel better. Herbs can cure small illnesses.”\n9. What can herbs do?\na) Make cars move\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make people laugh','teacher'),
(747,747,'10. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people\nb) Robots\nc) Trees\nTeacher reads:\n“Many animals live on land. Some help farmers by carrying heavy loads or guarding the farm.”\n11. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Horse\nb) Whale\nc) Lobster\n12. Where do these animals live?\na) In the sea\nb) On land\nc) In the sky\nTeacher reads:\n“Woodland animals like squirrels and tarsiers live among trees. Some hide when they see people.”\n13. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They swim\nc) They fly to the sea\nTeacher reads:\n“In the meadow, we see butterflies, bees, and birds. They fly around flowers.”\n14. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They swim\nb) They fly around flowers\nc) They dig tunnels\nTeacher reads:\n“In the forest, animals like monkeys and deer hide among the trees. In the sea, animals like\ndolphins and whales swim together.”\n15. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Deer and monkeys\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Pigs and cows\nLISTENING COMPREHENSION PRETEST','teacher'),
(748,748,'COMPREHENSIVE PRETEST (Lessons 11–20)\nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct answer.\n1. We use a blender to:\na) Wash plates\nb) Make juice\nc) Cook rice\n2. A television is used for:\na) Baking\nb) Watching shows\nc) Watering plants\n3. A pillow is used for:\na) Sleeping comfortably\nb) Cooking food\nc) Writing letters','teacher'),
(749,749,'4. Soap is used for:\na) Cleaning the body\nb) Sweeping the floor\nc) Cutting paper\n5. A car is found in the:\na) Garden\nb) Garage\nc) Bedroom\n6. A mountain is:\na) A tall landform\nb) A body of water\nc) A type of house\n7. A pond is:\na) A small body of water\nb) A large sea\nc) A mountain\n8. Gold is a type of:\na) Clothing\nb) Mineral\nc) Food\n9. A truck is used to:\na) Fly in the sky\nb) Carry heavy goods\nc) Swim in water\n10. Boracay Island is famous for its:\na) Snow\nb) White sand beach\nc) Tall buildings\n11. A soap dish is used to:\na) Store soap\nb) Plant flowers\nc) Keep toys\n12. A wardrobe is used to store:\na) Clothes\nb) Food\nc) Books\n13. A plateau is:\na) A flat land higher than the land around it\nb) A body of water\nc) A small hill','teacher'),
(750,750,'14. A funnel is used for:\na) Pouring liquids easily\nb) Playing music\nc) Carrying books\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Land\nb) Water\nc) Rails\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION (15 items)\nTeacher reads the passages assigned to each lesson.\nBased on Lesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The stove cooks\nvegetables and the rice cooker cooks’ rice. Plates and utensils are for eating.”\n16. What should we do in the kitchen?\na) Make it messy\nb) Keep it clean\nc) Leave water everywhere\n17. What do we put in the blender?\na) Rice\nb) Fruits\nc) Plates\nBased on Lesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the windows and a\nbookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do we sit?\na) Bookshelf\nb) Sofa\nc) Table\nBased on Lesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net protects from\ninsects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”','teacher'),
(751,751,'19. What protects us from insects?\na) Blanket\nb) Mosquito net\nc) Curtain\n20. Where do we keep clothes?\na) Wardrobe\nb) Table\nc) Floor\nBased on Lesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and poured into a\nbucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What do we use to wash hair?\na) Soap\nb) Shampoo\nc) Comb\n22. What do we step on after bathing?\na) Carpet\nb) Bath mat\nc) Soap dish\nBased on Lesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer help fix small\nparts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What lifts the car?\na) Hammer\nb) Trolley jack\nc) Wheel\n24. What tool is used to fix screws?\na) Screwdriver\nb) Funnel\nc) Pliers\nBased on Lesson 16 – Landforms\nTeacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide and flat. A\nshoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. What landform is tall?\na) Mountain','teacher'),
(752,752,'b) Hill\nc) Basin\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Desert\nb) Shoreline\nc) Glacier\nBased on Lesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) Lake and pond\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) River and spring\n28. What should we keep clean?\na) Land\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Cars\nBased on Lesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Toys\nb) Treasure\nc) Houses\n30. Which mineral is mentioned?\na) Plastic\nb) Gold\nc) Wood','teacher'),
(753,753,'Plants around Me\nThis is my garden.\nI\'ll plant flowers, vegetables, and grains.\nHere are the seeds of trees and herbs.\nThe sun will shine; the rain will fall.\nThe seeds will sprout, up tall.','teacher'),
(754,754,'Activity 1- Flowers\nFlowers\nFlowers are the beauty of nature.\nThey grow and bloom in different colors.\nThey gave us fragrant odor.\nFlowers are wonderful.\nOrchids\nDahlia\nRose\nSampaguita\nSunflower Sampaguita Tulips\nYellow Plumeria\nChrysanthemum\nAster','teacher'),
(755,755,'Activity 1A: Assessment\nA. Vocabulary (5 items)\nLesson 1A: Assessment\nDirections: Match the word with its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud the\nwords and meanings.)\n1. Beauty\na. Smells good\n2. Bloom\nb. Something nice to see\n3. Color\nc. To open like a flower\n4. Fragrant\nd. A shade like red, blue, or yellow\n5. Wonderful\ne. Very nice or amazing\nLesson 1B: Assessment\nB. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully to the teacher as the story is read aloud. Then\nanswer the questions.\n1. What is the beauty of nature in the story?\na. Trees\nb. flowers\nc. clouds\n2. What do flowers do?\na. They sleep\nb. They grow and bloom\nc. They jump\n3. Flowers bloom in different ______\n.\na. Colors\nb. sizes\nc. sounds\n4. What do flowers give us?\na. A fragrant odor\nb. A loud noise\nc. A bright light\n5. How does the story describe flowers?\na. Ugly\nb. wonderful\nc. scary','teacher'),
(756,756,'Activity 2- Vegetables\nVegetables in our garden.\nLegumes, leafy vegetables and grains\nThey give nutrients to our body and brains,\nTo keep us active and healthy mind\ncarrots\ncabbage\nradish\nlettuce\nbroccoli\ncauliflower\npotatoes\ntomato\nbean\nstring bean','teacher'),
(757,757,'Activity 2 A: Assessment\nA. Matching Type: In column A is the picture of vegetables. In column B\nis the name of the vegetables. Match column A and B by\nconnecting it with a line.\nA. Picture of vegetables\nB. Name of vegetables\n1.\na. carrots\n2.\nb. stringbeans\n3.\nc. tomato\n4.\nd. potato\n5.\ne. cabbage\nActivity 2B: Assessment\nStory for the teacher to read:\nVegetables\nVegetables in our garden. Legumes, leafy and grains. They give nutrients to\nour body and brains, to keep us active and healthy mind.\nDirections: Listen carefully to the story. Then answer the questions.\nA. Listening and Vocabulary Questions (5 items)\n1. Where can we find the vegetables in the story?\na. in the garden\nb. in the store\nc. in the forest\n2. Which of the following is a kind of vegetable mentioned in the story?\na. Fruits b. legumes c. candies\n3. What do vegetables give to our body and brain?\na. Toys\nb. nutrients\nc. noise\n4. Why are nutrients important for us?','teacher'),
(758,758,'Activity 3- Fruits\nFruits\nFruit makes us very strong.\nAnd keep us healthy for long.\nThey taste sour and sweet.\nThat everyone likes to eat.\ntiesa\ncashew\nguyabano\napple\natis\nstar apple santol\nmangosteen\nmacopa\nsiniguelas','teacher'),
(759,759,'Activity 3 A: Assessment\nA. Vocabulary Test\nDirections: Match the word with its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud.)\nTastes like candy\nStrong a. Tastes like candy\nah WwW N\nTo take food into the mouth\nHealthy b. To take food into the mouth\nHas a sharp taste like lemon\nSour c. Has a sharp taste like lemon\nd. Having power or energy.\nSweet e. Having power or energy\ne. Not sick; well\nEat c. Not sick; well\nB. Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as the story is read aloud. Then answer the\nquestions.\nquestions. What do fruits make us?\na. Weak\nb. Strong\nc. Sleepy\nWhat do fruits help keep us?\na. Busy\nb. Healthy\nc. Sad\nHow do fruits taste?\na. Sour and sweet\nBitter\nSalty\nWho likes to eat fruits?\na. Everyone\nb. Only children\nc.Noone\nWhat is the poem mostly talking about?\na. Games\nFruits\nb. Fruits c. Weather','teacher'),
(760,760,'Activity 4-\nActivity 4- Trees\nTrees are everywhere.\nThey give us clean and fresh air.\nLittle birds live up there.\nTrees are their shelter.\nacacia\nnarra\ngolden tree\nmabolo\nkamagong\nPine tree\nfalcata\ngemilina\nbalete','teacher'),
(761,761,'Activity 4- Assessment\nA. Vocabulary\nDirections: Match the word to its meaning. (Teacher may read aloud.)\nEverywhere a. To stay or make a home in\nFresh\noh Ww ny\nFresh b. Protection or a place to stay\nAir\nAir c. All around us; in many places\nShelter\nShelter d. What we breathe\nLive\nLive e. Clean or new\nListening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as the story is read aloud. Then answer the\nquestions.\nWhere are trees found according to the story?\na. In one place only\nb. Everywhere\nOnly in the city\nWhat do trees give us?\nDirty air\nb. Clean and fresh air\nNo air at all\nWho lives up in the trees?\na. Cats\nb. Little birds\nFish\nWhat is a shelter for the birds in the story?\nTrees\nb. Cars\nc. Houses\nWhat is the poem mostly talking about?\na. Games\nTrees\nb. Trees c. Weather','teacher'),
(762,762,'Activity 5- Herbs\nHerbs\nMagical herbs,\nGiven to this world.\nCan cure so much illness,\nYou’d never believe it would.\nlemongrass\npeppermint\ndill\noregano\neucalyptus\naloe vera\nRed basil\nsage\nTurmeric','teacher'),
(763,763,'Activity 5 Assessment\nPart 1: Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPart 1: Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension Direction: Choose the correct picture\n1. Which picture shows a “herb”?\na)\n(big tree)\nb)\n(small plant with leaves)\nc)\n(dog)\nWhich picture shows “cure”?\n(medicine) (gift) = c) (house)\na)\nWhich picture shows “magical”?\na) (sparkles) (apple) —c)\n4. What can the magical herb do?\na) (helps sick people) b) (makes art) c) (makes you run\nfast)\n5. Who received the magical herb? fast)\na)\nor a sad face if no (acat) c) (a king)\n6. Do you think herbs are helpful?\nPoint to a happy face\nyes\nor a sad face if no\nif yes\nInstructions for the Teacher:\n➢\nRead the poem/story aloud slowly and clearly.\n➢Ask the students to listen carefully because they will\nanswer some questions after.\nPart 2: Vocabulary\nChoose the correct answer.\n1. Choose the correct answer. What is a “herb”?\na)\na) Akind of magic wand\nb)\nb) A plant we can use for medicine or cooking\nc)\nc) A type of animal\nWhat does “cure” mean in the story?\na) To make someone feel better from illness\nb)\nb) To give someone a gift\nc)\nc) To make something disappear\nThe story says the herb is “magical.” What does “magical” mean?\na)\na) Ordinary\nb)\nb) Special and amazing\nc)\nc) Smal','teacher'),
(764,764,'Animals that | Know\nAnimals on land.\nHelp farmers in the farm.\nCreations in the sea, woodland and in the meadow\nMade by God for me and you.','teacher'),
(765,765,'Activity 6- Animals in the Land\nThe horse, cow and carabao.\nGo walk and walk going to the barn.\nThe dog says aww! aww! aww!\nAnd the cat says meow! meow! meow!\nUntil they meet little turkey\nand together, they play.\nCat\ncow\ndog\nhorse\ngoat\ncarabao\nChicken\npig\nturkey','teacher'),
(766,766,'Activity 6 Assessment:\nPart 1: Vocabulary Recognition\nInstruction: Look at the picture and choose the word that matches it.\n1.\nWhich animal is this?\na) Dog b) Horse c) Cat d) Turkey\n2.\nWhich animal is this?\na) Cow b) Horse b) Horse c) Dog d)\nCarabao\n3.\nWhich animal is this?\na) Turkey b) Cat c) Cow d) Dog\n4.\nWhat sound does this animal make?\na) Meow! b) Aww! c) Quack! d) Neigh!\n5.\nWhat sound does this animal make?\na) Meow! b) Aww! c) Moo! d) Gobble!\nPart 2: Listening Comprehension\nInstruction: Listen carefully to the story and answer the questions.\nWhere were the horse, cow, and carabao going?\na) To the river b) To the barn c) To the forest d)Toschool\nWho did the animals meet and play with?\na)Adog__ib) A turkey c) Acat d) Acow\nWhich animal says “aww! aww! aww!’?\na) Cat b) Dog c) Horse d) Carabao\nWhich animal says “meow! meow! meow!\" 2\na) Dog b) Cat c) Horse d) Turkey\nWhat do the animals do at the end of the story?\na) Sleep b) Eat c) Play d) Run away','teacher'),
(767,767,'Activity 7- Animals in the Woodland\nCome little squirrel.\nMeet baby tarsier.\nHide under the tree.\nWoodpecker is coming to prey.\nowl\ntoad\ntarsier\nmoth\nsquirrel\nwood mouse\nbeetle\nwoodpecker\nStag beetle','teacher'),
(768,768,'Activity 7 : Assessment\nSkills Focus: Vocabulary recognition, listening comprehension, animal\nidentification\nInstructions for Teacher:\n1. Instructions for Teacher: Read the story aloud slowly to the students.\nAsk the students to listen carefully.\n3. Complete the tasks below based on what they hear.\nPart 1: Vocabulary Matching\nDirections: Match the animal with the correct picture or word. Draw a line\nto match.\nWord\nPicture/Option\n1. tarsier\nowl /\ntoad /\ntarsier\n2. woodpecker\nowl /\nwoodpecker /\nbeetle\n3. squirrel\nwood mouse /\nsquirrel /\nmoth\n4. beetle\nbeetle /\nstag beetle /\ntoad\nPart 2: Listening Comprehension Questions\nDirections: Listen to the story and answer the questions.\n1. Who does the story ask to come first?\na)\nb) Owl\nb) Squirrel\nc)\nc) Woodpecker\nWhat animal is hiding under the tree?\na) Tarsier\nb) Squirrel\nc) Beetle\nWhich animal is coming as prey?\na)\na) Woodpecker\nb)\nb) Owl\nc)\nc) Toad\nWhich animals did you hear in the story? Circle all that apply.\nsquirrel, tarsier, woodpecker, owl, moth, toad\nPart 3: Fillin the Blanks\nDirections: Fill in the missing words from the story.\nlittle ______\n.\nDirections: Fill in the missing words from the story. Come little ;\nMeet baby .\nHide under the ______\n.\nis coming as prey','teacher'),
(769,769,'Activity 8- Animals in the Meadow\nAnimals in the Meadow\nThe birds in the sky go fly and fly.\nHere comes the butterfly, flying in the meadow.\nTo get the attention of me and you.\ngrasshopper\nbutterfly\nDragon fly\npraying mantis\nladybug\nhousefly\ngold pinch\nmosquito','teacher'),
(770,770,'Activity 8 Assessment\nLesson: Animals in the Meadow\nSkills Focus: Vocabulary recognition, listening comprehension, animal\nidentification\nInstructions for Teacher:\n1. Read the story aloud slowly to the students.\nAsk the students to listen carefully.\n3. Complete the tasks below based on what they hear.\nPart 1: Vocabulary Matching\nDirections: Match the animal with the correct picture or word. Draw a line to\nmatch.\nWord Picture/Option\nladybug / butterfly / bee grasshopper\n1. butterfly\n/ grasshopper / ladybug\n2. grasshopper\ngrasshopper / ladybug /\n/ housefly /\n3. ladybug\nbutterfly\n4. bee\nbee /\npraying mantis /\nbutterfly\npraying mantis /\n5. mosquito\nmosquito / ladybug\nPart 2: Listening Comprehension Questions\nDirections: Listen to the story and answer the questions.\nWhat flies in the meadow?\na) Butterfly\nb)\nb) Grasshopper\nc)\nc) Ladybug\nWhich animal is trying to get attention?\na)\na) Dragonfly\nb) Butterfly\nc)\nc) Mosquito\n3. Which animals did you hear in the story? Circle all that apply.\nbutterfly, dragonfly, grasshopper, ladybug, praying mantis, housefly,\ngold pinch, mosquito, bee\nPart 3: Fillin the Blanks\nDirections: Fill in the missing words from the story.\nThe birds in the ______\n, go fly and fly.\nHere comes the ______\n, flying in the meadow.\n3. To get the attention of and you.','teacher'),
(771,771,'Activity 9- Animals in the Forest\nAnimals in the Forest\nLook at the monkey.\nTeasing you and me.\nLook at the deer and the kangaroo.\nThey are hiding on you.\ndeer\nboar\nmonkey\nwild boar\nkangaroo\nbat\nsnake\nfox\neagle\nlion','teacher'),
(772,772,'Activity 9 Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson: Animals in the Forest\nSkills Focus: Vocabulary recognition, listening comprehension, animal\nidentification\nInstructions for Teacher:\n1. Instructions for Teacher: Read the story aloud slowly to the students.\nAsk the students to listen carefully.\n3. Complete the tasks below based on what they hear.\nPart 1: Vocabulary Matching\nDirections: Match the animal with the correct picture or word. Draw a line\nto match.\nWord\nPicture/Option\n1. monkey\nmonkey /\ndeer /\nkangaroo\n2. deer\ndeer /\nwild boar /\nsnake\n3. kangaroo\nkangaroo /\nbat /\nlion\n4. snake\nsnake /\nfox /\neagle\n5. bat\nbat /\nlion /\nfox\n6. eagle\neagle /\nwild boar /\nmonkey\n7. lion\nlion /\nfox /\nsnake\n8. fox\nfox /\neagle /\nbat\nPart 2: Listening Comprehension Questions\nDirections: Listen to the story and answer the questions.\n1. Who is teasing you and me?\na)\na) Monkey b) Deer c) Kangaroo\n2. Which animals are hiding?\na)\na) Deer and kangaroo’ b) Monkey andlion c) Eagle and fox\n3. Which animals did you hear in the story? Circle all that apply.\nmonkey, deer, kangaroo, snake, bat, eagle, lion, fox, wild boar\nPart 3: Fillin the Blanks\nDirections: Fill in the missing words from the story.\nLook at the ______\n.\nhRWN =\nTeasing and me.\nLook at the and the ;\nThey are hiding on ______\n.','teacher'),
(773,773,'Activity 10- Animals in the Sea\nAnimals in the Sea\nThe fish in the sea.\nGo swimming and swimming.\nUnder the deep blue sea.\nDolphins and whales are friends of me.\nshark\nwhale\ndolphin\nlobster\nsquid\ncrab\nstarfish\nshrimps\nshells','teacher'),
(774,774,'Activity 10 Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson: Animals in the Sea\nInstructions for Teacher:\n1. Read the story aloud slowly to the students.\n2. Ask the students to listen carefully.\n3. Complete the tasks below based on what they hear.\nPart 1: Vocabulary Matching\nDirections: Match the animal with the correct picture or word. Draw a line to\nmatch.\nWord\nPicture/Option\n1. dolphin\ndolphin / whale / shark\n2. whale\nwhale /\nfish /\ncrab\n3. shark\nshark /\ndolphin / lobster\n4. lobster\nlobster / crab /\nsquid\nsquid /\nlobster / crab\n5. squid\ncrab /\nsquid /\nfish\n6. crab\nstarfish / shells / shrimps\n7. starfish\nshrimps / starfish / shells\n8. shrimps\nshells /\nshrimps / starfish\n9. shells\nPart 2: Listening Comprehension Questions\nDirections: Listen to the story and answer the questions.\n1. Which animals are friends of the speaker?\na)\na) Shark and whale\nb)\nb) Dolphins and whale\nc) Fish and crab\n2. c) Fish and crab Where do the animals in the story live?\na) In the sky\nb)\na) In the sky b) On the land\nc)\nc) Under the deep blue sea\nWhich animals did you hear in the story? Circle all that apply.\nfish, dolphin, whale, shark, lobster, squid, crab, starfish, shrimps, shells\nPart 3: Fillin the Blanks\nDirections: Fill in the missing words from the story.\n1. Directions: The on the sea. Fill in the missing words from the story.\n2. Go and swim.\n3. Under the deep sea.\n4. and are friends of me.','teacher'),
(775,775,'Me and Our House\nCome and go with me to our house and see.\nHere is our kitchen where mama cooks for me.\nHere is our living room where | watch television.\nHere is our bathroom inside my room.\nHere is the garage where my daday fixes the\ncar for our family.','teacher'),
(776,776,'Activity 11- Things Found in the Kitchen\nThings Found in the Kitchen\nKeep our kitchen clean.\nWipe the spill water and drain.\nPut fruit on your blender.\nPrepare juice and share.\nwash basin\nkettle\nrefrigerator\ngas stove\nrice cooker\nblender\nplate\nSpoon\nfork','teacher'),
(777,777,'Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nActivity 11: Things Found in the Kitchen\nPart I: Vocabulary (5 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct meaning or\nword that fits.\nWe use a blender to:\na) Wash plates b) Make juice or mix fruits c) Cook rice\nA refrigerator is used to:\nb) Fry vegetables\na) Keep food cold __ b) Fry vegetables c) Hold water\nWe use a fork to:\na)\nc) Drink juice\na) Eat food b) Cook food on the stove c) Drink juice\nA kettle is used to:\na) Boil water\nb) Blend fruits\na) Boil water b) Blend fruits c) Wash dishes\n5. A gas stove is used to:\na) Cook food with heat bb) Store vegetables’ c) Eat food\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the passage below. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we must keep everything clean. Wipe spills and drain water.\nPut fruits in the blender to make juice. Use the rice cooker to cook rice and\nthe stove to cook vegetables. Plates, spoons, and forks are for eating.”\n6. What should we do if water spills in the kitchen?\na) Ignore it\nb) Wipe it and drain\nc) Pour more water\n7. What do we put in the blender?\na) Vegetables only\nb) Fruits\nc) Plates\n8. Which kitchen tool is used to cook rice?\na) Blender\nb) Rice cooker\nc) Kettle\n9. What do we use to eat food?\na) Plate, fork, spoon\nb) Blender\nc) Stove\n10. What should we do in the kitchen to stay safe and clean?\na) Keep it clean and organized\nb) Leave food everywhere\nc) Only cook, no cleaning','teacher'),
(778,778,'Activity 12- Things Found in the Living Room\nThings Found in the Living Room\nSet beside me.\nLet’s watch TV.\nSip the morning coffee.\nServed to you for free.\nvase\nframes\nbookshelf\nflower vase\nsofa\ntelevision\ncurtains\ncarpet\nelectric fan\nClock','teacher'),
(779,779,'Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nActivity 12: Things Found in the Living Room\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct word that fits.\n1. We sit on a sofa to:\na) Cook food\nb) Sit and relax\nc) Store books\n2. A television is used to:\na) Watch shows or movies\nb) Hold flowers\nc) Keep the room warm\n3. We put curtains on:\na) Windows\nb) Floor\nc) Walls\n4. A bookshelf is used to:\na) Sit on\nb) Store and display books\nc) Hold flowers\n5. A flower vase is used to:\na) Hold water and flowers\nb) Cover windows\nc) Tell time\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the passage below. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we can sit on the sofa and watch television. There is a\nbookshelf for books, a flower vase for decoration, and curtains on the\nwindows. A carpet and an electric fan keep the room comfortable. The\nclock tells the time.”\n6. Where do we sit in the living room to relax?\na) Bookshelf\nb) Sofa\nc) Television\n7. What do we use to hold flowers?\na) Flower vase\nb) Carpet\nc) Clock\n8. What keeps the room cool?\na) Carpet and electric fan\nb) Bookshelf\nc) Television\n9. Where do we keep our books in the living room?\na) Sofa\nb) Bookshelf\nc) Flower vase\n10. What is used to tell the time in the living room?\na) Carpet\nb) Clock\nc) Television','teacher'),
(780,780,'Activity 13- Things Found in the Bedroom\nThings Found in the Bedroom\nCome inside my room.\nKeep the light turning on.\nMama is coming home.\nI will never be alone.\nbed sheet\nblanket\npillow\nmosquito net\nwardrobe\nlampshade\nalarm clock\nmirror','teacher'),
(781,781,'Formative Assessment — Grade 2\nLesson 13: Things Found in the Bedroom\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\n1. We rest our head ona when we sleep.\na)\na) mirror b) pillow c) wardrobe\n2. The keeps us warm at night.\na)\na) blanket —_b) lampshade c) alarm clock\n3. We keep our clothes inside the\na)\na) mosquito net b) pillow c) wardrobe\n4. A gives light when the room is dark.\na)\na) lampshade __ b) bed sheet c) blanket\n5. A helps wake us up in the morning.\na)\na) mirror b) alarm clock c) bed\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher Reads:\n“In the bedroom, there is a soft bed with a pillow and a blanket. A bed\nsheet covers the bed. A mosquito net hangs to protect from insects at\nnight. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe. A lampshade gives light, and a\nmirror helps us see our face. The alarm clock rings to wake us up early.”\n6. What covers the bed?\na) Bed sheet\nb) Blanket\nc) Mirror\n7. What protects us from insects at night?\na) Lampshade\nb) Mosquito net\nc) Pillow\n8. Where do we put our clothes?\na) Blanket\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Bed\n9. What helps us see our face?\na) Alarm clock\nb) Lampshade\nc) Mirror\n10. What wakes us up in the morning?\na) Bed sheet\nb) Alarm clock\nc) Blanket','teacher'),
(782,782,'14:\nLesson 14:\nThings Found in the Bath Room\nIf you want to shower\nDon’t forget to bring towel.\nUse soap and shampoo\nBrush and comb are set for you.\nbath mat\npaper\nshampoo\ntoilet paper\nbucket\nsoap dish\nsoap\nbath cup\ncomb bath cup brush','teacher'),
(783,783,'Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 14: Things Found in the Bathroom\nPart |: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: bath mat, toilet paper, shampoo, soap, comb, brush, bucket,\nbath cup, soap dish\n1. bath cup, soap dish We use to wash our hair.\na)\na) shampoo b) comb c) bucket\n2. We place the soap ona .\na)\na) brush b) soap dish c) bath mat\n3. After taking a bath, we stand on the SO We will not slip.\na)\nb) toilet paper\na) bath mat b) toilet paper c) soap\n4. We use a to comb and fix our hair.\na)\na) brush b) comb c) bath cup\nfill\n______.\n5. When we need water for bathing, we can fill a\na)\nc) toilet paper\na) bucket b) shampoo c) toilet paper\nPart Il: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n\"If\ntowel.\n\"If you want to shower, don\'t forget to bring your towel. Use soap and\nhair.\nis\nin\nbathing, you may step on the bath mat so the floor will not get wet. You\nis\nWater is scooped using a bath cup and poured into the bucket. After\nwill\nbathing, you may step on the bath mat so the floor will not get wet. You\nToilet\nis\nin\ncan brush your hair using a brush or a comb. Toilet paper is also found in the\nyourself\nbathroom for keeping yourself clean.\"\nWhere do we keep the soap?\na) In the bucket b) On the soap dish c) In the bath cup\n7. What do we use to clean our hair?\na)\nc) toilet paper\na) shampoo b) brush c) toilet paper\n8. What helps keep the floor from getting wet?\na)\na) bath cup b) bath mat c) comb\n9. What can we use fo fix our hair after bathing?\na)\na) blanket b) towel c) brush or comb\n10. What do we use for cleaning ourselves in the bathroom?\na)\na) toilet paper b) bath mat c) bucket','teacher'),
(784,784,'Lesson 15- Things Found in the Garage\nThings Found in the Garage\nDo you really want to shop?\nOn the garage you can stop.\nPark there safely.\nTo keep you and your car safety.\ncar\nengine oil\nwheel\ncan\npliers screw driver\nfunnel\nhammer\ntrolley jack','teacher'),
(785,785,'Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 15: Things Found in the Garage\nPart |: Vocabulary (5 items)\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: car, engine oil, wheel, petrol can, pliers, screwdriver, trolley\njack, funnel, hammer\nA ______\nis used for fixing or turning screws.\na)\nA is used for fixing or turning screws. a) wheel lb) screwdriver c) funnel\n2. The helps the car move on the road.\na)\na) wheel b) hammer C) pliers\n3. A holds fuel that can be used for a car.\na) petrol can\nb) trolley jack\nc) engine oil\na) petrol can b) trolley jack c) engine oil We use a to make pouring liquid easier.\na)\na) funnel b) car c) hammer\n______ lift\ntire.\n5. A helps liff a car when changing a tire.\na) pliers\nb) trolley jack\nc) engine oil\nPart Il: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\nis\n\"In the garage, we can find many tools and things for the car. A car is parked\noil\nsafely inside the garage. Wheels help the car move, while engine oil keeps\nis\nfuel.\nlike\nthe engine running smoothly. There is a petrol can for storing fuel. Tools like a\npliers,\nhammer, pliers, and a screwdriver are used for fixing small parts. A funnel\noil\nspilling. trolley\nis\nlift\nhelps pour oil or petrol without spilling. A trolley jack is used fo lift the car when\nis\nchanging a wheel. The garage is a safe place for both the car and the\nit.\"\na) hammer b) petrol can c) funnel\na)\na) engine oil __b) petrol can c) funnel\nWhat is used to fix small parts?\na)\na) wheel 6b) hammer, pliers, and screwdriver = c) car\nlift\n8. What helps lift the car?\na) petrol can\nb) trolley jack\nc) engine oil\na) petrolcan _b) trolley jack c) engine oil What is used to store fuel?\na)\na) hammer b) petrol can c) funnel\n10. Where is the car parked safely?','teacher'),
(786,786,'Me and My\nMe and My Surroundings\nGod created heaven and Earth.\nBeautiful surrounding with fresh air to breath.\nKeep our environment clean and green.\nMake our place safe to live in.','teacher'),
(787,787,'Lesson 16- Landforms\nLandforms\nBeyond your imagination.\nLand has different forms.\nExperience the beauty of nature.\nmountain\nvalley\nplateau\nglacier\ndesert\nhill\nbasin\nshoreline\nplain','teacher'),
(788,788,'Formative Assessment – Grade 2\nLesson 16: Landforms\nPart I: Vocabulary\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct word that fits.\nWords to use: mountain, valley, plateau, glacier, hill, desert, basin, shoreline,\nplain\n1. A ______\nis a high landform with steep sides that is taller than a hill.\na) mountain\nb) plain\nc) shoreline\n2. A ______\nis a wide, flat area of land.\na) hill\nb) plain\nc) glacier\n3. A ______\nis a low area between mountains or hills.\na) valley\nb) plateau\nc) desert\n4. A ______\nis a large area of flat land that is higher than the land\naround it.\na) shoreline\nb) plateau\nc) basin\n5. A ______\nis a very dry place with lots of sand.\na) desert\nb) glacier\nc) hill\nPart II: Listening Comprehension\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short passage. Then\nchoose the correct answer.\nTeacher reads:\n\"The Earth has many different landforms. A mountain is tall and reaches\nhigh into the sky, while a hill is smaller and gently rounded. A valley lies\nbetween mountains and hills. A plain is a wide, flat area where many\npeople build houses and farms. A plateau is also flat but stands higher than\nthe land around it. Some places have glaciers, which are large, slow-\nmoving ice. A desert is hot and dry with very little water. The shoreline is the\nplace where land meets the water. A basin is a low area that can hold\nwater. These landforms make the Earth beautiful and exciting to explore.\"\nWhich landform is tall and reaches high into the sky?\na) hill\nb) mountain\nc) basin\n7. What landform is a low area between mountains or hills?\na)\na) valley b) shoreline c) plateau\n8. Which landform is flat and good for farms and houses?\na)\na) glacier b) plain c) desert\n9. What landform is made of slow-moving ice?\na) basin\nb) glacier\nc) hill\nWhere does the land meet the water?\na)\na) shoreline b) desert c) plateau','teacher'),
(789,789,'Lesson 17- Body of Water\nBody of Water\nThe spring, falls, pond, lake and river.\nEnhancing the beauty on Earth forever.\nOcean and sea are nice to see.\nKeep them clean and garbage free.\nocean\nsea\nriver\nstream\nspring\nfalls\nlake\npond\nditch','teacher'),
(790,790,'Lesson 17: Body of Water\nPart I: Vocabulary (5 items)\nDirections: Read each sentence. Choose the correct body of water that fits.\n(Teacher may show pictures of each body of water while reading.)\n1. A small body of water where frogs and fish can live is a ______\n.\na) pond\nb) ocean\nc) river\n2. A very big body of water with big waves is called the\n______.\na) sea\nb) ocean\nc) lake\n3. Water that comes from a high place and falls down is called\n______.\na) spring\nb) falls\nc) river\n4. A long body of water that flows from one place to another is a ______\n.\na) river\nb) lake\nc) pond\n5. A large body of water that is bigger than a pond but calmer than the\nsea is a ______\n.\na) lake\nb) falls\nc) ocean c) ocean\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nDirections: Listen carefully as your teacher reads the short poem. Then answer\nthe questions.\nTeacher Reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake and river, Enhancing the beauty on Earth\nforever. Ocean and sea are nice to see. Keep them clean and garbage\nfree.”\nQuestions:\n6. What are named in the poem that make Earth beautiful?\na) mountains\nb) bodies of water\nc) animals\n7. Which two bodies of water are described as “nice to see”?\na) lake and pond\nb) ocean and sea\nc) river and spring\n8. What should we keep clean and garbage-free?\na) the ocean and sea b) the classroom c) the trees\n9. Which body of water flows from place to place?\na) river\nb) pond c) lake\n10. Which body of water comes from the ground and is mentioned first in\nthe poem?\na) pond b) spring\nc) sea','teacher'),
(791,791,'Lesson 18- Mineral Resources\nMineral Resources\nEarth is rich in treasure.\nMore than we could ever measure.\nCoal, copper, gold and silver.\nElements on Earth layer upon layer.\ngold\nsilver\ncopper\nsalt\nlimestone\ncoal\naluminum\nsand and\nphosphate\ngravel','teacher'),
(792,792,'PART A — VOCABULARY WITH PICTURES\nDirections:\nMatch the picture to the correct word. Write the letter of the correct\nanswer.\nPicture Icons\n– gold\n– silver\n– copper (use magnet icon to represent metal)\n– coal\n– salt\n– limestone\n– phosphate (fertilizer symbol\nsubstitute)\n– aluminium (aluminum can)\n– sand & gravel\nItems:\nWord List:\n1. ______\nA. Coal\n2. ______\nB. Silver\n3. ______\nC. Sand & Gravel\n4. ______\nD. Limestone\n5. ______\nE. Aluminium\n6. ______\nF. Gold\n7. ______\nG. Salt\n8. ______\nH. Phosphate\n9. ______\nI. Copper\nPART B — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the short story aloud. Story: Mineral Resources\nEarth is rich of treasure. More than we could ever measure. Coal, copper,\ngold and silver. Elements on Earth layer upon layer.\nDirections:\nListen to the story. Then answer the questions.\n1. What is the story talking about?\na. Animals\nb. Mineral resources\nc. Weather\n2. Which of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\na. Silver\nb. Coal\nc. Plastic\n3. Name one mineral you heard from the story.\na. Gold\nb. Tree\nc. Water\n4. What word in the poem means “precious things found on Earth”?\na. Treasure\nb. Rock\nc. Soil\nd. Sand\n5. What does the poem say Earth is full of?\na. Treasure\nb. Food\nc. Water only\nPART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections: Use the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: gold • coal • silver • copper\nPeople use to make jewelry.\nto make jewelry.\n2. Many machines use wires.\nis black and used for fuel.','teacher'),
(793,793,'Transportation\nLesson 19- Transportation\nIn the street you can see.\nBuses, cars and taxi.\nIn the air there is a plane.\nOn the rails there is a train.\ntruck\nvan\nambulance\ntrain\ntaxi\nbicycle\nboat\nairplane\nship','teacher'),
(794,794,'GRADE 2 FORMATIVE ASSESSMENT\nLesson 19 —- Transportation\nPART A — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the short story aloud. Story: Transportation\nIn the street you can see. Buses, cars and taxi. In the air there is a plane. On\nthe rails there is a train.\nDirections:\nListen carefully to the story and answer the questions.\nWhere can you see buses, cars, and taxis?\na. In the street\nb. In the air\nc. On the rails\na. In the street b. In the air c. On the rails What travels in the air?\na. Train\nb. Plane\nc. Boat\nWhat moves on the rails?\na. Car b. Train c. Truck What moves on the rails?\nWhich of these is NOT mentioned in the story?\na. Bicycle b. Taxi c. Plane\nName one vehicle you heard in the story.\na. Car b. Tree c. Flower d.Sand Name one vehicle you heard in the story.\nPART B — VOCABULARY WITH PICTURES\nDirections: Match the picture to the correct word. Write the letter of the\ncorrect answer.\nPicture Icons :\n– truck\n– van\n– ambulance\n– bicycle\n— truck — ambulance — bicycle\n— train — taxi — boat — ship\n– train\n– taxi\n– boat\n– ship\n– airplane\nItems:\nWord List:\n1. ______\nA. Truck\n2. ______\nB. Van\n3. ______\nC. Ambulance\n4. ______\nD. Bicycle\n5. ______\nE. Train\n6. ______\nF. Taxi\n7. ______\nG. Boat\n8. ______\nH. Ship\n9. ______\nI. Airplane\nPART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections: Use the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: bicycle • train • airplane • truck\n1. People ride a to move around short distances.\n2. A travels on tracks.\nAn ______\nflies in the sky.','teacher'),
(795,795,'Lesson 20- Famous Location\nFamous Location\nWhere there is water, life is better.\nWhere there is greenness, air is fresh.\nRelax and refresh, Keep away from stress.\nBulkang Mayon\nBoracay Island\nBanaue Rice\nTerraces\nCoron Reef\nMaria Cristina\nDakak Beach\nFalls\nSohoton Cave\nPagsangjan\nHundred Islands\nFalls','teacher'),
(796,796,'PART A — VOCABULARY WITH PICTURES\nDirections: Match the picture to the correct word. Write the letter of the\ncorrect answer.\nPicture Icons :\ns‘\n<‘.- – Boracay Island\nh – Banaue Rice Terraces ˜u\n˙ – Bulkang Mayon L\ny\n˘ ·k – Coron Reef χ – Maria Cristina Falls Içˇ*\n³ ‘\n«_ – Dakak Beach\n˙\n⬛\n˙\nx¿ –\nÇ, – Hundred Islands\nPagsanjan Falls . – Sohoton Cave ’˜\n1. Items:\nWord List:\nh‘s y ______\n2. y\nA. Bulkang Mayon\nu ˜\nu ˙ ˙ ______\n3. ˙\nB. Banaue Rice Terraces\nL‘\n4. .-\n.- < ______\nC. Maria Cristina Falls\n5. ˘·\nk ˙ ______\n˙\nD. Dakak Beach\n6. χ ______\nE. Pagsanjan Falls\n7. Içˇ*\n«_ ______\nF. Sohoton Cave\n˙³ ‘x¿ ______\n8. ⬛\nG. Hundred Islands\n9.. ______\nH. Coron Reef\nÇ, ’˜ ______\n10. ’˜\nI. Boracay Island\nPART B — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the short story aloud. Story: Famous Location\nWhere there is water, life is better. Where there is greenness, air is fresh. Relax\nand refresh, Keep away from stress.\nDirections: Listen carefully to the story and answer the questions.\n1. What makes life better according to the story?\na. Water\nb. Cars\nc. Mountains\n2. What makes the air fresh?\na. Greenness\nb. Buildings\nc. Roads\n3. What should we do to keep away from stress?\na. Relax and refresh\nb. Sleep in class\nc. Run fast\n4. Which of these is a famous location mentioned in the lesson?\na. Banaue Rice Terraces\nb. Eiffel Tower c. Mount Everest\n5. Name one famous location you heard from the stor\na. Boracay Island\nb. School\nc. Street','teacher'),
(797,797,'PART C — SHORT WRITTEN TASK\nDirections:\nUse the word bank to complete each sentence.\nWord Bank: Boracay Island • Pagsanjan Falls • Bulkang Mayon • Banaue\nRice Terraces\n1. People visit ______\nto see beautiful beaches.\n2. ______\nis a famous volcano in the Philippines.\n3. You can ride a boat at ______\n.\n4. Farmers grow rice at ______\n.','teacher'),
(798,798,'POSTTEST: English – Grade 2 ( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10 only )\nPart I: Vocabulary (15 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence carefully. Choose the correct meaning of the\nunderlined word.\n1. Herbs can cure many illness. What does illness mean?\na) Birthday\nb) A sickness\nc) School subject\n2. Fruits can taste sweet or sour. What does sour mean?\na) Very cold\nb) Not sweet\nc) Too salty\n3. Flowers are the beauty of nature. What does beauty mean?\na) Something ugly\nb) Something nice to see\nc) Something loud\n4. Trees are everywhere. What does everywhere mean?\na) In many places all around\nb) Only in one place\nc) Not in many places\n5. Fruits make us healthy. What does healthy mean?\na) Strong and well\nb) Sick\nc) Dirty\n6. Vegetables keep us active. What does active mean?\na) Feeling weak\nb) Full of energy\nc) Feeling sleepy\n7. Some herbs are called magical. What does magical mean?\na) Special or amazing\nb) Cannot do anything\nc) Ordinary\n8. Animals in the meadow want our attention. What does attention mean?','teacher'),
(799,799,'a) To look and listen carefully\nb) To run away\nc) To ignore\n9. God made many animal creations. What does creations mean?\na) Things that are made\nb) Things that disappear\nc) Things that are broken\n10. Trees are the birds’ shelter. What does shelter mean?\na) A place to stay safe\nb) A type of fruit\nc) A kind of game\n11. Vegetables give nutrients to our body. What does nutrients mean?\na) Things that help us grow\nb) Toys for us to play\nc) Harmful things\n12. The monkey was teasing you and me. What does teasing mean?\na) Playing in a mean or silly way\nb) Helping nicely\nc) Sleeping quietly\n13. Flowers gave us a fragrant odor. What does fragrant mean?\na) Good smell\nb) Bad smell\nc) No smell\n14. Fruits give vitamins that help us grow strong.\na) Weak\nb) Full of energy and healthy\nc) Sleepy\n15. Flowers grow and bloom in different colors. What does bloom mean?\na) To open and show petals\nb) To hide\nc) To fall to the ground\n( For Lesson 1 to Lesson 10\nPart II: Listening Comprehension (15 items)\nonly)\nDirections: Listen carefully to your teacher as she reads the passage or question.\nChoose the correct answer.','teacher'),
(800,800,'16. Why do people like flowers?\na) Because they taste sweet\nb) Because they look bright and lovely\nc) Because they are loud\n17. What do flowers give?\na) A loud noise\nb) A good smell\nc) A sour taste\n18. How do vegetables help us?\na) They make us noisy\nb) They make us strong and healthy\nc) They make us sleepy\n19. What do vegetables give our body?\na) Smoke\nb) Toys\nc) Nutrients\n20. How do fruits taste?\na) Salty\nb) Bitter\nc) Sweet or sour\n21. What do fruits give our body?\na) Vitamins\nb) Sand\nc) Smoke\n22. What do trees give us?\na) Hot air\nb) Clean air\nc) Dirty air\n23. Why do birds live in trees?\na) Trees are safe\nb) Trees are cold\nc) Trees are noise\nLesson 5 – Herbs (Items 24–25)\n24. What can herbs do?\na) Make people laugh\nb) Help cure sickness\nc) Make cars move\n25. Who uses herbs?\na) Sick people','teacher'),
(801,801,'b) Robots\nc) Trees\n26. Which animal helps farmers?\na) Whale\nb) Lobster\nc) Horse\n27. Where do these animals live?\na) On land\nb) In the sea\nc) In the sky\n28. What do some woodland animals do when they see people?\na) They hide\nb) They fly to the sea\nc) They swim\n29. What do animals in the meadow do?\na) They fly around flowers\nb) They dig tunnels\nc) They swim\n30. Which animals swim together in the sea?\na) Pigs and cows\nb) Dolphins and whales\nc) Deer and monkeys','teacher'),
(802,802,'COMPREHENSIVE POSTTEST (Lessons 11–20)\nGRADE 2 – Vocabulary & Listening Comprehension\nPART I — VOCABULARY (15 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct answer.\n1. A blender is used to:\na) Cook rice\nb) Wash plates\nc) Make juice\n2. We use a television to:\na) Water plants\nb) Watch shows\nc) Bake food\n3. A pillow is mainly for:\na) Writing letters\nb) Sleeping comfortably\nc) Cooking meals','teacher'),
(803,803,'4. Soap is used to:\na) Cut paper\nb) Sweep the floor\nc) Clean the body\n5. You can find a car in the:\na) Bedroom\nb) Garage\nc) Garden\n6. A mountain is:\na) A body of water\nb) A type of house\nc) A tall landform\n7. A pond is:\na) A mountain\nb) A large sea\nc) A small body of water\n8. Gold is an example of a:\na) Mineral\nb) Food\nc) Clothing\n9. A truck is helpful for:\na) Flying in the sky\nb) Swimming in the ocean\nc) Carrying heavy goods\n10. Boracay Island is known for its:\na) Tall buildings\nb) White sand beach\nc) Snow\n11. A soap dish is used to:\na) Keep toys\nb) Store soap\nc) Grow plants\n12. We keep our clothes in the:\na) Bookshelf\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Refrigerator\n13. A plateau is:\na) A body of water\nb) A flat land higher than the land around it\nc) A small hill','teacher'),
(804,804,'14. A funnel helps us:\na) Carry books\nb) Pour liquids easily\nc) Play music\n15. A ship travels on:\na) Rails\nb) Land\nc) Water\nPART II — LISTENING COMPREHENSION\nTeacher reads the passages before learner’s answer.\nLesson 11 – Kitchen\nTeacher reads:\n“In the kitchen, we keep everything clean. Put fruits in the blender to make juice. The\nstove cooks vegetables, and the rice cooker cooks rice. Plates and utensils are for\neating.”\n16. What must we do in the kitchen?\na) Keep it clean\nb) Spill water everywhere\nc) Make it messy\n17. What do we put inside the blender?\na) Plates\nb) Rice\nc) Fruits\nLesson 12 – Living Room\nTeacher reads:\n“In the living room, we sit on the sofa and watch TV. There are curtains on the\nwindows and a bookshelf for books.”\n18. Where do people sit in the living room?\na) Sofa\nb) Table\nc) Bookshelf\nLesson 13 – Bedroom\nTeacher reads:\n“In the bedroom, the bed has a pillow, blanket, and bed sheet. A mosquito net\nprotects from insects. Clothes are kept in the wardrobe.”','teacher'),
(805,805,'19. What protects us from insects?\na) Curtain\nb) Blanket\nc) Mosquito net\n20. Where are clothes stored?\na) Floor\nb) Wardrobe\nc) Table\nLesson 14 – Bathroom\nTeacher reads:\n“Use shampoo and soap when bathing. Water is scooped with a bath cup and\npoured into a bucket. Step on the bathmat after bathing.”\n21. What is used to wash the hair?\na) Comb\nb) Shampoo\nc) Soap\n22. What do we step on after taking a bath?\na) Soap dish\nb) Carpet\nc) Bathmat\nLesson 15 – Garage\nTeacher reads:\n“In the garage, the car is parked safely. Tools like pliers, screwdriver, and hammer\nhelp fix small parts. A trolley jack lifts the car.”\n23. What tool lifts the car?\na) Wheel\nb) Hammer\nc) Trolley jack\n24. Which tool fixes screws?\na) Pliers\nb) Screwdriver\nc) Funnel\nLesson 16 – Landforms','teacher'),
(806,806,'Teacher reads:\n“A mountain is tall, a hill is smaller, and a valley lies between them. A plain is wide\nand flat. A shoreline is where land meets water.”\n25. Which landform is tall?\na) Basin\nb) Hill\nc) Mountain\n26. Where does land meet water?\na) Glacier\nb) Shoreline\nc) Desert\nLesson 17 – Bodies of Water\nTeacher reads:\n“The spring, falls, pond, lake, and river make Earth beautiful. The ocean and sea are\nnice to see. Keep them clean.”\n27. Which bodies of water are “nice to see”?\na) River and spring\nb) Lake and pond\nc) Ocean and sea\n28. What should be kept clean?\na) Cars\nb) Ocean and sea\nc) Land\nLesson 18 – Mineral Resources\nTeacher reads the poem.\n29. What is Earth rich in?\na) Treasure\nb) Houses\nc) Toys\n30. Which mineral is mentioned in the poem?\na) Wood\nb) Gold\nc) Plastic','teacher'),
(807,807,'SET A\nPRE-TEST Day 1-10 grade 9 to 10\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write its\nletter on the line.\nSection 1: Reading Comprehension\n______ 1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n______ 2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n______ 3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n______ 4. Where did the magical treehouse take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n______ 5. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n______ 6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house','teacher'),
(808,808,'______ 7. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n______ 8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n______ 9. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n______ 10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n______ 11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n______ 12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\n______ 13. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n______ 14. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals','teacher'),
(809,809,'______ 15. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n______ 16. Who was talking to each other in \"Summer Fun\"?\na. Lita and Lito\nb. Lina and Lino\nc. Lina and Leo\n______ 17. What were they talking about?\na. what to do during the summer\nb. what to have during the summer\nc. what to wear during the summer\n______ 18. The children in the story could be ______\na. brother and sister\nb. neighbors\nc. cousins\n______ 19. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na. pick flowers\nb. pick star apples\nc. go swimming\n______ 20. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na. doing something in the summer\nb. doing something in the house\nc. doing something that we like\n______ 21. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na. picking flowers\nb. cleaning up\nc. swimming\n______ 22. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain','teacher'),
(810,810,'______ 23. What does Nina want to do?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain\n______ 24. Who wants to play tag?\na. Ria\nb. Nina\nc. Ria and Nina\n______ 25. What is \"tag?\"\na. a card game\nb. a video game\nc. a running game\n______ 26. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na. Something might break\nb. Someone might get tired\nc. Something might get lost\n______ 27. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na. careless\nb. careful\nc. curious\n______ 28. Who was Curly?\na. a dog\nb. a doll\nc. a cat\n______ 29. Who gave Curly to Miriam?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n______ 30. Where does Uncle Max live?\na. Cebu\nb. Manila\nc. New York\n______ 31. On what occasion was Curly given?\na. birthday\nb. Christmas\nc. graduation','teacher'),
(811,811,'______ 32. Who helped Miriam open the box?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n______ 33. What words talk about the box?\na. big and light\nb. big and heavy\nc. small and light\n______ 34. What words talk about Curly’s mouth?\na. red\nb. pink\nc. yellow\n______ 35. What was Curly’s dress made of?\na. silk\nb. lace\nc. cotton\n______ 36. What word talks about her hair?\na. curly\nb. brown\nc. straight\n______ 37. What can Curly do?\na. talk\nb. sing\nc. walk\n______ 38. Where does Victor live?\na. in the city\nb. on a farm\nc. near the sea\n______ 39. Which word tells about their house?\na. nipa\nb. cement\nc. wooden\n______ 40. Who is Victor’s sister?\na. Nina\nb. Nora\nc. Nida','teacher'),
(812,812,'______ 41. Who is older, Victor or Nora?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Cannot be determined\n______ 42. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na. 3\nb. 4\nc. 5\n______ 43. Which one do they NOT have?\na. cow\nb. horse\nc. carabao\n______ 44. Who takes care of the horse?\na. Victor\nb. Father\nc. Mother\n______ 45. Who takes care of the carabao?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Father\n______ 46. Who takes care of the chickens?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Mother\n______ 47. Which one does Nora take care of?\na. goat\nb. chickens\nc. carabao\nSection 2: Vocabulary\n______ 48. In \"The Story of the First Thanksgiving,\" what does the word harvest mean?\na) a big ship\nb) the food that is gathered from crops\nc) a type of celebration\nd) a difficult time\n______ 49. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word nectar mean?\na) a sweet liquid found in flowers','teacher'),
(813,813,'b) the stem of a plant\nc) the journey a seed takes\nd) the roots of a flower\n______ 50. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word sprouted mean?\na) to be blown by the wind\nb) to be planted in a field\nc) to start to grow\nd) to collect food','teacher'),
(814,814,'SET B\nPRE-TEST Day 11-20 Grade 3-4\nInstructions: Read each question carefully and choose the best answer. Encircle the\nletter of your choice.\nVocabulary\n1. What is the best definition for coax?\na. to force someone\nb. to persuade gently\nc. to ignore someone\nd. to argue with someone\n2. If someone is distrustful, they are:\na. Very confident\nb. Lacking trust\nc. Extremely happy\nd. Easily persuaded\n3. The word despise most nearly means:\na. To admire greatly\nb. To dislike very much\nc. To feel sorry for\nd. To be jealous of\n4. A person who is arrogant:\na. Thinks they are better than others\nb. Is very shy and quiet\nc. Is kind to everyone\nd. Works very hard\n5. To apologize means to:\na. Express regret for a mistake\nb. Celebrate a victory\nc. Make a formal promise\nd. Give someone a gift\nGrammar and Writing\n6. Which sentence is punctuated correctly?\na. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice.\"','teacher'),
(815,815,'b. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nc. The fox said, \"You have a beautiful voice.\"\nd. The fox said \"You have a beautiful voice\".\n7. What is the simple predicate (verb) in this sentence: \"The greedy lion chased the\ndeer.\"\na. The greedy lion\nb. chased\nc. the deer\nd. chased the deer\n8. Which word is an antonym for sincerity?\na. Honesty\nb. Dishonesty\nc. Friendship\nd. Kindness\n9. What part of speech is the word huge in this sentence: \"The elephant had a huge\nbody.\"?\na. Noun\nb. Verb\nc. Adjective\nd. Adverb\n10. Which sentence is written in the future tense?\na. The farmer calls his sons.\nb. The farmer called his sons.\nc. The farmer is calling his sons.\nd. The farmer will call his sons.\nReading Comprehension\nRead the short passage and answer questions 11-13.\n\"The ants were angry at the elephant for spraying them with water. They decided to\nteach him a lesson. They crept into his ears and started biting him. The elephant\ncried and apologized, learning never to trouble others again.\"\n11. Why were the ants angry?\na. The elephant stepped on their home.\nb. The elephant sprayed them with water.\nc. The elephant ate their food.\nd. The elephant ignored them.\n12. How did the ants teach the elephant a lesson?\na. They told the other animals.\nb. They bit him inside his ears.\nc. They stole his food.\nd. They sprayed him with water.','teacher'),
(816,816,'13. What was the result of the ants\' action?\na. The elephant became angrier.\nb. The elephant never troubled anyone again.\nc. The elephant chased the ants away.\nd. The elephant became friends with the ants.\nLiterary Concepts\n14. The central lesson or message of a story is called the:\na. Plot\nb. Moral\nc. Setting\nd. Conflict\n15. The main problem that characters face in a story is the:\na. Solution\nb. Climax\nc. Conflict\nd. Theme\n16. \"The wind whispered through the trees\" is an example of:\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole\n17. A story that uses animals as characters to teach a lesson is called a:\na. Biography\nb. Fable\nc. Mystery\nd. Fantasy\n18. The high point or most exciting part of a story is the:\na. Exposition\nb. Rising Action\nc. Climax\nd. Falling Action\nGeneral Knowledge & Inference\n19. What is the primary purpose of a fable?\na. To explain historical events\nb. To teach a moral lesson\nc. To describe a scientific process\nd. To tell a funny story with no lesson\n20. If a character is described as \"cunning,\" they are most likely to be:\na. Honest and kind\nb. Shy and quiet','teacher'),
(817,817,'c. Clever and tricky\nd. Strong and brave\n21. What is the best source to find a synonym for the word \"huge\"?\na. A dictionary\nb. A thesaurus\nc. An encyclopedia\nd. An atlas\n22. What is the term for the feeling of sadness or pity you feel for a character?\na. Empathy\nb. Sympathy\nc. Anger\nd. Joy\n23. Which of these is a complete sentence?\na. The old tortoise slowly.\nb. Challenged the hare for a race.\nc. The hare ran very fast.\nd. Under the tree for some time.\n24. What do we call the narrator of a story who is also a character in the story?\na. First-person narrator\nb. Second-person narrator\nc. Third-person narrator\nd. Omniscient narrator\n25. What is the term for a word that means the opposite of another word?\na. Synonym\nb. Antonym\nc. Homophone\nd. Homonym\nContinuing with more general items...\n26. What is the opposite meaning of the word victory?\na. Success\nb. Defeat\nc. Contest\nd. Race\n27. Which word is a noun?\na. Run\nb. Beautiful\nc. Peace\nd. Quickly\n28. The phrase \"as slow as a tortoise\" is an example of a:\na. Metaphor\nb. Simile\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole','teacher'),
(818,818,'29. What is the purpose of the beginning of a story (exposition)?\na. To solve the problem\nb. To introduce characters and setting\nc. To present the most exciting action\nd. To provide the moral lesson\n30. Which of these is a theme that might be found in a fable?\na. The chemical process of photosynthesis\nb. The importance of honesty\nc. The history of ancient Rome\nd. The rules of a board game\n31. What does the prefix \"re-\" mean in the word \"rewrite\"?\na. Not\nb. Again\nc. Before\nd. After\n32. Which sentence uses correct subject-verb agreement?\na. The four sons argues.\nb. The four sons argue.\nc. The four sons is arguing.\nd. The four sons was arguing.\n33. What is the term for the actual, dictionary definition of a word?\na. Connotation\nb. Denotation\nc. Synonym\nd. Acronym\n34. In the story \"The Farmer and His Four Sons,\" what does the bundle of sticks\nsymbolize?\na. Individual strength\nb. Family quarrels\nc. Unity and strength\nd. Old age and weakness\n35. Which part of a story comes after the climax?\na. Exposition\nb. Rising Action\nc. Falling Action\nd. Introduction\n36. What is the term for a conversation between two or more characters?\na. Monologue\nb. Dialogue\nc. Narration\nd. Description','teacher'),
(819,819,'37. Which word best describes the fox in \"The Fox and the Crow\"?\na. Honest\nb. Generous\nc. Cunning\nd. Brave\n38. What is the best way to identify the moral of a fable?\na. Look at the title.\nb. Find the lesson the characters learn.\nc. Identify the main character.\nd. Count the number of animals.\n39. \"He was a lion in battle.\" This is an example of a:\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Onomatopoeia\n40. Which word is a verb?\na. Decision\nb. Decisive\nc. Decide\nd. Decisively\n41. What is the term for an exaggerated statement used for effect?\na. Simile\nb. Metaphor\nc. Personification\nd. Hyperbole\n42. Which of these is a compound word?\na. Therefore\nb. Sunshine\nc. Elephant\nd. Together\n43. What is the primary purpose of narrative writing?\na. To convince the reader\nb. To tell a story\nc. to explain how to do something\nd. To describe a person or place\n44. Which sentence is an opinion?\na. The hare lost the race.\nb. The tortoise has a shell.\nc. The hare is the fastest animal.\nd. The race was to the riverbank.\n45. What is the term for the feelings and ideas associated with a word (beyond its\ndictionary definition)?\na. Denotation\nb. Connotation\nc. Definition\nd. Pronunciation','teacher'),
(820,820,'46. What do you call the perspective from which a story is told?\na. Plot\nb. Setting\nc. Point of View\nd. Theme\n47. Which of these is a proper noun?\na. jungle\nb. farmer\nc. Birbal\nd. son\n48. What is the best way to understand a character\'s traits?\na. Look only at their name.\nb. See what they say, do, and what others say about them.\nc. Focus only on the story\'s setting.\nd. Read the first paragraph only.\n49. What is the name for a word that describes a verb (e.g., slowly, quickly)?\na. Adjective\nb. Adverb\nc. Noun\nd. Preposition\n50. The final part of a story where the conflict is resolved is called the:\na. Climax\nb. Rising Action\nc. Resolution\nd. Introduction\nPRE-TEST ANSWER KEY\n1.B\n11.B\n21.B\n31.B\n41.D\n2. B\n12.B\n22.B\n32.B\n42.B\n3. B\n13.B\n23.C\n33.B\n43.B\n4. A\n14.B\n24.A\n34.C\n44.C\n5. A\n15.C\n25.B\n35.C\n45.B\n6. B\n16.C\n26.B\n36.B\n46.C\n7. B\n17.B\n27.C\n37.C\n47.C\n8. B\n18.C\n28.B\n38.B\n48.B\n9. C\n19.B\n29.B\n39.B\n49.B\n10. D\n20.C\n30.B\n40.C\n50.C','teacher'),
(821,821,'GRADE 3 Intervention Activities\nActivity 1:\n\"The Mystery of the Missing Lunchbox\"\nSarah opened her backpack, but her lunchbox was gone! She looked\neverywhere. \"Where could it be?\" she wondered. She asked\nher friends, but no one had seen it. Suddenly, she remembered\nleaving it in the library after reading a book\nabout archaeology. She raced to the library and found it right where she left it.\nQuestions:\n1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs','teacher'),
(822,822,'Activity 2:\n\"The Magical Tree house Adventure\"\nJack and Annie climbed into their magical tree house. Today, the tree\nhouse took them to a tropical rainforest.\nThey saw colorful birds, heard monkeys\nchattering,\nand\ndiscovered\na\nhidden\nwaterfall. They learned about different\ntypes of plants and animals that live in the\nrainforest habitat.\nQuestions:\n1. Where did the magical tree house take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n2. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n3. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house','teacher'),
(823,823,'Activity 3:\n\"The Inventor\'s Workshop\"\nEmily loved inventing new things. Her workshop was filled\nwith tools, wires, and gadgets. One day, she decided to\nbuild a robot that could help her with her chores. After\nmany\nattempts, she finally created a robot that could sweep, dust, and even make her\nbed. She called it \"Handy Helper.\"\nQuestions:\n1. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n2. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n3. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend\nb) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster','teacher'),
(824,824,'Activity 4:\n“The Story of the First Thanksgiving”\nLong ago, the Pilgrims came to America on a ship called the Mayflower. They\nhad a difficult time finding food. The Native Americans, like the\nWampanoag tribe, helped them learn how to grow corn\nand other crops. The next year, they had a big feast to\ncelebrate their harvest. This feast is now known as\nThanksgiving.\nVocabulary Focus: Pilgrims, Mayflower, harvest, crops, tribe\nARAL Connection: Social studies vocabulary and understanding historical events.\nQuestions:\n1. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n2. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n4. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween','teacher'),
(825,825,'Activity 5:\n\"The Little Seed\'s Journey\"\nOnce upon a time, there was a little seed. The wind blew it far away from its\nparent plant. The seed landed in a field. Rain fell, and\nthe seed began to grow. It sprouted roots and a tiny\nstem.\nSoon, it became a beautiful flower. Bees came to collect\nnectar from the flower, helping it make more seeds.\nVocabulary Focus: parent, nectar, sprouted, stem, journey\nARAL Connection: Science-related vocabulary and understanding plant life cycles.\nQuestions:\n1. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n2. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n3. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water','teacher'),
(826,826,'Activity\n6: SET A\nSUMMER FUN\n“Let’s have some\nfun this summer,”\nsays Leo. “Let’s\nswim in the river,”\nsays Lina.\n“Let’s get some star\napples from the\ntree,” says Leo.\n“Let’s pick flowers,”\nsays Lina.\n“That is so much\nfun!” says Mama.\n“But can you help\nme dust the\nshelves too?”\n“Yes, we can\nMama,” they say.\n“Helping can be\nfun too!”\nQuestions\n1. Who were talking to each other?\na. Lita and Lito\nb. Lina and Lino\nc. Lina and Leo\n2. What were they talking about?\na. what to do during the summer\nb. what to have during the summer\nc. what to wear during the summer\n3. The children in the story could be ______\na. brother and sister\nb. neighbors\nc. cousins\n4. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na. pick flowers\nb. pick star apples\nc. go swimming\n5. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na. doing something in the summer','teacher'),
(827,827,'b. doing something in the house\nc. doing something that we like\n6. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na. picking flowers\nb. cleaning up\nc. swimming','teacher'),
(828,828,'Activity 7:\nSET B\nA RAINY DAY\nNina and Ria are looking out the window.\n“I do not like getting wet in the rain,” says Nina.\n“What can we do?” asks Ria.\n“We can play house,” says Nina.\n“Or we can play tag,” says Ria.\n“Okay, let’s play tag. You’re it!” says Nina.\nNina runs from Ria and bumps a lamp.\n“Oh no!” says Nina.\n“We must not play tag in the house.”\nQuestions\n1. What is it that Nina does not like?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. getting wet in the rain\n2. What does Nina want to do?\na. playing tag\nb. playing house\nc. gets wet in the rain\n3. Who wants to play tag?\na. Ria\nb. Nina\nc. Ria and Nina\n4. What is \"tag?\"\na. a card game\nb. a video game\nc. a running game\n5. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na. Something might break\nb. Someone might get tired\nc. Something might get lost\n6. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na. careless\nb. careful\nc. curious','teacher'),
(829,829,'Activity\n9: Set B\nA GIFT FROM UNCLE\nDo you have an uncle living far away?\nMiriam has. His name is Max. Miriam calls him\nUncle Max. He lives in New York.\nLast Christmas, Uncle Max sent Miriam a gift. It\ncame in a big heavy box. Father helped open the\nbox.\nThen they saw something very pretty. It was a big doll. It had round\nblue eyes and a small red mouth. It had a blue lace dress and curly black\nhair. Miriam called it Curly. She loved to play with it. What Miriam liked\nbest was the way Curly walked. Miriam would hold one of its hands and\nthey would walk together around the living room. Curly made Miriam\nhappy.\n1. Who was Curly?\na. a dog\nb. a doll\nc. a cat\n2. Who gave Curly to Miriam?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n3. Where does Uncle Max live?\na. Cebu\nb. Manila\nc. New York\n4. On what occasion was Curly given?\na. birthday\nb. Christmas c. graduation\n5. Who helped Miriam open the box?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Uncle Max\n6. What words talk about the box?\na. big and light\nb. big and heavy\nc. small and light\n7. What words talk about Curly’s mouth?\na. red\nb. pink\nc. yellow\n8. What was Curly’s dress made of?\na. silk\nb. lace\nc. cotton\n9. What word talks about her hair?\na. curly\nb. brown\nc. straight\n10. What can Curly do?\na. talk\nb. sing c. walk','teacher'),
(830,830,'Activity 10:\nSet A\nTAKING CARE OF ANIMALS\nVictor lives on a farm. He lives with his parents\nin a little nipa house. Victor has an elder sister\nnamed Nora. Victor and Nora help their parents.\nThey help take care of their animals. They have a\ncarabao, a horse, a goat, and some chickens.\nFather takes care of the horse. Victor takes care\nof the carabao. Mother takes care of the chickens.\nNora takes care of the\ngoat. Their animals are all fat and healthy. Each one takes care of their animal\nvery well.\n1. Where does Victor live?\na. in the city\nb. on a farm\nc. near the sea\n2. Which word tells about their house?\na. nipa\nb. cement\nc. wooden\n3. Who is Victor’s sister?\na. Nina\nb. Nora\nc. Nida\n4. Who is older, Victor or Nora?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Does not tell\n5. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na. 3\nb. 4.\nc.5\n6. Which one they do not have?\na. cow\nb. horse\nc. carabao\n7. Who takes care of the horse?\na. Victor\nb. Father\nc. Mother\n8. Who takes care of the carabao?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Father\n9. Who takes care of the chickens?\na. Nora\nb. Victor\nc. Mother\n10. Which one does Nora take care of?\na. goat\nb. chickens\nc. carabao','teacher'),
(831,831,'Activity 11:\nTHE BANANA PEELINGS\nCelso was eating bananas one evening. He threw the peelings out of\nthe window. The next morning, Celso got ready for school. He did not want\nto be late for school. He walked fast.\n“Ouch!” Celso cried as he stepped on some banana\npeelings. Down he fell. His clothes became dirty. His\nbooks dropped.\n“Are you hurt?” Mother asked running to him.\n“No, Mother, I am not hurt,” Celso said as he got up.\nHe looked at the banana peelings.\n“Somebody did not use the garbage can,” Mother\nsaid.\n“I threw these peelings last night, Mother. Next time, I will use the garbage\ncan,” said Celso.\n1.\nWhat did Celso eat?\na. bananas\nb. mangoes\nc. oranges\n2.\nWhen did he eat the fruit?\na. last night\nb. that morning\nc. last week\n3.\nWhen did he throw the peeling?\na. into the basket b. out of the window c. into the garbage can\n4.\nWhere was Celso going?\na. to church\nb. to market\nc. to school\n5.\nWhat sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late?\na. He walked fast\nb. He walked slowly c. He played on the way\n6.\nWho stepped on the banana peelings?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Celso\n7.\nWho saw Celso fall?\na. Father\nb. Mother\nc. Sister\n8.\nWho did not use the garbage can?\na. Mother\nb. Celso\nc. Sister\n9.\nWas Celso hurt?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell\n10.\nWhich word tells about Celso?\na. polite\nb. kind\nc. truthful','teacher'),
(832,832,'Activity 12:\nTHE NEWS BOY\nAt five o’clock in the afternoon, the train arrives in Naga City.\nThe train carries the newspapers from Manila. Alfredo, a Grade Four\npupil, sells newspapers after class in the afternoon. He sells for two\nhours. At seven o’clock, he goes home. He has time to study his\nlessons.\nAlfredo earns one hundred pesos a day. He wants to give\nhis money to Mother. But Mother told him to put his money in his piggy bank. Alfredo’s\nparents are not poor. They can give him money he needs, but Alfredo wants to sell\nnewspapers. He wants to earn his own money.\n1.\nWhere does Alfredo live?\na. in Manila\nb. in Naga City\nc. on a farm\n2.\nWhat time does the train arrive in Naga City?\na. four o’clock\nb. five o’clock\nc. six o’clock\n3.\nWhat carries the newspapers to Naga City?\na. a car\nb. a truck\nc. a train\n4.\nWhere do the newspapers come from?\na. Manila\nb. Cebu City\nc. Pasay City\n5.\nWhat does Alfredo do?\na. sells fruit\nb. sells candies\nc. sells newspapers\n6.\nHow long does Alfredo sell newspapers?\na. one hour\nb. two hours\nc. three hours\n7.\nHow much does he earn a day?\na. five pesos\nb. seventy-five pesos\nc. one hundred pesos\n8.\nWhat does he do with the money?\na. gives it to his mother.\nb. buy cakes and candies.\nc. keeps it in his piggy bank.\n9.\nWhat kind of a boy is Alfredo?\na. clean\nb. polite\nc. industrious\n10.\nAre his parents poor?\na. yes\nb. no\nc. does not tell','teacher'),
(833,833,'Activity 13:\nA SICK CLASSMATE\nOne morning, Miss Luna said to her Grade 3 class, “I got a letter\nfrom Teresa’s mother. Teresa cannot come to school. She is sick. The doctor\ntold her to stay in bed for a few days. What shall we do for Teresa?” “Let\nus visit her this afternoon,” said Linda.\n“Yes, let us visit her,” said the other children. That afternoon, the\nchildren went to visit Teresa. The girls brought her some fruits. The boys\nbrought her a can of biscuits. Miss Luna brought her some roses. Teresa was sleeping when\nthey arrived. Soon, she woke up. She was happy to see her teacher and classmates.\n1. Who is Miss Luna?\na. A nurse\nb. A mother\nc. A teacher\n2. What did she get one morning?\na. A letter\nb. A telegram\nc. A newspaper\n3. Who sent a letter?\na. Teresa\nb. Teresa’s mother\nc. Teresa’s father\n4. Why was Teresa absent?\na. She was sick.\nb. She was busy.\nc. She was away.\n5. Did a doctor treat her?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell.\n6. What did the children do?\na. They visited her.\nb. They sent flowers.\nc. They sent her letter.\n7. What did the girls bring?\na. Milk\nb. Fruits\nc. flowers\n8. What did the boys bring?\na. Fruits\nb. Roses\nc. biscuits\n9. Who brought some roses?\na. The girls\nb. The boys\nc. Miss Luna\n10. When did they visit Teresa?\na. Morning\nb. Afternoon\nc. evening','teacher'),
(834,834,'Activity 14: Set A\nTHE KITTEN\nOne rainy afternoon, Juan did not go straight home from\nschool. He had his raincoat on, so he did not get wet. Then he saw a\nkitten trembling in the grass. He stopped and looked at it. It began to\nmew very softly.\nJuan was sorry for the kitten. He picked it up and put it under his raincoat.\nHe brought it home. He put it near the stove with fire. The kitten looked at Juan and said,\n“\nMew, mew.” It wanted to say, “Thank you.” From that time on, the kitten became\nhis pet. He loved his pet very much.\n1. What time of the day was it?\na. Morning\nb. Noon\nc. afternoon\n2. What kind of afternoon was it?\na. Rainy\nb. Sunny\nc. cloudy\n3. Where was Juan going?\na. Home\nb. To school\nc. To church\n4. What was Juan wearing?\na. A hat\nb. A sweater\nc. A raincoat\n5. What did Juan see on the way?\na. Dog\nb. Kitten\nc. chick\n6. How did the kitten feel?\na. Hot\nb. Cold\nc. warm\n7. What did Juan feel for the kitten?\na. Pity\nb. Gladness\nc. happiness\n8. Where did he bring it?\na. Home\nb. School\nc. In the shade\n9. Where did he put the kitten?\na. Near the fire\nb. the table\nc. Near the bed\n10. Did the kitten like to stay near the fire?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell','teacher'),
(835,835,'Activity 14:\nSet B\nTHE COCONUT\nThe coconut is a tall palm tree. It has no branches. The trunk\nis strong. It makes a good post. We get oil from the ripe coconut\nmilk. The young coconut meat is good to eat. It is good for making\ncandies and salad.\nDoormats are made out of the coconut husk. The long coconut\nleaves are woven into baskets. Brooms are made from the midribs\nof the long leaves. Coconut shells are made into buttons, coconut\nshell banks, ash trays and many others. The stalk of the leaves how useful the coconut is!\nEvery part of it can be used.\n1. What word tells about the coconut tree?\na. Short\nb. Tall\nc. small\n2. Does the coconut tree have branches?\na. Yes\nb. No\nc. Does not tell\n3. What part of the coconut tree is good for a post?\na. Trunk\nb. Roots\nc. fruits\n4. From where can we get oil?\na. From coconut husk\nb. From ripe coconut milk\nc. From young coconut meat\n5. Which is good to eat?\na. Coconut husk\nb. Coconut shell\nc. Coconut meat\n6. What part is made into doormats?\na. Shell\nb. Husk\nc. midribs\n7. What can be made from the midribs?\na. Buttons\nb. Brooms\nc. candies\n8. What part is woven into baskets?\na. Husk\nb. Shell\nc. leaves\n9. Which part can be made into buttons?\na. Husk\nb. Shell\nc. midribs\n10. What is the use of the stalk of the leaves?\na. For fuel\nb. For post\nc. For food','teacher'),
(836,836,'Activity 15:\nGROWING VEGETABLE\nLino went with mother to market. They bought some vegetables. Mother\nsaid, “I was able to buy only some with my money. Vegetables cost much\nnow.”\nLino was sorry for Mother. They did not have much money. So, he said,\n“Let’s plant vegetables in our backyard. Then we will not have to buy\nthem in the market. “So, Lino planted three plots of\ntomatoes, two plots of eggplants and a plot of pechay. He had some amargoso climbing on\nthe bamboo fence. Lino worked in his garden after class every afternoon. He grew more\nvegetables than they could eat. Mother sold some of them in the market.\n1. Where did Mother and Lino go?\na. church\nb. school\nc. market\n2. What did they buy?\na. Fish\nb. Meat\nc. vegetables\n3. Which word tells about the vegetables?\na. Very cheap\nb. Cost much\nc. Very many\n4. Where did Lino plant vegetables?\na. In school\nb. On the farm\nc. In the backyard\n5. How many plots of tomatoes did he plant?\na. Two\nb. Three\nc. four\n6. How many plots were planted to eggplants?\na. One\nb. Two\nc. Three\n7. How many plots were planted to pechay?\na. One\nb. Two\nc. Three\n8. How many plots did he have in all?\na. Four\nb. Five\nc. Six\n9. What vegetables were climbing on the fence?\na. Beans\nb. Squash\nc. Amargosos\n10. Why did mother sell some vegetables?\na. She had no money.\nb. She did not like vegetables.\nc. They had more than they could eat.','teacher'),
(837,837,'Activity 16:\nA MOONLIGHT NIGHT\nThe moon was big and bright. The children played in the\nmoonlight. They played Hide and Seek. Mario hid behind the\nacacia tree. Andres hid\nbehind some bushes. Isabel hid behind a pile of hollow blocks. Rita\nis behind some banana plants. Edmund looked around but saw no\none. Just then someone moved behind the bushes. Edmund ran to\nsee who it was and found Andres. “One, two, three!” he said. “Now\nyou are ‘It’, Andres.’’ The children played and played. How happy they were!\n1. What part of the day was it?\na. night\nb. morning\nc. afternoon\n2. Where did the children play?\na. In the rain\nb. In the sunshine\nc. In the moonlight\n3. What game did the children play?\na. Hide and Seek\nb. Jump the Spine\nc. Cat and Mouse\n4. Who was the first ‘It’?\na. Mario\nb. Andres\nc. Edmund\n5. Who hid behind the acacia tree?\na. Mario\nb. Isabel\nc. Andres\n6. Who hid behind some bush?\na. Rita\nb. Isabel\nc. Andres\n7. Who hid behind hollow blocks?\na. Rita\nb. Mario\nc. Isabel\n8. Who hid behind some banana plants?\na. Rita\nb. Mario\nc. Isabel\n9. Who was the next ‘It’?\na. Mario\nb. Andres\nc. Edmund\n10. How did the children feel?\na. Tired\nb. happy\nc. sleepy','teacher'),
(838,838,'Activity 17:\nRAMON’S CAKE\nIt was recess time. Pedro and Ramon went to buy cakes. Then\nthey sat near the gate. They began to eat their cakes. Just then Oscar\nran against Ramon. Ramon’s cake fell to the ground.\n“Look what you did to my cake,” Ramon said.\n“I am sorry, Ramon. I did not mean to knock your cake down,”\nsaid Oscar.\n“Why did you not look where you were going?” asked Ramon.\n“Tony ran after me and I did not look where I was going,” said Oscar.\nRamon was angry. He was about to box Oscar.\n“Never mind,” said Pedro. “Oscar did not mean to knock you cake down, Ramon.\nI still have my cake. Let us divide it.”\n1. What time was it?\na. noon time\nb. recess time\nc. time to go home\n2. What did Ramon and Pedro buy?\na. cakes\nb. banana\nc. ice cream\n3. Where did they sit?\na. Near the stair\nb. Near the door\nc. Near the gate\n4. Who ran against Ramon?\na. Tony\nb. Pedro\nc. Oscar\n5. What happened to Ramon’s cake?\na. It fell down.\nb. Oscar got it.\nc. Ramon ate it.\n6. Who ran after Oscar?\na. Tony\nb. Pedro\nc. Ramon\n7. Who was angry?\na. Pedro\nb. Oscar\nc. Ramon\n8. What was Ramon about to do?\na. Cry\nb. go home\nc. box Oscar\n9. What did Pedro do?\na. He went away.\nb. He boxed Oscar.\nc. He gave Ramon some cake.\n10. Which boy would you like for a friend?\na. Pedro\nb. Oscar\nc. Ramon','teacher'),
(839,839,'Activity 18:\nSHINE!\nAntonio was the eldest child. They were six children in the\nfamily. His family was poor. His father was sick. His mother\nworked hard to earn money. She washed clothes for other people.\nBut mother sent Antonio to school. He was in Grade Four.\nAntonio helped Mother earn money. He worked after classes in the\nafternoon. When he arrived from school, he usually carried his box\nand\nshouted “Shine! Shine!” He earned ₱ 80.00 or more on school days. On Saturdays\nand Sundays, he earned three times as much.\nWould like a boy like Antonio for a friend?\n1. Which word tells about Antonio’s family?\na. rich\nb. poor\nc. wealthy\n2. What happened to his father?\na. got sick\nb. was killed\nc. went away\n3. How many children were in the family?\na. four\nb. five\nc. six\n4. Which word tells about Antonio?\na. Youngest\nb. second\nc. eldest\n5. Who worked hard to earn money?\na. Father\nb. mother\nc. Antonio\n6. What did mother do to earn money?\na. sold fruits\nb. sold vegetables c. washed clothes\n7. In what grade was Antonio?\na. Grade Three\nb. Grade Four\nc. Grade Five\n8. What did he do to help mother?\na. Sold bottles\nb. Shined shoes\nc.\nSold newspaper\n9. About how much did he earn on school days?\na. ₱ 80.00\nb. ₱ 40.00\nc. ₱ 60.00\n10. How much did he earn on Saturdays and Sundays?\na. ₱ 90.00\nb. ₱ 60.00\nc. ₱ 240.00','teacher'),
(840,840,'Activity 19:\nSet A\nFOWLS\nFowls are animals. They are animals with two feet and two wings.\nTheir bodies are covered with feathers. They give us eggs. Their\nmeat is good to eat. Chicken, ducks, turkeys and geese\nare fowls. They eat grains such as palay and corn.\nChicken like worms. They scratch in the ground to look\nfor worms.\nDucks and geese like to swim. They like to stay in the water.\nThey are water birds so they have webbed feet. Turkeys\nhave beautiful feathers. The male turkey spreads its tail like a fan. Geese\nare good watchers. They make loud noise when people come near. Fowls\nare\ngood to raise. Many people get rich because of poultry rising.\n1. What are fowls?\na. Plant\nb. trees\nc. Animals\n2. How many feet do fowls have?\na. Two\nb. Four\nc. Many\n3. What covers their bodies?\na. Hair\nb. Hide\nc. Feathers\n4. What make them fly?\na. Feet\nb. Wings\nc. Feathers\n5. Which is not a grain?\na. Corn\nb. Meat\nc. Palay\n6. Which does not have webbed feet?\na. Duck\nb. chicken\nc. goose\n7. Which one do fowls not give us?\na. Milk\nb. Eggs\nc. Meat\n8. Where do ducks and geese like to stay?\na. In the sand\nb. On the water\nc. On the branches\nof tress\n9. Why do chickens scratch on the ground?\na. To look for fish\nb. to look for water\nc. to look\nfor worms\n10. Which are good watchers?\na. ducks\nb. geese\nc. turkeys','teacher'),
(841,841,'Activity 20:\nTHE FIRST MONKEY\nLong time ago, there was a farmer who had a wide corn field.\nHe grew big and sweet corn. One day he saw some of his corn gone.\nMany corn plants had no more fruits. He wanted to catch whoever\nstole his corn.\nThe next day he hid behind a big mango tree. He carried a\nstick. He watched and watched until he saw a man coming.\nThe man passed through a broken part of the fence. The man began to pick some corn.\nThe farmer went from behind the mango tree and walked towards the man. The man\nsaw the farmer and started to run. The farmer ran after him but he could not catch him.\nThen he threw the stick at the man’s back and became a tail. The\nman went up the tree. He became smaller and smaller until he became the monkey.\n1. When did the story happen?\na. Last year\nb. A few years ago c. a long time ago\n2. What did the farmer have?\na. A rice field\nb. a camote field\nc. a corn field\n3. What words will tell about his corn?\na. Big and sweet\nb. small and sweet c. sweet and yellow\n4. What happened to his corn?\na. was stolen\nb. destroyed by insects\nc. destroyed by the\nwind\n5. Where did the farmer hide one day?\na. up the mango tree\nb. behind the guava tree c. behind the mango\ntree\n6. What did he carry?\na. A stick\nb. Some fruits\nc. some stones\n7. Who did he see come into the corn field?\na. A dog\nb. A man\nc. a monkey\n8. What did the farmer do to the man?\na. caught him\nb. threw the stick at him\nc. beat him with\nthe stick\n9. What happened with the stick?\na. was lost\nb. was broken\nc. became a tail\n10. What happened to the man?\na. became sick\nb. became a monkey\nc. became a corn\nplant','teacher'),
(842,842,'SET A\nPOST-TEST (Based on Days 1-10)\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write the\ncorresponding letter on your answer sheet.\n1. What was missing from Sarah\'s backpack?\na) her homework\nb) her lunchbox\nc) her pencil\nd) her book\n2. Where did Sarah remember leaving her lunchbox?\na) in the classroom\nb) in the cafeteria\nc) in the library\nd) on the bus\n3. What book was Sarah reading that made her forget her lunchbox?\na) a book about animals\nb) a book about space\nc) a book about archaeology\nd) a book about dinosaurs\n4. Where did the magical tree house take Jack and Annie?\na) to the desert\nb) to the mountains\nc) to a tropical rainforest\nd) to the beach\n5. What did they hear in the rainforest?\na) lions roaring\nb) monkeys chattering\nc) wolves howling\nd) elephants trumpeting\n6. What is the word for the place where plants and animals live?\na) city\nb) habitat\nc) school\nd) house\n7. What did Emily love to do?\na) sing songs\nb) invent new things\nc) play sports\nd) read books\n8. What was Emily\'s workshop filled with?\na) toys, games, and puzzles\nb) tools, wires, and gadgets\nc) books, pencils, and paper\nd) clothes, shoes, and hats\n9. What did Emily call her robot?\na) Rob Friend','teacher'),
(843,843,'b) Handy Helper\nc) Super Cleaner\nd) Dust Buster\n10. What was the name of the ship the Pilgrims came to America on?\na) the Santa Maria\nb) the Mayflower\nc) the Nina\nd) the Pinta\n11. Who helped the Pilgrims learn how to grow food?\na) the British\nb) the French\nc) the Spanish\nd) the Native Americans\n12. What is the name of the big feast they had to celebrate their harvest?\na) Christmas\nb) Easter\nc) Thanksgiving\nd) Halloween\nActivity 5: The Little Seed\'s Journey\n13. What blew the little seed far away?\na) the sun\nb) the rain\nc) the wind\nd) the snow\n14. What did the seed sprout?\na) leaves and branches\nb) roots and a tiny stem\nc) fruit and vegetables\nd) flowers and petals\n15. What did the bees collect from the flower?\na) pollen\nb) nectar\nc) seeds\nd) water\n16. Who were talking to each other?\na) Lita and Lito\nb) Lina and Lino\nc) Lina and Leo\n17. What were they talking about?\na) what to do during the summer\nb) what to have during the summer\nc) what to wear during the summer\n18. The children in the story could be ______\na) brother and sister\nb) neighbors\nc) cousins','teacher'),
(844,844,'19. Which of these will they do if they are hungry?\na) pick flowers\nb) pick star apples\nc) go swimming\n20. Doing something \"fun\" means ______\n.\na) doing something in the summer\nb) doing something in the house\nc) doing something that we like\n21. Which of these is the best example of being helpful?\na) picking flowers\nb) cleaning up\nc) swimming\n22. What is it that Nina does not like?\na) playing tag\nb) playing house\nc) getting wet in the rain\n23. What does Nina want to do?\na) play tag\nb) play house\nc) get wet in the rain\n24. Who wants to play tag?\na) Ria\nb) Nina\nc) Ria and Nina\n25. What is \"tag?\"\na) a card game\nb) a video game\nc) a running game\n26. Why wasn’t it a good idea to play tag in the house?\na) Something might break.\nb) Someone might get tired.\nc) Something might get lost.\n27. Which word tells what Ria and Nina should be?\na) careless\nb) careful\nc) curious\n28. Who was Curly?\na) a dog\nb) a doll\nc) a cat\n29. Who gave Curly to Miriam?\na) Father\nb) Mother\nc) Uncle Max\n30. Where does Uncle Max live?\na) Cebu','teacher'),
(845,845,'b) Manila\nc) New York\n31. On what occasion was Curly given?\na) birthday\nb) Christmas\nc) graduation\n32. Who helped Miriam open the box?\na) Father\nb) Mother\nc) Uncle Max\n33. What words talk about the box?\na) big and light\nb) big and heavy\nc) small and light\n34. What words talk about Curly’s mouth?\na) red\nb) pink\nc) yellow\n35. What was Curly’s dress made of?\na) silk\nb) lace\nc) cotton\n36. What word talks about her hair?\na) curly\nb) brown\nc) straight\n37. What can Curly do?\na) talk\nb) sing\nc) walk\nActivity 10: SET A - TAKING CARE OF ANIMALS\n38. Where does Victor live?\na) in the city\nb) on a farm\nc) near the sea\n39. Which word tells about their house?\na) nipa\nb) cement\nc) wooden\n40. Who is Victor’s sister?\na) Nina\nb) Nora\nc) Nida\n41. Who is older, Victor or Nora?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Does not tell','teacher'),
(846,846,'42. How many kinds of animals do they have?\na) 3\nb) 4\nc) 5\n43. Which one do they NOT have?\na) cow\nb) horse\nc) carabao\n44. Who takes care of the horse?\na) Victor\nb) Father\nc) Mother\n45. Who takes care of the carabao?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Father\n46. Who takes care of the chickens?\na) Nora\nb) Victor\nc) Mother\n47. Which one does Nora take care of?\na) goat\nb) chickens\nc) carabao\nVocabulary Focus\n48. In \"The Story of the First Thanksgiving,\" what does the\nword harvest mean?\na) a big ship\nb) a large feast\nc) the time when crops are gathered\n49. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word nectar mean?\na) a sweet liquid in flowers that bees collect\nb) the stem of a plant\nc) the journey a seed takes\n50. In \"The Little Seed\'s Journey,\" what does the word sprouted mean?\na) to be blown by the wind\nb) to be watered by the rain\nc) to start to grow','teacher'),
(847,847,'SET B\nPOST-TEST (Based on Days 11-20)\nInstructions: Read each question carefully. Choose the best answer and write\nthe corresponding letter on your answer sheet.\n1. What did Celso eat?\na) bananas b) mangoes c) oranges\n2. When did he eat the fruit?\na) last night b) that morning c) last week\n3. Where did he throw the peelings?\na) into the basket b) out of the window c) into the garbage can\n4. Where was Celso going?\na) to church b) to market c) to school\n5. What sentence tells that Celso did not want to be late?\na) He walked fast b) He walked slowly c) He played on the way\n6. Who stepped on the banana peelings?\na) Father b) Mother c) Celso\n7. Who saw Celso fall?\na) Father b) Mother c) Sister\n8. Who did not use the garbage can?\na) Mother b) Celso c) Sister\n9. Was Celso hurt?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n10. Which word tells about Celso?\na) polite b) kind c) truthful\n11. Where does Alfredo live?\na) in Manila b) in Naga City c) on a farm\n12. What time does the train arrive?\na) 4 o’clock b) 5 o’clock c) 6 o’clock\n13. What carries the newspapers to Naga City?\na) a car b) a truck c) a train\n14. Where do the newspapers come from?\na) Manila b) Cebu City c) Pasay City\n15. What does Alfredo do?\na) sells fruit b) sells candies c) sells newspapers\n16. How long does Alfredo sell newspapers?\na) one hour b) two hours c) three hours\n17. How much does he earn per day?\na) 5 pesos b) 75 pesos c) 100 pesos\n18. What does he do with the money?\na) gives it to mother b) buys cakes and candies c) keeps it in his piggy bank\n19. What kind of a boy is Alfredo?\na) clean b) polite c) industrious','teacher'),
(848,848,'20. Are his parents poor?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n21. Who is Miss Luna?\na) nurse b) mother c) teacher\n22. What did she get one morning?\na) a letter b) a telegram c) a newspaper\n23. Who sent the letter?\na) Teresa b) Teresa’s mother c) Teresa’s father\n24. Why was Teresa absent?\na) She was sick b) She was busy c) She was away\n25. Did a doctor treat her?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n26. What did the children do?\na) visited her b) sent flowers c) sent her a letter\n27. What did the girls bring?\na) milk b) fruits c) flowers\n28. What did the boys bring?\na) fruits b) roses c) biscuits\n29. Who brought some roses?\na) girls b) boys c) Miss Luna\n30. When did they visit Teresa?\na) morning b) afternoon c) evening\n31. What time of the day was it?\na) morning b) noon c) afternoon\n32. What kind of afternoon was it?\na) rainy b) sunny c) cloudy\n33. Where was Juan going?\na) home b) school c) church\n34. What was Juan wearing?\na) hat b) sweater c) raincoat\n35. What did Juan see on the way?\na) dog b) kitten c) chick\n36. How did the kitten feel?\na) hot b) cold c) warm\n37. What did Juan feel for the kitten?\na) pity b) gladness c) happiness\n38. Where did he bring it?\na) home b) school c) in the shade\n39. Where did he put the kitten?\na) near the fire b) the table c) near the bed\n40. Did the kitten like to stay near the fire?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n41. What word tells about the coconut tree?\na) short b) tall c) small\n42. Does the coconut tree have branches?\na) Yes b) No c) Does not tell\n43. What part of the coconut tree is good for a post?','teacher'),
(849,849,'a) trunk b) roots c) fruits\n44. From where can we get oil?\na) coconut husk b) ripe coconut milk c) young coconut meat','teacher'),
(850,850,'45. Which is good to eat?\na) coconut husk b) coconut shell c) coconut meat\n46. What part is made into doormats?\na) shell b) husk c) midribs\n47. What can be made from the midribs?\na) buttons b) brooms c) candies\n48. What part is woven into baskets?\na) husk b) shell c) leaves\n49. Which part can be made into buttons?\na) husk b) shell c) midribs\n50. What is the use of the stalk of the leaves?\na) for fuel b) for post c) for food','teacher'),
(851,851,'Pre- Assessment (Activities 1–10)\nInstructions: Choose the best word from the word bank to complete each\nsentence. Write the word on the line.\nHuge\nfriend\ngift\nClean\ndesk\nlearn\ndead\nCountry\npie\nabove\n1. The elephant was ______\n, towering over the other animals.\n2. Please keep your room ______\nand tidy.\n3. We took a vacation to the ______\nand enjoyed the scenery.\n4. A true ______\nis always there for you.\n5. I do my homework at my ______\n.\n6. We ate a delicious apple ______\nfor dessert.\n7. She gave him a ______\nfor his birthday.\n8. I want to ______\nhow to play the guitar.\n9. The plant is ______\nand dry.\n10. The airplane flew ______\nthe clouds.\nListening Comprehension Assessment (10 Items)\nInstructions: I will read a short sentence or passage. Listen carefully, then\nanswer the questions based on what you heard. Choose the best answer\nand write the letter of your choice on the line.\n(Read Aloud): \"The small, gray cat sat on the mat.\"\n11. What color was the cat? ______','teacher'),
(852,852,'a) White\nb) Black\nc) Gray\n(Read Aloud): \"There are nine students in the class today.\n12. How many students are in the class? ______\na) Ten\nb) Nine\nc) Eight\n(Read Aloud): \"The field was full of yellow flowers.\"\n13. What color were the flowers? ______\na) Red\nb) Yellow\nc) Blue\n(Read Aloud): \"The river flows through the city.\"\n14. What does the river flow through? ______\na) The country b) The field\nc) The city\n(Read Aloud): \"The child helped his neighbor.\"\n15. Who did the child help? ______\na) His brother b) His friend\nc) His neighbor\n(Read Aloud): \"The knife is on the desk.\"\n16. Where is the knife? ______\na) on the table b) on the desk c) on the chair\n(Read Aloud): \"I would like a piece of pie.\"\n17. What does the speaker want? ______\na) a piece of plate b) a piece of cake c) a piece of pie ( )\n(Read Aloud): \"She felt sad when the bird flew away.\"\n18. How did she feel? ______\na) happy\nb) sad\nc) angry\n(Read Aloud): \"The sun rises in the east.\"\n19. Where does the sun rise? ______\na) west\nb) south\nc) east','teacher'),
(853,853,'(Read Aloud): \"The book is under the table.\"\n20. Where is the book? ______\na) above the table b) beside the table c) under the table.','teacher'),
(854,854,'Pre- Assessment (Activities 11–20)\nA. Vocabulary Development (10 items)\nDirections: Read and complete the sentences by filling in the\nblank with the correct word from the box.\nWord Bank:\nheavy\nside\n1. I have muscles all over my ______\n.\n2. The chicken’s body is covered with ______\n.\n3. The duck has a big ______\n.\n4. A baby has twinkling ______\n.\n5. My two feet have long ______\n.\n6. The book is on the left ______\nof the table.\n7. The ______\nis full of words.\n8. The bag feels ______\n.\n9. The room is ______\nnow.\n10.\nThe food is ______\nfor everyone.\nB. Context clues.\nDirections: Supply the missing letters to make a meaningful word\nto complete the sentence.','teacher'),
(855,855,'11. Mother cooked b _ _ ns, small seeds that we eat as food\nwith rice.\n12. I ate a ba_ an_ , a long yellow fruit that is sweet and soft\ninside.\n13. The tree has many le_ a_es, the green parts that grow on\nbranches and help the plant make food.\n14. We listened to the news on the r_ d_ o, a device that plays\nmusic and voices.\n15. The ring is made of g_ _ d, a shiny yellow metal that is very\nvaluable.\nn ______.\n16. A small insect that can crawl and bite is called an ______\n17. A young cat that plays and meows is called a k i _ _ e _.\n18. All people together, everyone included, are called co_ _ uni_ y.\n19. A type of large herbivore with antlers that lives on farms or\nin the forest is a d _ _ r.\n20.A tool that keeps you dry in the rain is an _ m b _ e _ _ a .\nII. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nA. Directions: Listen carefully as the teacher reads each\nsentence. Fill in the blank with the correct word you hear.\nThe cat is sleeping on my bed. She raised her hand to answer\nthe question. The sun rises in the east every morning. I ate a\npiece of cake for dessert. The dog wagged its tail happily.\n21. The cat is sleeping on my ______\n.\n22. She raised her ______\nto answer the question.\n23. The sun rises in the ______\n.\n24. I ate a piece of ______\nfor dessert.\n25. The dog wagged its ______\nhappily.','teacher'),
(856,856,'B. Direction: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her\ndog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park,\nLila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always\nbrings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the\nbirds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond\nQuestions:\n26. Who does Lila go to the park with? ______\n27. What color is Lila’s dog? ______\n28. Name two things Lila does at the park. ______\n29. What does Lila bring with her to the park? ______\n30. What animals does Lila watch at the park? ______\nC. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLast weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The\nplace was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card\nso our friends would know where we were. Around the camp\nwas a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance,\nwe could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky\nand saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our\ncountry.\n31. Where is the book placed?\nA. On the floor\nB. On the left side of the table\nC. Under the chair\nD. On the right side of the room','teacher'),
(857,857,'A. The bag\nB. The room\nC. The page\nD. The table\n33. How does the bag feel?\nA. Clean\nB. Gone\nC. Heavy\nD. Enough\n34. What is the room like now?\nA. Dirty\nB. Full\nC. Clean\nD. Heavy\n35. What must each student do carefully?\nA. Read\nB. Write\nC. Count\nD. Clean\nD. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.','teacher'),
(858,858,'The farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will\npress the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will\npay the workers. In March, the children will march in the\nparade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The\nteam will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the\nclothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very\nbusy. At night, the children dream of a better future.\n36. What will the farmer plant?\nA. Trees\nB. Flowers\nC. Seeds\nD. Fruits\n37. What does the farmer do to the soil?\nA. Waters it\nB. Presses it\nC. Removes it\nD. Dries it\n38. When do the children march in the parade?\nA. January\nB. February\nC. March\nD. April\n39. What should people NOT do to animals?\nA. Feed them\nB. Watch them\nC. Kill them','teacher'),
(859,859,'D. Care for them\n40. What do the children dream of at night?\nA. Playing games\nA. A better future\nB. Going to school\nC. Traveling far','teacher'),
(860,860,'Point Act Game\nActivity 1\nDirections: Pick a word card inside the box or bag. Read the\nword. Find the words inside the classroom. Read, point, act\nand write them on the board (e.g. half ½, 9, 11, etc.) Do it again\nand again.\nwhite','teacher'),
