(863,863,'Hidden Letters\nActivity 4\nDirections: Fill in the missing letter in the repetitive words in the activity\nsheet. Words to write can be seen below.\nn ______\ni g ______\nb\no ______\nr\nc ______\nl ______\n______ e n\n______ e\n______ h\nb ______\nu\nr\nc\nh ______\nl\nd ______ ______ ______\nn\ne ______\ng h ______\no\nu ______\n______ h\n______ d ______\ne ______\nn ______\ni g ______\nb\no ______\nr\n______ ______ ______ ______ r ______\nn\nn\ne ______\n______ h\nb ______\nu ______\nc\nh ______\nl\nd\nr ______ ______\nh ______\nm ______\ne\nl\nf\np\ne ______\np\nl ______\n______ m\ns ______\nl ______\np ______\no ______\nl\ne\nh\n______ s\ne ______\nf\n______ e\no\np ______\ne\n______ m ______\n______ l\nf\np ______\no\np ______ ______\nh ______\nm\ns\ne ______ ______\np\ne ______\n______ l\ne\nb ______\no ______\nh ______\nr\nf\na ______\n______ y\n______ r ______\nt ______\ne r\n______ a\nm ______\nl ______\nb ______\no ______\nh\ne ______\nf ______\nm ______\nl\ny\n______ r ______\nt ______\ne r\n______ a ______\n______ y\nb\nr\no ______\nh ______\nr\nf ______\nm\n______ y\nf ______\n______ n\nd\n______ o\nt ______\ne r\n______ r ______\ne ______\nd\nm ______\nt\nh ______ ______\nf ______\n______ n ______\n______ o ______\n______ e r\n______ r ______\ne\nn\nd\nm ______\nt\nh ______\nr\nf\nr\ne ______\nd\nm o ______\nh e ______\nM ______\ns ______\nq ______\ne ______\nn\nk\nn\ng\nM\n______ s\n______ u ______\ne\nn\nK ______\nn ______\n______ s\ns ______\n______ u\ne ______\nn\n______ g\nM ______\ns ______\nq ______\n______ e ______\n______ n ______\n______ ______ s\nq\nu\ne\ne ______\nk ______\n______ g\npeople\nfamily\nking\nMiss\nqueen\nhimself\nhrothar childran friand mathar','teacher'),
(864,864,'Jumbled Letters\nActivity 5\nDirections: Arrange the letters below to form a word. Refer\nyour answer on the word definition below. Write your answer in\nthe blank.\n1\npac\n______ 8\nbirck ______\n2\npuc ______\n9\noblw ______\n3\nopt\n______ 10\nfenik ______\n4\nkesd ______\n11\npila ______\n5\n12\nnep ______\ncesa ______\n6\n______ 13\nipe ______\npincle\n7\n______ palet ______ ______\n1. It covers the head\n- cap\n2. A small bowl-shaped container use for drinking - cup\n3. A round container used for cooking food - pot\n4. A flat furniture used for writing, reading and other work - desk\n5. A box or container for pen and pencils - case\n6. A long, thin object made of wood with black end used for writing\n- pencil\n7. A flat dish where food is served or eaten - plate\n8. A small rectangular block made of clay use for building - brick\n9. A round, deep dish or basin used for food or liquid - bowl\n10. A blade fixed into a handle, used for cutting or as a weapon - knife\n11. A bucket used for fetching water - pail\n12. An instrument for writing or drawing with ink - pen\n13. A baked dish of fruit, or meat and vegetables - pie','teacher'),
(865,865,'Link the Letters\nActivity 6\nDirections: For each question, a grid letter is presented. Locate the words\nwithin the grid and draw a line from square to square to link the letters of\nthe words. Use the definition of words as clues.\ne\na\nn\no\na\nb\ne\ne\nl\nb\na\ns\nm\ns\nu\na\ns\na\nn\ng\nn\na\ne\na\nf\nm\nd\ns\na\ne\nb\ns\ns\ne\nb\nn\na\nb\no\nl\ne\nfruit with soft and\nan edible seed flat green structure in\n______ ______ pulpy flesh ______ ______\ne\na\nl\np\nl\nn\no\na\ne\ne\ns\ns\nb\na\ns\ne\ns\np\na\ng\na\nn\nt\nn\na\ne\nd\ne\nl\nl\np\ns\ns\ne\ns\ne\ns\ne\na\ns\na\np\nliving things like trees,\npart of plants uses A seed to eat as\n______ ______ flowers ______ ______\no\ne\na\no\ng\nb\ne\ng\nn\nu\na\nr\nm\ns\nb\ns\nd\na\nn\nl\nd\na\nn\ng\no\ns\nd\ng\no\nt\nf\no\ne\nl\na\nd\ns\ne\nt\ntransistor\nA present A precious yellow\njewelry','teacher'),
