(870,870,'Antonym\nActivity 9\nDirections:\nGive the antonyms of the following words. Match column A with\ncolumn B. Write your answer in the blank.\nAnswer\nColumn A\nColumn B\nWord Bank\nAntonyms -Opposite\n______ Meaning\nplant ______\nrepudiate\npay ______\ndie\nkill\n______ neglect\nkick ______\nloosen\nborn ______\nhalt\ncare ______\nrise\ndream ______\nuproot\npress ______\naccept\nmarch ______\nstart\nlead ______\nidle\nhang ______\nmoist\ndry ______\ndislike\nbusy ______\nfollow','teacher'),
(871,871,'Prep Paired\nActivity 10\nDirections: Complete the sentences using words from the word\nbank that makes it correct. A letter/s were given.\nWord\nabove\nbegan\nalmost\nbeside\nbank\noutside\neast\nago\nacross\n______ between\ncenter\nfront\nunder\n1. There is a mirror _ b_ _ _ the sink.\n2. Airplanes flew a_ _ _ _ the sky above us.\n3. The event happened a long time _ _ o.\n4. It’s _ lm _ _ _ time to go to bed.\n5. The boy is running _ u _ s _ _ _ the house to play.\n6. She saw his mother in their f _____gate.\n7. The sun rises in the ____ t.\n8. He sits b_ _ w_ _ _ his friends.\n9. Mother put the table at the _ _ _ t _ _ of the\nroom.\n10.\nOur dog lies down u_ _ _ _ the bed.\n11.\nThe teacher put the trash bin b_ _ i_ _\nthe door.\n12. She _ _ga_ to like me.','teacher'),
(872,872,'Post-assessment (Activity 1-10)\nA. Vocabulary Development (1–10)\nInstructions: Choose the best word from the word bank to complete each\nsentence. Write the word on the line.\nHuge\nfriend\ngift\ndead\nClean\ndesk\nlearn\nCountry\npie\nabove\n2\n1. We took a vacation to the ______\nand enjoyed the scenery.\n2. I do my homework at my ______\n.\n3. She gave him a ______\nfor his birthday.\n4. The elephant was ______\n, towering over the other animals.\n5. We ate a delicious apple ______\nfor dessert.\n6. A true ______\nis always there for you.\n7. The plant is ______\nand dry.\n8. The airplane flew ______\nthe clouds.\n9. Please keep your room ______\nand tidy.\n10. I want to ______\nhow to play the guitar.','teacher'),
(873,873,'B. Listening Comprehension (11–20)\nInstructions: Listen carefully as the teacher reads each sentence or\npassage. Choose the best answer and write the letter on the line.\n(Read Aloud): “The field was full of yellow flowers.”\n11. What color were the flowers? ______\na) Red\nb) Yellow c) Blue\n(Read Aloud): “The sun rises in the east.”\n12. Where does the sun rise? ______\na) west b) south\nc) east\n(Read Aloud): “The child helped his neighbor.”\n13. Who did the child help? ______\na) His brother\nb) His friend\nc) His neighbor\n(Read Aloud): “I would like a piece of pie.”\n14. What does the speaker want? ______\na) a piece of plate b) a piece of cake\nc) a piece of pie\n(Read Aloud): “There are nine students in the class today.”\n15. How many students are in the class? ______\na) Ten b) Nine\nc) Eight\n(Read Aloud): “The knife is on the desk.”\n16. Where is the knife? ______\na) on the table b) on the desk c) on the chair\n(Read Aloud): “The book is under the table.”\n17. Where is the book? ______\na) above the table b) beside the table c) under the table\n(Read Aloud): “The river flows through the city.”\n18. What does the river flow through? ______\na) The country\nb) The field c) The city\n(Read Aloud): “The small, gray cat sat on the mat.”\n19. What color was the cat? ______\na) White b) Black c) Gray\n(Read Aloud): “She felt sad when the bird flew away.”','teacher'),
(874,874,'Fill in the blank\nActivity 11\nDirections: Read and complete the sentences below by\nchoosing the correct words found inside the box.\nAnswer the worksheet activity by filling the blank.\nbody\neye\nbone\nfeather\nbill\nchin\nfoot\nhair\nLap\nmeat\nmouth\nFinger\nskin\n1. I have muscles all over my ______\n.\n2. The duck has a big ______\n.\n3. The chicken’s body is covered with ______\n.\n4. I have ten ______\nin my hands.\n5. The color of my ______\nis black.\n6. The ______\ncovering of frog is smooth.\n7. Mother cuddle the baby in her ______\n.\n8. A baby has twinkling ______\n.\n9. My two feet have long ______\n.\n10.\nA limping dog walk with one ______\nup.\n11.\nMy ______\nhas teeth and tongue inside.\n12.\nThe cow’s ______\nis so expensive.\n13.\nBabalu has a long ______\n.','teacher'),
