(883,883,'Sentence Completion\nActivity 20\nDirections:\n1. Select the correct word to complete each sentence.\n2. Choose the words in the box below.\n3. Write the correct answer in the blank.\nfavorite\nbeautiful\nnotice\nsince\nnecessary\npleasure\nthought\nbetter\nsuppose\nwritten\nperhaps\ngeneral\n1. My ______\nfruit is mango.\n2. Teachers ______\nto the parents about the meeting.\n3. It is ______\nto take care of ourselves.\n4. Watching a game gave me a great ______\n.\n5. He has two works ______\nhe graduated.\n6. You’d ______\nback off.\n7. The book provide ______\ninformation of the subject.\n8. Farmers ______\nnot interested in the new Farming.\n9. My name is ______\non the blackboard.\n10. I ______\nthat they are not ready for the class.\n11. Do you have any ______\nfor the lesson?\n12. She has the most ______\nsmile.','teacher'),
(884,884,'Post-Assessment (Activities (1–20)\nDirections: Read each question carefully. Choose or write the correct answer.\nA. Vocabulary Development (5 items)\nDirections: Read and complete the sentences by filling in the\nblank with the correct word from the box.\nWord Bank:\nheavy\nside\n1. The food is ______\nfor everyone.\n2. A baby has twinkling ______\n.\n3. The bag feels ______\n.\n4. The duck has a big ______\n.\n5. The book is on the left ______\nof the table.\n6. I have muscles all over my ______\n.\n7. The room is ______\nnow.\n8. My two feet have long ______\n.\n9. The ______\nis full of words.\n10. The chicken’s body is covered with ______\n.\nD. Context clues.\nDirections: Supply the missing letters to make a meaningful word\nto complete the sentence.','teacher'),
(885,885,'11. A young cat that plays and meows is called a k i _ _ e\n_.\n12. The ring is made of g_ _ d, a shiny yellow metal.\n13. A tool that keeps you dry in the rain is an _ m b _ e _ _\na.\n14. Mother cooked b _ _ ns, small seeds eaten with rice.\n15. A type of large herbivore with antlers is a d _ _ r.\n16. We listened to the news on the r_ d_ o.\n17. All people together are called co_ _ uni_ y.\n18. A small insect that can crawl and bite is an _ n _.\n19. I ate a ba_ an_, a long yellow fruit.\n20. The tree has many le_ a_es.\nII. Listening Comprehension (5 items)\nA. Directions: Listen carefully as the teacher reads each\nsentence. Fill in the blank with the correct word you hear.\nThe cat is sleeping on my bed. She raised her hand to answer\nthe question. The sun rises in the east every morning. I ate a\npiece of cake for dessert. The dog wagged its tail happily.\n21. The dog wagged its ______\nhappily.\n22. The sun rises in the ______\n.\n23. The cat is sleeping on my ______\n.\n24. I ate a piece of ______\nfor dessert.\n25. She raised her ______\nto answer the question.','teacher'),
(886,886,'B. Direction : Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLila loves going to the park. Every morning, she walks with her\ndog, Max. Max is a small brown dog with a fluffy tail. At the park,\nLila swings on the swings and plays on the slide. She always\nbrings a small snack and a bottle of water. Lila likes to watch the\nbirds in the trees and feed the ducks near the pond\nQuestions:\n26. What animals does Lila watch at the park? ______\n27. Who goes with Lila to the park? ______\n28. What does Lila bring with her? ______\n29. What color is Lila’s dog? ______\n30. Name two things Lila does at the park. ______\nE. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nLast weekend, our family went to a camp near the river. The\nplace was quiet and peaceful. We wrote our address on a card\nso our friends would know where we were. Around the camp\nwas a wide field with soft sand near the pond. In the distance,\nwe could see the blue sea. At night, we looked up at the sky\nand saw many stars. It was a beautiful land in a small city in our\ncountry.\n31. How does the bag feel?\nA. Gone\nB. Heavy\nC. Clean\nD. Enough\n32. What must each student do carefully?\nA. Write\nB. Read','teacher'),
(887,887,'C. Count\nD. Clean\n33. What is full of words?\nA. The page\nB. The bag\nC. The table\nD. The room\n34. Where is the book placed?\nA. Under the chair\nB. On the floor\nC. On the left side of the table\nD. On the right side of the room\n35. What is the room like now?\nA. Heavy\nB. Dirty\nC. Clean\nD. Full\nF. Directions: Listen carefully to the sentences. Choose the\ncorrect answer to each question. Encircle the letter of your\nanswer on your paper.\nThe farmer will plant seeds and care for them every day. He will\npress the soil so the seeds stay in place. At harvest time, he will\npay the workers. In March, the children will march in the\nparade. No one should kill animals because life is important. The\nteam will lead the program and kick the ball. They will hang the\nclothes to dry. The baby was born, and the parents were very\nbusy. At night, the children dream of a better future.\n36. What do the children dream of at night?\nA. Playing games\nB. Traveling far\nC. A better future\nD. Going to school\n37. When do the children march in the parade?\nA. April\nB. January','teacher'),
(888,888,'C. February\nD. March\n38. What will the farmer plant?\nA. Fruits\nB. Seeds\nC. Trees\nD. Flowers\n39. What should people NOT do to animals?\nA. Feed them\nB. Kill them\nC. Care for them\nD. Watch them\nWhat does the farmer do to the soil?\nA. Dries it\nB. Removes it\nC. Presses it\nD. Waters it','teacher'),
(889,889,'Pre- Test Assessment (Activity 1-10)\nI. Vocabulary Development: Synonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the same meaning as the\nunderlined word.\n1. A tragic accident happened on the road.\na. twin\nb. crash\nc. reply\nd. risk\n2. The view of the mountain is so beautiful.\na. low\nb. wash\nc. pretty\nd. dirt\n3. Please answer the question honestly.\na. select\nb. go\nc. reply\nd. mind\n4. I need to bathe the baby before dinner.\na. cover\nb. fix\nc. wash\nd. glue\n5. The chief decided to end the meeting early.\na. audience\nb. disagree\nc. leader\nd. day\n6. Did you choose the right materials for the project?\na. end\nb. start\nc. select\nd. time\n7. He received a double amount of reward.\na. earth\nb. low\nc. twin\nd. supper\n8. They went against the mayor\'s decision.\na. time\nb. disagree\nc. alone\nd. eating\n9. She will go to the market this afternoon.\na. begin\nb. move\nc. finish\nd. round\n10. Look at the big blue ocean.\na. time\nb. sea\nc. soil\nd. date','teacher'),
(890,890,'II. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning of\nthe underlined word.\n11. She began to cry after failing the test.\na. remember\nb. believe\nc. laugh\nd. worry\n12. We should act quickly to help the victim.\na. lie\nb. do nothing\nc. catch\nd. free\n13. Don\'t be careless when handling glass.\na. tomorrow\nb. careful\nc. south\nd. outdoors\n14. His camera produces blurry pictures.\na. end\nb. clear\nc. glad\nd. morning\n15. The sun rises in the evening.\na. start\nb. morning\nc. often\nd. lad\n16. She felt sad when her favorite toy broke.\na. truth\nb. glad\nc. strong\nd. ache\n17. He told a lie to avoid getting into trouble.\na. rejoice\nb. truth\nc. doubt\nd. worry\n18. He stays indoors all day when it rains.\na. outdoors\nb. lady\nc. sir\nd. yesterday\n19. The winter clothes are very thick.\na. weak\nb. thin\nc. healthy\nd. beautiful\n20. She visits her grandmother often.\na. tomorrow\nb. sometimes\nc. mountain\nd. men','teacher'),
(891,891,'III. Vocabulary Development: Noun or Verb (5 items)\nDirections: Read the word and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V).\n21. Spoke:\na. N\nb. V\n22. Thumb:\na. N\nb. V\n23. Heart:\na. N\nb. V\n24. Follow:\na. N\nb. V\n25. Shadow:\na. N\nb. V\nIV. Listening Comprehension & Vocabulary: Homophones (10 items)\nDirections: Read the sentence and choose the correct word in the\nparenthesis that completes the meaning.\n26. She has a slim (waist / waste).\na. waste\nb. waist\n27. His hard work was put into (waist / waste).\na. waste\nb. waist\n28. Father (war / wore) a nice long sleeve.\na. war\nb. wore\n29. Our houses (coast / cost) five million.\na. coast\nb. cost\n30. I live near the (coast / cost).\na. coast\nb. cost\n31. He who lives with hope will (die / dye) by hunger.\na. die\nb. dye\n32. Christopher Columbus set (sail / sale) for around the World in 1492.\na. sail\nb. sale\n33. Please, (wait / weight) just a moment!\na. wait\nb. weight','teacher'),
(892,892,'34. He spent the (hole / whole) day reading in bed.\na. hole\nb. whole\n35. This (rode / road) is too narrow for cars.\na. rode\nb. road\nV. Listening Comprehension: Context Clues (5 items)\nDirections: Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen carefully and\nwrite the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the line.\n36.(Teacher reads: \"A companion or colleague.\")\n37.(Teacher reads: \"A person who treats teeth and gums.\")\n38.(Teacher reads: \"Trousers or slacks.\")\n39.(Teacher reads: \"A vessel or a craft.\")\n40.(Teacher reads: \"The cause or explanation for something.\")','teacher'),
(893,893,'The Same Meanings\nActivity 1- Synonym\nDirections: Select the correct synonym of the given word from the\nbox below\nand write your answer on the blank\nprovided.\nglue\ncover\nincorrect\nbrain\nfix\npostman\ndown\nworld\ntwin\nsupper\nwash\nreply\npretty\ncrash\nlittle\n1. ______\naccident\n9. ______\nmailman\n2. ______\nbeautiful\n10. ______\nmend\n3. ______\nanswer\n11. ______\nmind\n4. ______\nbathe\n12. ______\nwrong\n5. ______\ndinner\n13. ______\nwrap\n6. ______\ndouble\n14. ______\npaste\n7. ______\nEarth\n15. ______\nshort\n8. ______\nlow','teacher'),
(894,894,'The Same Meanings\nActivity 2- Synonym\nDirections: Select the correct synonym of the given word from the\nbox below\nand write your answer on the blank\nprovided.\ntime\nstart\nleader\naudience\neating\nsea\nalone\nselect\nrisk\ndirt\ngo\ndisagree\nround\nday\nend\n9. ______\ncircle\n1. ______\nmove\n10. ______\ncrowd\n2. ______\nocean\n11. ______\ndanger\n3. ______\nseason\n12. ______\n4. ______\nagainst\n13. ______\ndining\n5. ______\nsolo\n14. ______\nsoil\n6. ______\nbegin\n15. ______\nfinish\n7. ______\nchief\n8. ______\nchoose','teacher'),
(895,895,'The Opposite Meanings\nActivity 3- Antonym\nDirections: Select the correct antonym of the given word from the\nbox below\nand write your answer on the blank\nprovided.\nsometimes\ntruth\nlad\noutdoors\nsad\nsouth\ndo nothing\ndoubt\ncareful\nfree\nblurry\nlaugh\nstart\nmorning\nremember\n1. ______\nact\n9. ______\nforget\n2. ______\nbelieve\n10. ______\nglad\n3. ______\ncareless\n11. ______\nindoors\n4. ______\ncatch\n12. ______\nlady\n5. ______\nclear\n13. ______\nlie\n6. ______\ncry\n14. ______\nnorth\n7. ______\nend\n15. ______\noften\n8. ______\nevening','teacher'),
(896,896,'The Opposite Meanings\nActivity 4- Antonym\nDirections: Select the correct antonym of the given word from the\nbox below and write your answer on the blank provided.\nweak\nmountain\ncalm\nrejoice\nmen\nbeautiful\nyesterday\nthin\nwinter\nhealthy\nma’am\nfork\ngather\nplenty\nhen\n9. ______\ntomorrow\n1. ______\nrooster\n10. ______\nugly\n2. ______\nseveral\n11. ______\nwoman\n3. ______\nspread\n12. ______\nache\n4. ______\nspoon\n13. ______\nworry\n5. ______\nsir\n14. ______\nvalley\n6. ______\nsick\n15. ______\ntough\n7. ______\nsummer\n8. ______\nthick','teacher'),
(897,897,'Read and Classify\nActivity 5 - Classify as Noun or Verb\nDirections: Identify the following words in the box below as noun or\nverb and\nwrite your answer on the proper column.\ntouch\nspoke\nsold\nfell\ntongue\nporch\ntoe\narm\nchalk\nfurniture\nheart\nscooter\nshirt\nshadow\nknee\nVerb\nNoun','teacher'),
(898,898,'Read and Classify\nActivity 6 - Classify as Noun or Verb\nDirection: Identify the following words in the box below as noun or\nverb and write your answer on the proper column.\nthroat\nthumb\nhot iron\nfill in\nchain\nchange\ncompany\ncoughing\ngrain\ngarage\nfollow\nguess\nlaid\nblind\nFacebook posts\nVerb\nNoun','teacher'),
(899,899,'Guess the Word\nActivity 7- Fill in the Missing Letters\nDirections: Read each item and supply the missing letters to form\nthe correct word. Select the words from the box below.\ndentist\nblood chance expect\nfellow\neither\ncaptain except\nb _ _ _ d\n1. red liquid that circulates in the arteries\nc a p _ _ _ _\n2. the person in command of a ship\nc _ _ n c e\n3. a possibility of something happening\nf e _ l _ w\n4. a companion or colleague\nf _ _ d\n5. to give food\ne x p _ _ t\n6. likely to happen\np _ _ _ d\n7. a unit of weight\ne x c _ _ t\n8. not including, other than\ne i _ _ _ r\n9. referring to a choice of two options\nd e _ _ _ s t\n10. a person who treats teeth and gums','teacher'),
(900,900,'Guess the Word\nActivity 8- Fill in the Missing Letters\nDirections: Read each item and supply the missing letters to form\nthe correct word.\nrather\nship\nreason\npoint\neverything\nnor\noveralls\nshape\nseveral\npants\nn _ r\n1. to indicate that each did not happen\no v _ _ _ l\nl s\n2. all in all or all together\np _ _ t s\n3. trousers or slacks\ns _ v e _ _ l\n4. not very many\np _ _ n t\n5. a dot\ne _ _ _ y t h _ n g\n6. all the things\ns h _ p\n7. formation of figure\np\nd\nr a _ _ _ r\n8. to indicate one’s preference in a particular matter\ns _ _ p\n9. a vessel or a craft\nr e a _ _ n\n10. cause or explanation','teacher'),
(901,901,'Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings\nActivity 9- Homophone\nDirection: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis.\n1. She has a slim (waist, waste).\n2. His hard work was put into (waist, waste).\n3. Thank God, the (war, wore) has ended.\n4. Father (war, wore) a nice long sleeve.\n5. Ana has a slender (body, buddy).\n6. My friend is my (body, buddy).\n7. Our houses (coast, cost) five million.\n8. I live near the (coast, cost).\n9. I like to (die, dye) my hair\n10. He who lives with hope will (die, dye) by hunger.\n11. I am happy (each, itch) time you are here.\n12. The (itch, each) will not go away.\n13. This money is your back and (forth, fourth) fare.\n14. He ranks (forth, fourth) in his class.\n15. I love crushed (ice, eyes) with milk and sugar.','teacher'),
(902,902,'Same Pronunciation but Different Meanings\nActivity 10 - Homophone\nDirection: Encircle the correct homophone inside the parenthesis.\n1. Christopher Columbus set (sail, sale) for around the World in\n1492.\n2. Please, (wait, weight) just a moment!\n3. He spent the (hole, whole) day reading in bed.\n4. This (rode, road) is too narrow for cars.\n5. One (cent, sent) is still has a value.\n6. (Our, hour) library has many books.\n7. How much is the taxi (fare, fair) to the hotel?\n8. I’ve (heard, herd) the French version of this song.\n9. She put her piano up for (sale, sail)\n10. Let us meet at the park in one (our, hour).\n11. She got on her bike and (road, rode) away.\n12. The cowboys rounded up the (heard, herd) of cattle.\n13. There is a big (hole, whole) on the road.\n14. He (sent, cent) his car to the shop.\n15. His (weight, wait) is twice his older brother.','teacher'),
(903,903,'Matching Meanings\nActivity 11- Match to Complete the Sentence\nDirection: In column A are the phrases. In column B are the words.\nMatch\ncolumn A with column B by drawing a line.\nColumn A\nColumn B\n1. I worship and pray in the ______\n.\na. eleven\n2. You are hurt and you feel the ______\n.\nb. peach\n3. The ______\nassists the doctor.\nc. root\n4. When you study in a dark room, you use ______\n.\nd. church\n5. When I sleep, I love to hug my big ______\n.\ne. pain\n6. Mother uses a colorful floor covering called ______\n.\nf. lamp\n7. Use ______\nin measuring the length of your pen.\ng. rug\n8. A ______\nand arrow can be used for hunting.\nh. silk\n9. Sweet potato is an example of a ______\ncrop.\ni. drawer\n10. In the garden, you can see some ______\n.\nj. butterflies\n11. My favorite color is ______\n.\nk. lie\n12. Don’t ______\n, tell the truth.\nl. ruler\n13. A ______\nis produced by silkworms.\nm. pillow\n14. Get my jewelry in the ______\n.\nn. nurse\n15. ______\nis the number after ten.\no. bow','teacher'),
(904,904,'Matching Meanings\nActivity 12- Match to Complete the Sentence\nDirection: In column A are the phrases. In column B are the words.\nMatch column A with column B by drawing a line.\nA\nB\n1. Save your money and deposit it in your ______\n.\na. market\n2. Every ______\nI take a nap.\nb. ought\n3. I ______\nhave my vitamins.\nc. cousin\n4. I ran five kilometres, and now I am ______\n.\nd. tub\n5. Give me one ______\npesos to buy a cake.\ne. thirsty\n6. ______\nis the number after nineteen.\nf. already\n7. Please get water from the ______\n.\ng. note\n8. You ______\nto try it sometimes.\nh. afternoon\n9. A ______\nis a silvery white metal.\ni. tomatoes\n10. Kindly take ______\nof the important events.\nj. thousand\n11. He used a knife ______\nof chopsticks.\nk. nickel\n12. My ______\nAna is the only relative I have.\nl. twenty\n13. Let us climb the ______\nto have an adventure.\nm. instead\n14. Maria goes to the ______\nto buy fruits.\nn. mountain\n15. ______\nare glossy red edible fruit.\no. bank','teacher'),
(905,905,'Giving Hints\nActivity 13- Context Clue\nDirection: Read the context clues to identify the correct meaning\nof the underlined word below.\n1. An automobile is a road vehicle, typically with four wheels,\npowered by an engine and able to carry a small number of\npeople.\na. bicycle\nb. car\nc. carriage\nd. truck\n2. A strip of material used to bind a wound or to protect an injured\npart of the body is called a bandage.\na. cloth\nb. plaster\nc. ribbon\nd. string\n3. The wound is bleeding, losing more blood and it’s scary.\na.\nclosing\nb. fine\nc. healing\nd. hemorrhaging\n4. I like to write on the blackboard because I have plenty of\nchalk, it’s mounted on the wall and it’s smooth.\na. bond paper b. cardboard\nc. chalkboard\nd. colored paper\n5. Our classroom is dusty, please bring me a broom, that is long,\nhandle for sweeping.\na. brush\nb. rag\nc. scrub\nd. sweeper\n6. The stomach is an internal organ where digestion of food occurs\na. abdomen\nb. brain\nc. heart\nd. lung\n7. Sandro speaks wisely as he expresses his ideas to the public with\npride.\na. dream\nb. rejoice\nc. shout\nd. talk','teacher'),
(906,906,'8. I love to drink lemonade because it quenches my thirst.\na. coffee\nb. lemon juice\nc. milk\nd. water\n9. Kindly use a ruler to measure his height.\na. calculate\nb. guess c. see d. write\n10. Please erase the writings to remove the prints on the wall.\na. wipe off\nb. write\nc. litter\nd. loiter','teacher'),
(907,907,'Giving Hints\nActivity 14- Context Clues\nDirection: Read the context clues to identify the correct meaning\nof the underlined word below.\n1. Mr. Berto is a butcher, he sells meat in his shop.\na. carpenter\nb. meat seller c. plumber\nd. teacher\n2. Can you reach that bag for me?, I need to get my snacks.\na. grab\nb. see\nc. sit\nd. stand\n3. I am tired, I need to rest and eat my lunch.\na. play\nb. relax\nc. smile\nd. watch\n4. What was the reason why she did not pass his module?\na. cause\nb. perception\nc. relevance\nd. statement\n5. Have you got any other dresses?\na. alternative b. okay\nc. same\nd. similar\n6. She is an intelligent lady with a heart.\na. doctor\nb. professor\nc. teacher\nd. woman\n7. A square has four sides.\na. hexagon\nb. parallelogram c. pentagon\nd. quadrilateral\n8. A light bump can still cause swelling on the skin.\na. box\nb. fight\nc. impact\nd. jump\n9. The bread is burnt and cannot be eaten.\na. delicious\nb. mouth-watering\nc. overcooked\nd. yummy','teacher'),
(908,908,'10. Listening to the music inspires me to do better in class.\na. poem\nb. speech\nc. story\nd. tune','teacher'),
(909,909,'Going Across and Down is Fun\nActivity 15- Crossword Puzzle\nDirection: Read each item and answer the crossword puzzle.\nACROSS:\n1. a cereal plant to\nmake flour, pasta and\n1)\n11)\npastry\n2. painful or aching\n12)\n3. shed tears because ______ ______\n3)\nof pain or sorrow\n4. a piece of cloth or\npaper\n5. a heavenly body\nappears to be\n2)\ntwinkling\n13)\n6. the planet on which\n4)\n14)\nwe live\n7. to relax\n8. to lay out or stretch\nout\n5)\n9. past participle of\nbegin\n7)\nDOWN:\n10. conflict or fighting ______ ______\n6)\n11. the number after\nten\n12. a large body of\n10)\nwater ______ ______\n13. the upper joint of\n8)\nthe human arm ______ ______ ______ ______\n15)\n14. a puree or mush\n15. to move or jump ______ ______ ______ ______\nsuddenly upward\n9)','teacher'),
(910,910,'Going Across and Down is Fun\nActivity 16- Crossword Puzzle\nDirection: Read each item and answer the crossword puzzle.\n8)\nACROSS:\n1. having no one else\n1)\npresent; solo\n2. expressing a doubt ______\nor choice between\n9)\nalternatives\n3. for preference ______ ______ ______\n2)\n13)\n4. a young human;\nlittle boy or little girl ______ ______ ______ ______\n5. a reply or response\n6. colored or shining\nlike gold\n3)\n7. a plane figure with\nfour equal straight ______ ______ ______\nsides\n10)\nDOWN: ______\n8. to wash or shower\n9. attractive or pretty ______ ______\n10. a tune or song\n11. a time of day\nspecified as an exact ______ ______\n14)\nnumber\n12. hazard or risk ______ ______ ______ ______\n13. the most common\n4)\n11)\n12)\nflower given on\nValentine’s Day\n5)\n14. used for\ntransportation ______\n15. medicine, remedy\nor cure\n6)\n15)\n7)','teacher'),
(911,911,'Developing Understanding Through Paragraphs\nActivity 17 – Short Passage\nDirection: Supply the missing word to complete the sentence in\nthe paragraph. Choose your answers from the box below.\nMother goes to the ______\nto prepare for their ______\nparty\n______ daughter will receive an award in her graduation ______\n.\nShe passes through a ______\nin going to the market. She buys the\ningredients for the gathering like ______\n, ______\n, ______\n, ______\nand ______\ncake. Then, she goes to the grocery store to buy\n______ spoons and forks. She wants to surprise her ______ and so,\nshe buys a blouse, a small ______ floral ______ and a ______\nwhich\nshe almost ______\n. In going home, she stops at a ______ store to buy\nmedicine.\nlettuce\npotatoes\nsize\nskirt\nstocking\ntomorrow\nwhose\ngolden\nforgot\ndrug\nchild\nchocolate\nbridge\nthanksgiving\nforks','teacher'),
(912,912,'Developing Understanding Through Paragraphs\nActivity 18 – Short Passage\nDirection: Supply the missing word to complete the sentence in\nthe paragraph. Choose your answers from the box below.\nBen wants to ______ his father. He likes to be a ______ and ______ his community.\nHe never gets ______ of studying. Every ______, he buys books about\nmedicine. His father ______ him so that Ben will be top in his class.\nHe receives award every ______\nbecause he has good\n______. And so, his father gives him a shirt with a soft ______\nand a\n______ jacket because he does ______ in his studies. Ben never stops\n______ he achieve his dream to ______ and become like his dad ______ he\nadmire so much.\ncopy\ncloth\nclass\ndoctor\nquarter\nserve\ntrains\nwhom\ntired\nmonth\nleather\nfinish\ngrades\nuntil\ngreat','teacher'),
(913,913,'Search for Meanings\nActivity 19 – Word Puzzle\nDirections: Complete each sentence by choosing the correct\nanswer from the box.\n1. It is used as a sweetener in food or drink.\n2. What is another word for shred?\n3. It is used to protect us from the rain or heat from the sun.\n4. What do we do when someone is in the hospital?\n5. What do we close when we wear our jeans?\n6. It’s faster when we cook in a ______\n?\n7. It’s proper to use ______\nwhen eating than with your bare\nhands.\n8. He is a serviceman who is willing to die for our country.\n9. We use it in when we cut papers.\n10. It is a kind of snack with spread as a filling.\n11. When we cook viand, we put ______\nto taste better.\n12. It is usually where slippers come from.\n13. We give a bunch of ______\non Valentine’s Day.\n14. Lend her your ______\nto wipe her tears.\n15. It is the time when it is midday.\nsugar\ntear\numbrella\nvisit\nzipper\nstove\nspoon\nsoldier\nscissors\nsandwich\nsalt\nrubber\nrose\nhandkerchief\nnoon ______ ______','teacher'),
(914,914,'Directions: Find and encircle the word in the puzzle.\nS U G A R R T Y U U I S H\nP T Y U O T E A R M R A A\nO S C I S S O R S B T N N\nO R T Y E U I O A R H D D\nN Q A S D F G H L E J W K\nS O L D I E R J T L K I E\nR U B B E R E R T L L C R\nG H J K L O I U Y A M H C\nZ X C V B N V I S I T G H\nZ I P P E R Q W T H W F I\nR T Y U I O S T O V E D E\nN O O N Q W E R T J A S F\nsugar tear\numbrella\nvisit zipper\nstove\nspoon\nsoldier\nscissors\nsandwich\nsalt\nrubber\nrose\nhandkerchief\nnoon','teacher'),
(915,915,'Search for Meanings\nActivity 20 – Word Puzzle\nDirections: Complete each sentence by choosing the correct\nanswer from the box.\n1. Wipe your mouth with a table ______\n.\n2. We see our reflection in the ______\n.\n3. Take your ______\nso that you will be well.\n4. Mother kissed the baby on the ______\n.\n5. A ______\nin English is interesting.\n6. Serve me a ______\n, I am thirsty.\n7. Please come to my ______\nfor further instruction.\n8. I need to go to the ______\nstore to buy milk.\n9. Give me the ______\n, we will fix our house.\n10. Open the ______\n, the car will pass through.\n11. A silky ______\nlightens up the room.\n12. The ______\nis fastened upon the wall.\n13. She fights for the Miss Universe ______\n.\n14. Use the ______\nto color your drawings.\n15. ______\nis the main ingredient of chocolates.\nnapkin\nmirror\nmedicine\nlips\nlesson\njuice\noffice\ngrocery\nhammer\ngate\ncurtain\ncupboard\ncrown\ncrayons\ncocoa','teacher'),
(916,916,'Directions: Find and encircle the word in the puzzle.\nM E D I C I N E L I P S L\nI J O F F I C E G A T E E\nR U Q W E R T Y R U I O S\nR I A S D F G H O J K L S\nO C Z X C V B N C M H Y O\nR E Q A W S F T E C Y U N\nH A M M E R G H R O W F H\nC U R T A I N B Y C H J K\nA E F G H T Y N Y O D F G\nC U P B O A R D R A F R Y\nN A P K I N E D G J K L T\nC R O W N C R A Y O N S D\nnapkin\nmirror\nmedicine\nlips\nlesson\njuice\noffice\ngrocery\nhammer\ngate\ncurtain\ncupboard\ncrown\ncrayons\ncocoa','teacher'),
(917,917,'Post-Test Assessment: (1-10)\nVocabulary and Listening Comprehension (Items 1–40)\nI. Vocabulary Development: Antonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the opposite meaning as\nthe underlined word.\n1. She felt glad when she won the medal.\na. strong\nb. sad\nc. truth\nd. ache\n2. The old photograph is very clear.\na. blurry\nb. light\nc. happy\nd. long\n3. He decided to lie about the broken vase.\na. truth\nb. doubt\nc. rejoice\nd. worry\n4. I will end my presentation with a summary.\na. often\nb. start\nc. tomorrow\nd. sir\n5. You must remember to lock the door.\na. forget\nb. lad\nc. act\nd. weak\n6. The children began to laugh at the funny story.\na. cry\nb. believe\nc. catch\nd. free\n7. He is too weak to lift the box.\na. strong\nb. thin\nc. ugly\nd. bad\n8. They went outdoors to play basketball.\na. north\nb. lady\nc. indoors\nd. sometimes\n9. She is very careful with her school supplies.\na. tomorrow\nb. careless\nc. south\nd. morning\n10. The blanket is too thin for this cold weather.\na. healthy\nb. thick\nc. beautiful\nd. pretty','teacher'),
(918,918,'II. Vocabulary Development: Synonyms (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that has the same meaning as the\nunderlined word.\n1. She is planning to select a new puppy.\na. deny\nb. reply\nc. choose\nd. mind\n2. The two brothers are twin sons.\na. cover\nb. fix\nc. double\nd. risk\n3. Did you reply to her email?\na. select\nb. go\nc. answer\nd. wash\n4. We must obey the chief\'s orders.\na. audience\nb. disagree\nc. leader\nd. day\n5. I need to go to the hospital for a check-up.\na. begin\nb. move\nc. finish\nd. end\n6. Please wash your hands before eating.\na. cover\nb. bathe\nc. fix\nd. glue\n7. The sea is rough today.\na. time\nb. ocean\nc. soil\nd. date\n8. He was against the idea of closing the park.\na. time\nb. disagree\nc. alone\nd. eating\n9. That was a terrible crash involving three cars.\na. answer\nb. bathe\nc. accident\nd. double\n10. What a pretty bouquet of flowers!\na. dirty\nb. noisy\nc. beautiful\nd. short','teacher'),
(919,919,'III. Vocabulary Development: Homophones (10 items)\nDirections: Choose the correct word inside the parenthesis that fits the\nsentence.\n1. My doctor told me to watch my (wait / weight).\na. wait\nb. weight\n2. What is the total (coast / cost) of the groceries?\na. coast\nb. cost\n3. You can use this color to (die / dye) your shirt.\na. die\nb. dye\n4. She used a needle to mend the (hole / whole) in her sock.\na. hole\nb. whole\n5. We need to hire a boat to (sail / sale) across the lake.\na. sail\nb. sale\n6. I hope we don\'t have another world (war / wore).\na. war\nb. wore\n7. This old furniture is just going to (waist / waste).\na. waist\nb. waste\n8. The (fair / fare) was much higher than expected.\na. fare\nb. fair\n9. The whole family (road / rode) the carousel.\na. road\nb. rode\n10. We went to the summer (fare / fair) yesterday.\na. fare\nb. fair\nIV. Listening Comprehension & Vocabulary: Noun, Verb, and Context Clues\n(10 items)\nDirections: Listen to the word or clue read by your teacher and follow the\ninstructions for each item.','teacher'),
(920,920,'Part A: Noun (N) or Verb (V) Your teacher will read a word aloud. Listen\ncarefully and identify if it is a Noun (N) or a Verb (V).\n1. (Teacher reads: \"chalk\")\na. N\nb. V\n2. (Teacher reads: \"fell\")\na. N\nb. V\n3. (Teacher reads: \"guess\")\na. N\nb. V\n4. (Teacher reads: \"porch\")\na. N\nb. V\n5. (Teacher reads: \"change\")\na. N\nb. V\nPart B: Context Clues Your teacher will read a definition/clue aloud. Listen\ncarefully and write the correct vocabulary word from Activities 7 or 8 on the\nline.\n6. (Teacher reads: \"The place where a car is kept, usually attached to a\nhouse.\")\n7. (Teacher reads: \"The thickest finger of the hand.\")\n8. (Teacher reads: \"A person who is in charge of a ship.\")\n9. (Teacher reads: \"The dark shape that is made when something blocks\nlight.\")\n10. (Teacher reads: \"To move in the same direction or track as someone\nelse.\")','teacher'),
(921,921,'Activity 1: Multiple Choice Vocabulary Review (Items 1–10)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the word that best completes the\nsentence or matches the definition.\n1. A sweet substance used to flavor food and drinks:\na. Salt\nb. Sugar\nc. Tear\nd. Blood\n2. An object you carry to protect yourself from rain:\na. Mirror\nb. Handkerchief\nc. Umbrella\nd. Drawer\n3. The opposite of \'to start\' or \'to begin\':\na. Copy\nb. Serve\nc. Finish\nd. Visit\n4. A short, pleated garment worn by a girl or woman:\na. Stocking\nb. Skirt\nc. Cloth\nd. Zipper\n5. A person whose profession is to treat the sick:\na. Soldier\nb. Butcher\nc. Doctor\nd. Pilot\n6. An eating utensil with prongs used to pick up food:\na. Spoon\nb. Fork\nc. Scissors\nd. Stove\n7. A drop of salty liquid that comes from the eye, often when\ncrying:\na. Juice\nb. Cocoa\nc. Tear\nd. Drug\n8. A type of public outdoor area where goods are bought and\nsold:\na. Church\nb. Bank\nc. Market\nd.\nBridge','teacher'),
(922,922,'9. A train is a type of transport that travels on tracks. The name for\nthe vehicle itself is:\na. Skirt\nb. Train\nc. Grades\nd. Month\n10. A fabric material made from the skin of an animal:\na. Rubber\nb. Cloth\nc. Leather\nd. Cotton','teacher'),
(923,923,'Activity 2: Fill in the Blank Puzzle\nDirections: Complete the following sentences using the most\nappropriate vocabulary word from the box below. Use each word\nonly once.\nWord Bank: stove, napkin, rose, church, twenty, soldier, thousand,\nvisit, noon, cupboard\n1. I bought a red ______\nto give to my mother.\n2. The ______\nhelps protect the country from enemies.\n3. Please keep the clean dishes inside the ______\ncabinet.\n4. We will ______\nour grandparents next week during the\nholidays.\n5. I need to borrow one ______\npesos to pay for the rent.\n6. We went to the ______\nto attend Sunday mass.\n7. The chef uses the ______\nto bake the bread.\n8. It is best to wipe your mouth with a ______\nafter eating.\n9. We ate lunch exactly at ______\n(12:00 PM).\n10. My savings account has over ______\ndollars.','teacher'),
(924,924,'Activity 3: Short Answer and Categorization\nDirections: Write the answer based on your knowledge of\nvocabulary.\n1. Name one item that is often used for wiping your nose or face.\n2. What is a term for a young person, either a boy or a girl?\n3. What word means the day after today?\n4. What is the measurement of how big or small something is?\n5. What is an amount of money equal to 25 cents?\n6. Name one item that can be used for cutting.\n7. Name one type of clothing item.\n8. What is the word for a place where clothes are kept, often with\na zipper?\n9. Where might a pharmacist sell medicine?\n10. What verb means \"to put money in a bank?\"','teacher'),
(925,925,'Activity 4: Definitions Matching\nDirections: Match the definitions with the correct vocabulary\nwords.\nDefinitions\nVocabulary Words\n1. A piece of cloth used for wiping one\'s A. Napkin\nnose or face.\n2. A young person, either a boy or a girl.\nB. Child\n3. The day after today.\nC. Tomorrow\n4. The measurement of how big or small D. Size\nsomething is\n5. An amount of money equal to 25 cents. E. Quarter','teacher'),
(926,926,'Activity 5: Matching Activity: Vocabulary Definitions\nDirections: Match each vocabulary word on the left with the\ncorrect definition on the right. Write the letter of the definition next\nto each word.\nVocabulary Words\nDefinitions\n1. Sugar\nA. An object carried to protect from rain\n2. Umbrella\nB. A profession treating sick individuals\n3. Finish\nC. A short garment worn by women\n4. Skirt\nD. A sweet substance used to flavor food\n5. Doctor\nE. A drop of liquid from the eye when crying\n6. Tear\nF. An eating utensil with prongs\n7. Fork\nG. A type of public area for buying and\nselling goods\n8. Market\nH. The opposite of starting or beginning\n9. Train\nI. A type of transportation that travels on\ntracks\n10. Leather\nJ. A fabric made from the skin of an animal','teacher'),
(927,927,'Activity 6: Fill in the Blank Definitions\nDirections: Complete each sentence with the appropriate\nvocabulary word.\n1. The place where a car is kept, usually attached to a house is\ncalled a ______\n.\n2. The thickest finger of the hand is the ______\n.\n3. A person who is in charge of a ship is known as the ______\n.\n4. The dark shape that is made when something blocks light is\ncalled a ______\n.\n5. To move in the same direction or track as someone else means\nto ______\n.\n6. A measurement of temperature is called ______\n.\n7. The act of deciding what to choose is known as ______\n.\n8. To make something clearer is to ______\n.\n9. The person who flies an airplane is called a ______\n.\n10. The liquid used for cooking food at high temperatures is called\n______.','teacher'),
(928,928,'Activity 7: Multiple Choice Questions\nDirections: Choose the letter of the correct answer.\n1. The place where a car is kept, usually attached to a house:\na. Garage\nb. Kitchen\nc. Bedroom\nd. Office\n2. The thickest finger of the hand is called the:\na. Index\nb. Thumb\nc. Pinky\nd. Ring\n3. A person who is in charge of a ship is:\na. Captain b. Sailor c. Mechanic\nd. Diver\n4. The dark shape created when something blocks light is known as:\na. Shadow b. Reflection c. Beam\nd. Glare\n5. To move in the same direction or track as someone else means to:\na. Follow\nb. Lead\nc. Attend\nd. Join\n6. The act of preparing food is called:\na. Cooking b. Arranging c. Eating d. Serving\n7. A tool used for writing:\na. Pencil\nb. Ruler\nc. Brush\nd. Paper\n8. The substance used in cooking that can add flavor:\na. Sugar\nb. Salt c. Pepper\nd. Oil\n9. The position of something in relation to its surroundings:\na. Location b. Direction c. Distance d. Area\n10. The person who makes laws in a government is called a:\na. Senator\nb. Mayor\nc. Judge\nd. Citizen','teacher'),
(929,929,'Activity 8: Match the Definitions\nDirections: Match each vocabulary term with the correct\ndefinition. Write the letter next to the number.\nVocabulary Terms\nDefinitions\n1. Garage\nA. Person in charge of a ship\n2. Thumb\nB. Dark shape made when light is\nblocked\n3. Captain\nC. Thickest finger on the hand\n4. Shadow\nD. Place to keep a car\n5. Follow\nE. Move in the same direction','teacher'),
(930,930,'Activity 9: Crossword Puzzle\nDirections: Complete the crossword puzzle using the clues below.\nClues:\nAcross: A dark shape made when something blocks light (6\nletters).\nDown: The place where you park your car (6 letters).\nDown: The thickest finger (5 letters).\nDown: To move in the same direction (6 letters).\nAcross: A person in charge of a ship (7 letters)','teacher'),
(931,931,'Activity 10: True or False\nDirections: Determine if each statement is true or false.\nA garage is a place to keep your car. (True/False)\nThe thumb is the smallest finger. (True/False)\nA captain is in charge of a ship. (True/False)\nA shadow is a bright spot created by light. (True/False)\nTo follow means to go in the opposite direction. (True/False)','teacher'),
(932,932,'Activity 11: Short Answer Questions\nDirections: Answer the following questions in one or two sentences.\nWhat is a garage used for?\nDescribe the function of a captain.\nWhat causes a shadow?\nExplain what it means to follow someone.\nWhy is the thumb considered the thickest finger?','teacher'),
(933,933,'Activity 12: Create a Sentence\nDirections: Use each of the following words in a complete\nsentence.\nGarage\nThumb\nCaptain\nShadow\nFollow','teacher'),
(934,934,'Activity 13: Vocabulary Riddles\nDirections: Solve the following riddles based on the vocabulary\nterms.\nI protect your vehicle from the rain and snow. What am I?\nI’m the thickest finger on your hand. What am I?\nI’m the dark outline you see when the light is behind you. What\nam I?\nI lead the crew as we sail across the sea. Who am I?\nI’m a term for moving behind someone. What am I?','teacher'),
(935,935,'Activity 14: Sorting Activity\nDirections: Sort the following words into two categories: People\nand Objects.\nCaptain\nGarage\nThumb\nShadow\nFollow','teacher'),
(936,936,'Activity 15: Word Search\nDirections: Find and circle the vocabulary words in the puzzle\nbelow.\nWords to find:\nGarage, Thumb, Captain, Shadow, Follow\nG A R A G E\nA Z X W E N\nC A P T A I\nT B V J O P\nI F L W T M\nN F S H C Y\nM U G A M A\nD H C I O A\nO H K F L N','teacher'),
(937,937,'Activity 16: Vocabulary Riddles\nDirections: Solve the following riddles based on the vocabulary\nterms.\nI am often praised for being appealing and lovely. What am I?\nI will help you find the answer to math problems. What am I?\nI encompass all the air, water, and living things around you. What\nam I?\nI can be a long trip or a quick outing. What am I?\nI help spark your creativity and push you to achieve more. What\nam I?','teacher'),
(938,938,'Activity 17: Word Search\nDirections: Find and circle the vocabulary words in the puzzle\nbelow.\nWords to find:\nBeautiful, Calculate, Environment, Journey, Inspire\nB E A U T I F U L\nW Q I X L O A E N\nC A L C U L A T E\nZ I O M Z R G T Y\nE N V I R O N M E\nN H H L K J E F Y\nT K U K M L Q N N','teacher'),
(939,939,'Activity 18: Fill in the Blank Definitions\nDirections: Complete each sentence with the appropriate\nvocabulary word.\nSomething that is pleasing to the senses can be described as\n______.\nTo find an answer through mathematical methods is to ______\n.\nThe world around us, including air, water, and land, is our\n______.\nA trip from one place to another is called a ______\n.\nTo motivate someone to do something positive is to ______\n.\nSomething that is hard to understand or unclear is ______\n.\nShowing admiration for someone is to give them ______\n.\nTo find something new or unknown is to ______\n.\nA difficult task that requires effort is a\n______.\nBeing inventive or original is described as being\n______.','teacher'),
(940,940,'Activity 19: Fill in the Blanks (2 points each)\nDirections: Complete each sentence using the appropriate\nvocabulary word from the box below. Use each word only once.\nWord Bank: Mysterious, Respect, Discover, Challenge, Creative\nThe universe is full of ______\nphenomena that scientists are still\ntrying to understand.\nIt is important to show ______\nto others, regardless of their\nbackground or beliefs.\nWhen you go on an adventure, you often ______\nnew places\nand experiences.\nCompleting a difficult task can be a(n) ______\nthat tests your\nabilities.\nBeing ______\nallows you to think outside the box and come up\nwith new ideas.','teacher'),
(941,941,'Activity 20: Multiple Choice (1 point each)\nDirections: Choose the letter of the correct answer.\nWhich word describes someone who enjoys taking risks and trying\nnew things?\na. Cautious\nb. Adventurous\nc. Indifferent\nd. Passive\nTo improve or make something better is to:\na. Decrease\nb. Enhance\nc. Neglect\nd. Ignore\nWhen someone feels upset or annoyed because of inability to\nachieve something, they feel:\na. Cheerful\nb. Frustrated\nc. Content\nd. Relaxed','teacher'),
(942,942,'Feeling thankful for what you have means you are:\na. Discontent\nb. Grateful\nc. Unappreciative\nd. Jealous\nAn idea or method that is new and creative is called:\na. Conventional\nb. Innovative\nc. Traditional\nd. Standard','teacher'),
(943,943,'PRETEST\nPart A — Numbers & Colors (1–4)\nInstructions: Read, understand and answer the questions correctly.\n1. Write the number: “seven” → ______\n2. Write the number word: “12 → ______\n”\n3. What color is the sky on a clear day?\na. blue\nb. red\nc. green\n4. Which word is a color?\na. run\nb. yellow\nc. happy\nPart B — Adverbs (5–6)\n5. Choose the adverb:\na. slowly\nb. tiger\nc. table\n6. Choose the sentence that uses an adverb correctly:\na. The cat runs quickly.\nb. The cat quickly.\nc. The quick cat run.\nPart C — Antonyms (7–8)\n7. Find the opposite of “big”:\na. tall\nb. small\nc. long\n8. The antonym of “happy” is ______\n.\na. sad\nb. joyful\nc. glad','teacher'),
(944,944,'Part D — Synonyms (9–10)\n9. Which word means the same as “fast”?\na) quick\nb) slow\nc) heavy\n10. A synonym for “begin” is ______\n.\na) start\nb) stop\nc) wait\nPart E — Nouns (11–12)\n11. Which word is a noun?\na) jump\nb) teacher\nc) slowly\n12. Choose the noun that names a place:\na) school\nb) red\nc) eat\nPart F — Human & Animal Body Parts (Matching) (13–15)\nMatch the word to the correct picture/description. Write the letter.\n13. ______\nTail\na) Helps animals balance\n14. ______\nEar\nb) Used for hearing\n15. ______\nHand\nc) Used for holding things\nPart G — Mini Crossword (16–17)\n16. Across (4 letters): Color of sky\n17. Down (5 letters): A number between six and eight\nPart H — Word Hunt (18)\n18. Circle and list three animals hidden in this string:\nXCCATRDTGHDOGASDGFRATZSDGRBIRDZSDGFOXDFHSH\n______, ______\n, ______','teacher'),
(945,945,'Part I — Word Pairing (19)\n19. Match the words that go together:\n1. hot\na. milk\n2. cold\nb. tea\nWrite the pairs: ______\n→ ______\n,\n______ → ______\nPart J — Matching Meaning (20)\n20. Match the word with its meaning:\n1. run\na. to move fast\n2. blue\nb. a color\nWrite: 1. ______\n,\n2. ______','teacher'),
(946,946,'Act Game\nActivity 1\nDirections: Pick a square word card inside a box or bag. Read the\nword. Find the word inside the classroom. Write them on the\nboard (e.g. half ½, 9, 11, etc.) Do it repeatedly.\nshape\nrecord\nsouth\nobject\nminute\nwhole\nunit\nbigger\ntoday\nnight\nspring\nhow\nwhen\nalways\nlive\ntime\nroad\ndraw\npair\ndress\ncounter\nflow\nmeasure ______','teacher'),
(947,947,'Match and Color\nActivity 2\nDirections: Find or search the words inside the box below in the\nworksheet. The words may appear vertically and horizontally. Color\nthe words with crayons.\na t\nl\nU\nc\nf\nf\nD\ny e l\nL\no w\ns\nk\nn\nv m ______\nP\na\nr\nt\ny\ng\nt\na p t\nw\nf\no\nr\nc\ne\nn\ne e s\na\nm n\ns\nh\nn\ne\nh r g\ng\na\ng\ne\nR\nr a s\nT\nd\nl\nn\nu\nr\ne\nt e\nS\nt\ne\nd\no\na\nf\na u a H\ne\na\nd\nn\nl\nf\np r a C\nt\nc\ne\nj\nt e s\nU\nb\nj\ne\nc\nt\nD\nsubject\nyellow\nforce\npair\nwrong\nsand\nwait\ngeneral\nskin\nparty\ntest\nahead\npractice\nside\ndifficult\nheavy\ntail\nenough\ndifferent\n______ ______ temperature','teacher'),
(948,948,'Word Search\nActivity 3\nDirections: Find and circle the words in the worksheet. The words\nappear horizontally, vertically or diagonally. The given words are\nlisted below.\nm a\nt\ne\nr\ni a\nl\nc\nb c g u e s s\nt\no\nl\nt\nh n g r ______\nh\nr\no n\nu g\ni n o n\no u g\no c o u e\nd o e\ns\nn h i\ns\nr\ny m\nn o r g a\ng a\nr d e n e n d\nn\nf\no\nr w a r d e\nt\ne a m h\nl e d\ns\ndoes\nsign\nguess\nride\nminor\nblood\nrich\ncat\nled\namount\nnote\nmaterial\nthousand forward huge region\nperiod\nteam\ncorner garden','teacher'),
(949,949,'Activity 4\nHidden Letters\nDirections: Fill in the missing letters in the given repetitive words.\nUse the provided words below.\no ______\np o ______\n______ e\nm\n______ l ______\no\nn\no\np\np ______\ns ______\nt\ne\n______ l ______\n______ n\n______ p ______\no\ns\nt ______\nm ______\n______ l ______\no\nn\no ______\n______ o ______\n______ e\n______ l ______\no ______\n______ d ______\n______ o\nn\n______ r\n______ u\ns\na ______\nd\nt\n______ o\nn\n______ a\nr\n______ o\nu ______\n______ d\nd ______\nt\n______ n\na ______\n______ u\ns\na\nd ______\n______ o ______\n______ r\no ______\ns\nw ______\n______ h\nt ______ ______ ______ ______\n______ l\n______ n\nd\n______ e ______\ng ______\nt\n______ s ______\na\nn ______\nw\ne\n______ h ______\n______ l\na ______\nd\nw ______\ng ______\nt\ns ______\n______ n\nd\nb\no\nr\nn\nd ______\ne ______\nn\n‘ ______\nr\na\nc\ne\nb ______\nr ______\n______ o ______\ns\nn ______\nt\n______ a ______\ne\n______ o\nr ______\nd ______\ne\ns ______\n‘\nt\nr ______\nc\ne\nb ______\n______ n\nd\no\ne ______\nn\n‘ ______\nr\na ______ ______\nc\na\nt\nt\nl\ne\nd\ne\na\nd\ns\ne\nn\ns\ne\n______ a ______\nt\nl\ne\nd ______\na ______\ns\n______ n\ns ______\nc ______\nt ______\nl ______\n______ e ______\nd\n______ e\n______ s\ne\nc\na ______\nt ______\ne\n______ ______ a\nd\n______ ______ ______ e\nn\n______ e\nk\nn\nd\n______ n ______\nb\nr\no\nt\nh\ne\nr\nk ______\n______ d\nb ______\no\nt\n______ e\nr\nk\nn ______\n______ r\no ______\nh\ne ______\nb ______\n______ t\nh ______\nr\nrace\nbrother\ndead\nborn\ncattle\nvarious\nkind\naddition doesn’t\nweight\nisland\nopposite\nsense\nmillion','teacher'),
