(1461,1461,'1. What is a synonym for \"puzzle\"?\n\n2. What is an antonym for \"shame\"?\n\n3. The word \"immense\" means:\n\n4. If you are \"adept\" at something, you are:\n\n5. A word that means the opposite of \"trite\" is:\n\n6. Which word means \"to be given permission\"?\n\n7. Choose the correct word: \"She has _____ hair.\"\n\n8. Which word describes a lack of strength?\n\n9. In the sentence, \"The speck of dust was miniscule,\" what does \"miniscule\" mean?\n\n10. \"The mischievous child hid his sister\'s toys.\" What does \"mischievous\" mean?\n\n11. Based on the sentence, \"He was sent to the penitentiary for his crime,\" a penitentiary is a:\n\n12. \"There was pandemonium in the streets after the championship win.\" Pandemonium means:\n\n13. A \"wager\" is another word for a:\n\n14. When someone is \"amiable,\" they are:\n\n15. To have \"rancour\" towards someone is to feel:\n\n16. If you look at something \"cursory,\" you look at it:\n\n17. To \"engender\" hope means to:\n\n18. An \"indolent\" student is:\n\n19. A \"supercilious\" look is:\n\n20. To \"vitiate\" water means to:\n\n21. To \"pacify\" a crying baby means to:\n\n22. A \"lucid\" dream is:\n\n23. \"Indigenous\" plants are:\n\n24. A person with \"charisma\" often has:\n\n25. To \"placate\" an angry person means to:\n\n26. What is a \"timetable\" used for?\n\n27. A \"dictionary\" is a book that contains:\n\n28. A \"student\" is primarily known for:\n\n29. A \"blackboard\" is typically found in a:\n\n30. To \"participate\" in a game is to:\n\n31. To \"cheat\" on a test is to:\n\n32. An \"edifice\" is most likely a:\n\n33. A \"portal\" could be described as a:\n\n34. An \"era\" in history is a:\n\n35. His \"version\" of the story is his:\n\n36. A \"cache\" of food is a:\n\n37. A \"dialogue\" in a play is the:\n\n38. A \"refugee\" often leaves their home because of:\n\n39. If you are \"furious,\" you are feeling:\n\n40. To \"discover\" a new island is to:\n\n41. To \"comfort\" a friend who is sad is to:\n\n42. If something happened \"recently,\" it happened:\n\n43. What is a \"shed\" commonly used for?\n\n44. A \"pond\" is a body of water that is:\n\n45. A \"calf\" is a young:\n\n46. A \"hose\" is typically used to:\n\n47. A \"swing\" is found on a:\n\n48. The word \"calculate\" is most related to:\n\n49. The primary goal of \"communication\" is to:\n\n50. If you \"trudge\" through snow, you walk:','teacher'),
(1462,1462,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A Day with Friends \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: The Logic Champion Maria loved a good challenge. She opened a book filled with difficult conundrums, or mind-exercising puzzles. After solving the last one, she felt a surge of pride, the exact opposite of mortification. She had no rancour for anyone, only kindness in her heart. She knew that causing pandemonium was not the way to celebrate, so she quietly enjoyed her victory, feeling far away from any penitentiary.\nApply What You Have Learned About Synonyms Synonyms are words that have the same or similar meaning.\n\n1. The book of logic contained many conundrums –mind exercising puzzle. Using the synonym clue the word conundrums in this sentence means\n\n2. Jackie was filled with mortification or shame, because of her careless remark. Using the synonym clue, the word mortification in this sentence means\n\n3. His rancour, or hatred of his brother has caused him to live his life as a lonely person. Using the synonym clue, the word rancour in this sentence means\n\n4. The man was sent to the penitentiary or prison for stealing cars. Using the synonym clue, the word penitentiary in this sentence means\n\n5. There was crazy pandemonium as people were trying to leave the rock concert. Using the synonym clue, the word pandomenium in this sentence means','teacher'),
(1463,1463,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A Day with Friends \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\nPassage: A Day with Friends Looking through his microscope, Leo saw a miniscule insect.\nHis amiable friend, Lance, made a wager that he couldn\'t draw it. Lance had an immense collection of art supplies. Suddenly, Sam mischievously snuck in and tickled them, almost ruining the drawing.\n\nApply What You Have Learned About Context Clues Context Clues are words in sentences that help you figure out the meaning of a difficult word that you do not know.\n\n1. The dirt in the paper was miniscule I could not even see it.\n\n2. My Lolo put up a wager that Manny Pacquiao will win the fight. He will treat all of us to dinner if Paquiao wins.\n\n3. Michael Jackson has an immense fan base. The whole world adores him.\n\n4. Lance is an amiable boy. He has lots of friends and outside school.\n\n5. Sam mischievously placed the fart pillow on Mom’s chair.','teacher'),
(1464,1464,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" Family Contrasts \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: Family Contrasts\n\nAt the family talent show, my naïve little brother thought everyone would win a prize. My aunt, an adept and agile dancer, performed beautifully. My uncle, however, didn\'t scowl at his own clumsy attempt; he laughed. We all agreed his idea for a comedy act was far from trite.\n\nApply What You Have Learned About Antonym Antonym context clues are words around a difficult word that mean the opposite or nearly the opposite as the word.\n\n1. We thought it was a brilliant idea, but our teacher thought it was trite.\n\n2. Mr. Lim is adept with crossword puzzles, while his wife is terrible at solving.\n\n3. Mother was suspicious when Danny handed her the bag, but my naïve little sister opened it anyway.\n\n4. Rather than scowl, dad had a huge smile on his face.\n\n5. Aunt Claire is an agile dancer; however, my cousin is quite clumsy.','teacher'),
(1465,1465,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Busy Week \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: The Busy Week My parents allowed me to go shopping, but I felt too weak from a long week. I had to tie a knot in my lace before we left. At the store, we saw my friend with red hair, who told us about a great sale on shoes.\n\nApply What You Have Learned About Homophones\n\nA homophone is a word that is pronounced the same as another word but has a different meaning.\nCircle the homophones that best fits the sentence.\n\n1. My parents (allowed/aloud) me to watch a movie with my friend.\n\n2. I kept getting a (not/knot) in my shoe after my basketball game.\n\n3. I felt (weak/week) after I worked the whole day.\n\n4. My mom waited for the (sale/sail) at the store before she went shopping.\n\n5. My friend Sarah has (red/read) hair.','teacher'),
(1466,1466,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Arrogant Leader \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: The Arrogant Leader The supercilious king was known for his indolent ways. His bad policies would vitiate the clean water supply, which would engender anger among the people. It took a wise advisor to pacify the crowds and Apply What You Have Learned About Vocabulary restore peace.\n\nFirst, Second, Third?\n\n1. vitiate\n\n2. indolent\n\n3. supercilious\n\n4. engender\n\n5. pacify','teacher'),
(1467,1467,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Inspiring Speaker \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: The Inspiring Speaker\n\nThe speaker had a remarkable charisma that captivated everyone. She gave a lucid explanation of the history of the indigenous people. She warned that a cursory study of history was not enough. Her powerful words could placate even the most critical listeners.\n\nApply What You Have Learned About Context Clues What Does It Mean?\n\n1. She paid only cursory attention to her parents’ final instructions.\n\n2. Her explanation of the situation was astonishing lucid.\n\n3. This country’s indigenous people were hunter-gatherers.\n\n4. The woman had a strange charisma, and we couldn’t stop looking at her.\n\n5. After our argument, it took over an hour to placate her.','teacher'),
(1468,1468,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A Student\'s Tools \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: A Student\'s Tools\n\nEvery student needs to be organized. First, check your timetable to see your first lesson. Pack your rucksack with all your books, including a dictionary. Don\'t forget you have a film to watch on the big screen in science class!\n\nApply What You Have Learned\n\nSituation\n\n1. You can carry your school books in this.\n\n2. Your class can watch a film or a DVD on this.\n\n3. This interesting book tells you what words mean.\n\n4. A person who studies.\n\n5. This will tell you the times of your lessons.','teacher'),
(1469,1469,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" School Rules \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: School Rules In the gym, the coach wrote the rules on a small blackboard. The main instruction was clear: never cheat during a game. She was happy to see so many students participate with honesty and energy.\nApply What You Have Learned About Vocabulary Complete the sentences with the words from the box\n\nblackboard      gym          participate instruction        cheat\n\n1. The teacher wrote something on the ______, but we couldn’t read it.\n\n2. You are not allowed to ______ at your final exams.\n\n3. Before you start with the test, please read the ______.\n\n4. For physical education we have to go to the ______.\n\n5. Many students ______ in activities after school, for example drama clubs or sports.','teacher'),
(1470,1470,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Field Trip\" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nThe Field Trip The class took a trip to a huge new science museum. \"This is terrific!\"\nMaria exclaimed. She saw a strange insect she had never seen before.\n\"You can depend on this museum to have cool exhibits,\" said the teacher. \"It\'s much better than the terrible one we visited last year.\"\nApply What You Have Learned About Synonyms Replace the italicized word with synonyms from the list below. Write your answer in the box.\n\ndepend on             huge            terrible    investigate terrific         strange            similar     increase\n\nThe pizza was awful. huge\n\n1. What a fantastic idea! (fantastic)\n\n2. You can trust her. She’s very responsible. (trust)\n\n3. The new sport center is enormous. (enormous)\n\n4. I’ve never seen an animal like that before. It looks weird! (weird)','teacher'),
(1471,1471,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A New Friend \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: A New Friend\n\nRecently, our class met a refugee named Amir. At first, he was sad, and we tried to comfort him. We helped him discover the fun parts of our city. One day, a bully was furious and yelled at Amir, but we stood up for our new friend.\n\nApply What You Have About Learned Vocabulary\n\nColumn A\n1. comfort\n2. refugee\n3. discover\n4. furious\n5. recently','teacher'),
(1472,1472,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Historian\'s Discovery\" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nThe Historian\'s Discovery The historian stood before the massive portal of the ancient edifice. She was studying a new era of history. In an old journal, she found one version of events that differed from all others. Following a clue, she discovered a secret cache of artifacts hidden behind a stone wall.\n\nApply What You Have Learned About Vocabulary\n\nCOLUMN I                            COLUMN II\n\nColumn A\n1. impressive door\n2. impressive building\n3. historical period\n4. account from a particular viewpoint\n5. hiding place','teacher'),
(1473,1473,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Writer\'s Room\" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nThe Writer\'s Room The writer was crafting a drama. He knew the denouement had to be satisfying for the audience. He included a funny anecdote from his own life and wrote sharp dialogue between the characters. The story wasn\'t a long fable, but it had a powerful message.\nApply What You Have Learned Crossword Puzzle: Word Search Game\n\nd     i    a       l      o     g      u   e   b     a\n\na     y    h       f      o     a      b   s   a     l\n\na     b    h       h      g     v      h   s   c     l\n\nc     m     x      h      q     u      o   a   e     e\n\nr    h     f     q        i    g      n   w   e     g\n\nb     c     x     a       a     v      x   b     s   o\n\ne     v    m       t      q     n      m   x   d     r\n\nn     a    n       e      c     d      o   t   e     y\n\nr    u    m      a       d     z      u   a     l   c\n\nd     e    n       o      u    m       e   n     t   t\n\n•   a play for theatre, radio, or television______\n•   the point in the story is resolved_______\n•    a short moral story ____________\n•   a short amusing or interesting story about a real incident or person _____________\n•   conversation between two or more people as a feature of a book, play or movie _______________\n\nFind the word being described horizontally, diagonally and vertically. Supply the correct answer in the blank.','teacher'),
(1474,1474,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A Big Day \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: A Big Day Today was so exciting! My sister is going to marry her best friend. After the ceremony, a live band will play music. I had to use the telephone to call all my friends to tell them the news. I even skipped soccer practice to be there!\n\nApply What You Have Learned About Vocabulary\n\nband                    practice exciting              telephone       marry\n\n1. The game was very ______ at the end.\n\n2. I watched my older sister ______ her childhood sweetheart.\n\n3. The ______ played a good song.\n\n4. We had a basketball ______ after school.\n\n5. I used my ______ to call my parents.','teacher'),
(1475,1475,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Soldier\'s Story \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: The Soldier\'s Story\n\nThe soldier searched beneath his bunk for his favorite magazine. He had grown a lot in height since joining the army. It took great courage to face his fears. He saw his mission not as a danger, but as an opportunity to prove himself.\n\nMagazine                         courage                beneath opportunity                     height\n\n1. I had to look ______ my bed for my shoes.\n\n2. I increased in ______ as I got older.\n\n3. I love to read a ______ for recreation.\n\n4. The soldiers have a lot of ______.\n\n5. I don’t often get this kind of ______.','teacher'),
(1476,1476,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Determined Explorer \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\nPassage: The Determined Explorer\n\nThe path up the mountain was steep, but Leo had to persevere. He would not quit. He knew that to succeed, he had to persist through the challenge.\n\nApply What You Have Learned About Vocabulary Frayer Model\n\nDefinition        Synonym                        Definition     Synonym\n\nvibrant                                    gorgeous Antonym              Sentence                    Antonym     Sentence\n\nSynonym                                Synonym Definition                                 Definition\n\nfabulous                                   splendid\n\nAntonym                       Sentence                           Sentence Antonym\n\nDefinitionn                   Synonym\n\namiable\n\nAntonym                         Sentence\n\nFill in the box with its correct information.','teacher'),
(1477,1477,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A Long Day for the Scientist \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: A Long Day for the Scientist\n\nAfter the police arrest the suspect, the detective had to calculate the exact timeline of the crime. Meanwhile, in the lab, a scientist began a new experiment.\nShe had to trudge through deep snow to get to her lab early. She heard a knock on her door just as she started.\n\nApply What You Have Learned Draw a vocabulary sketch note\n\nknock\n\nexperiment\n\ntrudge                            arrest                     calculate\n\nWrite your answer.','teacher'),
(1478,1478,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A Change of Heart\" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: A Change of Heart The big diamond was far from trashy; it was classy and beautiful. The owner was thankful, not ungrateful, for such a treasure. When asked if she loved it, her answer was \"yes,\" not \"no.\" Suddenly, a loud noise caused chaos, destroying the calmness in the room.\n\nApply What You Have Learned Directions; Complete this crossword puzzle . Write the antonym of the words provided in the clues.\n\n1                         2\n\n3                                          5\n\nAcross                                     Down\n\n1. Antonym of little\n\n2. Antonym of ungrateful\n\n3. Antonym of trashy\n\n4. Antonym of calmness\n\n5. Antonym of no','teacher'),
(1479,1479,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Lucky Day\" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\nPassage: The Lucky Day She carried a small talisman, her lucky charm, in her pocket. The chill in the air, the coldness of the morning, didn\'t bother her. She had the abilities and skills to win the contest. When she did, she couldn\'t just giggle; she let out a huge laugh!\n\nApply What You Have Learned\n\n3                                     5\n\nAcross                                     Down\n\n1. Synonym of little\n\n2. Synonym of giggle\n\n3. Synonym of lucky charm\n\n4. Synonym of coldness\n\n5. Synonym of skills','teacher'),
(1480,1480,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" A Day at the Farm \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: A Day at the Farm The children played on the old swing hanging from the tree. Nearby, a calf drank from a small pond. The farmer used a hose to water the plants and then put the tools away in the dusty shed.\nDire\n\n1.\n\nAcross\n\na seat suspended by ropes or chains, on which someone may sit and swing back and forth.\n\na flexible pipe for conveying a liquid or gas.\n\nthe young of the domestic cow or other bovine animal.\n\nDown\n\na small, rough building or lean-on, used 2     for shelter\n\na small area of still water, typically one formed naturally\n\n1. Across: a seat hung by ropes or chains, on which someone may sit and swing back and forth. Write the picture name.\n\n2. Down: a small, rough building or lean-to, used for shelter. Write the picture name.\n\n3. Across: a flexible pipe for carrying a liquid or gas. Write the picture name.\n\n4. Down: a small area of still water, usually one formed naturally. Write the picture name.\n\n5. Across: the young of the domestic cow. Write the picture name.','teacher'),
(1481,1481,'IMPORTANT: Please read the short story \" The Network of Life \" BEFORE you answer the questions below. It will help you!\n\nPassage: The Network of Life Good communication is more than just talk. It involves using a phone to call, writing an email, or sending a message. Most importantly, it requires us to listen carefully to what others are saying.\n\nApply What You Have Learned Word Association:\n\ncommunication\n\nSentence\n1.______________________________________________________\n2._______________________________________________________\n3.______________________________________________________\n4.______________________________________________________\n5.______________________________________________________\n\nSET A\n\nFill in the box a word that associates with the word given in the circle and use it in a sentence.','teacher'),
(1482,1482,'1. What is a synonym for \"puzzle\"?\n\n2. What is an antonym for \"shame\"?\n\n3. The word \"immense\" means:\n\n4. If you are \"adept\" at something, you are:\n\n5. A word that means the opposite of \"trite\" is:\n\n6. Which word means \"to be given permission\"?\n\n7. Choose the correct word: \"She has _____ hair.\"\n\n8. Which word describes a lack of strength?\n\n9. In the sentence, \"The speck of dust was miniscule, so we needed a microscope to see it,\" what does \"miniscule\" mean?\n\n10. \"The mischievous child hid his sister\'s toys.\" What does \"mischievous\" mean?\n\n11. Based on the sentence, \"He was sent to the penitentiary for his crime,\" a penitentiary is a:\n\n12. \"There was pandemonium in the streets after the championship win.\" Pandemonium means:\n\n13. A \"wager\" is another word for a:\n\n14. When someone is \"amiable,\" they are:\n\n15. To have \"rancour\" towards someone is to feel:\n\n16. If you look at something \"cursory,\" you look at it:\n\n17. To \"engender\" hope means to:\n\n18. An \"indolent\" student is:\n\n19. A \"supercilious\" look is:\n\n20. To \"vitiate\" water means to:\n\n21. To \"pacify\" a crying baby means to:\n\n22. A \"lucid\" dream is:\n\n23. \"Indigenous\" plants are:\n\n24. A person with \"charisma\" often has:\n\n25. To \"placate\" an angry person means to:\n\n26. What is a \"timetable\" used for?\n\n27. A \"dictionary\" is a book that contains:\n\n28. A \"student\" is primarily known for:\n\n29. A \"blackboard\" is typically found in a:\n\n30. To \"participate\" in a game is to:\n\n31. To \"cheat\" on a test is to:\n\n32. An \"edifice\" is most likely a:\n\n33. A \"portal\" could be described as a:\n\n34. An \"era\" in history is a:\n\n35. His \"version\" of the story is his:\n\n36. A \"cache\" of food is a:\n\n37. A \"dialogue\" in a play is the:\n\n38. A \"refugee\" often leaves their home because of:\n\n39. If you are \"furious,\" you are feeling:\n\n40. To \"discover\" a new island is to:\n\n41. To \"comfort\" a friend who is sad is to:\n\n42. If something happened \"recently,\" it happened:\n\n43. What is a \"shed\" commonly used for?\n\n44. A \"pond\" is a body of water that is:\n\n45. A \"calf\" is a young:\n\n46. A \"hose\" is typically used to:\n\n47. A \"swing\" is found on a:\n\n48. The word \"calculate\" is most related to:\n\n49. The primary goal of \"communication\" is to:\n\n50. If you \"trudge\" through snow, you walk:','teacher'),
(1483,1483,'1. What is a synonym for \"conundrum\"?\n\n2. What is an antonym for \"mortification\"?\n\n3. The word \"miniscule\" means:\n\n4. If an idea is \"trite,\" it is:\n\n5. A word that means the opposite of \"adept\" is:\n\n6. Which word means \"to be able to be heard\"?\n\n7. Choose the correct word: \"I will _____ the book tomorrow.\"\n\n8. Which word describes a period of seven days?\n\n9. In the sentence, \"The amiable shopkeeper always helped customers,\" what does \"amiable\" mean?\n\n10. \"She looked at the document with cursory attention.\" This means she looked at it:\n\n11. \"His rancour for his former friend was obvious.\" Rancour means:\n\n12. When there is \"pandemonium\" in a classroom, there is:\n\n13. To \"wager\" money on a game means to:\n\n14. A \"penitentiary\" is another word for a:\n\n15. If you do something \"mischievously,\" you do it:\n\n16. To \"engender\" discussion means to:\n\n17. An \"indolent\" worker is:\n\n18. A \"supercilious\" person acts:\n\n19. To \"vitiate\" the evidence means to:\n\n20. To \"pacify\" a crowd means to:\n\n21. A \"lucid\" explanation is:\n\n22. \"Indigenous\" animals are:\n\n23. A person with \"charisma\" has:\n\n24. To \"placate\" someone means to:\n\n25. If you give something \"cursory\" attention, you give it:\n\n26. A \"rucksack\" is used for:\n\n27. A \"dictionary\" helps you find:\n\n28. A \"student\" is someone who:\n\n29. A \"blackboard\" is used for:\n\n30. To \"participate\" means to:\n\n31. An \"edifice\" is a(n):\n\n32. A \"portal\" is a(n):\n\n33. An \"era\" is a:\n\n34. A \"version\" is:\n\n35. A \"cache\" is a:\n\n36. A \"dialogue\" is a:\n\n37. A \"refugee\" is someone who:\n\n38. If you are \"furious,\" you are:\n\n39. To \"discover\" means to:\n\n40. To \"comfort\" someone is to:\n\n41. \"Recently\" means:\n\n42. What is a \"calf\"?\n\n43. A \"pond\" is a:\n\n44. A \"shed\" is a:\n\n45. A \"hose\" is a:\n\n46. A \"swing\" is a:\n\n47. The main purpose of \"communication\" is to:\n\n48. To