(1684,1684,'The m anila Pulice D istrict will deploy at least 2k mpd oersonnel to secure sixty one Chatholic churchs in the city as the tra ditional simbang gabi or dawn mass starts today\n\nA minimum of 4 police off icers will be post in its church for the dawn mass, according to MPD director Brig.\n\nGen. Andre Dizon\n\nThe retof the Po lice officers will be on rotation for bicycle, motocycle, foot and\n\nmobile patrols, Dizon sad.\n\nHe saud roving Police officers cars would also be deploy to sicure the churches.\n\nThe mpd personnel will augmented by force multipliers from barangays, Diszon said.\n\nAmong the prominent churches to be secured by police are the MnailaCathedral and San Agustin Church in Intramuros, Sto. Niño Church in Tondo and the Minor Basilica f the Black Nazarene o R Quiapo Church.\n\nA total of thirteen k police personnel will be deployed protect to church- goers during the nine-day dawn mass, according to the national Capital Region Police Officeess ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ___________________________________________________________________________ ________________________