(1,'','assets/module/page-001.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-9.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [18.200000762939453, 22.75, 575.1900024414062, 828.25], \"xref\": 9, \"width\": 1707, \"height\": 2482}]'),
(2,'                                                                                                                     ii\n\n\nBUKIDNON’S UNIFIED LITERACY AND INTERVENTION GATEWAY (BULIG)\n\"DIVISION INNOVATION TO IMPROVE LEARNERS\' READING ABILITY\"\n Level 1 – Oral Language\n\nFirst Edition, 2025\n       Republic Act 8293, section 176 states that: No copyright shall subsist in any work of the\nGovernment of the Philippines. However, prior approval of the government agency or office wherein\n the work is created shall be necessary for exploitation of such work for profit. Such agency or office\nmay, among other things, impose as a condition the payment of royalty.\n\n       Borrowed materials (i.e., stories, poems, pictures, photos, etc.) included in this book are\nowned by their respective copyright holders. Every effort has been exerted to locate and seek\npermission to use  these  materials from their respective copyright owners. The publisher and\nauthors do not represent nor claim ownership over them.\n\nPublished by the Department of Education – Division of Bukidnon\nSchools Division Superintendent: Victoria V. Gazo, Ph.D., CESO IV\n\n\n\n\n\nPrinted in the Philippines by:\nDepartment of Education – Division of Bukidnon\nOffice Address: Fortich St., Sumpong, Malaybalay City, Bukidnon\n Telephone:     (088) 813-3634\nE-mail Address: bukidnon@deped.gov.ph','assets/module/page-002.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [14.149999618530273, 777.89990234375, 573.1600341796875, 834.8499145507812], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-14.png\", \"bbox\": [166.6999969482422, 256.5999755859375, 431.5, 269.79998779296875], \"xref\": 14, \"width\": 735, \"height\": 36}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-18.png\", \"bbox\": [83.5999984741211, 283.4999694824219, 129.60000610351562, 296.0999755859375], \"xref\": 18, \"width\": 127, \"height\": 34}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-20.png\", \"bbox\": [155.6999969482422, 283.5, 263.70001220703125, 309.29998779296875], \"xref\": 20, \"width\": 299, \"height\": 71}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-22.png\", \"bbox\": [83.5999984741211, 323.0999755859375, 363.20001220703125, 524.0999755859375], \"xref\": 22, \"width\": 776, \"height\": 558}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-26.png\", \"bbox\": [83.5999984741211, 531.1000366210938, 170.60000610351562, 543.7000122070312], \"xref\": 26, \"width\": 241, \"height\": 34}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-28.png\", \"bbox\": [191.6999969482422, 531.0999755859375, 394.8999938964844, 583.2999877929688], \"xref\": 28, \"width\": 564, \"height\": 145}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-30.png\", \"bbox\": [83.5999984741211, 592.2000122070312, 132.8000030517578, 604.7999877929688], \"xref\": 30, \"width\": 136, \"height\": 35}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-32.png\", \"bbox\": [191.6999969482422, 590.800048828125, 451.0, 669.4000244140625], \"xref\": 32, \"width\": 720, \"height\": 218}]'),
(3,'                                                                                                              iii\n\n\n                   PREFACE\n\n\n     Reading is the cornerstone of learning, yet it remains one of\nthe most pressing challenges in education today. In response, the\nDivision of Bukidnon proudly introduces Bukidnon’s Unified\nLiteracy and Intervention Gateway (BULIG) — a transformative\ninnovation designed  to improve  learners’ reading  ability and\nempower every child to succeed.\n\n   BULIG is more than a program; it is a unified movement for\nliteracy, built on collaboration, evidence-based strategies, and a\ndeep commitment to equity in education. This initiative bridges\ngaps in reading proficiency by providing targeted interventions,\ninnovative approaches, and sustainable support systems that\ncater to the diverse needs of learners across the division.\n\n    Anchored on this vision, the Division of Bukidnon integrates\nthe ARAL Program (Academic Recovery and Accessible Learning),\na national initiative focused on learning recovery and remediation.\nARAL provides structured and learner-centered interventions for\nthose struggling with foundational skills in reading and numeracy.\nBy complementing BULIG’s  mission, ARAL  strengthens  the\ndivision’s  comprehensive  approach  to  literacy,  ensuring  that\nlearners overcome difficulties and gain the confidence to succeed\nacademically. Together, these programs create a powerful synergy\nthat accelerates learning recovery and builds a strong foundation\nfor lifelong learning.\n\n    Through BULIG, we envision classrooms where every\nlearner reads with confidence. Comprehends with clarity, and\nlearns with purpose. This gateway opens  opportunities  for\nlifelong learning, ensuring that no child is left behind in the\njourney toward academic excellence and personal growth.\n\n     Together, let us make literacy not just a goal, but a reality for\nall.','assets/module/page-003.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [14.149999618530273, 777.89990234375, 573.1600341796875, 834.8499145507812], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(4,'                                                                                  iv\n\n                     Table of Contents\n                                                Page    Activity                   Title of Activity                                             Number\nPreliminary\nPages          Cover Page                                                                      i\n              Development Team of the Reading\n                                                                                                                                          ii                 Tool Kit\n                Preface                                                                                   iii\n                Table of Contents                                   iv\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 1                         1\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 2                          2\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 3                          3\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 4                          4\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 5                          5\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 6                          6\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 7, 9, 100                   7\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 11 & 12                     8\nPre-Assessment   Pre-test Lesson 12                        9\nPre-Assessment   Intervention Materials\nLESSON 1        Talking About One’s Self and One’s Family   9\nLESSON 2        Follow One-to-Two-Step Physical Directions    9\n                Give and Follow One-to-Two-Step VerbalLESSON 3                                               10                  Directions\nLESSON 4       Recognize Describing Words               11\nLESSON 5        Talk About Topics of Interest               16\nLESSON 6        Describe and Draw                       18\nLESSON 7        Using Story Chain                          19\nLESSON 8        Using Picture Talk                         20\nLESSON 9        Usin