(5,'Lesson Plan 6    Oral Language- Describe and Draw           55\n                  Oral Language Using Picture Story ChainLesson Plan 7                                            58                  Strategy\nLesson Plan 8    Oral Language Using Picture Talk Activities    64\n                  Recite, Clap & Smile- Little voices ShiningLesson Plan 9                                            67                Through Poems\nLesson Plan 10   Talk, Play & Share- Little voices Connecting   70\n                  Oral Language- Word Friends (WordLesson Plan 11                                           73                   Association)\nLesson Plan 12   Oral Language- Fun with Tongue Twisters      75\nPost –                   Post-test Lesson 1                         78Assessment\nPost –                  Post -test Lesson 2                        79Assessment\nPost –                  Post -test Lesson 3                        80Assessment\nPost –                  Post -test Lesson 4                        81Assessment\nPost –                  Post -test Lesson 5                        82Assessment\nPost –                  Post -test Lesson 6                        83\nAssessment\nPost –                  Post -test Lesson 7                        84Assessment','assets/module/page-005.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [14.149999618530273, 777.89990234375, 573.1600341796875, 834.8499145507812], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(6,'','assets/module/page-006.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [15.949999809265137, 775.5, 574.9600219726562, 832.4500122070312], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}, {\"path\": \"assets/module/image-64.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [77.0, 339.04998779296875, 521.6500244140625, 500.28997802734375], \"xref\": 64, \"width\": 1379, \"height\": 500}]'),
(7,'                                                              1\n   Name:\n\n\n\n\nLESSON 1: TALKING ABOUT ONE’S SELF AND ONE’S FAMILY\n\n    PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to share basic information about oneself and family.\n\n     1. “Tell me your name and age.”\n\n     2. “What is one thing you like to do for fun?”\n\n     3. “Who lives with you at home?”\n\n     4. “Tell me one thing about your mom, dad, or sibling.”\n\n     5. “What is your family’s favorite food to eat together?”\n\n                                                               Needs\n                   Excellent                        Satisfactory\n    Criteria                  Good (3pts)                  Improvement\n                      (4pts)                              (2pts)\n                                                                                (1pt)\n\n\n               Cover self (name,  Covers self + 2  Covers self +   Only shares 1-2\n\n                  age, likes) +3      details         1 detail         small Facts Completeness\n                   details                                           about self\n\n\n\n              Speech  is clear,  Mostly clear    Somewhat     Hard to\n\n                loud, and easy to with minor      unclear or quiet  understand; Clarity\n               understand       pauses                     mumbles\n\n\n\n                Shares info in a   Mostly logical   Somewhat     No clear order\n\n                  logical order       order            disorganized Organization\n                     (self-first, then\n\n                 family)','assets/module/page-007.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [6.050099849700928, 774.6000366210938, 588.2501220703125, 831.5490112304688], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(8,'                                                             2\n\n\nLESSON 2: FOLLOW ONE-STEP TO TWO-STEP PHYSICAL DIRECTIONS\n    PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n     Assesses prior ability to follow simple physical directions.\n\n     1. “Stand up.” (2-step)\n\n     2. “Walk to the window and point at something blue.” (2-step)\n\n     3. “Pick up the pencil and put it on the table.” (2-step)\n\n     4. “Turn around and clap your hands once.” (2-step)\n\n     5. “Go to the front of the room and wave at me.” (2-step)\n\n                                                              Needs\n\n   Criteria     Excellent (4pts)   Good (3pts)     Satisfactory    Improvement\n\n                                                           (2pts)            (1pt)\n\n\n              Performs all     Performs all    Performs 1-2     Performs few\n\n                steps exactly as   steps with 1     steps correctly    or no stepsCorrectness of\n                instructed       minor error                        correctlySteps\n\n\n              Follows the      Follows order   Mixes up most   No sense of order\n\n                exact order       with 1 small     stepsOrder of Steps\n               given           mix-up\n\n\n\n              Completes steps  Completes     Takes time to     Hesitates\n\n               quickly and       steps at steady   start/finish       heavily orTimeliness\n                confidently       pace                             refuses to try','assets/module/page-008.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [4.800099849700928, 774.25, 591.7001342773438, 831.1959838867188], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(9,'                                                             3\n\n\nLESSON 3: GIVE & FOLLOW ONE TO TWO-STEP VERBAL DIRECTIONS\n\n      (e.g., “Ask your younger sister to keep her toys away—what will you say?\n\n    Give at least two instructions”)\n    PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to phrase simple verbal instructions.\n\n     1. “If you want your friend to pass you a pencil, what will you say?” (1-\n\n     instruction)\n\n     2. “You want your sibling to do something for you. How will you say it?”\n\n      (1- instruction)\n\n     3. “What would you say to ask someone to open the window?” (1-instruction)\n\n     4. “If you want your mom to give you a snack, what will you say?” (1-instruction)\n\n     5. “Tell me how to ask a classmate if you need help.” (1-instruction)\n\n                                                          Needs\n                     Excellent                       Satisfactory\n   Criteria                    Good (3pts)               Improvement\n                         (4pts)                              (2pts)\n                                                                        (1pt)\n\n\n              Gives 2+ clear,  Gives 2         Gives a clear  Gives 0-1\n\n                  distinct           instructions (1   instruction    vague/unclear Number  of\n                 instructions 4    slightly unclear)                  instruction  Instructions\n\n\n              Language is     Mostly      A bit too       Confusing, too\n\n                 simple,           simple/friendly  Complex or    formal, or rude  Clarity &\n                  friendly, and     with minor        stern Tone\n                easy for a child   formality\n\n                  to understand\n\n                 Instructions     Mostly            Slightly off-    Unrelated to\n\n                  directly relate    relevant to the    topic          the task Relevance\n                  to “keeping my   task\n\n                 toys away”'