(10,'                                                             4\n\n\nLESSON 4: RECOGNIZE DESCRIBING WORDS\n\n     (color, shape, size, height, weight, length, distance, etc.)\n\n   PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to name basic describing words.\n\n     1. “Look at this red apple—what color is it?”\n\n     2. “Look at this big box—what word tells the size of the box?”\n\n     3. “Look at this round ball—what shape is the ball?”\n\n     4. “Look at this tall tree—what word tells us how high it is?”\n\n     5. “Look at this short pencil—what word tells us the length of the object?”\n\n\n                                                               Needs\n                                                      Satisfactory\n   Criteria      Excellent (4pts)    Good (3pts)                 Improvement\n                                                           (2pts)\n                                                                                (1pt)\n\n\n                All words are     Most words   Some words   No relevant\n\n                exactly             are relevant     are relevant     describing\n\n                describing the                                 words\n  Relevance\n                item/place/person\n\n\n\n               Uses 4+ different   Uses 2-3      Uses 1 type of  Repeats the\n\n                 types of descriptors  different types  descriptor      same word or  Variety\n                    (e.g. color + shape                                 uses none\n\n              + size)\n\n\n\n                 Descriptors are    Mostly correct Partially correct  Mostly\n\n            100% correct      with 1 minor                     incorrect Accuracy\n                                 mistake','assets/module/page-010.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [5.899899959564209, 776.9503784179688, 586.8499145507812, 833.8983764648438], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(11,'                                                             5\n\nLESSON 5: TALK ABOUT TOPICS OF INTEREST\n\n      (e.g., “Tell me what you think about this picture”)\n\n    PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to share basic thoughts about a topic.\n\n     1. “I’m showing you a picture of a dog—what do you think about it?”\n\n     2. “What is your favorite toy? Tell me one thing you like about it.”\n\n     3. “Look at this picture of a park—what would you do there?”\n\n     4. “What is your favorite cartoon? Tell me why you like it.”\n\n     5. “Look at this picture of ice cream—do you like it? Why or why not?”\n\n\n\n\n\n   Criteria    Excellent (4pts)  Good (3pts)      Satisfactory       Needs\n                                                          (2pts)     Improvement\n                                                                              (1pt)\n\n              Talks only     Mostly relevant Somewhat off-   Unrelated to\n\n               about           to the picture    topic at times     the picture\n\n                 details/ideas\n Relevance\n             from the\n\n                picture\n\n\nDepth of     Shares 3+      Shares 2       Shares 1 simple  Only says 1-2\n\nthought        ideas/opinions  ideas/opinions  idea/observation  words (e.g., “It’s\n\n                                                                               nice”)\n\n\n              Speech is clear, Mostly clear    Somewhat     Hard to\n\n               with good eye   with minor      unclear or quiet understand Clarity\n                contact         pauses','assets/module/page-011.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [5.899899959564209, 776.9503784179688, 586.8499145507812, 833.8983764648438], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(12,'                                                                     6\n\nLESSON 6: DESCRIBE IT AND I DRAW\n\n    (Show children a picture; they describe it so someone else can draw it)\n\n   PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to describe simple pictures in basic terms.\n\n     1. “I’m showing you a picture of a sun—describe it so I can draw it.”\n\n     2. “Describe this picture of a bird—tell me its color and shape.”\n\n     3. “I’m showing you a picture of a house—describe what it looks like.”\n\n     4. “Describe this picture of a flower—tell me its color and how many petals it\n\n     has.”\n\n     5. “Look at the picture of a car—describe its shape and color.”\n\n\n\n\n                   Excellent       Good         Satisfactory\n    Criteria                                                   Needs                                        (3pts)                       (4pts)                              (2pts)\n                                                      Improvement (1pt)\n\n\n               Describes 5+    Describes 3- 4   Describes 1-2   Describes no key\n\n             key elements   key elements    key elements    elements Detail\n                (people,\n\n                 objects, colors\n\n\n\n               Description is   Mostly clear    Somewhat      Impossible to\n\n              so clear,       enough to follow confusing       understand what’s Clarity\n             someone could                                 being described\n\n             draw it easily\n\n               Describes in a   Mostly logical  Somewhat     No clear order\n\n                logical order    order            disorganized\n\n                   (e.g., left to\n Organization\n                  right, top to\n\n              bottom)','assets/module/page-012.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [5.899899959564209, 776.9503784179688, 586.8499145507812, 833.8983764648438], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(13,'                                                            7\n\nLESSON 7: USING STORY CHAIN\n\n    (Each student has their own story; pair up to tell it in first person, then switch\n\n     pairs to retell the partner’s story)\n\n    PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to tell a short story in first person.\n\n     1. “Tell me a short story about something you did yesterday—start with ‘I’.”\n\n     2. “Tell me a story about a time you played with a friend—use ‘I’ when talking\n\n    about yourself.”\n\n     3. “Tell me a short made-up story about a magical animal—start with ‘I saw a\n\n    magical…’.”\n\n     4. “Tell me a story about something that made you happy—use ‘I’.”\n\n     5. “Tell me a short story about going to the park—start with ‘I went to the\n\n    park…’.”\n\n\nLESSON 8: USING PICTURE TALK\n     Pre-Test\n\n     1. Point to one thing in the picture and name it.\n\n     2. What color is the [object] in the picture?\n\n     3. Tell me about something big and/or small you see on the picture.\n\nLESSON 9: USING POEMS\n\n     Pre-test\n\n     1. Clap the rhythm of a nursery rhyme (e.g., \"Twinkle, Twinkle\").\n\n     2. Repeat a line from a simple poem after the teacher.\n\n     3. Do you like poems that rhyme? Why?\n\nLESSON 10: TALK, PLAY AND SHARE\n\n     Pre-Test\n\n     1. Describe what the people or animals in the picture are doing.\n\n    (Example: \"The girl is jumping.\")\n\n     2. What do you think the weather is like in the picture? How do you know?\n\n     3. Ask a friend: \"What do you like about this picture?\"','assets/module/page-013.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [5.899899959564209, 776.9503784179688, 586.8499145507812, 833.8983764648438], \"xref\": 12, \"width\": 2079, \"height\": 158}]'),
(14,'                                                            8\n\nLESSON 11: USING WORD ASSOCIATION\n\n    PRE-TEST (5 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to think of one word related to a given word\n\n     1. “I say ‘cat’—what’s one word that makes you think of ‘cat’?”\n\n     2. “I say ‘sun’—what’s one word that goes with ‘sun’?”\n\n     3. “I say ‘book’—what’s one word related to ‘book’?”\n\n     4. “I say ‘water’—what’s one word that makes you think of ‘water’?”\n\n     5. “I say ‘friend’—what’s one word that goes with ‘friend’?”\n\n\nLESSON 12: USING TONGUE TWISTERS\n    PRE-TEST (3 items)\n\n    Assesses prior ability to say simple tongue twisters slowly\n\n     1. “Say this slowly: ‘Red lorry, yellow lorry.’”\n\n     2. “Say this slowly: ‘She sells seashells by the seashore.’”\n\n     3. “Say this slowly: ‘Six sick sheep shepherds’ sheep.’”\n\n\n   Criteria         Excellent    Good (3pts)      Satisfactory       Needs\n                         (4pts)                             (2pts)     Improvement\n                                                                               (1pt)\n\n              Pronounces all  Most correct    Some        Many\n\n             words correctly  pronunciation    mispronunciati   mispronunciation Pronunciation\n              (even at speed)                 ons but still       s; hard to follow\n\n                                                   clear\n\n              Says the       Says it        Says it with     Stumbles heavily\n\n               tongue twister   smoothly once, 2-3 pauses       or can’t finish Fluency\n              smoothly 2+    with 1 pause\n\n                times\n\n\n Effort   &  Tries             Tries willingly,   Tries but is     Reluctant to try\n\n Confidence     enthusiastic     mostly loud      quiet/hesitant   or gives up\n\n                   ally, speaks\n\n                loudly','assets/module/page-014.jpg','[{\"path\": \"assets/module/image-12.jpeg\", \"bbox\": [5.89989995956420